training to expel the venom, Roll (Wits + Highest Martial Art) against the toxin's duration. Every 2 extra successes lowers the duration by 1. Completely eliminating the toxin from an envenomed weapon earns the martial artist one willpower.<br /> <b>Stone Ignores the Wind</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: Stone Stands Against the Ocean<br /> As a boulder is unmoved by breezes, the true warrior's heart is not moved by mere words. By performing mental katas, the wearer is able to ignore attempts to reduce intimacies. Use highest Martial Arts score in place of Integrity to figure Resolve.<br /> <br /> <b>Sapphire Evocations</b><br /> In order to unlock Whispers of Perfection's Sapphire Evocations, the Solar must first awaken at least two of its Emerald Evocations and have fully mastered one Martial Art.<br /> <b>Stars Surround the Moon</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: War 1, Essence 2, appropriate Martial Art 4 and form charm; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisites: Fists Break on Stone, Stone Stands Against the Ocean<br /> The beauty of the moon is enhanced by the stars around it. Such is the glory of the Exalted when they are surrounded by an army of mortals. By training a Might 0 battle group equipped with form weapons (such as training spearmen in White Reaper style) for one day per size factor, the Exalt grants the unit Might 1.<br /> <b>The Key That Locks Also Unlocks</b><br /> Cost: 5m;1wp; Mins: Medicine 2, Essence 2; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Stone Crushes the Scorpion<br /> The same knowlege that inflicts injuries can also treat them. The Exalt can treat non-amputating crippling effects and derangements by applying inducing her essence into specific chakras. Make a (Dexterity + Highest Martial Art) roll vs, the crippling penalty or 3,4, or 5 for a minor, major or defining derangement. Each extra succes lowers the penalty or derangement rating by 1.<br /> <b>The Smith's Favored Hammer</b><br /> Cost: 8m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 2, appropriate Craft specialty; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> A Craftsman uses the tools he knows best, even if they are not the tools another might choose. Once per craft project (but no more than once per day), the wearer may roll (Attribute + Martial Art) and add the result as non-charm successes to the project. Whispers of Perfection will allow an Exalt to attune to any artifact or hearthstone created using The Smith's Favored Hammer. This evocation specificly allows basic projects to be punched into existence; i.e., smashing a block of wood and picking a perfect wooden comb out of the kindling<br /> <br /> <b>Adamant Evocations</b><br /> In order to unlock Whispers of Perfection's Adamant Evocations, the Solar must first awaken at least two of its Sapphire Evocationsand have mastered three martial arts.<br /> <b>All-Encompassing Martial Mastery</b><br /> Cost: 6m; Mins: Essence 3; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: The Smith's Favored Hammer, The Key That Locks Also Unlocks<br /> A hero never knows what challenges the day may bring. With this charm, the Exalt may, once per session, with an appropriate stunt, substitue a Martial Art for any skill. Katas can be Performances or esoteric martial knowlege may help with Lore or Occult. It requires a major stunt to substitute Righteous Devil Style for Bureaucracy.<br /> <b>Shining Fist of Heaven</b><br /> Cost: -; Mins: Essence 4, mastery of 5 Martial Arts; Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Decisive<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> Virtuous Exalts project the authority of heaven against against all enemies of creation. While the hero has a form charm active in style he has mastered, his decisive attacks can do aggravated damage to demons, fae and undead.<br /> <b>Sifu's Wu-Jen Breaking Touch</b><br /> Cost: 6m,1wp; Mins: Essence 4, mastery of 5 Martial Arts; Type: simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Shining Fist of Heaven<br /> Fists that smash iron may also break subtler targets. The wearer of Whispers of Perfection may use a gambit to attempt to counter or distort sorcery using Martial Arts in place of occult. The martial artist must make a Martial Arts attack that targets the spell, with the normal target numbers for damaging sorcery. Completely negating a spell earns one willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right.<br /> <br /> Emerald, Sapphire and Adamant Evocations are not a thing.<br /> <br /> First Evocation. Permanent non-charm successes at ess 1 are bad. Admittedly, most of the time it will be adding Zero save against battle groups so it may well be limited. Now. How does the Legendary Size merit effect this?<br /> <br /> Second Evocation is fine.<br /> <br /> Third Evocation is unclear, to keep it simple it might be better to roll against the poisons Toxicity, or allowing the attuned to substitute wits + MA to Sta + Res against Poison.<br /> <br /> Forth Evocation is more or less fine, bit over priced maybe. Maybe make it so that it requires concentration and give it the Perilous keyword, cause if you're crashed, concentration is not a thing you have.<br /> <br /> Right, so if you want MAs to be mastered, I assume you mean at 5 dots because demanding charms up to Form Type is a bit of a tax and would drop the artifact down to 3 despite its power.<br /> <br /> Fifth Evocation... Flavorful. It's great, fits the theme and is useful. Might perhaps switch the duration to 'For as long as the Battle Group exists', and that way if they get wiped, you get a small surge of power as they break.<br /> <br /> Sixth Evocation. This is great for Derangements and low end crippling injuries. However, crippling penalties go up to -8, so you'll have difficulty meeting those. Also, this artifact seemingly lets you do everything with one ability. While this is good, you risk stealing other player's spotlights if you can literally punch all problems out of existence.<br /> <br /> Seventh Evocation. Not re-assuring from the 'I can punch everything to make it better front' BUT better than the previous one. Thematically appealing. That said, non-Charm Successes and possibly a tonne of them. Possibly none of them.<br /> <br /> Eight Evocation. No point repeating myself.<br /> <br /> Ninth Evocation. Should have the aggravated keyword. Otherwise, fine.<br /> <br /> Tenth Evocation. Again. No repetition and you should probably say whether or not they can use it at a range with styles that aren't normally ranged.<br /> <br /> It would also help having Type be below Cost and Mins, because it could be important when looking it up at a glance.<br /> <br /> And there's my two cents and I will admit, seeing the Emerald/Sapphire/Adamant split was something I found vexing, so I may have been somewhat harsh in my evaluation.<br /> <br /> I do like the restrictions on the Artifact, and the backstory is good. That said. It's a little too 'I can do everything' for what the past of the Artifact says about it. Maybe focus more on striking down the unworthy, possibly punching the badness out of them and go from there to being able to cure illnesses, derangements etc. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:55:48-07:00","id":894377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894345#post894345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Perception of Impulse (Orichalcum-and-Jade Infinite Chakram) Artifact (3)</b><br /> <br /> This infinite chakram is crafted of white jade, shot through with veins and runes of orichalcum inscribing the thirty-three names of Olgur-Zalesh. Crafted by a master smith of the Realm for his Immaculate cousin, it is specifically intended to hunt and kill demons - though it has slain more than one Anathema in its time as well. Marek the Bold was the first to die beneath its razor edge at the hands of Cynis Syazana, but not the last. At least three Lunars were killed by the Wyld Hunt that bore this chakram, and countless spawn of the Yozis have fallen to its strikes. For all that, it still hungers for the blood of demons.<br /> <br /> Whenever a Solar or Dragon-Blood who is attuned to this Artifact makes a successful <b>decisive</b> Thrown attack with Perception of Impulse against a demon, he adds that demon's Circle to his base Initiative upon resetting.<br /> <br /> <b>Ricochet</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Withering-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The least of Perception of Impulse's powers is a simple ricochet trick, guided by its wielder's Essence. This Evocation can only be activated when the wielder succeeds at a <b>decisive</b> Thrown attack made with Perception of Impulse. If the attack is successful, before resetting to base Initiative, the wielder can make one reflexive <b>withering</b> Thrown attack with Perception of Impulse at any one character within Close range of the first target. This Evocation's cost drops to 1m if either target is a demon.<br /> <br /> <b>Kiss of Momentum</b><br /> Cost: 10m ; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Ricochet<br /> <br /> Perception of Impulse amplifies its thrown force at its wielder's command. This Evocation is activated after a successful <b>decisive</b> Thrown attack made with Perception of Impulse. If the damage roll generates at least one success, the target is knocked prone by the force of the blow. The more damaging the blow, the more forcefully her opponent will be knocked away from him:<br /> <br /> For at least three successes, the opponent is lifted and bodily hurled into an object or surface within close range, hitting it with an impact equivalent to falling a short distance, destroying any less-obdurate objects she collides with, such as wooden furniture.<br /> <br /> At four or more successes, the foe is knocked into an object at close range with <i>tremendous</i> force, or is sent sailing a remarkable distance by the force of the blow. If the former, the opponent hits a surface with force sufficient to leave cracks in a stone wall, impacting with a surface as if he had fallen from a medium distance. If the latter, the force throws him to short range with a short-distance falling impact.<br /> <br /> If the target of this attack is a demon, the Evocation's cost drops to 5m.<br /> <br /> <b>Forceful Banishment</b><br /> Cost: 10m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Withering-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Kiss of Momentum<br /> <br /> Demons are tricky monsters, able to phase into and out of reality with a thought. Perception of Impulse dislikes this, and forces them back into the material world. This Evocation supplements a <b>withering </b>Thrown attack made with Perception of Impulse against a dematerialized entity. The attack deals no damage, unless the wielder can also strike dematerialized spirits, but if the attack is successful, the wielder may immediately engage in a battle of wits with the spirit. The wielder makes an immediate (Wits + Occult) roll against the spirit's Resolve. If successful, the spirit is forced to materialize reflexively and at no mote cost. The spirit cannot dematerialize for one round per point by which the Occult roll beat its Resolve unless it spends two Willpower to overcome this mind-influencing effect.<br /> <br /> If this Evocation is used against an unbound demon, instead of forcing the target to materialize, it banishes the demon instantly as if through the Demon of the First Circle spell. It literally hits the demon <i>so hard</i> it ceases to exist in Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First Evocation should allow for the withering attack after resetting the base initiative but immediately. Otherwise, the initiative gained is lost immediately upon resetting, which is only a problem if you play with a Rules Lawyer who's ire you have somehow managed to draw.<br /> <br /> Second Evocation nice.<br /> <br /> Third Evocation should have the Psyche Keyword. It also seems more like it should be a gambit, therefore decisive only and you could drop the price a tad Maybe 5m, 1wp since it's similar to sorcery? Also, it doesn't banish unbound demons of higher circles, apparantly, which is understandable but you might allow a Solar or DB to use it against Demons of the Second Circle as well.<br /> <br /> Overall, the artifact has a good theme to it, and the evocations clearly support the theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T16:07:56-07:00","id":894387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894377#post894377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Evocation should allow for the withering attack after resetting the base initiative but immediately. Otherwise, the initiative gained is lost immediately upon resetting, which is only a problem if you play with a Rules Lawyer who's ire you have somehow managed to draw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. Hadn't considered that. Will alter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894377#post894377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Evocation nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894377#post894377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third Evocation should have the Psyche Keyword. It also seems more like it should be a gambit, therefore decisive only and you could drop the price a tad Maybe 5m, 1wp since it's similar to sorcery? Also, it doesn't banish unbound demons of higher circles, apparently, which is understandable but you might allow a Solar or DB to use it against Demons of the Second Circle as well.<br /> <br /> Overall, the artifact has a good theme to it, and the evocations clearly support the theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will alter once I re-read the rules for gambits. Thank you!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T19:28:01-07:00","id":894505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894105#post894105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with others, please be aware of the formatting you do to an artifact before porting it over to the forums. It won't show up when you post, but when you try to quote anything it'll show all the tags from font, sizing, etc and it makes it a real struggle to go through bit by bit.<br /> <br /> I wanted to comment on Shattered Storm but it's just got too much in it for me to go through in the time I have at work. Suffice to say that I like their direction and structure, but I'm hesitant about allowing Balanced and Smashing tags on the same weapon, based on discussion I've seen in other threads. I'm sorry that I don't have the time to go through it step by step, because I'm not inherently against long evocation trees. I just don't have that kind of time to review them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for Sharkbite, I like your evocations for it. My questions are merely 2.<br /> <br /> 1) The essence pool the weapon gets. Does it come into existence full? Can it ONLY fill up from Sail actions? How long does it stay full for, forever? These details will be asked in game, so be specific.<br /> <br /> 2) Flash Flood feels at LEAST Essence 2 in power. An unblockable against multiple oppoents that also creates an environmental effect is super powerful. I'd drop the unblockable if you want it to stay Essence 1, personally. Also, I noticed that it creates a water pool 1 Range Band in diameter... meaning it only effects everything in Close range. However, Shark As Surfboard Approach lets you surf multiple range bands as long as it's in water. If you intended for FF to allow SASA to work for you, you'd need to use FF, move, FF again, move, FF again, and THEN cross 2 range bands back to the starting point. Does that make sense? I'm not saying FF is underpowered at all (far from it), but SASA doesn't really work with it as written (if that was the intent) so might need to rethink on that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With shattered storm, I'm cool with just removing the balanced tag. I mostly just liked the flavor of one blade being smashing and the other piercing. Balanced got tossed on as an afterthought because daiklaves get it. <br /> <br /> For sharkbite <br /> 1) The pool starts out empty and can only fill up from sail actions. It stays full until used. I will edit it<br /> 2) FF can lose the unblockable. I put it there because how do you block a pool of water, but I see your point about how powerful it is. I want to leave it at Essence 1 because all of the other evocations require a source of water. The intent with SASA was that you have to start your turn in water to use it, and it will carry you up to 2 range bands away even if that takes you outside the water.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1203-caladon","name":"Caladon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:22:04-07:00","id":894528,"title":"","content":"Okay, so in my first attempt at anything custom in Exalted (I very briefly played 2e, but I'm super psyched about 3e), I wanted to create a pair of artifact flame pieces that complemented both the Righteous Devil style and an Eclipse Caste who seeks to help Creation find unity against its enemies. Further, I wanted the pieces to be able to work as lesser artifacts when separate--my GM has the idea to start me off with one and have the other be discovered over the course of the story.<br /> <br /> I don't stress my inexperience to imply you should go easy, but rather to ask that if you have aaaaany advice, for, against, etc, anything at all, please let me know and explain if you can!<br /> <br /> I couldn't think of a decent smith name (I figured since they're guns, it'd make more sense to seek a southern smith as opposed to that famous western volcano smith), so figured maybe I'd seek some advice. Also, the name is still basically a work-in-progress...<br /> <br /> [[ <b>NOTE:</b> This has been revised. Please <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907881#post907881\">check here</a>. ]]<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Omens of the Pyre [Corona + Umbra] </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Orichalcum, Moonsilver, and Starmetal Flame Pieces) Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 [\u2022\u2022\u2022+\u2022\u2022\u2022]</span></b><br /> <br /> <i>Tags:</i> Lethal, Archery (Short), Flame, Mounted, One-Handed*, Slow<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In the glory and tumult of the First Age, Solars fought against all forms of Creation\u2019s enemies, from the raksha of the Wyld to the hellbeasts and demons of Malfeas, and even against their own kin, should they fall into wickedness. Such was the path of the Nameless Solar, known as the Pitiless Devil, the Blind Exemplar, and the Righteous Master all. He sought to purify the world with fire and will, and taught his unnamed arts to what few he deemed worthy to take up the mantle. This was the path taken by Heaven-Striving Flame.<br /> <br /> However, he lacked the inner rage of the Dawns, the single-minded devotion of the Zeniths, and the meticulous apathy of the Nights, for he received his second breath as a Harmonious Voice, a Wheel of Peace\u2014an Eclipse, exalted with the purpose of unifying differences into a cohesive whole that would be greater than the sum of its parts. He reconciled his roles by viewing himself as a gardener of Creation. With the righteous fury of his blaze, he pruned away at the weeds and decay that weakened Creation\u2019s beauty, such as Fair Folk and akuma, and with the compassionate warmth of his conviction, he nourished the life that deserved its chance to grow, if only he could know what it needed. This was the nature of his Eclipse, bearing both the might of the Unconquered Sun and the compassion of Luna as a bridge between and beyond. With this understanding, he sought out a gunsmith of great caliber near the Pole of Fire to request weapons that might represent the duality he would bring to his Righteous Master.<br /> <br /> [Gunsmith] knew precisely what was necessary, but her efforts took months and more than a few favors within the Heavenly Bureau. First, she obtained the metals required\u2014equal parts orichalcum and moonsilver, with a hint of refined starmetal. The metals were melted down in the heat of that same volcano, then divided for two separate alloys that needed to be worked in-tandem; one held two-parts orichalcum to its one-part moonsilver, and the other was reversed, while each carried trace amounts of the starmetal. But [Gunsmith] would not work these metals until the time was right and all was in place. In the meantime, she tasked Heaven-Striving Flame with three tasks, each more difficult than the last. First, she sent him to slay four different Fair Folk princes, each of a different Major Grace, in order to collect their Wyld essences. Second, she called for the blood of a Demon Prince justly slain for interfering with Creation. Third, and finally, she asked for a single tear, caught in its descent from the eyes of one who found genuine redemption and mercy from the growing cause of the Righteous Master.<br /> <br /> These conditions met, and Heaven-Striving Flame\u2019s virtue proven in her eyes, [Gunsmith] moved her work to the Imperial Mountain and bade her time until the awaited hour\u2014the coming of a total solar eclipse in the midst of Calibration. Only then would the raw essence of this craft most closely align to its would-be master. The moon rose, taking its place in front of the sun; [Gunsmith] held her tools, and her breath, until the blinding ring was set ablaze in the shadowed sky\u2014and like a machine divinely inspired, she set to work. It was as if time stopped within her workshop, the two-fold gaze of the celestial bodies bearing down on her through an oculus above.<br /> <br /> As the event came to a close, she was done, holding two masterpieces as one. Corona, forged to embody the indomitable might of the Unconquered Sun, glimmered with the brilliance of gold as moonsilver wound its way around the frame; Umbra, made to honor the primal guile of Luna, shone with ephemeral white beauty as orichalcum shone like starbursts in the streaks that held it. Both were infused with starmetal, particularly molded into the firing and triple-cylinder mechanisms, as well as lining their frames with ornate, prismatic filigree. In passing to the hands of Heaven-Striving Flame, their unified purpose blended together the essence of craft and wielder, revealing to him an awakening desire to cleanse the world of taint forever.<br /> <br /> When the Nameless Solar claimed his students in a blaze of judgment, Heaven-Striving Flame burned like the rest, and his pieces crashed to the floor. There they lay, buried in ash and, with the passing of time, sand and stone, waiting for the next virtuous wielder capable of using them both.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Evocations of Omens of the Pyre</b></span></u><br /> Omens of the Pyre is a single pair of flame pieces, but each piece is unique in both composition and essence. The weapons innately hold compassion toward Creation\u2019s ilk and fury for Creation\u2019s enemies (henceforth defined as including raksha, demons, Abyssals, and other non-divine outsiders), but most importantly, they ache to help their wielder fulfill some righteous ideal. Either piece can work on its own as a weaker, separate artifact, but together, they form a stronger, unified front.<br /> <br /> A Solar attuned to Corona who maintains an initiative advantage gains a +2 on influence and read intent roles; against enemies of Creation, she instead ignores 2 soak and hardness. A Solar attuned to Umbra who maintains an initiative advantage treats her enemies Resolve and Guile as weakened by -1; enemies of Creation instead have their Evasion and Parry are lowered by -1.<br /> <br /> A Lunar or Dragon-Blooded attuned to either piece instantly unlocks <b>Soul Fuels Ignition</b> free. A Lunar attuned to both gains +1 die on all attack rolls against a target each time she successfully Reads Intentions via <b>Soul Fuels Ignition</b> or she otherwise influences her target through the other evocations; these effects are cumulative against a single opponent, and doubled against enemies of Creation. A Dragon-Blooded attuned to both gains +1 die on all attack rolls against a target upon a successful Read Intentions via <b>Soul Fuels Ignition</b> and shares this bonus with all of her allies against this target; these effects are doubled against enemies of Creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Evocations of Omens of the Pyre</b></u><br /> Omens of the Pyre is a single pair of flame pieces, but each piece is unique in both composition and essence. The weapons innately hold compassion toward Creation\u2019s ilk and fury for Creation\u2019s enemies (henceforth defined as including raksha, demons, Abyssals, and other non-divine outsiders), but most importantly, they ache to help their wielder fulfill some righteous ideal. Either piece can work on its own as a weaker, separate artifact, but together, they form a stronger, unified front.<br /> <br /> A Solar, Lunar, or Dragon-Blooded who attunes to either piece unlocks <b>Soul Fuels Ignition</b> for free.<br /> <br /> A Solar or Lunar attuned to both who invests an extra 1 mote gains 1 non-charm die on in-combat social and damage rolls.<br /> <br /> A Dragon-Blooded attuned to both who invests an extra 1 mote gains 1 non-charm die on damage rolls.<br /> <br /> Against enemies of Creation, so long as the wielder maintains an Initiative advantage, they receive 1 additional non-charm die (to their respective bonuses).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Soul Fuels Ignition<br /> Cost:</b> 2m or 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> The devils of old converted internal power into external flame, setting their own essence ablaze to ignite the heart of their foe, and the wielder has learned this secret through the legend of her weapon. As the wielder inhales, she perceives flesh and bone as heart and soul, and in that moment of clarity she pulls the trigger, her own essence bursting forth as a bolt of golden gossamer flame that sets her victim\u2019s soul alight. In their unified burning, she can read his soul as much as her own, deducing the reason for her enemy\u2019s opposition.<br /> <br /> This evocation allows the wielder to forgo firedust, using motes of essence instead. Further, for an additional mote, her attack is enhanced with a Read Intentions action, which receives bonus dice equal to the number of extra successes on her attack roll; if successful, the primary Intimacy that drives her opponent to fight her is revealed to her in the essence-flames. She can use this multiple times, learning different Intimacies each time, going first through those most oppositional down to those benign.<br /> <br /> This affects battle groups, with the generally strongest opposing \u201cintimacy\u201d being revealed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wicked-Searing Coalescence<br /> Cost:</b> 4m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform, (Psyche)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant (One Scene)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Soul Fuels Ignition, Corona<br /> <br /> Many of Creation\u2019s foes cloak themselves in deceit and shadows, and Omens of the Pyre seeks to shine the light of the Unconquered Sun\u2019s fury upon them. As the wielder pulls the trigger and the hammer ignites the blaze, the weapon consumes the fires instantly, glowing with golden light. In that moment, divinity is channeled, and the barrel unleashes a burning ray of essence that causes even the staunchest of convictions to wither.<br /> <br /> As raw essence instead of billowing flame, the attack\u2019s possible range is increased by one band; as judgment manifest, the essence pressure weighs down upon the target, applying the user\u2019s Essence in successes on the attack roll. If successful against an enemy of Creation, this additionally inflicts a -1 penalty on all rolls for the rest of the scene, the manifest effects of divine judgment on their willfully opposing essence.<br /> <br /> Finally, if she knows the Intimacy that drives her opponent to oppose her, whether by <b>Soul Fuels Ignition</b> or other means, then the attack may double as an attempt to weaken that Intimacy by one level for the remainder of the scene (using [Charisma + Presence] as normal). This attempt receives bonus dice equal to the number of extra successes on her attack roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> This affects battle groups, affecting the generally-agreed oppositional Intimacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Villain-Revoking Lash</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Soul Fuels Ignition, Umbra<br /> <br /> <br /> Those who would openly oppose righteousness are blights on Creation, and Omens of the Pyre unveils Luna\u2019s wild contempt at their sin. The flames unleashed in this method move unnaturally, whipping around the target\u2019s hands and wrists (or whatever appendages are equipped with weapons) to sear them to the bone, preventing them from taking action against the wielder.<br /> <br /> This evocation supplements a <b>disarm</b> attempt. The attack roll enjoys her Essence in bonus dice. If successful, the target\u2019s weapon-wielding hand and wrist are burned, and he treats any actions with that hand with an off-hand penalty of -1 until it receives proper treatment. This charm explicitly allows disarming dual-wielders and applying the effects to both hands and wrists.<br /> <br /> Against enemies of Creation, the off-hand penalty is instead half the number of extra successes on the <b>Disarm Gambit</b> roll, rounded down, minimum 1.<br /> <br /> If the wielder knows her target\u2019s opposing Intimacy via <b>Soul Fuels Ignition</b> or other means, then a successful Disarm also creates an instant Instill roll to create a Minor Tie (Fearful Respect) toward the wielder.<br /> <br /> This charm can affect battle groups, under the condition that its cost increases by 2 motes for every Size category beyond 0, and a point of Willpower at Size 4 and above.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Purging God Presence<br /> Cost:</b> \u2014 (1a per bonus success, or 3m on failure); <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Dual Omens Culling<br /> <br /> As her flames burn the flesh of her foes, the wielder also burns away at their will to resist her purpose; at their lowest point, foes see her empowered conviction as raw, crushing presence. Against ordinary opponents, this presence is capable of inspiring them to atone for the immorality that brought them against her; against Creation\u2019s foes, this presence threatens to tear asunder the fabric of their existence.<br /> <br /> Should the wielder crash her target or otherwise reach an initiative advantage of 10+, her will presses down on the disadvantaged victim, enhancing a social influence roll (determined by opponent\u2019s classification according to Omens) of [Charisma+Presence+Essence] against Resolve.<ul><li>An ordinary opponent is forced to question everything that brought him against the might of the wielder. This acts as a reflexive attempt to Instill a Guilt-based Minor Tie matching the wielder\u2019s own purpose for fighting, such that he grows to sympathize with her cause; if such a tie already exists, or if <b>Villain-Revoking Lash</b> successfully instilled a tie of respect, this charm attempts to elevate it while also imparting the presence of this shared bond to both combatants in a moment of empathic union.</li> <li>Creation\u2019s foes feel as if the foundations of their lives are beginning to crumble as judgment settles upon them. If successful, the victim suffers a penalty on all actions equal to half the wielder\u2019s Essence (rounded up) for the remainder of the scene.</li> </ul><br /> If the wielder\u2019s anima banner is at the level of Iconic/Bonfire, she may instinctively convert levels of her anima into raw, overpowering presence, adding one success per level. In the event the target resists by spending Willpower, the wielder\u2019s righteous conviction may become mystically inflamed by their refusal, driven to seek retribution. For 3 motes, her next attack or influence roll against the same target within the same scene gains the strength of her opposed Intimacy in bonus dice.<br /> <br /> This ability can only reoccur on the same target if that target recovers from crash, and then crashes again due to the wielder\u2019s actions.<br /> <br /> This affects battle groups, occurring when the Magnitude track fills up and ignoring the penalty for socially targeting multiple people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prophet of Hope and Hellfire<br /> Cost:</b> 8m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous, Psyche, Aggravated<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Purging God Presence<br /> <br /> Just as valor must be balanced by temperance, so too must conviction be balanced by compassion, lest the righteous become the damned. The wielder aims at her target and ignites her eyes with the essence of her conviction such that they burn with the intensity of the sun\u2019s corona, allowing her, in a moment of searing clarity, to see the language of his conviction; by her fiery will, she reaches out to insist on surrender, and she knows the results by the stature of his soul.<br /> <br /> This charm enhances an Aim action with a Threaten action at no flurry penalty, gaining her anima level in bonus dice. Against ordinary foes, if she has instilled new Intimacies, it is instead a Persuade action playing on whichever new Intimacy is strongest, gaining the strength of the Intimacy in question in bonus dice in addition to her anima bonus; against enemies of Creation, if they have been affected by <b>Purging God Presence</b>, the Threaten roll instead gains her Essence in bonus dice in addition to her anima bonus.<br /> <br /> Should her effort completely succeed, the target finds his will to fight the wielder dwindling to nothing; he feels compelled to surrender at once and hear her out, and any temporary Intimacy effects she has caused become permanent. Should he somehow be convinced to join battle against her again in the same scene, the effects of failure immediately apply.<br /> <br /> Should her effort fail, the target perceives the coronal brilliance of her eyes turning black as the umbra of a solar eclipse, and he becomes cursed by her judgment; all Evocations henceforth treat the target as an enemy of Creation, and all her attacks on the target do aggravated damage instead of lethal, the righteous fury of wielder and weapon coming together to strike at his very soul.<br /> <br /> Should her effort fail against one who is already considered an enemy of Creation, all attacks do aggravated damage henceforth, and her next attack becomes a guaranteed success, receiving her Essence in bonus damage dice (aggravated if decisive).<br /> <br /> This affects battle groups, with her essence-sight judging the stature of their collective will.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Conflagrant Purification<br /> Cost:</b> 8m, 1wp, 1a per die; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous, Psyche, Aggravated, Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Prophet of Hope and Hellfire<br /> <br /> Judgment has been passed, and the defendant has been declared guilty of opposing Creation in the eyes of the Omens and their wielder. The punishment is a cleansing that will burn away his impurities or his life, the inferno striking beyond his physical form.<br /> <br /> This charm can only be used against one whose soul has resisted the effects of <b>Prophet of Hope and Hellfire</b>, and it supplements a <b>decisive</b> attack. However, rather burning at his body, it assaults his most oppositional Intimacy; as such, Resolve is used as a <b>Gambit difficulty</b> rather than Hardness, and it may not be enhanced using the Intimacy under assault. She may funnel the raw power of her anima into the strike, as well, gaining a bonus die for every level of flaring essence converted. Should the attack succeed at all, the Intimacy is destroyed, burned away in essence flame.<br /> <br /> If he is insistent on saving the Intimacy, the defender may spend 1 Willpower per rank, but never completely save it, bringing it only up to a rank below its original strength. If he does this, the fires that would burn it completely are instead vented into his flesh, and he takes levels of aggravated damage equal to the successes as a normal decisive attack.<br /> <br /> This affects battle groups, the fire of the attack swirling amongst them and seeping into each one to affect the group as a whole.<br /> <br /> If a Defining Intimacy is destroyed, or only preserved at Minor level, a sense of success fills the wielder's soul as she knows the target has a chance at redemption yet again\u2014refunding the point of willpower spent on the charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules: </b>This evocation unlocks in the event that <b>Prophet of Hope and Hellfire</b> is resisted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dual Omens Culling<br /> Cost:</b> 10m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 5<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Wicked-Searing Coalescence; Rebuke of the Blazing Ideal<br /> <br /> Sometimes, there is no hope of peace without action to spur it onward; as such, when the powers of Corona and Umbra are united under the purpose of a single wielder, they surge with the power of the solar eclipse, the grand omen perceived across the world as the combined ire of the Unconquered Sun and Luna. The wielder\u2019s reflexes surge with righteous essence, and in one motion, she unleashes a two-pronged blast of flame, an attack from each piece. The outcome varies on target and attack choice:<ul><li>If attacking the same target twice, the first attack may be withering and the second may be decisive. If so, the player simply rolls accordingly, with the decisive attack being treated as a staggered, near-instant follow-up.</li> <li>If attacking the same target twice, the attacks may both be withering. If so, the player rolls attack and damage once, applying the normal flurry penalty, dealing with all soak and other effects normally, before applying the same results again.</li> <li>If attacking two different targets, the attacks may <i>only</i> be withering. Each attack is treated normally, applying the normal flurry penalty.</li> </ul><br /> If she has learned of their opposing intent or influenced them in this battle, then the attacks carry the burning contempt of the Incarnae against those who continue to oppose the wielder, such that the wielder ignores her Essence in soak and hardness.<br /> <br /> Against enemies of Creation, all damage rolls enjoy double 10s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":11797,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","user":"Seeker","date":". 06-21-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:51:13-07:00","id":894774,"title":"","content":"I got this response to my first version of this item:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894374#post894374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Right.<br /> <br /> Emerald, Sapphire and Adamant Evocations are not a thing.<br /> <br /> First Evocation. Permanent non-charm successes at ess 1 are bad. Admittedly, most of the time it will be adding Zero save against battle groups so it may well be limited. Now. How does the Legendary Size merit effect this?<br /> <br /> Second Evocation is fine.<br /> <br /> Third Evocation is unclear, to keep it simple it might be better to roll against the poisons Toxicity, or allowing the attuned to substitute wits + MA to Sta + Res against Poison.<br /> <br /> Forth Evocation is more or less fine, bit over priced maybe. Maybe make it so that it requires concentration and give it the Perilous keyword, cause if you're crashed, concentration is not a thing you have.<br /> <br /> Right, so if you want MAs to be mastered, I assume you mean at 5 dots because demanding charms up to Form Type is a bit of a tax and would drop the artifact down to 3 despite its power.<br /> <br /> Fifth Evocation... Flavorful. It's great, fits the theme and is useful. Might perhaps switch the duration to 'For as long as the Battle Group exists', and that way if they get wiped, you get a small surge of power as they break.<br /> <br /> Sixth Evocation. This is great for Derangements and low end crippling injuries. However, crippling penalties go up to -8, so you'll have difficulty meeting those. Also, this artifact seemingly lets you do everything with one ability. While this is good, you risk stealing other player's spotlights if you can literally punch all problems out of existence.<br /> <br /> Seventh Evocation. Not re-assuring from the 'I can punch everything to make it better front' BUT better than the previous one. Thematically appealing. That said, non-Charm Successes and possibly a tonne of them. Possibly none of them.<br /> <br /> Eight Evocation. No point repeating myself.<br /> <br /> Ninth Evocation. Should have the aggravated keyword. Otherwise, fine.<br /> <br /> Tenth Evocation. Again. No repetition and you should probably say whether or not they can use it at a range with styles that aren't normally ranged.<br /> <br /> It would also help having Type be below Cost and Mins, because it could be important when looking it up at a glance.<br /> <br /> And there's my two cents and I will admit, seeing the Emerald/Sapphire/Adamant split was something I found vexing, so I may have been somewhat harsh in my evaluation.<br /> <br /> I do like the restrictions on the Artifact, and the backstory is good. That said. It's a little too 'I can do everything' for what the past of the Artifact says about it. Maybe focus more on striking down the unworthy, possibly punching the badness out of them and go from there to being able to cure illnesses, derangements etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>So,<br /> First Evocation: I know it's permanent non-charm successes, but in the vast majority of cases, it's +0, so I think it's OK<br /> <br /> Third Evocation: I phrased it just like Body-Purifying Admonitions (p. 344).<br /> <br /> Fourth Evocation: Changed it as suggested.<br /> <br /> I do mean knowing the form charms, which is kind of why it got a bit overpowered at the high end, I cut it back for the 3rd tier evocations.<br /> <br /> Sixth Evocation: I put a limit on how often it can be used, to prevent abuse. This was inspired by Ken curing the blind girl at the beginning of &quot;Fist of the North Star.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seventh Evocation: I eliminated the non-charm part of it and reduced the successes generated. This was inspired by Cologne from &quot;Ranma 1/2&quot; tapping a block of wood with her pipe, splitting it and casually pulling out an ear spoon. This evocation requires that the crafting project already exist. You can't punch stuff out of thin air.<br /> <br /> Eighth Evocation: Completely replaced. I really hadn't thought about stepping on other player character's shtiks.<br /> <br /> Ninth Evocation: Corrected<br /> <br /> Tenth Evocation. Clarified.<br /> <br /> And here is the New and Improved...<br /> <br /> <b>Whispers of Perfection (Silken Armor, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Dawn Caste martial artist Thundering Drum was offended by martial artists who relied on the finest weapons money and politcal connections could buy. He set out to create armor which would help him perfect his Martial Arts, and designed Whispers of Perfection. It is made from the silk of wood spiders, anhules and pattern spiders, which he interwove with orichalcum threads to create a brilliant red ghi, brocaded in gold and green and black with images of the creatures which inspired martial arts.<br /> <br /> Thundering Drum died on an expedition to the underworld, but his circlemates retrieved his panoply and passed it along to his successor, The Illustrious Chen Wu. Chen was killed 82 years later in the Usurpation, and the armor passed to her student/assassin First Leaping Tiger. Whispers of Perfection became the uniform of the sifu of the Greater Tiger All-Styles School in Parapet until RY 644 when Jade Caiman the Apostate declared that she had no worthy heirs, closed the school, and was buried with the armor in a tomb in Sijan in RY 670.<br /> <br /> The armor wants its wearers of develop their own power. Anyone attuned to Whispers of Perfection cannot attune to an artifact weapon or to a hearthstone with combat abilites. If one is already attuned to such an item, Whispers of Perfection will refuse to attune. Whispers of Perfection will never evoke a charm which directly aids in one-on-one combat against a mortal martial artist, but does have evocations which will help a martial artist to win against dishonorable enemies, or to perform other tasks where it is appropriate to ask for help.<br /> <br /> There are hints that if its wearer masters 25 seperate styles, this may unlock some special evocation.<br /> <br /> Whispers of Perfection possesses no hearthstone sockets.<br /> <br /> <b>1st Tier Evocations</b><br /> <br /> <b>Stone Stands Against the Ocean</b><br /> Cost: \u2014;<br /> Mins: Essence 1;<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> As waves break against a boulder, hordes break against the Exalted. This evocation is unlocked automatically on attuning to Whispers of Perfection. The wearer adds non-charm successes to join battle equal to the size factor of the largest battle group opposing him.This evocation only looks at number of attackers; legendary size does not activate it.<br /> <br /> <b>Fists Break on Stone</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp;<br /> Mins: Essence 2;<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Stone Stands Against the Ocean<br /> Just as an untrained fighter can crush his knuckles, those who attack the Exalted risk crushing themselves. If the wearer is ambushed, he has full defense and can launch an immediate decisive counterattack.<br /> <br /> <b>Stone Crushes the Scorpion</b><br /> Cost: 4m, 1wp;<br /> Mins: Essence 1;<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Stone Stands Against the Ocean<br /> Heroes do not fall to vermin and poisonous vermin deserve no mercy. When poisoned, the wearer uses her physical training to expel the venom, Roll (Wits + Highest Martial Art) against the toxin's duration. Every 2 extra successes lowers the duration by 1. Completely eliminating the toxin from an envenomed weapon earns the martial artist one willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Stone Ignores the Wind</b><br /> Cost: 4m;<br /> Mins: Essence 1;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisites: Stone Stands Against the Ocean<br /> As a boulder is unmoved by breezes, the true warrior's heart is not moved by mere words. By performing mental katas, the wearer is able to ignore attempts to reduce intimacies. Use highest Martial Arts score in place of Integrity to figure Resolve.<br /> <br /> <b>2nd Tier Evocations</b><br /> In order to unlock Whispers of Perfection's 2nd Tier Evocations, the Solar must first awaken at least two of its 1st tier Evocations and have learned the form charm of one Martial Art.<br /> <br /> <b>Stars Surround the Moon</b><br /> Cost: 5m;<br /> Mins: War 1, Essence 2, appropriate Martial Art 4 and form charm;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisites: Fists Break on Stone, Stone Stands Against the Ocean<br /> The beauty of the moon is enhanced by the stars around it. Such is the glory of the Exalted when they are surrounded by an army of mortals. By training a Might 0 battle group of at lest size 1 equipped with form weapons (such as training spearmen in White Reaper style) for one day per size factor, the Exalt grants the unit Might 1.<br /> <br /> <b>The Key That Locks Also Unlocks</b><br /> Cost: 5m;1wp;<br /> Mins: Medicine 2, Essence 2;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Stone Crushes the Scorpion<br /> The same knowledge that inflicts injuries can also treat them. The Exalt can treat non-amputating crippling effects and derangements by inducing her essence into specific chakras. Make a (Dexterity + Highest Martial Art) roll vs, the crippling penalty or 3,4, or 5 for a minor, major or defining derangement. Each extra success lowers the penalty or derangement rating by 1. If a condition is not completely removed, the condition returns at a rate of 1 dot per day. This evocation may be used by Whispers of Perfection's wearer once per day, but on anyone else only once per month.<br /> <br /> <b>The Smith's Favored Hammer</b><br /> Cost: 8m, 1wp;<br /> Mins: Essence 2, appropriate Craft specialty;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> A Craftsman uses the tools he knows best, even if they are not the tools another might choose. Once per craft project (but no more than once per day), the wearer may roll (Attribute + Martial Art) and add half the result (round down) as successes to the project. Whispers of Perfection will allow an Exalt to attune to any artifact or hearthstone created using The Smith's Favored Hammer. This evocation specificly allows basic projects to be punched into existence; i.e., smashing a block of wood and picking a perfect wooden comb out of the kindling<br /> <br /> <b>3rd Tier Evocations</b><br /> In order to unlock Whispers of Perfection's third Tier Evocations, the Solar must first awaken at least two of its 2nd Tier Evocations and know the form charms of two martial arts.<br /> <br /> <b>The Master's Harsh Tutelege</b><br /> Cost: 5m;<br /> Mins: Essence 4;<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: The Key That Locks Also Unlocks<br /> The sifu is foremost a teacher. Stubborn students need more brutal lessons. This charm can only be used on an opponent who, in this scene, attacked the Exalt from ambush, with poison, or with significantly superior numbers (generally by commanding or being part of a battle group.) The hero may use a gambit to roll (a social stat + Martial Arts) vs. Resolve to instill a minor tie of deferential respect. A crashed opponent cannot spend willpower against this attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Shining Fist of Heaven</b><br /> Cost: -;<br /> Mins: Essence 4, mastery of 5 Martial Arts;<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Decisive, Aggravated<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> Virtuous Exalts project the authority of heaven against against all enemies of creation. While the hero has a form charm active, his decisive attacks can do aggravated damage to demons, fae and undead.<br /> <br /> <b>Sifu's Wu-Jen Breaking Touch</b><br /> Cost: 6m,1wp;<br /> Mins: Essence 4, mastery of 5 Martial Arts;<br /> Type: simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Shining Fist of Heaven<br /> Fists that smash iron may also break subtler targets. The wearer of Whispers of Perfection may use a gambit to attempt to counter or distort sorcery using Martial Arts in place of occult. The Exalt must make a Martial Arts attack, using the normal range of that attack, which targets the spell. The normal target numbers for damaging sorcery apply. Completely negating a spell earns one willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11828,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11828-ikari-gendo","user":"Ikari Gendo","date":". 05-21-2016, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11828-ikari-gendo","name":"Ikari Gendo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11828_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:38:52-07:00","id":894809,"title":"","content":"Much improved. That said, the mention of Emerald/Sapphire/Adamant Evocations isn't a thing and is a throwback to the Leak, so I might avoid those. That said, a system of tiered evocations is fine for the occasional artifact. Not all of them though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T19:34:00-07:00","id":895238,"title":"","content":"<b>DARK SOULS 3: ABYSS WALKERS BOSS WEAPON (skip to 2:05)</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sgToAWR8N2Y\" data-code=\"sgToAWR8N2Y\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/sgToAWR8N2Y/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> Inspired by the boss's weapon in the second phase of the fight.<br /> <br /> My real darling Evocation in the following post is &quot;Warding Flames&quot;, which is my absolute best attempt to model the tactical wonder that is creating a temporary shield (of sorts) with each and every swing of your weapon.<br /> <br /> When conjuring other elements, such as wind, water, or earth, the waves might <i>actually</i> work like shields!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>WAKE OF FIRE (Red Jade Daiklave) <i>Medium; Melee, Lethal, Balanced</i></b><br /> <br /> This wonder was forged by a rival to the creator of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=823906#post823906\">Seething Drake</a> and Ashwright, who placed more value in conjuring fire with grace and control than in generating overwhelming heat. It went on to have a long and storied history in the hands of a Prince of the Earth who made it his mission to guard Creation against the depredations of the Restless Dead and other Anathema.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Wake of Fire:</b><br /> A Terrestrial or Solar Exalt may reflexively commit 3 motes to this sword to set the blade ablaze, adding +4 to the raw damage of its attacks and enabling the use of its Evocations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Warding Flames</b><br /> <i>3m; Supplemental, Instant; Uniform; Essence 1 \u2013 None</i><br /> <br /> This Charm supplements a swinging attack with the sword, producing a streamer of fire that traces the blade's arc. These flames guard the opening left in the swordsman's defenses and perhaps provide him a chance to escape. The flames die out quickly, so the window of opportunity is short.<br /> <br /> Until the swordsman's next turn, the target of the attack will be exposed to a bonfire environmental hazard if she opposes a Disengage action made by the swordsman, targets him with a Rush action, makes use of a successful Rush action's reflexive movement towards him, or attempts to use a non-projectile attack against him. She can only be subjected to one bonfire from this Evocation per round.<br /> <br /> These protections are automatically extended to anyone the swordsman is protecting with a Defend Other action, and he may choose to include someone he is holding in a clinch as well, should some magic allow him to maintain his hold and attack another character in the same turn.<br /> <br /> This Evocation is less effective against battle groups, which can surround the swordsman and attack from unprotected angles; when making a close range attack, a battle group may choose to ignore the bonfire in return for foregoing any attack or damage bonus from Size.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Veils of Fire</b><br /> <i>5m; Simple, One Round; Perilous; Essence 1 \u2013 Warding Flames</i><br /> <br /> By swinging the sword vigorously about himself, the swordsman may cut off all avenues of approach with walls of flame.<br /> <br /> Until the swordsman's next turn, a bonfire environmental hazard afflicts anyone he desires who enters his range band. He cannot use this Evocation while embattled, as minding his defense does not permit him to swing freely enough to employ this Evocation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Salamander's Tail Dare</b><br /> <i>5m; Reflexive, One Round; No Keywords; Essence 1 \u2013 No Prerequisites</i><br /> <br /> The swordsman trails his sword behind him as he runs, and his sword trails behind it fire.<br /> <br /> Supplement a movement action that takes the swordsman into another range band; it may be a reflexive movement action provided by a successful Disengage or Rush action.<br /> <br /> Until the swordsman's next turn, anyone who enters the range band where the swordsman ended the supplemented Movement action will suffer a bonfire environmental hazard, so long as they traveled roughly the same path. Someone closing in from the other side or diving down from above is not exposed.<br /> <br /> Additionally, anyone using the movement provided by a successful Rush action to pursue the swordsman and enter the range band he vacated (or anyone using a Disengage's reflexive action to enter the vacated range band in order to escape him) will also suffer a bonfire environmental hazard. But even if the swordsman somehow traveled more than one range band and the pursuer (or escapee) does likewise, she suffers only one exposure due to moving through the flames quickly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rushing Firestorm Concentration</b><br /> <i>+1m; Permanent; Uniform; Essence 2 \u2013 Salamander's Tail Dare</i><br /> <br /> Why leave behind perfectly good fire? Sword and swordsman may cooperate to pull their trail of fire forward, to launch it at their enemies.<br /> <br /> If the swordsman used Salamander's Tail Dare previously in this turn, he may cancel the effects of that Evocation to extend the range of a bonfire created with Dragon's Sword Blast by one range band, or to double the raw damage of any single bonfire conjured with this sword.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if the swordsman used Warding Flames previously in this turn, he may cancel the effects of that Evocation to double the raw damage of a bonfire conjured with Salamander's Tail Dare.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dragon's Sword Blast</b><br /> <i>5m; Simple, Instant; Uniform; Essence 1 \u2013 None</i><br /> <br /> This Charm supplements an attack with the sword, projecting a wave of fire out to short range. A target struck at short range is afflicted with a bonfire environmental hazard. A target struck at close range suffers an additional amount of raw damage equal to the raw damage of a bonfire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fire Dancer Mastery</b><br /> <i>Variable; Reflexive, Instant; Perilous; Essence 2 -- Dragon's Sword Blast</i><br /> <br /> The swordsman may spend motes or points of Initiative to raise the environmental hazard difficulty rating of a bonfire created by this sword as though the difficulty were a static value derived from their (Dexterity + Melee) total. Dragon-Blooded count a Melee Specialty for Wake of Fire as applicable for their dice-cap.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scorched Earth</b><br /> <i>6m; Simple, One Round; Uniform; Essence 3 \u2013 Dragon's Sword Blast, Veils of Fire </i><br /> <br /> The swordsman targets a range band at short range. Until the swordsman's next turn, a bonfire environmental hazard afflicts anyone currently within that range band whose first action is not moving out of the range band (a successful Disengage action counts) as well as anyone who enters that range band. This Charm's range can be extended by Rushing Firestorm Concentration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cutting Off Escape</b><br /> <i>6m, 1wp; Simple, One Round; Uniform; Essence 3 \u2013 Dragon's Sword Blast, Veils of Fire </i><br /> <br /> As per Dragon's Sword Blast, but must be made against an opponent at close range so that the fire may wash past and burn behind them. Not only is the target subjected to a bonfire environmental hazard, but she cannot attempt to Disengage from the swordsman until after his next turn without being subjected to a second bonfire.<br /> <br /> This Charm's range can be extended by Rushing Firestorm Concentration, so that it may target an opponent at short range and force them to attempt a Disengage action to move away from the swordsman on their next turn, or else suffer a bonfire.<br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-22-2016, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T23:25:29-07:00","id":895942,"title":"","content":"I really like this artifact, mechanically and thematically, but shouldn't the Evocations have costs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T06:55:46-07:00","id":896057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=895942#post895942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like this artifact, mechanically and thematically</div> </div> </div> </div>Glee!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but shouldn't the Evocations have costs? </div> </div> </div>Sorry.<br /> <br /> Wasn't sure which costs were appropriate, and I mostly wanted to get the VISUAL and MECHANICAL representations down and out of my head before I lost the interest to finish. Especially because I still have other projects I want to finish as well.<br /> <br /> I wasn't even sure what attunement bonus this weapon should give, but at least I can blame that on not knowing exactly what Dragon-Blooded Charms will let Terrestrials do with swords and fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:22:35-07:00","id":896140,"title":"","content":"Okay, I went back and added in some costs that should be roughly okay.<br /> <br /> I also settled the attunement bonus and made the initial idea into another Evocation, and I folded Vigorously Burning Bridges into Rushing Firestorm Concentration.<br /> <br /> Sorry for not taking the time to offer a more complete product from the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:36:47-07:00","id":896150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=896140#post896140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I went back and added in some costs that should be roughly okay.<br /> <br /> I also settled the attunement bonus and made the initial idea into another Evocation, and I folded Vigorously Burning Bridges into Rushing Firestorm Concentration.<br /> <br /> Sorry for not taking the time to offer a more complete product from the start.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to apologize! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This is all for fun, and I think you've done a magnificent job. After re-reading with the mote costs added, I can't say anything except that I would love to have this weapon in my games. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:00:55-07:00","id":896164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=896150#post896150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't say anything except that I would love to have this weapon in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Maybe you'd also like my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=870249#post870249\">starmetal mirror shield</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:28:31-07:00","id":897187,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">If anyone has the time, I would love to get a thorough critique of this artifact weapon. I'm doing a bunch of unusual stuff with it, and I'm not sure how balanced I can get it on my own. In case anything's off about the formatting, I originally tried copy-pasting this from a file, but that went...very wrong.<br /> <br /> <b>Huang and Loong</b> (Orichalcum and Red Jade Flametongue Repeaters), Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> There are a few paired flametongue repeaters in existence, such as Huang and Loong. They are unusual in how talkative they are, even when not attuned. While their voices often cannot be heard over the roar of their flames, the wielder can usually make them out. Huang is more talkative, never afraid to let her soothing voice be heard, exhorting the wielder to never hold back and never miss an opportunity to strike. Loong speaks rarely, yet simmers with unmotivated anger, taunting enemies about the inevitability of their deaths.<br /> <br /> Huang and Loong are fairly young, as artifacts go. They were forged well into the Shogunate Era, as an example to the spirit world about the rising dominance of the Immaculate Philosophy. Huang and Loon were once a goddess of the hearth and a lesser elemental dragon of fire (respectively), entwined in a romance that offended a powerful Shogun. The irony of their downfall is that as immortal weapons of love and glory, Huang and Loong are known and respected by many, while the Shogun who ordered their deaths is scarcely remembered even by the ghosts of former subjects.<br /> <br /> Huang and Loong are modeled strangely, for flametongue repeaters. They have revolving cylinders, but fire from the bottom chamber rather than the top. This leaves much room for ornamentation on their low-set barrels, carved from yasal crystal and gilded with orichalcum. Huang is modeled after a majestic species of bird long forgotten, her beak resting atop the muzzle and her dimly glowing eyes judging all who meet their gaze. Loong is modeled after a serpentine dragon, his coils gracing the sides of the barrel and his yawning mouth, with drooping tongue, barely managing to stay above the muzzle. They have no hearthstone slots.<br /> <br /> Huang and Loong can be wielded paired with no off-hand penalty. Each holds five shots, and they may be reloaded simultaneously. A single five-mote attunement is sufficient for both. They are medium archery weapons.<br /> <br /> <b>Tags:</b> Lethal, Archery (Short), Flame, Mounted, One-Handed, Special<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Huang and Loong</b><br /> Each attack with Huang and Loong creates a buildup of searing heat within the weapons, but without a mote commitment it dissipates almost as fast as it is stoked. The wielder may reflexively commit a single mote after attacking (hit or miss) to retain and control the heat, creating one point of a unique resource called a &quot;divine ember&quot;, which are manipulated by evocations. Divine embers dissipate at the end of the scene, if unused, and the commitment may be released reflexively at no cost (save for a display that obviates stealth).<br /> <br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blooded may draw power from the divine embers when reloading both Huang and Loong. Roll one die for each divine ember, gaining one initiative if there are any successes. Each success also counts as a peripheral mote spent for the purposes of anima flare.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Crucible Cannonade Flare</b><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Essence 1; Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Withering-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> As the divine embers build up within Huang and Loong, the flames they release are stoked ever hotter. A withering attack enhanced by this evocation can have some of its withering damage rolled as decisive damage dice which ignore hardness (instead of granting initiative). Up to one level may be converted at 1-5 divine embers, two levels at 6-10 embers, or three levels at 11+ embers (this does not consume any embers). The wielder decides how many levels to convert before the attack is rolled, but this may be reduced if she does not roll enough withering damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phoenix Spreads Her Wings</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 3; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Withering-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Crucible Cannonade Flare<br /> <br /> The wings of the phoenix cast a burning shadow across all the battlefield, bringing all under her gaze. This evocation allows the wielder to make a withering attack once each with Huang and Loong without the usual penalties or restrictions of a flurry. Withering damage dealt by these attacks does not grant the wielder any initiative, but are still compatible with its prerequisite. She gains only the base initiative for hitting and any initiative breaks.<br /> <br /> The player is explicitly allowed to stunt this so as to appear to be making even more attacks than are mechanically represented, taking a dozen or perhaps even more shots.<br /> <br /> If the wielder knows Resplendent Crimson Thunder, she may pay a three-mote surcharge on this evocation when she activates it after reloading Huang and Loong, and make three attacks instead of two. If the wielder knows Funereal Blaze, she can pay a total of 7m, 1wp activating this evocation after reloading Huang and Loong to make two attacks with each, for a total of four. Regardless, these attacks still follow the rules given above.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dragon Stokes His Flame</b><br /> Cost: - (1+m); Mins: Essence 2; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Crucible Cannonade Flare<br /> <br /> The heart of the fire dragon is a blazing furnace, and no strife can do anything but make it burn brighter. This charm can be activated while rolling Join Battle in order to generate up to three divine embers. Increase this limit by one each if the wielder knows Resplendent Crimson Thunder or Funereal Blaze.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Resplendent Crimson Thunder</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 3; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Phoenix Spreads Her Wings, Dragon Stokes His Flame<br /> <br /> The wielder vents the built-up heat of Huang and Loong outward, unleashing a blastwave of superheated air and smoke. This evocation requires 2+ divine embers to be activated, and creates a decisive attack that does not need to be aimed, ignores hardness, and does not require ammunition. Instead of using initiative for decisive damage, the wielder uses the number of divine embers as the raw damage, consuming all of them. This attack also does not reset the wielder's initiative, and does not cause her to lose initiative if the attack misses. On a miss, she loses 2 divine embers if she had 2-10, or 3 at 11+, instead of consuming all of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> In order to awaken this evocation, the wielder must create a new positive Defining intimacy towards another character of her own volition. Thereafter, the ability to use this evocation relies on maintaining this intimacy and the relationship this represents, as much as the story and circumstances allow. The wielder cannot activate any of Huang and Loong's evocations against them, even if she is betrayed. If the subject of the intimacy dies, the wielder may form a new one that qualifies for this evocation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Funereal Blaze</b><br /> Cost: - (+3a); Mins: Essence 4; Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Resplendent Crimson Thunder<br /> <br /> The wielder uses the heat of her divine embers to ignite her anima banner, unleashing an enormous plume of flame that dances and writhes across the battlefield. This evocation modifies Resplendent Crimson Thunder when activating it after crashing a non-trivial opponent while totemic. Her anima banner is returned to the dim level to power an attack that targets all crashed enemies within range, otherwise following the rules of Resplendent Crimson Thunder. Only a single attack roll is made, but it adds extra successes to the raw damage against each target. Furthermore, the wielder gains motes (outside of her normal pools) equal to her initiative to enhance this attack with instant charms, with any excess being lost.<br /> <br /> After performing the Funereal Blaze, the wielder both consumes all of her divine embers and resets to base initiative. This upgrade may only be used once per scene, with no reset.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> In order to awaken this evocation, the wielder must have gone through some great loss, such as the death of someone represented by a positive Defining tie. Thereafter, the ability to use this evocation relies on maintaining a Defining intimacy towards the memory of what was lost. The wielder cannot use any of Huang and Loong's evocations if doing so would somehow disrespect this memory.<br /> <br /> The loss must have been inflicted by outside forces. The wielder cannot simply cut herself off from a Defining intimacy (or have an ally do it) to be able to purchase Funereal Blaze, unless the target of the intimacy did something to deserve such abandonment.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1543-iethloc","user":"Iethloc","date":".  New version of Funereal Blaze 05-24-2016, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1543-iethloc","name":"Iethloc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1543_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T22:34:19-07:00","id":897583,"title":"","content":"Posting this while its on my mind. <br /> <br /> A bit of a joke present for my Supernal Brawler player. Theme here is just &quot;cram as many rediculous anime powers into one spot as possible while having them connect to each other&quot;. Take it for what it is i guess. <br /> <br /> <b>Sublime Percussion (Orichalcum Smashfists \u2022 \u2022 \u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Sublime Percussion is a net of moonsilver chain linking the hardened and glorious segments of Orichalcum etched with ancient script and a few hollows that once contained precious gem settings. In its normal state, the artifact looks like little more than a gaudy mess but once attuned it takes its rightful place, wrapped about the forearms of its master like a set of golden scale bracers. When set into combat positioning the chains wrap about the hands of its master and link the segments together to form impressive gauntlets. The missing gem settings do not detract from the appearance of the weapons, instead serving as a message to those that would see Sublime Percussion in the form it was crafted for - perfection of form, no room for arbitrary embellishments. <br /> <br /> <b>Attune:</b> A Solar or Lunar Exalted that attunes to Sublime Percussion may freely flurry the \u2018ready weapon\u2019 action without penalty, to bring the artifact to bear against their enemies. The magic of the artifact allows it to conform to any natural weapons possessed by its master and grants the light artifact weapon traits to any hoof, claw, fist or other such natural limbs regardless of the form they take. <br /> <br /> <b>Semblance of the Youthful Sun Dragon</b><br /> Cost: 4m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Prerequisite: None<br /> Once activated, this evocation grants the attuned exalt a Drive pool that fills during battle. Each attack suffered (whether successful or not) grants one Drive point and when the attuned exalt suffers <b>decisive</b> damage, they gain one drive point plus the wound penalty of the box marked for each health level lost. <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> Semblance of the Youthful Sun Dragon may be activated a second time for the cost of 2m as a reflexive action. Once active, the exalt no longer gains drive points but can spend those already accumulated to replace the initiative cost of any charm, ability or action (including gambits) but may not add more drive to a single <b>decisive</b> attack than their permanent Essence score. <br /> <br /> <b>Zone of the Hot-Spirited Tiger</b><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: Semblance of the Youthful Sun Dragon<br /> Activating this evocation allows the attuned exalt access to one weapon tag of their choosing from Reaching, Smashing, Chopping or Piercing. They may apply it immediately to their attack. Paying any requisite costs. <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> While the special activation of Semblance of the Youthful Sun Dragon is active, this charm\u2019s mote cost can be replaced by drive points. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Solemnity of the One Punch Man</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: Zone of the Tiger<br /> Solemnity of the One Punch Man is a <b>decisive</b> attack that has raw damage equal to the number of drive points spent since Semblance of the Youthful Sun Dragon was activated. This attack does not reset the attuned exalt to base initiative after attack resolution but in all other ways counts as a <b>decisive</b> attack, including losing initiative for failing. <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> If the attuned exalt has not attacked the target of this evocation at all during the current combat, this charm loses the perilous keyword and can explicitly launch a <b>decisive</b> attack from initiative crash. Succeeding at such an attack immediately resets the attuned exalt to base initiative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T11:31:52-07:00","id":898024,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Emerald Rose</span></b></span><br /> <i>(Sorcerous Initiation, Merits, and Evocations)</i></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#2F4F4F\">Of all artifacts dealing with Malfeas, none is so beautiful or as desired as the Emerald Rose. It appears to be a precisely carved blooming rose made of emerald, with a twisted adamant stem. The bloom is as large as two clenched fists, and the stem long and sturdy enough to wield the artifact like a mace, if one was inclined to try using it for such (treat as a light artifact weapon with the Bashing tag). It is no fragile crystal though; the rose is seemingly indestructible.<br /> In truth, the Emerald Rose is formed from the crystalized tears of Ligier, who was forced to cry once during the 1st age by a performance so beautiful that even the fetish souls of Malfeas wept.<br /> Those who stare into the emerald petals of the rose find reflected back on them glimpses of an ancient text. Those of sorcerous persuasions can discover that the rose reflects back upon them an image seen in it's surface long ago: an intact copy of the bindings and agreements that lock the Primordials within Malfeas. Further study shows many other sorcerous writs and documents from throughout the ages, including one book not yet written.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2F4F4F\">~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <b>Gathering Rituals:</b><br /> The sorcerer can grip the stem of the Emerald Rose tightly, biting the thorns into her hands and drawing her blood into the artifact and converting them into sorcerous motes. By taking 1 level of aggravated damage, the sorcerer can make a full Willpower+Occult roll, gaining 1 sorcerous mote per success garnered on the roll. This damage disappears at the beginning of a new day, but the sorcerer can only use this ability when she has no damage from prior uses of the rose.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#2F4F4F\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The sorcerer can call upon the sorcerous writings reflected upon the rose's petals, allowing them to stunt casting her spell through the rose. They gain a number of sorcerous motes for the spell equal to the stunt rating +2.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#2F4F4F\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The sorcerer can make the rose the focus of a summoning ritual, rolling Intelligence+Occult to accrue sorcerous motes. Every success gains her 1 mote from any summoning spell, but when used with any of the demon summoning spells, they generate 2 motes per success. These motes last 1 day per dot of essence of the exalt, and can be used to fuel spells.<br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <b>Merits of the Emerald Rose:</b><br /> Mark of the Emerald Sun (o)<br /> This ability works like Infernal Nobility (See Bargain with Mara) except it is the fact they carry a tear of Ligier that garners the demon's respect.<br /> Smells half as sweet (oo)<br /> Sometimes someone attuned to the Emerald Rose can smell when a summoned creature is not loyal to her. When the sorcerer is within short range of a summoned demon or elemental that is not loyal to her or a task assigned by her, she may make a Perception+Occult roll, difficulty 3, to be alerted to their presence. This is the only time that the Emerald Rose has a scent.<br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <b>Evocations:</b><br /> Emerald Lackey Designation:<br /> Cost: 5m, 1w, - (1m)<br /> Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite: None<br /> The Emerald Rose is a scepter of authority over demons. The exalt may touch the Rose to the body of a materialized demon and grant it improved prowess and marking it as the exalt's favored creature.<br /> The motes spent on this evocation are committed while the evocation is active, but willpower spent recovers normally. This effect lasts indefinitely, or until the end of the scene in which the exalt ends her commitment to this evocation.<br /> A demon graced by Emerald Lackey Designation is made a better servant, increasing the demon's physical attributes, join battle, soak, and granting them a hardness equal to the exalt's essence score. Should the exalt's essence increase while this evocation is in effect, the demon's bonuses increase to match.<br /> Once per scene, the exalt may spend 1m to pull the demon to them from anywhere in creation to her side.<br /> Special Activation Rules: An exalt who knows the Demon of the First Circle spell automatically learns this evocation the next time they pick up the Emerald Rose.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#2F4F4F\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Emerald Rebuke<br /> Cost: - (2m)<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: Emerald Lackey Designation<br /> Sometimes an example needs to be made. Whenever the exalt uses the Emerald Rose to make a decisive attack on a demon they summoned, they may pay 2m to have their attack count Double 10's, and add extra successes to damage.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#2F4F4F\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Emerald Siphon<br /> Cost: 3m/8m<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: Emerald Rebuke<br /> This evocation is explicitly allowed to be activated while the exalt is making the shape sorcery action. When activated, the exalt may siphon 1 mote of essence from every summoned demon she controls within close range of her, adding those motes to her sorcerous motes gathered for that turn. A demon loyal to her cannot refuse this siphoning, but cannot give motes it doesn't have.<br /> The exalt may instead pay 8 motes to siphon essence from every demon under her control within short range.</span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1401,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","user":"rungok","date":". 05-24-2016, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T11:44:39-07:00","id":898031,"title":"","content":"first artifact (for first game even)<br /> <b>The Treacherous Hunting Star (***** Orichalum Soulsteel Bow)</b><br /> An artifact from the first age, when war between the Chosen of the Sun was as possible as war against the enemies of creation, The Treacherous Hunting Star was forged with the ideology &quot;Cut off the head and the body will fall&quot;. Used from the First Age through the Usurpation to find those essence-empowered commanders and warriors and drive their mortal flocks away from them, the Hunting Star has passed from hand to hand before being lost in the South East during a war against the Giants of Dis. <br /> <br /> <b>Attune</b>: Upon attunement, for 3 extra motes anyone with an essence pool gets receives a +1 non charm bonus to Awareness checks.<br /> <br /> <b>Find the Quarry</b><br /> Cost: 3m Mins Essence 1<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration:Scene<br /> Knowing friend from foe, least from great, is key to the battlefield. Use of this charm replicates the spirit charm Measure on the Wind, with the perquisite that the person being examined is engaged in combat or clearly a combatant (a guard or captain off duty, for example).<br /> <br /> <b>Terror of The Hunt</b><br /> Cost:3m, 1wp Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive?<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration:Scene<br /> The bearer of the hunting star makes his presence clear, and his aim apparent. Mortals fear the hunter who seeks not just any quarry, but the chosen of the Gods and Dragons. Whenever a battle-group makes a route check, you may add your Essence to the difficulty.<br /> <br /> <b>Slayer of Kings</b><br /> Cost:5m Mins:Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> The arrows of the Hunting Star lust for the blood of the chosen, for champions that stand apart. When used to supplement a decisive attack against a target with an essence pool, the attack does bonus dice equal to the essence rating or the level of anima banner, whichever is higher.<br /> <br /> <b>The Heavens Weep</b><br /> Cost: 7m 2wp Mins:Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration; Scene<br /> So hateful is the Hunting Star to the Chosen, that it strives to shun even the Unconquered Sun and darken the earth. Firing an arrow that draws all light into itself, the Hunting Star makes day seem as night. Hungry dead and other ghosts treat the scene as they would any night, and mortal battle groups must make a rally check or flee in terror. Champions of the Sun seem to shine in this supernatural night, taking penalties to Stealth checks as if there anima banner was at bonfire. <br /> Of course, the Sun cannot be stopped by a mere arrow, now matter how full of malice. At the end of the scene the sun shines through again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:10:17-07:00","id":898061,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to post saying I've been very busy at work and can't do a thorough reading of the lovely Artifacts people have been posting (and so many!) but quick readings show great flavor and thoughtful mechanics. Whenever I get some freed time I will come reply here, but I don't want people thinking I've vanished or don't care. Just busy! Keep creating!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:09:37-07:00","id":898198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=898061#post898061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wanted to post saying I've been very busy at work and can't do a thorough reading of the lovely Artifacts people have been posting (and so many!) but quick readings show great flavor and thoughtful mechanics. Whenever I get some freed time I will come reply here, but I don't want people thinking I've vanished or don't care. Just busy! Keep creating!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great to hear! I figured you were just busy--there have been a LOT of artifacts in the past week, which compounds the amount of time it takes to give each one a decent critique, I'd imagine. I was going to sort of quote myself if nothing came up by Thursday, but that was just to be sure it wasn't lost in the sea of other new artifacts (many of which look super cool). I'm eager to hear what you have to say, since I have no idea what I'm doing and you're definitely one of the artifact gurus around here, but I totally understand being busy, so no rush at all! Life comes first <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:17:24-07:00","id":898207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=898031#post898031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">first artifact (for first game even)<br /> <b>The Treacherous Hunting Star (***** Orichalum Soulsteel Bow)</b><br /> An artifact from the first age, when war between the Chosen of the Sun was as possible as war against the enemies of creation, The Treacherous Hunting Star was forged with the ideology &quot;Cut off the head and the body will fall&quot;. Used from the First Age through the Usurpation to find those essence-empowered commanders and warriors and drive their mortal flocks away from them, the Hunting Star has passed from hand to hand before being lost in the South East during a war against the Giants of Dis.<br /> <br /> <b>Attune</b>: Upon attunement, for 3 extra motes anyone with an essence pool gets receives a +1 non charm bonus to Awareness checks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a bonus die or bonus success?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=898031#post898031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Find the Quarry</b><br /> Cost: 3m Mins Essence 1<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration:Scene<br /> Knowing friend from foe, least from great, is key to the battlefield. Use of this charm replicates the spirit charm Measure on the Wind, with the perquisite that the person being examined is engaged in combat or clearly a combatant (a guard or captain off duty, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make this Duration Instant. I would also try to more precisely define what &quot;clearly a combatant&quot; might include. Maybe something as specific as &quot;a person carrying a weapon other than a knife.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=898031#post898031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Terror of The Hunt</b><br /> Cost:3m, 1wp Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive?<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration:Scene<br /> The bearer of the hunting star makes his presence clear, and his aim apparent. Mortals fear the hunter who seeks not just any quarry, but the chosen of the Gods and Dragons. Whenever a battle-group makes a route check, you may add your Essence to the difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very nice. I like that it's scene-long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=898031#post898031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Slayer of Kings</b><br /> Cost:5m Mins:Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> The arrows of the Hunting Star lust for the blood of the chosen, for champions that stand apart. When used to supplement a decisive attack against a target with an essence pool, the attack does bonus dice equal to the essence rating or the level of anima banner, whichever is higher.</div> </div> </div> </div>As written, these are Charm dice, which makes the cost probably too high. If these are non-Charm dice, then I think you're good!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=898031#post898031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Heavens Weep</b><br /> Cost: 7m 2wp Mins:Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration; Scene<br /> So hateful is the Hunting Star to the Chosen, that it strives to shun even the Unconquered Sun and darken the earth. Firing an arrow that draws all light into itself, the Hunting Star makes day seem as night. Hungry dead and other ghosts treat the scene as they would any night, and mortal battle groups must make a rally check or flee in terror. Champions of the Sun seem to shine in this supernatural night, taking penalties to Stealth checks as if there anima banner was at bonfire.<br /> Of course, the Sun cannot be stopped by a mere arrow, now matter how full of malice. At the end of the scene the sun shines through again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this thematically. Mechanically, it may be a bit underpowered for its cost. Maybe drop it to 5m, 1w?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thematically, I'm not sure why an Orichalcum bow hates the sun. Maybe make it jade-and-soulsteel instead? Just my two cents. Overall, I like it a lot!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T15:37:44-07:00","id":898301,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Jade-soulsteel might work better, it was Orichalcum to attune more directly tie as a 'Solar made weapon to fight other Solars' idea. <br /> The attune was meant to be bonus dice. I'll probably adjust the prices and charm-vs-noncharm dice (I'm still getting the hang of that).<br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T16:46:37-07:00","id":898381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=898198#post898198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's great to hear! I figured you were just busy--there have been a LOT of artifacts in the past week, which compounds the amount of time it takes to give each one a decent critique, I'd imagine. I was going to sort of quote myself if nothing came up by Thursday, but that was just to be sure it wasn't lost in the sea of other new artifacts (many of which look super cool). I'm eager to hear what you have to say, since I have no idea what I'm doing and you're definitely one of the artifact gurus around here, but I totally understand being busy, so no rush at all! Life comes first <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ya I was thinking the same thing, since I think a fair number of us are not exactly great at Homebrewing this thread has kind of become the closest thing to a valid soundboard until arms comes out. It also helps that Hero goes out of his way to comment on most of the artifacts which is really helpful since alot of them do get lost at sea so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T23:43:18-07:00","id":898714,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay, and a massive thank you to both The Unsung Hero and Brennanhawkwood for your help. To refresh for anyone who has forgotten, this is regarding Lurking Shade the Soulsteel threaded cloak, with the Concept of &quot;Hides wearer for ambushes in combat.&quot; When I tried to quote both The Unsung Hero and Brennanhawkwood the site didn't seem to like it, so rather than fiddle with stuff I shall try to go through the points of both responses as methodically as possible:<br /> <br /> TUH Theme - Nice to have that opinion backed up, I'll stick with the cloak. Do you have any ideas of a similar theme for a pair of short daiklaves? I can respect a reluctance to add to the mile high pile of magic swords, but as far as I remember there are no short daiklaves in the core book. I literally just had an idea of two lovers trapped in the Soulsteel, but the only problem is that fits a single blade (one soul in each edge, with the detailing across the Orichalcum never quite touching) rather than the pair.<br /> <br /> TUH Attunement - I like the idea of adding an automatic success on Stealth while in shadows, but I would be grateful for opinions on an idea that I will be discussing below<br /> <br /> TUH NBS &amp; SU - For the dice adders I originally intended to boost the maximum possible bonus as well, by either Stealth or Essence, however I absentmindedly left that out. What is your opinion on, instead of a separate charm, just make the evocations extend the limit? Like<br /> <br /> Nothing but Shadows<br /> Cost: 2m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Add Stealth to Dodge when calculating the maximum evasion boost limit (though there must be a better way of saying that)<br /> <br /> <br /> Sundering Umbra<br /> Cost: 2m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Add Stealth to Melee/Martial Arts/Etc. when calculating the maximum accuracy boost limit<br /> <br /> TUH Other Evocations - Thank you for the compliment on Fading Specter. I will probably be adding willpower to Confusing Darkness and may re-order the evocations, but they also depend on that idea I mentioned earlier, which is still farther along<br /> <br /> Brennanhawkwood 1 - Yes, I'm pretty sure I intended Mute to be there, but I have a new idea that is still yet farther along<br /> <br /> Brennanhawkwood 2 - As written, the Anima probably would ruin these evocations, as before NEW IDEA<br /> <br /> TUH Anima - I had an idea of, instead of the cloak absorbing/burning off the Anima, have the Anima feed into the cloak, with the &quot;black, shadowy mist/smoke&quot; becoming more pronounced as the Anima brightens, with the Iconic bit appearing in the mist/smoke once it gets that far. It would still ruin Stealth outside of combat, as a large cloud of moving mist/smoke isn't exactly the most inconspicuous effect you can have, but it would not effect the stealth rolls needed for the evocations. In fact, I could also make my attunement bonus feed into it, maybe a boost to evasion at Burning and Bonfire/Iconic as you are surrounded by basically a moving smoke bomb.<br /> <br /> <br /> Attunement:<br /> Dim: the cloak provides one automatic success on Stealth rolls while within shadows<br /> Glowing: ... I have no clue<br /> Burning: +1 to Evasion<br /> Bonfire/Iconic: +2 to Evasion<br /> <br /> Nothing but Shadows<br /> Same as above, but requires Glowing<br /> <br /> Sundering Umbra<br /> Same as above, but requires Glowing<br /> <br /> Fading Specter<br /> Unchanged, but now requires Burning<br /> <br /> Deceptive Reversal<br /> Cost: 5m Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Counterattack, Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Sundering Umbra<br /> <br /> Gain a decisive counterattack, requires Burning<br /> <br /> Confusing Darkness<br /> Cost: 6m, 1w Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Fading Specter &amp; Deceptive Reversal<br /> <br /> Turn a surprise attack into an ambush, requires Bonfire/Iconic<br /> <br /> I changed Deceptive Reversal to 5m, because it doesn't really have all the extras that would make it cost more, and that's 2 more than Solar Counterattack, so I feel that it doesn't replace that charm. However it is very similar to said charm; I want a counterattack in there, as I don't want to require Solar Counterattack to make the cloak work as I want it to, but redundancy is (quite often) repulsive. Any improved ideas are welcome.<br /> <br /> I guess, in summary, my questions are:<br /> <br /> 1. Do you agree with my altered Evocations/costs/ordering?<br /> <br /> 2. Does my Attunement idea work, and in your opinion how much extra should it costs in motes?<br /> <br /> 3. Do you have any idea for a Glowing bonus?<br /> <br /> 4. Is there any way to make Deceptive Reversal more interesting?<br /> <br /> 5. What Artifact Level would this be? I originally set out to make a 3 dot artifact, but this is looking more like 4 or 5 dot.<br /> <br /> 6. Honestly though, is this just the Abyssal Anima effect? I can't seem to find it when I looked in my old books, but I wouldn't be surprised if &quot;black, shadowy mist/smoke&quot; is what the Abyssals get instead of bright glowing light. If this seems too Abyssal, then I'll have to redo it to be Anima Suppression like The Unsung Hero suggested.<br /> <br /> 7. (My apologies for the sheer number of questions) Anyone have an idea for the short daiklaves, and if not, any ideas how I can force star crossed and dead lovers to work?<br /> <br /> As before, thank you to anyone who bothered to read this far, and thank you in advanced to anyone who responds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11802-grasswatcher","name":"grassWatcher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T08:38:07-07:00","id":898957,"title":"","content":"So, worked up an artifact for my character to use in a just-started campaign (I'm not starting with the artifact, but the ST has promised that I'll find it at some point), and would like some input. I've already had help &amp; input on the evocations from SrGrvsaLot and RocketPropelledGrenade (the ST) on the RPG.net forums, but am curious what folks here would think about it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Livewood Heart (Green Jade Short Powerbow) Artifact (3)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once, there was a great tree on a hill. It sat in the sun, and the years turned, and it was content. Then a boy came, and he spoke to the tree; he told it of his joys, and his sorrows. Of his hopes, and his dreams, and his fears. The years passed, and through good times and bad, the boy returned again and again to tell the tree of his life, and the tree was glad.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Until one day the boy came and told the tree that he must leave, and he knew not when he would return. The tree was desolate, but the boy had been chosen by the sun, and that call would not be denied. And so the tree gave unto the boy a piece of its heart, that they might always be together, no matter the distance between them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And so the boy journeyed, and became a great hero. But before he could return, darkness came to the hill; the winds grew hot, and the sun was blocked by sheets of ash, and the tree burned. Through the piece of heartwood he carried, the boy felt the tree\u2019s anguish, and in his grief and his anger, he took the tree\u2019s heart and used it to fashion a bow, that he might take revenge upon those who had stolen his closest friend from him.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And yet, the tree was not truly dead, for that piece of its heart still lived, and its love tempered the boy\u2019s anger, reminding him that death is ever a part of life, and new life springs from the dead, for such is the cycle to which all that live are bound.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Livewood Heart is a composite short powerbow made of ancient - but still living - wood and green jade, blended together with no visible seam or join. If planted in moist soil, it will put down roots and sprout branches, but these will separate easily if an Exalt attunes to the bow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Livewood Heart has two hearthstone sockets, set into the inside of the bow\u2019s curve, one each directly above and below the grip.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evocations of Livewood Heart</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Solar or Dragonblooded who attunes to Livewood Heart gains One Root Spirit at no cost.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><i>One Root Spirit</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 1m </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Reflexive </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 1 day </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> None</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">When the character uses One Root Spirit, he reaches out and plucks a branch from a nearby bush or tree, transforming it into a living arrow. This can be done a part of a normal attack with Livewood Heart without requiring a flurry or they may be saved for later, but no more than one arrow may be transformed per turn and no other bow may use these these living arrows, as they tend to latch onto any wooden or earthen surface and take root inside. If they are not planted within 1 day of being transformed, they will wither and die, becoming useless as ammunition for Livewood Heart (though perhaps an excellent source of arrow shafts for lesser bows).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><i>Spreading Tendrils Offense</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 1m </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Supplemental </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 1 turn </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Uniform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> One Root Spirit</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The character's living arrow grows and changes mid-flight, branching and recombining in unpredictable organic patterns that make it extremely distracting, even to a wary foe. An attack supplemented by this evocation imposes a -2 onslaught penalty, instead of the normal -1.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><i>Tangling Root Glamour</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 4m, 2i </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Supplemental </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Instant </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Uniform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> One Root Spirit</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The character's living arrow grows fiercely as it approaches the target, tangling them in a mass of rampant vegetation that makes it difficult to move. If an attack supplemented by this evocation is successful, the target is effectively prone. They may not be literally knocked to the ground, but the vines that pin them to a wall or bind their elbows to their knees impose exactly the same penalty, and that penalty may be removed by a combat movement action, equivalent to &quot;rise from prone.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><i>Hungry Roots Consumption</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 8m, 1wp </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Simple </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 1+ turns </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Decisive Only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Spreading Tendrils Offense, Tangling Root Glamour</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The character's living arrow latches onto a target, seeking out their blood and rooting within, whereupon it quickly devours this powerful source of life energy to fuel its out-of-control growth.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">This charm allows the character to use a special Difficulty 3 gambit. If the gambit succeeds, the arrow takes root in the target's body and begins growing, dealing one health level of lethal damage immediately, and an additional health level of damage on each of the target's turns, continuing until the target has suffered damage equal to the wielder's Dexterity. The target also suffers a -2 penalty to all actions, and a -1 penalty to Parry and Evasion, for the remainder of the scene, due to the pain of the living plants expanding through their body. If the target is killed by the damage from this Evocation, or while the damage from it is ongoing, plants completely overtake their entire body, sprouting from every orifice in a grisly display of nature run amuck.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">This evocation may be used once per scene unless reset by the wielder of Livewood Heart drawing a living arrow from the mass of vegetation that sprouted from a victim killed under the effects of Hungry Root Consumption.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11863,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11863-jondera","user":"Jondera","date":". 05-25-2016, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11863-jondera","name":"Jondera","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:16:38-07:00","id":899388,"title":"","content":"Nice.<br /> <br /> <br /> tencount","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T20:25:26-07:00","id":899693,"title":"","content":"Just a little something I decided to do as an experiment with the Evocations systems - specifically playing with the question of &quot;what would an artifact weapon with no Essence 2+ Evocations look like?&quot; It's more likely to be fodder for an NPC concept or &quot;free&quot; introductory artifact than something a player will choose during chargen.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">The White Cadet Blade</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">(White Jade Reaver Daiklaive, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <br /> The White Cadet Blade was once one of a set of five jade swords \u2013 one for each element \u2013 forged by the crafts instructor of the Academy of Harmonious Jade Dragons during the Shogunate. The esteemed martial arts college held a swordsmanship competition each season for those students who had not enrolled more than a year ago. The winner in each season received one of the five jade cadet blades as a trophy to be worn until the next year\u2019s contest in that season, at which time the student was expected to pass it to the next champion.<br /> The cadet blades were a daiklaive of red jade, a reaper daiklaive of green jade, a grand daiklaive of black jade, a short daiklaive of blue jade, and a reaver daiklaive of white jade. The five cadet blades marked those who showed exceptional promise, but those champions who meditated upon the blades found that more advanced martial disciplines came to them more easily. The swords\u2019 creator intended that they be teaching aides as well as trophies, but he did not wish that any student should grow too reliant upon them and so grow reluctant to pass them to the next champion, and so they were forged to diminish in power as the champion grew in knowledge.<br /> <br /> For fifty years the five cadet blades passed from champion to champion, and the academy\u2019s masters noticed, but hardly remarked, the subtle resonance between the weapons that caused each blade to call to the others. It wasn\u2019t until Jade Grass Drifting, the champion of the Green Cadet Blade, killed Crimson Running River (the champion of the Red Cadet Blade) in an unsanctioned duel and seized the red blade for himself that anyone understood why the old crafts instructor had stipulated that no student should wield two cadet blades at once, for Jade Grass Drifting discovered he could learn from both cadet blades. Knowing he would be stripped of them because of his forbidden duel, he fled the academy. The other champions discovered that they could sense the red and green blades through their own and, enraged by the theft of two of the cadet blades, they wished to bring Jade Grass Drifting to justice and return the cadet blades to the academy.<br /> <br /> The masters of the academy forbade this, for they knew that the cadet blades the champions carried would fail the eager students and so fall into the hands of outsiders. Their decree held for several years, until the champion of the Black Cadet Blade undertook that quest without the masters\u2019 approval. She did not return, and so the number of cadet blades at the Academy of Harmonious Jade Dragons was reduced to two. The masters of the academy locked away the remaining cadet blades in separate vaults, but a well-meaning young student overcame the wards that protected the Blue Cadet Blade and disappeared on the same quest that had taken the champion of the Black Cadet Blade.<br /> <br /> The academy was hard-hit by the Great Contagion, which killed everyone who knew how to access the White Cadet Blade, and so the Scarlet Empress\u2019s forces found the school abandoned except for a handful of students and a single master teacher, whom House Cathak convinced to join the staff at the Academy of Bells. The White Cadet Blade was recovered by one of that master\u2019s former students in the teacher\u2019s twilight days. It again became a trophy and teaching tool at the Academy of Bells, although no student was allowed to keep it for more than a season at a time \u2013 a rule that seems to have spared it from the fate of its brother blades for several centuries. A year ago, however, the White Cadet Blade and its champion disappeared along with four other Dragon-Blooded students, so ending the legacy of the cadet blades of the Academy of Harmonious Jade Dragons. Those who knew the young Dynasts say the five hoped to gather all five cadet blades together, but the artifacts are surely so scattered across Creation by now, and so no one expects to see the champion, his friends, or the White Cadet Blade ever again.<br /> The White Cadet Blade is intended as a teaching tool only and does not have a hearthstone socket.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Evocations of the White Cadet Blade</span></span><br /> <br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blooded who attunes to the White Cadet Blade can sense the direction in which the next nearest cadet blade lies. Additionally, if she gives the daiklaive freely to another Solar or Dragon-Blooded with Essence 1, she receives a full refund of all Experience (and Solar Experience) she has spent on the artifact\u2019s Evocations and may immediately spend these without the need for training time. If the former champion unlocked White Blade Cadet and/or White Blade Champion, she almost always uses some of this Experience to purchase the Charms those Evocations granted her (provided her Essence is now high enough).<br /> <br /> <b>Ruthless Reaver\u2019s Chop</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> The White Cadet Blade guides the student\u2019s hand through the chopping motions that leverage the reaver daiklaive\u2019s weight, adding force to her strikes until she has mastered her technique. When making a chopping attack with the White Cadet Blade, the wielder increases the raw damage of a <b>withering</b> attack by an additional (6 - twice Essence) or treats the target\u2019s Hardness as an additional (6 - twice Essence) lower on a <b>decisive</b> attack. For example, the <b>withering</b> chopping attack of a wielder with Essence 1 inflicts an additional 7 raw damage (4 due to this Evocation, plus the usual 3 for chopping), and the <b>decisive</b> chopping attack by an Essence 1 wielder treats the target\u2019s Hardness as 6 lower (4 for the Evocation, plus 2 for due to chopping). This is 5 raw damage or 4 Harness lower at Essence 2, and this Evocation grants no advantage to a wielder with Essence 3 or higher.<br /> <br /> <b>Penultimate Executioner\u2019s Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Ruthless Reaver\u2019s Chop<br /> The White Cadet Blade teaches its pupil to wait for the moment when her opponent is most vulnerable before launching the attack that separates head from shoulders. The wielder may activate this Evocation when she crashes an opponent or achieves initiative shift on a <b>withering</b> attack with White Cadet Blade to gain additional Initiative equal to (6 - twice Essence). A wielder with Essence 2, for example, would gain 7 Initiative by crashing an opponent (2 for this Evocation, plus the normal 5) and would gain 2 additional Initiative after achieving initiative shift. One with Essence 1 would gain 9 Initiative or 4 extra Initiative, while one with Essence 3 or higher receives no benefit from this Evocation.<br /> <br /> <b>White Blade Cadet</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Penultimate Executioner\u2019s Strike<br /> The White Cadet Blade helps its apprentice master a technique that lies just beyond her grasp. When the wielder unlocks this Evocation, she chooses one Athletics, Integrity, Melee, or Resistance Charm for which she meet all prerequisites except its Essence requirement. She may instead choose a Martial Arts Charm that meets these criteria, but the style must be compatible with chopping swords. Regardless, she can use that Charm following normal activation rules so long as she is attuned to and carries White Cadet Blade. This Evocation cannot be used as a prerequisite for other Charms, but it can be used as a prerequisite for Charms gained through White Blade Champion or other Cadet Blade Evocations that allow the wielder to gain access to Charms.<br /> <br /> <b>White Blade Champion</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Black Blade Cadet<br /> The White Cadet Blade provides her prot\u00e9g\u00e9 with a final lesson, sometimes building on the technique it already taught her and sometimes guiding her down a different educational path. When the wielder masters this Evocation, she chooses a second Athletics, Integrity, Melee, or Resistance Charm per the prerequisite Evocation. This Evocation cannot be used as the prerequisite for other Charms except for those granted by other Cadet Blade Evocations that grant the wielder access to Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 05-25-2016, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T20:31:13-07:00","id":899700,"title":"","content":"I like that it gets worse as your essence goes up, making it 1.clearly a training sword and 2. giving people a good reason to pass it on to their pupils. There's some interesting narratives in that.<br /> ...<br /> ...<br /> *yoink*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:42:28-07:00","id":900225,"title":"","content":"Ad me to the list of yoinking artifact thieves. Great job!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","name":"7 questions vanquish god","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11843_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:57:09-07:00","id":900274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=892693#post892693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first attempt at creating... well, anything really... for 3E!<br /> <br /> <b>Luminous Rapture (Orichalcum Powerbow) Artifact (3)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Neat. But I would include starmetal in its design.<br /> <br /> Not simply because it came from one of the Maidens, but because it deals with ephemeral concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:13:39-07:00","id":900436,"title":"","content":"<b>Red Queen (Devil May Cry 4)</b><br /> <br /> <i>Revving:</i> You can use a Miscellaneous action to revv up the engine, filling one of three Lamps. You can spend one Lamp to enhance an attack with the Red Queen; an Ex-Attack. Grants a bonus to a Rush action, an attack roll, or a damage roll.<br /> <br /> <i>Command Attack(s)</i>: Expends (more than one / all available) Lamps for bonuses to a Rush action, an attack roll, a Rush action flurried with an attack roll, <i>and </i>any damage roll. Quite possibly, all of the Command Attacks are represented as one Evocation; fancier, individuated applications of this explosive power would instead rely on the user's own Melee or Martial Arts Charms; Nero was not an unskilled swordsman who swung the Red Queen around blindly.<br /> <br /> <i>Ex-Act:</i> Reflexively fill a Lamp (or reduce the Lamp cost of an enhanced attack by one) when you beat an enemy's Defense.<br /> <br /> <i>Max-Act:</i> As Ex-Act, but if your attack enjoys a number of extra successes at least equal to the target's Essence score, you fill ALL three Lamps after the attack is over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:18:02-07:00","id":900440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=900274#post900274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat. But I would include starmetal in its design.<br /> <br /> Not simply because it came from one of the Maidens, but because it deals with ephemeral concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Done and done!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:58:27-07:00","id":900473,"title":"","content":"Hello~<br /> We're starting up a campaign in a week or so and I had a few extra dots left to create artifacts with.<br /> <br /> I've written up two sister artifacts, each at 4 dots: Angelheart Vial and Decree of Iona, one of which is owned by my player character (Vial), while the other is owned by her rival (Decree). Angelheart Vial is a pendant that encourages the wearer to play as a guardian angel, protecting their chosen ward while Decree of Iona is the opposite, a circlet that encourages the wearer to fight the opposition to protect their partner. Together, their theme is &quot;Sacrificing One's Self for the Person the Love&quot;, and the pair of artifacts is developed to encourage the theme through their evocations.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>\u300c<b>Angelheart Vial</b>\u300d</u></span>(Artifact Pendant: ****)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attunement: 2m<br /> <br /> A small and elegant pendant crafted of orachalcum, glowing with a soft aura of warmth and safety. From the brooch, hangs a vial, slotted for a single gem. The pendant's wards and magic stem from the love the wearer has towards another, and strengthened if her love is returned.<br /> When attuned, the wearer is as if she were protected by the heavens. Attacks and blows miss her, as if the threads of fate were twisted, as so the blows would never have hit.<br /> <br /> Soulbond: If the wearer and the target each have a major or greater intimacy of love (Agape, Phileo,Stroge, or Eros), towards the other, upon performing a ritual, the wearer may declare the target to be her Soulbond. The wearer may not be soulbonded with more than one person. If the wearer's intimacy towards her Soulbound is *defining*, her Soulbound is aware of the wearer's every intimacy.<br /> <br /> Passive effect:<br /> While attuned with the pendant, the wearer receives +1 to parry and evasion, which does not count as dice provided by a charm.<br /> <br /> Evocations of \u300cAngelheart Vial\u300d:<br /> <br /> \u300cSeraph's Heavenly Ward\u300d (Cost: 3m; Type: Simple; Duration: Indefinite):<br /> While within a close vicinity of each other and the wearer is both attuned and committed her motes to the ward, the wearer's Soulbond is protected by the Angelheart, channeled through the pair's bond. The Soulbond adds half the wearer's Parry or Evasion, whichever is greater, rounded down, to his Soak.<br /> <br /> \u300cAngel's Sacrifice\u300d(cost: 5m; Type: Simple; Duration: Indefinite):<br /> Prerequisite: \u300cSeraph's Heavenly Ward\u300d, Essence 2<br /> The wearer links her own body with her Soulbond, taking a part of his suffering as her own.<br /> If her Soulbond would take damage to their Health Track, they take only half, rounded up. The remaining damage they would have taken is instead dealt to the wearer's Health Track.<br /> <br /> \u300cGrand Aegis of the Seraph\u300d (Cost:-; Type: Permanent; Duration:Permanent):<br /> Preqioste: \u300cAngel's Sacrifice\u300d, Essence 2<br /> The guardian spirit of the \u300cAngelheart Vial\u300d grants the wearer greater defenses. While the wearer is in combat and nearby her Soulbond and her intimacy towards him is defining, the passive defensive bonus granted by \u300cAngelheart Vial\u300d is doubled.<br /> In addition, the wearers intimacy towards her Soulbond may never be lowered by any external influence.<br /> <br /> \u300cIn The Dawn, Two Souls Entwined\u300d(Cost: 7m; Type: Simple; Duration: Indefinite):<br /> Prerequiste: \u300cGrand Aegis of the Seraph\u300d, Essence 2<br /> While the wearer keeps her commitment to this evocation and her Soulbond has motes committed to \u300cIn The Dawn, Two Souls Entwined\u300d, the cost of \u300cAngel's Sacrifice\u300d &amp; \u300cGrand Aegis of the Seraph\u300d is reduced to 0m.<br /> In addition, the wearer receives the passive effect of \u300cDecree of Iona\u300d.<br /> If either of the pair ceases their commitment to either evocation, the other's commitment to their respective evocation is revoked as well.<br /> <br /> \u300cAngel's Grace\u300d(Cost: 7m; Type: Reflexive; Duration: Instant):<br /> Prerequisite: \u300cGrand Aegis of the Seraph\u300d, Essence 3<br /> If the wearer has a defining intimacy towards her Soulbond, and her Soulbond has his last Health Level filled, she may expend the energy of the Hearthstone held within the pendant, performing a single miracle to save her Soulbond.<br /> In its last moments, the pendant returns to the wearer all of the motes she has committed to the evocations granted by the pendant, but it's forever shattered inert, having exhausted all of its magical power.<br /> Any non-zero Health Levels are removed from the Soulbond's health track, their Essence Pool is filled to 50%.<br /> All of the pendant's passives and evocations immediately cease their protection.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200b<u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u300cDecree of Iona\u300d</span></b></u> (Artifact Circlet:****)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attunement: 2m<br /> <br /> A small and elegant circlet crafted of orachalcum, glowing with a soft aura of warmth and safety. From the brooch, hangs a vial, slotted for a single gem. The circlet's wards and magic stem from the love the wearer has towards another, and strengthened if her love is returned.<br /> When attuned, the wearer is as if her blade was carrying Iona's Will. The power of the Heavens guide her sword, ensuring it will reach its mark.<br /> <br /> Soulbond: If the wearer and the target each have a major or greater intimacy of love (Agape, Phileo,Stroge, or Eros), towards the other, upon performing a ritual, the wearer may declare the target to be her Soulbond. The wearer may not be soulbonded with more than one person. If the wearer's intimacy towards her Soulbound is *defining*, her Soulbound is aware of the wearer's every intimacy.<br /> <br /> Passive effect:<br /> While attuned with \u300cDecree of Iona\u300d, the wearer is granted -1 to the opponent's defense when making a *decisive* attack.<br /> <br /> Evocations of \u300cThe Decree of Iona\u300d:<br /> <br /> \u300cSeraph's Ethereal Shield\u300d (Cost: 2m, 2i, Type: Reflexive; Duration: Instant):<br /> The wearer's protection surrounds her Soulbond in a protective halo, reducing the onslaught penalty suffered by the Soulbond by (Intimacy Towards Soulbond/2), rounded down.<br /> If the Soulbond is a Celestial Exalt, this protection is extended until the Soulbond's next turn.<br /> <br /> \u300cCelestine Rush on Seraphic Wings\u300d (cost: 3m, 1wp; Type: Supplemental; Duration: Instant):<br /> Prerequisite: \u300cSeraph's Ethereal Shield\u300d<br /> In a flurry of essence and wings, the Soulbond wills his body to reach her. His anima flares for a brief moment, the image of angelic wings behind him, as he rushes at high speed to reach his partner. If the Soulbond is flurrying a defend other action with a misc. or move action to protect the wearer, the flurry penalty he takes is reduced by 1.<br /> <br /> \u300cGrand Blade of the Seraph\u300d (Cost:\u2013; Type: Permanent; Duration:Permanent):<br /> Prerequiste:\u300cCelestine Rush on Seraphic Wings\u300d, Essence 2<br /> \u300cThe Decree of Iona\u300d increases the Heavenly power it grants to the wearer to defeat the foes that would threaten her Soulbond.<br /> The passive of \u300cThe Decree of Iona\u300d is enhanced, channeling the essence of the Soulbond through itself and entwining it with the wearer's blade as well.<br /> While together and nearby in combat and her intimacy towards her Soulbond is defining, his spirit is bound tightly with her own. Together, the Soulbond strikes with the wearer, reducing the target's hardness by his (Essence)/2, minimum 1.<br /> In addition, the wearers intimacy towards her Soulbond may never be lowered by any external influence.<br /> <br /> \u300cIn The Dusk, Two Souls Entwined\u300d (Cost: 7m; Type: Simple; Duration: Indefinite)<br /> Prerequiste: \u300cGrand Blade of the Seraph\u300d, Essence 2<br /> While the wearer keeps her commitment to this evocation and her Soulbond has motes committed to \u300cIn The Dawn, Two Souls Entwined\u300d, the cost of \u300cSeraph's Ethereal Shield\u300d &amp; \u300cCelestine Rush on Seraphic Wings\u300d is reduced by 2m.<br /> In addition, the wearer receives the defensive passive of \u300cAngelheart Vial\u300d.<br /> If either of the pair ceases their commitment to either evocation, the other's commitment to their respective evocation is revoked as well.<br /> <br /> \u300cThe Heaven's Defied\u300d (Cost: 7m; Type: Reflexive; Duration: Instant)<br /> If the wearer has a defining intimacy of love towards her Soulbond, and she would have last Health Level filled, the wearer may expend the energy of the Hearthstone held within the pendant to perform a single miracle to save her life.<br /> The circlet channels the energy within the Hearthstone, consuming all of it in a single moment, and turns the essence into a lifeline, reviving the wearer in a cloud of white, angelic motes of essence.<br /> In its last moments, the pendant returns to the wearer all of the motes she has committed to the evocations granted by the pendant, but it's forever shattered, having exhausted all of its magical power.<br /> Any non-zero health levels are healed from the wearer's health track and their essence pool is restored to 50%.<br /> \u300cThe Decree of Iona\u300d's passives and \u300cGrand Blade of the Seraph\u300d's protection immediately cease their protection.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Both artifacts define a new term, a &quot;Soulbond&quot;. A Soubond is someone the wearer loves dearly, whether it be romantically, or a strong tie between warriors tested in battle, or the loving towards her family, that the wearer cherishes. The Vial and the Decree are powered by that love, and in turn, make her intimacy a profound strength. The key is that the intimacy must be shared. Just as much the wearer loves her Soulbond, the Soulbond must care equally for her and likewise have an intimacy of love towards the wearer. The Angel and the Decree bind their souls together. Across time and space, they will always be connected through the magic within the artifacts.<br /> Together, the two artifacts are built to encourage their players and their characters to roleplay couple, and rewards them for doing so, though they can still be used in a non-romantic fashion.<br /> <br /> Angelheart Vial is themed becoming a shield for the person they loves. The pendant's passive is minor, but significant and encourages the wearer to take more defensive actions in combat. The evocations ask the wearer to commit her essence to the Vial, receiving nothing in return, but granting her Soulbond multiple defensive buffs to his Soak and damage prevention to his health track, rather taking a portion of that damage herself. The evocations are designed to encourage the Soulbond to fight at their greatest potential in combat and rewards them with protections for getting dirty in combat. Finally, the penultimate evocation rewards the wearer for her for dedication, increasing its defensive bonus further still, and as long she is near her Soulbond and their intimacy is at its highest possible, it grants a very powerful defense and protects the intimacy she treasures so much from external influence.<br /> <br /> Decree of Iona is themed around becoming oneself a blade to protect the person they loves. The circlet gives a passive that helps the wearer in combat, and Iona's Will empowers her, reducing the opposition's defenses. It's evocations are nearly all actives, unlike the Vial's, which are auras. The first reduces the Soulbond's Onslaught penalty, scaling with their intimacy, while the second supplements the Soulbond's flurried Defend Other actions. Each encourage the Soulbond to play the role of a protector, jumping to the defense of the wearer, and reward him for doing so. Finally, the penultimate evocation rewards the wearer for her for dedication, increasing her ability fight in combat while she is near her Soulbond by helping her pierce through hardness.<br /> <br /> The two artifacts have capstones that are intended to be paired and mirrored. Both capstones actually do <b>nothing</b>, providing no new benefit for either the wearer or her Soulbond. However, when the Soulbond is attuned to the respective sister artifact, the true power of the evocations are unlocked. Angelheart Vial's capstone drastically reduces the cost of maintaining its evocations while granting the wearer the offensive passive of Decree of Iona. Similarly, Decree of Iona's capstone reduces the essence cost of it's two actives, and provides the wearer the defensive passive of Angelheart Vial. By <b>sharing</b> their burden together as equals, they empower the their partner, easing the weight on their shoulders and supporting them as they play their role for the other.<br /> <br /> Each artifact also has one additional evocation that isn't dependent on the rest: a one time use super ability that revives an exalt from near death. The evocation on the Vial lets the wearer restore her Soulbond from near death, while the evocation on the Decree is the mirror, restoring the wearer and giving them one more shot to keep fighting and end the battle. Each is meant to be the ultimate<br /> <br /> All the evocations, combining together with the capstones, are very much intended to resemble wedding vows, with their flavor text and quotations further reinforcing the idea. Unfortunately, those aren't on my pastebin at the moment so I couldn't copy them over here.<br /> <br /> I'd love feedback on the evocations and how well their evocations express what their respective artifact is intended to encourage. Any help or advice on appropriately costing each artifact would be very much appreciated as well!.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Fixed some broken wording","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11858,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11858-seibahismaiwaifu","user":"SeibahIsMaiWaifu","date":". 05-26-2016, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11858-seibahismaiwaifu","name":"SeibahIsMaiWaifu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T15:59:23-07:00","id":901490,"title":"","content":"Ok need some help, assisting a player, he is trying to get his hands on a artifact, in my game, but he is having issues with coming up with ideas for thrown artifact evocations and im having trouble helping him. so i asked the exalted community, help me please <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S the idea for the artifact at first was a wind based chakram but im willing for any ideas to help stir some inspiration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1215-black-orchid","name":"black orchid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1215_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T16:02:49-07:00","id":901491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>black orchid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=901490#post901490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the idea for the artifact at first was a wind based chakram but im willing for any ideas to help stir some inspiration</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out this shameless plug! <a href=\"https://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/2016/05/20/artifacts-and-evocations/\" target=\"_blank\">https://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.c...nd-evocations/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T21:24:27-07:00","id":901715,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I'm still working on both the fluff and the mechanics of a Tattoo like Mara's Shadow Tattoo for Sorcerers except for a variation of the Pact with the Ifrit Lord initiation. Can I get feedback on this? I basically combined the Burning Name Merit with Wood Dragon's Claws, and I'm not really liking it so far. Any ideas on what to do or how to do it are very appreciated. Any ideas for evocations would be rad too.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brand of the Elemental Flame</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A rare gift offered by the powerful Elemental Dragons of Flame, this Brand is a sign of the favor of an Elemental Dragon, for only they know the secret to render the purest Essence of Flame, culled from the bodies of powerful fire elementals and rendered into the clay-like paste needed to make the tattoos.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Brand is not given out lightly, as no mortal has the power to unlock its potential, and many Exalted lack the drive and the passion to do so. Those who have proven worthy of the Elemental Dragon\u2019s favor have been passionate warriors and orators, brilliant artists and blazing pathfinders. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those who bear the mark of Elemental Flame go forward with flames that leap to their aid and stoke the fire in their belly. Elementals recognize the mark</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evocations of the Brand of Elemental Flame</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attuning to the Brand of Elemental Flame requires 5 motes and grants the first Evocation for the Brand for free.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Elemental Flame Suffusement</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: -- Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Brand of Elemental Flame allows the tattoo-bearer to call upon the mighty Elemental Flame to aid them in battle. This evocation grants access to Elemental Flame, allowing the sorcerer to call forth epic blasts of flames, sending them streaming from her eyes, fingertips, or mouth, to her enemies. While this ability has some mundane uses such as to light a campfire or incinerate ropes that bind her hands, it can also be used as an attack, rolling (Intelligence + Occult) to direct the flames, which are treated as a medium artifact archery weapon with the natural, lethal, flame, thrown (short), and mounted tags.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Additionally, Elemental Flame Suffusement offers access to the following powers while attuned to the Brand:</span></span><ul><li>Sudden Immolation Touch (6m; Simple; Instant; Decisive-only): The sorcerer can perform an immolation gambit with a difficulty of 3, her target becomes immolated by the Elemental Flame with no brand to ground it. They suffer 1L a round until they can take a miscellaneous action to put out the fire, usually a Dexterity + Athletics check with a difficulty of 3.</li> </ul><ul><li>Flame-Shaping Gesture (3m; Reflexive; Instant): Warping and twisting her fire, the sorcerer may solidify and shape their Elemental Flame into a weapon, allowing it to take on the profile of a medium melee artifact weapon if so desired, along with granting them the tag of her choice for the rest of the scene. She might form the flames into a lash of scourging fire to grant them the flexible tag, reshape the flames into a large hammer to grant them the smashing tag, or similar. Only one tag can be granted by this power at a time. This requires that the Sorcerer use Dexterity + Melee to attack their opponents as well, but flame-forged weapons can only be used at close range.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T12:06:05-07:00","id":902931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=901715#post901715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so I'm still working on both the fluff and the mechanics of a Tattoo like Mara's Shadow Tattoo for Sorcerers except for a variation of the Pact with the Ifrit Lord initiation. Can I get feedback on this? I basically combined the Burning Name Merit with Wood Dragon's Claws, and I'm not really liking it so far. Any ideas on what to do or how to do it are very appreciated. Any ideas for evocations would be rad too.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brand of the Elemental Flame</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A rare gift offered by the powerful Elemental Dragons of Flame, this Brand is a sign of the favor of an Elemental Dragon, for only they know the secret to render the purest Essence of Flame, culled from the bodies of powerful fire elementals and rendered into the clay-like paste needed to make the tattoos.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Brand is not given out lightly, as no mortal has the power to unlock its potential, and many Exalted lack the drive and the passion to do so. Those who have proven worthy of the Elemental Dragon\u2019s favor have been passionate warriors and orators, brilliant artists and blazing pathfinders. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those who bear the mark of Elemental Flame go forward with flames that leap to their aid and stoke the fire in their belly. Elementals recognize the mark</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evocations of the Brand of Elemental Flame</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attuning to the Brand of Elemental Flame requires 5 motes and grants the first Evocation for the Brand for free.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Elemental Flame Suffusement</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: -- Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Brand of Elemental Flame allows the tattoo-bearer to call upon the mighty Elemental Flame to aid them in battle. This evocation grants access to Elemental Flame, allowing the sorcerer to call forth epic blasts of flames, sending them streaming from her eyes, fingertips, or mouth, to her enemies. While this ability has some mundane uses such as to light a campfire or incinerate ropes that bind her hands, it can also be used as an attack, rolling (Intelligence + Occult) to direct the flames, which are treated as a medium artifact archery weapon with the natural, lethal, flame, thrown (short), and mounted tags.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Additionally, Elemental Flame Suffusement offers access to the following powers while attuned to the Brand:</span></span><ul><li>Sudden Immolation Touch (6m; Simple; Instant; Decisive-only): The sorcerer can perform an immolation gambit with a difficulty of 3, her target becomes immolated by the Elemental Flame with no brand to ground it. They suffer 1L a round until they can take a miscellaneous action to put out the fire, usually a Dexterity + Athletics check with a difficulty of 3.</li> </ul><ul><li>Flame-Shaping Gesture (3m; Reflexive; Instant): Warping and twisting her fire, the sorcerer may solidify and shape their Elemental Flame into a weapon, allowing it to take on the profile of a medium melee artifact weapon if so desired, along with granting them the tag of her choice for the rest of the scene. She might form the flames into a lash of scourging fire to grant them the flexible tag, reshape the flames into a large hammer to grant them the smashing tag, or similar. Only one tag can be granted by this power at a time. This requires that the Sorcerer use Dexterity + Melee to attack their opponents as well, but flame-forged weapons can only be used at close range.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>This artifact is rather hard to react to since your intention for it is unclear. The flavor text paints it as something aimed at sorcerers and that is meant to compliment greatly passionate characters. however, the powers granted by this artifact upon attunment seem too numerous, and focused solely on fire mastery and weapon creation. What aspect of the artifact would you like it to be about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","user":"7 questions vanquish god","date":". 05-29-2016, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","name":"7 questions vanquish god","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11843_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T19:26:10-07:00","id":903207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>7 questions vanquish god</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=902931#post902931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This artifact is rather hard to react to since your intention for it is unclear. The flavor text paints it as something aimed at sorcerers and that is meant to compliment greatly passionate characters. however, the powers granted by this artifact upon attunment seem too numerous, and focused solely on fire mastery and weapon creation. What aspect of the artifact would you like it to be about?</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's based on Mara's Shadow Tattoo, from the Beloved by Mara initiation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3, page 467</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demonic Tattoos: Mara has marked the sorcerer, taking<br /> one or more of her own souls and rendering it down into<br /> a midnight-black tattoo that spirals around her chakras.<br /> The sorcerer may unlock Evocations from these tattoos<br /> that allow her to manipulate or gain power from shadows<br /> or darkness, alter her control spell to incorporate<br /> elements of darkness and subversion, or manipulate or<br /> empower summoned demons, such as by turning them<br /> into living shadows.</div> </div> </div> </div>But adapted to the Pact with the Ifrit Lord shaping ritual. It is a sorcererous tattoo that can unlock evocations, so it's definitely for sorcerers. The things I thought it might directly aid with are control of fire and enflaming passion, but it was sort of a half-baked effort since I'm not really certain how to make evocations at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T19:51:29-07:00","id":903226,"title":"","content":"I've had a couple people ask me to write up the other four Cadet Blades of the Academy of Harmonious Jade Dragons. Together they push 5,000 words, however, <a href=\"http://fourmoonspress.com/Exalted/CadetBlades.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">so I've made a pdf of all five cadet blades available on my web space here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T21:22:34-07:00","id":903259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SeibahIsMaiWaifu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=900473#post900473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello~<br /> We're starting up a campaign in a week or so and I had a few extra dots left to create artifacts with.<br /> <br /> <b>WORDS</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the artifacts and think they're fairly well balanced, even to the point where I'd say they're fine being artifact 3 each. Just that I really think the attunement costs are too low, and the passive benefits are also amazingly good. +1 defense and a permanent -1 to the opponent's defense basically? I think some better passives could be made, even if its just &quot;Learn first charm of the evocation tree&quot;<br /> <br /> In a bit of self promotion, I'm wondering if anyone can review the artifacts I made over in my other thread. The BFG I'm worried about being overpowered, but it seems fine. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902537-rip-and-tear-until-it-s-done-doom-artifact-weapons-essence-pulse-cannon\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-pulse-cannon</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T05:37:20-07:00","id":903414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=903259#post903259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like the artifacts and think they're fairly well balanced, even to the point where I'd say they're fine being artifact 3 each. Just that I really think the attunement costs are too low, and the passive benefits are also amazingly good. +1 defense and a permanent -1 to the opponent's defense basically? I think some better passives could be made, even if its just &quot;Learn first charm of the evocation tree&quot;<br /> <br /> In a bit of self promotion, I'm wondering if anyone can review the artifacts I made over in my other thread. The BFG I'm worried about being overpowered, but it seems fine. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902537-rip-and-tear-until-it-s-done-doom-artifact-weapons-essence-pulse-cannon\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-pulse-cannon</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Iv'e read both artifacts and found some criticism to levy about the strength of their heat mechanic. However, further consideration makes me question the need for criticism of any kind, The intent of the weapon is clear - destroy foe and background with gay abandon reserved otherwise only for high-level brawl users. So although the base heat mechanic is too powerful for my taste, it doesn't seem the type of unbalance that makes the artifact unfun or frustrating to anyone willing to accept the weapons overt premise.<br /> In conclusion, while i would hesitate to approve of this artifact at my table for &quot;General Use&quot;, you've done a good job creating a proper exalted BFG, fit for a frothing fit of unstoppable carnage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","user":"7 questions vanquish god","date":". 05-30-2016, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","name":"7 questions vanquish god","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11843_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:32:08-07:00","id":903745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=823902#post823902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Caudex\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Crowning Coercion (Black Jade / Starmetal Goremaul ***)</span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, reading this one, I think my <b>Omens of the Pyre</b> might be significantly underpowered for a 5-dot... xD<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T22:39:56-07:00","id":903967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>7 questions vanquish god</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=903414#post903414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Iv'e read both artifacts and found some criticism to levy about the strength of their heat mechanic. However, further consideration makes me question the need for criticism of any kind, The intent of the weapon is clear - destroy foe and background with gay abandon reserved otherwise only for high-level brawl users. So although the base heat mechanic is too powerful for my taste, it doesn't seem the type of unbalance that makes the artifact unfun or frustrating to anyone willing to accept the weapons overt premise.<br /> In conclusion, while i would hesitate to approve of this artifact at my table for &quot;General Use&quot;, you've done a good job creating a proper exalted BFG, fit for a frothing fit of unstoppable carnage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well obviously the weapons may not be acceptable in every game premise. They're mainly for modern/Sci-fi/Autochtonian usage over vanilla. They can exist in Vanilla persay, but they're a better fit for other games I'm willing to admit. <br /> <br /> Heat is certainly strong I admit, as it gives a lot of passive bonuses for the Plasma gun, there were a few reasons for it. <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A weapon that actually helps majorly one of Archery's biggest weaknesses, withering attacks. Heat buffs it quite a bit, but it also takes quite a bit to actually warm it up. Unless its a super major battle, most fights will be over by turn 8 barring use of the capstone (Which resets heat down to zero after a few turns). While I am willing to admit that Heat bonuses may be too strong, there shouldn't be anything with an artifact that takes time to warm up right? I may tone down the amount of heat levels though, as originally I had them at 1/3/5/7, and not one for every level along 1-8</li> <li>Spray-And-Pray and Point-Blank give some powerful bonuses, but in doing so you won't gain any heat in the ground (It costs One heat to fire in these forms), so you're still highly rewarded for kiting an opponent moreso than anything.</li> <li>The BFG doesn't use heat, it'd be broken as hell after use, unless you confused the Plasma Gun for the BFG</li> <li>Volcano Cutter is probably still stronger than the BFG overall IMO</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T23:31:40-07:00","id":903980,"title":"","content":"Do multiple attacks generate multiple points of heat? Archery is full of those","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","name":"7 questions vanquish god","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11843_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T01:21:39-07:00","id":904032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>7 questions vanquish god</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=903980#post903980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do multiple attacks generate multiple points of heat? Archery is full of those</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch. No that isn't my intention. One per round. I'll fix that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T09:53:35-07:00","id":904230,"title":"","content":"I know I've been pretty quiet on here of late. Just been needing a break. But I did come up with a toy this morning on a whim. I was thinking about how unless you already have a particular artifact in mind, it can be hard to come up with one on the fly. Maybe it's just me.<br /> <br /> Anyways, here is my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dxy9auJi1SOKk0coNGCRC1X6tkmzvtyMswVnYNjs0Eo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Random Artifact Creator</a>. Don't go getting too excited now, it's not as robust as you're thinking. All it does is pick a weapon/armor, a magical material or two, and a few properties from those materials, and puts them together. Really it's just an idea machine for those who want to create but don't have a starting point, so it's probably a niche audience. But there it is. I would like to add a naming mechanic to it someday, but that'll take a lot more work.<br /> <br /> I've also included it on my website (linked in my signature) for future reference.<br /> <br /> Really excited to see more people participating in this thread, both building, and critiquing. Go Community Go!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T11:00:20-07:00","id":904286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904230#post904230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I've been pretty quiet on here of late. Just been needing a break. But I did come up with a toy this morning on a whim. I was thinking about how unless you already have a particular artifact in mind, it can be hard to come up with one on the fly. Maybe it's just me.<br /> <br /> Anyways, here is my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dxy9auJi1SOKk0coNGCRC1X6tkmzvtyMswVnYNjs0Eo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Random Artifact Creator</a>. Don't go getting too excited now, it's not as robust as you're thinking. All it does is pick a weapon/armor, a magical material or two, and a few properties from those materials, and puts them together. Really it's just an idea machine for those who want to create but don't have a starting point, so it's probably a niche audience. But there it is. I would like to add a naming mechanic to it someday, but that'll take a lot more work.<br /> <br /> I've also included it on my website (linked in my signature) for future reference.<br /> <br /> Really excited to see more people participating in this thread, both building, and critiquing. Go Community Go!</div> </div> </div> </div>This looks cool. I'll be sure to use it!<br /> People here have been doing a great job, but it was your work who got me interested in this thread in the first place. We would all love to see more from you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","name":"7 questions vanquish god","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11843_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:41:22-07:00","id":904406,"title":"","content":"<b>Shrieking Wraith's Requiem (Soulsteel Powerbow, Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> Forged by the Mask of Winters as a prize for a loyal deathknight, he abandoned his plans for the bow when a Solar offered him her own powerbow in trade. Genuinely impressed by the honesty and generosity inherent in the naive gesture, the Mask of Winters offered her Shrieking Wraith's Requiem as a gift in exchange, forming a tiny but existent spark of cooperative goodwill within the heart of the Deathlord. Now, the Night Caste named Hua Li wields Requiem, unaware of the power that slumbers within.<br /> <br /> Shrieking Wraith's Requiem is a recurve powerbow of soulsteel, with a grip wrapped in hide peeled from Juggernaut himself and a string of tightly-coiled human hair, treated with a wraith's Essence for strength. The risers are sculpted into gleaming soulsteel skulls, while the limbs are carved into elaborate bone motifs. When fired, the bow sometimes seems to scream softly, the skulls' mouths opening and closing with the motion of the bow.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Shrieking Wraith's Requiem</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Abyssal Exalt who attunes to Shrieking Wraith's Requiem for five motes gains one dot in the Whispers Merit for free. Additionally, while attuned, the user can increase their Whispers rating by spending experience points. All Whispers gained in this manner, including the initial free dot, are lost if attunement lapses, but return if the user re-attunes to the bow.<br /> <br /> <b>Shriek of the Void</b><br /> Cost: 1m/die or success; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> When infused with Essence, Requiem literally screams as she releases a nocked arrow, sending the missile on its way trailed by spiraling streamers of necrotic Essence. On a <b>withering</b> attack against a living target, the Exalt spends up to her (Whispers) rating in motes before making the attack. If the attack hits, each mote spent adds a single die to the post-soak damage of the attack. This strike has the potential to increase minimum damage (see <b>Ex3</b>, p. 184).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Requiem for the Damned</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Shriek of the Void<br /> <br /> By charging Requiem with her own Essence, the wielder may temporarily awaken the spirits of those dead trapped within the bow, calling them forth into a phantasmal dirge. The skulls on the bow literally move and sing, a blasphemous glossolalia of dozens, if not hundreds, of spectral voices. This Evocation is a Performance-based Inspire action, using the wielder's (Charisma + Performance) and adding her (Whispers) as automatic successes against the Resolve of her audience. If successful, the group is struck with either extreme sadness and lassitude or fear, at the Storyteller's discretion, depending on the context of the scene. This Evocation functions equally well on the living or the mindful dead, though the dead almost always experience depression rather than terror. It generally has no effect on mindless undead. If used in conjunction with the Dawn Caste anima power, however, even mindless undead can know fear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clutching Wraith's Embrace</b><br /> Cost: 5m (+1W); Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Requiem for the Damned<br /> <br /> Those slain by Shrieking Wraith's Requiem may know no peace; only an eternity of sorrowful wandering in the inhospitable wastes of the Underworld. This Evocation supplements a <b>decisive</b> attack. If the target is slain by this attack, at the end of the scene his <i>hun</i> soul will rise as an unquiet ghost, while his <i>po</i> will stir fitfully in his corpse. At the Storyteller's discretion, the corpse is more likely to become a hungry ghost, while the <i>hun</i> spirit WILL become a ghost. If magic such as the Zenith's anima power is used on the corpse before the end of the scene, this Evocation's effect is negated. If used against a battle group, this Evocation costs an extra Willpower to activate, but it can animate the entire battle group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":".  Adding in suggestions... 06-01-2016, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T22:32:11-07:00","id":904726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=903259#post903259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like the artifacts and think they're fairly well balanced, even to the point where I'd say they're fine being artifact 3 each. Just that I really think the attunement costs are too low, and the passive benefits are also amazingly good. +1 defense and a permanent -1 to the opponent's defense basically? I think some better passives could be made, even if its just &quot;Learn first charm of the evocation tree&quot;<br /> <br /> In a bit of self promotion, I'm wondering if anyone can review the artifacts I made over in my other thread. The BFG I'm worried about being overpowered, but it seems fine. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/902537-rip-and-tear-until-it-s-done-doom-artifact-weapons-essence-pulse-cannon\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-pulse-cannon</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I'll discuss with my ST about lowering them to 3 dot artifacts. I felt that the two ultimate evocations of a resurrection were miraculous enough to warrant the four dots because there weren't any charms in the Core that were similar in such a fashion.<br /> <br /> As a side note, the intent was that the two artifacts couldn't be worn together. The &quot;wife&quot; and the &quot;husband&quot; each wear one of the two sister pendants. I'll make that explicit in our shared homebrew folders.<br /> <br /> I'm going to give a very quick review of your two artifacts from DOOM.<br /> They're overpowered and break the rules of the system. <br /> A very important part of game balance, especially with 3E, is that each charm tree plays very strong to it's niche.<br /> This is very much intentional.<br /> By making each charm tree very strong at it's intended niche, no charm tree is useless or theoretically better than the others.<br /> This is the very reason why card games like Magic: The Gathering have survived for over twenty years, with the Legacy metagame supporting over twenty to thirty different archetypes and decks.<br /> For a more modern example, DOTA 2 is also like this where in a very large number of heroes are picked every TI because they are all so niche that they can co-exist.<br /> <br /> <b>Niches and specialization breed diversity in gameplay and builds</b>.<br /> <br /> Let's examine this in the context of Exalted 3E combat abilities:<br /> <br /> <b>VERY LONG WALL OF TEXT AHEAD ON GAME AND MECHANIC DESIGN</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Archery: <br /> The majority of the cascades focus on combat at short and greater range, enhancing combat at medium range, with a very strong focus on sniping and finishing a target but with NO stealth options outside of &quot;snipe them from extreme ranges&quot;.<br /> <br /> Athletics: <br /> The <b>only</b> tree that gives you a variety of movement options around the battlefield and supplements your join battle and disengages in ways that few other trees can match.<br /> <br /> Brawl:<br /> The <b>only</b> tree with a focus in not only grapples but also heavy dps. Brawl is <b>the</b> go to tree for raw, pure, damage. That is it's niche and it fulfills the fantasies very well.<br /> <br /> Dodge:<br /> The <b>perfect defense</b> tree, and focusing only on that with a smattering of utility. Everything in the tree is built around dodging, evading, and completely negating onslaught.<br /> This is also the <b>only</b> tree with a true perfect defense in 3E with Seven Shadows Evasion.<br /> Yes. This is VERY much intentional by design.<br /> <br /> Thrown:<br /> Ranged attacks with light weapons, but unlike Archery, focuses on delivering them through <b>stealth</b>, offering ways to deal heavy damage in bursts. In addition, this is the <b>only</b> tree that has <b>debuff</b> charms as part of its core. Furthermore, this is the <b>only</b> combat tree with charms that do <b>true AOE</b> damage. Other trees have multi-attack charms but no other ability lets you hit multiple targets in a rain of kunai like Throw does.<br /> In addition, Throw is <b>the</b> &quot;alpha strike&quot; ability with a whole cascade of charms that work together to instantly defeat foes from the very first attack. There is NO other ability in the game that provides support for such play style.<br /> Again, all of this is VERY much intentional by design, providing <b>clear</b> distinctions between the two core ranged combat abilities as so both types of characters are viable.<br /> <br /> Melee:<br /> Melee is special in that it's the <b>single</b> jack of all stats combat ability. No other combat ability has the sheer versatility of Melee. It has offensive charm cascades in Excellent Strike. It has defensive charm cascades in Dipping-Swallow Defense. It has utility charm cascades in things like Call The Blade. It has heavy damage and DPS abilities. It has strong burst abilities. It has evocation boosters and dice tricks.<br /> Melee, by intentional design, does it all, <b>but</b>, it doesn't do it nearly as well as any other of the combat abilities.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts:<br /> MA is unique in that it sits in between Charms and Sorcery in terms of sheer power. Go through the charms. Mote per mote and by cost, MA charms and Forms offer <b>far</b> more raw power than any combat ability. <br /> Shining Point is the strongest DPS tree by the very nature of giving you a <b>second</b> attack action from it's sword. <br /> Crane offers defenses and counter attacks that make Melee users weep in jealousy. <br /> Dreaming Pearl gives evasion that no other combat tree par Dodge can match. <br /> Righteous Devil trades the range of Archery or Throw for sheer, raw, power at short and close range, in addition to, with very clever mechanics if I may add, shifting the ideal combat range from Far-&gt;Short to Medium-&gt;Close.<br /> Steel Devil is the only tree that focuses on duel-wielding swords and multiple attacks, offering ways to inflict massive onslaught penalties.<br /> White Reaper is the inverse in that it's the only tree that offers so many charms that completely turn onslaught on its head to rival, if not surpass, Brawl.<br /> <br /> MA again follows the same idea that <b>every</b> martial art is specialized and niche to the outright extreme, trading away the utility and sprawling charm cascades of the core abilities for very specialized MA charms and forms that are very strong at what they do, but absolutely pitiful outside that niche.<br /> It then offers the unique advantage of being able to <b>flow</b> between the forms to match the situation, offering versatility and utility with heavy investment, but still unable to match the level of utility of Melee or a combination of the core combat abilities.<br /> <br /> In this way, every MA is viable in some way. There is no &quot;One True Build&quot; because each ability has so many glaring weaknesses that they can't possibly be relied on to deal with everything. <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's on this that the balance system of Exalted's combat thrives and why it's so damn good in 3E, which is why <b>breaking</b> it is the worst possible thing to do, especially with evocations, which lack the same sort of investment MA or charm cascades do.<br /> <br /> <b>SIDE NOTE</b> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It's this specialization and niches to preserve balance and variety in builds that makes me dislike @Daerian's &quot;Danmaku&quot; and &quot;Thrown&quot; charms and consider them to be bad game design in the context of Exalted 3E. I am massive Touhou and shmup fan (I've 1cc'd every mainline Touhou game on Normal+ etc. blah blah). While the fluff is cool, it's attempting to turn Throw into something it's not, pushing it into the niches that are occupied by Sorcery and Archery (consistent AOE and range respectively). In addition, the LAST thing the tree needs is strong defensive charms because Christ almighty is a balance breaker. Danmaku, however wonky, can be fluffed away under the existing charms for Throw, anyways. In all honesty, I would never allow that homebrew at my table and would reject it outright. It's excellent work and reasoning but it's just going at it the wrong way. If you wanted to make a true danmaku spell, with a huge AOE damaging attack that could rival something like Barrier:\u300cBoundary of Life and Death\u300d(personal favorite spell card), a sorcerous spell at Celestial level is the way to go. The game explicitly already has Love Sign:<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u300c</span></span></span>Master Spark<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u300d</span></span></span>in it anyways (Death Ray).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Your designs, especially for the Plasma Gun, <b>cover up too many weaknesses of Archery</b>. <br /> You said it yourself:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A weapon that actually helps majorly one of Archery's biggest weaknesses </div> </div> </div>This is bad game design and the quickest way to create a game breaker outside of a &quot;I WIN&quot; button or obscene stats.<br /> <br /> Archers aren't supposed to be able to kite extremely well in Exalted. It is why you have to take an Aim action to reliably hit at Medium and Long range and why Extreme range is almost impossible without specific charms and heavy investment. It's why Aim actions incur so many penalties, to prevent you from aiming, firing, and backing away and repeating forever, and same for flurries.<br /> It's why Righteous Devil Form exists as the <b>single</b> exception to this, turning Archery on its head and letting you Aim and Reload in one motion, because it wants you to use Firewands in close and short range, but then limits you to firewands that can't shoot past Short range (Medium with charms).<br /> The turn requirement is irrelevant because the bonuses, even at low heat, are so good that the capstones don't matter.<br /> <br /> Also, the light artifact version is one handed which means a user can maintain any heat level he wants indefinitely by using two and alternating fire, which again, completely breaks the game's balance.<br /> <br /> In addition to the extremely strong Heat passive which can easily be gamed, the rest of the evocations are also extremely powerful. <br /> Remember, evocations aren't supposed to be strong as charms. They're supposed to do cool and unique things, but they will never be able to match the efficiency and power of a charm.<br /> <br /> As for the BFG. It's cool. Like the Plasma Rifle, it hits the flavor of the gun spot on with the mechanics. <br /> Except it's a &quot;I WIN&quot; button.<br /> Volcano Cutter requires set up and investment for it's massive, over the top, army killing and fight ending evocations.<br /> Your BFG does not.<br /> Volcano Cutter creates a cool minigame in managing your Eruptions.<br /> Your BFG is &quot;Point at target; It goes boom.&quot;<br /> Volcano Cutter is a five dot artifact because of its raw power and complexity of mechanics.<br /> Your BFG is lacks the complexity to warrant a budget of 5 dots and offers too much power for far too much ease of access. <br /> <br /> This guy absolutely requires a &quot;once per story&quot; if not &quot;once per chronicle&quot; attached to it's evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11858-seibahismaiwaifu","name":"SeibahIsMaiWaifu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T00:23:02-07:00","id":904766,"title":"","content":"<br /> I'll reply to your issues in bullet points.<ul><li>There is such thing as niche's and diversity, then there are problems within the design tree of the charms themselves. Thrown and Archery are very well known for this. They're known for Alpha striking, and do so extremely hard and at relative safety of range, but once you've blown your wad, its difficult to bounce back. Thrown is also heavily criticized as having the same people in 2e, which has a high stealth focus but some people want to do something other than stealth with it. Range is a very powerful too yes, as there is no better defense than just making it impossible for the opponent to attack you back. I support the Danmaku Thrown charms for adding some holes in the charm tree. I disagreed with the charm that lets you use Thrown as a parry defense, but it barely tetters on the edge case for being allowable. Do I think Archery should have easier access to sniping people at extreme ranges? Yes, but I do not think Thrown should never be allowed to reach that point. &quot;Yes but&quot; is an important part of game design too, and it can be done while still making each and every thing unique.</li> <li>I am very familiar with the charm trees you listed. Also Athletics isn't the only tree which allows for bounding around the battlefield, Dodge does it very well too. Also no Thrown is not the only tree with a debuff, Ox-Stunning Blow exists in Brawl. Melee is also an odd tree, in which its good going in until you reach some sort of point where you're insanely strong, kinda like a Bethesda game, to the point where Brawl barely inches out on it. Over and Under Method may be the only clash its got, but its so good it makes Brawl question its own clash charms. Also Shining Point also has a onslaught reversal charm, in fact the only one in the game that puts onslaught on the opponent, so White Reaper isn't the only one that does this.</li> <li>I meant to cover up Archery's weaknesses <b>somewhat</b> with the Inferno cannon, but did you read the charms and figure out how it can be used in play? Yes, heat builds withering damage, but it does so over time. Lots of time. You can use it at medium range and at close range with some good benefits, but there are cons to this. You won't gain heat during the turn (unless you're under the capstone buff), Archery is STILL better at point blank/Long range shots (Accuracy Without Distance gives aim bonuses instantly, There is No Wind allows you to treat close range as short range and don't cost initiative to actually use. That's why I made them use initiative and heat, they're emergency buttons and not &quot;Let's attack at whatever range we want!&quot;), heat gives some amazing buffs especially with the expansion to go with 8 heat but that's eight turns of basically optimal battle conditions (We have a charm that give some very nice bonuses in exchange for heat, but once your heat is blown you need to build up again. Even the capstone can only give you three or so power with this per turn and you need a ton of WP to make this effective), and lastly reloading also gets rid of all your heat. This doesn't come into play for most battles, but for major battles or long treks this is a very real problem.</li> <li>The low end heat bonuses could use some reorganization, but are fine. A +2 to reloading checks is very welcome if you want to maintain high heat, +1 minimum damage is nice but if you're dealing ping damage then you're already halfway up shit-creek, a +1 to post soak withering is nice but hardly game breaking. Ignoring some mundane soak seems powerful, in which it can let you put some extra sting on anyone wearing mundane armour (Battlegroups, non-resistance Exalts, people without artifact armour), but the piercing tag for archery is IMO better as it only cost 1i to attempt and makes it so that you ignore 4 soak from any armour piece. Even when you get to ESS 5 when it is higher, you'd still need four turns to optimally set it up. This weapon doesn't like aiming in one action, and certainly doesn't like reloading in one action either. I will cede to admit that higher heats and/or the order of the heat effects could be rejiggered, but unless you present a stronger case I'm not going to see how anything is wrong. Again I'm not giving Archery an allotment of withering attack charms for cheap, easy access. I'm giving a few good options but need to be done in a specific playstyle in order to activate properly. I tend to think of it more like Shining Point, in where it has a ton of decisive attack charms, but Liquid Steel Flow is a very welcome withering damage adder, and you need to be very careful when you intend to decisive attack as it'll end Liquid Steel.</li> <li>It should be a medium artifact weapon and... I accidentally put the one-handed tag there mistaking it for two handed. That I will correct that. Secondly due to artifact rules, its a unique weapon and not a paired one, there is not technically a second version of the Inferno Cannon. Other Essence Pulse Cannons? Probably hundreds, but no other Inferno Cannons.</li> <li>Evocations when made are designed for an Exalt type. The book even says that if a DB attunes to a weapon, his charms will be different and possibly weaker than the Solar versions. Hell I even think you can replicate Solar charms so long as you can use that charm in very innovative ways, such as how the Dawn Fangs did it. I don't like doing this as its a lot of work in thematic/power/balance perspectives, but it can be done. Secondly as mentioned, they shouldn't be stronger than native charms. I'm making them to be on par with, but not completely overpowering them. They shouldn't be useful all the time, but should present an option to the person in how they want to proceed with how to engage their opponent and the choices they make.</li> <li>BFG's gimmick is that it does a really good job at blowing up your opponents... and the really flashy options make you only do it once. Hell, I'll even say Volcano Cutter is overall stronger than this. Grand Eruption makes a permanent danger point on the field upon use. Hell, its capstone has only a two turn step-up in where you can use Grand Eruption then smack people with the capstone instantly for a hugely damaging attack. Not only that, it can also cover a far wider area in doing so with just an extra turn of set up. The BFG-9000 can do a monstrously powerful attack, but you'll need to build up a lot more initiative to make it come even close to the Volcano Cutter, and the capstone even fries the weapon in which you'll need to get it repaired! So yes, it also requires a bit of setup to reach the insane capstone power that it could reach with Volcano Cutter.</li> <li>Complexity does not make a five dot, in fact I think saying complexity/power/whatever of a five dot artifact shouldn't be said with confidence until we see more five dot artifacts.</li> <li>The Capstone charm for the BFG-9000 does have a once per story limit on the capstone and a once per scene on the second highest charm on it.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T00:49:53-07:00","id":904775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904406#post904406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shriek of the Void</b></div> </div> </div> </div>First thought... is this a charm from another ability? - Yes it is, Fire and Stones Strike - But Better.<br /> <br /> Second Thought... Oof; I reckon Solar Archery lacks straight-up decisive damage adders for a reason and looking at this tells me why. I know it's small numbers but they really add up and make all the difference - given the proliferation of multi-attacks Archery swings around. If they do increase decisive damage it requires set-up first or an Essence 5 charm. I don't actually know if Evocations should be balanced assuming use with Native Charms (because they would be used in combos) but this gives me pause. As an example; A Solar archer with 9i can splatter 3 dudes in <i>artifact heavy plate</i> (assuming they have no other hardness charms or effects active) for the cost of 8m, 1wp with this charm and Feathered Death; that's three attacks at 11i, only requires essence 2.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't personally allow it but I have no better suggestion at this point. The additional withering support for Archery is welcome without being overpowering though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904406#post904406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Requiem for the Damned</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I Like! Super cheap but not individually powerful enough to warrant more cost than it has. Question; how would this interact with the Dawn Anima Banner?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904406#post904406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Clutching Wraith's Embrace</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I like!... not sure why I'm paying 5m, 1wp for the effect though, feels like it should have a follow up evocatino to capitalise on this or an Abyssal charm set that interacts with ghosts more directly than the Solar one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T02:44:27-07:00","id":904809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904406#post904406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Clutching Wraith's Embrace</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1W; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Requiem for the Damned<br /> <br /> Those slain by Shrieking Wraith's Requiem may know no peace; only an eternity of sorrowful wandering in the inhospitable wastes of the Underworld. This Evocation supplements a <b>decisive</b> attack. If the target is slain by this attack, at the end of the scene his <i>hun</i> soul will rise as an unquiet ghost, while his <i>po</i> will stir fitfully in his corpse. At the Storyteller's discretion, the corpse is more likely to become a hungry ghost, while the <i>hun</i> spirit WILL become a ghost. If magic such as the Zenith's anima power is used on the corpse before the end of the scene, this Evocation's effect is negated.</div> </div> </div> </div>So does this mean if I use this against a Battlegroup, do I get a battle of hungry ghosts to rampage around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T03:44:59-07:00","id":904833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904809#post904809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So does this mean if I use this against a Battlegroup, do I get a battle of hungry ghosts to rampage around?</div> </div> </div> </div>That could explain the high cost of this charm i suppose. However, since a singe hungry ghosts isn't much use in exalted combat, i would recommend two different costs - one for attacking groups and one for individuals. Raising your enemy as an hungry ghost is great shock value, but i would be unwilling to pay willpower for the privilege.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","name":"7 questions vanquish god","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11843_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T03:49:21-07:00","id":904838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>7 questions vanquish god</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904833#post904833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could explain the high cost of this charm i suppose. However, since a singe hungry ghosts isn't much use in exalted combat, i would recommend two different costs - one for attacking groups and one for individuals. Raising your enemy as an hungry ghost is great shock value, but i would be unwilling to pay willpower for the privilege.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more thinking of ambushing an enemy attack group, running, then letting the Hungry Ghost rampage as a guerilla warfare tactic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T04:04:57-07:00","id":904844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904838#post904838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was more thinking of ambushing an enemy attack group, running, then letting the Hungry Ghost rampage as a guerilla warfare tactic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be cool, powerful, and worth the willpower. that is exactly why i would recommend the two separate costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","name":"7 questions vanquish god","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11843_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:35:56-07:00","id":904917,"title":"","content":"So I could use some help, my mind is a bit fried, and I can't think of any good evocations or set up from my artifact other than a few basic ideas on what I want it to be and what I want it to do. Can the workshop help me with this?<br /> <br /> Lion's Pride<br /> Blue Jade and Orichalcum Reaper Daiklave Artifact 3<br /> Long ago in an age forgotten this daiklave was forged for a hero that time has forgotten all about except for the fact that they were a supreme duelist, so much so that it was said they were favored of the very gods of dueling. All that is known about them now is that they are recorded to history as the Lion. Their blade, and their pride is called Lion's Pride and was the royal treasure of a small kingdom near the dreaming sea. This blade was a symbol of the rulers of that kingdom for many years and was said to be the source of the kingdom's pride. Though it has been well maintained, polished, and kept sharp Lion's pride has not fought a duel since the shogunate. IT is even hinted at that the Empress herself fought a duel against Lion's Pride and it's original owner, over what they fought was not clear for at the time she was not empress, but rather a captain. Some say it was over an apology, some say it was over who would be the dominant in bed, but those who more deeply study the history of the Lion believe that they fought to prove who's boasts were empty, and who's were true. <br /> Evocations of Lion's Pride<br /> When Lion's pride Strikes it roars like a lion when it strikes with an evocation fueled strike. Possible effects like blasting the other off their feet, back range bands, over all though it's evocations should inspire a sense of that duelis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:38:42-07:00","id":904955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904775#post904775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First thought... is this a charm from another ability? - Yes it is, Fire and Stones Strike - But Better.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely Fire and Stones Strike. It has to be used on a living target, and you have to be attuned to <i>this bow</i> for it to work, and you have to have bought up the Whispers Merit... but I can definitely see the concern. I'm wanting to add <i>something</i> to this player's oomph, since she's feeling really left out in the combat scheme. She's not particularly crunch-savvy, this being her first Exalted game ever, and neither am I (this being my first 3E game ever). <br /> <br /> Would you recommend re-pricing it? 2m/die? +1W? Or would you recommend scrapping it altogether? If scrapping it, what else would you recommend in its place?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904775#post904775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Thought... Oof; I reckon Solar Archery lacks straight-up decisive damage adders for a reason and looking at this tells me why. I know it's small numbers but they really add up and make all the difference - given the proliferation of multi-attacks Archery swings around. If they do increase decisive damage it requires set-up first or an Essence 5 charm. I don't actually know if Evocations should be balanced assuming use with Native Charms (because they would be used in combos) but this gives me pause. As an example; A Solar archer with 9i can splatter 3 dudes in <i>artifact heavy plate</i> (assuming they have no other hardness charms or effects active) for the cost of 8m, 1wp with this charm and Feathered Death; that's three attacks at 11i, only requires essence 2.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't personally allow it but I have no better suggestion at this point. The additional withering support for Archery is welcome without being overpowering though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe leave it priced as-is but remove the <b>decisive</b> effect?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904775#post904775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Like! Super cheap but not individually powerful enough to warrant more cost than it has. Question; how would this interact with the Dawn Anima Banner?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hadn't considered that. I'd leave it to the individual ST. I'd say used in conjunction with the Dawn anima banner, it <i>could</i> make mindless undead afraid, if that fit contextually with the scene. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904775#post904775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like!... not sure why I'm paying 5m, 1wp for the effect though, feels like it should have a follow up evocatino to capitalise on this or an Abyssal charm set that interacts with ghosts more directly than the Solar one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's designed for an Abyssal, so they should have something to work with the subsequent ghosts. Mostly, it's a thematic thing for Oblivion. Maybe I'll make the Willpower cost only present if you're using it on a battle group?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T10:09:47-07:00","id":905032,"title":"","content":"Well, I had an artifact on the backburner for a while and was struck with inspiration today, so I gave it a go. I've not dealt with powers that affect Onslaught penalties much, so I don't know how broken this is. I expect it's pretty potent, so I'm ready to dial it back if need be.<br /> <br /> Before I get to it though, I did a short update to my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dxy9auJi1SOKk0coNGCRC1X6tkmzvtyMswVnYNjs0Eo/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\">Random Artifact Creator</a>. It'll do some names now. The lists are short, but easy to add on to for it to randomly generate weapon names.<br /> <br /> Anyways, on to my new weapon. I showed I hadn't done much with Red Jade, so here we go!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Torrid Pugilism (Red Jade Smashfists ***)</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">No one talks about the underground brawling clubs of the Blessed Isle. When people think of combat arenas, they think of colosseums and Martial Arts tournaments, both legal and illegal. But deep in the seediest districts in the heart of the Empire, no words are spoken: fists do the talking. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Brawler\u2019s Challenge was set up as an illegal fighting tournament to see who is the best of unformalized combat, but in reality it is a deathmatch where few contests end with 2 survivors. Raging Horse, an old Dragon-Blooded boxer who retired from the navy, was the champion for a full year, a duration never before achieved in the Brawler\u2019s Challenge. Tougher than nails, it was thought the old Fire-Aspect would reign forever. Not all rulers fall eventually.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">It was a young officer, barely 60 with hair of bright orange and brilliant gauntlets of Red Jade, who walked into the ring and challenged Raging Horse to a match. Raging Horse accepted, eager to put the young pup in her place. But as the old veteran soon found out, the woman with the Jade gauntlets should not have been underestimated. The match was over in mere moments, with Raging Horse a broken heap on the floor, and blood dripped from the now burning smashfists of the young officer. As the crowd cheered, the officer raised her fist as if to claim her new title. \u201cMy name is Pai-li Burning Petal, agent of the All-Seeing Eye. You are all under arrest pending investigation of further crimes against the Empress and the Empire.\u201d </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">That was the last night of Brawler\u2019s Challenge. Many more such tournaments still exist, but they are more careful of their reputation, for fear of the uncanny power of the young officer with the Red Jade Smashfists.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Torrid Pugilism is a pair of Smashfists made of ironsilk with plates and studs of Red Jade. They extend almost halfway up to the elbow and are heavily reinforced on the knuckles. When in combat, the air around them quivers with waves of heat, but to the wielder, they feel light and cool, the ironsilk allowing the gloves to breathe. There is a hearthstone socket on the back of each Smashfist.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Evocations of Torrid Pugilism</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">A Solar or Dragon-Blood who attunes to Torrid Pugilism causes the smashfists to radiate extra heat when in combat. The first </span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Withering</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\">attack the exalt makes against any given foe each round adds an extra point of Onslaught penalty. This effect can occur throughout combat, but only against foes that the Exalt attacked first, for Torrid Pugilism favors the bold. Any foe that has made an attack roll against the exalt first is ineligible for this bonus for the rest of combat.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Oppressive Buffet</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">2m </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Essence 1</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Type: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Supplemental</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Withering-Only, Stackable</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Until end of next turn</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisites: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">None</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The brawler who strikes with single-minded fury is unrelenting and Torrid Pugilism is fueled by such a warrior. This evocation enhances a </span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">withering</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\">attack causing 1 point of Onslaught penalty to persist until the end of the Exalt\u2019s next turn. This power is stackable up to a maximum of (the higher of 3 or the Exalt\u2019s Essence), but is cancelled if an attack is directed against any other foe. This evocation is incompatible with Battlegroups as the gauntlets prefer to battle one-on-one.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Nimble Blitz</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">3m </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Essence 1</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Type: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Supplemental</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">None</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisites: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">None</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Torrid Pugilism seeks weakness in its foes and rushes to punish such weakness. The wielder of these smashfists may activate Nimble Blitz to add the foe\u2019s current Onslaught penalty as a bonus to the exalt\u2019s own Rush pool as non-charm dice. This bonus cannot exceed a maximum of (the higher of 3 or the Exalt\u2019s Essence) and can only be used once per foe per combat, unless reset by raising a foe\u2019s Onslaught penalty to 4 from 0.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Searing Reversal</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">4m, 1wp </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Essence 2</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Type: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Decisive-Only</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisites: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Oppressive Buffet</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">With a backflash of fury, the exalt turns their disadvantage upon their foes. This evocation creates a difficulty 3 gambit where the exalt touches their foe and sears a brand upon them. If successful, this brand expels the exalt\u2019s current Onslaught penalty resetting them to zero, and transfers it to their foe. This penalty lasts for (the higher of 3 or the Exalt\u2019s Essence) rounds, though the exalt will resume accruing Onslaught penalties after activating Searing Reversal. Onslaught penalties are gained after the attack is resolved.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">If the foe is currently under the effects of Oppressive Buffet, Searing Reversal may also copy the exalt\u2019s current wound penalty for a single round. This does not remove the penalties from the exalt, and the copied penalty fades at the beginning of the foe\u2019s next turn.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Special Activation Rules</b>:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Searing Reversal can only be unlocked by landing a Decisive attack against a foe that had an Onslaught penalty of 4 or greater.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Inferno Smash</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">5m, 1wp </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Type: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Decisive-Only, Perilous</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisites: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Nimble Blitz, Searing Reversal</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The relentless strikes of the brawler are a sweet melody to Torrid Pugilism, but the final act, the climax of the song, is the sweetest of all. The exalt may activate Inferno Smash to create a </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Decisive </b>attack in an attempt to finish off a battered foe. This attack grants the foe\u2019s current Onslaught penalty in bonus dice to the damage roll. Additionally, the exalt may double up to (Essence) 10\u2019s on their damage roll should any appear.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">If the foe is not incapacitated by Inferno Smash, their current Onslaught penalty after attack resolution persists for an extra round (on top of any other persistent effects), resetting at the end of the exalt\u2019s next turn. Inferno Smash may only be used once per combat per foe.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 06-03-2016, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T11:09:25-07:00","id":905060,"title":"","content":"Okay, trying again as a complete noob to the process of making artifacts and evocations, I am attempting to make a sorcerous relic akin to Mara's Shadow Tattoos, but for the sorcerous initiation Pact with the Ifrit Lord.<br /> <br /> Mara's Shadow Tattoos are described thusly:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3, page 467</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Demonic Tattoos: Mara has marked the sorcerer, taking<br /> one or more of her own souls and rendering it down into<br /> a midnight-black tattoo that spirals around her chakras.<br /> The sorcerer may unlock Evocations from these tattoos<br /> that allow her to manipulate or gain power from shadows<br /> or darkness, alter her control spell to incorporate<br /> elements of darkness and subversion, or manipulate or<br /> empower summoned demons, such as by turning them<br /> into living shadows.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>So if we're converting this, I'm seeing a couple potential powers.<ul><li>Manipulate or gain power from fire or passion.</li> <li>Alter her control spell to incorporate elements of fire and passion</li> <li>Manipulate or empower summoned elementals, such as by turning them into... more fire?</li> </ul>So I guess I have those guidelines. Since it's a sorcerous relic that I imagine, like the Talisman, is equivalent in worth to a four dot relic, I'm thinking it might have between 1-2 Evocations per each of these things it could theoretically do, or maybe 1 per thing, with 1 starting Evocation and 1 &quot;final&quot; evocation that requires the others. What do you guys think? Do you have any advice on mechanics to scrutinize?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:44:57-07:00","id":905197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905060#post905060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Manipulate or gain power from fire or passion.</li> <li>Alter her control spell to incorporate elements of fire and passion</li> <li>Manipulate or empower summoned elementals, such as by turning them into... more fire?</li> </ul>So I guess I have those guidelines. Since it's a sorcerous relic that I imagine, like the Talisman, is equivalent in worth to a four dot relic, I'm thinking it might have between 1-2 Evocations per each of these things it could theoretically do, or maybe 1 per thing, with 1 starting Evocation and 1 &quot;final&quot; evocation that requires the others. What do you guys think? Do you have any advice on mechanics to scrutinize?</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly advise against gaining power from fire or passion, given that two of the pact's shaping rituals do exactly that. Manipulating flames would likewise be hard to do without stepping on the toes of the Burning Name merit. So that leaves us with manipulating passion, which, I think, could be an interesting design space to build around.<br /> Altering control spells to incorporate elements of fire and passion... sounds redundant to me, to be honest. A fire sorcerer can reasonably be expected to pick fire- and passion-related control spells <i>anyway</i>, in which case this offers little.<br /> Turning elementals into &quot;more fire&quot; sounds fairly boring. On the other hand, things like allowing fire elementals to hide within natural sources of flame might be cute. Of course, determining how exactly such effects would manipulate or empower summoned elementals would be significantly easier if we knew anything about the particular quirks of the Ifrit lord who granted the artifact.<br /> <br /> I'd also try and do something about the fact that your character's body is now heavily impregnated with fiery essence. Effects like bleeding gouts of flame when struck, immolating melee attackers with a decisive counterattack, that kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T16:07:37-07:00","id":905245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905197#post905197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I strongly advise against gaining power from fire or passion, given that two of the pact's shaping rituals do exactly that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't really thinking of a dice adder or sorcerous mote adder for that one, but alright.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905197#post905197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manipulating flames would likewise be hard to do without stepping on the toes of the Burning Name merit. So that leaves us with manipulating passion, which, I think, could be an interesting design space to build around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that necessarily a bad thing? Burning Name only has a sort of limited application of that sort of thing anyway, and it's not as if there's a Sorcery spell that lets you do cool things with fire. It seems like a good spot for an Evocation to live in, offering a more dramatic but different ability to interact with fire versus Burning Name.<br /> <br /> I'm definitely interested in exploring that metaphorical flame, but it'd be cool to do so in the context of its literal manifestation. We have a shaping ritual that lets us tap into Intimacies for sorcerous motes, for example. What about tapping into Intimacies for something else?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905197#post905197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Altering control spells to incorporate elements of fire and passion... sounds redundant to me, to be honest. A fire sorcerer can reasonably be expected to pick fire- and passion-related control spells <i>anyway</i>, in which case this offers little.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my concern as well, especially because unlike Mara's Shadow Tattoos, we're not lacking for potential control spells with fire elements as opposed to shadows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905197#post905197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turning elementals into &quot;more fire&quot; sounds fairly boring. On the other hand, things like allowing fire elementals to hide within natural sources of flame might be cute. Of course, determining how exactly such effects would manipulate or empower summoned elementals would be significantly easier if we knew anything about the particular quirks of the Ifrit lord who granted the artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly being tongue-in-cheek while looking at some of the ideas proposed for the Shadow Tattoo. I guess for narrative context, my ST and I took the Pact with the Ifrit Lord and made it into a pact with a Lesser Elemental Dragon of Fire, who, after running the character, a passionate, prodigy Twilight sorcerer, through a gauntlet to test their passion for the acquisition of knowledge/their inner fire, granted them the secrets of sorcery/the tattoo made from ground-down Elemental Fire as a mark of his favor. That was the fluff we were running with thusfar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905197#post905197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also try and do something about the fact that your character's body is now heavily impregnated with fiery essence. Effects like bleeding gouts of flame when struck, immolating melee attackers with a decisive counterattack, that kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking this same thing! A thing it could possibly interact with might be their anima banner as well, since I'm sure between this and the fire control spell that they're using that their anima banner has a lot of fiery elements.<br /> <br /> A question I have: Is there precedent for Evocations interact with merits? I have an idea for a first Evocation that combines this idea of having their body being suffused with fiery essence and bleeding fire when struck, and also thinking as a side effect it could potentially augment the Burning Name merit. Is that verboten or could it be a thing? I'm imagining it as a secondary element of it. Like, &quot;If you have the Burning Name merit, x or y happens.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T16:43:20-07:00","id":905256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905245#post905245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A question I have: Is there precedent for Evocations interact with merits? I have an idea for a first Evocation that combines this idea of having their body being suffused with fiery essence and bleeding fire when struck, and also thinking as a side effect it could potentially augment the Burning Name merit. Is that verboten or could it be a thing? I'm imagining it as a secondary element of it. Like, &quot;If you have the Burning Name merit, x or y happens.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not precedent, but given the artifacts and Evocations we have, it wouldn't be unreasonable. Especially for supernatural and sorcerous merits were it makes sense.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:43:26-07:00","id":905314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904955#post904955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's definitely Fire and Stones Strike. It has to be used on a living target, and you have to be attuned to <i>this bow</i> for it to work, and you have to have bought up the Whispers Merit... but I can definitely see the concern. I'm wanting to add <i>something</i> to this player's oomph, since she's feeling really left out in the combat scheme. She's not particularly crunch-savvy, this being her first Exalted game ever, and neither am I (this being my first 3E game ever).<br /> <br /> Would you recommend re-pricing it? 2m/die? +1W? Or would you recommend scrapping it altogether? If scrapping it, what else would you recommend in its place?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can safely add withering supplements to Archery attacks without worrying too much about unbalancing it, the danger is just in front up adding dice to decisive attacks since archery has so many multi-hit charms that would benefit even from a few extra numbers.<br /> <br /> I think the Evocation certainly has potential as a withering support charm. You could capitalize on the soulsteel theme by making it a kind of social withering attack. As is you could drop the WP cost and make it +raw withering damage per mote spent up to whispers maximum rating. It's not very flavorful though, I reckon it should inflict some kind of status on the enemy in addition to its damage (instilling an emotion, perhaps) that later evocations could build on...<br /> <br /> Actually that gives me an idea.<br /> <br /> Switch Shriek of the Void and Requiem for the Damned in the evocation tree order. Give Shriek a base cost of 2m, bonus raw withering damage for 1m per additional damage up to whispers rating and layer some bonus post-soak damage based on the strength of their intimacy (+2, +3, +4 respectively) inflicted by Requiem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=904955#post904955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's designed for an Abyssal, so they should have something to work with the subsequent ghosts. Mostly, it's a thematic thing for Oblivion. Maybe I'll make the Willpower cost only present if you're using it on a battle group?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool. I wouldn't suggest building long-term control into the artifact without upping its cost to 4 or 5 dots anyway - Abyssal tech will probably deal more with directly influencing ghosts, or necromancy which would supplement the evocation nicely. I'd recommend giving the attuned user a turn of control over the slain victim's ghosts or compelling them in some way to aide the attuned user... hmmm.... providing cover by floating near the artifact? Providing some kind of general bonus/spendable resource ala White Reaper Halos? I'll think more on this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T22:01:13-07:00","id":905407,"title":"","content":"So I came up with a tentative first Evocation for the Brand of Elemental Flame as I've named it. What do you guys think of this?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Refer to later verson downthread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 06-03-2016, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T05:15:33-07:00","id":905553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905407#post905407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I came up with a tentative first Evocation for the Brand of Elemental Flame as I've named it. What do you guys think of this?<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Elemental Flame Suffusement</span></span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2m </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Brand of Elemental Flame suffuses the sorcerer\u2019s Essence with fiery power. Her skin is warm to the touch, and in moments of great tension, it can be felt bubbling on the surface of the tattoos themselves, which light up with the light of the fire contained within. The sorcerer\u2019s Essence is so saturated with flame that any opportunity to let it out can be explosive.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any wounds that break the skin release a gout of flame at the attacker, burning them with the brilliance of the sorcerer\u2019s fiery Essence. If she suffers lethal damage, she may expend 2 motes reflexively for a gout of flame to surge from her skin, burning her attacker. This is treated as an environmental hazard that must be dodged with a Dexterity + Athletics check at a difficult of Essence or three, whichever is higher. Failure means the attacker suffers 2L as if they\u2019d been exposed to a fire.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh. I'd up the cost and make it a decisive counterattack with Stamina+Occult that deals (Essence + wound penalty) dice of damage (and, obviously, resolves after taking the hit and rolling damage). Because if your character is even halfway effective, opponents who have a realistic chance of damaging her won't be particularly concerned about a difficulty 3 Dex+Athletics check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T09:13:06-07:00","id":905695,"title":"","content":"For evaluation and critique:<br /> <br /> Imperial Mandate of Flames<br /> <br /> This is one of Ysyr's great treasures, captured during a war with Prasad some centuries ago. Forged in the depths of the South by a Solar during the early First Age, of pure red jade and had an illustriuous history, seeing much battle against the invaders of Creation and a less illustrious history in squables between the Dragon-Blooded. Eventually, this moved a Sidereal to remove it from its current owner after he used it in a most dishonourable fashion. Then, it gathered dust for a while, until it was given to the Dragon-Blooded during the Usurpation, during which it was shattered and the shards captured by a Solar craftsman, who reforged it for his only remaining circle mate, piecing it back together and binding it in Orichalcum. More powerful than before, the armour and the Dawn within it were said to strike the Dragon-Blooded with the force of a falling star, laying waste to several armies before the Solar finally fell to the strange arts of the Sidereals, who once more captured the armour. However, the Solar's ghost began to pursue them across Creation, and eventually even struck the gates of Heaven. Rather than placate the furious ghost, a Sidereal reworked the armour with Starmetal characters, allowing the power of the armour to affect the ghost. Then it was given to a Dragon-Blooded champion who battled and defeated the ghost. This Dragon-Blooded Exalt then travelled to the Southeast, where Prasad would one day be, and settled there. And the rest, as they say, is history.<br /> <br /> Heavy Artifact Armour of Red Jade, Orichalcum and Starmetal with a single Hearthstone socket on the inside. A Solar, Sidereal or Dragon-Blood who attunes to the Artifact doubles his soak against flame based attacks, gains an additional 3 hardness against them and doubles 8s against environmental hazards based on fire or heat. <br /> <br /> Blessed Flames: Radiance<br /> Cost: -(1m); Mins: Ess 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> When casting a fire-based spell, for every sorcerous mote by which the caster exceeds the amount required for the spell, a small, sourceless flame flares into existence around the attuned. These flames provide a source of light and may be directed at a target with a wits + occult roll, by paying 1m. They have the traits of a light artifact weapon with the Thrown(Short), Mounted, Lethal and Flame tags.<br /> <br /> Blessed Flames: Demonlight<br /> Cost: 1m ; Mins: Ess 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Blessed Flames: Radiance<br /> Gathering 5 flames gained through the previous Evocation and binding them together with his own essence, the attuned may create a larger, pale blue flame. This flame renders all immaterial creatures within short range visible for one instant before forcing its way down the throat of the attuned.<br /> <br /> Blessed Flames: Starfire<br /> Cost: 5m, 2wp ; Mins: Ess 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Aggravated, Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Blessed Flames: Demonlight <br /> Having swallowed the demonlight, the Attuned may over the course of one turn gather all of the remaining flames within himself, before releasing them with a horrific scream, unleashing a beam of red-silver energy that vaporizes metal and stone and burns flesh. The beam is aimed with Wits + Occult, and may not strike any target beyond medium range. This attack is very exhausting and as such may be used only once per scene, and inflicts a -1 wound penalty which may only be healed by one night of rest and is cumulative with other wound penalties.<br /> <br /> Blessed Flames: Emperor Blaze<br /> Cost: 5m ; Mins: Ess 4<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Prerequisite: Blessed Flames: Starfire<br /> Having unleashed the blast of starfire, the Attuned is vulnerable. Armour, however, is meant for protection and draws on the bearer's remaining essence automatically, phasing it through the armour and creating a blaze of multi-hued, beautiful flames around the bearer. Any fire based attacks or hazards are absorbed by the flames, and any attacks from close range suffer a -3 penalty from the bright light. Furthermore, anyone within close range of the bearer suffers the effects of a Bonefire Hazard. The wounds and penalty are all an illusion, however, albeit a very realistic one and may be resisted by paying 1wp every turn one wishes to ignore the flames. After the first activation, the attuned may use this without using the prerequisite<br /> Special Activation Rules: This Evocation awakens for free and activates automatically after the use of the prerequisite once the attuned meets the minimums.<br /> <br /> Blessed Flames: Pyroclastic Judgement<br /> Cost: 1m ; Mins: Ess 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Blessed Flames: Emperor Blaze<br /> This evocation requires the attuned to use Blessed Flames: Starfire and then build up 10 more flames, turn these into Demonlights and swallow both of them, all while surrounded by the Emperor Blaze. He may then activate this final evocation. A pillar of flame surrounds him, and carries him to medium range above the ground into the eye of a tornado of flame. From there he may unleash large blasts of fire which strike everything within short range of their point of impact. The attack may not be dodged though the centre of the flames is solid enough to be deflected or even returned with a successful dex + melee/brawl/MA against the bearers attack roll of wits+occult. The bearer may further use Blessed Flames: Radiance as if he had at least one flame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:53:10-07:00","id":905772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905695#post905695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For evaluation and critique:<br /> <br /> Imperial Mandate of Flames<br /> &lt;i&gt;Snip&lt;/i&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that this one has similar build up as Volcano Cutter requiring a lot of work to get the final power. Also, I'm stealing the idea of burning bonus sm in order to trigger effects. That's brilliant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T11:15:11-07:00","id":905785,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hey guys, this is the first artifact I've come up with and its for black orchids post (Im the player mentioned in it) from a few pages ago.<br /> <br /> The weapon itself, in its base form, is a separating chakram that the wielder forges a primal bond with an unlocks some innate connection to some beast spirits kept locked away in it.<br /> <br /> I present to you:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primal Fangs Wheel (Artifact 4; Moonsilver Infinite Chakram)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Viewing her future husband as unwilling to do the things he must when the time arises due to his morals, Grim Ebony set out to forge a weapon to assist and influence him when the need comes to do as he must. The pack does as it must, but her wolf was hesitant. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">She hunted down ten thousand beasts, and took a claw or fang, barb or spine, to use in the forging of the weapon. Each animal's natural arsenal was used as the core of the blades and she used the carcasses to heat her forge. Each blade was quenched in the blood of prey animals to enhance the predators spirit of the weapon. After the sickles were quenched, they were put onto a band of orichalcum and blessed by gods of predator animals and the gods of hunts. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The weapon proved a valuable gift for her bondmate, who carried it with him for centuries. After he was murdered in the Usurpation she tried to use the weapon in retaliation but to no avail and the weapon has been used as a beautiful gift of the Dynasts ever since; be it for weddings or forging alliances, this weapon promotes unity. Its last owner was a Sesus patriarch who wished to form such an alliance.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primal Fangs Wheel\u2019s surface is a shimmer of silver that only becomes more magnificent to view when the weapon is being used at night or during the use of Evocations. Stalking is about 2 foot in diameter with a deceptively thin but wide blade, made up of hundreds of interlocking sickle shaped moonsilver blades with delicate starmetal filigree. Four much larger \u201cclaws\u201d sit at equal spacing, all interwoven on a thin band of orichalcum etched with moonsilver and starmetal decoration. Due to the weapons design and function, it is impossible for Grim Ebony to have been able to produce it with a hearthstone socket. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The spirit of the weapon is unruly, like a pack of undisciplined hounds, and takes a harsh master to keep in line; to this date no Dragonblooded has kept the spirit of Primal Fang Wheel in check and it yearns for its true master. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Evocations of Primal Fangs Wheel</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Solar or Lunar who attunes to Primal Fangs Wheel gains an uncanny insight into the rush of combat, the weapon ushering its wielder into the hunt, gaining an additional +1 on Join Battle, stealth and awareness rolls to spot danger.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Savage Wolves Assail</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4m </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Uniform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The master commands and the pack obeys. When this Evocation is used four distinct grouping of sickle blades gather around the main claws and sail through the air on a path towards the wielders target on a trail of silvery white essence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The roll gains (Perception) double 9\u2019s. If used against a battlegroup, the battlegroup\u2019s Size is added to the number of doubles rolled and the roll gains double 8\u2019s as well.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Diving Raptor\u2019s Descent</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5m </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dual</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As the wielder unleashes the spirits of the hunting raptors, trails of white essence follows as the blades gather into flocks, taking flight to assail the victim with talons and beak leaving a wake of blood and terror.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Shrieking Wheel splits into numerous smaller sections and fans out to attack an enemy or battlegroup within range. If used as <b>withering</b> the attack converts (Perception) dice of post soak into automatic successes and if used as <b>decisive</b> it converts the lesser of (Perception or Essence) dice of raw damage into automatic successes. If used against a battle group, the <b>withering</b> attack removes bonuses to soak from size and the <b>decisive</b> doubles raw damage for calculating extra damage levels.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defiant Matriarch Stance</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 6m, 2i, 1wp </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> One Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Savage Wolves Assail, Diving Raptor\u2019s Descent</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As the two begin to feel the ebb and flow of each other, so to does the bond of faithful beast grow stronger towards its master. With a staunch stance, the wielder takes the weapon in both hands and flares of silver white essence explode out on the trail of the blades as they begin to orbit the wielder, like a lioness protecting her cubs.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Using this Evocation gives the wielder full cover from the orbiting blades while removing the advantage any assailants get from engaging the wielder in melee. Against a battlegroup they do not gain any benefits of might or superior damage due to magnitude as the individual blades parry their attacks away from hitting the wielder. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pack Retaliation Technique</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 4m, 1i </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Decisive-only, Counterattack</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Mother Wolf Approach</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The pack retaliates, attacking with fury and grim determination against those who to seek to injure or kill their master, throwing themselves into the fray. The blades follow the attack to slay the aggressor pulsing with silver-gold light, to punish him for such an act.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pack Retaliation Technique is a counter attack ability that targets using the normal counter-attack rules but allows the attack to reach out to short range, as the blades don't want to leave the wielders side. The Evocation creates a counter attack using the wielders Thrown as a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> attack. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Activation Rules:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Using Pack Retaliation Technique ends the activation of Defiant Matriarch stance for the rest of the scene. It can be reset if the wielder crashes a non-trivial opponent after unleashing a savage attack; be it through the use of Charms or a well described stunt.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primeval Spirits Merge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10m, 2wp </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> One Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pack Retaliation Technique</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Meditating on the beast spirits that reside in the blade, the wielder release a loud call; a growl or shrill shriek of some kind and summons a sleeping beast from the shards. The Essence of both mingle, causing the wielders anima to take on a brilliant combination of their natural essence plus the silvery red contours, lying over them like a ghostly cape and hood of the ancient beasts they have released back into Creation. The blades gather in a large circling flock, the centre of the wheel in line with the root chakra of the wielder.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the wielder activates Call Forth the Primeval Beast they gain numerous static benefits for the remainder of the scene. The first is that they gain an additional 8 hardness that can stack with other sources, as well as +2 dice on all combat related actions and gaining an additional 1 point of Initiative every turn. On top of this the wielder also converts 2 dice of </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">or </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">post soak dice into automatic successes and gain a +1 to their Resolve when a situation arises of someone or something attempting to intimidate, threaten, plead with or lie to. Finally, due to the innate and powerful connection of the myriad of ancient beasts, the wielder also receives a Defining level Intimacy for the scene of \u201cI must shed my prey\u2019s blood\u201d.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Special Activation Rules:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Call Forth the Primeval Beast is a tiring Evocation, and takes its toll on the wielder's body and the connection between warrior and weapon. To be able to reuse Primeval Spirits Merge the wielder must find a worthy prey animal and kill it, bathing the weapon in its blood and feasting upon the raw meat.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11900-grynder","name":"Grynder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T08:05:07-07:00","id":906417,"title":"","content":"Hello people and Exalted community once again. And you The Unsung Hero, love most of your posts.<br /> <br /> Anyway, despite being proud game master for numerous RPGs and long time Exalted fan (and storyteller), I find myself in difficult situation.<br /> I've home brewed several artifacts and evocations for my players for the 3rd edition, some with their help. However, my newest group has a player whose wish for a sword and resulting thought process has created me a challenge for creating an artifact that I have not been able to overcome yet.<br /> <br /> Maybe a little background information of the situation is in order first.<br /> The player is new to Exalted, though not beginner role player. He wanted to have a Masamune kind of swordsmith Twilight. Initial concept was him being a 100 year old swordsmithing hermit, but since it wouldn't make sense for having a Solar that old (...or you could, but then it would be good that all player characters be 100 year old surviving solar exaltations that weren't locked down) we came to a compromise.<br /> His character hails from the end of the First Age. He was present when the Usurpation happened. However, he was young and had exalted quite recently (details matter not, as one will notice soon). He got away and traveled with a pile of magical materials far away into the eastern wyld, attempting to forge a weapon that would smite the dragon blooded for the Usurpation. Since creating potent enough weapon would have taken lot of time (don't start with the Thousand Forge Hands, he bought it only after the game started) and he wanted to get to the fight as soon as possible, he made a deal with a Raksha Noble named &quot;Prince Laavdhi&quot;. The Raksha allowed him to use a special location deep in the eastern Wyld known as &quot;the Valley of Times&quot;. Not a time travelling device (I dislike time travelling too) but a certain kind of stasis area, where time slows down, allowing for really long tasks or projects to be done without barely any time passing for the user. As an inexperienced Solar, he made a fateful deal with Prince Laavdhi. He forged his artifact with his own hands, but only after he left the Valley, he noticed how he had been tricked. Time did move slower related to him, but it moved normally for everything else outside the valley. Creating the artifact had taken millenia. Moreover, Prince Laavdhi mockingly informed the solar that even memories not related directly to the task at hand in the Valley will lose track of character and vanish to the Wyld. If the Twilight wanted even some of those memories back, he'd have to come back one day and either beg Prince Laavdhi to fish them out of chaos or beat him to do it. Twilight can remember barely anything from the First Age, only that things were...different then, but cannot specify why or how they were different.<br /> And so it is that the player's Twilight wanders Creation with a sword created in a metaphysical time capsule to fight in the Usurpation that ended before the weapon was even finished.<br /> I call it &quot;Ekidnon, Sword of Retribution&quot;.<br /> <br /> The problem is: What kind of evocations I'd give for something like that? I've thought numerous approaches: better defenses against people that have already hit him (defense doesn't really have thematic link to &quot;Retribution&quot;), then I thought of &quot;Retribution points&quot; he can spend to fuel effects and he gains them by getting hit or having negative intimacy towards his target (too much book-keeping) and finally I gave the sword ONE evocation based on the first evocation of Beloved Adorei, except it reveals only directly opposing intimacies to the wielder or his intimacies.<br /> I could hit my head to the table long enough to figure something out, but at least I thought I could ask for advice. Not asking anyone to create it for me though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11221-turtleking","name":"Turtleking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T08:34:14-07:00","id":906430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grynder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905785#post905785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(COLOR=#a64d79][FONT=Arial]Primal Fangs Wheel (Artifact 4; Moonsilver Infinite Chakram)(/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> (COLOR=#000000][FONT=Arial]Viewing her future husband as unwilling to do the things he must when the time arises due to his morals, Grim Ebony set out to forge a weapon to assist and influence him when the need comes to do as he must. The pack does as it must, but her wolf was hesitant. (/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy tags Batman! Once again, please be cautious about copy-pasting your work from Word into the forums. It puts coding tags everywhere and makes it a slog for people to quote. That said, I'm very excited for a Chakram!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grynder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905785#post905785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spirit of the weapon is unruly, like a pack of undisciplined hounds, and takes a harsh master to keep in line; to this date no Dragonblooded has kept the spirit of Primal Fang Wheel in check and it yearns for its true master.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this implying that Dragon-Blooded can't use it? That's fine if it is, just checking if it's flavor or mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grynder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905785#post905785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evocations of Primal Fangs Wheel<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Solar or Lunar who attunes to Primal Fangs Wheel gains an uncanny insight into the rush of combat, the weapon ushering its wielder into the hunt, gaining an additional +1 on Join Battle, stealth and awareness rolls to spot danger.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Is this +1 die or +1 success? And either way, I'd put an additional attunement cost on a free benefit across multiple die pools (Join battle being an especially good one). 1 mote is probably enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grynder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905785#post905785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Savage Wolves Assail</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4m </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Uniform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The master commands and the pack obeys. When this Evocation is used four distinct grouping of sickle blades gather around the main claws and sail through the air on a path towards the wielders target on a trail of silvery white essence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The roll gains (Perception) double 9\u2019s. If used against a battlegroup, the battlegroup\u2019s Size is added to the number of doubles rolled and the roll gains double 8\u2019s as well.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>So first, I'm pretty sure this is just affecting the attack roll, right? It doesn't specify if it's the attack or damage roll, but I'm going to continue assuming it's attack roll.<br /> <br /> I was going to comment on doubling 9's on Decisive attacks, but it's actually just on the damage roll that you don't, so this is legit territory. I'm a fan of adding a limited number of them, so that's cool. On the battlegroup part, let's say they have Perception 3 and a Size 2 BG. Does the attack get 5 d9's and 5 d8's? Does it get 5 doubles chosen across the 9's and 8's? Specify. For 4m, I'd probably say go 5 across both, but it wouldn't take much to convince me that 5 and 5 isn't viable even at that cost. Maybe a mote extra. Just gut feelings there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grynder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905785#post905785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Diving Raptor\u2019s Descent</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5m </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dual</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As the wielder unleashes the spirits of the hunting raptors, trails of white essence follows as the blades gather into flocks, taking flight to assail the victim with talons and beak leaving a wake of blood and terror.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Shrieking Wheel splits into numerous smaller sections and fans out to attack an enemy or battlegroup within range. If used as <b>withering</b> the attack converts (Perception) dice of post soak into automatic successes and if used as <b>decisive</b> it converts the lesser of (Perception or Essence) dice of raw damage into automatic successes. If used against a battle group, the <b>withering</b> attack removes bonuses to soak from size and the <b>decisive</b> doubles raw damage for calculating extra damage levels.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This one feels good, though I'll be honest, I don't think I've ever had anyone in my group use a Decisive attack against a battlegroup (since you can't gain significant initiative from them). That said, it is a sizable bonus so there's some merit. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grynder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905785#post905785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Defiant Matriarch Stance</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 6m, 2i, 1wp </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> One Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Savage Wolves Assail, Diving Raptor\u2019s Descent</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As the two begin to feel the ebb and flow of each other, so to does the bond of faithful beast grow stronger towards its master. With a staunch stance, the wielder takes the weapon in both hands and flares of silver white essence explode out on the trail of the blades as they begin to orbit the wielder, like a lioness protecting her cubs.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Using this Evocation gives the wielder full cover from the orbiting blades while removing the advantage any assailants get from engaging the wielder in melee. Against a battlegroup they do not gain any benefits of might or superior damage due to magnitude as the individual blades parry their attacks away from hitting the wielder. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Full cover for a whole scene without the drawbacks? Wowza. My gut says OP, especially since you can keep throwing your weapon (right?). It can move with you, while making you immune to all ranged attacks but doesn't keep you from throwing your own weapon? The thing that is creating your cover?<br /> <br /> Someone may come tell me it's valid, but I have to go with my gut and say this is too strong. I'd call it balanced if you had to hold your weapon to gain it and as soon as you throw it it ends. Or if it only granted you Heavy Cover, which is still very good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grynder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905785#post905785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pack Retaliation Technique</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 4m, 1i </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Decisive-only, Counterattack</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Mother Wolf Approach</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The pack retaliates, attacking with fury and grim determination against those who to seek to injure or kill their master, throwing themselves into the fray. The blades follow the attack to slay the aggressor pulsing with silver-gold light, to punish him for such an act.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pack Retaliation Technique is a counter attack ability that targets using the normal counter-attack rules but allows the attack to reach out to short range, as the blades don't want to leave the wielders side. The Evocation creates a counter attack using the wielders Thrown as a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> attack. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Activation Rules:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Using Pack Retaliation Technique ends the activation of Defiant Matriarch stance for the rest of the scene. It can be reset if the wielder crashes a non-trivial opponent after unleashing a savage attack; be it through the use of Charms or a well described stunt.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It has been noted that there are no &quot;normal counter-attack rules&quot; in the book, every charm does it a little differently, so you're going to need to spell it out here 1) when during attack resolution it activates, 2) does it stop or negate the incoming attack, 3) since it's Decisive, what happens when it responds to a Withering attack, how much of your initiative do you get to use? You'll need to look through the examples in the book and model it after one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grynder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905785#post905785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Primeval Spirits Merge</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10m, 2wp </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> One Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pack Retaliation Technique</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Meditating on the beast spirits that reside in the blade, the wielder release a loud call; a growl or shrill shriek of some kind and summons a sleeping beast from the shards. The Essence of both mingle, causing the wielders anima to take on a brilliant combination of their natural essence plus the silvery red contours, lying over them like a ghostly cape and hood of the ancient beasts they have released back into Creation. The blades gather in a large circling flock, the centre of the wheel in line with the root chakra of the wielder.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the wielder activates Call Forth the Primeval Beast they gain numerous static benefits for the remainder of the scene. The first is that they gain an additional 8 hardness that can stack with other sources, as well as +2 dice on all combat related actions and gaining an additional 1 point of Initiative every turn. On top of this the wielder also converts 2 dice of </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">withering </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">or </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">decisive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">post soak dice into automatic successes and gain a +1 to their Resolve when a situation arises of someone or something attempting to intimidate, threaten, plead with or lie to. Finally, due to the innate and powerful connection of the myriad of ancient beasts, the wielder also receives a Defining level Intimacy for the scene of \u201cI must shed my prey\u2019s blood\u201d.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Special Activation Rules:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Call Forth the Primeval Beast is a tiring Evocation, and takes its toll on the wielder's body and the connection between warrior and weapon. To be able to reuse Primeval Spirits Merge the wielder must find a worthy prey animal and kill it, bathing the weapon in its blood and feasting upon the raw meat.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. That's <b>beefy</b>. I'll start by saying that 8 hardness is a lot, especially when added to stuff. I'm HOPING that the +2 dice on all combat related actions counts as charm-added dice, in which case it's fine. A <i>mote drip</i> is VERY powerful. I would give this charm the Perilous keyword at least, and end it when crashed. <br /> <br /> Converting post soak dice is fine, but there is no soak for Decisive, so it's just converting 2 normal damage dice into successes, right?<br /> <br /> I'd like to see a little more about what it means to have that defining intimacy. Does it mean they're incapable of running away? Do they have to kill their foe? Or just do at least 1 level of damage? It feels like it was added in there to help confine the charm, but the Principle is broad enough that it's not very confining.<br /> <br /> You have a lot of powerful effects in this weapon, making me ponder whether Artifact 4 is enough (it probably is, but just barely). But then again, you also cost them pretty damn high, which really does offset it. I don't care for &quot;powerful and persistent, but expensive&quot; effects myself, but it doesn't make them badwrong necessarily. On the flipside, you have a very cool predator themed weapon. Not all of the evocations add to that theme (like the cover one), but some of them get it spot on (like the first few). I think this is a good addition to our forum collection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T08:42:31-07:00","id":906436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Turtleking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906417#post906417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I call it &quot;Ekidnon, Sword of Retribution&quot;.<br /> <br /> The problem is: What kind of evocations I'd give for something like that? I've thought numerous approaches: better defenses against people that have already hit him (defense doesn't really have thematic link to &quot;Retribution&quot;), then I thought of &quot;Retribution points&quot; he can spend to fuel effects and he gains them by getting hit or having negative intimacy towards his target (too much book-keeping) and finally I gave the sword ONE evocation based on the first evocation of Beloved Adorei, except it reveals only directly opposing intimacies to the wielder or his intimacies.<br /> I could hit my head to the table long enough to figure something out, but at least I thought I could ask for advice. Not asking anyone to create it for me though.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we know a lot about the twilight's story and where he went to forge the blade, but we know very little about the blade itself. Why is it a Sword of Retribution? If we try to design it by the name alone, Retribution means <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">punishment inflicted on someone as vengeance for a wrong or criminal act. So is it a blade of justice or revenge? Does it hung true criminals or those the exalt deems criminals (maybe via opposing intimacies)? Is it holy vengeance or bloody vengeance? What materials is it made out of? I like to look at the lists in the back of the book to get ideas for what effects I could play with. <br /> <br /> From your first idea, it could use attacks to learn Intimacies, and then use those Intimacies to fuel/empower attacks against them so long as they are opposed to yours. Bonuses to damage are great if the goal is to kill. Or maybe it's more social than that, and it starts leveraging Intimacies to add Guilt or Regret to their heart to make them start to repent. Perhaps with a capstone similar to Righteous Devil Style's where it gives them a chance to redeem themselves or die.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it's more simple than that, and it's just a beefy sword of light where it considers attacking you or your friends (ties) as crimes and gains retribution points that it uses to strike with vengeance. The more you are attacked, the more you can hit back.<br /> <br /> Just a few thoughts for ya. Good luck!</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T08:53:28-07:00","id":906445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Turtleking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906417#post906417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I call it &quot;Ekidnon, Sword of Retribution&quot;.<br /> <br /> The problem is: What kind of evocations I'd give for something like that? I've thought numerous approaches: better defenses against people that have already hit him (defense doesn't really have thematic link to &quot;Retribution&quot;), then I thought of &quot;Retribution points&quot; he can spend to fuel effects and he gains them by getting hit or having negative intimacy towards his target (too much book-keeping) and finally I gave the sword ONE evocation based on the first evocation of Beloved Adorei, except it reveals only directly opposing intimacies to the wielder or his intimacies.<br /> I could hit my head to the table long enough to figure something out, but at least I thought I could ask for advice. Not asking anyone to create it for me though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Onslaught converters, some way to bounce back Anima Flux, maybe an Instill attack to break up groups, and some Battle Group hosing abilities would be a good start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:13:14-07:00","id":906454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905695#post905695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imperial Mandate of Flames</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, armor! Me likey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905695#post905695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blessed Flames: Radiance<br /> Cost: -(1m); Mins: Ess 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> When casting a fire-based spell, for every sorcerous mote by which the caster exceeds the amount required for the spell, a small, sourceless flame flares into existence around the attuned. These flames provide a source of light and may be directed at a target with a wits + occult roll, by paying 1m. They have the traits of a light artifact weapon with the Thrown(Short), Mounted, Lethal and Flame tags.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question here is what kind of action is attacking someone with the flame? Can it be reflexively? If they have 5 flames, can they do 5 consecutive attacks against a nearby target at the same time, regardless of actions taken? Or does it have to be their combat action to do it like Burning Name? One of these things is supremely unbalanced. The other is just cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905695#post905695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blessed Flames: Demonlight<br /> Cost: 1m ; Mins: Ess 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Blessed Flames: Radiance<br /> Gathering 5 flames gained through the previous Evocation and binding them together with his own essence, the attuned may create a larger, pale blue flame. This flame renders all immaterial creatures within short range visible for one instant before forcing its way down the throat of the attuned.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you use a simple action to combine flames and immaterial creatures become visible, then the Demonlight gets swallowed and the creatures are invisible again. If I gathered that right, you're unable to really DO anything to those creatures, because it's a Simple charm, so your action is done. And no allies can do anything either because it's Instant duration. I get that you're supposed to use Demonlights to build up for the final evocation, but at Essence 2 I can't envision the reason you'd use this evocation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905695#post905695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blessed Flames: Starfire<br /> Cost: 5m, 2wp ; Mins: Ess 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Aggravated, Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Blessed Flames: Demonlight<br /> Having swallowed the demonlight, the Attuned may over the course of one turn gather all of the remaining flames within himself, before releasing them with a horrific scream, unleashing a beam of red-silver energy that vaporizes metal and stone and burns flesh. The beam is aimed with Wits + Occult, and may not strike any target beyond medium range. This attack is very exhausting and as such may be used only once per scene, and inflicts a -1 wound penalty which may only be healed by one night of rest and is cumulative with other wound penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the intro sentence seems to imply this takes a full turn of prep before you can use it. I don't think that's the intent, so a small tweak might help that. Otherwise, it's... a very expensive normal Decisive attack that gets to use Occult. Since it has to be built up, I'm not sure there's a need for 2wp in the cost. Flight of the Brilliant Raptor could be done in the same number of actions and could do more damage. <br /> <br /> I actually just noticed the Aggravated keyword. If I hadn't noticed that, I don't think I would have known that it deals Aggravated damage. If such is the case, you should probably put it in the text too, as well as give the -1 wound penalty an &quot;additional&quot; qualifier. As in &quot;additional -1 wound penalty&quot; for clarity's sake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905695#post905695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blessed Flames: Emperor Blaze<br /> Cost: 5m ; Mins: Ess 4<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Prerequisite: Blessed Flames: Starfire<br /> Having unleashed the blast of starfire, the Attuned is vulnerable. Armour, however, is meant for protection and draws on the bearer's remaining essence automatically, phasing it through the armour and creating a blaze of multi-hued, beautiful flames around the bearer. Any fire based attacks or hazards are absorbed by the flames, and any attacks from close range suffer a -3 penalty from the bright light. Furthermore, anyone within close range of the bearer suffers the effects of a Bonefire Hazard. The wounds and penalty are all an illusion, however, albeit a very realistic one and may be resisted by paying 1wp every turn one wishes to ignore the flames. After the first activation, the attuned may use this without using the prerequisite<br /> Special Activation Rules: This Evocation awakens for free and activates automatically after the use of the prerequisite once the attuned meets the minimums.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should note that the first mechanic nullifies the attunement benefits of this armor which grant defense bonuses against fire attacks. This seems to grant fire immunity for a scene which is very powerful, and if true, I'd up the cost a bit. Also forcing opponents to pay 1wp every turn to ignore an illusion is wicked strong in this edition. This needs a big cost boost as is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905695#post905695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blessed Flames: Pyroclastic Judgement<br /> Cost: 1m ; Mins: Ess 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Blessed Flames: Emperor Blaze<br /> This evocation requires the attuned to use Blessed Flames: Starfire and then build up 10 more flames, turn these into Demonlights and swallow both of them, all while surrounded by the Emperor Blaze. He may then activate this final evocation. A pillar of flame surrounds him, and carries him to medium range above the ground into the eye of a tornado of flame. From there he may unleash large blasts of fire which strike everything within short range of their point of impact. The attack may not be dodged though the centre of the flames is solid enough to be deflected or even returned with a successful dex + melee/brawl/MA against the bearers attack roll of wits+occult. The bearer may further use Blessed Flames: Radiance as if he had at least one flame.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, I have a soft spot for pinnacles that draw off of multiple (especially all) previous evocations in a weapon. So kudos on that.<br /> <br /> However, there's some missing details. What is the range of these &quot;large blasts of fire&quot;? We only know how big their AoE is after impact. The flow of the writing made it difficult to determine how the mechanics of this attack worked. So it creates a single decisive attack, using Wits + Occult as the attack roll, is undodgable but may be parried and can be returned upon the attacker with a sort of Clash mechanic (though that's meaningless, because the wielder is immune to all sources of fire with Emperor Blaze, which must be activated to use this evocation).<br /> <br /> Oh, but actually, this lets him hover up there for a scene, so it's not a single Decisive, it just lets you make special Decisive attacks. Yeah, I was onboard for the cheap cost because of how much buildup it required, but I can't get behind scene-long effects for as cheap as 1m. I'd up the cost. That said, with some mechanics clarifications, I'm actually a fan of the direction of this evocation.<br /> <br /> So it may not have come across in my readthru but I actually like this armor <b>a lot</b>. There's some stuff to clean up, but it's evocative and consistent in it's design philosophy from start to finish. I think I would have made it Medium or Light armor myself, but that's just a matter of taste. There's nothing wrong with this being Heavy. Good show!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:20:03-07:00","id":906463,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I've done more than 1 or 2 artifact reviews without using the word <i>evocative</i>. I really like that word.<br /> <br /> Plus, y'know... <i>Evocati</i>ons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:35:17-07:00","id":906474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jondera</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=898957#post898957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Livewood Heart (Green Jade Short Powerbow) Artifact (3)</span></span><br /> <br /> (COLOR=#333333](FONT=Verdana]<i>One Root Spirit</i>[/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> (COLOR=#333333](FONT=Verdana]Cost:[/FONT][/COLOR](COLOR=#333333](FONT=Verdana] 1m [/FONT][/COLOR]<span style=\"color:#333333\">(FONT=Verdana]Type:[/FONT]</span>(COLOR=#333333]<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Reflexive </span>[/COLOR]<span style=\"color:#333333\">(FONT=Verdana]Mins:[/FONT]</span>(COLOR=#333333]<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Essence 1</span>[/COLOR]<br /> (COLOR=#333333](FONT=Verdana]Duration:[/FONT][/COLOR](COLOR=#333333](FONT=Verdana] 1 day [/FONT][/COLOR](COLOR=#333333](FONT=Verdana]Keywords:[/FONT][/COLOR](COLOR=#333333](FONT=Verdana] None[/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> <br /> (COLOR=#333333](FONT=Verdana]When the character uses One Root Spirit, he reaches out and plucks a branch from a nearby bush or tree, transforming it into a living arrow. This can be done a part of a normal attack with Livewood Heart without requiring a flurry or they may be saved for later, but no more than one arrow may be transformed per turn and no other bow may use these these living arrows, as they tend to latch onto any wooden or earthen surface and take root inside. If they are not planted within 1 day of being transformed, they will wither and die, becoming useless as ammunition for Livewood Heart (though perhaps an excellent source of arrow shafts for lesser bows).[/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>Another friendly reminder to be wary of copying charms from Word. This forum likes to make needless tags, making replies hard for people. I made a few of them visible for this quote to show what it looks like to me.<br /> <br /> As for the Evocation, it's a nice, flavorful description of Phantom Arrow Technique. I dig it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jondera</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=898957#post898957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><i>Spreading Tendrils Offense</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost:[</span></span>COLOR=#333333]<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 1m </span>[/COLOR]<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Supplemental </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 1 turn </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Uniform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> One Root Spirit</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The character's living arrow grows and changes mid-flight, branching and recombining in unpredictable organic patterns that make it extremely distracting, even to a wary foe. An attack supplemented by this evocation imposes a -2 onslaught penalty, instead of the normal -1.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Also simple but good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jondera</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=898957#post898957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><i>Tangling Root Glamour</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 4m, 2i </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Supplemental </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Instant </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\">FONT=Verdana]Keywords:[/FONT]</span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Uniform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> One Root Spirit</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The character's living arrow grows fiercely as it approaches the target, tangling them in a mass of rampant vegetation that makes it difficult to move. If an attack supplemented by this evocation is successful, the target is effectively prone. They may not be literally knocked to the ground, but the vines that pin them to a wall or bind their elbows to their knees impose exactly the same penalty, and that penalty may be removed by a combat movement action, equivalent to &quot;rise from prone.&quot;</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, another simple yet elegantly written evocation. Very nice! I like the cost too!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jondera</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=898957#post898957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><i>Hungry Roots Consumption</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 8m, 1wp </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Simple </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Mins:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> 1+ turns </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Decisive Only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Spreading Tendrils Offense, Tangling Root Glamour</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The character's living arrow latches onto a target, seeking out their blood and rooting within, whereupon it quickly devours this powerful source of life energy to fuel its out-of-control growth.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">This charm allows the character to use a special Difficulty 3 gambit. If the gambit succeeds, the arrow takes root in the target's body and begins growing, dealing one health level of lethal damage immediately, and an additional health level of damage on each of the target's turns, continuing until the target has suffered damage equal to the wielder's Dexterity. The target also suffers a -2 penalty to all actions, and a -1 penalty to Parry and Evasion, for the remainder of the scene, due to the pain of the living plants expanding through their body. If the target is killed by the damage from this Evocation, or while the damage from it is ongoing, plants completely overtake their entire body, sprouting from every orifice in a grisly display of nature run amuck.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">This evocation may be used once per scene unless reset by the wielder of Livewood Heart drawing a living arrow from the mass of vegetation that sprouted from a victim killed under the effects of Hungry Root Consumption.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Alright this one needs a bit of looking. Dealing 3-5 (let's be honest, no one with Dex &lt; 3 is really going to use a bow) automatic damage over time with no way to stop it is pretty potent. I'm not saying it's broken, but it is strong. These typically have some sort of thing where the target has to use a miscellaneous to remove the arrow or something. So they don't HAVE to die, but they lose an action doing it. It's just something to consider.<br /> <br /> I like the penalties, but I would reorder it to remove possible misreading. Generally, a defense can be considered an action, but you have different penalties to them. So I would say &quot;target also suffers a -1 penalty to Parry and Evation, and a -2 penalty to all other actions&quot; to avoid people wondering if the -2 and -1 stack to a -3.<br /> <br /> Overall I actually really like this bow. It's simple but clean. Evocative of a bow made of wood. (though I imagine a lot of these effects will end up in the Dragon-Blooded Archery charmset) Only the last one needs considering, but I dig it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:41:58-07:00","id":906479,"title":"","content":"Okay, so messing with the evocation:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#a64d79\">Elemental Flame Suffusement</span></b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m Mins: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Counterattack, Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> The Brand of Elemental Flame suffuses the sorcerer\u2019s Essence with fiery power. Her skin is warm to the touch, and in moments of great tension, it can be felt bubbling on the surface of the tattoos themselves, which light up with the light of the fire contained within. The sorcerer\u2019s Essence is so saturated with flame that any opportunity to let it out can be explosive.<br /> <br /> Any wounds that break the skin release a gout of flame at the attacker, burning them with the brilliance of the sorcerer\u2019s fiery Essence. After she suffers lethal damage from a decisive attack, she may expend 4 motes to make a reflexive decisive counterattack at close range using a gout of flame that surge from her wound, burning her attacker. This counterattack is made with an attack pool equal to Stamina + Occult and has raw damage equal to the sorcerer's Essence + Wound Penalty, with her wound penalty being the worst one she is currently suffering. For example, if she suffered damage into her -4 health level and has an Essence of 2, she is rolling 6 dice for raw damage.<br /> <br /> Additionally, if the sorcerer possesses the Burning Name Merit, her internal fire enhances the flames she may summon by invoking her patron. The flames she may summon using that merit gain the traits of a medium artifact weapon with the lethal, flame, mounted and thrown (medium) tags.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> I based the cost off the counterattack abilities in the melee but given its more limited circumstances (after you've been damaged) I thought it was fair to waive the willpower cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 06-03-2016, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:50:57-07:00","id":906490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906479#post906479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so messing with the evocation:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#a64d79\">Elemental Flame Suffusement</span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this Evocation. How far away can the flames burn an attacker? If I get shot from Long (or Extreme!) range, can I burn the attacker or am I limited to Flame weapon ranges?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:55:51-07:00","id":906494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906479#post906479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so messing with the evocation:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#a64d79\">Elemental Flame Suffusement</span></b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m Mins: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Counterattack, Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> The Brand of Elemental Flame suffuses the sorcerer\u2019s Essence with fiery power. Her skin is warm to the touch, and in moments of great tension, it can be felt bubbling on the surface of the tattoos themselves, which light up with the light of the fire contained within. The sorcerer\u2019s Essence is so saturated with flame that any opportunity to let it out can be explosive.<br /> <br /> Any wounds that break the skin release a gout of flame at the attacker, burning them with the brilliance of the sorcerer\u2019s fiery Essence. After she suffers lethal damage from a decisive attack, she may expend 4 motes reflexively to make a reflexive decisive counterattack using a gout of flame that surge from her wound, burning her attacker. This counterattack is made with an attack pool equal to Stamina + Occult and has raw damage equal to the sorcerer's Essence + Wound Penalty, with her wound penalty being the worst one she is currently suffering. For example, if she suffered damage into her -4 health level and has an Essence of 2, she is rolling 6 dice for raw damage.<br /> <br /> Additionally, if the sorcerer possesses the Burning Name Merit, her internal fire enhances the flames she may summon by invoking her patron. The flames she may summon gain the traits of a medium artifact weapon with the lethal, flame, mounted and thrown (medium) tags.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very cool. you do say reflexive 1 too many times in the second sentence of the second paragraph. And you should probably state the range that this gout of flame can counter attack to in the base attack. Otherwise, I like this one a lot.<br /> <br /> One thing I noticed though is that your extra benefit for the Buirning Name merit is... almost useless. This evocation is (rightly) Decisive-only, which means the Flame tag doesn't matter, and the Thrown (Medium) tag doesn't matter (aside from establishing range. Being a medium weapon doesn't matter because it's Decisive. And it already deals Lethal damage (I assume. Actually that isn't established in the base, you should specify), so that just leaves the Mounted tag. So consider that in your advantage. Maybe all it does is extend the range and grant the mounted tag, though you still need to establish the base range of this evocation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:00:53-07:00","id":906496,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906494#post906494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is very cool. you do say reflexive 1 too many times in the second sentence of the second paragraph. And you should probably state the range that this gout of flame can counter attack to in the base attack. Otherwise, I like this one a lot.<br /> <br /> One thing I noticed though is that your extra benefit for the Buirning Name merit is... almost useless. This evocation is (rightly) Decisive-only, which means the Flame tag doesn't matter, and the Thrown (Medium) tag doesn't matter (aside from establishing range. Being a medium weapon doesn't matter because it's Decisive. And it already deals Lethal damage (I assume. Actually that isn't established in the base, you should specify), so that just leaves the Mounted tag. So consider that in your advantage. Maybe all it does is extend the range and grant the mounted tag, though you still need to establish the base range of this evocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed the reflexive thing.<br /> <br /> Added a statement indicating it works at close range for the counterattack.<br /> <br /> I just added a clarifying statement: It doesn't modify the decisive counterattack, it modifies the flame summoned by the merit, enhancing its traits. For this part I want to reflect that having all that fiery Essence inside you has a number of lesser side effects, but I'm worried that it overloads the Evocation, so I'm not sure how to approach it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Here's a version with an additional description.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Elemental Flame Suffusement</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Counterattack, Decisive-Only</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Brand of Elemental Flame suffuses the sorcerer\u2019s Essence with fiery power. Her skin is warm to the touch, and in moments of great tension, it can be felt bubbling on the surface of the tattoos themselves, which light up with the light of the fire contained within. The sorcerer\u2019s Essence is so saturated with flame that any opportunity to let it out can be explosive.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any wounds that break the skin release a gout of flame at the attacker, burning them with the brilliance of the sorcerer\u2019s fiery Essence. After she suffers lethal damage from a decisive attack, she may expend 4 motes to make a reflexive decisive counterattack at close range using a gout of flame that surge from her wound, burning her attacker. This counterattack is made with an attack pool equal to Stamina + Occult and has raw damage equal to the sorcerer's Essence + Wound Penalty, with her wound penalty being the worst one she is currently suffering. For example, if she suffered damage into her -4 health level and has an Essence of 2, she is rolling 6 dice for raw damage.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Additionally, the presence of such a large amount of fiery essence has a number of side effects. The sorcerer\u2019s internal heat is a constant, keeping her warm. This provides (Essence) automatic success to resist appropriate environmental hazards such as extreme cold or bonfires. The sorcerer\u2019s skin is always warm to the touch. If the sorcerer possesses the Burning Name Merit, her internal fire enhances the flames she may summon by invoking her patron. The flames she may summon using that merit gain the traits of a medium artifact weapon with the lethal, flame, mounted and thrown (medium) tags.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 06-03-2016, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:29:20-07:00","id":906532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906496#post906496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Elemental Flame Suffusement</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Counterattack, Decisive-Only</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Brand of Elemental Flame suffuses the sorcerer\u2019s Essence with fiery power. Her skin is warm to the touch, and in moments of great tension, it can be felt bubbling on the surface of the tattoos themselves, which light up with the light of the fire contained within. The sorcerer\u2019s Essence is so saturated with flame that any opportunity to let it out can be explosive.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any wounds that break the skin release a gout of flame at the attacker, burning them with the brilliance of the sorcerer\u2019s fiery Essence. After she suffers lethal damage from a decisive attack, she may expend 4 motes to make a reflexive decisive counterattack at close range using a gout of flame that surge from her wound, burning her attacker. This counterattack is made with an attack pool equal to Stamina + Occult and has raw damage equal to the sorcerer's Essence + Wound Penalty, with her wound penalty being the worst one she is currently suffering. For example, if she suffered damage into her -4 health level and has an Essence of 2, she is rolling 6 dice for raw damage.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>On second thought, I think it's way too cheap for what it can potentially do (9 dice of lethal damage, independently of initiative? yikes!).<br /> <br /> So I'd go with 4m, 1+ i for the cost, raw damage equal to wound penalty + (Initiative spent, up to a maximum of the sorcerer's Essence), and make it ignore hardness.<br /> <br /> Edit: on third thought, I think ignoring hardness actually isn't really in the core of its theme. Bulky artifact armor <i>should </i>protect against fire. However, an Ess 2 upgrade that lets the character infuse the flames with the fury of her solar Essence, paying a surcharge (maybe equal to half the total damage, round up?) to make the counterattack ignore hardness sounds reasonable to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 06-03-2016, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:44:21-07:00","id":906542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906532#post906532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On second thought, I think it's way too cheap for what it can potentially do (9 dice of lethal damage, independently of initiative? yikes!).<br /> <br /> So I'd go with 4m, 1+ i for the cost, raw damage equal to wound penalty + (Initiative spent, up to a maximum of the sorcerer's Essence), and make it ignore hardness.<br /> <br /> Edit: on third thought, I think ignoring hardness actually isn't really in the core of its theme. Bulky artifact armor <i>should </i>protect against fire. However, an Ess 2 upgrade that lets the character infuse the flames with the fury of her solar Essence, paying a surcharge (maybe equal to half the total damage, round up?) to make the counterattack ignore hardness sounds reasonable to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a valid point. I had neglected the fact that it doesn't actually spend your initiative so it's free damage and doesn't reset you. If it reset you, that'd be a different matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:50:38-07:00","id":906547,"title":"","content":"Okay, what about this as a final?<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Elemental Flame Suffusement</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Counterattack, Decisive-Only</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span> The Brand of Elemental Flame suffuses the sorcerer\u2019s Essence with fiery power. Her skin is warm to the touch, and in moments of great tension, it can be felt bubbling on the surface of the tattoos themselves, which light up with the light of the fire contained within. The sorcerer\u2019s Essence is so saturated with flame that any opportunity to let it out can be explosive.<br /> <br /> Any wounds that break the skin release a gout of flame at the attacker, burning them with the brilliance of the sorcerer\u2019s fiery Essence. After she suffers lethal damage from a decisive attack, she may expend 4 motes and initiative up to her Essence score to make a reflexive decisive counterattack at close range using a gout of flame that surge from her wound, burning her attacker. This counterattack is made with an attack pool equal to Stamina + Occult and has raw damage equal to the sorcerer's Initiative Spent + Wound Penalty, with her wound penalty being the worst one she is currently suffering. For example, if she suffered damage into her -4 health level and has an Essence of 2, she is rolling 6 dice for raw damage. If successful, the attack does not reset her to base Initiative.<br /> <br /> At Essence 2+, she may infuse the flames with the power of her Solar Essence, spending motes equal to half the raw damage to make it ignore hardness.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the presence of such a large amount of fiery essence has a number of side effects. The sorcerer\u2019s internal heat is a constant, keeping her warm. This provides (Essence) automatic success to resist appropriate environmental hazards such as extreme cold or bonfires. The sorcerer\u2019s skin is always warm to the touch. If the sorcerer possesses the Burning Name Merit, her internal fire enhances the flames she may summon by invoking her patron. The flames she may summon using that merit gain the traits of a medium artifact weapon with the lethal, flame, mounted and thrown (medium) tags.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:57:49-07:00","id":906556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906547#post906547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This counterattack is made with an attack pool equal to Stamina + Occult and has raw damage equal to the sorcerer's Initiative Spent + Wound Penalty, with her wound penalty being the worst one she is currently suffering. For example, if she suffered damage into her -4 health level and has an Essence of 2, she is rolling 6 dice for raw damage. If successful, the attack does not reset her to base Initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your first sentence says that the raw damage pool is Initiative spent + Wound Penalty, but your second sentence gives an example using Essence in the calculation, and your third sentence says it doesn't rest to base initiative, suddenly implying that the amount of initiative spent is flexible instead of all of it like a normal attack. Needs consistency and clarification. The first sentence implies it's a normal decisive attack which gets to add the current Wound Penalty to the damage, but the last sentence seems to modify it and imply it's a variable amount of damage. And, if the exalt chose to use ALL of their initiative, the last sentence implies it would either NOT actually spend any initiative, or it would leave the exalt in Crash. <br /> <br /> I would clean this up by simply saying it's a normal decisive attack with Stamina + Occult for a attack pool, and adds current Wound Penalty to the damage pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:01:45-07:00","id":906558,"title":"","content":"Okay, iterated again.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Elemental Flame Suffusement</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4m (7m) <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Counterattack, Decisive-Only</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> None</span><br /> The Brand of Elemental Flame suffuses the sorcerer\u2019s Essence with fiery power. Her skin is warm to the touch, and in moments of great tension, it can be felt bubbling on the surface of the tattoos themselves, which light up with the light of the fire contained within. The sorcerer\u2019s Essence is so saturated with flame that any opportunity to let it out can be explosive.<br /> <br /> Any wounds that break the skin release a gout of flame at the attacker, burning them with the brilliance of the sorcerer\u2019s fiery Essence. After she suffers lethal damage from a decisive attack, she may expend 4 motes to make a reflexive decisive counterattack at close range using a gout of flame that surge from her wound, burning her attacker. This counterattack has Stamina + Occult as its attack pool and adds the Sorcerer\u2019s current highest wound penalty to her raw damage. If successful, the attack resets her to base Initiative.<br /> <br /> At Essence 2+, she may infuse the flames with the power of her Solar Essence, spending 3 additional motes to make it ignore hardness.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the presence of such a large amount of fiery essence has a number of side effects. The sorcerer\u2019s internal heat is a constant, keeping her warm. This provides (Essence) automatic success to resist appropriate environmental hazards such as extreme cold or bonfires. The sorcerer\u2019s skin is always warm to the touch. If the sorcerer possesses the Burning Name Merit, her internal fire enhances the flames she may summon by invoking her patron. The flames she may summon using that merit gain the traits of a medium artifact weapon with the lethal, flame, mounted and thrown (medium) tags.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 06-03-2016, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:02:52-07:00","id":906559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906547#post906547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental Flame Suffusement</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, you could <b>lower</b> the power of this and simply make the damage pool be equal to the current Wound Penalty only. It's a smaller amount of damage, but could be activated more often (since it doesn't interact with initiative) and the cost would make sense still. And it would make sense for foes with hardness to ignore it. I like of like this version better, but either works.<br /> <br /> Edit: The version you just posted is good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:07:54-07:00","id":906561,"title":"","content":"So I'm thinking &quot;actually, 10 xp for the ability to spend even more motes on an already costly Evocation that isn't guaranteed to hit (and which comes with the implicit additional cost of the health levels you lose - after all, if you take no damage, you can't activate it) just so you can ignore Hardness sounds like a fairly crappy deal&quot;. I'm also thinking the more fireblood you have gushing out of you, the easier time you should have hitting your opponent with it, which is the exact opposite of how it actually works now (Sta+Occult is a rolled action, thus subject to wound penalty).<br /> <br /> So how about &quot;Whenever you activate its prerequisite, you can spend additional motes equal to your current wound penalty to make Elemental Flame Suffusement ignore Hardness and convert wound penalties that would apply to your Sta+Occult roll to bonus dice instead&quot;? Probably way too cheap (you effectively gain +2 dice per mote spent, plus the ability to ignore Hardness), but making it double your current wound penalty would make the ability hideously overcosted (12m, Xi at -4). Making it cost an extra WP would run into the problem that the ability in its current form is completely useless against anything with Hardness at low Essence, and WP is an extremely limited resource, so this would effectively shut down its usage in such cases.<br /> <br /> All things considered, I'd go with &quot;spend additional motes and anima levels equal to your current wound penalty, with bonfire counting as 4 levels for the purposes of this Evocation&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:12:26-07:00","id":906566,"title":"","content":"I'm very appreciative of the help, but I am having a hard time parsing what you're saying at the end. How should it be changed to be better? Should I just note that the roll to attack ignores the wound penalty? Where does the Anima Banner enter into it? Some clarification would be really appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:21:56-07:00","id":906577,"title":"","content":"So, clarification how I imagine this to look like:<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental Flame Suffusement<br /> Cost</b>: 4m, 1+i <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Counterattack, Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> The Brand of Elemental Flame suffuses the sorcerer\u2019s Essence with fiery power. Her skin is warm to the touch, and in moments of great tension, it can be felt bubbling on the surface of the tattoos themselves, which light up with the light of the fire contained within. The sorcerer\u2019s Essence is so saturated with flame that any opportunity to let it out can be explosive.<br /> <br /> Any wounds that break the skin release a gout of flame at the attacker, burning them with the brilliance of the sorcerer\u2019s fiery Essence. After she suffers lethal damage from a decisive attack, she may expend 4 motes and at least one Initiative to make a reflexive decisive counterattack at close range using a gout of flame that surge from her wound, burning her attacker. This counterattack is made with an attack pool equal to Stamina + Occult and has raw damage equal to the sorcerer's Wound Penalty + (Initiative spent activating this Evocation, up to a maximum of the sorcerer's Essence), with her wound penalty being the worst one she is currently suffering.<br /> <br /> <b>Indomitable Sun-Blaze Infusion</b> (or whatever fancy name you want it to have)<br /> <b>Cost</b>: - (1+m, 1+a) <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Elemental Flame Suffusement<br /> <br /> (blah blah fluff text about charging the prerequisite up with the Solar Essence of your anima)<br /> <br /> This Evocation permanently upgrades its prerequisite, allowing the character to spend a surcharge of additional motes and anima levels equal to her current wound penalty (with bonfire counting as 4 levels for this purpose) whenever she activates Elemental Flame Suffusement. This lets her convert wound penalties that affect her Stamina+Occult roll into bonus dice instead, and causes the Evocation's damage to ignore Hardness.<br /> <br /> I hope this clears things up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 06-03-2016, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T12:24:57-07:00","id":906629,"title":"","content":"Well my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905032#post905032\">last one</a> didn't get any attention, but I had another one come up. My friend needed a Direlash for their npc, so I rolled one up on my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dxy9auJi1SOKk0coNGCRC1X6tkmzvtyMswVnYNjs0Eo/edit#gid=184168765\" target=\"_blank\">Artifact Creator</a>. I got Blue/White Jade, <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Harness/Manifest Lightning and Immobilize People or Things. So I knocked this guy out for fun.</span></span><br /> <br /> *Edit* Ugh, I just found out that all my posts are suddenly full of the nasty tags too. I thought I had that problem fixed. Bleh. Trying to edit that out now.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Bolt Lash (Blue/White Jade Direlash ***)</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Another glory from the legendary twilight Bright Judgement, the Bolt Lash is a miracle born of a thousand near-death experiences. Bright Judgement sought to harness a true bolt of lightning. However, the power of an elemental lord was insufficient, and lightning created by sorcery would not do either. Trial after trial, it seemed nothing could create the weapon she envisioned in her mind. At least, the Twilight committed herself to catching a true bolt of lightning.<br /> <br /> And so, Bright Judgement built a tower of cold iron high into the sky from atop her mountain in the North. And atop that spire she waited, for this bolt must be pure and natural. She could not conjure a storm or it would be tainted. For days and weeks she waited patiently, until the first storm finally came. The iron spire drew strike after strike, but quick as she was, Bright Judgement could not outpace the sky. Her attempts to catch a bolt of lightning were too slow, and eventually the storm passed.<br /> <br /> Two years went by, with Bright Judgement standing on her spire passing the days and weeks between storms, and risking death time and again to catch a single pure bolt of lightning. The day she finally succeeded, she almost believed it to be a dream. The quivering bolt seared her hand and struggled to escape, but her conviction held her hand true.<br /> <br /> Bringing the bolt back to her workshop, she hammered the bolt into a large ingot of Blue Jade. When the fusion seemed it would hold, she spent another year carefully forging the ingot into a weave which she then turned into a long Direlash. Despite the might of the Blue Jade, the angered bolt of lightning was nearly too much for it to handle, and so she anchored the Blue Jade with a handle made of White, to keep the power in check and direct it. It was not Bright Judgement\u2019s greatest triumph, but it was her hardest earned and her hands proudly bore the scars from that project for the rest of her days.<br /> <br /> Bolt Lash is a Blue and White Jade Direlash. The length is an almost pure 10 foot length of woven Blue Jade, capable of channeling an uncanny amount of electric energy, while the handle is a rod of White Jade wrapped in insulating mammoth leather. It has a single hearthstone socked in the butt of the grip. When unattuned, Bolt Lash lies curled in a neat coil and cannot be extended. It also acts as a very strong lightning rod until it is attuned, causing few to be willing to store it unused.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Evocations of Bolt Whip</span></b><br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blooded who attunes to Bolt Whip burns away an extra point of initiative from foes on successful Withering attacks against prone targets. This extra point of initiative damage is not gained by the exalt.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Shock Thrash</span></b><br /> Cost: 1m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Withering-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The power of lightning is awe-inspiring, and brings its victims to their knees. Each successful Withering attack enhanced with Shock Thrash causes a jolt of electricity in the victim, forcing them to roll (Stamina + Resistance) to avoid being knocked prone. The difficulty of this roll is 1, but is increased by the number of shock charges held by Bolt Lash at the beginning of the attack.<br /> <br /> Each use of Shock Thrash regardless of success of the attack increases the number of shock charges by 1 after attack resolution. Bolt Lash can hold a maximum of 5 shock charges, which fade after combat ends at a rate of 1 charge per minute.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Stunning Flog</span></b><br /> Cost: 3m, 1+ Shock Charges Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Shock Thrash<br /> <br /> There is no bolder way to proclaim your might than to keep your foes down. A foe that is truly beaten, cannot raise a hand against you. Stunning Flog can only be activated against a foe who is already prone. An attack so enhanced adds the number of expended shock charges to the difficulty of the target\u2019s attempts to rise from prone. Regardless of whether the target succeeds or not, the difficulty lasts and applies to future attempts should they be knocked prone again, fading at 1 point of difficulty per round.<br /> <br /> Each time the target fails to rise from prone while affected by Stunning Flog, Bolt Lash gains a shock charge.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Thunder Crash</span></b><br /> Cost: 5m, 3+ Shock Charges Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Stunning Strike<br /> <br /> Thunder resounds and with a deafening crash it brings even the mighty low. Thunder Crash creates a Decisive attack that expends at least 3 shock charges. If the target is not prone, on a successful hit, the target is automatically knocked prone and the difficulty to stand up in increased by 3 for 1 round. If the target is already prone, the target has no choice but to remain prone for their next action and cannot even attempt to stand.<br /> <br /> If Bolt Lash has extra shock charges in excess of the cost, they may be expended to convert up to (extra expended charges) extra successes on the attack roll into damage dice on the damage roll.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Lightning Arc</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Cost: 5m, 1wp, 5 Shock Charges Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual, Perilous<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Thunder Crash<br /> <br /> Suffusing the whip with the fury of the sky, the weapon transforms into a solid bolt of lightning which twitches and arcs from nearby surfaces. This grants a variety of effects to Bolt Lash.</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bolt Lash may extend to attack foes up to Short range. Additionally, prone foes at Short range are considered embattled with the exalt for all purposes</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The white-hot light of the whip is searing, doubling threshold successes on Witheringattack rolls for purposes of determining damage</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Disarm gambits that utilize Bolt Lash gain 1 automatic success</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Decisive Savaging attacks against foes that are grappled by Bolt Lash gain 2 extra dice of damage</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stealth is rendered impossible for the wielder of Bolt Lash for the duration of Lightning Arc</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This evocation lasts until the end of the scene or until the exalt is Crashed.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 06-03-2016, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T13:01:31-07:00","id":906655,"title":"","content":"Ok, so after some revision brought on from the sagely Unsung Hero here is some of the changes to the Primal Fangs Wheel. If they aren't put into here, then they were good to go/nothing &quot;negative&quot; was said about them (there is no negative critique). Hopefully this will balance this relatively insane weapon; go hard or go home.<br /> <br /> There was a bit of text from the previous post brought up about the weapon rebelling against Dragon-Blooded but that is more of a flavour piece rather than flat mechanics (other than Dragon-Blooded don't gain access to its Evocations)<br /> <br /> (Another note, I dont precisely know how to fix all the tags. If it happens again I'll do more digging in how to fix it)<br /> <br /> <b>Savage Wolves Assail</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> The master commands and the pack obeys. When this Evocation is used four distinct grouping of sickle blades gather around the main claws and sail through the air on a path towards the wielders target on a trail of silvery white essence.<br /> <br /> The attack roll gains (Perception) double 9\u2019s. If used against a battlegroup, the battlegroup\u2019s Size is added to the number of doubles rolled and the roll gains double 8\u2019s as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Defiant Mother Bear Stance</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m, 2i, 1wp <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> As the two begin to feel the ebb and flow of each other, so to does the bond of faithful beast grow stronger towards its master. With a wide stance, the wielder takes the weapon in both hands and flares of silver white essence begin to gather before wielder and weapon roar out in unison, the ground shuddering at the release.<br /> <br /> Defiant Matriarch Stance causes a social influence action that affects all who can see and hear the wielder. The wielder rolls Appearance+Presence gaining (Essence) automatic successes and rolls against Resolve of those present, on a success those affected gain a Major strength Intimacy towards the wielder of Fear. The effect can be resisted by spending the wielders Essence in Willpower.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3+ the wielder gains automatic successes equal to the affected targets level of intimacy on social influence to do with instilling actions or threatening. Any attempt to bargain with the prey proves the wielder weak, and the weapon puts this as a curse, removing successes equal to the intimacies strength.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Retaliation Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1i, (+1wp) <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-only, Counterattack, Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant or Until Next Round<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Savage Wolves Assail, Diving Raptor\u2019s Descent<br /> <br /> The pack retaliates, attacking with fury and grim determination against those who to seek to injure or kill their master, throwing themselves into the fray. The blades follow the attack to slay the aggressor pulsing with silver-gold light, to punish him for such an act.<br /> <br /> Pack Retaliation Technique is a counterattack that is usable after the wielder takes <b>withering</b> damage and can make an immediate <b>decisive</b> attack action dealing a base amount of damage equal to the number of <b>withering </b>damage the wielder just took. This attack does not use up the wielder's attack action, nor does it reset their initiative value.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3+ the wielder may spend a point of Willpower to make the Evocation last until their next turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Primeval Spirits Merge</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 10m, 2wp <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Pack Retaliation Technique, Defiant Mother Bear Stance<br /> <br /> Meditating on the beast spirits that reside in the blade, the wielder release a loud call; a growl or shrill shriek of some kind and summons a sleeping beast from the shards. The Essence of both mingle, causing the wielders anima to take on a brilliant combination of their natural essence plus the silvery red contours, lying over them like a ghostly cape and hood of the ancient beasts they have released back into Creation. The blades gather in a large circling flock, the centre of the wheel in line with the root chakra of the wielder.<br /> <br /> When the wielder activates Call Forth the Primeval Beast they gain numerous static benefits for the remainder of the scene. The first is that they gain 6 hardness that doesn\u2019t stack with armour, as well as +2 charm based dice on all combat related actions and gaining an additional 1 point of Initiative every turn.<br /> <br /> On top of this the wielder also converts 2 dice of <b>withering</b> damage into auto successes and lowers the enemies hardness by 2 for <b>decisive</b> damage. The wielder gains +1 to their Resolve when a situation arises of someone or something attempting to intimidate, threaten, plead with or lie to.<br /> <br /> Finally, due to the intense and powerful connection to the myriad of ancient beasts, the wielder receives a Defining level Intimacy for the scene of \u201cI must shed my prey\u2019s blood\u201d. The wielder instinctively ignores allies and will viciously assail the nearest targets, starting with those who have an Intimacy of fear, whether naturally or through Defiant Mother Bear Stance, and then working through the rest of the enemies present. If an ally attempts to stop them through calming words or begging for compassion, they can succeed through an instill or bargain social action but the wielder gains the extra dice associated with the Defining level intimacy. If violence or threats of violence are issued then the wielder adds them to their \u201cprey list\u201d, unless the wielder spends their own (Essence) in Willpower to ignore it.<br /> <br /> If the wielder is put into Initiative Crash, but are put into -3 rather than usual. The effects of Primeval Spirits Merge ceases and the wielder is left fully aware of their failings to shed their prey's blood, and for the rest of the combat scene suffer a -2 on all dice rolls.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules:<br /> Call Forth the Primeval Beast is a tiring Evocation, and takes its toll on the wielder's body and the connection between warrior and weapon. To be able to reuse Primeval Spirits Merge the wielder must find a worthy prey animal and kill it, bathing the weapon in its blood and feasting upon the raw meat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11900,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11900-grynder","user":"Grynder","date":". 06-03-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11900-grynder","name":"Grynder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T17:27:11-07:00","id":906831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906629#post906629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905032#post905032\">last one</a> didn't get any attention, but I had another one come up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I didn't really feel qualified to try, but I suppose this is a workshop!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Bolt Lash (Blue/White Jade Direlash ***)</span></span></span></b> </div> </div> </div>I love the story-context for this thing, and combining blue and white in this way is an awesome concept. I even like the consequence of leaving it unattuned--fits well within its creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Evocations of Bolt Whip</span></b><br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blooded who attunes to Bolt Whip burns away an extra point of initiative from foes on successful Withering attacks against prone targets. This extra point of initiative damage is not gained by the exalt. </div> </div> </div>My first thought was this seemed really weak--and then I kept reading...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Shock Thrash</span></b><br /> Cost: 1m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Withering-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The power of lightning is awe-inspiring, and brings its victims to their knees. Each successful Withering attack enhanced with Shock Thrash causes a jolt of electricity in the victim, forcing them to roll (Stamina + Resistance) to avoid being knocked prone. The difficulty of this roll is 1, but is increased by the number of shock charges held by Bolt Lash at the beginning of the attack.<br /> <br /> Each use of Shock Thrash regardless of success of the attack increases the number of shock charges by 1 after attack resolution. Bolt Lash can hold a maximum of 5 shock charges, which fade after combat ends at a rate of 1 charge per minute. </div> </div> </div>So this is an unstoppable build-up, then? So long as the user spends 1m per turn, regardless of either the success of the strike or the success of the prone-roll, they'll have full charges within 5 rounds, and the difficulty of the prone-roll increases each and every time, up to 6, with no chance of error.<br /> <br /> Part of me feels like charges should be expended to increase the difficulty (on a 1-to-1 basis), but I've <b><i>also</i></b> come to realize over the past week or so that my idea of &quot;too strong&quot; is actually way off. I'd like to hear your reasoning all the same--might help me better understand!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Stunning Flog</span></b><br /> Cost: 3m, 1+ Shock Charges Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Shock Thrash<br /> <br /> There is no bolder way to proclaim your might than to keep your foes down. A foe that is truly beaten, cannot raise a hand against you. Stunning Flog can only be activated against a foe who is already prone. An attack so enhanced adds the number of expended shock charges to the difficulty of the target\u2019s attempts to rise from prone. Regardless of whether the target succeeds or not, the difficulty lasts and applies to future attempts should they be knocked prone again, fading at 1 point of difficulty per round.<br /> <br /> Each time the target fails to rise from prone while affected by Stunning Flog, Bolt Lash gains a shock charge. </div> </div> </div>Knock them down, then keep them down. Fits the theme and works mechanically pretty well, I'd imagine--though I kind of tilt my head at getting a new charge because someone remains prone while the difficulty is enhanced. Why does the charge form? Or does that really matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Thunder Crash</span></b><br /> Cost: 5m, 3+ Shock Charges Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Stunning Strike<br /> <br /> Thunder resounds and with a deafening crash it brings even the mighty low. Thunder Crash creates a Decisive attack that expends at least 3 shock charges. If the target is not prone, on a successful hit, the target is automatically knocked prone and the difficulty to stand up in increased by 3 for 1 round. If the target is already prone, the target has no choice but to remain prone for their next action and cannot even attempt to stand.<br /> <br /> If Bolt Lash has extra shock charges in excess of the cost, they may be expended to convert up to (extra expended charges) extra successes on the attack roll into damage dice on the damage roll. </div> </div> </div>And keep them down forever! Keeping a good flow from one to the next. My only question is about the effect against a Not-Prone: why not say &quot;their first attempt to stand after this attack&quot;? Were you interested more in the idea that the thunder crash wears off naturally after that duration?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\">Lightning Arc</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Cost: 5m, 1wp, 5 Shock Charges Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual, Perilous<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Thunder Crash<br /> <br /> Suffusing the whip with the fury of the sky, the weapon transforms into a solid bolt of lightning which twitches and arcs from nearby surfaces. This grants a variety of effects to Bolt Lash.</span>[/FONT][/SIZE]<ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bolt Lash may extend to attack foes up to Short range. Additionally, prone foes at Short range are considered embattled with the exalt for all purposes</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The white-hot light of the whip is searing, doubling threshold successes on Witheringattack rolls for purposes of determining damage</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Disarm gambits that utilize Bolt Lash gain 1 automatic success</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Decisive Savaging attacks against foes that are grappled by Bolt Lash gain 2 extra dice of damage</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Stealth is rendered impossible for the wielder of Bolt Lash for the duration of Lightning Arc</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This evocation lasts until the end of the scene or until the exalt is Crashed.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I like the inclusion of the 1wp cost--feels thematically appropriate for someone trying to bend genuine lightning to her will. All of the effects also fit well with what coursing lightning would do. I can't really think of any suggestions. My first thought was that this felt more like the start of a second branch after Shock Thrash, as it doesn't seem to particularly <i>need</i> the other two evocations in the same way they have subsequently needed the one before. It's certainly the most potent stand-alone, but rather than feeling like a final culmination of the abilities before, it feels only like reaching the &quot;pure&quot; form lying within the metals--still finale-esq, but not in such a way that it wraps the package together. Of course, this isn't a necessity by any means, I'd imagine--just an opinion to consider!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T17:43:01-07:00","id":906838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906831#post906831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I didn't really feel qualified to try, but I suppose this is a workshop!</div> </div> </div> </div>All feedback is appreciated, especially from untrained eyes! Worst case scenario, that's how <i>you</i> learn to become trained! And someone we end up looking at stuff we know so long, we miss the obvious problem in front of our face. Happens to me all the time. So someone without that bias is good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906831#post906831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the story-context for this thing, and combining blue and white in this way is an awesome concept. I even like the consequence of leaving it unattuned--fits well within its creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906831#post906831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first thought was this seemed really weak--and then I kept reading...</div> </div> </div> </div> This is becoming one of the more difficult sections to invent for me anymore. I find myself coming back and redoing it after I've made my evocation tree, so I can tie it in with the theme of my tree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906831#post906831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is an unstoppable build-up, then? So long as the user spends 1m per turn, regardless of either the success of the strike or the success of the prone-roll, they'll have full charges within 5 rounds, and the difficulty of the prone-roll increases each and every time, up to 6, with no chance of error.<br /> <br /> Part of me feels like charges should be expended to increase the difficulty (on a 1-to-1 basis), but I've <b><i>also</i></b> come to realize over the past week or so that my idea of &quot;too strong&quot; is actually way off. I'd like to hear your reasoning all the same--might help me better understand!</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience with the game is that it's actually kind of unusual to have a combat last more than 3-4 rounds. It can happen, but few do. So anything that makes you build up over time is limiting. That said, this is supplemental, so CAN be used on multi-attack charms to build up faster.<br /> <br /> This being the intro evocation, it is the foundation for everything else. If the charges had to be spent to get the benefit, there would be little desire to use this, even with the future stuff building off of it. And honestly, this evocation is somewhat weak. The average Sta+Res roll for a foe any given ST puts you against is probably going to be 5 or 6. Anyone lower isn't really worth putting this weapon's special effort into, and anyone higher will require a lot of activations of this evocation to get any benefit out of. So it's a small passive benefit at a cheap cost, and it doesn't screw you later to utilize this benefit. But it's not particularly overpowering. Most foes will probably hit a difficulty 2 or 3 most of the time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906831#post906831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knock them down, then keep them down. Fits the theme and works mechanically pretty well, I'd imagine--though I kind of tilt my head at getting a new charge because someone remains prone while the difficulty is enhanced. Why does the charge form? Or does that really matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding the charge was honestly an afterthought. I wanted more than one way to gain charges so it's not a useless weapon in a 3 round fight. Thematically, it doesn't really matter, though I kind of think of it as stealing their effort to power the weapon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906831#post906831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And keep them down forever! Keeping a good flow from one to the next. My only question is about the effect against a Not-Prone: why not say &quot;their first attempt to stand after this attack&quot;? Were you interested more in the idea that the thunder crash wears off naturally after that duration?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I assumed anyone prone (who's not a tiger stylist) is going to try to stand any given chance they can if they're not standing. It's not a big difference, but this is only an Essence 2 evocation, so I didn't want it to be TOO strong. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906831#post906831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the inclusion of the 1wp cost--feels thematically appropriate for someone trying to bend genuine lightning to her will. All of the effects also fit well with what coursing lightning would do. I can't really think of any suggestions. My first thought was that this felt more like the start of a second branch after Shock Thrash, as it doesn't seem to particularly <i>need</i> the other two evocations in the same way they have subsequently needed the one before. It's certainly the most potent stand-alone, but rather than feeling like a final culmination of the abilities before, it feels only like reaching the &quot;pure&quot; form lying within the metals--still finale-esq, but not in such a way that it wraps the package together. Of course, this isn't a necessity by any means, I'd imagine--just an opinion to consider!</div> </div> </div> </div>Originally, this tree stopped at Thunder Crash, but as a point of personal aesthetic preference, I hate ending Evocation trees at Essence 2. 3 Is a really nice stopping point to me, so I try to scale things up. However, neither of my first two evocations made sense at 2, and I was tired of writing Essence 3 Decisive Attack capstones (a LOT of my weapons have those). So I tried to come up with something else. I hadn't done a form in a long time, so I went with that direction. I agree, it's a little out of place with the rest, but that's largely because it was an afterthought. I came up with the first and third evocations in a 5 minute conversation with my friend who needed the weapon. I came up with 2 and 4 today at work while bored.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback! It is appreciated!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:05:26-07:00","id":906855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=906838#post906838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My experience with the game is that it's actually kind of unusual to have a combat last more than 3-4 rounds. It can happen, but few do. So anything that makes you build up over time is limiting. That said, this is supplemental, so CAN be used on multi-attack charms to build up faster.<br /> <br /> This being the intro evocation, it is the foundation for everything else. If the charges had to be spent to get the benefit, there would be little desire to use this, even with the future stuff building off of it. And honestly, this evocation is somewhat weak. The average Sta+Res roll for a foe any given ST puts you against is probably going to be 5 or 6. Anyone lower isn't really worth putting this weapon's special effort into, and anyone higher will require a lot of activations of this evocation to get any benefit out of. So it's a small passive benefit at a cheap cost, and it doesn't screw you later to utilize this benefit. But it's not particularly overpowering. Most foes will probably hit a difficulty 2 or 3 most of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, I hadn't taken the brevity of typical combat and general enemy sturdiness into account--I tend to play glass-cannons with more Dex and Dodge than Stam and Resist, respectively. Perception bias, ho!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Adding the charge was honestly an afterthought. I wanted more than one way to gain charges so it's not a useless weapon in a 3 round fight. Thematically, it doesn't really matter, though I kind of think of it as stealing their effort to power the weapon. </div> </div> </div>I can get behind the &quot;stealing power&quot; concept--the wasted kinetic effort being siphoned away as electric energy. Definitely keep it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Originally, this tree stopped at Thunder Crash, but as a point of personal aesthetic preference, I hate ending Evocation trees at Essence 2. 3 Is a really nice stopping point to me, so I try to scale things up. However, neither of my first two evocations made sense at 2, and I was tired of writing Essence 3 Decisive Attack capstones (a LOT of my weapons have those). So I tried to come up with something else. I hadn't done a form in a long time, so I went with that direction. I agree, it's a little out of place with the rest, but that's largely because it was an afterthought. I came up with the first and third evocations in a 5 minute conversation with my friend who needed the weapon. I came up with 2 and 4 today at work while bored. </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I wouldn't call it out of place so much as a new branch of power--I read it and immediately sort of imagined the old Allegory of the Cave, wherein the whip itself is just the closest human approximation and the form-shift is the weapon attaining its truest essence. And for those few battles that drag on to that point, it really marks a turning point of power.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T05:53:46-07:00","id":907071,"title":"","content":"So this is actually my first attempt at making an artifact wholecloth. Feedback would be welcome.<br /> <br /> <i>Rambling bullshit I can\u2019t actually call \u201edesign intent\u201d with a straight face</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Remember the first Evocation update on Kickstarter? The one with the huge-ass, sprawling Evocation tree for Volcano Cutter? While I definitely think the new, pared-down designs are much more helpful in narrowing down and really accentuating the themes and characters of individual artifacts, I couldn\u2019t help but feel disappointed that the Evocation named <i>Bones and Hope to Ashes and Flame</i> couldn\u2019t make it to the final product. This Artifact is basically my way of rectifying that. However, I felt that the original name was a bit overblown; I also thought that soulsteel-jade alloys are surprisingly underutilized, and an artifact whose shtick is literally turning hope to ash is Abyssal as fuck. Thus, Pyre-Kindler was born.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe ***)</b><br /> <br /> <b>History</b><br /> The siege of Thorns was a bloody and brutal affair. Each hour seemed to birth new horrors, and the ragged remnants of the city\u2019s defenders were forced to give ground again and again, until there was nowhere left to fall back to. At this moment, when all seemed lost, a lone Dragon-Blooded hero awoke the long-slumbering spirit of her daiklave Hope\u2019s Gleam Eternal, rallied her broken comrades, and prepared for a desperate last stand. Empowered by the newly forged bond between wielder and weapon, she and her companions tore through the ranks of the dead, drove back the teeming hordes, and eventually reached the towering corpse-flesh throne of the Deathlord himself. There, she spat a defiant challenge at the Mask of Winters, mocking the sorcerer-king for hiding behind the walls of his rotting cage, and daring him to engage her in single combat.<br /> Her request was granted. The Deathlord came crashing down wreathed in darkness, his visage akin to some perverse cthonic reflection of a falling star. There they clashed at the feet of the Juggernaut; seething fury strained against deathly chill, fervent blows fueled by anger and loss were turned away by calculating strokes perfected through millennia of practice. Three times did their blades meet, and with each strike, the necromancer grew more terrifying to behold in his grave-born majesty \u2013 but her resolve did not waver, not even in her last moment, when the Mask of Winters\u2019 final blow sundered her blade apart and cleft her body in twain. The last Dragon-Blooded defender of the city fell unbroken.<br /> At least this is how the Midnight Caste, Exultant Dirge Echoed Sevenfold, told her story before asking his audience \u2013 a gathering of the city\u2019s greatest artists, poets and philosophers, living or dead \u2013 to commemorate her passing. Some of them showed an appreciation for the star-crossed romance in the futility of her struggle; judging them worthy and enlightened souls, the Abyssal granted them the privilege of becoming a part of his design.<br /> For four days and nights he worked without stopping, while reciting the poems, eulogies and songs \u2013 their creators\u2019 last compositions, for they were now being worked on the anvil, along with the shards of the broken blade \u2013 and it is said that the living and the dead wept alike during this time, not for the families and friends they lost, nor for their city that turned into a death-tainted shadow of the home they once had, but for that nameless, fallen Dragon-Blooded hero. Such was the heart-rending beauty of his performance that when the first rays of light broke on the fifth day, when the ringing of his anvil ceased and he finally fell silent, even the Juggernaut shed a single tear the size of a house. The Midnight plunged the white-hot blade into it as it fell, evaporating it entirely and covering the neighborhood in a mist that hasn\u2019t lifted ever since; and at that moment, Pyre-Kindler was born.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b><br /> The blade of this massive grimscythe is made from a single piece of red jade with razor-thin cracks running through its entire length, while the haft is black soulsteel, with streaks of red jade worked into the metal. Occasionally \u2013 mostly at dusk, when the dying embers of sunlight grace the weapon at <i>just</i> the right angle \u2013 faces can be glimpsed within the jet-colored alloy; whether their mouths gape open in tortured screams or worshipful ecstasy, hard to say.<br /> Pyre-Kindler features a single hearthstone socket where the haft meets the blade.<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement</b><br /> Whenever a Solar or Abyssal who\u2019s attuned to Pyre-Kindler crashes an opponent, she may forego the bonus Initiative gained from Initiative Break, and gain 5 motes instead. These motes are stored in Pyre-Kindler and are lost at the end of the scene, or if the wielder\u2019s attunement is broken. Motes stored in Pyre-Kindler can only be spent on Charms that enhance or create social actions taken to erode positive Intimacies towards Creation or the living, to instill or strengthen Intimacies based on accepting or exulting in death, or to persuade targets exploiting Intimacies of fatalism or death-seeking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Pyre-Kindler</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Light the Pyre</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 6m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Psyche<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> The fiery Essence of this weapon does not awaken lightly; only death can rouse its flames. However, when it does, it\u2019s a terrifying sight to behold, leaving only ashes and broken spirits in its wake.<br /> Whenever the wielder reduces a significant opponent to Incapacitated, she can activate this Evocation to consign the body to the flames of Pyre-Kindler, instantly burning it to cinders. Treat this as a Charisma+Presence-based instill action to evoke fear, hopelessness, acceptance towards the inevitability of death, or a similarly appropriate Intimacy in all onlookers, made without the usual penalties for multiple targets (and silent communication, should the character offer no commentary). Moreover, those who held a positive Intimacy to the deceased increase the Willpower cost of rejecting this influence by one.<br /> Motes spent on enhancing the triggering attack reduce the cost of this Evocation on a two-for-one basis, potentially even reducing it to zero.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Passion-Scouring Persuasion</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1+m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> Pyre-Kindler is an artifact forged from the souls of Thorns\u2019 greatest artists, poets and rhetoricians. It can lend its weight not just to the blows, but also to the statements of its wielder \u2013 albeit the weapon\u2019s grim outlook makes it better suited to certain lines of argument than others.<br /> Passion-Scouring Persuasion can be used to enhance a social influence action placed in a flurry with an attack from Pyre-Kindler. Resolve the attack first; if it hits, the wielder may spend motes to remove flurry penalties from her social influence roll on a one-for-one basis. This Evocation can be activated to enhance social actions intended to weaken Intimacies towards Creation or the living, or strengthen Intimacies of hopelessness or fatalism even if the accompanying attack misses; if it hits, such influence gains an automatic success.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hope-to-Ash Ignition</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-only, Psyche<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Light the Pyre, Passion-Scouring Persuasion<br /> <br /> Thorns\u2019 last Dragon-Blooded fought valiantly, but in the end, her struggles were futile. Her body, her weapon and her city were broken alike. Seeing the same hope and passion in another causes Pyre-Kindler to lash out with the intent to burn it all away: the weapon almost seems to swing with a will of its own, surrounded by a corona of flame.<br /> Hope-to-Ash Ignition is a <b>decisive</b> attack that adds [Intimacy's strength] extra dice to its damage roll if the target holds a positive Intimacy that can be considered passionate or hopeful; however, they can voluntarily reduce the strength of the Intimacy in question to reduce the damage accordingly. If multiple Intimacies satisfy the criteria, only the strongest counts. In case of ties, if the wielder is aware of the Intimacies in question, she may choose which one to target; otherwise, the victim chooses.<br /> <b>Special activation rules</b>: Hope-to-Ash Ignition can't be used twice in the same fight, unless reset by instilling a major or defining Intimacy of grim fatalism in the original target or one of his allies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Life\u2019s Vexations Seared Away</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1wp; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Stackable, Psyche<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Hope-to-Ash Ignition<br /> <br /> The ultimate expression of Pyre-Kindler\u2019s spirit and the chivalry of death, the flames of this Evocation burn away not the flesh of its victim, but the ties that bind him to the land of the living, allowing him to experience the peace of the grave and be reborn enlightened.<br /> When the wielder reduces an opponent to Incapacitated with its prerequisite, she may activate this Evocation to cause the target to immediately stabilize. For every level of Health damage that would\u2019ve taken the victim beyond Incapacitated, she may reduce the intensity of an Intimacy that ties the target to Creation or the living by one step; she\u2019s explicitly permitted to reduce any Intimacy by multiple steps as long as the excess damage allows her to do so. Upon activating Life\u2019s Vexations Seared Away, the wielder immediately becomes aware of every viable target Intimacy for its effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 06-20-2016, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:23:06-07:00","id":907132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe ***)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Oooo, excellent material combination. I agree, not enough of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Attunement</b><br /> Whenever a Solar or Abyssal who\u2019s attuned to Pyre-Kindler crashes an opponent, she may forego the bonus Initiative gained from Initiative Break, and gain 5 motes instead. These motes are stored in Pyre-Kindler and are lost at the end of the scene, or if the wielder\u2019s attunement is broken. Motes stored in Pyre-Kindler can only be spent on Charms that enhance or create social actions taken to erode positive Intimacies towards Creation or the living, to instill or strengthen Intimacies based on accepting or exulting in death, or to persuade targets exploiting Intimacies of fatalism or death-seeking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good attunement bonus. Feeds the rest of the weapon well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Light the Pyre</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 6m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Psyche<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> The fiery Essence of this weapon does not awaken lightly; only death can rouse its flames. However, when it does, it\u2019s a terrifying sight to behold, leaving only ashes and broken spirits in its wake.<br /> Whenever the wielder reduces a significant opponent to Incapacitated, she can activate this Evocation to consign the body to the flames of Pyre-Kindler, instantly burning it to cinders. Treat this as a Charisma+Presence-based instill action to evoke fear, hopelessness, acceptance towards the inevitability of death, or a similarly appropriate Intimacy in all onlookers, made without the usual penalties for multiple targets (and silent communication, should the character offer no commentary). Moreover, those who held a positive Intimacy to the deceased increase the Willpower cost of rejecting this influence by one.<br /> An Abyssal may alternatively fuel this Evocation by channeling the deathly essence of his anima through the weapon, subtracting two motes from the cost per level of anima shed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. An excellent opening evocation. While I know what you were going for, I would clarify this text to say that when the wielder uses Pyre-Kindler to reduce a significant opponent to Incap. The reason for interjecting what's doing the damage is to make sure no one can insta-kill someone they've knocked to Incap with Bashing, which should be unconscious, not dead. In truth, it should probably say &quot;least lethal health level&quot; but putting the name in is probably enough.<br /> <br /> Any reason you didn't let DBs use this weapon? It has Jade in it. That's hardly a hard rule, I'm just curious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Passion-Scouring Persuasion</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1+m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> Pyre-Kindler is an artifact forged from the souls of Thorns\u2019 greatest artists, poets and rhetoricians. It can lend its weight not just to the blows, but also to the statements of its wielder \u2013 albeit the weapon\u2019s grim outlook makes it better suited to certain lines of argument than others.<br /> Passion-Scouring Persuasion can be used to enhance a social influence action placed in a flurry with an attack from Pyre-Kindler. Resolve the attack first; if it hits, the wielder may spend motes to remove flurry penalties from her social influence roll on a one-for-one basis. This Evocation can be activated to enhance social actions intended to weaken Intimacies towards Creation or the living, or strengthen Intimacies of hopelessness or fatalism even if the accompanying attack misses; if it hits, such influence gains an automatic success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems fine to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hope-to-Ash Ignition</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-only, Psyche<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Light the Pyre, Passion-Scouring Persuasion<br /> <br /> Thorns\u2019 last Dragon-Blooded fought valiantly, but in the end, her struggles were futile. Her body, her weapon and her city were broken alike. Seeing the same hope and passion in another causes Pyre-Kindler to lash out with the intent to burn it all away: the weapon almost seems to swing with a will of its own, surrounded by a corona of flame.<br /> If the target of this attack holds a positive Intimacy that can be considered passionate or hopeful, they take (Intimacy's strength) extra dice of damage; however, they can voluntarily reduce the strength of the Intimacy in question to reduce the damage accordingly. If multiple Intimacies satisfy the criteria, only the strongest counts. In case of ties, if the wielder is aware of the Intimacies in question, she may choose which one to target; otherwise, the victim chooses.<br /> <b>Special activation rules</b>: Hope-to-Ash Ignition can't be used twice in the same fight, unless reset by instilling a major or defining Intimacy of grim fatalism in the original target or one of his allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, I was going to put this comment at the end, but there's a step missing in a few of your social mechanics. Almost every weapon that has an effect against an Intimacy someone holds requires you to <i>learn</i> of that Intimacy first. It shouldn't auto-target, you should have to spend the effort &quot;charm, evocation, or normal&quot; to Read Intentions to figure it out. Now this isn't as necessary when everything is build on Creating an Intimacy like in your first Evocation. But even that and the second one mention eroding one and you give no abilities in here to learn them, nor do you even mention that it's required. <br /> <br /> Then we get to Hope-to-Ash Ignition, which even mentions that it auto-targets because it has different benefits based on whether the wielder knows the Intimacy. I can't personally get behind that. I feel you should have to learn it first. OTHERWISE, I think this is a good evocation. Although I'd mention that it &quot;adds (Intimacy's strength) extra dice to the damage roll&quot; so there's no confusion that it's not auto-damage, it's based on the Decisive attack (if I'm reading you right).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Life\u2019s Vexations Seared Away</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1wp; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Stackable, Psyche<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Hope-to-Ash Ignition<br /> <br /> The ultimate expression of Pyre-Kindler\u2019s spirit and the chivalry of death, the flames of this Evocation burn away not the flesh of its victim, but the ties that bind him to the land of the living, allowing him to experience the peace of the grave and be reborn enlightened.<br /> When the wielder reduces an opponent to Incapacitated with its prerequisite, she may activate this Evocation to cause the target to immediately stabilize. For every level of Health damage that would\u2019ve taken the victim beyond Incapacitated, she may reduce the intensity of an Intimacy that ties the target to Creation or the living by one step; she\u2019s explicitly permitted to reduce any Intimacy by multiple steps as long as the excess damage allows her to do so. Upon activating Life\u2019s Vexations Seared Away, the wielder immediately becomes aware of every viable target Intimacy for its effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, THAT'S an interesting effect. Kind of nullifies the first evocation, but still very in theme. Aside from what I mentioned above about learning someone's Intimacies, I'm gonna call this one cool imo. <br /> <br /> Overall, a very consistent theme. Evocations build on each other and are sure to make a nihilist out of anyone you... don't want to kill. I guess you'd use this to drive someone mad or maybe hope to make them loyal to the Underworld? Still very cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:40:08-07:00","id":907136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907132#post907132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, I was going to put this comment at the end, but there's a step missing in a few of your social mechanics. Almost every weapon that has an effect against an Intimacy someone holds requires you to <i>learn</i> of that Intimacy first. It shouldn't auto-target, you should have to spend the effort &quot;charm, evocation, or normal&quot; to Read Intentions to figure it out. Now this isn't as necessary when everything is build on Creating an Intimacy like in your first Evocation. But even that and the second one mention eroding one and you give no abilities in here to learn them, nor do you even mention that it's required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the second one enhances a normal instill action taken to erode an Intimacy, and is therefore subject to the standard rules governing them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907132#post907132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then we get to Hope-to-Ash Ignition, which even mentions that it auto-targets because it has different benefits based on whether the wielder knows the Intimacy. I can't personally get behind that. I feel you should have to learn it first.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I see it, it comes with a high enough cost (5 motes, a reset condition, and effectively locking you out of your capstone if you blow it in an untimely manner) to discourage gambling. Also, I wanted to support characters with crappy Socialize scores whose players can still make educated guesses based on the behavior of the NPCs in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907132#post907132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I'd mention that it &quot;adds (Intimacy's strength) extra dice to the damage roll&quot; so there's no confusion that it's not auto-damage, it's based on the Decisive attack (if I'm reading you right).</div> </div> </div> </div>You absolutely are, and I'm going to edit it accordingly.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907132#post907132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, THAT'S an interesting effect. Kind of nullifies the first evocation, but still very in theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Pyre-Kindler's ideal game plan is to go in, burn somebody down to their last health levels, then finish them off with a big decisive enhanced by Hope-to-Ash Ignition, which procs Life's Vexations Seared Away hopefully with enough health levels of excess damage to be able to tear down <i>all</i> of their relevant Intimacies.<br /> <br /> The attunement effect is intended to help you avoid an accidental early overkill (&quot;meh, I bet they have a bunch of Ox-Bodies, let's chuck a 20-Initiative decisive at them and keep Hope-to-Ash Ignition on hold for now&quot; &quot;SPLAT&quot; &quot;Oops&quot;) in addition to giving you free motes. LtP's role partially comes in as a consolation prize if you screw up (&quot;well, you didn't manage to turn your guy into Death Buddha, but at least everybody around is <i>super</i> impressed now&quot;); but it's also meant to help you reset Hope-to-Ash Ignition by either creating a Minor Intimacy of fatalism, or giving you a supporting Intimacy you can use to strengthen an Intimacy of fatalism you created through normal means.<br /> <br /> So, all in all, the intention for it is to support the capstone, not to be obviated by it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907132#post907132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall, a very consistent theme. Evocations build on each other and are sure to make a nihilist out of anyone you... don't want to kill. I guess you'd use this to drive someone mad or maybe hope to make them loyal to the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its primary use case is indeed your archetypal Midnight preacher demonstrating the fundamental meaninglessness of life, but Vexations is intentionally worded in a way that makes it useful in pretty much any situation where you'd want to commit impromptu neuro-surgery with a giant flaming scythe (at least in most games, antagonists tend to have motivations that stem from attachments related to Creation or the living, all of which can be burned away by the kiss of Pyre-Kindler).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":".  Edited to explain the point of the capstone and how the first Evocation relates to it. 06-04-2016, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:48:59-07:00","id":907141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907136#post907136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the second one enhances a normal instill action taken to erode an Intimacy, and is therefore subject to the standard rules governing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah forget my commentary on the 2nd one. I'm still groggy today. 2nd one is fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907136#post907136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, it comes with a high enough cost (5 motes, a reset condition, and effectively locking you out of your capstone if you blow it in an untimely manner) to discourage gambling. Also, I wanted to support characters with crappy Socialize scores whose players can still make educated guesses based on the behavior of the NPCs in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're trying to do, but if it's auto-targetting intimacies the player doesn't know about then it's the only thing in the game that does that. It's your weapon and your table, so I'm not gonna say you're doing it wrong, but my feedback is that it's too strong if you allow that. My 2 cents.<br /> <br /> Don't take that as a criticism of the whole thing though. I love this weapon a lot and I'd probably take it to my table with the small tweak to that third evocation. It's great stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:53:47-07:00","id":907145,"title":"","content":"I could really use feed back on this artifact. Please pick apart and find any mechanical flaws.<br /> <br /> Lion's Pride<br /> Artifact 4 lightning glass and Oricalcum Reaper Daiklave.<br /> <br /> Long ago in the Shogunate there lived an exigent named The Lion of Nobel Causes, or just the Lion. He was the exigent of a god of duels, but no one knows which any more and his legend has suffered and most records of him were destroyed in the great contagion.<br /> <br /> What is known of him is he founded the nation of Valosia, was the sire of the royal bloodline, and that he also fathered a lot of children among the peasants. This has lead to some theories that he was chosen of the God of romantic duels and lovers quarrel.<br /> <br /> The Lion is even said to have dueled the empress, back when she was a private. There are many theories on what the duel was over. Some say she tripped while emptying her commanders chamber pot and spilled the contents upon him. Others say they dueled for the company of a pretty youth. Most hold that the duel was over the withholding of an apology.<br /> <br /> Lion's pride holds up its first master's sense of honor this blade was forged to fight duels. The blade will only a tune to those with a principal to a code of honor or dueling code. As well they are required to have a tie of love or devotion to [ST chosen group that fits]<br /> <br /> Evocations of Lion's Pride<br /> When an atuned weilder drops a target to an initiative less than their own with an attack made with Lion's Pride they may spend 1m to take a reflexive aim action to strike with the speed of lighting at the opening they have created.<br /> <br /> Brilliant Stroke<br /> Cost: 2m, Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Withering - Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> With a shocking effect the lightning glass unleashes a discharge into a foe who was just crashed to slow their thoughts, and confuse the muscles. The struck foe must pass a stamina + resistance check against a duration equal to 1+the value of the Principal used to power this weapon. That foe suffers a penalty to all actions equal to the value of the intimacy of love that powers the blade, and a defense penalty equal to the half that value for the resisted duration.<br /> <br /> Roaring Counter Attack<br /> Cost: 4m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only, Counter Attack<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> With a peel and a crash like a lion falling open it's foe Lion's Pride reacts to it's owner's deflection of an attack and rewards them with an opening to launch a quick counter attack. The blade crackling with power of passion as the Orichalcum glows with pulse and sync to the honor in it's welder's heart. This charm creates a counter attack in response to an attack that the weirder has successfully parried. The user may add double 9's up to the value of the principal to Dueling to the attack roll, and add damage equal to the value of the empowering tie.<br /> <br /> Lone Predator Challenge<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence: 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisite: Roaring Counter Attack<br /> <br /> The enemies of The Lion were many, but those nobel enough or brave enough to face him alone often fond themselves outmatched. Issuing a challenge, the user rolls (Charisma + Presence + the empowering Principal) against the resolve of all enemies. If he succeeds, then they gain a Major Tie to Honorable Duels. The enemies may then choose one among them to go first, as long as the Solar does not cheat and the fight remains a duel, then any other enemy with the Intimacy takes a penalty equal the the empowering Principal on attacks against the Exalt. The chosen opponent takes the same penalty on rolls to Withdraw or Disengage or fight someone beside the Exalt, or benefit from another cheating on their behalf. Until the elected enemy is defeated (or yields) the other enemies may circle, taunt, and push combatants back into the fight. The exalts enemy as a part of the activation of this charm may select if the duel is to first blood, or to the death at the start of it.<br /> <br /> These effects may be ignored if the target pays a Willpower, but if the foe chosen to face him spends this willpower then the user gains a bonus die to all attacks until the end of the scene that does not count as a die from charms.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: This evocation is awoken automatically after the Exalt faces a battle group or wins the affections of one in the bedroom.<br /> <br /> Satisfaction of Honor<br /> Cost 8m, 1bhl, 1wp: Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: 1 Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Lone Predator Challenge<br /> Summoning the swift power of the lightning strike and the motivating power of love this weapon burns with great power in a fearsome mean that elevates it above all it's brethren bringing with it devastating power. For the remainder of the scene attack rolls reroll up to the empowering principal in failed dice. If any number of enemies are in short range of the target who resisted Lone Predator Challenge then lightning arcs from the target to these dishonorable wretches creating an unblock able attack with the same number of successes as the first attack, dealing levels of damage equal to the empowering tie. If the target themselves resisted the Challenge then this damage is increased by essence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 06-04-2016, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:35:00-07:00","id":907167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907132#post907132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any reason you didn't let DBs use this weapon? It has Jade in it. That's hardly a hard rule, I'm just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't believe I edited comments about the third Evocation in my original response post and forgot about this one.<br /> <br /> Well, mechanically, I think the attunement bonus is certainly <i>nice</i>, but non-essential to the Artifact's function. Fluffwise, I think the blade is, in a sense, heartbroken about its last wielder; being held by a Dragon-Blooded causes it to recall the trauma of getting violently sundered apart, which is, for lack of a better word, distressing to it to the extent of preventing it from responding to their elemental nature.<br /> <br /> If a player came to me with &quot;this is super cool and I want to play a Dragon-Blooded who eventually manages to overcome this effect and forge a new connection with the weapon, maybe even drawing out fragments of its original nature&quot;, I'd obviously allow them to do so. Maybe ask them to commit two additional motes until some story event restores their connection.<br /> <br /> <br /> Btw. I'd also appreciate comments about the fluffy bits; this was also my first attempt at trying to write in the tone associated with Exalted, and English not being my first language, I can't accurately gauge how successful it's been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T10:47:10-07:00","id":907178,"title":"","content":"<b>The Yozi Little Red ball of Elsewhere (Artfact ***)</b><br /> <br /> This Small red ball that has been see going around Mafias. Demons enjoy his ball so much for it fendish abilities. This ball was created by some unknown demon who was sick and tired of people summoning him for things he could not do like &quot; I want to be young forever &quot; or &quot; Make me Immortal &quot;. <br /> <br /> The Yozi Little Red Ball can only be activated by a Yozi demon. The demon need only spend a single mote and then toss or give the ball to the intended target. Once the target takes the ball *Poof* they disappear. The person who vanishes is transported into elsewhere. The only way the subject can return is if the ball is reactavited in the same mannor as it was orginal used. This means who ever was sent to elsewhere returns to where they left and the new person takes there place. This only works on Exalted and Mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T11:21:04-07:00","id":907201,"title":"","content":"New, much (I hope) improved version of my Shotstaff artifact. Changed a lot of Evocations, reformed it into Melee weapon with Summoner style. Pretty much new Artifact.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental Heart (*****)</b><br /> Different than many wonders, the powers of Elemental Heart do not come from ancient legacy or power of its past wielders. It was forged only recently, by one lone Twilight girl living in her manse, ancient and powerful spirit guardians of Solar long gone her only friends.<br /> When she was cast into raging waves of ocean, it was supposed to be her end \u2013 but Fate is not always right. Terrified she was, she still cling to her life and somehow survived to land on island too small to be shown on any map of the West \u2013 but one housing powerful manse of long-gone golden king. Small as she was, only eight years old, she was able to outsmart and befriend ancient elemental spirits tied to the place \u2013 and then solve and overcome defense systems protecting manse itself. It was then as she draw Second Breath and become new master of the place \u2013 new Children of Twilight. Friend to elementals tied to the place and lady over manse itself, she was safe there.<br /> In years to come, she learned a lot. She studied ancient arts of channeling essences and creating wonders. She had read more books than most people ever see in their lives. She initiated herself into Sorcerous arts. But it was not enough to sate her thirst for knowledge. She wanted, no... needed to travel the world, to understand it and use her knowledge to help others... but also expand what she knew. But she knew about dangers of the world \u2013 and that she would need to protect herself. There were weapons in manse \u2013 old ones, powerful blades used by ancient warriors of tales long forgotten \u2013 but she didn\u2019t know how to wield them. So she did what true Copper Spiders did best \u2013 she took materials she had, ancient pile of raw orichalcum and starmetal stored in manse and asked her friends for help. Each of them have given two gifts \u2013gift of power, to fight for things dear to her and gift of defense, to protect her from harm in her travels. And then, using her own mastery and powers given to her by them she forged new weapon \u2013 her own legacy that will protect her in years to come, in her travels to the end of the known world.<br /> <br /> Elemental Heart at first glance seems to be perfectly crafted orichalcum wrackstaff, with beautifully carved motifs of four elementals and poetry written in Old Realm symbols. Carvings of elementals are inlaid with corresponding jade colors - black, blue, red and white, while ends of the staff were given Starmetal bands. While the weapon can be used as simple wrackstaff, its true power lies deeper, in the core of the staff. There, inside the indestructible orichalcum lie masterfully forged channels for Essence that move mystical force of wielder and join them with elemental powers of Creation, channeled through elemental guardians \u2013 claw of each one of them was composed into the staff.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Elemental Heart:</b><br /> Special rules: Characters with Lore or Occult Supernal treats all Evocations of Elemental Heart as her Supernal Charms for purpose of qualifying for prerequisite and experience costs (which means she can learn them at Essence 1 for 8 experience points each). When character attunes to Elemental Heart she gains Essence of Blaster and Essence of Summoner Evocations for free.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence of Blaster: </b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp ; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> Knowing the power of Elements lying in her weapon, young Twilight learned to target her weapon not by eye, but with elements of Creation. As she struck the air, her weapon blow moved upon Essence to hit enemies. This attacks emanate as powerful Essence blasts, hitting her enemies and stopping them in their tracks.<br /> The Solar is capable of making Melee attacks up to Short range by hitting her enemies with blast of Essence instead of weapon itself. She can also attack enemies at medium range if she takes Aim action first. Attacks made further than close range do not add Solar Strength to damage. This effect cannot be used for counterattacks if they are done from further than close range. When combined with Iron Raptor Technique this Evocation allows attacking enemies at long range without Aim action.<br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> This Evocation awakens at no cost when wielder of the Elemental Heart attunes to her weapon.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence of Summoner: </b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> Knowing the power of Elements lying in her weapon, young Twilight internalized lessons of all elements.<br /> When Solar\u2019s use Evocation based on one of the Spirits who contributed to creation of her weapon, she gains special bonus until the end of her next action after this Evocation effects stops. She can have any number of bonuses active at the same time, but each of them do not stack with itself.<br /> Gaea \u2013 reduce raw damage taken by one (for both withering and decisive damage)<br /> Aquarius \u2013 add one to Character Evasion (this doesn\u2019t count as dices added by Charms)<br /> Sylphe \u2013 increase Elemental Heart accuracy by one<br /> Bloodflame \u2013 add one dice to raw damage of Withering and Decisive attacks<br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> This Evocation awakens at no cost when wielder of the Elemental Heart attunes to her weapon.<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts of Friendship: </b><br /> Cost: - ; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Essence of Summoner<br /> As the pact with Spirits was done, young Twilight learned true value of friendship. She wished that even if she would have to fight in her travels, she would be able to become friends with everyone afterwards.<br /> The user of Elemental Heart can always spare enemies hit by her Essence blasts - no Bashing damage from her attacks can injure a character further than Incapacitated. If character is spared in this way, she immediately passes out and remains unconscious until end of the Scene, when she wakes up automatically healing Incapacitated health level. When any character is rendered unconscious by this effect, both Ragin Heart\u2019s user and character rendered unconscious automatically gain minor positive Tie to each other, with context chosen by their respective players and deemed dramatically appropriate by Storyteller. This effect can be resisted at normal cost of 1 WP. If any character decides to resist, both instances are automatically resisted.<br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> This Evocation awakens at no cost when wielder of the Elemental Heart will make friendship pact with Spirits who contributed to creation of this weapon. It can also be bought normally for experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Gaea\u2019s Vestments </b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: Essence of Summoner<br /> The Earth spirit is unmoving and powerful \u2013 it was him who has given young girl protection she needed when entering giant, unknown world.<br /> This Charm creates powerful forcefield of earthen essence, which combines with user\u2019s own anima to create set of powerful mystical clothes protecting her from blows and damage. Upon this Evocation activation Solar\u2019s clothes instantly changes into dramatically appropriate garments forged from her Essence and infused with earthly defenses channeled from her Shotstaff.<br /> While this evocation is active, the Solar or her new clothes can\u2019t be hurt by light contact with normally damaging edges. Garments created by this Evocation have no Mobility Penalty, but count as Medium Armor for purposes of allowed Charms and Martial Arts styles. It has Soak of Solar\u2019s (Intelligence+Lore) and Hardness of Solar\u2019s (Intelligence). This Evocation is incompatible with other armor.<br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> This Evocation awakens at no cost when wielder of the Elemental Heart has at least Major Tie of friendship towards Spirit of Earth who contributed to creation of this weapon. It can also be bought normally for experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Gaea\u2019s Force</b><br /> Cost: 8m ; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Gaea\u2019s Vestments<br /> Calling upon the power and friendship of lesser elemental dragon of earth, the Essence inside Shotstaff thunders with pure might, Solar\u2019s attack hitting enemies with pure force of avalanche. As she attacks, phantom, barely humanoid form of stone giant erupts from her staff and giant fist follows her attack.<br /> Charm is activated after a successful withering or decisive attack made at close or short range. When used with withering attack if the attack does at least as much damage as her target\u2019s Stamina, the target is knocked down and back an entire range band. This force is sufficient to end a rush against any target.<br /> When used with decisive attack if the damage roll generates at least one success, the target is knocked prone by the force of the blast. The more damaging the blow, the more forcefully her opponent will be knocked away from her:<br /> For at least three successes, the opponent is lifted and bodily hurled into an object or surface within close range to him, hitting it with an impact equivalent to falling a short distance (see falling damage, p. 232), destroying any less-obdurate objects he collides with, such as wooden furniture.<br /> At four or more successes, the foe is knocked into an object at close range with tremendous force, or is sent sailing a remarkable distance by the force of the blow. If the former, the opponent hits a surface with force sufficient to leave cracks in a stone wall, impacting with a surface as if he had fallen from a medium distance. If the latter, the force of the blow throws him one range band back with a short-distance falling impact.<br /> At five or more successes, the foe is thrown to short range and suffers an impact like falling from a medium height.<br /> At Essence 3+, double the successes for determining the distance the victim is hurled.<br /> The player should include the environment in their stunts to enhance this Charm\u2019s effectiveness, for example aim to hurl her opponent into a spike protruding from a surface, turning the damage lethal, or knock her enemy from a rooftop, causing him to suffer a fall from a much greater distance. She cannot however affects angle at which enemy is thrown (for example, she cannot throw enemy into ceiling).<br /> <i>Comment: Everybody loves Heaven Thunder Hammer. Cost increased, effects weakened by removing Initiative gain and 7+ option, added much stronger Force Without Fire as Withering option.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Aquarius\u2019 Sphere</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: Essence of Summoner<br /> It was Water Spirit who was most afraid when young Twilight left them, knowing of dangers of the world and inexperience of their young master and friend. From his concern this Evocation was born to protect her even as she left.<br /> This Evocation creates mystical forcefield around Solar, shielding her from harm, imposing itself between her and strikes of her foes. This forcefield always takes Defend Other action when Solar is attacked, using Solar\u2019s (Intelligence+Occult) dice pool. If enemy succeed at overcoming forcefield defense this Charm loses its power for (6-Solar\u2019s Essence) actions.<br /> This Charm automatically deactivates if Solar suffers Initiative Crash.<br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> This Evocation awakens at no cost when wielder of the Elemental Heart has at least Major Tie of friendship towards Spirit of Water who contributed to creation of this weapon. It can also be bought normally for experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Aquarius\u2019 Flowing Grace</b><br /> Cost: 4m ; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Aquarius\u2019 Sphere<br /> Calling upon the power and friendship of lesser elemental dragon of water, phantom, beautiful form of translucent humanoid erupts from her staff, mirroring Solar\u2019s moves and attacking as she did.<br /> This Evocation allows the Solar to make two decisive attack rolls and choose the better of the two results for determining damage.<br /> <i>Comment: Shadow Wind Slash (however Supplemental instead of Simple), cost 2 motes more.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sylphe\u2019s Wind Shield</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One turn<br /> Prerequisites: Essence of Summoner<br /> The gift of Spirit of Air was simple \u2013 by channeling her Essence, young Twilight was able to protect herself from all what would travel though air to hurt her.<br /> Upon activation of this Evocation terrible winds start to blow around Solar, protecting her from arrows and different projectiles. Treat her as having full cover against normal ranged attacks, while attacks supported by magic (including Artifact weapons) suffer (Solar\u2019s Essence) penalties. Additionally, while this Evocation is active double Solar\u2019s movement speed.<br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> This Evocation awakens at no cost when wielder of the Elemental Heart has at least Major Tie of friendship towards Spirit of Air who contributed to creation of this weapon. It can also be bought normally for experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Sylphe\u2019s Accuracy</b><br /> Cost: 4m ; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: Sylphe\u2019s Wind Shield<br /> Calling upon the power and friendship of lesser elemental dragon of Air, phantom, beautiful form of winged humanoid erupts from her staff, helping to guide Solar\u2019s attacks.<br /> Supplemented attack ignores all penalties from visual (such as smoke, fog, and pitch darkness) and non-visual conditions such as high winds and so on.<br /> <i>Comment: There Is No Wind and Sight Without Eyes in one Charm as scene-long effect.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Bloodflame\u2019s Burning Reversal</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Clash, Dual <br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Essence of Summoner<br /> Spirit of Fire gift was as Spirit itself \u2013 powerful, deadly and decisive, calling on Spirits rage to protect young Chosen.<br /> This Evocation allows Solar to make special (Intelligence+Occult) reflexive clash attacks against enemy <b>Withering</b> or <b>Decisive</b> attacks as flames erupt from her Shotstaff in barely humanoid form and giant fist of flame moves to intercept her enemies. This does not count as the Solar\u2019s combat action. If Clashed attack was decisive, Solar\u2019s win Clash and her attack does at least three health levels of damage, the target catches on fire, and must contend with (Solar\u2019s Essence) lethal dice of damage every turn until he\u2019s able to extinguish himself. Burning enemies don\u2019t count as ongoing effect for purposes of <b>Essence of Summoner</b> effects<b>.</b><br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> This Evocation awakens at no cost when wielder of the Elemental Heart has at least Major Tie of friendship towards Spirit of Fire who contributed to creation of this weapon. It can also be bought normally for experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodflame\u2019s Power</b><br /> Cost: 3m ; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Bloodflame\u2019s Burning Reversal<br /> Calling upon the power and friendship of lesser elemental dragon of fire, the Solar\u2019s attack while barely humanoid form explodes around her and giant fist of flame follows her attacks.<br /> Through the use of this Charm, the Solar infuse her attack with fire and boosts the damage of an attack based on the distance it\u2019s made from, adding +4 dice against an enemy at close range, +3 against an enemy at short range and +1 to enemies further away. If the attack does at least three health levels of damage, the target catches on fire, and must contend with (Solar\u2019s Essence) lethal dice of damage every turn until he\u2019s able to extinguish himself.<br /> If the blast strikes flammable materials, a violent blaze instantly seeks to consume the struck object. This fire is natural, and may spread to surrounding objects or cause combustible materials to explode.<br /> <i>Comment: Weaker Phoenix Flies on Golden Wings mechanic, but with added Fiery Arrow Attack burning. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Storm of Century</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp ; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: Gaea\u2019s Force, Aquarius\u2019 Flowing Grace, Sylphe\u2019s Accuracy, Bloodflame\u2019s Power<br /> Calling upon power of all her friends, young Twilight unleashed ultimate power of four elements upon the world. As she stands in the middle of four raging elements, no enemy dares to strike her.<br /> When this Charm is active, Solar rolls (2xEssence) with tag Overwhelming (Essence) dices on each turn to inflict withering damage on all other characters within short range. This effect doesn\u2019t increase Solar Initiative. Against enemies in Initiative Crash and trivial opponents this Charm constitutes an environmental hazard (Damage (Solar\u2019s Essence+2) L/action, Difficulty (Solar\u2019s Essence+2) ) resisted with (Dexterity+Dodge). Solar may exclude every person to whom he has some positive Intimacy from suffering effects of this Charm.<br /> This Charm automatically deactivates if Solar suffers Initiative Crash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T12:51:17-07:00","id":907806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907178#post907178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Yozi Little Red ball of Elsewhere (Artfact ***)</b><br /> <br /> This Small red ball that has been see going around Mafias. Demons enjoy his ball so much for it fendish abilities. This ball was created by some unknown demon who was sick and tired of people summoning him for things he could not do like &quot; I want to be young forever &quot; or &quot; Make me Immortal &quot;.<br /> <br /> The Yozi Little Red Ball can only be activated by a Yozi demon. The demon need only spend a single mote and then toss or give the ball to the intended target. Once the target takes the ball *Poof* they disappear. The person who vanishes is transported into elsewhere. The only way the subject can return is if the ball is reactavited in the same mannor as it was orginal used. This means who ever was sent to elsewhere returns to where they left and the new person takes there place. This only works on Exalted and Mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it this could only work if the summoner failed the binding roll? If so, then it's definitely an amusing story-hook artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:22:27-07:00","id":907881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894528#post894528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Omens of the Pyre [Corona + Umbra] </span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Orichalcum, Moonsilver, and Red Jade Flame Pieces) Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 [\u2022\u2022\u2022+\u2022\u2022\u2022]</span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>After some more digging and looking at other people's artifacts, I figured I'd rework this one before it got any critique or attention. I'm more confident about the attunement bonuses and the early charms, but from <b>Dual Omens Culling</b> onward I'm unsure. Any critique, suggestions, or comments would seriously help my mindset x-x<br /> <br /> <u><b>Evocations of Omens of the Pyre</b></u><br /> Omens of the Pyre is a single pair of flame pieces, but each piece is unique in both composition and essence. The weapons innately hold compassion toward Creation\u2019s ilk and fury for Creation\u2019s enemies (henceforth defined as including raksha, demons, Abyssals, and other non-divine outsiders), but most importantly, they ache to help their wielder fulfill some righteous ideal. Either piece can work on its own as a weaker, separate artifact, but together, they form a stronger, unified front.<br /> <br /> A Solar, Lunar, or Dragon-Blooded who attunes to either piece unlocks <b>Soul Fuels Ignition</b> for free.<br /> <br /> A Solar or Lunar attuned to both who invests an extra 1 mote gains 1 non-charm die on in-combat social and damage rolls.<br /> <br /> A Dragon-Blooded attuned to both who invests an extra 1 mote gains 1 non-charm die on damage rolls.<br /> <br /> Against enemies of Creation, so long as the wielder maintains an Initiative advantage, they receive 1 additional non-charm die (to their respective bonuses).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Soul Fuels Ignition<br /> Cost:</b> 2m or 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> The devils of old converted internal power into external flame, setting their own essence ablaze to ignite the heart of their foe, and the wielder has learned this secret through the legend of her weapon. As the wielder inhales, she perceives flesh and bone as heart and soul, and in that moment of clarity she pulls the trigger, her own essence bursting forth as a bolt of golden gossamer flame that sets her victim\u2019s soul alight. In their unified burning, she can read his soul as much as her own, deducing the reason for her enemy\u2019s opposition.<br /> <br /> This evocation allows the wielder to forgo firedust, using motes of essence instead. Further, for an additional mote, her attack is enhanced with a Read Intentions action, which receives bonus dice equal to the number of extra successes on her attack roll; if successful, the primary Intimacy that drives her opponent to fight her is revealed to her in the essence-flames. She can use this multiple times, learning different Intimacies each time, going first through those most oppositional down to those benign.<br /> <br /> This affects battle groups, with the generally strongest opposing \u201cintimacy\u201d being revealed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wicked-Searing Coalescence<br /> Cost:</b> 4m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform, (Psyche)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant (One Scene)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Soul Fuels Ignition, Corona<br /> <br /> Many of Creation\u2019s foes cloak themselves in deceit and shadows, and Omens of the Pyre seeks to shine the light of the Unconquered Sun\u2019s fury upon them. As the wielder pulls the trigger and the hammer ignites the blaze, the weapon consumes the fires instantly, glowing with golden light. In that moment, divinity is channeled, and the barrel unleashes a burning ray of essence that causes even the staunchest of convictions to wither.<br /> <br /> As raw essence instead of billowing flame, the attack\u2019s possible range is increased by one band; as judgment manifest, the essence pressure weighs down upon the target, applying the user\u2019s Essence in successes on the attack roll. If successful against an enemy of Creation, this additionally inflicts a -1 penalty on all rolls for the rest of the scene, the manifest effects of divine judgment on their willfully opposing essence.<br /> <br /> Finally, if she knows the Intimacy that drives her opponent to oppose her, whether by <b>Soul Fuels Ignition</b> or other means, then the attack may double as an attempt to weaken that Intimacy by one level for the remainder of the scene (using [Charisma + Presence] as normal). This attempt receives bonus dice equal to the number of extra successes on her attack roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> This affects battle groups, affecting the generally-agreed oppositional Intimacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Villain-Revoking Lash</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Soul Fuels Ignition, Umbra<br /> <br /> <br /> Those who would openly oppose righteousness are blights on Creation, and Omens of the Pyre unveils Luna\u2019s wild contempt at their sin. The flames unleashed in this method move unnaturally, whipping around the target\u2019s hands and wrists (or whatever appendages are equipped with weapons) to sear them to the bone, preventing them from taking action against the wielder.<br /> <br /> This evocation supplements a <b>disarm</b> attempt. The attack roll enjoys her Essence in bonus dice. If successful, the target\u2019s weapon-wielding hand and wrist are burned, and he treats any actions with that hand with an off-hand penalty of -1 until it receives proper treatment. This charm explicitly allows disarming dual-wielders and applying the effects to both hands and wrists.<br /> <br /> Against enemies of Creation, the off-hand penalty is instead half the number of extra successes on the <b>Disarm Gambit</b> roll, rounded down, minimum 1.<br /> <br /> If the wielder knows her target\u2019s opposing Intimacy via <b>Soul Fuels Ignition</b> or other means, then a successful Disarm also creates an instant Instill roll to create a Minor Tie (Fearful Respect) toward the wielder. <br /> <br /> This charm can affect battle groups, under the condition that its cost increases by 2 motes for every Size category beyond 0, and a point of Willpower at Size 4 and above.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Purging God Presence<br /> Cost:</b> \u2014 (1a per bonus success, or 3m on failure); <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Dual Omens Culling<br /> <br /> As her flames burn the flesh of her foes, the wielder also burns away at their will to resist her purpose; at their lowest point, foes see her empowered conviction as raw, crushing presence. Against ordinary opponents, this presence is capable of inspiring them to atone for the immorality that brought them against her; against Creation\u2019s foes, this presence threatens to tear asunder the fabric of their existence.<br /> <br /> Should the wielder crash her target or otherwise reach an initiative advantage of 10+, her will presses down on the disadvantaged victim, enhancing a social influence roll (determined by opponent\u2019s classification according to Omens) of [Charisma+Presence+Essence] against Resolve.<ul><li>An ordinary opponent is forced to question everything that brought him against the might of the wielder. This acts as a reflexive attempt to Instill a Guilt-based Minor Tie matching the wielder\u2019s own purpose for fighting, such that he grows to sympathize with her cause; if such a tie already exists, or if <b>Villain-Revoking Lash</b> successfully instilled a tie of respect, this charm attempts to elevate it while also imparting the presence of this shared bond to both combatants in a moment of empathic union.</li> <li>Creation\u2019s foes feel as if the foundations of their lives are beginning to crumble as judgment settles upon them. If successful, the victim suffers a penalty on all actions equal to half the wielder\u2019s Essence (rounded up) for the remainder of the scene.</li> </ul><br /> If the wielder\u2019s anima banner is at the level of Iconic/Bonfire, she may instinctively convert levels of her anima into raw, overpowering presence, adding one success per level. In the event the target resists by spending Willpower, the wielder\u2019s righteous conviction may become mystically inflamed by their refusal, driven to seek retribution. For 3 motes, her next attack or influence roll against the same target within the same scene gains the strength of her opposed Intimacy in bonus dice.<br /> <br /> This ability can only reoccur on the same target if that target recovers from crash, and then crashes again due to the wielder\u2019s actions.<br /> <br /> This affects battle groups, occurring when the Magnitude track fills up and ignoring the penalty for socially targeting multiple people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prophet of Hope and Hellfire<br /> Cost:</b> 8m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous, Psyche, Aggravated<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Purging God Presence<br /> <br /> Just as valor must be balanced by temperance, so too must conviction be balanced by compassion, lest the righteous become the damned. The wielder aims at her target and ignites her eyes with the essence of her conviction such that they burn with the intensity of the sun\u2019s corona, allowing her, in a moment of searing clarity, to see the language of his conviction; by her fiery will, she reaches out to insist on surrender, and she knows the results by the stature of his soul.<br /> <br /> This charm enhances an Aim action with a Threaten action at no flurry penalty, gaining her anima level in bonus dice. Against ordinary foes, if she has instilled new Intimacies, it is instead a Persuade action playing on whichever new Intimacy is strongest, gaining the strength of the Intimacy in question in bonus dice in addition to her anima bonus; against enemies of Creation, if they have been affected by <b>Purging God Presence</b>, the Threaten roll instead gains her Essence in bonus dice in addition to her anima bonus.<br /> <br /> Should her effort completely succeed, the target finds his will to fight the wielder dwindling to nothing; he feels compelled to surrender at once and hear her out, and any temporary Intimacy effects she has caused become permanent. Should he somehow be convinced to join battle against her again in the same scene, the effects of failure immediately apply.<br /> <br /> Should her effort fail, the target perceives the coronal brilliance of her eyes turning black as the umbra of a solar eclipse, and he becomes cursed by her judgment; all Evocations henceforth treat the target as an enemy of Creation, and all her attacks on the target do aggravated damage instead of lethal, the righteous fury of wielder and weapon coming together to strike at his very soul.<br /> <br /> Should her effort fail against one who is already considered an enemy of Creation, all attacks do aggravated damage henceforth, and her next attack becomes a guaranteed success, receiving her Essence in bonus damage dice (aggravated if decisive).<br /> <br /> This affects battle groups, with her essence-sight judging the stature of their collective will.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Conflagrant Purification<br /> Cost:</b> 8m, 1wp, 1a per die; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous, Psyche, Aggravated, Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Prophet of Hope and Hellfire<br /> <br /> Judgment has been passed, and the defendant has been declared guilty of opposing Creation in the eyes of the Omens and their wielder. The punishment is a cleansing that will burn away his impurities or his life, the inferno striking beyond his physical form.<br /> <br /> This charm can only be used against one whose soul has resisted the effects of <b>Prophet of Hope and Hellfire</b>, and it supplements a <b>decisive</b> attack. However, rather burning at his body, it assaults his most oppositional Intimacy; as such, Resolve is used as a <b>Gambit difficulty</b> rather than Hardness, and it may not be enhanced using the Intimacy under assault. She may funnel the raw power of her anima into the strike, as well, gaining a bonus die for every level of flaring essence converted. Should the attack succeed at all, the Intimacy is destroyed, burned away in essence flame.<br /> <br /> If he is insistent on saving the Intimacy, the defender may spend 1 Willpower per rank, but never completely save it, bringing it only up to a rank below its original strength. If he does this, the fires that would burn it completely are instead vented into his flesh, and he takes levels of aggravated damage equal to the successes as a normal decisive attack.<br /> <br /> This affects battle groups, the fire of the attack swirling amongst them and seeping into each one to affect the group as a whole.<br /> <br /> If a Defining Intimacy is destroyed, or only preserved at Minor level, a sense of success fills the wielder's soul as she knows the target has a chance at redemption yet again\u2014refunding the point of willpower spent on the charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules: </b>This evocation unlocks in the event that <b>Prophet of Hope and Hellfire</b> is resisted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dual Omens Culling<br /> Cost:</b> 10m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 5<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Wicked-Searing Coalescence; Rebuke of the Blazing Ideal<br /> <br /> Sometimes, there is no hope of peace without action to spur it onward; as such, when the powers of Corona and Umbra are united under the purpose of a single wielder, they surge with the power of the solar eclipse, the grand omen perceived across the world as the combined ire of the Unconquered Sun and Luna. The wielder\u2019s reflexes surge with righteous essence, and in one motion, she unleashes a two-pronged blast of flame, an attack from each piece. The outcome varies on target and attack choice:<ul><li>If attacking the same target twice, the first attack may be withering and the second may be decisive. If so, the player simply rolls accordingly, with the decisive attack being treated as a staggered, near-instant follow-up.</li> <li>If attacking the same target twice, the attacks may both be withering. If so, the player rolls attack and damage once, applying the normal flurry penalty, dealing with all soak and other effects normally, before applying the same results again.</li> <li>If attacking two different targets, the attacks may <i>only</i> be withering. Each attack is treated normally, applying the normal flurry penalty.</li> </ul><br /> If she has learned of their opposing intent or influenced them in this battle, then the attacks carry the burning contempt of the Incarnae against those who continue to oppose the wielder, such that the wielder ignores her Essence in soak and hardness.<br /> <br /> Against enemies of Creation, all damage rolls enjoy double 10s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":11797,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","user":"Seeker","date":". 06-21-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T19:01:11-07:00","id":908034,"title":"","content":"So, I'm at total loss with trying to come up with evocations for an artifact.<br /> <br /> My friend is playing a Righteous Devil Style cowboy inspired by Harry Dresden, and he had enough dots to start with an Artifact Heavy Firewand, along with very solid stats in all his key abilities.<br /> Issue is, I can't think of any evocations or even a theme to help him with fleshing the thing out, let alone even an attunement bonus.<br /> He's an Solar Eclipse, with Supernal in Occult so he can play the fantasy of a sorcerer from the get go, so he only has *three* charms in Righteous Devil: Blossom of Inevitable Demise, Cloud of Ebon Devils, and Kiss of the Sun Concentration, and they are his only offense based charms, with a few in Dodge for defense, and the rest in Presence, Socialize, Occult, and other utility charms.<br /> He's specialized in his build, but relatively well off in a balanced set of skills so far, which absolutely wonderful for a first time player.<br /> <br /> Thing is, he completely out DPS's the Solar Dawn, even without an attunement bonus or evocations from the Firewand.<br /> <br /> At Essence 1, straight from char gen, he's able to solo any of the Dragonblooded enemies from the core book, even the Essence 3 Experienced Fireblood.<br /> It's not even a fair fight, with the Fireblooded being forced to burn motes on Excellencies and defensive charms *every* turn just to stay alive from the sheer raw damage of the Righteous Devil.<br /> It's even more silly when the Fireblood is Initiative Crashed on the <b>First</b> turn, because the Righteous Devil is allowed to reflexively aim when joining battle and has a very solid join battle pool.<br /> In one of the sims we ran, the Righteous Devil managed a one-round kill on the Fireblood in the first shot, and then found out he could do so reliably: <br /> Sensory Acuity Prana+Full Excellency on Join Battle to build up a very high initiative (20 successes for 23i starting).<br /> Decisive attack with Blossom and Kiss of the Sun for 18 Lethal damage. <br /> <br /> So now we're trying to come up with evocations and an attunement bonus for his Firewand, and I'm having trouble, because <b>what could I possibly give this thing</b>?<br /> He already has all the damage he could ever ask for, and it's only going to increase as we gain essence and he can unlock the rest of the Righteous Devil Forms.<br /> Giving him free parry or defenses or soak feels very wrong, because he's already able to deal so much damage that giving him resistance and tank stats to complement it is disgusting.<br /> Mobility is even more gross, making it even more trivial for him to kite and stay at short or medium range.<br /> I'm not sure what kind of utility to give the wands, as it all seems very broken. <br /> I had the idea of letting the wand be a conduit that helps generates Sorcery Motes, but that feels wrong as well when it comes to fluff (He's the best assassin in the group anyways. Turns out, with that high Join Battle pool, and the right preparations, it's trivial to cast Flight of the Brilliant Raptor on Round 1, killing someone from long range in a giant fireball).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11858-seibahismaiwaifu","name":"SeibahIsMaiWaifu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T19:17:50-07:00","id":908045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SeibahIsMaiWaifu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=908034#post908034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm at total loss with trying to come up with evocations for an artifact.<br /> <br /> My friend is playing a Righteous Devil Style cowboy inspired by Harry Dresden, and he had enough dots to start with an Artifact Heavy Firewand, along with very solid stats in all his key abilities.<br /> Issue is, I can't think of any evocations or even a theme to help him with fleshing the thing out, let alone even an attunement bonus.<br /> He's an Solar Eclipse, with Supernal in Occult so he can play the fantasy of a sorcerer from the get go, so he only has *three* charms in Righteous Devil: Blossom of Inevitable Demise, Cloud of Ebon Devils, and Kiss of the Sun Concentration, and they are his only offense based charms, with a few in Dodge for defense, and the rest in Presence, Socialize, Occult, and other utility charms.<br /> He's specialized in his build, but relatively well off in a balanced set of skills so far, which absolutely wonderful for a first time player.<br /> <br /> Thing is, he completely out DPS's the Solar Dawn, even without an attunement bonus or evocations from the Firewand.<br /> <br /> At Essence 1, straight from char gen, he's able to solo any of the Dragonblooded enemies from the core book, even the Essence 3 Experienced Fireblood.<br /> It's not even a fair fight, with the Fireblooded being forced to burn motes on Excellencies and defensive charms *every* turn just to stay alive from the sheer raw damage of the Righteous Devil.<br /> It's even more silly when the Fireblood is Initiative Crashed on the <b>First</b> turn, because the Righteous Devil is allowed to reflexively aim when joining battle and has a very solid join battle pool.<br /> In one of the sims we ran, the Righteous Devil managed a one-round kill on the Fireblood in the first shot, and then found out he could do so reliably:<br /> Sensory Acuity Prana+Full Excellency on Join Battle to build up a very high initiative (20 successes for 23i starting).<br /> Decisive attack with Blossom and Kiss of the Sun for 18 Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> So now we're trying to come up with evocations and an attunement bonus for his Firewand, and I'm having trouble, because <b>what could I possibly give this thing</b>?<br /> He already has all the damage he could ever ask for, and it's only going to increase as we gain essence and he can unlock the rest of the Righteous Devil Forms.<br /> Giving him free parry or defenses or soak feels very wrong, because he's already able to deal so much damage that giving him resistance and tank stats to complement it is disgusting.<br /> Mobility is even more gross, making it even more trivial for him to kite and stay at short or medium range.<br /> I'm not sure what kind of utility to give the wands, as it all seems very broken.<br /> I had the idea of letting the wand be a conduit that helps generates Sorcery Motes, but that feels wrong as well when it comes to fluff (He's the best assassin in the group anyways. Turns out, with that high Join Battle pool, and the right preparations, it's trivial to cast Flight of the Brilliant Raptor on Round 1, killing someone from long range in a giant fireball).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>RDS Eclipse seems to be super popular!<br /> <br /> My advice, and I'm very biased as you can tell from my artifact attempt above, is to bring in different mechanics entirely that would <i>supplement</i>, rather than <i>strengthen</i>, the Righteous Devil. What types of abilities would <i>fit</i> well with the concept?<br /> <br /> My take was incorporating Intimacy-attacks, with my RDS wanting to weaken the corrupt's &quot;sinful&quot; ties and principles to the point where they don't even want to fight or be &quot;evil&quot; anymore. You can see this idea in the RDS flavor (both 3E and 2E), and with the description of <b>Caress of 1,000 Hells</b>, which forcefully gives them a Defining Tie toward whatever redemptive path is generally agreed upon. So an artifact tied to the RDS could enhance that concept tree.<br /> <br /> You could also go for more gambit-based evocations, such that the RDS's artifact allows him to more accurately manipulate his flames for specific purposes (&quot;Curve the flame&quot; rather than &quot;Curve the bullet&quot;), giving Disarm options, fear affects, etc.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You could also tie it into the Occult tree if you want to synthesize the two concepts. Extra damage to spirits, stuff that supplements (rather than replicates) Occult charms, et cetera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T22:44:34-07:00","id":908900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=908045#post908045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> RDS Eclipse seems to be super popular!<br /> <br /> My advice, and I'm very biased as you can tell from my artifact attempt above, is to bring in different mechanics entirely that would <i>supplement</i>, rather than <i>strengthen</i>, the Righteous Devil. What types of abilities would <i>fit</i> well with the concept?<br /> <br /> My take was incorporating Intimacy-attacks, with my RDS wanting to weaken the corrupt's &quot;sinful&quot; ties and principles to the point where they don't even want to fight or be &quot;evil&quot; anymore. You can see this idea in the RDS flavor (both 3E and 2E), and with the description of <b>Caress of 1,000 Hells</b>, which forcefully gives them a Defining Tie toward whatever redemptive path is generally agreed upon. So an artifact tied to the RDS could enhance that concept tree.<br /> <br /> You could also go for more gambit-based evocations, such that the RDS's artifact allows him to more accurately manipulate his flames for specific purposes (&quot;Curve the flame&quot; rather than &quot;Curve the bullet&quot;), giving Disarm options, fear affects, etc.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You could also tie it into the Occult tree if you want to synthesize the two concepts. Extra damage to spirits, stuff that supplements (rather than replicates) Occult charms, et cetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tying it to extra damage to spirits would be a cool idea. I was toying around with passives and evocations to that this afternoon, but I don't think I have enough for a full tree.<br /> Right now, I'm working with the idea of a set of fire pieces that revolve around mobility and encourage the user to constantly be fighting close to the enemy and always keep rushing rather than hanging back at medium range. Dash in, dash out, shoot, reload, move, etc.<br /> <br /> Currently, almost all of the power budget is tied up in [Glass Slinger]. Frankly, I like it that way. It's a cool way to enable the fantasy of a gunslinger. I just hope that it's added damage is relatively balanced. At Essence 1, it's a 6d10 roll, which on average rolls 3, slowly scaling up to 5i as the user increases their essence. <br /> <br /> Sorry, I don't think I'm sober enough to try and format this right now.<br /> <br /> [Sacred Heath &amp; Blood Steppes]<br /> Light Artifact Fire Pieces (Orichalcum &amp; Red Jade): ***<br /> Attunement: 5m<br /> <br /> Twin fire wands; sisters forged from the Burning Sands of the far South, their barrels hum with the golden touch of the high desert sun. Thirsty and Parched, they starve for more and more essence, requiring a Solar or Fire hearthstone to function, and essence to fire. Hammered on an anvil of sands in the kiln breathed forth by the Tyrant of the Sands, the two sisters were gifted by their Solar master the flames of the Unconquered Sun. When a Solar attunes to them once more, the desert sands will turn to glass from their burning convictions.<br /> <br /> Evocations:<br /> Passive:<br /> While the Solar remains relentless in battle, [Sacred Heath &amp; Blood Steppes] dance with glee, increasing their overwhelming damage by +2, doubled against Spirits.<br /> In addition, when the Solar first learns an evocation of [Sacred Heath &amp; Blood Steppes], he learns [Glass Slinger] for free.<br /> <br /> [Glass Slinger] (Cost:\u2013 ; Type: Permanent; Duration: Indefinite):<br /> While attuned with [Sacred Heath &amp; Blood Steppes], if their wielder successfully lands a withering attack after supplementing an attack or rush action with an evocation of [Sacred Heath &amp; Blood Steppes] or a charm from Righteous Devil Form, he may make a *second* attack.<br /> The Solar makes a *second* attack at any target in range, rolling (Overwhelming+Essence) with double 10's and gaining initiative equal to the number of success.<br /> **Might just change this to number of success on the withering damage roll, roll that many dice for the *second* attack**<br /> The Solar may not supplementary or reflexively use any charms or evocations with this second attack.<br /> <br /> [Piercing Flame] (Cost: 3m; Type: Supplemental; Duration: Instant):<br /> The heat of Solar Fire melts the strongest and heaviest armors and withers them to glass. When [Piercing Flame] supplements a *withering* attack, it reduces the targets Soak by (Essence). When supplementing a *decisive* attack, it instead ignores (Essence/2, rounded up) Hardness.<br /> <br /> [Ardent Blaze] (Cost: 3m, 3i; Type: Simple; Duration: Instant):<br /> Taking aim, the Solar unleashes a fiery sun of blue-white flames that explode into a spiraling wave of fire, marking those who sin in the sands for judgement. This charm is a difficulty 2 gambit, and on success, marks the target and any enemy in close range with [Inferno Enraged], harmless blue-white flames that persist until the end of the Solar's next turn.<br /> When the Solar or his ally land a *withering* attack, *gambit*, *evocation*, or *charm* on a enemy marked with [Inferno Enraged], until the end of the Solar next turn, he may double up to (Essence) 9's on a Rush action.<br /> [Ardent Blaze] explicitly counts as an action that triggers [Glass Slinger]<br /> <br /> [Relentless Pursuit] (Cost 3m; Type: Supplemental; Duration: Instant):<br /> The Solar is hellbent in his pursuit, gliding over the sands as he hunts down those who dare stain the sands with dishonored blood, without a care for his own safety.<br /> When the Solar flurries a *rush* or *disengage* action, the defense penalty he suffers increases to -2, but the flurry penalty he takes is reduced to -1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11858-seibahismaiwaifu","name":"SeibahIsMaiWaifu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T05:01:18-07:00","id":909050,"title":"","content":"<b>Benevolent Unyielding Patron (Artifact 3)</b><br /> <br /> This lovingly crafted white jade chain shirt was created only two decades after the Great Contagion by Amilar Hadates, a renowned warrior of the Seventh Legion. For decades Hadates had known no fear on the battlefield, even when it seemed the whole world was dying all around him and legions of monstrous Fair Folk invaded. He only truly tasted fear for the first time when his freshly exalted daughter told him that she wished to leave Lookshy and explore what remains of the world. As Hadates would be unable to keep her safe while she was gone, he created Benevolent Unyielding Patron to do just that.<br /> <br /> A Dragonblood or Solar Exalt who commits two extra motes when attuning to Benevolent Unyielding Patron finds that when she struggles he will always be there to make things better. After taking initiative damage from a withering attack, Benevolent Unyielding Patron returns one point of initiative to his wearer, seeking to soothe his charge.<br /> <br /> <b>It\u2019s Dangerous Out There</b><br /> Cost: 1m per die Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The world is a dangerous place that the young are seldom prepared to face. Luckily, Benevolent Unyielding Patron knows that foes that may seem deadly to a child are still prone to exploitable flaws.<br /> <br /> When the wearer of this armor is hit by a withering attack and her enemy rolls damage, she may spend one mote per 1 in the enemy\u2019s damage roll. For every mote spent, the enemy must reroll successful damage dice, starting with 10s and working down from there. Against a decisive attack, the number of motes spent cannot exceed the wearer\u2019s essence.<br /> <br /> This evocation unlocks for an attuned Dragonblood or Solar wearer at no cost when she is crashed by an obviously superior opponent or when her last -2 health level is filled in. Unlocking the evocation will retroactively allow it to be used on the attack that crashed or damaged her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>They Only Want One Thing</b><br /> Cost: 8m Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: It\u2019s Dangerous Out There<br /> <br /> Children do not have the experience or wisdom of their parents. They trust anyone. Benevolent Unyielding Patron knows better; one should never let down one\u2019s guard, even amongst those who seem like friends.<br /> <br /> For the rest of the scene after activating this evocation, Benevolent Unyielding Patron helps his wearer prepare for attacks from those she is cautious of. These are individuals that the wearer has succeeded on a Read Intentions action during the scene. Against such foes (or friends), increase Benevolent Unyielding Patron\u2019s armored soak by 4 and hardness by 2 as well as the wearer\u2019s Resolve by 1. In addition, whenever such a person within short range fails at a non-trivial action they are attempting, she may spend one mote to gain a point of initiative.<br /> <br /> When activating this evocation the wearer may reflexively use a Read Intentions action against a single target. Using this evocation makes it impossible to form or strengthen positive intimacies towards anyone that the wearer has used a Read Intentions action on for one day (except by magic).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Always Watching Over You</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: They Only Want One Thing<br /> <br /> What the wearer of Benevolent Unyielding Patron needs to understand is that everything that she accomplishes is only because she had such a caring figure watching over her.<br /> <br /> When being attacked by a deadly blow, Benevolent Unyielding Patron will himself strike back against a foe. Using Always Watching Over You creates an immediate clash against a decisive attack (including attacks for which the wearer could not apply her defense) using a pool equal to her Soak with [Essence] automatic successes. Succeeding at the clash causes blades, arrows, or fists to rebound back at their attacker with a damage pool equal to the wearer\u2019s Resolve plus the strength of any negative intimacy she bears for the attacker or something he represents.<br /> <br /> This evocation may only be used once until it is reset by spending a scene consoling oneself with or seeking wisdom from an elder or authority figure (never an equal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","user":"Kunoichi","date":". 09-11-2016, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T07:47:32-07:00","id":909165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909050#post909050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Benevolent Unyielding Patron (Artifact 3)</b><br /> <br /> A Dragonblood or Solar Exalt who attunes to Benevolent Unyielding Patron finds that when she struggles he will always be there to make things better. After taking initiative damage from a withering attack, Benevolent Unyielding Patron returns one point of initiative to his wearer, seeking to soothe his charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay, artifact armor! Except... we don't know what it's made out of. I could see Starmetal actually... *Edit, I JUST noticed the tiny text that states this is white jade. I'm not sure I see the effects that make this white jade based on it's design, but you DID pick something so... IGNORE ME!<br /> <br /> In other news, this attunement bonus is a VERY powerful passive effect that 1) should probably have an additional attunement cost (I'd say at least 2 motes) and 2) needs a little clarification. It says it <i>returns</i> one mote after it takes initiative damage. How does this interact with it's attacker? Do they get 1 less mote? What if the attack would crash you to 0, but then you go up to 1. Does the attacker get the crash bonus? Things to consider in designing mechanics like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909050#post909050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>It\u2019s Dangerous Out There</b><br /> Cost: 1m per die Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The world is a dangerous place that the young are seldom prepared to face. Luckily, Benevolent Unyielding Patron knows that foes that may seem deadly to a child are still prone to exploitable flaws.<br /> <br /> When the wearer of this armor is hit by a withering attack and her enemy rolls damage, she may spend one mote per 1 in the enemy\u2019s damage roll. For every mote spent, the enemy must reroll successful damage dice, starting with 10s and working down from there. Against a decisive attack, the number of motes spent cannot exceed the wearer\u2019s essence.<br /> <br /> This evocation unlocks for an attuned Dragonblood or Solar wearer at no cost when she is crashed by an obviously superior opponent or when her last -2 health level is filled in. Unlocking the evocation will retroactively allow it to be used on the attack that crashed or damaged her.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like there's a balance concern in this charm, but conceptually I actually like it a lot! I think my concern is that it starts with the 10's and works down, for merely 1m per die. This may not actually be an issue, but it's my only hesitation from throwing my full support behind this evocation effect. I do like it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909050#post909050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>They Only Want One Thing</b><br /> Cost: 8m Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: It\u2019s Dangerous Out There<br /> <br /> Children do not have the experience or wisdom of their parents. They trust anyone. Benevolent Unyielding Patron knows better; one should never let down one\u2019s guard, even amongst those who seem like friends.<br /> <br /> For the rest of the scene after activating this evocation, Benevolent Unyielding Patron helps his wearer prepare for attacks from those she is cautious of. These are individuals that the wearer has succeeded on a Read Intentions action during the scene. Against such foes (or friends), increase Benevolent Unyielding Patron\u2019s armored soak by 4 and hardness by 2 as well as the wearer\u2019s Resolve by 1. In addition, whenever such a person within short range fails at a non-trivial action they are attempting, she may spend one mote to gain a point of initiative.<br /> <br /> When activating this evocation the wearer may reflexively use a Read Intentions action against a single target. Using this evocation makes it impossible to form or strengthen positive intimacies towards anyone that the wearer has used a Read Intentions action on for one day (except by magic).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a cool evocation mechanic. It's powerful, but expensive and has some requirements too. I like it as is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909050#post909050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Always Watching Over You</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: They Only Want One Thing<br /> <br /> What the wearer of Benevolent Unyielding Patron needs to understand is that everything that she accomplishes is only because she had such a caring figure watching over her.<br /> <br /> When being attacked by a deadly blow, Benevolent Unyielding Patron will himself strike back against a foe. Using Always Watching Over You creates an immediate clash against a decisive attack (including attacks for which the wearer could not apply her defense) using a pool equal to her Soak with [Essence] automatic successes. Succeeding at the clash causes blades, arrows, or fists to rebound back at their attacker with a damage pool equal to the wearer\u2019s Resolve plus the strength of any negative intimacy she bears for the attacker or something he represents.<br /> <br /> This evocation may only be used once until it is reset by spending a scene consoling oneself with or seeking wisdom from an elder or authority figure (never an equal).</div> </div> </div> </div>This one needs a look at. Conceptually, I think I get it, but is it a clash or a counterattack? A clash is where you and a foe attack at the same time and only the highest score gets to deal damage. A counterattack is a response to an incoming attack and it's a case by case whether the first attack still has any effect. Decide which direction you plan to go with this, then phrase it and keyword it properly and this artifact looks solid! Not nearly enough artifact armor out there, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T08:50:42-07:00","id":909198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909165#post909165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yay, artifact armor! Except... we don't know what it's made out of. I could see Starmetal actually... *Edit, I JUST noticed the tiny text that states this is white jade. I'm not sure I see the effects that make this white jade based on it's design, but you DID pick something so... IGNORE ME!<br /> <br /> In other news, this attunement bonus is a VERY powerful passive effect that 1) should probably have an additional attunement cost (I'd say at least 2 motes) and 2) needs a little clarification. It says it <i>returns</i> one mote after it takes initiative damage. How does this interact with it's attacker? Do they get 1 less mote? What if the attack would crash you to 0, but then you go up to 1. Does the attacker get the crash bonus? Things to consider in designing mechanics like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way its intended is that the attacker's initiative gain isn't affected except in the case where you would be un-crashed by the return of an initiative.<br /> <br /> Oh and the reason its white jade is because it makes you more sturdy (kind of), and because I was going along with the Earth Aspect tendencies to be more traditional. As this is a very paternalistic &quot;father knows best&quot; type of armor, it seemed appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909165#post909165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there's a balance concern in this charm, but conceptually I actually like it a lot! I think my concern is that it starts with the 10's and works down, for merely 1m per die. This may not actually be an issue, but it's my only hesitation from throwing my full support behind this evocation effect. I do like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured it's balanced by the requirement of dice that come up as 1. As they'd only be on average 10% of the damage dice, I don't see this being a thing that has much effect on average, but can rarely be a nice treat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909165#post909165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a cool evocation mechanic. It's powerful, but expensive and has some requirements too. I like it as is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I wasn't too sure how to price it, but it seemed good, and it encourages a type of action that you don't see much in combat. Also, if I were ever to make evocations for something inspired by Kimbery, it seems a good one for that too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909165#post909165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one needs a look at. Conceptually, I think I get it, but is it a clash or a counterattack? A clash is where you and a foe attack at the same time and only the highest score gets to deal damage. A counterattack is a response to an incoming attack and it's a case by case whether the first attack still has any effect. Decide which direction you plan to go with this, then phrase it and keyword it properly and this artifact looks solid! Not nearly enough artifact armor out there, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's a clash that's structured similar to a counterattack, but isn't actually a counterattack. So if you win the roll, you don't get hit, if they win, you get hit harder.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the comments and all. This was a burst of inspiration after a few weeks of trying to make a white jade chain shirt. &quot;Why not make it a patronizing male figure?&quot; Hehe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:43:27-07:00","id":909382,"title":"","content":"<b>Soul\u2019s Reflection \u2013 Moonsilver Grimscythe (****)</b><br /> <br /> Forged by a No Moon sorcerer for her impulsive Changing Moon lover and packmate, Soul\u2019s Reflection is intended to give the wild-hearted trickster some pause before charging into a situation \u2013 or at least to better equip him if and when he charges in anyway. The haft of the grimscythe is plain, but the head is shaped like a bird\u2019s skull, with the blade extending beneath the beak. The blade itself is polished to a mirror-shine that never fades or tarnishes, within which can sometimes be seen the true nature of things.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Soul\u2019s Reflection</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Lunar Exalt who attunes to Soul\u2019s Reflection for five motes finds his body moving instinctively to react to danger, adding one die to his Join Battle.<br /> <br /> <b>Intuiting the Heart</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> When the wielder of Soul\u2019s Reflection gazes into the mirror-sheen of the blade, he can see the truth of a person reflected therein with but a single, intuitive glance. This Evocation is a reflexive Read Intentions action to determine one of a target\u2019s Intimacies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Intuiting the Soul</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Intuiting the Heart<br /> <br /> True intuition is more than simply a hunch, but a deeper understanding which the mirror-blade of Soul\u2019s Reflection can impart in an instantaneous flash of inspiration. This Evocation is a reflexive Profile Character action that can be taken after a handful of seconds of interaction rather than a full five minutes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Intuition\u2019s Shield</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Intuiting the Soul<br /> <br /> Knowledge is power, and intuition is nothing if not knowledge. This Evocation provides a permanent +1 non-Charm bonus to the wielder\u2019s Guile against any character he has profiled using its prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Robbery of Instinct</b><br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Withering-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> It is not enough to function on instinct alone. Understanding of one\u2019s opponents brings a keener knowledge of their movements. This Evocation supplements a <b>withering</b> attack, allowing the Exalt to steal a number of additional Initiative from the target on a successful attack equal to the number of that target's Intimacies he knows.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Application of Instinct</b><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One Action<br /> Prerequisites: Robbery of Instinct<br /> <br /> True instinct is more than intuition; it is action melded with thought, bordering on precognition. This Evocation may be activated to raise the wielder\u2019s Evasion by (the higher of Essence or 3) against the last enemy he has profiled using a Profile Character action.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sudden Instinct</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1W; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Clash, Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Application of Instinct, Intuiting the Heart<br /> <br /> Against those he understands, the Exalt moves like lightning, acting before even he fully understands why. Yet instinct is not action without thought, but one with it, melding the two into a fluid whole. This Evocation allows the wielder to make a reflexive clash attack with Soul\u2019s Reflection against an attack directed at him by a target against whom he has successfully used a Read Intentions or Profile Character action in the same scene, regardless of his place in the Initiative order. This does not count as the wielder\u2019s combat action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":". 06-08-2016, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T14:10:52-07:00","id":909470,"title":"","content":"<b>Eraint-Gwyn, the Chaos Breaker (Artifact </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <b>White Jade &amp; Moonsilver Prosthetic Arm)</b><br /> In the burning plains of the Southern Wyld there is a bubble of perfect stability, a meadow of no more than twenty acres dominated by a majestic shrine built in the style of the First Age. Powerful spells defend it from the ravages of chaos but Raksha leave it untouched for fear of the treasure which it holds. Within the shrine lies a simple burial site, poems in an ancient scripts decorate the wall and a single alter holds a single box of richly inscribed Moonsilver three feet in length. Within this box lays what seems to be the severed arm of a White Jade statue covered in beautiful Moonsilver patterns.<br /> Held up to the stump of an Exalt\u2019s limb the White Jade that composes the arm begins to shift and mold, fusing to the stump and reconfiguring itself into an exact replica of the lost limb, every vein, detail and even brand copied in the White jade and Moonsilver. Many Fair Folk princes remember the Silver-Armed King, whether he was born of the moon or the sun, whether she was a man or a woman or whether it was a single individual or a title worn by many Exalted none can truly recall for the King ended all of the Fair Folk to ever see scourge.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Eraint-Gwyn</b><br /> <br /> <b>Attunement:</b> This artifact requires that the user have the Amputee Flaw to represent a missing arm, once the attunement cost of 8 is committed the character is treated as not having the Amputee Flaw. While attuned the players unarmed attacks are treated as medium artifact weapons as the powers of the artifact spread across the chakras of the King\u2019s body.<br /> <br /> <b>Indomitable Silver-White Form</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> The Silver-Armed King has no fear of the Wyld for he marches encased in order, with a shimmer the flesh of the King morphs into a moving statue of Silver-White matter which is provides both conventional protection and immunity to the ravages of chaos. The Silver White Form provides the King with protection equivalent to Medium Artifact Armour in addition to the benefits of Integrity-Protecting Prana for as long as it remains active. Wyld-Shaping attempts receive a -2 penalty while this charm is active as its power dampens manipulation of Chaos.<br /> Indomitable Silver-White Form is incompatible with any form of armour but explicitly does not interfere with any Martial Art.<br /> <br /> <b>Order Overwhelms Chaos</b><br /> Cost: 4m or 8m Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Indomitable Silver-White Form<br /> The Silver-Armed King will crush all chaos in her path, with a roar of rage her blows shatter the falsehoods of fae-flesh. Order Overwhelms Chaos supplements any unarmed attack against any foe with the Cold Iron Bane Merits, the attack now deals aggravated damage.<br /> At Essence 3+ the Exalt may choose to pay 8m to apply the charm to foes that do not have the Cold Iron Bane Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Creation Claims Its Prize</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp or 12m, 2wp Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Order Overwhelms Chaos<br /> It is a King\u2019s duty to punish crimes and what greater crime is there than to stand against Creation? As his Silver-White blows strike his target, the foul denizen of Chaos begins to feel their body begin to Calcify as the blows of the King take on the power of Creation itself, once the Fae is overwhelmed nothing remains but a marble statue, usually one with a frozen look of horror.<br /> When paying 6m, 1wp to enhance a Withering Unarmed attack against a creature of the Wyld the foe of the King loses (Total Post-Soak Damage/2) Initiative from their Initiative pool. At Essence 5+ the King gains any Initiative points taken from the foe in this manner.<br /> 12m, 1wp may be paid to enhance an Unarmed Decisive Attack against a creature of the Wyld which applies a -2 penalty to the Hardness of the foe. Should at least one health level of damage result from an attack enhanced by Creation Claims Its Prize then the target takes receives a -1 penalty to their Mobility. Any Fair Folk slain by Creation Claims Its Prize is Calcified regardless of location.<br /> This charm can only be used while Indomitable Silver-White Form is active.<br /> <br /> <b>Magnanimity of the Silver-White King</b><br /> Cost: 20m, 2wp +8xp Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> The King looks upon the Calcified remains of his foes and decides to cement Creations victory, arranging the Calcified remains of five Raksha nobles around himself while in the deep Wyld the King erupts his shell in a flash of prismatic light flash-forging a loyal servant from the broken shells of his foes and sending ripples of his power across the Wyld.<br /> This charm requires the remains of five Raksha nobles Calcified by the prerequisite and instantly creates a being equivalent to one created by an Ambition 2, Finesse 3 Sorcerous Working. The Circle of the Working is determined by the average level of the Calcified Nobles, Essence 3 results in a Terrestrial creation, Essence 4 results in a Celestial creation and Essence 5 results in a Solar creation. Finesse 3 represents the King\u2019s general intent for her servant and the residual characteristics of slain Raksha.<br /> The creation has a permanent Defining Tie (Loyalty to the Silver-Armed King) and a Major Tie (Hatred for the Wyld). Only (Essence/2) beings created by Magnanimity of the Silver-White King can live at any given time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:15:43-07:00","id":909607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909382#post909382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Solar or Lunar Exalt who attunes to Soul\u2019s Reflection for five motes finds his body moving instinctively to react to danger, adding one die to his Join Battle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fits the flavor well enough. I assume it's intentionally a charm die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909382#post909382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Intuiting the Heart</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> When the wielder of Soul\u2019s Reflection gazes into the mirror-sheen of the blade, he can see the truth of a person reflected therein with but a single, intuitive glance. This Evocation is a reflexive Read Intentions action to determine one of a target\u2019s Intimacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>3 motes for effectively negating a flurry penalty both from the attack and the social action. Won't get used much outside combat. On the other hand, it's a weapon intended for a Changing Moon - it's reasonable to assume they'll have their own magic to boost Read Intentions outside of combat. A solid workhorse option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909382#post909382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Intuiting the Soul</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Intuiting the Heart<br /> <br /> True intuition is more than simply a hunch, but a deeper understanding which the mirror-blade of Soul\u2019s Reflection can impart in an instantaneous flash of inspiration. This Evocation is a reflexive Profile Character action that can be taken after a handful of seconds of interaction rather than a full five minutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Five motes, ouch. Using this power is going to eat into the reserves of anyone embroidered in a life-and-death struggle against an equal foe (they'll spend motes on enhancing their defensive suite if nothing else, and they'll probably also spend motes on enhancing the profile action itself, because at this cost, they literally can't afford having to try again).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909382#post909382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Intuition\u2019s Shield</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Intuiting the Soul<br /> <br /> Knowledge is power, and intuition is nothing if not knowledge. This Evocation provides a permanent +1 non-Charm bonus to the wielder\u2019s Guile against any character he has profiled using its prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another solid, if mechanically uninteresting boost. I have a bit of a hard time reconciling the calculating nature of a passive Guile increase (you know him, therefore you can play him better) with a sudden flash of intuition and insight, but hey, it's the player's job to stunt it in a way that makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909382#post909382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Robbery of Instinct</b><br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Withering-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> It is not enough to function on instinct alone. Understanding of one\u2019s opponents brings a keener knowledge of their movements. This Evocation supplements a <b>withering</b> attack, allowing the Exalt to pay 2m to steal (Essence) additional Initiative from the target on a successful attack. This Evocation only functions if the attacker knows at least one of the target\u2019s Intimacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Starts out fairly weakly (half as cost-effective as Fire and Stones Strike, and limited to a single die of damage), but pulls way ahead later on. Now, the problem is that it's a Grimscythe, so it'll have rather absurd damage pools to begin with, and it also gets to stack with FSS. My problem with it is partially the fact that it gets to be at least twice as mote-efficient as FSS at Ess 4+, and partially that this is an Essence 1 Charm that's supposed to establish the Artifact's unique identity, but instead of being a flashy new toy that expands a character's starting combat options, it's a solid lategame powerhouse instead.<br /> <br /> Me, I'd have it fiddle around with the Initiative Break system somehow (heavy weapons are naturally great at breaking people in a single strike, so it's a good synergy between the evocation and the base stats). Maybe grant a passive Initiative bonus equal to the number of your opponent's known Intimacies when you crash someone with an attack made with the weapon. Maybe make it a reflexive Charm you can activate to roll (Essence/2, round up) extra damage dice after you succeeded in an attack and rolled damage, which you lose if the modified damage roll doesn't cause the opponent to crash (your instinctual understanding of your opponent helps you capitalize on their fatal weaknesses and maneuver them into a position of vulnerability).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909382#post909382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Application of Instinct</b><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One Action<br /> Prerequisites: Robbery of Instinct<br /> <br /> True instinct is more than intuition; it is action melded with thought, bordering on precognition. This Evocation may be activated to raise the wielder\u2019s Evasion by (the higher of Essence or 3) against any enemy he has profiled using a Profile Character action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so that's why Intuiting the Soul is so expensive!<br /> <br /> Well, I think this is a terrible idea. You effectively hand the wielder 5 free motes a turn right from the start, which only gets better over time. That's a really really massive advantage, and it basically means the outcome of combat will largely be decided by the success of the original Profile action - which, I feel compelled to add, doesn't even have to happen in the combat, a Lunar (or a Stealth/Larceny-focused Solar, for that matter) can just follow the target around, profile them, and reap massive benefits once combat starts. Even if we ignore that this is basically an Infinity Ability Mastery effect with all of its resultant pitfalls, the Evocation rewards careful preparation and planning, the exact opposite of what the entire Artifact's theme is about.<br /> <br /> I <i>strongly</i> suggest redesigning this power from the ground up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909382#post909382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sudden Instinct</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1W; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Clash, Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Application of Instinct, Intuiting the Heart<br /> <br /> Against those he understands, the Exalt moves like lightning, acting before even he fully understands why. Yet instinct is not action without thought, but one with it, melding the two into a fluid whole. This Evocation allows the wielder to make a reflexive clash attack with Soul\u2019s Reflection against an attack directed at him by a target against whom he has successfully used a Read Intentions or Profile Character action in the same scene, regardless of his place in the Initiative order. This does not count as the wielder\u2019s combat action.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good, powerful capstone that encapsulates and rewards the reckless fighting style it's supposed to supplement. Nice synergy with the +2 clash bonus from using a heavy weapon. Well done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T08:02:40-07:00","id":910086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909607#post909607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fits the flavor well enough. I assume it's intentionally a charm die.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909607#post909607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 motes for effectively negating a flurry penalty both from the attack and the social action. Won't get used much outside combat. On the other hand, it's a weapon intended for a Changing Moon - it's reasonable to assume they'll have their own magic to boost Read Intentions outside of combat. A solid workhorse option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909607#post909607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Five motes, ouch. Using this power is going to eat into the reserves of anyone embroidered in a life-and-death struggle against an equal foe (they'll spend motes on enhancing their defensive suite if nothing else, and they'll probably also spend motes on enhancing the profile action itself, because at this cost, they literally can't afford having to try again).</div> </div> </div> </div>I maybe should drop it to 4m, just so people can get that Peripheral boost without flaring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909607#post909607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another solid, if mechanically uninteresting boost. I have a bit of a hard time reconciling the calculating nature of a passive Guile increase (you know him, therefore you can play him better) with a sudden flash of intuition and insight, but hey, it's the player's job to stunt it in a way that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks... I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909607#post909607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe grant a passive Initiative bonus equal to the number of your opponent's known Intimacies when you crash someone with an attack made with the weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, I like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909607#post909607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, so that's why Intuiting the Soul is so expensive!<br /> <br /> Well, I think this is a terrible idea. You effectively hand the wielder 5 free motes a turn right from the start, which only gets better over time. That's a really really massive advantage, and it basically means the outcome of combat will largely be decided by the success of the original Profile action - which, I feel compelled to add, doesn't even have to happen in the combat, a Lunar (or a Stealth/Larceny-focused Solar, for that matter) can just follow the target around, profile them, and reap massive benefits once combat starts. Even if we ignore that this is basically an Infinity Ability Mastery effect with all of its resultant pitfalls, the Evocation rewards careful preparation and planning, the exact opposite of what the entire Artifact's theme is about.<br /> <br /> I <i>strongly</i> suggest redesigning this power from the ground up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your input. Note that it only gives the bonus against that specific character, and that the weapon is INTENDED to encourage preparation and planning, in the hopes that the Changing Moon would take advantage of that. It's also supposed to provide some help when he inevitably doesn't follow through with that preparation. Also note that it only lasts one action. <br /> <br /> EDIT: I changed the wording to specify that it only functions against THE LAST person profiled, so you can't stack Profile Character actions and get bonuses against everyone. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909607#post909607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good, powerful capstone that encapsulates and rewards the reckless fighting style it's supposed to supplement. Nice synergy with the +2 clash bonus from using a heavy weapon. Well done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":". 06-08-2016, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T08:37:37-07:00","id":910105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909470#post909470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Eraint-Gwyn, the Chaos Breaker (Artifact </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <b>White Jade &amp; Moonsilver Prosthetic Arm)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Attunement:</b> This artifact requires that the user have the Amputee Flaw to represent a missing arm, once the attunement cost of 8 is committed the character is treated as not having the Amputee Flaw. While attuned the players unarmed attacks are treated as medium artifact weapons as the powers of the artifact spread across the chakras of the King\u2019s body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone wants Medium weapons.. No one's ever happy with a Light or Heavy these days...<br /> <br /> In other news, love the whole prosthetic arm bit, though as above, I'd have personally modeled it after a smashfist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909470#post909470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Indomitable Silver-White Form</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> The Silver-Armed King has no fear of the Wyld for he marches encased in order, with a shimmer the flesh of the King morphs into a moving statue of Silver-White matter which is provides both conventional protection and immunity to the ravages of chaos. The Silver White Form provides the King with protection equivalent to Medium Artifact Armour in addition to the benefits of Integrity-Protecting Prana for as long as it remains active. Wyld-Shaping attempts receive a -2 penalty while this charm is active as its power dampens manipulation of Chaos.<br /> Indomitable Silver-White Form is incompatible with any form of armour but explicitly does not interfere with any Martial Art.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate opening with this, but I plain don't like this evocation. It feels too much like a &quot;I want all the best things that usually conflict with each other, as easily as possible&quot; ability. You have a medium artifact weapon that can't me disarmed for starters. Then you can give yourself Medium armor that works with martial arts anyways while also making your possessions immune to the Wyld, and making you very resistant to it. All activated without spending an action. And it lasts for a whole scene.<br /> <br /> All of the individual combinations work without breaking the system. Even stacking them together isn't impossible. But the first impression is &quot;twink power&quot; at least to me. If you really wanted all these effects, I would at the very least require a Simple activation of the power instead of Reflexive. The user needs some sort of effort for this much payoff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909470#post909470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Order Overwhelms Chaos</b><br /> Cost: 4m or 8m Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Indomitable Silver-White Form<br /> The Silver-Armed King will crush all chaos in her path, with a roar of rage her blows shatter the falsehoods of fae-flesh. Order Overwhelms Chaos supplements any unarmed attack against any foe with the Cold Iron Bane Merits, the attack now deals aggravated damage.<br /> At Essence 3+ the Exalt may choose to pay 8m to apply the charm to foes that do not have the Cold Iron Bane Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this power. Actually, I think it's overpriced. Since it only works against those with the Cold Iron Bane, I'd be comfortable with this being 1 or 2 motes, easily. AND Essence 1. It's not that strong. Being able to apply it to anyone at Essence 3? Make that 4 or 5m.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909470#post909470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Creation Claims Its Prize</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp or 12m, 2wp Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Order Overwhelms Chaos<br /> It is a King\u2019s duty to punish crimes and what greater crime is there than to stand against Creation? As his Silver-White blows strike his target, the foul denizen of Chaos begins to feel their body begin to Calcify as the blows of the King take on the power of Creation itself, once the Fae is overwhelmed nothing remains but a marble statue, usually one with a frozen look of horror.<br /> When paying 6m, 1wp to enhance a Withering Unarmed attack against a creature of the Wyld the foe of the King loses (Total Post-Soak Damage/2) Initiative from their Initiative pool. At Essence 5+ the King gains any Initiative points taken from the foe in this manner.<br /> 12m, 1wp may be paid to enhance an Unarmed Decisive Attack against a creature of the Wyld which applies a -2 penalty to the Hardness of the foe. Should at least one health level of damage result from an attack enhanced by Creation Claims Its Prize then the target takes receives a -1 penalty to their Mobility. Any Fair Folk slain by Creation Claims Its Prize is Calcified regardless of location.<br /> This charm can only be used while Indomitable Silver-White Form is active.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little unclear how the Withering portion of this power works. Is total post-soak damage the die pool or the rolled Final damage? And is this <i>on top of</i> the normal initiative damage it deals? Needs clarification.<br /> <br /> The Decisive portion of this power is uh.. well, how long do those penalties last? Are they stackable? And even if they are, 12m, 2wp is unbelievably overpriced. The Decisive portion is not very strong at all unless I'm missing something. There's effects that ignore hardness entirely that are a fraction of that cost. So give this one a once-over. Decide what the goal of the evocation is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=909470#post909470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Magnanimity of the Silver-White King</b><br /> Cost: 20m, 2wp +8xp Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> The King looks upon the Calcified remains of his foes and decides to cement Creations victory, arranging the Calcified remains of five Raksha nobles around himself while in the deep Wyld the King erupts his shell in a flash of prismatic light flash-forging a loyal servant from the broken shells of his foes and sending ripples of his power across the Wyld.<br /> This charm requires the remains of five Raksha nobles Calcified by the prerequisite and instantly creates a being equivalent to one created by an Ambition 2, Finesse 3 Sorcerous Working. The Circle of the Working is determined by the average level of the Calcified Nobles, Essence 3 results in a Terrestrial creation, Essence 4 results in a Celestial creation and Essence 5 results in a Solar creation. Finesse 3 represents the King\u2019s general intent for her servant and the residual characteristics of slain Raksha.<br /> The creation has a permanent Defining Tie (Loyalty to the Silver-Armed King) and a Major Tie (Hatred for the Wyld). Only (Essence/2) beings created by Magnanimity of the Silver-White King can live at any given time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one as is. It's perfect and a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the prosthetic arm, and I like your choices of materials for the theme and direction of your artifact. But that opening power just strikes a wrong chord with me. I'm trying to be very clear that I'm not saying it's a badwrongfun evocation. This is strictly a personal preference, influencing my review.<br /> <br /> Am I the only one who can't think of this without imagining the Winter Soldier? ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:17:56-07:00","id":910128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910105#post910105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone wants Medium weapons.. No one's ever happy with a Light or Heavy these days...<br /> <br /> In other news, love the whole prosthetic arm bit, though as above, I'd have personally modeled it after a smashfist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truthfully I was thinking of making it a Light Artifact would be too weak but if it really would result in something that broken would a Light Artifact be more balanced? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910105#post910105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hate opening with this, but I plain don't like this evocation. It feels too much like a &quot;I want all the best things that usually conflict with each other, as easily as possible&quot; ability. You have a medium artifact weapon that can't me disarmed for starters. Then you can give yourself Medium armor that works with martial arts anyways while also making your possessions immune to the Wyld, and making you very resistant to it. All activated without spending an action. And it lasts for a whole scene.<br /> <br /> All of the individual combinations work without breaking the system. Even stacking them together isn't impossible. But the first impression is &quot;twink power&quot; at least to me. If you really wanted all these effects, I would at the very least require a Simple activation of the power instead of Reflexive. The user needs some sort of effort for this much payoff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truthfully I was going for killer-marble-statue with the artifact but I guess I failed to consider how powerful it would be, would Light Armour and a Simple action be better? Also the Wyld-Shaping is two way, YOU cant properly Wyld-Shape while it active either, my wording wasnt very clear though so I get the mix up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910105#post910105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this power. Actually, I think it's overpriced. Since it only works against those with the Cold Iron Bane, I'd be comfortable with this being 1 or 2 motes, easily. AND Essence 1. It's not that strong. Being able to apply it to anyone at Essence 3? Make that 4 or 5m.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I will definitely take the advice on the price, my thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910105#post910105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a little unclear how the Withering portion of this power works. Is total post-soak damage the die pool or the rolled Final damage? And is this <i>on top of</i> the normal initiative damage it deals? Needs clarification.<br /> <br /> The Decisive portion of this power is uh.. well, how long do those penalties last? Are they stackable? And even if they are, 12m, 2wp is unbelievably overpriced. The Decisive portion is not very strong at all unless I'm missing something. There's effects that ignore hardness entirely that are a fraction of that cost. So give this one a once-over. Decide what the goal of the evocation is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Withering deals with Final damage and it dealt in addition yes. The Decisive Penalties are meant to last for (Essence) Days, I made a note to fill that in but forgot about it, will definitely cheapen though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910105#post910105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this one as is. It's perfect and a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the prosthetic arm, and I like your choices of materials for the theme and direction of your artifact. But that opening power just strikes a wrong chord with me. I'm trying to be very clear that I'm not saying it's a badwrongfun evocation. This is strictly a personal preference, influencing my review.<br /> <br /> Am I the only one who can't think of this without imagining the Winter Soldier? ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually appreciate the advice since I am still figuring out Home-brewing and I am glad that it wasnt a complete mess since I was not terribly confident in it. I was actually trying to play on the Nuada Airgetlam myth since it seemed ironically appropriate for a Wyld-Focused arm but Winter Soldier is actually a fun image too.<br /> My thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:27:48-07:00","id":910245,"title":"","content":"So here's what I've made so far for my 17 Artifacts:<br /> <br /> Artifact types<br /> Goremaul--------------1<br /> Warfans--------------- 1<br /> Grand Grimcleaver 1<br /> Shield------------------ 2<br /> Longfang-------------- 1<br /> Razor Harness------ 1<br /> Skycutter--------------1<br /> Chain Shirt----------- 1<br /> Powerbow------------- 1<br /> Reaper Daiklave---- 1<br /> Wrackstaff------------ 2<br /> Articulated Plate---- 1<br /> Grand Daiklave------ 1<br /> Smashfist------------- 1<br /> Direlash---------------- 1<br /> <br /> Magical Materials (1 means a single material was used, 2 means it was half the materials used. Takes two 2's to make 1 artifact)<br /> Black Jade-------------2 1<br /> Blue Jade---------------2 1 2<br /> White Jade-------------2 1 2<br /> Green Jade-------------1<br /> Red Jade----------------2 1<br /> Orichalcum-------------2 1 2 1 1 1<br /> Moonsilver--------------1 2<br /> Starmetal----------------2<br /> Soulsteel-----------------1 2 2<br /> <br /> There's a lot one could infer from this about either materials I like or don't like. Or, you could infer what materials are more or less difficult to derive powers from their aspects.<br /> <br /> Anyways, my point. I need an idea. I made my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dxy9auJi1SOKk0coNGCRC1X6tkmzvtyMswVnYNjs0Eo/edit#gid=184168765\" target=\"_blank\">Artifact Generator</a> to help with ideas, but I'm not getting any of them off the ground. So I'll turn to folks for input. What should I make next? I'm not committing to using any given suggestion, I'm just looking for inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 06-08-2016, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:45:25-07:00","id":910254,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest making a Dragon Sigh Wand, maybe made out of soulsteel. I always liked the flame weapons and I'd love to see more of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1543-iethloc","name":"Iethloc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1543_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:48:15-07:00","id":910257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910245#post910245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What should I make next? I'm not committing to using any given suggestion, I'm just looking for inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one of my NPCs needs a mirror-themed moonsilver reaper daiklave, with Evocations centered around reaffirming the wielder's self (&quot;*glances in the mirror* oh right, this is who I <i>really </i>am&quot;). I may get around to making it myself eventually (right now I'm thinking about porting Bleach's soul slayers to Exalted as practice), but I'm kind of short on inspiration in that vein.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:55:37-07:00","id":910337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910245#post910245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, my point. I need an idea but I'm not getting any of them off the ground. So I'll turn to folks for input. What should I make next? I'm not committing to using any given suggestion, I'm just looking for inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to see an unconventional artifact made by Unsung, Red Jade eyes that fire blasts of essence or a grimoire bound in prehensile Starmetal chains that weaponizes history would be awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:12:12-07:00","id":910351,"title":"","content":"<b>Aegis of Compassion \u2013 White Jade and Starmetal Daiklave (***)</b><br /> <br /> One of the prized possessions of House V'Neef, the Aegis of Compassion has been used (some would say abused) to hunt and subdue Anathema for two centuries. Wyld Hunts bearing the Aegis of Compassion have a much higher rate of returning with a captive to the Nail, and the Empress herself has commended its wielders no fewer than three times. Despite, or perhaps because of, these accolades, the blade feels almost sullen in the hands of a shikari, functional but mildly resentful. In truth, it was forged not to hunt, but to preserve.<br /> <br /> The Aegis of Compassion is crafted as a long, square-ended daiklave of white jade with an intricate draconic shape cut into the width of the blade. Three starmetal rings are punched through the back edge of the blade, and a long, crimson tassel dangles from the pommel. It bears a single socket for a hearthstone.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Aegis of Compassion</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blood who attunes to the Aegis of Compassion for five motes can replace the Lethal tag with the Bashing tag at will.<br /> <br /> <b>Striking the Wicked Hand</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The Aegis of Compassion ever strives to protect its wielder, even when it sullenly resents the uses to which it is put. When an attacker strikes the wielder, the blade attempts to parry almost of its own accord, striking the attacker's hand and weakening his blow. This Evocation can be activated in response to a <b>withering</b> attack that successfully strikes the wielder despite his Parry Defense, immediately reducing the attack's minimum damage by one. This effect <b>can</b> reduce the minimum damage of an attack made by a non-Artifact weapon to zero.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pacify the Hurtful Arms</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Striking the Wicked Hand<br /> <br /> The Aegis of Compassion dislikes other weapons, for they are meant to injure. The blade strikes truest when disarming a foe rather than slaying him. Unfortunately for the sword, it has too often been used to do both in rapid succession. This Evocation supplements a disarm gambit, reducing its difficulty by one and re-rolling 6s until 6s fail to appear. This gambit cannot be used to disarm a shield; if so attempted, the gambit automatically fails. Shields are not weapons, at least in the eyes of the Aegis. Perhaps some part of it wishes it had been forged into a shield instead of a sword.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Aegis of Compassion</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Pacify the Hurtful Arms<br /> <br /> With this final Evocation, for which the blade itself was named, the wielder can produce cover from any ambient terrain - or even, if no such terrain is present, from a blurring afterimage of the sword. This Evocation functions as a reflexive but otherwise standard Take Cover action, which lasts for only an instant, enough to assist against a single attack and no more. The cover provided depends on the stunt used to describe creating it - a level one stunt provides light cover, level two provides heavy, and a level three stunt provides full cover. This Evocation functions by using the blade to chop cover from the surrounding scenery - hacking down a tree to fall in the way of an incoming attack, churning up a clod of dirt and clay to intercept a blow, or even simply utilizing the blade's blurring afterimage to provide an instant's cover. This last option is always available and always counts as a level one stunt. Remember that repetitive stunts rapidly lose interest and thus only the afterimage can be used repeatedly to create cover. Any other cover so created must be original and imaginative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":". 06-08-2016, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:12:52-07:00","id":910352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910337#post910337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see an unconventional artifact made by Unsung, Red Jade eyes that fire blasts of essence or a grimoire bound in prehensile Starmetal chains that weaponizes history would be awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:13:43-07:00","id":910353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910352#post910352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seconding the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thirding the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:28:23-07:00","id":910366,"title":"","content":"..that weaponizes <i>history </i>you say...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:29:25-07:00","id":910369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910366#post910366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..that weaponizes <i>history </i>you say...</div> </div> </div> </div>But please don't forget about starmetal chains ;-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T15:34:09-07:00","id":910370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910366#post910366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..that weaponizes <i>history </i>you say...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya Iiked the idea of the Deliberative wanting things like incarnate history and Terrestrial lineages, major battles and campaigns, etc in a much more durable and less flammable form.. and being the First Age it would of course be in 3(r)D! Do it as you wish but it would clearly be glorious!<br /> <br /> Good to see that I am not alone on the 'weaponize history' boat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 06-08-2016, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T16:56:27-07:00","id":910405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910351#post910351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Aegis of Compassion \u2013 White Jade and Starmetal Daiklave (***)</b><br /> <b>Evocations of the Aegis of Compassion</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blood who attunes to the Aegis of Compassion for five motes can replace the Lethal tag with the Bashing tag at will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fitting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910351#post910351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/B]<br /> <b>Striking the Wicked Hand</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The Aegis of Compassion ever strives to protect its wielder, even when it sullenly resents the uses to which it is put. When an attacker strikes the wielder, the blade attempts to parry almost of its own accord, striking the attacker's hand and weakening his blow. This Evocation can be activated in response to a <b>withering</b> attack that successfully strikes the wielder despite his Parry Defense, immediately reducing the attack's minimum damage by one. This effect <b>can</b> reduce the minimum damage of an attack made by a non-Artifact weapon to zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds about right. In most cases, this is going to be equivalent to 1 extra soak gained from Spirit Strengthens the Skin, which costs 1m/die. The ability to make non-artifact weapon hits irrelevant doesn't justify the cost by itself, in my eyes (you're basically spending three times the normal amount in order to eliminate the possibility of taking damage, that's a good deal pretty much only if you're at initiative 1-2 and that damage can crash you), but the synergies with Resistance charms that reset after not taking damage from X attacks make this a very potent and desirable effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910351#post910351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pacify the Hurtful Arms</b><br /> Cost: 4m,1W; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Striking the Wicked Hand<br /> <br /> The Aegis of Compassion dislikes other weapons, for they are meant to injure. The blade strikes truest when disarming a foe rather than slaying him. Unfortunately for the sword, it has too often been used to do both in rapid succession. This Evocation supplements a disarm gambit, reducing its difficulty by one. This gambit cannot be used to disarm a shield; if so attempted, the gambit automatically fails. Shields are not weapons, at least in the eyes of the Aegis. Perhaps some part of it wishes it had been forged into a shield instead of a sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... really pricey for what basically amounts to conjuring up +2 Initiative from thin air. Drop the WP cost at least. I'd say 3m would be a reasonable price for the effect as written, but I'd actually rather give it a bonus than reduce the cost. It's a starmetal alloy, how about fiddling with target numbers a bit, like granting reroll 6s on the attack roll in addition to the difficulty reduction, for 4 motes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910351#post910351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Aegis of Compassion</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Pacify the Hurtful Arms<br /> <br /> With this final Evocation, for which the blade itself was named, the wielder can produce cover from any ambient terrain - or even, if no such terrain is present, from a blurring afterimage of the sword. This Evocation functions as a reflexive Take Cover action, which lasts for only an instant, enough to assist against a single attack and no more. The cover provided depends on the stunt used to describe creating it - a level one stunt provides light cover, level two provides heavy, and a level three stunt provides full cover. This Evocation functions by using the blade to chop cover from the surrounding scenery - hacking down a tree to fall in the way of an incoming attack, churning up a clod of dirt and clay to intercept a blow, or even simply utilizing the blade's blurring afterimage to provide an instant's cover. This last option is always available and always counts as a level one stunt. Remember that repetitive stunts rapidly lose interest and thus only the afterimage can be used repeatedly to create cover. Any other cover so created must be original and imaginative.</div> </div> </div> </div>And we're already at the capstone. Short and to the point, I like it.<br /> <br /> However, I'm not entirely convinced that tying its effectiveness to stunt rating is the way to go. It basically means a player is tremendously unlikely to get full cover out of it (3 point stunts are supposed to be highlights of the entire session, with only one or two awarded to the entire group!), and even medium cover won't happen all that often (the guideline says players are supposed to get two or three per session, so even if they get one or two during combat, those aren't very likely to be actions enhanced by this charm).On the other hand, the pricing looks appropriate with that assumption in mind (3 motes for +1 non-charm defense is fairly generous, but balanced by the fact that it's basically useless if the battlefield already has plenty of cover).<br /> <br /> Also, the wording is slightly unclear - it's said to function as a reflexive Take Cover action (which is rolled with Dex + Dodge), yet it has the wielder using the blade to create cover from the scenery. Does it count as a Take Cover action that's automatically successful? Is it a regular Take Cover action? Maybe a Take Cover action that's rolled with Melee instead of Dodge? Hard to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T22:15:13-07:00","id":910570,"title":"","content":"So, here's a quick question regarding 2E -&gt; 3E conversion.<br /> <br /> There's a 3-dot artifact in <b>The Wonders of the Lost Age</b> (<b>The Books of Sorcery, Vol. I</b>) known as <b>Wound Mending Needles</b> (p. 66). They're a 3-dot, and their use is basically as-named: for cheap, they speed up Bashing healing; for moderate, the speed up Lethal healing; and for a large price (by comparison), they speed up Aggravated healing. Additionally, they will purge poison from the target if all poison-caused damage is healed by the needles.<br /> <br /> There's some more mechanics text, but that's the quick summary. So, question: would this just be a 2-dot by 3E's system, with those described effects and costs? Or would this a 3-dot, with those being evocations? If evocations, would it all simply be one evocation, or broken down into three evocations determined by damage type?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>EDIT</u></b>: Wow I completely forgot about the &quot;Additional Artifacts&quot; section in the book around page 601. So yeah, it'd just port over basically exactly as is, 3-dots and all. Sorry for the wasted post, but hopefully it helps others? &gt;_&lt;;;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":11797,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","user":"Seeker","date":". 06-09-2016, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T06:00:17-07:00","id":910712,"title":"","content":"Hello here is another artifact in need of a peer review. I'm a little worried the capstone might be too powerful but I was unsure of where else to go with it. I tried to make sure that the player had plenty of reasons to expend charges, so every charm after essence 1 requires at least one charge, All but 1 evocation benefit from expending a charge.<br /> <br /> Ravaging Flame<br /> Artifact 4 Soul steel and Red Jade Reaper Daiklave<br /> <br /> Forged for a Dragon Blooded agent of the First and Forsaken Lion, Ravaging Flame has earned it's name quickly as it hacked through armies, torn through defenses and burned a bloody swath through history. When the shogunate came to an end the Daiklave was glutted on battle and it's legacy was considered long and graced in slaughter. Eventually though that Dragon Blooded traitor was put down and is blade with thrust deep into river Styx without a realization that it had been given back to it's master. This malevolent blade passed from one servant to another until finally it awoke in a blaze of bloodshed that would have made the Neverborn weep tears of joy.<br /> <br /> Eventually the blade wound up in the hands of an abyssal who died at the hands of a newly returned Solar who claimed the blade for himself. Breaking the pattern of it being returned to the underworld by those who did not understand it's nature. For this blade was forged from the vindictive souls of those who burned to death. The red jade in the blade channels the rage they feel and the need to burn with the same fires they were burnt to death in. The soul steel channels their need to bring suffering and brings it to blazing upon the fools who stand against this blade.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Ravaging Flame</b><br /> When a tuned by a Solar, Dragon Blood, or Abyssal this blade burns brighter and hotter than at any other time. When ever it successfully deals lethal damage with a decisive attack it generates a flame charge.<br /> Each flame charge adds +1 withering damage. Ravaging Flame can only hold 4 charges.<br /> <br /> <b>Shield Shattering Blow</b><br /> <b>Cost </b>3m, 3i ; <b>Mins</b> essence 1<br /> <b>type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> The burning vengeance of the vengeful ghosts traded within the steel of this sword will not be denied just because someone happens to be quick with a shield. This Evocation brings the cleaving blade against the foolish thing that attempts to block it and rends and burns though it. Against mundane shields and weapons this evocation destroys what ever was used to parry the attack shattering it. Against an artifact it is thrown 1 range band away.<br /> <i>Special Activation Rules:</i> If a flame charge is expended as a part of activating this charm, than the blast of shattering flame burn the person holding the shield and they take an amount of damage equal to the overpower value of the weapon, this Initiative is gained by the weirder but not the +1 for a successful hit. If this causes initiative crash this bonus is also not gained.<br /> <br /> <b>Pyre Flame Radiance</b><br /> <b>Cost</b> -; <b>Mins</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanet<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decsiive - Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Gorging on the fire of life Ravaging Flame glows brighter than it would after just tasting blood. Generate 2 flame charges when a foe is slain with the weapon.<br /> <br /> <b>Burning Armor Touch</b><br /> <b>Cost</b> 3m, 1+ FC; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Pyre Flame Radiance, Shield Shattering Blow<br /> The burning spirits traded within the blade set alight the flesh of another making their armor, burning hot, and setting clothing on fire. This charm supplements a decisive attack and causes the subject if hit to be lit on fire taking environmental damage every round for a number of rounds equal to essence + Flame Charges expended. The difficulty to avoid this damage is increased by 1 for every flame charge expended.<br /> <br /> <b>Pyre Burns</b><br /> <b>Cost</b> 4m, 1+ FC; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-Only<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Burning Armor Touch<br /> The Roar of the funeral pyre brings such a strong heat that it can slowly cook the audience if they are not careful to stand back far enough. Thus does life fear fire, injuries from such are sever and fester easily, and worse yet cause pain that is so terrible those who die from this method of execution prey to suffocate before the flames finish with them as a final mercy. So it is with the flames of rage this weapon channels. The spirits burned to death seek to visit that pain and fate on others and they will stop at nothing to do so. For every Flame charge expended up to 1/2 the initiative gained apply a -2 penalty to dice pools, and a -1 penalty to defense for essence rounds as the painful burn from contact with the blade make movement and though more difficult.<br /> <br /> <b>Burning Ghostfire Torrent</b><br /> <b>Cost</b> 5m, 1wp, 1+FC; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Pyre Burns<br /> It doesn't take long for those who have mastered the Ravaging Flame to to realize that the power to project a holocaust of it's fire exists but it takes mastery of self to be able to draw out that power and deliver it to the field of battle without being immolated one's self. This charm creates a ranged decisive attack out to short range which adds Essence automatic success, this attack is unblockable. This attack Consumes the users Initiative, they we be left with 0 initiative regardless if it hits or misses, and all Flame Charges on the blade are likewise consumed. Decrease the target number for damage success by 1 for each Flame Charge charge consumed to a minimum of 4. Any excess charges add +2 damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":".  Adjusted some language for clarity and balance. 06-09-2016, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T09:37:00-07:00","id":910877,"title":"","content":"So I did a cursory outline for this tome concept. I ended up with two distinct Evocation trees. I decided to include them both into the artifact and it is now ginormous. I am generally very reluctant to have artifacts with big trees, not because I dislike the concept, but because honestly, no one wants to give play by play feedback on an item that'll take 30+ minutes to review. That said, I think my direction is surprisingly solid, so I'm sticking with it. Hoping to finish it today, but might be tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T09:52:41-07:00","id":910895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910712#post910712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravaging Flame; Artifact 4 Soul steel and Red Jade Reaper Daiklave<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Ravaging Flame</b><br /> When a tuned by a Solar, Dragon Blood, or Abyssal this blade burns brighter and hotter than at any other time. When ever it successfully deals lethal damage with a decisive attack it generates a flame charge.<br /> Each flame charge adds +1 withering damage. Ravaging Flame can only hold 4 charges.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume this means +1 withering damage passively on future attacks, as opposed to having to spend the charges to gain that? Either is fine, just a point of clarification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910712#post910712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shield Shattering Blow</b><br /> <b>Cost </b>3m, 3i ; <b>Mins</b> essence 1<br /> <b>type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> The burning vengeance of the vengeful ghosts traded within the steel of this sword will not be denied just because someone happens to be quick with a shield. This Evocation brings the cleaving blade against the foolish thing that attempts to block it and rends and burns though it. Against mundane shields and weapons this evocation destroys what ever was used to parry the attack shattering it. Against an artifact it is thrown 1 range band away.<br /> <i>Special Activation Rules:</i> If a flame charge is expended as a part of activating this charm, than the blast of shattering flame burn the person holding the shield and they take an amount of damage equal to the overpower value of the weapon, this Initiative is gained by the weirder but not the +1 for a successful hit. If this causes initiative crash this bonus is also not gained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personal preference, I'd make this a modified Disarm gambit rather than an automatically successful effect on any attack you spend the cost on. Probably just make it 3m and normal Disarm difficulty with same end effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910712#post910712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pyre Flame Radiance</b><br /> <b>Cost</b> -; <b>Mins</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanet<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decsiive - Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> Gorging on the fire of life Ravaging Flame glows brighter than it would after just tasting blood. Generate 2 flame charges when a foe is slain with the weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910712#post910712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Burning Armor Touch</b><br /> <b>Cost</b> 3m, 1+ FC; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Pyre Flame Radiance, Shield Shattering Blow<br /> The burning spirits traded within the blade set alight the flesh of another making their armor, burning hot, and setting clothing on fire. This charm supplements a decisive attack and causes the subject if hit to be lit on fire taking environmental damage every round for a number of rounds equal to essence + Flame Charges expended. The difficulty to avoid this damage is increased by 1 for every flame charge expended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presuming this is equivalent to a bonfire, I would add words to state that explicitly. Also, is this a normal environmental effect or a supernatural one? Can it be put out or do they just endure it? Not imbalanced either way, I think, just needs a few words of clarity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910712#post910712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pyre Burns</b><br /> <b>Cost</b> 4m, 1+ FC; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-Only<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Burning Armor Touch<br /> The Roar of the funeral pyre brings such a strong heat that it can slowly cook the audience if they are not careful to stand back far enough. Thus does life fear fire, injuries from such are sever and fester easily, and worse yet cause pain that is so terrible those who die from this method of execution prey to suffocate before the flames finish with them as a final mercy. So it is with the flames of rage this weapon channels. The spirits burned to death seek to visit that pain and fate on others and they will stop at nothing to do so. For every Flame charge expended up to 1/2 the initiative gained apply a -2 penalty to dice pools, and a -1 penalty to defense for essence rounds as the painful burn from contact with the blade make movement and though more difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they can spend 4 flame charges to give them a -8 on all dice pools and a -4 penalty for at least 2 rounds? That's extremely brutal. I would reduce the die pool penalty by half (-1) or I'd reduce the duration to a single round. Say the end of the wielder's next turn. Otherwise, good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910712#post910712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Burning Ghostfire Torrent</b><br /> <b>Cost</b> 5m, 1wp, 1+FC; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Pyre Burns<br /> It doesn't take long for those who have mastered the Ravaging Flame to to realize that the power to project a holocaust of it's fire exists but it takes mastery of self to be able to draw out that power and deliver it to the field of battle without being immolated one's self. This charm creates a ranged decisive attack out to short range which adds Essence automatic success, this attack is unblockable. This attack Consumes the users Initiative, they we be left with 0 initiative regardless if it hits or misses, and all Flame Charges on the blade are likewise consumed. Decrease the target number for damage success by 1 for each Flame Charge charge consumed to a minimum of 4. Any excess charges add +2 damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>So using this crashes the wielder. Per the rules of the book:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 Page 194</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a character enters Initiative Crash as a result of his own actions (such as by using a disengage action, which costs 2 Initiative to attempt, with only 2 Initiative remaining), he immediately loses another 5 Initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>So while it is VERY powerful, it's more punishing than you may realize. If you want to stick with this effect, I'd set it to 1 so they're not self-crashed.<br /> <br /> That said, this is off-the-bat a well designed and balanced weapon. Most of my commentary is rules clarifications, not broken things. It's cool, and you know me, I love charge-based mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T10:38:47-07:00","id":910941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910895#post910895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume this means +1 withering damage passively on future attacks, as opposed to having to spend the charges to gain that? Either is fine, just a point of clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are Correct is is passive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910895#post910895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personal preference, I'd make this a modified Disarm gambit rather than an automatically successful effect on any attack you spend the cost on. Probably just make it 3m and normal Disarm difficulty with same end effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I can do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910895#post910895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Excellent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't lie I just copied that from Black Wind, and changed the flavor text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910895#post910895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presuming this is equivalent to a bonfire, I would add words to state that explicitly. Also, is this a normal environmental effect or a supernatural one? Can it be put out or do they just endure it? Not imbalanced either way, I think, just needs a few words of clarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, yes it is supposed to be bonfire, I'll adjust that, and label it as a supernatural effect. Thank you for that feedback.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910895#post910895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So they can spend 4 flame charges to give them a -8 on all dice pools and a -4 penalty for at least 2 rounds? That's extremely brutal. I would reduce the die pool penalty by half (-1) or I'd reduce the duration to a single round. Say the end of the wielder's next turn. Otherwise, good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm adjusting that down to match the till end of wielder's next turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910895#post910895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So while it is VERY powerful, it's more punishing than you may realize. If you want to stick with this effect, I'd set it to 1 so they're not self-crashed.<br /> <br /> That said, this is off-the-bat a well designed and balanced weapon. Most of my commentary is rules clarifications, not broken things. It's cool, and you know me, I love charge-based mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll make that change I was hoping to avoid the self crash rule by stating you were reset to 0, but for the sake of clarity I'll say reset to 1. Glad to hear that the mechanics were mostly solid and just needed some polishing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:21:08-07:00","id":911033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=910941#post910941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll make that change I was hoping to avoid the self crash rule by stating you were reset to 0, but for the sake of clarity I'll say reset to 1. Glad to hear that the mechanics were mostly solid and just needed some polishing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm not so sure, personally. I mean, first of all, the mechanics simply don't reflect the flavor text (&quot;the power to project a holocaust of it's fire exists but it takes mastery of self to be able to draw out that power and deliver it to the field of battle without being immolated one's self&quot; - yet it comes with no risk of <i>actually </i>immolating yourself). A bigger problem I see is that granting an average of +0.3 successes per damage die is a lot harder to balance around than if it were a flat amount. It's roughly equal to +3 damage for every 10 Initiative. That's a lot of variance. I guess it's balanced by the WP cost and the soft reset condition (you want to build up to at least 3 flame charges, so you probably need to wound and drop a guy at the very least); nevertheless, it's really not how I'd have designed the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:00:40-07:00","id":911212,"title":"","content":"<b>The Captain\u2019s Bulwark \u2013 Orichalcum Shield (***)</b><br /> <br /> The Captain\u2019s Bulwark dates back to the Primordial War, when an aspiring Twilight forged the discus of unbreakable orichalcum to protect his circlemate from the worst ravages the enemies of the gods could offer. It was carried into battle by one of the finest warriors of the Solar host, who won victory after victory against the spawn of the Primordials. In the end, the warrior himself was lost in a reality flux in battle with one of the Primordials themselves, and neither his Exaltation nor the shield have been seen since.<br /> <br /> The Captain\u2019s Bulwark was a concave disk of orichalcum with straps of behemoth-leather. Its design was deliberately subdued, providing a greater focus on the Captain than the shield. Its outer surface was most famously lacquered with a series of concentric circles around a central image of the sun, though its current appearance could be wildly different, if it even still exists.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Captain\u2019s Bulwark:</b><br /> <br /> A Solar who attunes to the Captain\u2019s Bulwark gives the weapon the Thrown (Short) tag.<br /> <br /> <b>Righteous Ricochet</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The least of the Bulwark\u2019s powers is a simple ricochet trick, guided by its wielder\u2019s Essence. This Evocation can only be activated when the wielder succeeds at a <b>withering </b>Thrown attack made with the Captain\u2019s Bulwark. If the attack is successful, immediately before gaining any Initiative, the wielder can make one reflexive <b>decisive </b>Thrown attack with the Captain\u2019s Bulwark at any one target within Close range of the first target.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Righteous Recall</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Call the Blade<br /> <br /> The Captain\u2019s Bulwark always returns to its wielder\u2019s hand, sometimes by thoroughly circuitous routes. This Evocation is a permanent enhancement to its prerequisite, reducing the Charm\u2019s mote cost to zero if it is being used to recall the Captain\u2019s Bulwark.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Righteous Recoil</b><br /> Cost: 6m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The nature of the Bulwark is to absorb the force of any incoming attack, and so it does. This Evocation may be used in response to any attack that overcame its wielder\u2019s Parry Defense, if that Defense was calculated using the Captain\u2019s Bulwark. Any knockdown or knockback effects caused by that attack are wholly nullified, as the Bulwark absorbs and disperses the force of the blow without consequence to its wielder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":".  Suggested edits made 06-10-2016, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:57:04-07:00","id":911306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=911212#post911212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Captain\u2019s Bulwark \u2013 Orichalcum Shield (***)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Captain\u2019s Bulwark:</b><br /> <br /> A Solar who attunes to the Captain\u2019s Bulwark for five motes gives the weapon the Thrown (Short) tag.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wondered how long it would take someone to make this. All artifact weapons start at 5 motes, so is this 5 additional motes or 5 flat? Because you can probably just not say anything about the attunement to make it clearer if it's not additional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=911212#post911212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Righteous Ricochet</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Withering-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The least of the Bulwark\u2019s powers is a simple ricochet trick, guided by its wielder\u2019s Essence. This Evocation can only be activated when the wielder succeeds at a <b>decisive</b> Thrown attack made with the Captain\u2019s Bulwark. If the attack is successful, immediately after resetting to base Initiative, the wielder can make one reflexive <b>withering</b> Thrown attack with the Captain\u2019s Bulwark at any one target within Close range of the first target.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a mere 5 motes, you can almost completely nullify the downside of a Decisive attack by immediately attempting a Withering! Obviously, it's not a guarrantee, but I'm not sure I actually like this effect's impact on the game mechanics, because it means you're not likely to often end up in the danger zone. If it was reversed, letting you do a Decisive after a Withering, or even 2 Decisive's back to back (with the second one only using Base Initiative) I'd be more favorable to it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=911212#post911212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Righteous Recall</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Call the Blade<br /> <br /> The Captain\u2019s Bulwark always returns to its wielder\u2019s hand, sometimes by thoroughly circuitous routes. This Evocation is a permanent enhancement to its prerequisite, reducing the Charm\u2019s mote cost to zero if it is being used to recall the Captain\u2019s Bulwark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing wrong with this one, aside from I feel it's odd to fork it off of a melee charm instead of just creating an evocation that says you can reflexively call it back to you. Otherwise, it seems like the sort of thing the Captain <i>should</i> be able to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=911212#post911212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Righteous Recoil</b><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The nature of the Bulwark is to absorb the force of any incoming attack, and so it does. This Evocation may be used in response to any attack that overcame its wielder\u2019s Parry Defense, if that Defense was calculated using the Captain\u2019s Bulwark. Any knockdown or knockback effects caused by that attack are wholly nullified, as the Bulwark absorbs and disperses the force of the blow without consequence to its wielder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reluctant to approve of anything that perfectly nullifies an effect like knockback, especially at Essence 1, and <b>especially</b> for 1 mote. It could be bonus dice to it, or it could be like 6m in cost. But I've seen (and personally designed) a lot of knockback affects, and to negate them for a one-time evocation purchase and 1 mote is... dismissive.<br /> <br /> But conceptually, this is all in the right space! Could go upwards from here with adding ricochets, deflecting attacks, absorbing falling damage, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:03:05-07:00","id":911310,"title":"","content":"Well, here it is. My Artifact Grimoire. It is <b>enormous</b> by my standards. It clocks in at 7 evocations, in 2 trees which meet at the top. Some of it is solid. Some of it is shakey. I think one evocation is broken. I KNOW it's a slog, but since I made this on crowd recommendation, I'd appreciate a little feedback. Thanks guys!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Opus of Antiquity (Starmetal Grimoire/Dire Chains *****)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> Orphene Sagastorm was one of the first twilights to ever grace Creation. Receiving her second breath at the end of the great war of the gods, she showed no talent for combat, and yet she loved war. She displayed no skill at politics, yet she never missed a debate. She claimed no skill in the Occult, yet she studied books and scrolls from every corner of the globe. Orphene loved one thing before all others: history. She wanted to witness and record every major battle, every sweeping decree, every fact of history so that it was never lost to the ravages of time.<br /> <br /> It was to this end that she set down to forging her masterwork. Together with her Sidereal partner, a woman of limitless patience, who loved Orphene despite being forever second to her thirst for knowledge, the twilight set to creating a single central tome to record her work. She wove the pages from the silk of pattern spiders, the binding from thin filiments of Starmetal, and the cover bound in the leather of a rare god-blooded elk blessed with immortality by the moon and the stars. The book was then wrapped with chains of solid Starmetal and fixed with a lock of pure Orichalcum which bared no keyhole.<br /> <br /> The pages would keep only the events recorded by fate in the purest form through the eyes and words of its author. The binding and cover would keep the words eternal and unravaged by time, while also allowing an infinite number of pages to exist within its confines. The chains would keep the knowledge and power of infinite history written within contained and safely channeled. The lock would ensure none but those worthy of the book could ever release its potent power.<br /> <br /> The Opus of Antiquity is a Starmetal Grimoire wrapped in Dire Chains. It functions as a weapon when it needs to, but is primarily designed as a record of history. The book may be carried with one hand, but when the chains are active, it must be wielded with two hands to contain the powers of the book in the absence of its restraints. When not in use, the chains will retract to bind the book closed and the lock will snap shut, once again containing the power of the Opus.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800080\">Evocations of Opus of Antiquity</span></b><br /> When a Solar or Sidereal spends the cost of 7 motes to attune to the Opus of Antiquity, the exalt can feel through the chains that bind the ancient tome. With but a thought, the unbreakable lock on these ancient restraints snaps open and the chains come alive. The Starmetal chains move in accordance to the will of the wielder and can extend beyond their apparent length to accomplish their goal within Close range. For all intents and purposes, these function as Dire Chains with the usual tags under the control of their wielder.<br /> <br /> The exalt may substitute their Lore rating for Melee or Martial Arts to control the chains, but then the cap for dice added from charms is half the normal pool rounded up. Attacks with the chains may be enhanced as normal with Martial Arts or Melee charms, but must use the appropriate ability rating to do so.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Unbound Knowledge</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Uniform<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> The chains that hold the Opus of Antiquity are attuned to knowledge, and can reveal it as easily as withhold it. An successful attack supplemented by Unbound Knowledge reveals a single piece of information about the target chosen by the exalt upon activating this evocation.<ul><li>The highest rated combat ability and its strength (number of dots). If used multiple times, this evocation reveals the next highest combat ability, or the highest non-combat ability if none remain</li> <li>An Intimacy that is actively being pursued or defended at the moment and its intensity. If used multiple times, this reveals another related Intimacy and so on until no applicable Intimacies remain</li> <li>The target\u2019s permanent Essence or Willpower score</li> </ul>Only 1 piece of knowledge may be revealed per attack. If the exalt knows at least 2 pieces of knowledge about a foe, they increase all defenses against that target by 1. This increase is a non-charm bonus. Facts discovered through means other than this power cannot benefit Opus of Antiquity or its evocations and must still be revealed through this Unbound Knowledge. All discovered facts fade from the Opus\u2019 knowledge at the end of the scene.<br /> <i>Authors notes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I wanted a hook to hang future evocations off of with the chains, and with Starmetal as the selected material, I decided to have it <i>reveal hidden truths</i> about the target. And, while it is building up for future powers, it also needed an immediate benefit to this knowledge, hence the defense. Basically, it's <i>translating one kind of power for another</i>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Primer of Yesteryear</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> The Opus is a history book without peer and the words within it are a living document of the past. When the exalt faces a problem to be solved through Bureaucracy, Investigation, Lore, or Occult, they may attempt to use the Opus of Antiquity to help aid them.<br /> <br /> When the exalt successfully introduces an original fact that explains a past event in history and how it tangentially relates to a current subject or problem, the wielder may open the Opus and channel the event through it. The historical event referenced then appears as a ghostly image before the exalt and any gathered. The display shows the event accurately, but the only sound that plays is the narration of the event as recorded by the original author. By spending a scene analysing this projection, the exalt gains a flash of insight into the current predicament and gains the lower of 3 or Essence non-charm automatic successes on a roll to learn or apply such knowledge. This event cannot be referenced for the same purpose more than once.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> Primer of Yesteryear only unlocks to an exalt who has spent either a season or a story studying the lessons and stories of the Opus of Antiquity. This means at least 8 hours of study a week for the duration.<br /> <i>Authors notes:</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This is the beginning of my other tree, where it was suggested that I &quot;weaponize history&quot;. It needed to start small, so I figured... this is a history book, it should benefit Lore somehow. So this was an attempt to <i>reveal hidden truths</i> combined with <i>exuding God-miracles. </i>This was also my first attempt at something I saw the devs mention recently. Evocations are supposed to be a story and/or representation of the relationship one has with their artifact. It's not just a power-stick. This is why Special Activation Rules exist and why some weapons are designed with restrictions for learning, unlocking, and using their evocations. It wants you to have a relationship with your artifact. SO, the Opus has 2 trees. The chains which you can learn regardless and just be a chain book guy, and then the pages which require effort and study, giving you time to really connect with the book. That was my thinking anyways.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Art of War</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4m, 1+A <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Counterattack<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Unbound Knowledge<br /> <br /> The Opus of Antiquity contains knowledge of strategums and maneuvers from dozens of histories famous and infamous warlords. By channeling this knowledge, the exalt gains insight into how to counter the actions of their foes.<br /> <br /> Once the exalt has gathered at least 3 pieces of knowledge about a foe revealed via Unbound Knowledge, they may reflexively activate Art of War in response to a gambit from that target. Declared after a successful attack roll but before the gambit is rolled, the exalt may spend the cost of the evocation and shed levels of their anima to increase the difficulty of the gambits being attempted by 1 per Anima level.<br /> <br /> If the attacking gambit is unsuccessful after using Art of War, the wielder may reflexively attempt to counter with an identical gambit if they haven\u2019t used their combat action yet this round.<br /> <i>Authors notes:</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Back to the chains. I had a different effect in mind for this one until I came upon the name Art of War. Brilliant for a comprehensive book of history right? Of course this book will contain strategies of famous warlords, so I figured it should be useful in countering such strategies. If I were more knowledgable in mass combat rules, I'd include stuff for actual Strategems. So if you're savvy in that area, this is where you'd add that ability to this artifact. Anyways this falls into <i>unraveling tactics</i>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Adversary Composition</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 10m, 1wp <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Art of War<br /> <br /> <br /> Through knowledge of a thing, one can begin to understand its nature. Through knowledge of nature, one can transfigure the understanding of a thing. When the exalt knows at least 5 pieces of knowledge revealed via Unbound Knowledge, they may unleash a special gambit attack against foe that warps a quality of their nature. This attack is a shaping effect and is subject to any rules that interact with such.<br /> <br /> On a successful gambit at difficulty equal to the target\u2019s Essence, the exalt chooses an aspect to alter in their target. For every 2 threshold successes on the gambit roll, the exalt may select an additional effect to inflict upon their foe.<ul><li>Alter the emotional context of a Tie or swap the context (positive/negative) of a Principle</li> <li>Swap the intensities of two revealed Intimacies</li> <li>Swap the rating of a revealed combat ability with that of a revealed non-combat ability</li> <li>Swap the rating of any two Attributes from different categories (Physical/Mental/Social). Use of this power does not confer knowledge of those Attribute ratings</li> <li>Swap Personal/Peripheral essence pools</li> <li>Swap Essence and Willpower ratings. Temporary Willpower above the new permanent rating is reduced by an equal number</li> <li>Other effects may be negotiated with Storyteller. All effects must be a swapping of current states, never created or eliminated ones</li> </ul>All changes last for the rest of the scene before fading away and reverting to normal.<br /> <i>Author's notes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This... is the evocation I feel pretty shaky about. I tried to come up with a long list of interesting powers of <i>translating one kind of power into another</i> and <i>striking or harnessing e<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">phemeral </span></span></i><i>concepts</i> but I admit to struggling with this the most. I'm very open to other suggestions, but I didn't want it to interact with Initiative or Defense scores at all, because that quickly unbalances things. It's supposed to be a <b>weird</b> one and I think I succeeded in that regard.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Doctrine of History</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 10m <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: 8 hours<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Primer of Yesteryear<br /> <br /> For an exalt that has learned to truly harness their Essence, the Opus of Antiquity lies waiting for their contribution. The lorekeeper activates the evocation and then spends at least 8 uninterrupted hours recording every conceivable detail of a significant event that they have personally witnessed. The cost of this evocation is committed for the duration of the recording, and if the session is interrupted, the power deactivates and the words the exalt recorded evaporate from the pages as dust in a breeze.<br /> <br /> At the end of this session, the Opus of Antiquity glows brightly with starry light as the words are committed to the tome forever. The recorded event is forever bound to the Opus and may be recalled in the future via Primer of Yesteryear. Additionally, the exalt who recorded it is granted a free permanent specialty pertaining to the subject of which they wrote. Finally, spending time recording events in the Opus is considered a magically accelerated training session. Training times for raising a single knowledge-based non-combat Ability, or Mental-based Attribute may be completed entirely during the duration of Doctrine of History.<br /> <br /> This evocation cannot be used more than once per story unless reset by using Primer of Yesteryear to resolve another significant situation.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules</b>: Doctrine of History may only be learned after the exalt resolves at least 3 problems or situations thanks to the evocation Primer of Yesteryear, as learning to understand the function and flow of the recorded history and its powers is crucial to properly contributing to the volume.<br /> <i>Author's notes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Back over to the history tree, this evocation is meant to be the one that keys it's predicessor. Yes, it <b>is</b> weird that it takes a higher essence evocation to create things for a lesser one to use, but I wanted it to represent a higher mastery of Essence to be able to interact with the book on such a level. Anyone can pull information from it, but it takes a master to write <b>to</b> it. I got to the end of it though and found it didn't have... much bite. Much mechanical benefit to it. So I tacked on the increased training time as an afterthought. I don't know how it translated in the end, but if it feels weird, that's why.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Yarn of Battle</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 10m, 1wp, +(5+m, 1+wp) <b>Mins</b>: Essence 4<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Doctrine of History<br /> <br /> The stories of many great and terrible battles are recorded in the pages of the Opus of Antiquity. At the decree of the lorekeeper, the armies of these battles stand ready to be commanded. Activating Yarn of Battle causes misty images of armies long forgotten to appear before the exalt. This army is not made of spirits, they are simply reflections of history and are very real to the foes of the exalt.<br /> <br /> This evocation creates a Battlegroup of Battle Ready Troops. The context of their appearance is left at the behest of the wielder based on which battle they were summoned from, but their stats remain the same. Yarn of Battle creates a Size 1 group with Poor Drill, and Might 0. However, for every 5 additional motes spent on the activation, the exalt may increase the Size by 1. For every additional Willpower spent, they may increase the Drill by 1. By increasing the reset of this evocation to one Season, the exalt may Increase the Might to 1.<br /> <br /> This Battlegroup is loyal to the wielder of the Opus and vanishes at the end of the scene. This evocation may only be used once per day unless extended to 1 season as written above.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules</b>: Yarn of Battle may only be learned after the exalt has contributed the story of at least 3 significant events to the Opus of Antiquity via the evocation Doctrine of History.<br /> <i>Author's notes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This evocation I knew would be in there from the first moment it was suggested to me. It was the first thought I had. Summon an army from history. I like this one a lot. I <b>think</b> I have the power-up balanced. I could just as easily be convinced that it should take 10m per increase in Size, but I was trying to compare it to similar abilities (of which there aren't many). This is yet another example of requiring the bond between wielder and artifact to improve.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Saga Convocation</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 15m, 1wp <b>Mins</b>: Essence 5<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Yarn of Battle, Adversary Composition<br /> <br /> The greatest power of the Opus of Antiquity is its terrifying ability to absorb the heroes of past generations. Those upon death\u2019s door who willingly submit to the will of the Opus may choose to become a champion of the book instead of dying. This power effectively removes the will of the subject (and removing their ability to be a PC) making them a slave to the book and records them as an echo within the pages of the tome.<br /> <br /> Alternately, when a Decisive attack with the Opus of Antiquity successfully deals a foe\u2019s last health level of damage, the exalt may reflexively activate Saga Convocation attempt to force the foe into the book instead of killing them. This functions as a contested permanent Willpower roll, with a bonus or difficulty of the difference between (exalt\u2019s Resolve - target\u2019s Resolve). On a failure, the target dies normally instead.<br /> <br /> All such characters absorbed into the Opus are pulled in via the Starmetal chains and are considered Retainers. Yarn of Battle upgrades upon learning Saga Convocation to allow the summoning of these champions for the base evocation cost with no ability to upgrade them. These champions are much more potent than the echoes of armies long past, retaining their charms, abilities, and other powers. However, the Opus struggles to contain such power, and using a champion in this manner releases it at the end of the scene. The tome may contain no more than 3 champions at a time.<br /> <i>Author's notes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The capstone. I must have rewritten this one the most. I think it ended up working out as balanced. It was hard coming up with a difficulty to drag something into it. I couldn't think of all the possible situations that could be in here, but at least Willpower rolls aren't modifiable. But I'm happy with how it came out. Believe it or not, the <b>willing</b> subject was the afterthought on this one. I also loved the idea of the chains pulling a foe into the book to be trapped as a servant. hehe </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 06-10-2016, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:43:45-07:00","id":911337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=911310#post911310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, here it is. My Artifact Grimoire. It is <b>enormous</b> by my standards. It clocks in at 7 evocations, in 2 trees which meet at the top. Some of it is solid. Some of it is shakey. I think one evocation is broken. I KNOW it's a slog, but since I made this on crowd recommendation, I'd appreciate a little feedback. Thanks guys!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Opus of Antiquity (Starmetal Grimoire/Dire Chains *****)</b></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is simply magnificent, my only complaint is that I can only Like it once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:41:14-07:00","id":911386,"title":"","content":"I went back and added my personal comments about the design of each evocation in there. Whew, I'm pooped. To bed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T06:26:05-07:00","id":911611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=911310#post911310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Through knowledge of a thing, one can begin to understand its nature. Through knowledge of nature, one can transfigure the understanding of a thing. When the exalt knows at least 5 pieces of knowledge revealed via Unbound Knowledge, they may unleash a special gambit attack against foe that warps a quality of their nature. This attack is a shaping effect and is subject to any rules that interact with such.<ul><li>On a successful gambit at difficulty equal to the target\u2019s Essence, the exalt chooses an aspect to alter in their target. For every 2 threshold successes on the gambit roll, the exalt may select an additional effect to inflict upon their foe.</li> <li>Alter the emotional context of a Tie or swap the context (positive/negative) of a Principle</li> <li>Swap the intensities of two revealed Intimacies</li> <li>Swap the rating of a revealed combat ability with that of a revealed non-combat ability</li> <li>Swap Personal/Peripheral essence pools</li> <li>Swap Essence and Willpower ratings. Temporary Willpower above the new permanent rating is reduced by an equal number</li> <li>Other effects may be negotiated with Storyteller. All effects must be a swapping of current states, never created or eliminated ones</li> </ul><br /> All changes last for the rest of the scene before fading away and reverting to normal.<br /> <i>Author's notes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This... is the evocation I feel pretty shaky about. I tried to come up with a long list of interesting powers of <i>translating one kind of power into another</i> and <i>striking or harnessing e<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">phemeral </span></span></i><i>concepts</i> but I admit to struggling with this the most. I'm very open to other suggestions, but I didn't want it to interact with Initiative or Defense scores at all, because that quickly unbalances things. It's supposed to be a <b>weird</b> one and I think I succeeded in that regard.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Just a suggestion, but if this Evocation is to translate on power into another and for me the Essence/Willpower swap seems a MASSIVE deal, but what about a translation of attribute dots? Shifting a Charismatic warlord into an attractive concubine through moving some attributes around as long as it sticks with the caps. Or it could break those caps by allowing you to make someone fantastic at one aspect and reducing their capabilities in another for a brief time. I dunno, I feel under qualified for this kind of thing but there's no time like the present to have a go at critique.<br /> <br /> That and the rest of this artifact sounds amazing so its pretty much out there when put against a sword or suit of armour. Kudos on the mental gymnastics by the way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11900-grynder","name":"Grynder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T08:21:28-07:00","id":911670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grynder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=911611#post911611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a suggestion, but if this Evocation is to translate on power into another and for me the Essence/Willpower swap seems a MASSIVE deal, but what about a translation of attribute dots? Shifting a Charismatic warlord into an attractive concubine through moving some attributes around as long as it sticks with the caps. Or it could break those caps by allowing you to make someone fantastic at one aspect and reducing their capabilities in another for a brief time. I dunno, I feel under qualified for this kind of thing but there's no time like the present to have a go at critique.<br /> <br /> That and the rest of this artifact sounds amazing so its pretty much out there when put against a sword or suit of armour. Kudos on the mental gymnastics by the way</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the comments! So I knew not all of these were necessarily going to even be a punishment on characters, just something to fuck with them. Swapping Willpower and Essence scores will obviously massively increase most Essence ratings and reduce most Willpower ratings. While this might increase some calculations that base off Essence scores, it explicitely removes excess Willpower from your pool for the duration, so you have fewer resources in that regard. That can be useful at times.<br /> <br /> I liked your Attribute idea and added it to the list. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T09:14:20-07:00","id":911706,"title":"","content":"I am having trouble coming up with an artifact flame piece for a character I am designing. I would like to supplement rather than improve Righteous Devil Style but I am having trouble even conceptualizing something that won't be unbalanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11958-zerobadguy","name":"ZeroBadguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T14:41:55-07:00","id":911903,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">Ok so not quite as epic as the Book of Weaponised History but I'm posting this up anyway. Earth Cracker is a hammer inspired from one of my circle mates in the game I'm taking part in that adds some defence benefits at first then causes minor aggressive until the capstone. Any comments or feed back is welcome as usual <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Earth Cracker (Artifact 3; White Jade Goremaul)</b><br /> <br /> During the First Age, the mortal White Obelisk exalted as a member of the Dawn Caste for defence during the siege of the palace of Baiya. Her first task was a retaliation attack but before she committed she was inspired to forge a weapon that could allow her and her alone to lead a siege.<br /> <br /> Earth Cracker was the answer. Having bested a greater earth elemental, Multifaceted Terrani, to a duel it agreed to help the young Solar channel her dream. In the depths of his court, they cold forged the hammer with the force of Creations earth itself. Next the head of the hammer was carved and molten orichalcum poured into the recesses of the faces and forged into a collar where the head meets haft.<br /> <br /> When the Usurpation took place Obelisk became furious at the betrayal and assaulted the island where a garrison of traitors was holed up. The weapon and wielder both full of wrath sank the island and killed the betrayers with their death throes.<br /> <br /> The huge head of the weapon has been carved from a single large piece of white jade to depict the image of a ram on either side, with a collar just before the rams head of orichalcum leading to the haft of the weapon. The haft is decorated in old realm runes, tailored to more specific sentences and grammar of earth elementals. The weapon has a hearth stone socket between the ram heads.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Earth Cracker</b><br /> Solars and Dragon-Blooded attuning to Earth Cracker feel heavily attuned to the earth around them. They gain their essence in automatic successes to resist knock down or knock back.<br /> <br /> <b>Raise the Stones Bones</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive or Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Withering Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant or One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> The earth and dirt never forget, holding generations of fallen comrades, family and friends. When the wielder of Earth Cracker invokes Raise the Stones Bones, she strikes the ground and forces a large slab of stone to rent the earth and prevent another fallen comrade.<br /> <br /> Raise the Stones Bones creates a protective barrier which provides heavy cover; when used as a Reflexive defend other action, the Evocation adds the wielders (Essence) to their own Parry or Evasion and improving soak by 2 from up to short range before breaking apart at the end of the round.<br /> <br /> At Essence 2+ and cost of 6m, 1wp Raise the Stones Bones can create (Essence x2) heavy cover barriers as a Simple action out to (Essence) range bands that last for the scene, but provide no benefit to defences or soak.<br /> <br /> At the end of a round or scene, depending on how the Evocation was used, the stone pillars drop away into tiny multifaceted pieces of stone, dirt and escaping essence.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules<br /> If used in its Simple format the Raise the Stones Bones can only be used once a scene, unless the wielder of the weapon systematically destroys each pillar, releasing the essence back into the earth.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremor Incanting Method</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 2i <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> As the hammer strikes the ground, the spirits residing within answer the call and bring forth a rapid shaking like which follows an earthquake.<br /> Tremor Incanting Method creates a knock down effect affecting all who are within short range. All trivial opponents fall prone without contest while battlegroups and non trivial enemies such as<br /> Exalted, spirits and mortal heroes must pass a Stamina+Athletics difficulty 4.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3+ Tremor Incanting Method draws forth even more of the roiling aggression beneath the soil that causes the ground to shudder, shake and split in the affected area that creates and environmental hazard that causes 3B at difficulty 3 for Essence turns.<br /> <br /> <b>Invoking Terrani\u2019s Fangs</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Raise the Stone Bones, Tremor Incanting Method<br /> <br /> With an immense war cry, the wielder bellows out for Terrani who still resides within the bones of the world to join his essence with the weapons again. As the essence of weapon and spirit mingle, a terrifying fang of stone careens out of the earth ripping the ground as it travels to its target before colliding and crumbling into the stones that formed it.<br /> <br /> Invoking Terrani\u2019s Fangs creates a withering attack that can attack up to long range. At close range the attack roll gains double 7s and knocks enemies prone, short range gains double 8s and the enemy must resist falling prone with a Stamina+Athletics at difficulty 4, medium range double 9s and long range provides no additional benefit beyond attacking at that range.<br /> <br /> As a repurchase, the wielder can spend an additional 2m, Invoking Terrani\u2019s Fangs doesn\u2019t destroy the \u201cfang\u201d afterwards but instead bulwarks it with additional jutting slabs. For the rest of the scene the fang remains as an additional piece of heavy cover that isn\u2019t affected by Raise the Stones Bones limit.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3+ for an additional 1wp the wielder can use the fangs eruption to destroy stone pillars already called forth by Raise the Stone Bones. Adding this provides the wielder with (Essence) non-charm automatic successes on a withering attack roll, as well as converting (Essence) post soak damage dice. This improvement cannot gain any benefit from the previous Essence based improvement.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules</b><br /> The wielder must have Strength 4+ and a speciality with the weapon or during a siege.<br /> <br /> <b>Rending the Worlds Form</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 8m, 1wp, 3a <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Invoking Gaia\u2019s Fangs<br /> <br /> Plunging the head of the hammer into the ground beneath the wielders feet small rents around the hammer blow span outward, causing orbs of white-grey essence to escape the cracks in the world. As the head is released from the earth, a shockwave ripples along the rented lines and the full power comes into effect.<br /> <br /> Rending the Worlds Form causes an earthquake and rented fissures out to six range band that demolishes buildings, entraps living beings and kills the unwary who are too close.<br /> Within the first two range bands all mundane structures are destroyed without contest and all living beings suffer damage as if they have fallen from medium height. Trivial opponents suffer the effects without contest and mightier opponents, such as gods and the Exalted roll Stamina+Athletics at difficulty 4.<br /> At range bands three and four the shock wave causes 30 dice of damage against mundane structures and causes living enemies to suffer damage as if falling from a short range band after failing a Stamina+Athletics difficulty 4.<br /> At the last two range bands the effects dwindle out, causing 15 dice of damage to mundane structures and causing living enemies to fall prone after a much easier roll at difficulty 2<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules<br /> The wielder must have Strength 4+ and a speciality with the weapon or during a siege. Rending the Worlds Form can only be used once per story, its reset condition requiring the wielder to bury the weapon in a cavern anywhere on Creation for three nights and three days with earthy smelling incense burning. During this time the weapon cannot be unearth prematurely or the ritual must begin again.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11900-grynder","name":"Grynder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T16:36:09-07:00","id":911962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZeroBadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=911706#post911706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am having trouble coming up with an artifact flame piece for a character I am designing. I would like to supplement rather than improve Righteous Devil Style but I am having trouble even conceptualizing something that won't be unbalanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woo flame pieces and RDS!<br /> <br /> Okay, so, first thing to talk about is what way you want to supplement RDS. What is your character bringing, as a concept, to the Righteous Devil Style? Is your character a cautious justicar, trying to compromise before letting loose the fires of judgment? Then perhaps more social evocations, or gambits aiming to disable rather than kill. Is she a rugged in-your-face vigilante who shoots first and asks questions later, sure of her own righteousness? Then perhaps an altered flame piece that works more like a short-range blunderbuss or shotgun, aiming to punish enemies for getting close. Or maybe he's a surgical one-man strike force, going for accuracy, crippling, and stealth--admittedly hard for a FLAME weapon, but the evocations could bring in some momentary blinding and disorientation while they stay on the move, never giving his target a chance to counter.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you're looking to supplement, rather than embody, then you need to consider how your character is <i>different</i> from that Unnamed Solar, the original Righteous Devil. What new approach is your character bringing to the table?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T16:39:59-07:00","id":911965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZeroBadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=911706#post911706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am having trouble coming up with an artifact flame piece for a character I am designing. I would like to supplement rather than improve Righteous Devil Style but I am having trouble even conceptualizing something that won't be unbalanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are at least 2 or 3 Flame Pieces in this topic, didn't you find them to your tastes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T17:28:38-07:00","id":911989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=911962#post911962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Woo flame pieces and RDS!<br /> <br /> Okay, so, first thing to talk about is what way you want to supplement RDS. What is your character bringing, as a concept, to the Righteous Devil Style? Is your character a cautious justicar, trying to compromise before letting loose the fires of judgment? Then perhaps more social evocations, or gambits aiming to disable rather than kill. Is she a rugged in-your-face vigilante who shoots first and asks questions later, sure of her own righteousness? Then perhaps an altered flame piece that works more like a short-range blunderbuss or shotgun, aiming to punish enemies for getting close. Or maybe he's a surgical one-man strike force, going for accuracy, crippling, and stealth--admittedly hard for a FLAME weapon, but the evocations could bring in some momentary blinding and disorientation while they stay on the move, never giving his target a chance to counter.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you're looking to supplement, rather than embody, then you need to consider how your character is <i>different</i> from that Unnamed Solar, the original Righteous Devil. What new approach is your character bringing to the table?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is excellent advice. I was thinking of the surgical one man strike force. And Daerion, I must have missed the previous flame pieces when I was reading the topic. I do a lot of this right before I go to sleep and it can cause me to miss things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11958-zerobadguy","name":"ZeroBadguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T17:48:55-07:00","id":912001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZeroBadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=911989#post911989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is excellent advice. I was thinking of the surgical one man strike force. And Daerion, I must have missed the previous flame pieces when I was reading the topic. I do a lot of this right before I go to sleep and it can cause me to miss things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well mine's currently up for critique--you can see the link in my signature, it's the one called <b>Omens of the Pyre [Corona+Umbra]</b>. They follow more along the lines of the &quot;cautious justicar&quot;, however.<br /> <br /> As for the one-man strike force, you'd want evocations that work toward mixing survivability and pressure. Gambit-supplement evocations are always a great idea, including coming up with new gambits--such as, for instance, one that aims to blind them with an essence-enhanced flame that sears white-hot rather than orange and yellow. Maybe some evocations that tie in with Athletics and Dodge in some way, keeping yourself at exactly the right distance, pushing or disengaging as necessary. If you're looking to press more into the control-aspect, maybe an evocation that sets the scene ablaze, turning it into an environmental hazard that they have to keep up with--either they take the constant damage, or they get funneled into tighter corners, making your shots that much easier.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T17:52:52-07:00","id":912004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b