-evocation-workshop?p=894528#post894528\"> [3E] The Artifact and Evocation Workshop - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894528#post894528\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894528#post894528 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I've been thinking recently that there are more topics popping up around Artifacts and their associated Evocations. These are great for individual critique, but having each one be its own individual topic means that after the feedback it falls off the front page. That's too bad, because a lot of these ideas are pretty awesome and could be really useful to others for use in their own games. So in the interest of 1) cutting down on the topic-clutter, and 2) consolidating everybody's neat ideas in one place, I thought it might be nice to have a single topic where folks can post their Artifacts and </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907881#post907881\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...881#post907881</a> (never version)<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=897187#post897187\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=897187#post897187\"> [3E] The Artifact and Evocation Workshop - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=897187#post897187\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=897187#post897187 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I've been thinking recently that there are more topics popping up around Artifacts and their associated Evocations. These are great for individual critique, but having each one be its own individual topic means that after the feedback it falls off the front page. That's too bad, because a lot of these ideas are pretty awesome and could be really useful to others for use in their own games. So in the interest of 1) cutting down on the topic-clutter, and 2) consolidating everybody's neat ideas in one place, I thought it might be nice to have a single topic where folks can post their Artifacts and </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T01:50:06-07:00","id":912153,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Threw this together on a whim since I couldn't sleep. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I adapted and expanded on the old 2.5 charm, from the Ink Monkeys (Thousand-Arms Prana, to be exact), until I had something fun out of it.<br /> I'm sure someone here will find a use for this because I don't think we'll be using it in this upcoming campaign.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800080\">Grand Forge of the Desert Tyrant</span></b> (Orichalcum Artifact ****):<br /> <a href=\"http://store.tcgplayer.com/magic/product/show?ProductName=Attunement&amp;partner=AUTOANY&amp;affiliate_id=autocard&amp;utm_campaign=affiliate&amp;utm_source=autocard&amp;utm_medium=card\" target=\"_blank\">Attunement</a>: 7m<br /> Prerequisites:<br /> Martial Arts/Archery/Melee/Thrown 5<br /> A Definitive Intimacy towards upholding ideals of Justice and Heroism.<br /> <br /> <b>Lore/Fluff:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> A Solar knelt in the bloodstained sands, his essence spent, his will gone.<br /> The Wyld ruler who had claimed the far Southern steppes.<br /> With his thirteen greatest knights beside him.<br /> The tattered remains of his grand army stood before the Solar.<br /> Only he remained between them and the edges of Creation.<br /> A fight he could not win.<br /> A battle that was already lost.<br /> A war that had ended the moment it had begun.<br /> Yet the Solar would not accept defeat.<br /> In the falling ashes of his sorrow.<br /> The Solar answered the Desert's roar.<br /> He signed the Tyrant's Pact,<br /> And the Tyrant bestowed upon his soul.<br /> A piece of the Dragon's majestic flames.<br /> <br /> In it's inactive state, the Grand Forge of the Tyrant exists as a simple orichalcum pendant with a single, inlaid socket for a hearthstone. Upon placing a Solar, Fire, or Earth hearthstone within the socket, the Solar makes an unbreakable pact with the Tyrant of the Sands. The Elder Dragon bestows upon the Solar a fragment of his eternal fire in exchange for the Solar's service as the Will of the Tyrant's Ideals. The pendant and the hearthstone melt into a river of essence and flow into the Solar's, becoming a mystic code of draconic runes etched onto the Solar's own skin.<br /> <br /> His mystic code is the bridge between his essence and the Grand Forge of the Tyrant. A mythical workshop of the a Solar from the first age, he shaped the Forge from the wyld itself, until it was a reflection of his soul. To this day, the Forge exists far away in the Wylds, lost and distant, protected by dragon fire that incinerates all those who would enter its boundary. Five towers, arranged in a pentagram, each powered by three greater hearthstones: one Solar, one of Fire, and one of Earth, hold the Grand Forge stable against the ravaging chaos.<br /> Essence pours from the towers, flowing in streams of golden motes that saturate the atmosphere, wavering in the heat of the flames. The sound of countless heavy hammers falling on anvils fills the air, the sound deafening as the give birth to new arms.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Grand Forge smiths the raw essence in the atmosphere into new weapons, each crafted to fit the soul of its chosen hero of justice, imbued with the inferno of the Tyrant's Fire, unable to wielded by any other and costing no motes for him to attune to. The weapons it forges are stored Elsewhere: sharpened, polished, and loaded, waiting for their master to will them from their storage to his hands. In addition, the Forge holds extra slots for the Solar, letting him store weapons of his choosing in Elsewhere as well, where the Grand Forge will protect and even repair them.<br /> <br /> The Forge is able to create infinite copies artifact weapons, each without a soul and lacking any evocations, but he may only retrieve up to one set at a time from Elsewhere, using Wind War God's Armory to do so (Paired weapons such as war fans, slashing swords, pieces, etc. count as one set), and retrieving a new set of weapons from the forge causes the previous set to fade into essence, disappearing in a golden cloud of motes.<br /> <br /> Only upon becoming the Will of the Tyrant may the Solar attune with the pendant and unlock it's evocations. Furthermore, as long as he remains the Will of the Tyrant, the Solar retains all the effects granted by his Hearthstone, and regenerates an additional mote of essence outside of combat.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Evocations of the Grand Forge of the Tyrant:</b></span><br /> Passive:<br /> While attuned with the Grand Forge, whenever the Solar draws weapon brought forth from it's flames, he may treat it as if he had the Quickdraw (****) merit for any ability.<br /> <br /> Wind War God's Armory<br /> Cost: \u2013 (1m); Type: Permanent; Duration: Indefinite<br /> Keywords: Stacking<br /> Requirements: N/A<br /> <br /> The Lawgiver may pay one mote to indefinitely store up to (Essence x2) weapons Elsewhere, hidden away in the boundary between nothing, including close- and long-range weapons, in addition to the weapons created and stored by the forge. This passive also expressly permits the storage of shields.<br /> The Solar may reflexively store as many weapons as she wishes Elsewhere, at a rate of one mote per (Essence x 2) weapons.<br /> To retrieve a weapon stored in this manner, or one of the generic artifact weapons produced by the forge, the Solar must concentrate on that weapon and pay an additional 1m mote, reflexively causing the weapon to summon itself from Elsewhere, falling downward into the ground before her, within arms reach for her to immediately draw without penalty.<br /> <br /> As long as the Solar maintains an Essence commitment to this Charm, he may sheath weapons in Elsewhere without cost, up to her storage limit. The Solar may release all the motes committed to storing his weapons in Elsewhere as a Simple action, causing them to fall to the ground around the him in a circle ([Essence x 2] x [number of committed motes released]) yards in diameter, in addition to an uncountable assortment of generic artifact weapons.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800080\">That Which Defies Heaven\u2013 Endless Claws of the Tyrant</span></b>:<br /> Cost: 7m, 1wp; Type: Reflexive; Duration: Scene<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Requirements: Wind War God's Armory<br /> <br /> From around the Solar, countless portals to Elsewhere open, held open in a swirling pool of essence motes. From this array of essence, the Grand Forge releases weapon after weapon, firing them in a deadly <a href=\"http://store.tcgplayer.com/magic/product/show?ProductName=Rain%20of%20Blades&amp;partner=AUTOANY&amp;affiliate_id=autocard&amp;utm_campaign=affiliate&amp;utm_source=autocard&amp;utm_medium=card\" target=\"_blank\">Rain of Blades</a>. A hail of swords, spears, axes, halberds, every known blade in creation pours forth from the Grand Forge, becoming golden bands of light that tear through foes that dare challenge the Tyrant's ideals.<br /> <br /> Once deployed, the Solar may use the Grand Forge as a weapon for his attacks, allowing him to make attacks at up to Medium range, crushing his foe in a withering storm of blades.<br /> The Grand Forge is Heavy Artifact Ranged weapon with the weapon tags Archery (Medium) and Lethal, that explicitly allows it's attacks to be used with Archery and Righteous Devil Form.<br /> When he makes an attack, the countless blades launched by the Grand Forge work together, pincering the enemy and granting the him double 9's on his attack roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800080\">The Living Archive That Bequeaths New Blades</span></b>:<br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp; Type: Simple; Duration: Scene<br /> Requirements: That Which Defies Heaven\u2013 Striking Claws of the Tyrant<br /> <br /> The Grand Forge is a record, the collection of every memory it's Creator had of war.<br /> A sword that he touched, he instinctively understood.<br /> It's memories and evocations were laid bare to him, and he knew the sword as if it were a part of his soul as well.<br /> Thus, the Solar who raised this forge archived a record of every weapon and arm that has existed in creation in his time. Lost within this library are weapons from the First Age so ancient, so carefully forged with evocations of magic so grand that little today could compare. Every artifact today can be said to have descended from some legendary artifact hidden within the Forge's archives, and so the Forge knows every weapon and evocation that could possibly exist.<br /> <br /> The Solar opens his mind in meditation, letting the Forge touch his soul and carry his spirit Elsewhere. Within the Grand Forge, the Solar may search the lost archives, and with the aid of the Fires gifted by the <a href=\"http://store.tcgplayer.com/magic/product/show?ProductName=Dragon%20Tyrant&amp;partner=AUTOANY&amp;affiliate_id=autocard&amp;utm_campaign=affiliate&amp;utm_source=autocard&amp;utm_medium=card\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Tyrant</a>, craft from his own Essence a new artifact weapon with a single evocation of his own design, or a single evocation he witness used by another's weapon. From then on, the Forge will produce a copy of the weapon for the Solar to draw from Elsewhere as he wills.<br /> The Lawgiver may re-purchase this evocation up to (Essence*2) times, each time forging a new blade or arm.<br /> The Solar should work with the Storyteller to help fashion new artifact weapons that both approve of.<br /> <br /> Sample Artifacts produced by this evocation:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\">Upon the battlefield, the Solar knelt...</span></i><br /> <b>\u300cAvon Sign: Socratic Spring &amp; Romantic Autumn\u300d</b> (M. White and Black Jade Artifact Straight Swords: ***)<br /> Prerequisite: Essence 1<br /> <b>Lore:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Twin married blades, one black and one white, that were once the personal blades of the Solar who's spirit raised the Forge of Heaven. The Solar may choose to draw either blade or both when he wills Spring and Autumn to him. As once they were an extension of the nameless legendary blacksmith, these swords resonate with desire for justice in the Lawmaker's heart. Spring &amp; Autumn are unique. As they were the Nameless Solar's personal blades, the Forge of Heaven is naturally attuned to them, and is able to create a new copies immediately, without delay.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Evocation:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u300cNameless Sign: Triple Linked Crane Wings\u300d (Cost:3m 3i; Type: Supplemental; Duration: Instant):</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Lawmaker is a flurry of blades, in an instant striking three times, pulling three sets of the blade from the Forge of Heaven and cutting down his opponent.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">When the Lawmaker successfully strikes a withering attack with Spring or Autumn, he adds (Dex/2, rounded up)+3 to his raw damage, weaving the blade's wife into the attack. If he is using Fire Pieces, both his Fire Pieces are considered unloaded after his attack.</span><br /> <i>...Intoxicated in Victory</i><br /> <br /> <i>Alone in graveyard of blades...</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>\u300cClockwork Sign: Luna Dial Time Alter Blade\u300d</b> (S. Moonsilver Artifact Knife: ****)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite: Essence 3</span><br /> <b>Lore:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">An intricate knife etched with a clockwork design on its blade, this knife was the favored weapon of a Night Solar who devoted herself to hunting Demons. With a natural control over time, the woman would stalk the night, slaying any demon that dared to stand before her, until one day, she vanished </span><a href=\"http://store.tcgplayer.com/magic/product/show?ProductName=Into%20Thin%20Air&amp;partner=AUTOANY&amp;affiliate_id=autocard&amp;utm_campaign=affiliate&amp;utm_source=autocard&amp;utm_medium=card\" target=\"_blank\">Into Thin Air</a><span style=\"color:#000000\">. Once upon a time, the woman and the Nameless Solar had fought, and he preserved a copy of her knife within the forge.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Evocation: \u300cThe World: Solar Accel\u300d (Cost: 5m, 1wp; Type: Supplemental; Keywords: Dual Duration: Instant):</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Luna Dial is innately attuned to the linear passage of time. For a moment, time slows to a crawl for the Lawgiver as he wills his body to move in &quot;frozen&quot; time. Enhancing a movement action up to medium range, he flashes past his opponent, standing before or aside them, poised and ready to strike, before time resumes to flow.</span><br /> <i>... Between the Border of Life and Death</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\">His soul pained with the tears he shed...</span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>\u300cHound of the Isle: Gae Bolg\u300d</b> (H. Soulsteel Artifact Spear: ****)<br /> Prerequisite: Essence 4<br /> <b>Lore:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> A cursed spear, dyed red from the hearts it has consumed. It was carved from the remains Curruid's skull, obtained then by Sc\u00e1thach, before passed down to her student, a Dawn Solar named C\u00fa Chulainn. The Hound of Chulainn was among the greatest spearmen in First Age. A peerless combatant who could take on armies of the Wyld with this cursed spear and win. There is only one thing that is sure about this spear. It seeks the heart of every target, and it will stop at nothing to pierce everyone in its way.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Evocation:\u300cScarlet Sign: Demon Spear Piercing with Death\u300d(Cost: 6m, 1wp, 1ht; Type: Supplemental; Keywords: Decisive-Only, Perilous; Duration: Instant)<br /> Gorging itself on the life essence of the the Lawgiver, the spear reveals its true shape. When thrown as the Solar makes a decisive attack, the cursed spear rewrites destiny, bending and sharply changing angles as it advances to it's target, avoiding all obstacles and defenses until it attempts to strike the opponents heart in one, single, thrust. The Lawgiver may forgo up to (Dexterity+Combat Ability) initiative, up to (Essence x2) initiative total and roll it as direct damage that ignores hardness. If the strike incapacitates a non-trivial opponent, the initiative invested in it is recovered by the Lawgiver.<br /> This evocation may only be used once per scene.</span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\">...His Will shaped the Wyld anew.</span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Grand Forge of the Desert Tyrant.</i><br /> <b>\u300cFaerie Sign: Sword of Promised Victory\u300d</b> (H. Orachalcum Artifact Grand Daiklave: *****) (Thank you to /tg/)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite: Essence 5</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Lore:</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">A blessed sword, it is an almost plain-looking daiklave made of the purest orichalcum, though it can never be described as anything but a work of art. The hilt and handle are inlaid with blue jade tiles, while the blade has elegant runes carved into it, which are filled with the same jade. It is a blade that channels the light of the sun and cloaks itself with the power of the wind, striking down those who turned their back from the sun's radiance. It glows with the brilliance and radiant warmth of the sun, and only those chosen by the Unconquered Sun may attune to it.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Evocation: \u300cPendragon Sign: Radiant Solar Flare\u300d (Cost: 10m, 3</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">a, 1wp; Type: Simple; Keywords: Decisive-Only, Perilous; Duration: Instant)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">With an ungodly surge of power, the Solar channels the power of the Sun through the blade, annihilating the unworthy that dare stand in their way. This charm may only be used when Iconic and immediately after paying the cost, the Lawgiver's anima flares with the essence he is channeling, and rises to Bonfire as he swings his blade downward with the godly and righteous power of the sun. </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">It is an undodgeable Decisive strike against all targets out to Long range and a width of 1 range band (like Death of Obsidian Butterflies). The attack is rolled once and the base damage against all targets struck is equal to the Solar's initiative, which resets to base after all damage is rolled.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">This evocation may be use only once per story. Upon finishing the attack, the sword shatters, requiring the Forge to build it anew.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11858-seibahismaiwaifu","name":"SeibahIsMaiWaifu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:22:56-07:00","id":912299,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hey guys, another artifact I churned out today. Feels like a good one even if its cliched for Soulsteel but it serves it purpose. Comments and critique accepted as always.<br /> <br /> <b>Sanguine Bartizan (Soulsteel Lamellar)</b><br /> <br /> Created during the Age of Sorrow by Weeping Raiton Ascending, a Liminal hunted across the North by the Wyld Hunt, who was later slain, the armour hidden within a Solar tomb, due to the Liminals shocking resemblance. Before he was slain he had crafted a piece of armour to help him deliver retribution to those who would ignore the boundaries of life and death.<br /> <br /> The lamellar is precise and accurate, each plate a work of art in its own right. On the underside, strips of dire bat hide were riveted into place by small green jade rivets onto the backside of soulsteel plates all etched with the imagery of bats in flight, which were to become the essence channels for the blood. The bands, rather than put horizontally were put diagonally instead, creating a mural within the plates.<br /> <br /> The complete suit carries on its bat motifs, with the vambraces of the armour having the visage of the bats carved into it and the greaves carrying the wings in its decoration. The full motif is a sky full of bats flying towards a central moon of extremely polished soulsteel where there is a small inset for a hearthstone. All of the blood channels run around this moon and eventually escape going down the dire bat skirt.<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement Bonus:</b><br /> A Solar, Abyssal or Liminal who attunes to the armour can add the higher of Resistance or Integrity to their dying levels. For an additional 2m the armour improves their healing rate by the wearers Essence in hours. This effect stacks with any improved healing rate charms by removing the additional time after the initial charm effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Buoyed by Blood</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: - <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1, Stamina 3, Resistance 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> Like a boat in the ocean is raised by the waters, so to is the wielder raised by their own blood. As the blood runs down the channels of the armour, it becomes hardened and protects the wearer from further injury due to their own sacrifice.<br /> <br /> Buoyed by Blood provides the wearer with +1 additional soak and hardness, but only while the wearer is suffering from wound penalties. This evocation can be purchased up to Essence/2 times (rounding up) for a maximum of +3 soak/hardness.<br /> <br /> <b>Magnified in Agony</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m, 1lhl <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Buoyed in Blood<br /> As blood runs through the armour down the essence channels, the wearer finds themselves lighter, stronger and more determined in their agony.<br /> <br /> For the rest of the scene the armour turns wounds penalties into positives. If the wearer of Sanguine Bartizan is Crashed then Magnified in Agony ends and for the following turn their suffering is two-fold and they suffer from twice the normal wound penalties.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> Magnified in Agony cannot be purchased with experience and is automatically unlocked the first time the wearer is reduced to Incapacitated through any source of damage dealt through combat (environmental hazards don\u2019t count).<br /> <br /> <b>Might through Suffering</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m, 1lhl <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Magnified in Agony<br /> The essence in the wearers blood begins to soak back in, sinking into the leather underneath the plates, and wetting the skin of the wearer giving a renewed vigour in their anguish.<br /> <br /> The Evocation provides the wearer with additional strength, giving +1 to strength based actions per wound penalty the wearer is suffering from that count as non-charm dice.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> Might through Suffering cannot be purchased through experience and is automatically unlocked the first time the wearer survives for at least the Essence minimum in rounds at -4 wound penalties.<br /> <br /> <b>Retribution from Martyrdom</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m, 1wp, 2a <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-Only, Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> Feeding the lost blood with Essence and some of the wearers anima, it causes it to float out of the essence channels and begin to congeal into the air. The blood can take the form of whichever the wielder chooses as long as it is bladed (scythes, sword blades, chakrams etc) and streamers of black brown essence trail behind them.<br /> <br /> Retribution from Martyrdom creates a scene long counterattack that lashes out to kill any who attack at close range, doing a <b>decisive </b>attack with a dice pool of (current wound penalties + Essence) and base damage is equal to (current wound penalties x2)<br /> <br /> The Evocation doesn't end when the wearer of Sanguine Bartizan is unconscious, instead it carries on protecting them and deals (wound penalties x3) damage instead, attacking all who come within close range. If the wearer is crashed however, the Evocation ends prematurely and cancels all other active Evocations along with it.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> Retribution from Martyrdom cannot be purchased through experience and is automatically unlocked the first time the wearer is plunged into dying levels.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11900-grynder","name":"Grynder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T08:38:41-07:00","id":912818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SeibahIsMaiWaifu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=912153#post912153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Threw this together on a whim since I couldn't sleep. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I adapted and expanded on the old 2.5 charm, from the Ink Monkeys (Thousand-Arms Prana, to be exact), until I had something fun out of it.<br /> I'm sure someone here will find a use for this because I don't think we'll be using it in this upcoming campaign.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Gates of Babylon, Unlimited Blade Works and Touhou in one artifact? Nice.<br /> However, I have one big problem this this write up! There is no way Cu Chulainn was Solar, he was certainly a Lunar!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T11:38:53-07:00","id":912889,"title":"","content":"The talk about Righteous Devil Style inspired me to make another flame piece artifact. I originally designed it for synergy with Righteous Devil style, but it kind of went off into its own direction. They should still work together, though.<br /> <br /> Also, do you guys think it's okay for an artifact flame piece to have multiple shots? I've been running on that assumption when I make these and I've never actually asked anyone before.<br /> <br /> <b>Gravewright</b> (Soulsteel and Starmetal Flametongue Repeater), Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> In the end, there is no escape from the grave. Even the gods meet their occasional doom from wandering heroes or monsters...or even each other. The Gravewright embodies this inevitability, though none know who forged it. As far as anyone knows, Gravewright is as old as death itself and made by it, too.<br /> <br /> Gravewright brings not glory to its wielder, but damnation to her enemies. It emits a terrible gravity in combat, punishing anyone who tries to escape judgment. Many a wielder have been Righteous Devils, but this weapon gives even them pause, for it tears away pieces of the soul from those it slays. Many fear wielding it does something similar to oneself, a fear that is perhaps not so unfounded.<br /> <br /> Gravewright first become widely known when used by Laughing Flames, a Lunar Righteous Devil, who used it to slay one of the directional gods of war long ago. This god of war had been one of tactical retreats and repositioning, powers that became useless in the sights of Gravewright. Few details of the battle are still remembered save that the god of war had, in her last moments, begged the Lunar to stop using Gravewright for her own sake.<br /> <br /> The sights and hammer of Gravewright are made of starmetal, shining in contrast against the two over-under soulsteel barrels. The grip, whatever material it actually is, is wrapped in the unbreakable hide of some forgotten beast, said to be the first life Gravewright ever claimed. Gravewright has a single hearthstone socket beneath the barrel, just in front of the trigger guard.<br /> <br /> Gravewright is a medium archery weapon that can hold two shots, which can be reloaded simultaneously. It attunes for five motes.<br /> <br /> <b>Tags:</b> Lethal, Archery (Short), Flame, Mounted, One-Handed, Special<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Gravewright</b><br /> By attuning for an additional two motes, withering ranged attacks made with Gravewright at close range deal an additional automatic level of withering damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Gravedigging Humility</b><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Essence 1; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> With either precision or force, a shot from the Gravewright forces a target to the ground, as if they were ready to enter their own grave. This evocation creates a difficulty 2 gambit. If successful, the target is knocked prone, and any disengage action they may have been taking is ended.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Inescapable Iron Diligence</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> None may escape from the sights of the Gravewright. When an enemy takes a disengage action (regardless of success), the wielder may activate this evocation to reflexively aim at them. If she was already aiming at them (or aims again before attacking), she gains the initiative the target spent to disengage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fear-the-Reaper Mien</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 2; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Gravedigging Humility, Inescapable Iron Diligence<br /> <br /> It is best for enemies of Gravewright's wielder to meekly accept their fates. While this evocation is active, every enemy within medium range of the wielder must roll to rise from prone (instead of just close range), and the difficulty to do so is raised to 4. It also costs an additional initiative to disengage from the wielder.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Heel-Biting Plume</b><br /> Cost: 7m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 2; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Fear-the-Reaper Mien<br /> <br /> It's not the same as cutting, but an Achilles tendon burned away is still useless. After knocking down a target with an aimed Gravedigging Humility, the wielder may activate this evocation to immediately roll her remaining initiative to deal damage, as with a normal decisive attack. The target is forced to accept a crippling injury that impairs their mobility (generally an injured leg), negating as much of the damage as possible. This does not count against the once per story limit for crippling injuries. Once per fight, with no reset.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cloak of Lost Souls</b><br /> Cost: 1m or 4m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 3; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Heel-Biting Plume<br /> <br /> Not even death is an escape from the Gravewright. After slaying a target while Fear-the-Reaper Mien is active, the wielder may spend a single mote to rip their hun soul (or equivalent) from their body and bind it to Gravewright. For all intents and purposes, they are permanently slain, similar to Ghost-Eating Technique. Reducing the size of a battle group usually allows at least one soul each time. The souls may optionally become visible when the wielder's anima is at burning or above, a river of silent torment flowing from Gravewright.<br /> <br /> At any time, the wielder may simply choose to release the soul, whereupon it either dissolves or returns to Lethe, as appropriate to its nature. They are also released like this upon the death of the wielder. What Gravewright does with the wielder's own soul is unknown.<br /> <br /> Before a decisive attack roll, the wielder may activate this charm again for four motes and one temporary willpower to fire one of her captive souls, whirling and screaming as it burns into nothingness at last. The shot does not require ammunition, and one die of raw damage is converted into an automatic level of damage, plus one more die converted for each stunt level awarded to the attack (if any). It also has an additional effect according to the nature of the soul used. Some examples are as follows:<br /> <br /> <b>Chilling:</b> The souls of the Abyssal Exalted and other deathly creatures (such as ghosts) chill instead of burn. If hit, for the rest of the scene the target takes a -2 penalty on all actions. They may take a miscellaneous action (which may be flurried) to warm themselves back up to remove the penalty, if they have some means to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Corrosive:</b> Some souls, along with the essence of demons, seethe with great vitriol, firing chemical lances instead of flame. If hit, the target's withering soak is reduced by 2 for the rest of the scene. This may be undone by a miscellaneous action to wipe themselves off, which may be flurried.<br /> <br /> <b>Holy:</b> The souls of the Solar Exalted along with other holy (more or less) beings burn away the impure. The attack deals aggravated damage to creatures touched by darkness, such as natives of Malfeas or the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <b>Humble:</b> The souls of many mortals burn only dimly, making the attack difficult to see. The target must roll (Wits + Awareness) at difficulty 4, or suffer a -2 penalty to their defense.<br /> <br /> <b>Shifting:</b> The souls of the Lunar Exalted and other shapeshifters lend their protean nature to the shot, giving it a form that molds itself to fit around (or through) any cover less than full, negating its benefits.<br /> <br /> This list is not exhaustive, nor is it required to use these exact effects for souls of the same type (a particularly bitter Solar could yield a corrosive soul, for example). Unique souls give unique effects when fired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1543-iethloc","user":"Iethloc","date":".  New fancier capstone and bumped up to artifact 4 06-15-2016, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1543-iethloc","name":"Iethloc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1543_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T02:42:15-07:00","id":913322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iethloc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=912889#post912889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The talk about Righteous Devil Style inspired me to make another flame piece artifact. I originally designed it for synergy with Righteous Devil style, but it kind of went off into its own direction. They should still work together, though.<br /> <br /> Also, do you guys think it's okay for an artifact flame piece to have multiple shots? I've been running on that assumption when I make these and I've never actually asked anyone before.<br /> <br /> <b>Gravewright</b> (Soulsteel and Starmetal Flametongue Repeater), Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> In the end, there is no escape from the grave. Even the gods meet their occasional doom from wandering heroes or monsters...or even each other. The Gravewright embodies this inevitability, though none know who forged it. As far as anyone knows, Gravewright is as old as death itself and made by it, too.<br /> <br /> Gravewright brings not glory to its wielder, but damnation to her enemies. It emits a terrible gravity in combat, punishing anyone who tries to escape judgment. Many a wielder have been Righteous Devils, but this weapon gives even them pause, for it tears away pieces of the soul from those it slays. Many fear wielding it does something similar to oneself, a fear that is perhaps not so unfounded.<br /> <br /> Gravewright first become widely known when used by Laughing Flames, a Lunar Righteous Devil, who used it to slay one of the directional gods of war long ago. This god of war had been one of tactical retreats and repositioning, powers that became useless in the sights of Gravewright. Few details of the battle are still remembered save that the god of war had, in her last moments, begged the Lunar to stop using Gravewright for her own sake.<br /> <br /> The sights, hammer, and cylinder of Gravewright are made of starmetal, shining in contrast against the bulky soulsteel barrel. The grip, whatever material it actually is, is wrapped in the unbreakable hide of some forgotten beast, said to be the first life Gravewright ever claimed. Gravewright has a single hearthstone socket beneath the barrel, just in front of the trigger guard.<br /> <br /> Gravewright is a medium archery weapon that can hold five shots, which can all be reloaded simultaneously. It attunes for five motes.<br /> <br /> <b>Tags:</b> Lethal, Archery (Short), Flame, Mounted, One-Handed, Special<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Free levels of withering damage are somewhat unbalanced. Might I suggest an additional attunement cost of 2m? Also, it should include which types of Exalts it affects, which in this case would seem to be Abyssals, Sidereals and Solars.<br /> <br /> Gravedigging Humility: Decent, and not straight up the smashing tag for ranged attacks. Possibly overpriced, I'd allow it for 1m.<br /> <br /> Inescapable Iron Diligence(I apoligise for not separating them out, my Forum-fu isn't that good) Seems fine.<br /> <br /> Fear-the-Reaper Mien: (Come on Baby, don't) This is slightly confusing. Does it make rising from prone a contested action or does it raise the difficulty or both? Because while the first two on their own are fine(for 3m, 1wp even), both at the same time is quite powerful. Also, if it does make a contested action, what ability does it use? It sounds like it would use Appearance + Presence or some such. Especially for a Scene-long.<br /> <br /> Heel-Biting Plume: No. That's way to cheap for what it does. First of all, it removes the downside of Gambits which is fine. But then you're forcing a crippling injury, which is a very powerful effect, since it also doubles wound penalties for the rest of the scene, and it doesn't count against the limit either. The limit you've placed at the end is unlikely to be relevant given the rest of the charm will effectively end the fight if you're hitting from anywhere above 10 or 15 initiative.<br /> <br /> Cloak of Lost Souls is fine, save that it could do with adding a 1m or 2m surcharge, but rather than have the soul vanish, I'd have the gun absorb it. Also, as a suggestion for an additional evocation, the ability to release such souls by shooting them at people with effects based on the nature of the soul might make for a more impressive capstone.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for multiple shots, I might allow two or three, but 5, I feel, might make it too powerful.<br /> <br /> Overall, I feel this is more Artifact 4 rather than 3.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","user":"Myradmir","date":". 06-13-2016, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T08:40:26-07:00","id":913404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=913322#post913322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free levels of withering damage are somewhat unbalanced. Might I suggest an additional attunement cost of 2m? Also, it should include which types of Exalts it affects, which in this case would seem to be Abyssals, Sidereals and Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering whether this might need an additional attunement cost. I originally wanted this to be available to any Exalt, actually. Brilliant Sentinel has its attunement power available to everyone, as an example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=913322#post913322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fear-the-Reaper Mien: (Come on Baby, don't) This is slightly confusing. Does it make rising from prone a contested action or does it raise the difficulty or both? Because while the first two on their own are fine(for 3m, 1wp even), both at the same time is quite powerful. Also, if it does make a contested action, what ability does it use? It sounds like it would use Appearance + Presence or some such. Especially for a Scene-long.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's just a matter of confusing wording. It's supposed to just force everyone to have to roll at increased the difficulty. I'll re-word it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=913322#post913322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heel-Biting Plume: No. That's way to cheap for what it does. First of all, it removes the downside of Gambits which is fine. But then you're forcing a crippling injury, which is a very powerful effect, since it also doubles wound penalties for the rest of the scene, and it doesn't count against the limit either. The limit you've placed at the end is unlikely to be relevant given the rest of the charm will effectively end the fight if you're hitting from anywhere above 10 or 15 initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about a cost of 7m, 1wp instead? Maybe make it just once per fight, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=913322#post913322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cloak of Lost Souls is fine, save that it could do with adding a 1m or 2m surcharge, but rather than have the soul vanish, I'd have the gun absorb it. Also, as a suggestion for an additional evocation, the ability to release such souls by shooting them at people with effects based on the nature of the soul might make for a more impressive capstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I wasn't satisfied with this evocation. If I raise the artifact rating, maybe it'd be a good idea to rewrite it to gather and shoot souls instead. I like that idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=913322#post913322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for multiple shots, I might allow two or three, but 5, I feel, might make it too powerful.<br /> <br /> Overall, I feel this is more Artifact 4 rather than 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was an artifact version of the flame piece that came with 5 shots that didn't make it into the final PDF (which is where I got the term flametongue repeater). Maybe it was removed because it was unbalanced. I'll probably make it a double-barreled monstrosity with one shot in each barrel.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1543-iethloc","name":"Iethloc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1543_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T09:38:58-07:00","id":913455,"title":"","content":"Here's my latest creation for the forum to critique.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Windsong</b></u><br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact: Blue Jade Far Talon<br /> Light Artifact Thrown Weapon<br /> Tags: Lethal, Thrown (Medium), Cutting<br /> <br /> <u><b>Appearance</b></u><br /> An elegantly designed dagger made of sky blue jade, with a several holes across its body so that it &quot;sings&quot; when thrown.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attunement</b></u><br /> Benefit Attunement Cost: 0<br /> - Vanishes after being thrown and reappears in the wielder\u2019s hand unless evocation or charm says otherwise<br /> - While constructed for flight, Windsong can be used in hand to hand combat. Windsong is considered a Light Mundane Melee Weapon with the Lethal tag for hand-to-hand combat.<br /> Benefit Attunement Cost: +2m<br /> - Windsong is in tune to the flow of all that surrounds it, and is willing to share this insight. Convert 1 die on any awareness roll to a success and add +1 to parrying with Windsong.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Evocations</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Following the Wind\u2019s Lead</b><br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive.<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> One Line Summary: Improve the attack of following range attacks from other ranged allies. Windsong\u2019s call draws the notice of all archers and throwers to follow it as it hits its mark. After a successful attack on an opponent at short range or further, allied ranged attackers that are currently aiming (took an aim action on their latest turn and have yet to act) at other targets may spontaneously switch their target to the wielder\u2019s opponent at no expense. Switching allies will maintain any bonus accrued by aiming if they were aiming for a second turn. They will all have the ability to hit target the new target if at Medium or Long range, limited by their weapon\u2019s range. Also, all switched ranged attacks treat the target\u2019s defense as one lower as long the ally fires on their next turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Whistle Down the Wind</b><br /> Cost: 6m (2i+ depending on the distract gambit)<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Following the Wind\u2019s Lead<br /> One Line Summary: Help an another\u2019s disengage action and knock back the opposition When an ally within medium range and line of sight is attempting to disengage from any number of opponents, you may instantly aid them with a distract gambit. The gambit works as normal, with the disengager being the beneficiary and the difficulty the attack roll equalling the highest evasion of those contesting the disengage action. However, instead of transferring initiative upon success, the ally gains (gambit difficulty - 2) successes to add to the their disengage roll. Should the disengage succeed, all opponents involved are flung 1 range band away from the wielder and the ally, landing prone, by a sudden burst of air. Using this Charm allows the Exalt to act out of turn, but acts as her combat action for the turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Out of the Blue</b><br /> Cost: 4m<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Whistle Down the Wind<br /> One Line Summary: Toss Windsong high into the air on one round, sneak attack a target within medium range on the next round<br /> <br /> The wind is more heard and felt, rarely seen. Under this truth, Windsong can strike unseen. On their turn, the wielder selects a target they can see within medium range, and then tosses Windsong high into the air, where it disappears from sight. On the next round on the wielder\u2019s turn, like a bolt from the blue, Windsong dive-bombs the target. First, roll (Dexterity + Stealth) against the target\u2019s (Perception + Awareness). If the wielder wins by 1 or more successes, the incoming attack is considered a surprise attack, if by 5 or more successes, it\u2019s considered an ambush. Make a decisive attack, applying the results of the contested roll. This attack cannot benefit from any simple charms.<br /> <br /> While Windsong is airborne, the wielder can make separate simultaneous actions as long they do not include a decisive attack. Delaying one\u2019s action also delays Windsong\u2019s attack and withering attacks made by the wielder while Windsong is in flight do not add to the wielder\u2019s initiative.<br /> <br /> At the end of the tick, Windsong will return to the wielder\u2019s hand as long as one hand is free. Otherwise, it appears on the ground near the wielder\u2019s body. At that point, the wielder\u2019s initiative resets.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: Can only be used if the wielder is not grappled and once per target per fight. This charm can be flurried with another action as long as it follows all other flurry rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","user":"Binary Phantom","date":".  updated based on feedback recieved 06-14-2016, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T03:19:20-07:00","id":913979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=913455#post913455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my latest creation for the forum to critique.</div> </div> </div> </div>And critique I shall!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=913455#post913455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Attunement</b></u><br /> Benefit Attunement Cost: +1m<br /> - Windsong is in tune to the flow of all that surrounds it, and is willing to share this insight. Convert 1 die on any awareness roll to a success and add +1 to parrying with Windsong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Converting 1 die to a success is, on average, the equivalent of adding +1 non-charm die to the roll (you turn 0.5 successes into 1). Increasing Parry by 1 is the equivalent of a 2m Excellency. That's a pretty hefty passive bonus, so I'd bump up the attunement cost to +2m.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=913455#post913455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Following the Wind\u2019s Lead</b><br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive.<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> One Line Summary: Improve the attack of following range attacks from other ranged allies.<br /> <br /> Windsong\u2019s call draws the notice of all archers and throwers to follow it as it hits its mark. After a successful attack on an opponent at short range or further, allied ranged attackers that are currently aiming at other targets may spontaneously switch their target to the wielder\u2019s opponent at no expense. Also, all ranged attacks treat the target\u2019s defense as two lower until the wielder\u2019s next turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conceptually, a good first Evocation, but the wording is unclear. Does &quot;allied ranged attackers that are currently aiming at other targets&quot; mean &quot;allied ranged attackers who took the Aim action on their last turn&quot;? If yes, does &quot;may spontaneously switch their target to the wielder's opponent at no expense&quot; include &quot;retain bonus dice gained from aiming&quot;, or does it just allow them to make an attack out to medium+ range without aiming? Moreover, does the last effect last until the beginning, or the end of the wielder's next turn?<br /> <br /> In any case, effectively reducing the target's defense by 2 is an incredibly potent effect (+2 non-charm automatic successes on <i>all</i> incoming ranged attack rolls!), and a smart party can reap massive benefits from this if they're built around doing so. I'd either add a WP to the cost, or bump it up to 4 motes and give it a reset condition, with the assumption that you're modelling the opposition on the corebook's Antagonists session, most of whom have no convenient way to negate defense penalties. If your table regularly features opponents who can do so, the Evocation is fine as-is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=913455#post913455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Whistle Down the Wind</b><br /> Cost: 6m (2i+ depending on the distract gambit)<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Following the Wind\u2019s Lead<br /> <br /> One Line Summary: Help an another\u2019s disengage action and knock back the opposition<br /> When an ally within medium range and line of sight is attempting to disengage from any number of opponents, you may instantly aid them with a distract gambit. The gambit works as normal, with the disengager being the beneficiary and the with the mean evasion of those contesting the disengage setting the difficulty the attack roll. However, instead of transferring initiative upon success, the ally gains (gambit difficulty - 2) successes to add to the their disengage roll. Should the disengage succeed, all opponents involved are flung 1 range band away from the wielder and the ally, landing prone, by a sudden burst of air. Using this Charm allows the Exalt to act out of turn, but acts as her combat action for the turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how this expands on the native niche of Thrown as the tricky, gambit-oriented fighting style. On the other hand, I think using mean Evasion is quite unwieldy (are you rounding up or down? doesn't the math get annoying to deal with when there's 3+ opponents hanging around?). Just use the highest rating. Otherwise, it seems okay (cost is pretty hard to figure out - it lets you break initiative order, but that's basically Thunderclap Rush Attack, which costs 3 motes, but it also adds 1-3 non-charm successes to a disengage, but it's also tied to succeeding on an attack roll and has an Initiative cost, but it also moves people around and knocks them down, which is basically Mournful Crane's Cry, which costs 3m, but this is AoE, but MCC flings people away for 2 range bands - in any case, if you sum up the effects, 6 motes and the inherent costs of making a Distract gambit sound about right).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=913455#post913455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Out of the Blue</b><br /> Cost: 7m<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Whistle Down the Wind<br /> One Line Summary: Toss Windsong high into the air on one round, surprise attack a target within medium range on the next round<br /> <br /> The wind is more heard and felt, rarely seen. Under this truth, Windsong can strike unseen. On their turn, the wielder selects a target they can see within medium range, and then tosses Windsong high into the air, where it disappears from sight. On the next round on the wielder\u2019s turn, like a bolt from the blue, Windsong dive-bombs the target. Make a decisive attack, with (wielder\u2019s stealth - target\u2019s awareness, minimum 1) automatic successes on the attack roll. Should the attack hit, ignore (1 + excess successes) hardness. If this were to reduce the hardness below 0, treat the hardness as 0 and convert up to (remaining excess successes) dice into successes on the damage roll. This attack cannot benefit from any simple charms.<br /> <br /> While Windsong is airborne, the wielder can make separate simultaneous actions as long they do not include a decisive attack. Delaying one\u2019s action also delays Windsong\u2019s attack and withering attacks made by the wielder while Windsong is in flight do not add to the wielder\u2019s initiative.<br /> <br /> At the end of the tick, Windsong will return to the wielder\u2019s hand as long as one hand is free. Otherwise, it appears on the ground near the wielder\u2019s body. At that point, the wielder\u2019s initiative resets.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: Can only be used if the wielder is not grappled and once per target per fight. This charm can be flurried with another action as long as it follows all other flurry rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like a pretty fun effect. Mechanically, it's a bit all over the place (summary says it lets you surprise attack a target, but it isn't <i>actually </i>a surprise attack, and the way it interacts with hardness is just... bwuh?). If you assume artifact armor to be rare, the damage boost can get out of hand quite quickly, but then again, the cost is incredibly high (about 15 motes if you full Excellency it, assuming Awareness 4 on part of the enemy, which strikes me as reasonable for most combatants important enough to warrant using a capstone on). And, of course, it runs into the problem of artifact armor and a decent Awareness score taking quite a lot out of its teeth, at which point you're stuck with an incredibly pricey effect that's of little benefit above Initiative 10 (and why would you launch your big decisive doomcombo while below Initiative 10?).<br /> <br /> So, umm, I'd basically make it an attempt to re-establish surprise, forget about the Hardness interaction, and reduce the cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T07:37:49-07:00","id":914083,"title":"","content":"I've spent ALL DAY thinking it was Wednesday or Thursday already... but it's <b>Tuesday</b>. So now I'm depressed.<br /> <br /> Cheer me up. What are some ideas for a Green Jade artifact that has <b>nothing to do with plants or wood</b>. Bonus points if it's <b>not a sword</b>, double bonus points if it's <b>not a bow</b>, triple bonus points if it <b>does</b> have to do with plants or wood but in a sufficiently <i><b>interesting and unique way </b></i>such that I am inspired to write it. Fair warning, that last one will be a challenge because I've seen a lot and I'm <i>ver</i><i>y</i> bored with the plant evocations.<br /> <br /> A reminder of it's properties<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Green Jade</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Green jade resonates with the element of wood. Its Evocations control plants, make things grow or wither, produce manifestations of wood, establish rapport with the natural world, siphon Essence from living things or transfer it into them, and manifest toxins.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 06-14-2016, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T07:59:48-07:00","id":914094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914083#post914083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've spent ALL DAY thinking it was Wednesday or Thursday already... but it's <b>Tuesday</b>. So now I'm depressed.<br /> <br /> Cheer me up. What are some ideas for a Green Jade artifact that has <b>nothing to do with plants or wood</b>. Bonus points if it's <b>not a sword</b>, double bonus points if it's <b>not a bow</b>, triple bonus points if it <b>does</b> have to do with plants or wood but in a sufficiently <i><b>interesting and unique way </b></i>such that I am inspired to write it. Fair warning, that last one will be a challenge because I've seen a lot and I'm <i>ver</i><i>y</i> bored with the plant evocations.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A giant grimcleaver which is the favored weapon of a reverse-lumberjack?<br /> <br /> (I'll let <i>you </i>figure out what a reverse-lumberjack would be or how it'd even look like.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T07:59:57-07:00","id":914095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914083#post914083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've spent ALL DAY thinking it was Wednesday or Thursday already... but it's <b>Tuesday</b>. So now I'm depressed.<br /> <br /> Cheer me up. What are some ideas for a Green Jade artifact that has <b>nothing to do with plants or wood</b>. Bonus points if it's <b>not a sword</b>, double bonus points if it's <b>not a bow</b>, triple bonus points if it <b>does</b> have to do with plants or wood but in a sufficiently <i><b>interesting and unique way </b></i>such that I am inspired to write it. Fair warning, that last one will be a challenge because I've seen a lot and I'm <i>ver</i><i>y</i> bored with the plant evocations.<br /> <br /> A reminder of it's properties</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We could use some Artifact throwing knives. How about a set of knives that can secrete poisons, eventually siphoning Essence back to the user through poison? Is that too plant-based?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T08:29:09-07:00","id":914105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914083#post914083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've spent ALL DAY thinking it was Wednesday or Thursday already... but it's <b>Tuesday</b>. So now I'm depressed.<br /> <br /> Cheer me up. What are some ideas for a Green Jade artifact that has <b>nothing to do with plants or wood</b>. Bonus points if it's <b>not a sword</b>, double bonus points if it's <b>not a bow</b>, triple bonus points if it <b>does</b> have to do with plants or wood but in a sufficiently <i><b>interesting and unique way </b></i>such that I am inspired to write it. Fair warning, that last one will be a challenge because I've seen a lot and I'm <i>ver</i><i>y</i> bored with the plant evocations.<br /> <br /> A reminder of it's properties</div> </div> </div> </div>A flute that allows advanced communications with animals and provides affects similar to the survival charms but can make animals more civilised like the haltans intelligent ones (the name eludes me)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11900-grynder","name":"Grynder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:02:00-07:00","id":914121,"title":"","content":"A staff that causes the withering of the opponents limbs, leaving them a dry husk by the end of the battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:16:42-07:00","id":914130,"title":"","content":"While I admit that I love the <i>concept</i> (or at least phrasing) of &quot;Reverse-Lumberjack&quot;, in the end it's just an axe that makes trees grow. I'll put a pin in that one for now. <br /> <br /> The flute has potential, but I'll have to give it a sit to make sure it doesn't just copy Survival charms. That's a design strategy I prefer to avoid where possible. But it's a thematic space I can dig. Of course, it could probably be made pretty simply as a 2 dot artifact without evocations. Charm an animal and make it calm and obedient for a scene or a day or something. May have Essence charmed animals. Or shit, make it useable by mortals too.<br /> <br /> Do we have artifact throwing knife templates in the core? *looks* Wow there's not even MORTAL throwing knives in the book. I guess they'd have to be modeled after Shurikens. But then any Thrown weapon could be used.. I haven't done anything with poisons yet but it's not too tricky. As long as I avoid plant associations it'll feel original to me I suppose. I'll play around with that idea in my head and see if I can get it to stick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:27:09-07:00","id":914137,"title":"","content":"I have a long-standing idea for a matched set of five longfangs, one of each color of jade. The green one is going to have the ability to merge into a target's body, a la Avalon in FSN, and grant them the ability to heal a limited amount of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:29:40-07:00","id":914140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914083#post914083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've spent ALL DAY thinking it was Wednesday or Thursday already... but it's <b>Tuesday</b>. So now I'm depressed.<br /> <br /> Cheer me up. What are some ideas for a Green Jade artifact that has <b>nothing to do with plants or wood</b>. Bonus points if it's <b>not a sword</b>, double bonus points if it's <b>not a bow</b>, triple bonus points if it <b>does</b> have to do with plants or wood but in a sufficiently <i><b>interesting and unique way </b></i>such that I am inspired to write it. Fair warning, that last one will be a challenge because I've seen a lot and I'm <i>ver</i><i>y</i> bored with the plant evocations.<br /> <br /> A reminder of it's properties</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's what I've been able to come up with so far:<br /> <br /> <b>Lakashim, the Pulse of Life</b><br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact: Green Jade Silken Armor<br /> <br /> <b><u>Appearance</u></b><br /> Strands of green jade with the silk of some long lost race of moth are woven into a dozen braided pairs that come together in a spiral on the wearer\u2019s upper left chest, above the heart.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Evocations</u></b><br /> Hear the Pulse of Creation<br /> One Line Summary: sense all of the living nearby, downgrade ambush and surprise attacks to surprise attacks and normal attacks, respectively<br /> <br /> Pounding Dance of the Worldheart<br /> One Line Summary: WIP<br /> <br /> One Pulse, One Soul, One Act<br /> One Line Summary: WIP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:34:28-07:00","id":914146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914130#post914130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have artifact throwing knife templates in the core? *looks* Wow there's not even MORTAL throwing knives in the book. I guess they'd have to be modeled after Shurikens. But then any Thrown weapon could be used.. I haven't done anything with poisons yet but it's not too tricky. As long as I avoid plant associations it'll feel original to me I suppose. I'll play around with that idea in my head and see if I can get it to stick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mundane knives(p 581) have the Thrown (Short) tag, so they can be thrown but not very far. Throwing knives would have the advantage of usable in a parry without charms or stunts so I would use the knife statblock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","user":"Binary Phantom","date":". 06-14-2016, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:37:11-07:00","id":914148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914083#post914083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've spent ALL DAY thinking it was Wednesday or Thursday already... but it's <b>Tuesday</b>. So now I'm depressed.<br /> <br /> Cheer me up. What are some ideas for a Green Jade artifact that has <b>nothing to do with plants or wood</b>. Bonus points if it's <b>not a sword</b>, double bonus points if it's <b>not a bow</b>, triple bonus points if it <b>does</b> have to do with plants or wood but in a sufficiently <i><b>interesting and unique way </b></i>such that I am inspired to write it. Fair warning, that last one will be a challenge because I've seen a lot and I'm <i>ver</i><i>y</i> bored with the plant evocations.<br /> <br /> A reminder of it's properties</div> </div> </div> </div>A Soulsteel Green Jade armor that drains life and vitality from its wearer to power its evocations. Bonus points if you can throw in Kill la Kill references with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11948-walker-of-the-yellow-path","name":"Walker of the Yellow Path","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:43:37-07:00","id":914149,"title":"","content":"Here's what I've got for a fancier capstone for the Gravewright. I didn't want to go over the usual 5 evocations for an artifact, so this ended up being a dual function charm. I don't think that's really a problem. If it seems okay, I'll edit it into the original post and bump it up to artifact 4.<br /> <br /> Overall, I'm not sure about the balance of this evocation and the various souls, but I still like the concept. I felt that emulating Generalized Ammunition Technique (with its adding damage based on the stunt) was worth doing. I was tempted to make the soul shots unblockable (being immaterial and all), but I didn't want it to do so many big things at once. I also thought of making the soul explode and hit an area, but this is supposed to work with Righteous Devil Style and I didn't want it to compete with Dancing Devil Trigger Finger.<br /> <br /> <b>Cloak of Lost Souls</b><br /> Cost: 1m or 4m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 3; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Heel-Biting Plume<br /> <br /> Not even death is an escape from the Gravewright. After slaying a target while Fear-the-Reaper Mien is active, the wielder may spend a single mote to rip their hun soul (or equivalent) from their body and bind it to Gravewright. For all intents and purposes, they are permanently slain, similar to Ghost-Eating Technique. Reducing the size of a battle group usually allows at least one soul each time. The souls may optionally become visible when the wielder's anima is at burning or above, a river of silent torment flowing from Gravewright.<br /> <br /> At any time, the wielder may simply choose to release the soul, whereupon it either dissolves or returns to Lethe, as appropriate to its nature. They are also released like this upon the death of the wielder. What Gravewright does with the wielder's own soul is unknown.<br /> <br /> Before a decisive attack roll, the wielder may activate this charm again for four motes and one temporary willpower to fire one of her captive souls, whirling and screaming as it burns into nothingness at last. The shot does not require ammunition, and one die of raw damage is converted into an automatic level of damage, plus one more die converted for each stunt level awarded to the attack (if any). It also has an additional effect according to the nature of the soul used. Some examples are as follows:<br /> <br /> <b>Chilling:</b> The souls of the Abyssal Exalted and other deathly creatures (such as ghosts) chill instead of burn. If hit, for the rest of the scene the target takes a -2 penalty on all actions. They may take a miscellaneous action (which may be flurried) to warm themselves back up to remove the penalty, if they have some means to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>Corrosive:</b> Some souls, along with the essence of demons, seethe with great vitriol, firing chemical lances instead of flame. If hit, the target's withering soak is reduced by 2 for the rest of the scene. This may be undone by a miscellaneous action to wipe themselves off, which may be flurried.<br /> <br /> <b>Holy:</b> The souls of the Solar Exalted along with other holy (more or less) beings burn away the impure. The attack deals aggravated damage to creatures touched by darkness, such as natives of Malfeas or the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <b>Humble:</b> The souls of many mortals burn only dimly, making the attack difficult to see. The target must roll (Wits + Awareness) at difficulty 4, or suffer a -2 penalty to their defense.<br /> <br /> <b>Shifting:</b> The souls of the Lunar Exalted and other shapeshifters lend their protean nature to the shot, giving it a form that molds itself to fit around (or through) any cover less than full, negating its benefits.<br /> <br /> This list is not exhaustive, nor is it required to use these exact effects for souls of the same type (a particularly bitter Solar could yield a corrosive soul, for example). Unique souls give unique effects when fired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1543-iethloc","name":"Iethloc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1543_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:13:38-07:00","id":914172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914130#post914130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I admit that I love the <i>concept</i> (or at least phrasing) of &quot;Reverse-Lumberjack&quot;, in the end it's just an axe that makes trees grow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I swear I'm gonna make this artifact one day and I'm gonna make it not suck. Reverse-Lumberjack, 4-dot Green Jade and Starmetal Grimcleaver, here I come.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:15:41-07:00","id":914174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914172#post914172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I swear I'm gonna make this artifact one day and I'm gonna make it not suck. Reverse-Lumberjack, 4-dot Green Jade and Starmetal Grimcleaver, here I come.</div> </div> </div> </div>Godspeed, good octocat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:16:48-07:00","id":914178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=913979#post913979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And critique I shall!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Converting 1 die to a success is, on average, the equivalent of adding +1 non-charm die to the roll (you turn 0.5 successes into 1). Increasing Parry by 1 is the equivalent of a 2m Excellency. That's a pretty hefty passive bonus, so I'd bump up the attunement cost to +2m.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Conceptually, a good first Evocation, but the wording is unclear. Does &quot;allied ranged attackers that are currently aiming at other targets&quot; mean &quot;allied ranged attackers who took the Aim action on their last turn&quot;? If yes, does &quot;may spontaneously switch their target to the wielder's opponent at no expense&quot; include &quot;retain bonus dice gained from aiming&quot;, or does it just allow them to make an attack out to medium+ range without aiming? Moreover, does the last effect last until the beginning, or the end of the wielder's next turn?<br /> <br /> In any case, effectively reducing the target's defense by 2 is an incredibly potent effect (+2 non-charm automatic successes on <i>all</i> incoming ranged attack rolls!), and a smart party can reap massive benefits from this if they're built around doing so. I'd either add a WP to the cost, or bump it up to 4 motes and give it a reset condition, with the assumption that you're modelling the opposition on the corebook's Antagonists session, most of whom have no convenient way to negate defense penalties. If your table regularly features opponents who can do so, the Evocation is fine as-is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I like how this expands on the native niche of Thrown as the tricky, gambit-oriented fighting style. On the other hand, I think using mean Evasion is quite unwieldy (are you rounding up or down? doesn't the math get annoying to deal with when there's 3+ opponents hanging around?). Just use the highest rating. Otherwise, it seems okay (cost is pretty hard to figure out - it lets you break initiative order, but that's basically Thunderclap Rush Attack, which costs 3 motes, but it also adds 1-3 non-charm successes to a disengage, but it's also tied to succeeding on an attack roll and has an Initiative cost, but it also moves people around and knocks them down, which is basically Mournful Crane's Cry, which costs 3m, but this is AoE, but MCC flings people away for 2 range bands - in any case, if you sum up the effects, 6 motes and the inherent costs of making a Distract gambit sound about right).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Seems like a pretty fun effect. Mechanically, it's a bit all over the place (summary says it lets you surprise attack a target, but it isn't <i>actually </i>a surprise attack, and the way it interacts with hardness is just... bwuh?). If you assume artifact armor to be rare, the damage boost can get out of hand quite quickly, but then again, the cost is incredibly high (about 15 motes if you full Excellency it, assuming Awareness 4 on part of the enemy, which strikes me as reasonable for most combatants important enough to warrant using a capstone on). And, of course, it runs into the problem of artifact armor and a decent Awareness score taking quite a lot out of its teeth, at which point you're stuck with an incredibly pricey effect that's of little benefit above Initiative 10 (and why would you launch your big decisive doomcombo while below Initiative 10?).<br /> <br /> So, umm, I'd basically make it an attempt to re-establish surprise, forget about the Hardness interaction, and reduce the cost.</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>I've upped the attunement cost, as suggested.</li> <li>Follow the Wind's Lead now clarifies who gains the benefit and I lowered the defense penalty to a -1.</li> <li>Whistle Down the Wind now uses the highest evasion.</li> <li>Out of the Blue is now 4m and now simply provides a surprise attack or an ambush, depending how well the contested roll to establish stealth goes.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T15:01:13-07:00","id":914404,"title":"","content":"Sorry, inspiration struck! It needs some mechanical help, though.<br /> <br /> <b>The Adder's Fang (Green Jade Throwing Knife - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> Forged during the height of the Shogunate for one of Shogun Shuoqing's favored daimyos, the Adder's Fang is a perfectly balanced throwing knife of green jade with a trio of pearls set into the hilt. The Fang has a long and storied history of murder, including the assassination of Shogun Shuoqing by his daimyo. In fact, everyone who has ever given the Adder's Fang as a gift has, thus far, been killed by it. Whether this is a true curse or merely ill fortune is hotly debated by those who discuss such things.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Adder's Fang</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blood who attunes to the Adder's Fang grants the weapon the Balanced and Special tags. The Special tag indicates that the Fang, once thrown, returns to its wielder's hand like an Infinite Chakram. The Fang otherwise behaves as a Light Artifact Thrown weapon with the Thrown (Short) tag.<br /> <br /> <b>Adder's Venom</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The least and most obvious power of the Adder's Fang is to produce a dose of a highly-potent nerve toxin, injected into a victim's bloodstream by even the smallest scratch. The toxin goes to work on the victim's chakras in seconds, slowing his reactions and causing his muscles to spasm and twitch uncontrollably. A successful decisive attack made with this Evocation injects the target with a dose of Snake Venom.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Toxic Bond</b><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Adder's Venom<br /> <br /> The power of the Adder's Fang is not merely in the wound it deals, but in the venom that courses through the target's veins thereafter. By activating this Evocation, the wielder can forge an instantaneous bond between herself and any target currently suffering from at least one dose of Snake Venom applied through this Evocation's prerequisite. This bond funnels the strength sapped by the venom from the victim into the wielder. Any Initiative lost due to Adder's Venom this turn is immediately gained by the wielder.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Venomous Whisper</b><br /> Cost: 5m,1W; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Toxic Bond<br /> <br /> The magic of the Adder's Fang is such that it can poison the mind as well as the body. This Evocation can be activated only when a target is suffering from Adder's Venom and has been the target of Toxic Bond in the same scene. While the poison courses through his veins, he begins to hallucinate, and the wielder of the blade gets a single, tortured glimpse of his psyche, functioning as a reflexive Read Intentions action to determine a Minor Tie. In that instant, she can metaphysically <i>twist </i>and cause that existing Tie of Minor strength to invert its emotional context, from hate to love, for example, or from pleasure to disgust. She must know the Tie she seeks to twist, and she cannot change the emotional context in any way but reversing it - she could not turn a man's love of his wife into lust, for example - only hatred.<br /> <br /> If used against the same target, and the same Tie, in the same scene, reduce the Evocation's cost to 3m and the Evocation can intensify the Tie to Major strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":". 06-14-2016, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T16:16:39-07:00","id":914446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914404#post914404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Adder's Fang (Green Jade Throwing Knife - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Adder's Fang</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blood who attunes to the Adder's Fang grants the weapon the Balanced and Special tags. The Special tag indicates that the Fang, once thrown, returns to its wielder's hand like an Infinite Chakram. The Fang otherwise behaves as a Light Artifact Thrown weapon with the Thrown (Short) tag.<br /> <br /> <b>Adder's Venom</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The least and most obvious power of the Adder's Fang is to produce a dose of a highly-potent nerve toxin, injected into a victim's bloodstream by even the smallest scratch. The toxin goes to work on the victim's chakras in seconds, slowing his reactions and causing his muscles to spasm and twitch uncontrollably. A successful decisive attack made with this Evocation injects the target with a dose of Snake Venom.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Toxic Bond</b><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Adder's Venom<br /> <br /> The power of the Adder's Fang is not merely in the wound it deals, but in the venom that courses through the target's veins thereafter. By activating this Evocation, the wielder can forge an instantaneous bond between herself and any target currently suffering from at least one dose of Snake Venom applied through this Evocation's prerequisite. This bond funnels the strength sapped by the venom from the victim into the wielder. Any Initiative lost due to Adder's Venom this turn is immediately gained by the wielder.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Venomous Whisper</b><br /> Cost: 5m,1W; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Toxic Bond<br /> <br /> The magic of the Adder's Fang is such that it can poison the mind as well as the body. This Evocation can be activated only when a target is suffering from Adder's Venom and has been the target of Toxic Bond in the same scene. While the poison courses through his veins, he begins to hallucinate, and the wielder of the blade gets a single, tortured glimpse of his psyche, functioning as a reflexive Read Intentions action to determine a Minor Tie. In that instant, she can metaphysically <i>twist </i>and cause that existing Tie of Minor strength to invert its emotional context, from hate to love, for example, or from pleasure to disgust. She must know the Tie she seeks to twist, and she cannot change the emotional context in any way but reversing it - she could not turn a man's love of his wife into lust, for example - only hatred.<br /> <br /> If used against the same target in the same scene, reduce the Evocation's cost to 3m and the Evocation can intensify the Tie to Major strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>A pretty straightforward weapon. I honestly have no commentary for it as the powers seem pretty simple. The first evocation is a straight copy from Spring Razor (I was looking at it today for inspiration), the second one looks decent too. My only complaint might be that Venomous Whisper has an Intimacy twisting power which is sort of out of theme for Green Jade. It's not <i>bad</i> it just feels out of place. I have the initial outline for a different version, but I admit that it's just not catching for me. Mine was more complex, but possibly less desirable as a consequence. If I make it come together I'll post it, but I might drop it. There's a reason I've been stuck on Green Jade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T16:18:22-07:00","id":914448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914446#post914446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A pretty straightforward weapon. I honestly have no commentary for it as the powers seem pretty simple. The first evocation is a straight copy from Spring Razor (I was looking at it today for inspiration), the second one looks decent too. My only complaint might be that Venomous Whisper has an Intimacy twisting power which is sort of out of theme for Green Jade. It's not <i>bad</i> it just feels out of place. I have the initial outline for a different version, but I admit that it's just not catching for me. Mine was more complex, but possibly less desirable as a consequence. If I make it come together I'll post it, but I might drop it. There's a reason I've been stuck on Green Jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly had no idea I was 'porting over from Spring Razor. I haven't even read that weapon's Evocations. Still, I appreciate the commentary, and I may keep whacking at that last power, just to see what I can do to make it feel more in theme. And I'd still love to see yours, if it happens to click!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T23:42:53-07:00","id":914696,"title":"","content":"<b>Sky-Bender (Black &amp; White Jade and Starmetal Aegis Shield, Artifact 4)</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>The Base</b><br /> <br /> An artifact Heavy Shield (<i>Accuracy +1 Damage +12 Defense +0 Overwhelming 5 Attunement 7 Tags: Chopping, Lethal, Melee, Shield, Smashing</i>)<br /> <br /> <b>Concept</b><br /> <br /> It was forged by the Solar that captured Isidoros single-handedly, at great personal sacrifice (their entire Legion), and echoes the legendary powers of that particular Yozi.<br /> <br /> <b>Description</b><br /> <br /> A great matte disc of Black Jade, covered in a coarse but intricate engraving in Old Realm script, rendered in wire-fine White Jade and Starmetal, describing a lament for a worthy opponent at the cessation of hostility. Has a single Hearthstone Setting, on the rear face, off-center, in line with the hand-grip.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Skybender</b><br /> <br /> This Heavy Shield finds its greatest potential in the hands of those who are self-reliant, driven, and relentless. Exalts of any kind that attune to Skybender add their Anima level to any Parry Defense they make with it, at a cost of reducing their Evasion by an equal amount, as the Black Boar was never one to flee from a fight, but rather to allow His foes to bask in His singularity.<br /> <br /> Solars that attune to Skybender are drawn to greater acts of bravado and heroism, often heedless of risks to life, limb, and welcome company; they add their Anima level to Resolve when defending an Intimacy relating to fighting on, be it against a worthy adversary or in the face of terrible odds.<br /> <br /> Sidereals, in contrast, find the solidity of Skybender\u2019s fate allows them to ground their own; while attuned, witnesses add the Vizier\u2019s Anima level to rolls to recall his presence.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded, whose forebearers paid the greatest cost in bringing Skybender into existance, add their Anima level to their Hardness and Soak while attuned.<br /> <br /> <b>Veil of Personal Magnetism</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m, 1a per level of Cover, optionally 1wp (+1wp) <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> One turn<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> Skybender, living up to its name, diffuses its Bearer\u2019s Anima into a gauzy haze that throws mirages and deflects attacks.<br /> This Evocation supplements a Take Cover action, allowing the Bearer to channel his Anima to bolster his Defense. The Bearer\u2019s Anima must, at a minimum, be at Glowing to use this ability. For every level of Anima committed, the Bearer may treat his Cover as one degree better, to a maximum of Full. At the start of the Bearer\u2019s next turn, his Anima fades to dim. Optionally, if no Cover is available, the Bearer may spend a point of temporary Willpower to summon viable Cover from his own Anima with this Evocation. This cover may move with him, and there are no additional limitations on available actions he can take while this power is active.<br /> At Essence 2 and above, the Bearer may expend an additional Willpower to extend the Cover granted or improved by this Evocation to a Battle Group of a Size no greater than his Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Lacuna of Crushing Eminence</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1a <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche, Uniform, Clash<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> indefinite<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Veil of Personal Magnetism<br /> <br /> In blocking his adversary\u2019s strikes, Skybender draws its bearer\u2019s quarry into his orbit with the strength of a collapsing star.<br /> The Bearer may clash a withering or decisive attack with such singular skill that it stokes the enemy\u2019s fear and respect. This clash attack does no damage, but, in addition to the penalty to Defense, allows the Bearer to make a reflexive Instill action (rolling Charisma + Melee), adding threshold successes from the Clash to the roll, and creating or improving an Intimacy of Awe toward the Bearer. This Intimacy lasts until a week passes with the Bearer not being within Essence miles of the Target or the Bearer is Crashed by the Target. The Bearer\u2019s Anima must be at Glowing before using this Charm, resets to Dim at the beginning of his next turn, and counts as the Bearer\u2019s attack action.<br /> <br /> <b>All Falls to Force</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m, 1wp <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Turn<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Lacuna of Crushing Eminence<br /> <br /> Marked as worthy opponents, the Bearer\u2019s foes are drawn to the hunt.<br /> When using Skybender to defend himself, the Bearer may use this Evocation to make those they cherish inapplicable targets. All incoming attacks must target him until his next turn. During this time, if his defense is penetrated, those whom he holds an Intimacy towards, or who hold an Intimacy toward him, cannot be attacked. His Anima must be at Burning to use this Evocation.<br /> <br /> <b>Magnanimous Adversary Ansible</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m, 1+a <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> All Falls to Force, Lacuna of Crushing Eminence<br /> <br /> Distance means little to those who are the center, and Skybender was born in the shadow of the center.<br /> While the Bearer's Anima is at least at Glowing, those that recognize his greatness, and are bathed in it, are always readily at hand. The Bearer may invoke this Evocation to instantaneously close the distance between himself and one that either bears an Intimacy toward him or that he bears an Intimacy toward, appearing at their side as if he had been there all along. The distance he may cross is proportional to his Anima level; at Glowing, he may cross Short distances, at Burning, Medium, at Iconic, Long. He may hold the activation of this Charm to Clash a Withering or Decisive Attack made against or by the subject of the Tie with Skybender. This counts as the Bearer's Attack Action, and causes his Anima to fade back to Dim.<br /> <br /> <b>Unassailable Whim-Driven Behemoth</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 3a <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> All Falls to Force, Lacuna of Crushing Eminence, Magnanimous Adversary Ansible<br /> <br /> At the heights of power, those who\u2019ve truly bonded with Skybender are like unto the great beasts of ages uncounted.<br /> When the Bearer\u2019s Anima becomes Iconic, Skybender\u2019s magic makes it extraordinarily difficult for Trivial enemies to engage him in combat, regardless of their numbers. He does not take onslaught penalties from any attack made by Trivial opponents or Battle Groups, although magically inflicted onslaught penalties still apply against him. Withering attacks made by such enemies cannot drop him below 1 Initiative unless they have a post-soak damage of 10 dice (although attackers can still gain the full amount of Initiative damage dealt). Decisive attacks made by such enemies cannot deal more than (3 + attacker\u2019s Strength) levels of damage to the Bearer with a single attack, not counting any levels of damage added by Charms or other magic. This Evocation ends prematurely if the Bearer is Crashed, causing their Anima to fade to Dim.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Feedback welcomed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":".  Added costs and a Hearthstone Setting, and reworked a few of the powers. 06-16-2016, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T05:05:17-07:00","id":914755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914083#post914083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've spent ALL DAY thinking it was Wednesday or Thursday already... but it's <b>Tuesday</b>. So now I'm depressed.<br /> <br /> Cheer me up. What are some ideas for a Green Jade artifact that has <b>nothing to do with plants or wood</b>. Bonus points if it's <b>not a sword</b>, double bonus points if it's <b>not a bow</b>, triple bonus points if it <b>does</b> have to do with plants or wood but in a sufficiently <i><b>interesting and unique way </b></i>such that I am inspired to write it. Fair warning, that last one will be a challenge because I've seen a lot and I'm <i>ver</i><i>y</i> bored with the plant evocations.<br /> <br /> A reminder of it's properties</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like you need the Green Jade Tea Lantern; a small spouted pot that allows an exalt to brew their essence into various drinks, posibly even allowing them to invest a few motes into an otherwise mortal imbiber to form familiar-like bonds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T07:59:12-07:00","id":914828,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Says I posted at 9:59. sure. I started posting at 9:59. I finished posting about 16:00.<br /> <br /> I've never create an artefact or evocations before, but I had this idea while pondering an alternative character for the game I'm in, and I want to get some feedback before I go in supplication to my ST. Formatting stolen wholesale from Jen's Lunar Eclipse (since it's also a mask, and I like the colours Jen used). I've included a few additional options for charms, because I had so many ideas and didn't know which ones would work best. Only one of the capstones is actually included in the final evocation set, so the capstone A is really jsut an extension of the previous ability, but one i'm not comfortable keeping if the other capstone is also in. This is all based largely on fluff and what I want the artefact to feel like, but I'm under no illusions that this is mechanically fine as it is - if you guys could set me straight, that'd be great.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Eyes of the Raksha (Moonsilver and Black Jade Mask ****)</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Eyes of the Raksha is a new artefact, crafted only months ago for the disfigured artist, Silent Song. It enhances and projects the ever-growing insanity of the wearer, helping others see the world as he does. The mask is also associated with scalding steam and burning water - the tools used to torture Silent Song moments prior to his Exaltation.<br /> <br /> The first evocation of Eyes of the Raksha is unlocked if the wearer has a Derangement. If the wearer loses their Derangement, they lose access to all the evocations of Eyes of the Raksha until they regain their Derangement, although evocations with special activation rules must be unlocked again. The wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha beholds the world in an entirely alien way, and may automatically dismiss any attempt or situation that would remove their Derangement. (These rules are in place to allow for a character to regain their sanity if they should choose, but not require them to do so, and supports the heroic image of a character throwing away their source of power, only to return to it, contrite, when times are dire and the world needs them once more). The Black Jade is there because I want the mask to have steam associations, but the Black Jade isn't represented in this set of evocations.<br /> <br /> Keyword: Maddening Insight. Maddening Insights represent the.. well, the maddening insights, accrued by those who face the Eyes of the Raksha. The Eyes feeds off of this power to tip the balance of situations towards true, deep madness, and those who wield its strength.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><b>Seeing Through the Eyes of the Raksha</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: None</span></span><br /> <br /> When the wearer is Seeing Through the Eyes of the Raksha, they can impart their understanding to the people around them, gracing everyone with the unwelcome insights she has gleaned from the union, and filling her foes with uncertainty.<br /> <br /> As a reflexive action, when the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha makes a successful social action, or someone makes a successful social action against her, her opponent gains one Maddening Insight. A character may only have as many points of Maddening Insight as the wearer has Essence, and must reroll successes on their first action each round equal to the number of Maddening Insight they possess, starting with non-doubled dice. At the end of a scene, any Maddening Insights are lost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><b>Lunatic's Alternate Truth</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m per threshold success; Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Seeing Through the Eyes of the Raksha</span></span><br /> <br /> Lunatic's Alternate Truth upgrades its prerequisite and costs 2 mote per threshold success scored against her on a social roll.<br /> <br /> What is madness to the mad? Anyone can see meaning where there is none, but only the insight of lunacy allows one to see nothing where there is something. Sharing this true understanding, the wearer of the Eyes hides what is and presents a much more palatable &quot;truth&quot; to those who enquire.<br /> <br /> When using Seeing Through the Eyes of the Raksha to add a point of Maddening Insight (if they cannot or do not gain another point for any reason, this evocation does not apply) when she is the target of social influence, the wearer of the Eyes pays 2 motes per threshold success her opponent scored, and simply lies about the result. A Profile action provides a false profile, a Read Intentions gives a false intimacy, a Persuade gives the impression of success but the wearer is simply unimpressed. Unless the wearer of the Eyes does something that clearly violates the falsehood she has provided, this alternative truth is as real to the other character as a success would normally be, and violating the alternative truth does not provide insight into the actual truth.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: Lunatic's Alternate Truth cannot be unlocked with XP. Instead, it automatically unlocks after someone with Maddening Insight makes a successful social action against the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha, and cannot gain a point of Maddening Insight because they are already at the limit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><b>Ultimate Refuge of the Wise</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1m +2m per Maddening Insight; Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche, Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Seeing Through the Eyes of the Raksha</span></span><br /> <br /> The wise man knows that he knows nothing, and everyone else knows even less. When a foe is blinded by sight or deafened by hearing, the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha releases them from their burden, freeing them to partake of the sheer intention of their actions without heed to the falsehood of &quot;result&quot;.<br /> <br /> The wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha may turn successes on a roll into points of initiative at a 1:1 ratio. This effect may be used on the wearer, or anyone with Maddening Insight, by spending at least 1 point of their Maddening Insight and 1 mote, plus 2 more motes per point of Maddening Insight spent. The ratio of Successes to Initiative is Maddening Insight spent to 1 initiative. When using it on themselves, the wearer of the Eyes transfers successes to initiative 1:1.<br /> <br /> (In pure maths - The cost is 1 mote + 2X motes, and yields a ratio of X Successes to 1 initiative, where X is the Maddening Insights spent, or a flat 1 Success per initiative for herself. Although I feel like the effect is probably too much hassle if I have to use algebra to express it)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Teachings Absent of Meaning</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: -; Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Ultimate Refuge of the Wise</span></span><br /> <br /> Teachings Absent of Meaning upgrades its prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Imparting an absence of knowledge is a difficult task, even for those who know nothing, but it is always worthwhile. By completely opening the mind of an opponent gifted with true understanding, the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha can transform all action into resultless intention.<br /> <br /> When the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha spends all of the Maddening Insight on an opponent with this evocation's prerequisite, the number of successes required to turn into a single point of initiative is doubled. Conversely, by opening her own mind, she can convert her own successes to initiative at a rate of 1 success to 2 initiative.</span></span><br /> <br /> (In pure maths - This changes the prerequisite to cost 1 mote + 2X motes, and yield a ratio of 2X Successes to 1 initiative, where X is the Maddening Insights spent, or 1 Success to 2 initiative for herself)<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: Teachings Absent of Meaning cannot be unlocked with XP. Instead it automatically unlocks after the wearer of the Eyes of Raksha gains Essence 3 and uses its prerequisite to expend the maximum number of Maddening Insights on an opponent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Philosophy of Nothing - Capstone A</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1m per Maddening Insight; Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Ultimate Refuge of the Mind</span></span><br /> <br /> The Philosophy of Nothing upgrades its prerequisite.<br /> <br /> The student of the Eyes of the Raksha comes to a sudden realisation - The false dichotomy they have constructed between intent and result is just that, a falsehood. Imparting this knowledge, even for a fleeting moment, brings the world to a halt.<br /> <br /> When the wearer of the Eyes uses Ultimate Refuge of the Wise or Teachings Absent of Meaning, the effect can be applied to Threshold successes or successes after soak.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: Teachings Absent of Meaning cannot be unlocked with XP. Instead it automatically unlocks after the wearer of the Eyes of Raksha reduces the total number of successes on a roll to 0, while increasing the target's initiative to 16 or more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Opportunities to Learn - Capstone B</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1i per Maddening Insight; Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche, Decisive, Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Teachings Absent of Meaning, Lunatic's Alternate Truth</span></span><br /> <br /> As a teacher of oblivion and a preacher of absence, the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha earns and requires great strength to perform the feats required of her, and she will not always be able to handle the task without help. Fortunately, the strength of the mad is not restricted for their own use, and as quickly as enlightenment is granted, it can be taken away.<br /> <br /> By spending points of Maddening Insight from any characters present in the scene, the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha can bring the false reality crashing back into the minds of the mad, reducing their initiative by the number of Maddening Insights spent from that character. The wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha gains an equal amount of initiative. (This is in here because the initiative cost listed represents a barrier to use, rather than a cost proper). Any character crashed by this evocation has not fully come to terms with the reality he is presented with, and regains one Maddening Insight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":11875,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","user":"Rowanas","date":". 06-17-2016, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T09:23:38-07:00","id":915651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914828#post914828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eyes of the Raksha (Moonsilver and Black Jade Mask ****)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a VERY cool artifact and an impressive first attempt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914828#post914828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><b>Seeing Through the Eyes of the Raksha</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: None</span></span><br /> <br /> When the wearer is Seeing Through the Eyes of the Raksha, they can impart their understanding to the people around them, gracing everyone with the unwelcome insights she has gleaned from the union, and filling her foes with uncertainty. As a reflexive action, when the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha makes a successful social action, or someone makes a successful social action against her, the other character gains one Maddening Insight. A character may only have as many points of Maddening Insight as the wearer has Essence, and must reroll successes on their first action each round equal to the number of Maddening Insight they possess, starting with non-doubled dice. At the end of a scene, any Maddening Insights are lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Go through your evocations and unify your terms. &quot;Other person&quot; should be target, foe, victim or something along those lines. Other person is too vague, especially when listing multiple situations that can trigger it. Otherwise, a good starting evocation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914828#post914828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><b>Lunatic's Alternate Truth</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m per threshold success; Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Seeing Through the Eyes of the Raksha</span></span><br /> <br /> Lunatic's Alternate Truth upgrades its prerequisite and costs 1 mote per threshold success scored against her on a social roll.<br /> <br /> What is madness to the mad? Anyone can see meaning where there is none, but only the insight of lunacy allows one to see nothing where there is something. Sharing this true understanding, the wearer of the Eyes hides what is and presents a much more palatable &quot;truth&quot; to those who enquire. When using Seeing Through the Eyes of the Raksha to add a point of Maddening Insight (if they cannot or do not gain another point for any reason, this evocation does not apply) when she is the target of social influence, the wearer of the Eyes simply lies about the result. A Profile action provides a false profile, a Read Intentions gives a false intimacy, a Persuade gives the impression of success but the wearer is simply unimpressed. Unless the wearer of the Eyes does something that clearly violates the falsehood she has provided, this alternative truth is as real to the other character as a success would normally be, and violating the alternative truth does not provide insight into the actual truth.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: Lunatic's Alternate Truth cannot be unlocked with XP. Instead, it automatically unlocks after someone with Maddening Insight makes a successful social action against the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha, and cannot gain a point of Maddening Insight because they are already at the limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how the cost of this evocation interacts with the text. Basically the only mechanics I see are a perfect defense, but your cost shows a variable cost. This needs clarification. Might I also recommend breaking up your paragraphs a bit. It's a bit dense to read through to separate the mechanics and the flavor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914828#post914828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#a64d79\"><b>Ultimate Refuge of the Wise</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1m +2m per Maddening Insight; Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche, Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Seeing Through the Eyes of the Raksha</span></span><br /> <br /> The wise man knows that he knows nothing, and everyone else knows even less. When a foe is blinded by sight or deafened by hearing, the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha releases them from their burden, freeing them to partake of the sheer intention of their actions without heed to the falsehood of &quot;result&quot;. The wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha may spend 3 motes to turn successes on a roll into points of initiative at a 1:1 ratio. This effect may be used on the wearer, or anyone with Maddening Insight, by sacrificing a point of their Maddening Insight. For an additional expenditure of 2 motes per extra point of Maddening Insight, the wearer may worsen the ratio by 1, so by spending 5 motes and 3 points of Maddening Insight, 3 successes become 1 point of initiative. The wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha chooses how much or how little of the Maddening Insight to spend. When using it on themselves, the wearer of the Eyes transfers successes to initiative 1:1</div> </div> </div> </div>The wording of this evocation is weird. I thought I understood it but you have a lot of different costs in the text but only 1 cost in the charm details at the top. In general, I'm cool with the idea of converting Maddening Insight into Initiative, but make sure the math is clear and concise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914828#post914828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Teachings Absent of Meaning</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: -; Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Ultimate Refuge of the Wise</span></span><br /> <br /> Teachings Absent of Meaning upgrades its prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Imparting an absence of knowledge is a difficult task, even for those who know nothing, but it is always worthwhile. By completely opening the mind of an opponent gifted with true understanding, the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha can transform all action into resultless intention. When the Raksha spends all of the Maddening Insight on an opponent with this evocation's prerequisite, the number of successes required to turn into a single point of initiative is doubled. Conversely, by opening her own mind, she can convert her own successes to initiative at a rate of 1 success to 2 initiative.</span></span><br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: Teachings Absent of Meaning cannot be unlocked with XP. Instead it automatically unlocks after the wearer of the Eyes of Raksha gains Essence 3 and uses its prerequisite to expend the maximum number of Maddening Insights on an opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This will make more sense when its prerequisite is cleared up. What is the goal of these evocations? Is it for you the wearer to gain initiative? Or the target? The description goes back and forth between focuses it can be hard to follow. Very flavorful descriptions and concepts, but your logic needs to be clear to follow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914828#post914828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Philosophy of Nothing - Capstone A</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1m per Maddening Insight; Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Ultimate Refuge of the Mind</span></span><br /> <br /> The Philosophy of Nothing upgrades its prerequisite.<br /> <br /> The student of the Eyes of the Raksha comes to a sudden realisation - The false dichotomy they have constructed between intent and result is just that, a falsehood. Imparting this knowledge, even for a fleeting moment, brings the world to a halt. When the wearer of the Eyes uses Ultimate Refuge of the Wise or Teachings Absent of Meaning, the effect can be applied to Threshold successes or successes after soak.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: Teachings Absent of Meaning cannot be unlocked with XP. Instead it automatically unlocks after the wearer of the Eyes of Raksha reduces the total number of successes on a roll to 0, while increasing the target's initiative to 16 or more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems solid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914828#post914828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Opportunities to Learn - Capstone B</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 1i per Maddening Insight; Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche, Decisive, Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: Teachings Absent of Meaning, Lunatic's Alternate Truth</span></span><br /> <br /> As a teacher of oblivion and a preacher of absence, the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha earns and requires great strength to perform the feats required of her, and she will not always be able to handle the task without help. Fortunately, the strength of the mad is not restricted for their own use, and as quickly as enlightenment is granted, it can be taken away. By sacrificing points of Maddening Insight from any characters present in the scene, the wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha can bring the false reality crashing back into the minds of the mad, reducing their initiative by the number of Maddening Insights sacrificed from that character. The wearer of the Eyes of the Raksha gains an equal amount of initiative. (This is in here because the initiative cost listed represents a barrier to use, rather than a cost proper). Any character crashed by this evocation has not fully come to terms with the reality he is presented with, and regains one Maddening Insight.</div> </div> </div> </div>So overall this artifact has some really cool stuff going for it, and I love the unique direction it's going. But it is had to follow some of the math logic in it, just based on the wording. Put some paragraphs in, read some of the mechanics sections outloud for clarity, and make sure the listed cost represents what the text says, and this will be a winner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T09:30:28-07:00","id":915654,"title":"","content":"So here's the daggers I made. I wrestled with these for a long time, only to decide that I didn't like my poison mechanic. As soon as I removed that, it all fell into place. Also I'm sad to say that my brain is running dry on flavor-text. So no story with this one. I'm kind of ashamed of myself, but I'm just not there and I'm anxious to get these done and posted.<br /> <br /> I invented Godrippers as a category, but basically they're long thin artifact daggers. They could have been short daiklaves, but I didn't want them to be perceived as swords. That said, I don't see any reason these couldn't be used with Steel Devil Style. There wouldn't be a done of synergy anyways, so no harm is done.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Heartleeches (Green Jade Godrippers ***)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> The Heartleeches are a pair of long artifact daggers made of Green Jade. They are molded in a wicked, barbed pattern which makes them nasty to pull out of a target impaled by them. They seem to reflect light in odd colors. Godrippers function as Light Artifact Weapons with the Melee, Lethal, Thrown (Short), and Piercing tags. There is a hearthstone socket in the pommel of each Heartleech.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Evocations of Heartleeches</b></span><br /> Solars or Dragonblooded who attune to the Heartleeches regain (Essence) free motes of essence once per turn when they successfully deal damage with a Decisive attack.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Spirit Bane Strike</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m (+1wp) <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Uniform<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> The Heartleeches cut at the soul of their target, slicing away pieces of their divinity. An attack supplemented with Spirit Bane Strike may exchange threshold successes from their attack roll to burn away an equal amount of Essence from the victim. Alternatively, for an extra willpower in cost, the exalt may burn away a single point of Willpower from the target.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Soul Exhausting Stab</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4m, 1wp <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Spirit Bane Strike<br /> <br /> With a mighty throw or a forceful thrust, the Heartleech digs into the victim, coopting their power for the exalt. Soul Exhausting Stab is a special Decisive attack that if successful, after the damage phase the Heartleech is left embedded in the body of the target. As long as the exalt is holding the other Heartleech, the daggers steal 1 mote of essence from the target and grant it to the exalt at the start of each round. The dagger may be removed by the exalt as a reflexive action if in close range. The target may remove the dagger as a miscellaneous action, but doing so deals 2 dice of Lethal damage that ignores hardness. Alternatively, they may more carefully remove it and ignore the damage, but the miscellaneous action becomes unflurriable.<br /> <br /> For 2 additional motes in the activation of this evocation (or after a second successful use of it with the other Heartleech, in which case waive the willpower cost) the exalt may embed the second dagger into the target as well. While both godrippers are stuck into the target, the feedback from the drain causes an Essence-bleed of 5 motes at the start of each round, although these motes are simply lost as the exalt is not holding either of the daggers. Removing each Heartleech must be a separate miscellaneous action for the target.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Heart Tearing Skewer</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 6m, 1wp <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Soul Exhausting Stab<br /> <br /> With a smooth motion, the exalt retrieves their weapons much to their foe\u2019s dismay. Heart Tearing skewer may only be activated when Soul Exhausting Stab has been used to have at least 1 Heartleech embedded in the target. Grabbing hold of the godripper, the exalt tears it free sundering their foe and scattering their power.<br /> <br /> This evocation is a Decisive attack that gains Essence bonus dice on the attack roll. If the attack is successful, the exalt shatters all non-permanent magical effects that the target may have around them, ending them prematurely. Additionally, the target\u2019s heart is weakened by the power of the blades, causing all willpower expenditures to require an extra point to use for the remainder of the scene. This includes charm and spell costs, overturning social influence, and die rerolls.<br /> <br /> If the attack is enhanced with Spirit Bane Strike, each threshold success burns away 2 essence instead of 1, or if used to attack their willpower pool, it burns away 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","user":"The Unsung Hero","date":". 06-16-2016, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T09:43:09-07:00","id":915665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915654#post915654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I invented Godrippers as a category, but basically they're long thin artifact daggers. They could have been short daiklaves, but I didn't want them to be perceived as swords. That said, I don't see any reason these couldn't be used with Steel Devil Style. There wouldn't be a done of synergy anyways, so no harm is done.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Heartleeches (Green Jade Godrippers ***)</b></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well done, sir! I like these, and would use them in my campaign as-is!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T09:53:14-07:00","id":915671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915665#post915665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well done, sir! I like these, and would use them in my campaign as-is!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! The hard part (after giving up on the poison mechanic, which would have been much more interesting but also more complex) was after I created them, I realized they were useless against anything without an Essence pool. In fact, in retrospect, I should have made the 2nd evocation have an effect that impacted Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T09:55:49-07:00","id":915672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915671#post915671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you! The hard part (after giving up on the poison mechanic, which would have been much more interesting but also more complex) was after I created them, I realized they were useless against anything without an Essence pool. In fact, in retrospect, I should have made the 2nd evocation have an effect that impacted Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Useless,&quot; except, y'know, for stabbing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T09:57:00-07:00","id":915673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915672#post915672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Useless,&quot; except, y'know, for stabbing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'll leave it as is, simply as a builder for the pinnacle. It's not great against mortals or beasts without mote pools, but it's ok to have a specialized weapon like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T09:59:30-07:00","id":915676,"title":"","content":"So I am now up to 19 artifacts. I've made 1 pure item out of each material and mixed of all but Green (Green is now the only one besides Orichalcum to have more than 1 pure artifact). I still don't end up liking Green Jade or Starmetal much. Even Moonsilver is giving me more ideas, and that's the least clear set of rules of all the materials. Just interesting to note. <br /> <br /> Thanks to everyone who jumps in when we ask for inspiration. This thread is a credit to the community!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T11:38:41-07:00","id":915737,"title":"","content":"Here's some more critique fodder for you guys! My PC's circle explored their first First Age tomb in the beginning of the year, where they acquired an orichalcum chain shirt. I've finally gotten around to giving it a name and evocations.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Lights the Night</span></b><br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact: Orichalcum Chain Shirt<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Origin</span></b></u><br /> Found in First Age tomb of the solar who trapped Golden Maya, an Unshaped, centuries before the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Appearance</span></b></u><br /> This chain shirt is built with butted orichalcum links that cover down to the thighs and to the elbow for its sleeves. Lights the Night closes at the front with three silver palmette-form clasps. The pattern of the chain linkage form an ogival lattice design across the entire armor. Due to its otherwise simple design, Lights the night has no hearthstone sockets.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><u><b>Attunement</b></u></span><br /> Attunement Bonus Cost: 0m<br /> - Upon attunement, Guiding Candles Through Rough Waters is learned at no experience cost<br /> Attunement Bonus Cost: +1m<br /> - Non-night caste Solars and Fire-Aspected Dragonblooded may raise their anima from dim to glowing and from glowing to burning for 4 peripheral motes each.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Evocations</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Guiding Candles Through Rough Waters</span></b><br /> Cost: 6m<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> One Line Summary: Rally armies or stop panicking crowds with your literal light<br /> <br /> The warm glow of Lights the Night is a beacon that the masses can rally behind, lead the lost home, bring calm where there is frightful darkness. Upon activation, the wearer and all allies are more resilient against panic. When the target of a social influence action to instill fear, the target may add (wearer\u2019s current anima rating) to their resolve. If the wearer is commanding a battle group, the group can reroll (current anima rating) dice once, taking the better of the rolls, to resist rout and to rally around the wearer. Finally, the ability for the wearer to guide others through treacherous terrain is significantly improved, negating penalties from poor visibility and adding 1 success to all others in long range to safely navigate around dangerous obstacles.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: Usable once per scene. This evocation can only be activated when the wearer is already at the glowing anima level or higher and will end prematurely if it should fall to the dim anima level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Like a Beacon of Indomitable Brilliance</span></b><br /> Cost: 3m 1a 1i<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Withering-Only, Perilous<br /> Duration: One attack against the wearer<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Guiding a Candle Upon Rough Waters<br /> One Line Summary: Creatures of darkness must spend additional motes to attack the wearer.<br /> <br /> Darkness, no matter its form, is simply a lack of light, in one way or another. It is this lacking that the Light\u2019s the Night\u2019s inner light taxes shades, the soulless and the damned. Whenever a creature of darkness attempts a withering attack against the wearer, the attacker must spend an additional (wearer\u2019s current anima rating before expending it) in motes. If the attacker was already spending essence on the attack, they must pay this tax on top of the essence already spent.<br /> <br /> If the attacker cannot fully pay the surcharge in essence, the attacker must pay what they can and then the rest are paid in successes removed from the attack roll. If the loss of successes is enough that the attack misses or if the attack would hit but is fully absorbed by soak before minimum damage is applied, the wearer is recouped the anima loss.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spreading the Eternal Light</span></b><br /> Cost: 5m 3a 1W<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Like a Beacon of Indomitable Brilliance<br /> One Line Summary: Release one\u2019s anima to ignite the anima banners of allied exalts and a bonus for mortals Even in the purest void, a single candle can start a brilliant bonfire and thus even the smallest light can flare into a new dawn. By letting go of their anima and letting it wash over those around them, the wearer can energize the soul of all other surrounding allies that the wearer has a positive tie with. The eligible allies must be within 3 range bands of the wearer. Each ally gains initiative equal to the strongest positive tie they have for the wearer.<br /> <br /> In addition, each exalted ally feels their anima supercharged, gaining up to the wearer\u2019s respective intimacy rating in anima levels.<br /> <br /> Finally, eligible mortals gain the following boons:<br /> - Ignore up to (wearer\u2019s intimacy rating for the mortal) of dice lost to penalties<br /> - On their next action, they can reroll all 1\u2019s until 1\u2019s disappear.<br /> <br /> Useable only once per scene.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","user":"Binary Phantom","date":".  first update post feedback 06-17-2016, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T12:43:30-07:00","id":915769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915654#post915654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Evocations of Heartleeches</b></span><br /> Solars or Dragonblooded who attune to the Heartleeches regain (Essence) free motes of essence any time they successfully deal damage with a Decisive attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, 15m of free stuff when I smack people with Iron Whirlwind+Invincible Flurry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e an