/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:41:22-07:00","id":915819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915802#post915802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Make the mote generation work once per turn and it should be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Done ten characters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:46:24-07:00","id":915820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915737#post915737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Lights the Night</span></b><br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact: Orichalcum Chain Shirt<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><u><b>Attunement</b></u></span> - non-night caste Solar and Fire-Aspected Dragonblooded Exalted may pay 1 additional motes to lessen the cost of raising from dim to glowing anima and glowing to burning anima to 4 peripheral motes each. This will reduces the amount of essence respired from 5 to 4 motes/(turn or hour, as applicable)<br /> - Upon attunement, Guiding Candles Through Rough Waters is learned at no experience cost<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Evocations</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Guiding Candles Through Rough Waters</span></b><br /> Cost: 6m<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> One Line Summary: Rally armies or stop panicking crowds with your literal light<br /> <br /> The warm glow of Lights the Night is a beacon that the masses can rally behind, lead the lost home, bring calm where there is frightful darkness. Upon activation, the wearer and all allies are more resilient against panic. When the target of a social influence action to instill fear, the target may add (wearer\u2019s current anima rating) to their resolve. If the wearer is commanding a battle group, the group can reroll (current anima rating) dice once, taking the better of the rolls, to resist rout and to rally around the wearer. Finally, the ability for the wearer to guide others through treacherous terrain is significantly improved, negating penalties from poor visibility and adding 1 success to all others in long range to safely navigate around dangerous obstacles.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rules: Usable once per scene. This evocation can only be activated when the wearer is already at the glowing anima level or higher and will end prematurely if it should fall to the dim anima level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Like a Beacon of Indomitable Brilliance</span></b><br /> Cost: 3m 1a 1i<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Withering-Only, Perilous<br /> Duration: One attack against the wearer<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Guiding a Candle Upon Rough Waters<br /> One Line Summary: Creatures of darkness must spend additional motes to attack the wearer.<br /> <br /> Darkness, no matter its form, is simply a lack of light, in one way or another. It is this lacking that the Light\u2019s the Night\u2019s inner light taxes shades, the soulless and the damned. Whenever a creature of darkness attempts a withering attack against the wearer, the attacker must spend an additional (wearer\u2019s current anima rating before expending it) in motes. If the attacker was already spending essence on the attack, they must pay this tax on top of the essence already spent.<br /> <br /> If the attacker cannot fully pay the surcharge in essence, the attacker must pay what they can and then the rest are paid in successes removed from the attack roll. If the loss of successes is enough that the attack misses or if the attack would hit but is fully absorbed by soak before minimum damage is applied, the wearer is recouped the anima loss.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spreading the Eternal Light</span></b><br /> Cost: 5m 3a 1W<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Like a Beacon of Indomitable Brilliance<br /> One Line Summary: Release one\u2019s anima to ignite the anima banners of allied exalts and a bonus for mortals<br /> <br /> Even in the purest void, a single candle can start a brilliant bonfire and thus even the smallest light can flare into a new dawn. By letting go of their anima and letting it wash over those around them, the wearer can charge the anima of any other exalt that the wearer has a positive tie with. The targeted exalt must be within line-of-sight. The exalt gains the wearer\u2019s intimacy rating in anima levels and gain initiative equal to the strongest positive tie they have for the wearer.<br /> <br /> Benevolent mortals in line-of-sight also benefit from this act, gaining the initiative as an exalt does and gaining the following:<br /> - Ignore up to (wearer\u2019s intimacy rating for mortal) of dice lost to penalties<br /> - On their next action, they can reroll all 1\u2019s until 1\u2019s disappear.<br /> <br /> Useable only once per scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one. My only hesitation is how much of the rules revolve around all participants having mote pools, but you do account for that in the end. The attunement bonus is interesting and unique (and frankly almost punishing) and the rest of it seems to work out pretty well. I'm not sure if Mortals get the bigger benefit or Exalts on that last evocation, but I guess if I'm not sure, then it's relatively balanced (someone else may say otherwise). <br /> <br /> I love artifacts that use Anima levels and this seems to do it pretty well. Nice jorb!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T16:02:38-07:00","id":915899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915737#post915737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Lights the Night</span></b><br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact: Orichalcum Chain Shirt</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool artifact. Love it thematically. However...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915737#post915737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><u><b>Attunement</b></u></span> - non-night caste Solar and Fire-Aspected Dragonblooded Exalted may pay 1 additional motes to lessen the cost of raising from dim to glowing anima and glowing to burning anima to 4 peripheral motes each. This will reduces the amount of essence respired from 5 to 4 motes/(turn or hour, as applicable)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a terrible deal. Think of it as effectively raising the artifact's attunement cost in any combat by (duration in turns). Unless you have really twinked-out PCs, most combats with important adversaries can be assumed to last at least 5 turns. I don't doubt that being able to raise your anima 1m cheaper <i>can</i> be a benefit, but it's definitely not a benefit worth paying a 5m attunement surcharge for.<br /> <br /> Since I think having an easy-to-raise anima is a double-edged sword in itself (with a 4m/level cost, you can only raise static values by 1 from peripheral before you start glowing!), I'd just ditch the last sentence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915737#post915737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spreading the Eternal Light</span></b><br /> Cost: 5m 3a 1W<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Like a Beacon of Indomitable Brilliance<br /> One Line Summary: Release one\u2019s anima to ignite the anima banners of allied exalts and a bonus for mortals<br /> <br /> Even in the purest void, a single candle can start a brilliant bonfire and thus even the smallest light can flare into a new dawn. By letting go of their anima and letting it wash over those around them, the wearer can charge the anima of any other exalt that the wearer has a positive tie with. The targeted exalt must be within line-of-sight. The exalt gains the wearer\u2019s intimacy rating in anima levels and gain initiative equal to the strongest positive tie they have for the wearer.<br /> <br /> Benevolent mortals in line-of-sight also benefit from this act, gaining the initiative as an exalt does and gaining the following:<br /> - Ignore up to (wearer\u2019s intimacy rating for mortal) of dice lost to penalties<br /> - On their next action, they can reroll all 1\u2019s until 1\u2019s disappear.<br /> <br /> Useable only once per scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be missing something here, but I genuinely can't see how the ability to give a single person a maximum of 4 Initiative while raising their anima to bonfire once per scene is such a powerful ability that it has to cost 5 motes, a WP, and an action.<br /> <br /> I'd just flat-out have it affect everybody within 3 range bands of the wearer (and have it grant the Initiative bonus to mortals as well). Might be really powerful in a really specific situation (more than two characters are in range who a/ have Melee as their combat ability of choice, b/ have just used OWTB last turn,and c/ are within 3 range bands of the wearer, but also conveniently in position to attack somebody on their next turn), but I'm just not really seeing a situation like that emerge very often organically in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 06-16-2016, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T16:05:09-07:00","id":915900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=914696#post914696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sky-Bender</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>The Base</b><br /> <br /> An artifact Heavy Shield (<i>Accuracy +1 Damage +12 Defense +0 Overwhelming 5 Attunement 7 Tags: Chopping, Lethal, Melee, Shield, Smashing</i>)<br /> <br /> <b>Concept</b><br /> <br /> It was forged by the Solar that captured Isidoros single-handedly, at great personal sacrifice (their entire Legion), and echoes the legendary powers of that particular Yozi.<br /> <br /> <b>Description</b><br /> <br /> A great matte disc of Black Jade, covered in a coarse but intricate engraving in Old Realm script, rendered in wire-fine White Jade and Starmetal, describing a lament for a worthy opponent at the cessation of hostility.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Skybender</b><br /> <br /> This Heavy Shield finds its greatest potential in the hands of those who are self-reliant, driven, and relentless. Exalts of any kind that attune to Skybender add their Anima level to any Parry Defense they make with it, at a cost of reducing their Evasion by an equal amount, as the Black Boar was never one to flee from a fight, but rather to allow His foes to bask in His singularity.<br /> <br /> Solars that attune to Skybender are drawn to greater acts of bravado and heroism, often heedless of risks to life, limb, and welcome company; they add their Anima level to Resolve when defending an Intimacy relating to fighting on, be it against a worthy adversary or in the face of terrible odds.<br /> <br /> Sidereals, in contrast, find the solidity of Skybender\u2019s fate allows them to ground their own; while attuned, witnesses add the Vizier\u2019s Anima level to rolls to recall his presence.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded, whose forebearers paid the greatest cost in bringing Skybender into existance, add their Anima level to their Hardness and Soak while attuned.<br /> <br /> <b>Veil of Personal Magnetism</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m, 1a per level of Cover, optionally 1wp (+1wp) <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> One turn<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> Skybender, living up to its name, diffuses its Bearer\u2019s Anima into a gauzy haze that throws mirages and deflects attacks.<br /> This Evocation supplements a Take Cover action, allowing the Bearer to channel his Anima to bolster his Defense. The Bearer\u2019s Anima must, at a minimum, be at Glowing to use this ability. For every level of Anima committed, the Bearer may treat his Cover as one degree better, to a maximum of Full. At the start of the Bearer\u2019s next turn, his Anima fades to dim. Optionally, if no Cover is available, the Bearer may spend a point of temporary Willpower to summon viable Cover from his own Anima with this Evocation. This cover may move with him, and there are no additional limitations on available actions he can take while this power is active.<br /> At Essence 2 and above, the Bearer may expend an additional Willpower to extend the Cover granted or improved by this Evocation to a Battle Group of a Size no greater than his Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Lacuna of Crushing Eminence</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1a <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche, Uniform, Clash<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> indefinite<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Veil of Personal Magnetism<br /> <br /> In blocking his adversary\u2019s strikes, Skybender draws its bearer\u2019s quarry into his orbit with the strength of a collapsing star.<br /> The Bearer may clash a withering or decisive attack with such singular skill that it stokes the enemy\u2019s fear and respect. This clash attack does no damage, but, in addition to the penalty to Defense, allows the Bearer to make a reflexive Instill action (rolling Charisma + Melee), adding threshold successes from the Clash to the roll, and creating or improving an Intimacy of Awe toward the Bearer. This Intimacy lasts until a week passes with the Bearer not being within Essence miles of the Target or the Bearer is Crashed by the Target. The Bearer\u2019s Anima must be at Glowing before using this Charm, resets to Dim at the beginning of his next turn, and counts as the Bearer\u2019s attack action.<br /> <br /> <b>All Falls to Force</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m, 1wp <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Turn<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Lacuna of Crushing Eminence<br /> <br /> Marked as worthy opponents, the Bearer\u2019s foes are drawn to the hunt.<br /> When using Skybender to defend himself, the Bearer may use this Evocation to make those they cherish inapplicable targets. All incoming attacks must target him until his next turn. During this time, if his defense is penetrated, those whom he holds an Intimacy towards, or who hold an Intimacy toward him, cannot be attacked. His Anima must be at Burning to use this Evocation.<br /> <br /> <b>Magnanimous Adversary Ansible</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m, 1+a <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> All Falls to Force, Lacuna of Crushing Eminence<br /> <br /> Distance means little to those who are the center, and Skybender was born in the shadow of the center.<br /> While the Bearer's Anima is at least at Glowing, those that recognize his greatness, and are bathed in it, are always readily at hand. The Bearer may invoke this Evocation to instantaneously close the distance between himself and one that either bears an Intimacy toward him or that he bears an Intimacy toward, appearing at their side as if he had been there all along. The distance he may cross is proportional to his Anima level; at Glowing, he may cross Short distances, at Burning, Medium, at Iconic, Long. He may hold the activation of this Charm to Clash a Withering or Decisive Attack made against or by the subject of the Tie with Skybender. This counts as the Bearer's Attack Action, and causes his Anima to fade back to Dim.<br /> <br /> <b>Unassailable Whim-Driven Behemoth</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 3a <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> All Falls to Force, Lacuna of Crushing Eminence, Magnanimous Adversary Ansible<br /> <br /> At the heights of power, those who\u2019ve truly bonded with Skybender are like unto the great beasts of ages uncounted.<br /> When the Bearer\u2019s Anima becomes Iconic, Skybender\u2019s magic makes it extraordinarily difficult for Trivial enemies to engage him in combat, regardless of their numbers. He does not take onslaught penalties from any attack made by Trivial opponents or Battle Groups, although magically inflicted onslaught penalties still apply against him. Withering attacks made by such enemies cannot drop him below 1 Initiative unless they have a post-soak damage of 10 dice (although attackers can still gain the full amount of Initiative damage dealt). Decisive attacks made by such enemies cannot deal more than (3 + attacker\u2019s Strength) levels of damage to the Bearer with a single attack, not counting any levels of damage added by Charms or other magic. This Evocation ends prematurely if the Bearer is Crashed, causing their Anima to fade to Dim.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Feedback welcomed.</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea what to set the Artifact Rating at though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 06-16-2016, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T16:17:50-07:00","id":915909,"title":"","content":"I was hoping to get some assistance with a Grimscythe that I am putting together for a character. When I was talking with the other players about using a scythe, there were several jokes about it being like the one from RWBY. Thinking about the scenes of Ruby Rose slicing through hordes of Grimm, I got the image of a Solar carving their way through a horde of Fair Folk, and decided that this Grimscythe had been crafted to hunt down incursions from the Wyld.<br /> <br /> I would like to have 5 or 6 evocations in it, but I am not quite sure what to do for the other 2-3. I don't have a description, but there would be a hearthstone socket, probably on the base of the blade. For the design, I figured White Jade would be appropriate for the great force delivered in the capstone evocation. My Storyteller felt that Soulsteel would be an appropriate second material.<br /> <br /> The Kill Must Be Clean was actually suggested by my Storyteller for the weapon. I see it as the capstone of the evocation list, and would not have any objection to making an additional evocation or two a prereq. I wanted to have some sort of fast movement evocation, to emulate the way Ruby moves around in the show that inspired this, but wasn't quite sure what to do that's not just a copy of an existing charm. I would also like to have one or two more combat evocations, possibly designed around dealing with battle groups, like the packs that hobgoblins and silverwights typically form.<br /> <br /> I am looking forward to any suggestions you might have.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Erufukira, the Death of Fair Folk (Soulsteel/White Jade Grimscythe Artifact 3)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Evocations of Erufukira</span></span><br /> When a Solar, Abyssal, or Dragon-Blood is attuned to Erufukira, it guides their hand in all fights against its primary foes, giving 1 automatic attack success vs Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Hunter Is Never Prey</span></span><br /> Cost: -<br /> Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> Once the Exalted is attuned to Erufukira, the weapon makes sure that he is aware when forces from the Wyld are in the area. If there are Fair Folk or other beings purely of the Wyld within medium range of the wielder, he will automatically sense their presence. This does not give him a location or even a direction, it only lets him know they are present. He will also detect the presence of Wyld mutants, but only within short range.<br /> When the wielder becomes aware of their presence, he can try to locate/track them. He takes an action to make a Perception+Awareness check, applying any Awareness charms normally. For each 9 rolled, he gains a single mote of Essence, and for each 10 rolled, two motes, which can only be used to offset the costs of the Awareness charms used for this check.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Pack Is No Protection</span></span><br /> Cost: 4m, 1 wp<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> When the Fair Folk invade, they often come in large numbers. This is no protection against the wielder of Erufukira. When facing a battle group and making a decisive attack, the damage bonus is doubled, to 2 levels of automatic damage per 4 damage dice. If a charm is being used that lets him make multiple decisive attacks in a round, he pays the wp cost only for the first attack, paying only 4m for each additional attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Kill Must Be Clean</span></span><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: The Pack Is No Protection<br /> Every hunter knows that the prey should be taken out as quickly and cleanly as possible. When making a decisive attack against any creature of the Wyld, he may add the weapon's attack and damage bonus. If a charm is being used that lets him make multiple decisive attacks in a round, he pays the wp cost only for the first attack, paying only 6m for each additional attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11979,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11979-docsavagejm","user":"DocSavageJM","date":". 06-17-2016, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11979-docsavagejm","name":"DocSavageJM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T16:26:38-07:00","id":915914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915900#post915900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No idea what to set the Artifact Rating at though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd go with 4.<br /> <br /> Also, do something about Carnal Sustenance Repaste because it can realistically go up to 3-4 free Initiative/turn without needing to be particularly tricksy about when and how you employ it. It's frankly insane for a scenelong 2m commitment as written (but even if the intent was that you can't gain Initiative from the same person twice, I'd still bump it up to 4-6m at least). It probably shouldn't be an Essence 2 Charm either.<br /> <br /> ...Speaking of things that shouldn't be, I think Inevitable Morsel Obsession and Carnal Sustenance Repaste are both quite terrible names for the effects they supposedly describe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 06-16-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T16:55:05-07:00","id":915924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSavageJM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915909#post915909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Solar, Abyssal, or Dragon-Blood is attuned to Erufukira, it guides their hand in all fights against its primary foes, giving 1 automatic attack success vs Fair Folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glancing at Adorei, I'm fairly confident nothing will break if you make this a non-charm success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSavageJM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915909#post915909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mins: Essence 1, Awareness 2<br /> Mins: Essence 2, Melee or Martial Arts(White Reaper) 3<br /> Mins: Essence 2, Melee or Martial Arts(White Reaper) 5</div> </div> </div> </div>I... don't think it's customary for Evocations to have ability prerequisites.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSavageJM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915909#post915909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Pack Is No Protection</span></span><br /> Cost: 4m, 1 wp<br /> Mins: Essence 2, Melee or Martial Arts(White Reaper) 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> When the Fair Folk invade, they often come in large numbers. This is no protection against the wielder of Erufukira. When facing a battle group and making a decisive attack, the damage bonus is doubled, to 2 levels of automatic damage per 4 damage dice. If a charm is being used that lets him make multiple decisive attacks in a round, he pays the wp cost only for the first attack, paying only 4m for each additional attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how valuable Willpower is in Exalted 3E, and how costly it is to make decisives against battle groups (both in terms of initiative that could've been spent to damage something that can't be defeated just by throwing witherings at it and hoping something will stick, and in terms of the vulnerability that comes with having to hang around with base Initiative after the deed is done), I believe the fact that this Evocation only benefits decisives is enough of an opportunity cost in itself (I've genuinely never seen a PC make a decisive against a battle group, ever). I suggest dropping the WP cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSavageJM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915909#post915909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Kill Must Be Clean</span></span><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp<br /> Mins: Essence 2, Melee or Martial Arts(White Reaper) 5<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: The Pack Is No Protection<br /> Every hunter knows that the prey should be taken out as quickly and cleanly as possible. When making a decisive attack against any creature of the Wyld, he may add the weapon's attack and damage bonus. If a charm is being used that lets him make multiple decisive attacks in a round, he pays the wp cost only for the first attack, paying only 6m for each additional attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Grimscythes have a base damage rating of <b>14</b>. I'm not quite sure this is what you mean by &quot;the weapon's damage bonus&quot;, but if yes, it's a terrible, terrible idea. By comparison, Shining Starfall Execution costs 6 motes and only adds a maximum of 5 dice, and it comes with pretty strict restrictions on when and how you need to use it to get that much mileage out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 06-17-2016, 05:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T18:43:03-07:00","id":915957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915914#post915914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd go with 4.<br /> <br /> Also, do something about Carnal Sustenance Repaste because it can realistically go up to 3-4 free Initiative/turn without needing to be particularly tricksy about when and how you employ it. It's frankly insane for a scenelong 2m commitment as written (but even if the intent was that you can't gain Initiative from the same person twice, I'd still bump it up to 4-6m at least). It probably shouldn't be an Essence 2 Charm either.<br /> <br /> ...Speaking of things that shouldn't be, I think Inevitable Morsel Obsession and Carnal Sustenance Repaste are both quite terrible names for the effects they supposedly describe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Took your advice and replaced CSR with something more on-theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T05:43:02-07:00","id":916142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915651#post915651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a VERY cool artifact and an impressive first attempt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. It popped into my head while walking home from work. I'm generally a little verbose, so I'm not surprised it was a slog to get through, but I appreciate that you did and I only wish I could repay the favour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915651#post915651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Go through your evocations and unify your terms. &quot;Other person&quot; should be target, foe, victim or something along those lines. Other person is too vague, especially when listing multiple situations that can trigger it. Otherwise, a good starting evocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't use opponent originally, because I considered situations in which a PC uses social influence on the bearer of the mask. Mechanically they are, however temporarily, your opponent in the scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915651#post915651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how the cost of this evocation interacts with the text. Basically the only mechanics I see are a perfect defense, but your cost shows a variable cost. This needs clarification. Might I also recommend breaking up your paragraphs a bit. It's a bit dense to read through to separate the mechanics and the flavor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had made assumptions there. Assumptions fixed. Basically, it's more expensive to lie if your opponent aced their social roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915651#post915651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wording of this evocation is weird. I thought I understood it but you have a lot of different costs in the text but only 1 cost in the charm details at the top. In general, I'm cool with the idea of converting Maddening Insight into Initiative, but make sure the math is clear and concise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maths fixed. Even added the algebra version below, for clarity. Is a cost of 1 mote too cheap to switch as many of your own successes as you like into initiative? I feel like the loss of the actual action is probably enough cost in itself, but I'd appreciate some additional feedback now that the numbers are a bit clearer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915651#post915651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This will make more sense when its prerequisite is cleared up. What is the goal of these evocations? Is it for you the wearer to gain initiative? Or the target? The description goes back and forth between focuses it can be hard to follow. Very flavorful descriptions and concepts, but your logic needs to be clear to follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the initiative/success switching evocations, the goal is for you to be able to switch your successes to initiative in a pinch, and also for you to be able to do the same to your opponents. The idea intrigued me when I first thought up the Eyes of the Raksha, because changing out successes for initiative sounds like a terrible thing to do, or a fantastic thing to do, depending on the situation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915651#post915651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems solid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915651#post915651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So overall this artifact has some really cool stuff going for it, and I love the unique direction it's going. But it is had to follow some of the math logic in it, just based on the wording. Put some paragraphs in, read some of the mechanics sections outloud for clarity, and make sure the listed cost represents what the text says, and this will be a winner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent. If you could pass your discerning eye back over the edited evocations and pass down some additional judgement, I would greatly appreciate it. Maybe one day I'll be able to actual contribute to this thread, instead of just leeching <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":11875,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","user":"Rowanas","date":". 06-17-2016, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:20:39-07:00","id":916177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915899#post915899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool artifact. Love it thematically. However...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is a terrible deal. Think of it as effectively raising the artifact's attunement cost in any combat by (duration in turns). Unless you have really twinked-out PCs, most combats with important adversaries can be assumed to last at least 5 turns. I don't doubt that being able to raise your anima 1m cheaper <i>can</i> be a benefit, but it's definitely not a benefit worth paying a 5m attunement surcharge for.<br /> <br /> Since I think having an easy-to-raise anima is a double-edged sword in itself (with a 4m/level cost, you can only raise static values by 1 from peripheral before you start glowing!), I'd just ditch the last sentence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I may be missing something here, but I genuinely can't see how the ability to give a single person a maximum of 4 Initiative while raising their anima to bonfire once per scene is such a powerful ability that it has to cost 5 motes, a WP, and an action.<br /> <br /> I'd just flat-out have it affect everybody within 3 range bands of the wearer (and have it grant the Initiative bonus to mortals as well). Might be really powerful in a really specific situation (more than two characters are in range who a/ have Melee as their combat ability of choice, b/ have just used OWTB last turn,and c/ are within 3 range bands of the wearer, but also conveniently in position to attack somebody on their next turn), but I'm just not really seeing a situation like that emerge very often organically in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your added feedback. I do think I'll drop the respiration sentence. And I'll clear up the wording on Spreading the Eternal Light. I actually meant it to be AoE, not just single target, so my bad on that.<br /> <br /> no issue on either of the two other charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:12:34-07:00","id":916211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916142#post916142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had made assumptions there. Assumptions fixed. Basically, it's more expensive to lie if your opponent aced their social roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is better. While it is assumed, I'd throw in a clause saying you have to spend enough to cancel all of their threshold successes or something, just to make sure no one misreads it, but it's a lot better already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916142#post916142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maths fixed. Even added the algebra version below, for clarity. Is a cost of 1 mote too cheap to switch as many of your own successes as you like into initiative? I feel like the loss of the actual action is probably enough cost in itself, but I'd appreciate some additional feedback now that the numbers are a bit clearer.<br /> <br /> With the initiative/success switching evocations, the goal is for you to be able to switch your successes to initiative in a pinch, and also for you to be able to do the same to your opponents. The idea intrigued me when I first thought up the Eyes of the Raksha, because changing out successes for initiative sounds like a terrible thing to do, or a fantastic thing to do, depending on the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I get the personal exchange, it's clear (also I'd put it at maybe 2m or 3m base). And i get your desire for why you might want to change someone elses, I'm behind that entirely. But it's still not very clear how it maths out when targeting someone else. So it costs Base plus 1m per maddening insight you spend, and it's 1 maddening insight per 1 success turned into 1 initiative when targeting yourself. When it's targeting someone else, it's Base plus 1m per maddening insight you spend, and it's... this is where it breaks down for me. Maybe my math brain isn't working. It sounds like however many maddening insights you spend is how many successes you can convert (1:1), but they all only turn into 1 initiative. Combined. So why would someone ever spend more than one? Or are you saying they have to spend insight to convert all of their successes into a single combined initiative?<br /> <br /> I LIKE this effect, I really do. But I'm just not following the math when targeting someone other than yourself. Maybe it makes sense to everyone else and I'm just being fuzz-brained today, but you're right that it shouldn't need algebra to explain it. I don't want you to give up on this effect, but it needs very simple words to describe it. There's a few charms in the core book that are a failure because it's too hard to follow the math they want you to do to get the effect. Don't let this happen to you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:19:19-07:00","id":916218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916177#post916177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no issue on either of the two other charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>None as far as I can see.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T10:10:02-07:00","id":916293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916218#post916218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None as far as I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div> cool, consider Lights the Night up-to-date now<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T10:29:08-07:00","id":916309,"title":"","content":"Is it better now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T11:02:02-07:00","id":916328,"title":"","content":"<b>Spirit Razor (Orichalcum Dire Lance \u2013 Artifact ***)</b><br /> An exorcist\u2019s dream, Spirit Razor has existed since the High First Age, a tool for Solar Exalted to root out the intruders from the Underworld by understanding and banishing them. An orichalcum haft-and-blade with an azure tassel binding at the join, Spirit Razor is an elegant weapon, engraved with dozens of mudras and prayers to the Unconquered Sun and dedicated to the placation of ghosts. Though it is efficacious at doing so, this is not a weapon made simply to slay spirits. It is meant to be carried by one who truly wishes to understand and benefit them.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Spirit Razor</b><br /> A Solar Exalted who attunes to Spirit Razor finds his blade more efficaciously slices through ghosts. When using Spirit-Cutting Attack against a ghost, its cost is reduced to 0m.<br /> <br /> <b>Reading the Immaterial</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Withering-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Spirit Razor grants its wielder uncanny insight into the minds of spirits, the better to aid in placating them or, in the case of ghosts, laying them to rest. This Evocation may be activated after a successful <b>withering</b> attack with Spirit Razor against a spirit. Reading the Immaterial allows the wielder to make a reflexive Read Intentions action against that spirit, re-rolling 6s until 6s no longer appear. If successful, the wielder learns one of the spirit\u2019s Intimacies. Against a ghost, he also learns the nature of one of its Fetters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rending the Immaterial</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Reading the Immaterial<br /> <br /> Spirits belong in the spirit world, and their invasion into Creation can be seen as an affront. Still, Spirit Razor does not wish simply to drive them away, but to slay their concerns so they do not return. This Evocation supplements a <b>decisive</b> attack with Spirit Razor against a spirit. If successful, Rending the Immaterial can immediately reduce the strength of a known Intimacy or Fetter by one level. If this reduces the Intimacy or Fetter to non-existence, the spirit takes no damage from the attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Putting the Immaterial to Rest</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Ghost-Eating Technique, Rending the Immaterial<br /> <br /> Souls are a precious commodity, and should not be wasted simply by devouring them. When a Solar who knows this Evocation uses Ghost-Eating Technique to slay a ghost, he may choose to regain no Essence. If he so chooses, the ghost is sent to Lethe rather than devoured by the Solar, sending the spirit on to its properly ordained reincarnation. The catharsis of doing so allows the Solar to gain one temporary Willpower; this may put the Solar above his normal maximum, or even above ten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":". 06-17-2016, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T12:35:23-07:00","id":916365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916328#post916328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Spirit Razor (Orichalcum Dire Lance \u2013 Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Spirit Razor</b><br /> A Solar Exalted who attunes to Spirit Razor finds his blade more efficaciously slices through ghosts. When using Spirit-Cutting Attack against a ghost, its cost is reduced to 0m.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see an issue with this mechanic, but as a matter of pure <i>personal taste</i> I don't care for evocations that specifically interact with the mechanics of Exalted charms. Something about it doesn't sit right to me, but there's no rules against it. Hell, in the early development, it was a feature of Evocations. Anyways it's the foundation of this artifact, so it's fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916328#post916328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Reading the Immaterial</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Spirit Razor grants its wielder uncanny insight into the minds of spirits, the better to aid in placating them or, in the case of ghosts, laying them to rest. This Evocation may be activated after a successful <b>withering</b> attack with Spirit Razor against a spirit. Reading the Immaterial allows the wielder to make a reflexive Read Intentions action against that spirit, re-rolling 6s until 6s no longer appear. If successful, the wielder learns one of the spirit\u2019s Intimacies. Against a ghost, he also learns the nature of one of its Fetters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Needs Withering-only keyword, otherwise legit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916328#post916328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Rending the Immaterial</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Reading the Immaterial<br /> <br /> Spirits belong in the spirit world, and their invasion into Creation can be seen as an affront. Still, Spirit Razor does not wish simply to drive them away, but to slay their concerns so they do not return. This Evocation supplements a <b>decisive</b> attack with Spirit Razor against a spirit. If successful, Rending the Immaterial can immediately reduce the strength of a known Intimacy or Fetter by one level. If this reduces the Intimacy or Fetter to non-existence, the spirit takes no damage from the attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totes legit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916328#post916328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Putting the Immaterial to Rest</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Ghost-Eating Technique, Rending the Immaterial<br /> <br /> Souls are a precious commodity, and should not be wasted simply by devouring them. When a Solar who knows this Evocation uses Ghost-Eating Technique to slay a ghost, he may choose to regain no Essence. If he so chooses, the ghost is sent to Lethe rather than devoured by the Solar, sending the spirit on to its properly ordained reincarnation. The catharsis of doing so allows the Solar to gain one temporary Willpower; this may put the Solar above his normal maximum, or even above ten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Super legit. A logically ordered, simply designed artifact with evocations that build off of each other. I think this last one works very well as a Permanent evocation. My only complaint is my personal grudge against stopping evocation trees before Essence 3. It's mechanically sound and awesome. I'm not even sure what you'd DO with it at Essence 3.<br /> <br /> You are getting good at this, sir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T12:55:42-07:00","id":916381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916365#post916365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are getting good at this, sir.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;blushing and turning colors&gt; Why, thank you!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T16:37:14-07:00","id":916481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916309#post916309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it better now?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, even though I have my doubts about the appropriateness of the word &quot;ansible&quot; in Exalted. I guess it's <i>kinda</i> okay in the context of a giant pig that also happens to be a black hole?<br /> <br /> Also, considering that Godspeed Steps (the Solar Charm that allows for a rush across 3 range bands) costs 4m 1wp, I really recommend tying the maximum distance crossed with Magnanimous Adversary Ansible to Intimacy strength in addition to the anima levels (with one range band for a Minor Intimacy, two for Major and three for Defining). Requiring a spending of anima levels works well as a pacing mechanism, but doesn't have the same long-term bite as a Willpower cost. Thus, the effect needs to be narrower in scope than the comparable Charm - this is accomplished well enough by it only being usable on targets the wearer has a Defining Intimacy towards (or vice versa), and this restriction also fits the fluff well.<br /> <br /> As a personal taste thing, I'd also set the cost to a fixed anima level (I'd go with 3 because the 2m base cost already compares favorably to Godspeed Steps, no need to buff the Evocation even more) - both in the interest of avoiding unnecessary complexity and to make it easier to word the effect in a clear and concise manner. However, I don't think this is necessary for balance purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T17:53:19-07:00","id":916517,"title":"","content":"Another little experiment, this time with an artifact weapon type that didn't even make the core rules. Poor little shuriken. :-(<br /> <br /> Also a bit of a nod to folks who find Thrown Charms a little too subtle. Also, who doesn't like killer bees? Math might be a little fuzzy on this one.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Swarming Bees Moonstar</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">(Moonsilver and Orichalcum Shuriken, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> This artifact was the gift of a nameless Lunar for a Dawn who boasted mastery of countless weapons but seldom saw strategic value in small throwing weapons, including shuriken. The Lunar challenged herself to create an artifact shuriken capable of turning the tide of a battle. It is unclear whether the weapon lived up to her goal in the eyes of the Dawn for whom she forged it, but Swarming Bees Moonstars was discovered among the grave goods in a tomb of five Solars. It has since seen use among Exalted who work in teams of other Chosen, for its Evocations make it excellent for creating openings for the wielder\u2019s allies.<br /> <br /> To all appearances, this artifact is a single shuriken with a yellow-and-black stripe motif dividing it into six wedges. If attuned, however, each time the Exalt throws it, another, identical shuriken appears in her hand. There is no limit to the number of duplicates (called its bees) this artifact can produce. However, all the copies other than the one the wielder currently holds disappear at the end of the combat. This artifact never requires an ammunition check. Swarming Bees Moonstar has a single hearthstone slot at the center of the shuriken.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Evocations of Swarming Bees Moonstar</span><br /> <br /> A Solar or Lunar who spends an additional two motes to attune this artifact enjoys additional benefits when using its Evocations (described below).<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Angry Bee</span></b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Stackable, Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Three or [Essence] rounds (whichever is higher)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> The Chosen\u2019s shuriken hovers around its target on later turns, diving and swooping so that he remains off-balance. Activate when making a <b>withering</b> attack with Swarming Bees Moonstar. Whether or not the attack succeeds, the shuriken continues to menace the target for a number of rounds equal to the Exalted\u2019s Essence or three (whichever is higher). This is treated as an attack against the target solely for the purpose of imposing onslaught penalties against him, resolved on the wielder\u2019s turn. Multiple bees increase the onslaught penalty as though they were multiple attackers.<br /> <br /> The victim of this Evocation can end it prematurely by moving at least one range band away from the bee on his turn (but see Inescapable Swarm below).<br /> <br /> When attuned by a Solar or Lunar, this Evocation loses the Withering-only keyword and gains the Uniform keyword, instead, allowing the wielder to use it to enhance <b>decisive</b> attacks, as well.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Inescapable Swarm</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One round<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Angry Bee<br /> The Chosen\u2019s bees pursue their target wherever he might go. The Exalt can only use this Evocation against an opponent who is currently being harried by one of her bees using the prerequisite Evocation. She may direct one of the bees to make a <b>withering</b> or <b>decisive</b> attack against its victim as long as he remains within close range of the bee. This is considered a Thrown attack made by the Exalt with the shuriken and is always treated as being made at close range from the victim. If used to make a <b>decisive</b> attack it eliminates one of the bees plaguing the target, even if it had duration remaining.<br /> <br /> Additionally, if the victim attempts to move away from the bees, he must make a successful disengage attempt, which the bees resist using the Exalted\u2019s Dexterity + Thrown with automatic successes equal to her Essence.<br /> <br /> When the artifact is attuned by a Solar or Lunar, use of this Evocation extends the duration of one of the bees assailing its target by one additional round.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sting to Death</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Inescapable Swarm<br /> The Chosen directs her bees to sting their target to death. The Exalt may spread her total Initiative between a number of <b>decisive</b> attacks not exceeding the number of bees surrounding the target. Initiative must be spread as evenly as possible between the attacks. In addition, the damage roll enjoys double-10s. The wielder\u2019s Initiative does not reset until she has completed every attack. Each attack she enhances with this Evocation reduces the number of bees harrying the target by one.<br /> <br /> When the artifact is attuned by a Solar or Lunar, the wielder may throw another shuriken as part of the activation of this Evocation, increasing the maximum number of attacks by one. She must be able to attack the target with a thrown weapon to take advantage of this effect. He cannot be hidden behind a wall, for example, or beyond the range of her shuriken.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Swarm Ascending</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp or 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One round<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Angry Bee<br /> A single shuriken circling one opponent\u2019s head like a lone hornet shatters into a swarm of bees pursuing every nearby enemy. Choose a target currently affected by Angry Bee. The bees\u2019 onslaught penalty affects all the Chosen\u2019s enemies within short range of the initial target. As long as the primary target is assailed by at least one bee, this Evocation can be renewed on subsequent turns at a cost of three motes.<br /> <br /> When attuned by a Solar or Lunar, the wielder may instead spend eight motes and one Willpower to activate this Evocation. If she does so, the swarm of bees extends to medium range from the primary target.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Deadly Stinging Swarm</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sting to Death<br /> This Evocation upgrades Angry Bee, shrinking the flitting shuriken assailing their targets to the size of insects, allowing them to slip through armor easily. Anyone suffering an onslaught penalty caused by the wielder\u2019s harrying bees also suffers an environmental hazard that deals dice of lethal damage equal to the bees\u2019 onslaught penalty each round. Victims may resist this damage with a successful Stamina + Resistance roll against a difficulty equal to the Exalted\u2019s Essence.<br /> <br /> If attuned by a Solar or Lunar, increase the difficulty and damage dice of this Evocation by one each.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Swarm Descends</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Deadly Stinging Swarm, Swarm Ascends<br /> The wielder can use Inescapable Swarm and Sting to Death against anyone within the swarm. Additionally, activation of Inescapable Swarm against at least one enemy prevents all enemies from leaving the swarm without a disengage action, and Sting to Death counts all the bees within short range of its target when determining the maximum number of decisive attacks it can execute.<br /> <br /> When attuned by a Solar or Lunar, the bees created by the first Evocation of this artifact instead last until the end of the scene (or until used up by Inescapable Swarm or Sting to Death). However, the onslaught penalty any target suffers due to the bees cannot exceed the Chosen\u2019s Essence, regardless of the number of harrying him. Additionally, Sting to Death can attack targets within medium range of its target.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T20:07:22-07:00","id":916583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915924#post915924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I... don't think it's customary for Evocations to have ability prerequisites.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason that didn't register when I was looking at the examples, and I set the prereqs like charms. I have gone back and removed those.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915924#post915924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Grimscythes have a base damage rating of <b>14</b>. I'm not quite sure this is what you mean by &quot;the weapon's damage bonus&quot;, but if yes, it's a terrible, terrible idea. By comparison, Shining Starfall Execution costs 6 motes and only adds a maximum of 5 dice, and it comes with pretty strict restrictions on when and how you need to use it to get that much mileage out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the reasons I've posted this on here. I've gone between thinking it's a great ability and that it's an overpowered ability, so I needed some other people's thoughts. Looking over some of the charms in Single Point after you mentioned Shining Starfall gave me an idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Kill Must Be Clean</span></span><br /> Cost: 3m, 1 wp<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: <br /> <br /> Every hunter knows their prey should be taken as quickly and cleanly as possible. The wielder of Erufukira knows that sometimes, it is worth taking a disadvantageous position, if you can end the fight. When facing a foe with lower initiative, the wielder may add the difference in Initiative to the raw damage of his attack, which cannot exceed his own Initiative, and if facing a creature of the Wyld, may double up to (Dexterity) 9s in the attack roll. If the attack fails, his Initiative is set equal to his enemies before suffering the Initiative loss for an unsuccessful attack.If the attack was against a creature of the Wyld, his initiative will instead decrease by 5 or the difference in Initiative, whichever is lower.<br /> <br /> I know it is just a slight variation of Fatal Stroke Flash, but it fits with what the original version was doing, providing a way to potentially take down a powerful Fair Folk adversary quickly. Normally, with Mastery on the original, you would automatically get (Essence) 9s doubled, here you are paying a slight extra cost to get the double 9s and the reduced penalty, against creatures of the Wyld only. Do you think the extra cost is fine where it is, or does it need to be a little higher? I'm not sure how strong the double 9s is considered, and with the reduced penalty, even if you are going after someone with a much lower initiative, you are still potentially losing 7 or 8 initiative, compared to the 2 or 3 you would lose on a normal decisive. I know there should be prerequisite Evocations, but since I haven't figured out what the other Evocations in the weapon will be yet, that will be filled in later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11979-docsavagejm","name":"DocSavageJM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T02:34:42-07:00","id":916744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSavageJM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916583#post916583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Kill Must Be Clean</span></span><br /> Cost: 3m, 1 wp<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites:<br /> <br /> Every hunter knows their prey should be taken as quickly and cleanly as possible. The wielder of Erufukira knows that sometimes, it is worth taking a disadvantageous position, if you can end the fight. When facing a foe with lower initiative, the wielder may add the difference in Initiative to the raw damage of his attack, which cannot exceed his own Initiative, and if facing a creature of the Wyld, may double up to (Dexterity) 9s in the attack roll. If the attack fails, his Initiative is set equal to his enemies before suffering the Initiative loss for an unsuccessful attack.If the attack was against a creature of the Wyld, his initiative will instead decrease by 5 or the difference in Initiative, whichever is lower.<br /> <br /> I know it is just a slight variation of Fatal Stroke Flash, but it fits with what the original version was doing, providing a way to potentially take down a powerful Fair Folk adversary quickly. Normally, with Mastery on the original, you would automatically get (Essence) 9s doubled, here you are paying a slight extra cost to get the double 9s and the reduced penalty, against creatures of the Wyld only. Do you think the extra cost is fine where it is, or does it need to be a little higher? I'm not sure how strong the double 9s is considered, and with the reduced penalty, even if you are going after someone with a much lower initiative, you are still potentially losing 7 or 8 initiative, compared to the 2 or 3 you would lose on a normal decisive. I know there should be prerequisite Evocations, but since I haven't figured out what the other Evocations in the weapon will be yet, that will be filled in later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it looks fine, <s>albeit I'd double up to (Strength), not (Dexterity) 9s for increased White Reaper synergy</s> nevermind, there's a Charm for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":"06-18-2016, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T21:57:33-07:00","id":917794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSavageJM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=915909#post915909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping to get some assistance with a Grimscythe that I am putting together for a character. When I was talking with the other players about using a scythe, there were several jokes about it being like the one from RWBY. Thinking about the scenes of Ruby Rose slicing through hordes of Grimm, I got the image of a Solar carving their way through a horde of Fair Folk, and decided that this Grimscythe had been crafted to hunt down incursions from the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Below is the revised version of Erufukira, based on input from Aluminiumtrioxid and additional ideas I have had. I still need help in figuring out what to do for the movement evocation(I Live For The Chase). Any input or suggestions on that or the existing evocations are welcome, and I would especially like to thank Aluminiumtrioxid for the help he has already provided.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Erufukira, the Death of Fair Folk (Soulsteel/White Jade Grimscythe Artifact 3)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Evocations of Erufukira</span></span></span><br /> When a Solar, Abyssal, or Dragon-Blood is attuned to Erufukira, it guides their hand in all fights against its primary foes, giving 1 automatic non-charm attack success vs Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Hunter Is Never Prey</span></span></span><br /> Cost: -<br /> Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> Once the Exalted is attuned to Erufukira, the weapon makes sure that he is aware when forces from the Wyld are in the area. If there are Fair Folk or other beings purely of the Wyld within medium range of the wielder, he will automatically sense their presence. This does not give him a location or even a direction, it only lets him know they are present. He will also detect the presence of Wyld mutants, but only within short range.<br /> When the wielder becomes aware of their presence, he can try to locate/track them. He takes an action to make a Perception+Awareness check, applying any Awareness charms normally. For each 9 rolled, he gains a single mote of Essence, and for each 10 rolled, two motes, which can only be used to offset the costs of the Awareness charms used for this check.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Pack Is No Protection</span></span></span><br /> Cost: 4m<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: The Hunter Is Never Prey<br /> When the Fair Folk invade, they often come in large numbers. This is no protection against the wielder of Erufukira. When facing a battle group and making a decisive attack, the damage bonus is doubled, to 2 levels of automatic damage per 4 damage dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I Live For The Chase</span></span></span><br /> Cost:<br /> Mins:<br /> Type:<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration:<br /> Prerequisites: The Hunter Is Never Prey<br /> Undetermined movement evocation<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Kill Must Be Clean</span></span></span><br /> Cost: 3m, 1wp<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: I Live For The Chase, The Pack Is No Protection<br /> <br /> Every hunter knows their prey should be taken as quickly and cleanly as possible. The wielder of Erufukira knows that sometimes, it is worth taking a disadvantageous position, if you can end the fight. When facing a foe with lower Initiative, the wielder may add the difference in Initiative to the raw damage of his attack(this bonus cannot exceed his own Initiative), and if facing a creature of the Wyld, may double up to (Dexterity) 9s in the attack roll. If the attack fails, his Initiative is set equal to his enemies before suffering the Initiative loss for an unsuccessful attack. If the attack was against a creature of the Wyld, his Initiative will instead decrease by 5 or the difference in Initiative, whichever is lower, before suffering the Initiative loss.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I Know All Their Tricks</span></span><br /> Cost: -(5m, 1wp)<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: I Live For The Chase, The Pack Is No Protection<br /> Erufukira protects its wielder from the hazards of Wyld energies, drawing upon his connections with Creation to stabilize his body and mind. When exposed to Wyld energies in the environment, he may pay 5m, 1wp to immunize his mind, body, and equipment to the effects for as long as the motes remain committed. In addition, when targeted by a shaping or mentally influencing attack by a creature of the Wyld, he may pay the same cost to raise his defense against that attack by the level of his Intimacy with something physical in Creation. This could be a person he loves, a treasure he covets, or a city he has sworn to defend. It may not be an abstract, such as a love of justice, or the desire to end slavery. Finally, if targeted by an effect from a creature of the Wyld that can only be defended against by spending Willpower, such as a lorelei's Beguiling Idyll, he may lower the Willpower cost by 1, to a minimum of 1. This reduction does stack with other sources of reduction, and in combination, could lower the cost to 0. In the above example of the lorelei, if he had this evocation, was touching iron, and was warned of the danger by another character, he would pay 0wp to negate the effect.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">My Life For Creation</span></span><br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp, 3+lhl<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: The Kill Must Be Clean, I Know All Their Tricks<br /> <br /> During the Fair Folk invasion at the time of the Great Contagion, a Dragon-Blooded wielding Erufukira was defending the city of Chiaroscuro. He knew that they could not hold out against the massive forces attacking, but was determined to give the people of the city as much time as he could. He gave his life to empower the Grimscythe, and when the attack was done, nearly a third of the attacking force was dead or fleeing. This kept the remaining inhabitants safe until the Empress unleashed the Realm Defense Grid.<br /> When this evocation is activated, the wielder must pay a minimum of one third of his remaining health levels or 3 health levels, whichever is greater, although he may pay more. If he has less than 3 health levels remaining, he automatically spends what health levels he has. My Life For Creation allows the wielder to make up to (Stamina) decisive attacks, against either individuals or battle groups within Medium range. No target may be hit more than once. A single attack roll is applied to all targets, although damage is rolled separately. Each attack has a base damage of the wielder's Strength, and Initiative is divided evenly among them. In addition, each attack gains a bonus to the damage equal to the number of health levels paid for the evocation. He does not reset to base Initiative until all the attacks have been resolved, and may make these attacks even if the health levels spent would take him to Incapacitated, collapsing after the attacks are finished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11979,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11979-docsavagejm","user":"DocSavageJM","date":".  Updated the evocation I Know All Their Tricks 06-21-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11979-docsavagejm","name":"DocSavageJM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T03:50:46-07:00","id":917922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSavageJM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=917794#post917794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I Know All Their Tricks</span></span><br /> Cost:<br /> Mins:<br /> Type:<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration:<br /> Prerequisites: I Live For The Chase, The Pack Is No Protection<br /> A protective evocation. Not quite sure how to word or cost this. I am looking to give a bonus to Resolve against Fair Folk effects such as Insidious Terror Mien or Untouchable Performer Technique, as well as a bonus against effects that would mutate the wielder, either from being in the Wyld directly or directed attacks. The defense would be based on an Intimacy the wielder has with something physical in Creation, such as a loved one, a hated enemy, or a place you are tied to. It can not use an abstract Intimacy, such as a hatred of slavery or a love of justice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have the book on hand, but you could look at similar Integrity charms (of which there are a few) and see if that helps guide you to a price. Also has ideas on how to word the thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T09:34:34-07:00","id":918076,"title":"","content":"<b>Shield of Melthar-Khun (Orichalcum Shield - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> Currently hanging in the trophy room of Satrap Ledaal Gao, the Shield of Melthar-Khun was forged by and for its namesake, a shining Solar Exalted of the Dawn Caste in the high First Age. When one of his circlemates fell in battle against a rampaging behemoth, Melthar-Khun swore he would never again allow such a thing to occur. In preparation for his circlemate\u2019s reincarnation, he undertook a training regime of strict defense, becoming one of the finest vanguards in the Solar host. Thanks largely to this shield, Melthar-Khun and his young, reincarnated circlemate were among the last to fall during the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> The shield itself is a concave hemi-cylinder, emblazoned with a turtle-shell pattern and lacquered with a pair of twin lightning bolts. It seems almost to leap to the defense of others, which has occasionally proven detrimental to the wielder\u2019s personal safety.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Shield of Melthar-Khun</b><br /> A Solar Exalt who attunes to the shield and takes a Defend Other action subtracts one additional Initiative from any attacker who beats his defense and chooses to strike his defended charge. The Solar steals this additional Initiative.<br /> <br /> <b>Under My Protection</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Those who would strike the defended see their blades turned aside by the edge of the shield, for it will not tolerate their temerity. This Evocation can be activated when the wielder has taken a Defend Other action, his Defense has been overcome by an attacker, and the attacker chooses to strike the defended charge. Each 1 on the attacker\u2019s roll to strike the charge subtracts a success from the attacker\u2019s final roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Iron Body Stance</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Under My Protection<br /> <br /> Let it not be said that the Shield of Melthar-Khun does not protect its wielder as well. Whenever a Solar who knows this Evocation and is wielding the Shield of Melthar-Khun takes a Defend Other action, his Soak is increased by 2 and his Hardness is increased by 1 for the duration of the Defend Other action. This soak and Hardness explicitly stack with all other sources.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Guardian\u2019s Retributive Strike</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Counterattack, Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Iron Body Stance<br /> <br /> Woe to those who would strike the charge of the wielder of the Shield of Melthar-Khun. The wielder may use this Evocation in response to any attack while he is using a Defend Other action that beats his defense and chooses to strike at his protected charge, creating a Melee counterattack with the Shield of Melthar-Khun that occurs after the opponent\u2019s attack result but before the damage has been rolled. This attack functions as a regular <b>decisive</b> attack. Guardian\u2019s Retributive Strike does not count as the wielder\u2019s combat action and cannot be used in response to another counterattack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":". 06-20-2016, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T11:34:12-07:00","id":918153,"title":"","content":"And its companion piece - <br /> <br /> <b>Mushi Armor \u2013 Orichalcum and White Jade Articulated Plate (Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> Forged during the Shogunate for a sworn brotherhood, five identical suits of this armor were initially created, though only three are known to exist in the Time of Tumult. Each is a suit of immaculately crafted articulated plate, white jade decorated in orichalcum trim. One suit stands in the hallways of the Imperial Manse, one in the storehouses of Lookshy, and one is wielded by a newly-Exalted Anathema in the threshold. <br /> <br /> The armor is designed to protect the wearer even as he or she protects her sworn brothers. It tightens the bonds of friendship until they are themselves armor against even the most grievous attacks. A full brotherhood of Dragon-Blooded, each contained within a suit of this armor, would be a potent force indeed. <br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Mushi Armor</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blooded who attunes to this armor gains 1 point of Initiative when taking a Defend Other action. This benefit cannot occur more than once per turn. <br /> <br /> <b>The Ties that Bind</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The first power of the armor is to bind its wearer to his charge, ensuring that a firm bond is forged between brothers. This Evocation may be activated whenever the wearer is attacked while taking a Defend Other action while wearing this armor. He automatically gains a Minor Tie of brotherhood toward his charge. If he already has a Tie of brotherhood, that Tie is instead strengthened by one level. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Brother\u2019s Bond</b><br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Withering-only<br /> Duration: One turn<br /> Prerequisites: The Ties that Bind<br /> <br /> The stronger the wearer\u2019s love for his brother, the stronger the armor becomes. This Evocation may be activated whenever the wearer is attacked while taking a Defend Other action while wearing this armor. His <b>withering</b> soak increases by an amount determined by the strength of his Tie toward the defended character: +2 soak for a Minor Tie, +3 soak for a Major Tie, or +4 soak for a Defining Tie. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Self-as-Selflessness Stance</b><br /> Cost: 1m/Initiative; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: The Brother\u2019s Bond<br /> <br /> \u201cThose who would strike my brother would strike me.\u201d This is the mudra of the Mushi Armor. This Evocation may be activated whenever the wearer is attacked while taking a Defend Other action while wearing this armor. He may steal from the attacker a number of points of Initiative equal to his Tie towards the defended character: 1 Initiative for a Minor Tie, 2 for a Major, and 3 for a Defining Tie. This Initiative is stolen immediately before the attack is resolved, which can affect the outcome of a <b>decisive</b> attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T13:01:35-07:00","id":918207,"title":"","content":"So here is my first complete attempt at creating an artifact with evocations in EX3. Not sure how balanced it is so I'd appreciate some feedback and suggestions to improve/fix it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Charm of the Weasel</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Origin</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Many years ago a lunar craftsman became enamored with the humble weasel and the way this unique and fascinating predator worked. From his fascination came the charm of the weasel a trinket inspired by the weasel and a gift for the lunar craftsman's night caste lover. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Appearance</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This artifact takes the form of a moonsilver armband shaped as a coiled weasel wrapping around the wearers arm. The artifact has a single hearthstone socket between the front claws of the weasel making it appear as if the the artifact is holding onto the hearthstone. Additionally the artifacts eyes change color to mimic any hearthstone that is inserted into it. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attunement </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with most hunters the weasel can see its prey long before the prey see them any exalt attuned to the charm of the weasel gain +1 on all visual awareness checks and have no difficulty seeing in anything other than pure darkness. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Evocations</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bones of Rubber</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Allows the exalt to squeeze through any opening that they can get their head through</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The weasel is a predator that\u2019s path cannot easily be barred. This evocation allows the exalt to channel the ability of the weasel to fit through any opening which they can get their head through. One this evocation is active should the exalt be able to move her head through an opening her body flows and adjusts to make it through the space as well. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prey of the Weasel</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 6m</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Bones of Rubber</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Once the Exalt locates her quarry she chases it until it is hers</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The weasel is a predator that shuns the tactic of stalk and ambush in favor of flush and chase. The exalt may reflexively activate this evocation to mark her prey, be it a person, animal, or item. Once the prey has been mark the exalt will chase it down till it\u2019s hers. The exalt gets +1 to all stamina and perception rolls to locate/acquire her quarry.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special rules: The exalt must see, hear, or smell her prey to activate this evocation and the sense used will determine the difficulty of tracking. Also the exalt must continue tracking until she finds her prey, if she loses the trail or gives up the evocation ends and the prey is no longer marked.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Changing one\u2019s Coat</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m, 1wp</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Indefinite</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Prey of the Weasel</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Allows the Exalt to change her outward appearance to blend in with her surroundings </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Just as the weasel changes its coat from brown to white so can the exalted. An exalt using this evocation can change their outward appearance to blend in with the scenery. This evocation allows the exalt to change the color, texture, and feel of their clothing. Additionally the exalt can affect their skin and hair as well changing them to blend with their surroundings. Once the commitment to this evocations lapses the exalts appearance returns to normal </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special rules: Should the charm of the weasel have the chameleon stone socketed into it the following additional effects are available. The evocation allows access to the hearthstones innate ability and expands upon it. The exalt may now change not only their hair, eye, and skin color but also their clothing and equipment to blend into any situation.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9195-shadowmage","user":"ShadowMage","date":". 06-21-2016, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9195-shadowmage","name":"ShadowMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9195_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T08:28:25-07:00","id":918635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=917922#post917922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have the book on hand, but you could look at similar Integrity charms (of which there are a few) and see if that helps guide you to a price. Also has ideas on how to word the thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have updated the post and would appreciate any feedback that you or anyone else would care to give.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11979-docsavagejm","name":"DocSavageJM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T12:10:49-07:00","id":918732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=912004#post912004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=886128#post886128\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...128#post886128</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894528#post894528\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894528#post894528\"> [3E] The Artifact and Evocation Workshop - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894528#post894528\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=894528#post894528 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I've been thinking recently that there are more topics popping up around Artifacts and their associated Evocations. These are great for individual critique, but having each one be its own individual topic means that after the feedback it falls off the front page. That's too bad, because a lot of these ideas are pretty awesome and could be really useful to others for use in their own games. So in the interest of 1) cutting down on the topic-clutter, and 2) consolidating everybody's neat ideas in one place, I thought it might be nice to have a single topic where folks can post their Artifacts and </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907881#post907881\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...881#post907881</a> (never version)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=897187#post897187\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...187#post897187</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just like to note, in case anyone had seen the previous &quot;newer version&quot;, that I've edited the Omens after some extremely welcome feedback. Rather than post them <b><i>again</i></b>, I just figured I'd note it here.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I'm thinking of putting together an index of all these artifacts that could maybe be put into the front page somewhere. So many to search through...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T15:21:16-07:00","id":918834,"title":"","content":"It's a very good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T19:19:11-07:00","id":918910,"title":"","content":"Alright, so!<br /> <br /> A friend of mine asked me to help put together a Reaper Daiklave, Orichalcum + Starmetal (+ Black Jade?), to be used with her Single Point Shining Into the Void style. <b>Concept:</b> Singing sword.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I've started on so far is the attunement evocation and one of the actual evocations (maybe first, maybe later). As always, I'd really appreciate any advice and suggestions with where to go.<br /> <br /> First up: Attunement!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Evocations of [Unnamed]</u></b><br /> A Solar or Sidereal attuned to [Unnamed] unleashes the singing spirit of the blade, whose ethereal voice sings to the mind and soul of its wielder with enchanting power. As the Exalt earns an advantage, the spirit\u2019s voice shifts within her. The following are the weapon\u2019s <b>Aria</b> levels.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Sotto Voce </b>(0 or fewer Initiative): +1 non-Charm bonus to Parry.<br /> \u2022 <b>Agitato </b>(1-4 Initiative): +1 non-Charm success to rush actions.<br /> \u2022 <b>Subito </b>(5-9 Initiative): The character may aim reflexively for a <b>withering</b> attack.<br /> \u2022 <b>Bravura </b>(10-14 Initiative): +3 bonus to Parry.<br /> \u2022 <b>Trionfante </b>(15+ Initiative): The character\u2019s aim actions also convey the benefits (but not costs) of a full defense action.<br /> <br /> The <b>Aria </b>levels are given quantities 1 (Sotto Voce) through 5 (Trionfante) for the purposes of evocation calculation.<br /> <br /> <br /> As is pretty clear, the inspiration was drawn directly from <b>Moonlit Huntress</b> (pp. 617-18) and, for the last bit, <b>Shining Ice Mirror</b> (pp. 618-19). For reference in power comparisons:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u><b>Evocations of Moonlit Huntress</b></u><br /> A Solar or Lunar attuned to Moonlit Huntress gains a blessing from the weapon, which fluidly shifts depending on her standing in the ebb and flow of battle:<br /> \u2022 No Moon (0 or fewer Initiative): +1 non-Charm success to Stealth rolls.<br /> \u2022 Waning Moon (1-4 Initiative): +1 non-Charm success to disengage actions.<br /> \u2022 Half Moon (5-9 Initiative): +2 non-Charm successes to Awareness rolls.<br /> \u2022 Waxing Moon (10-14 Initiative): +3 automatic successes to rush and disengage actions.<br /> \u2022 Full Moon (15+ Initiative): The character may aim reflexively from up to long range for a <b>decisive</b> attack. Doing so grants no aiming bonus.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><u>Evocations of Shining Ice Mirror</u></b><br /> A Solar who pays two extra motes to attune to Shining Ice Mirror may partake of its perfect balance and discerning spirit so that an aim action taken with the intent to strike with the blade also conveys the benefits (but not costs) of a full defense action.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The latter (Shining Ice Mirror) is thematically perfect for the martial arts style, and potent enough to warrant an additional +2 attunement cost. However, in synthesizing this and Moonlit Huntress' tiered-attunement system for the singing concept, I figured that by putting it last (and requiring the most Initiative) would perhaps balance it out (at least compared to reflexively-aimed long range shots).<br /> <br /> Honestly, though, I could use suggestions regarding <b><i>all</i></b> of the bonuses. I tried to convert them as equally as possible (1 auto-success = 1 static boost = 2 dice), but even then I'm not quite sure if they work thematically. What might work better than rush? Should I grant ability roll bonuses instead? Etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next up, though, here's the first actual evocation I've developed for it. As you'll see, I'm going for a bardic type of plan, with some of the evocations being maintained songs or connections.<br /> <br /> <b>Haunting Refrain</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m per turn; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> The wielder ushers forth the spirit\u2019s voice from the blade, establishing a mystic link to her target so he hears the blade\u2019s unsettling song. The wielder rolls [Essence + Aria] against her target\u2019s Resolve. If successful, the target hears the refrain at full volume, losing Initiative equal to half the weapon\u2019s momentary Aria (rounded up) at the beginning of his turn, for as many turns as she maintains the link. If the roll fails, the target only hears the murmuring voice at the back of his mind; the roll repeats every turn the evocation is maintained until successful.<br /> <br /> This evocation can target multiple foes, with the cost per turn increasing by 2 motes for every additional target.<br /> <br /> This evocation can target battlegroups, with the cost multiplied by Size (minimum 3m).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Immediate concerns: Cost?! Initiative loss amount?! Understandable concept?!?! And so on.<br /> <br /> Hella PEACH, yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":11797,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","user":"Seeker","date":". 06-22-2016, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T04:34:01-07:00","id":919027,"title":"","content":"As I currently play a charecter using SPSIVS I'm a fan of your concept. However, there is an inconsistency in the cost of targeting additional opponents using the evocation you've written up - the cost section seems to price additional targets at 3m, while the description text places the cost at 2m.. As for a name, how about &quot;Perfected Voice of Nothing&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","user":"7 questions vanquish god","date":". 06-22-2016, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11843-7-questions-vanquish-god","name":"7 questions vanquish god","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11843_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T05:53:09-07:00","id":919053,"title":"","content":"+3 parry! I don't know if that's reasonable - i'm not great at giving out mechanics advice, but that seems... waaaay out of whack with the same initiative-scaling item you quoted in your inspiration, as well as being a huge increase on the normal defence scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T08:01:55-07:00","id":919089,"title":"","content":"So I need some help guys. With your feedback and guidance, I've been able to put together a number of great 3-dot artifact.<br /> In the game I'm running, I have a resistance-supernal dawn, who favors two-handed cudgels and warhammers. He doesn't have any artifacts, at the moment, and, talking to his player, would be delighted to acquire a grand goremaul that provided some additional defensive effects somewhere down the line.<br /> <br /> So forumites, your mission, should you choose to accept it, is to design a <u>4-dot Grand Goremaul</u> that will make Bolsh, a veritable the colossus of the north, even closer to unassailable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T08:13:34-07:00","id":919095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919089#post919089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I need some help guys. With your feedback and guidance, I've been able to put together a number of great 3-dot artifact.<br /> In the game I'm running, I have a resistance-supernal dawn, who favors two-handed cudgels and warhammers. He doesn't have any artifacts, at the moment, and, talking to his player, would be delighted to acquire a grand goremaul that provided some additional defensive effects somewhere down the line.<br /> <br /> So forumites, your mission, should you choose to accept it, is to design a <u>4-dot Grand Goremaul</u> that will make Bolsh, a veritable the colossus of the north, even closer to unassailable.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you want a weapon that creates defensive effects, eh? Does this character tend to take purely defensive actions like Defend Other or Full Defense? Or do they tend to make attacks and just sort of be a Juggernaut?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T08:40:42-07:00","id":919112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919095#post919095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you want a weapon that creates defensive effects, eh? Does this character tend to take purely defensive actions like Defend Other or Full Defense? Or do they tend to make attacks and just sort of be a Juggernaut?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mixture of both, the series of fights they've already survived have required both approaches from him. He's growing in the defend-other tree of melee.<br /> <br /> Bolsh works on a slow-and-steady mindset. He's an endurance hunter, pursuig his prey down just fast enough that they drive themselves into exhaustion, at which point he calmly and mercifully snaps its neck in one swift move (hands the size of shovels, he has). If there's no neck to snap, a blow with his sledge is enough to kill most animals, though this is messier and attracts all types of scavengers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T09:05:47-07:00","id":919122,"title":"","content":"Noticed a lack of Sailing artifacts so I thought I would try one out.<br /> <br /> <b>Skidbladnir, Scepter of the Dreadnought-Blessed (Artifact </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <b>Green Jade Goremaul)</b><br /> <br /> Legends of mighty warships are ample in the great oceans of Creation, what many fail to realize is that many of these legends refer to the work of the same weapon. This ancient Goremaul was created for an ancient admiral from a time before Shogunate who wished to grant the vessel that had served him faithfully in his mortal life the power to rival the finest warship from amongst his glorious navy. Since that time this Scepter has passed through the hands of hundreds of wielders who used it to elevate many mortal vessels to glory, from massive capital ships to impossibly nimble coursers. Most recently Skidbladnir has come into the possession of a successful Outcaste reaver based near Wavecrest who has recently begun to prey of Guild shipping.<br /> <br /> Skidbladnir appears as a Goremaul of considerable ornamentation engraved in with ornate silver inscriptions retelling the epics of its past masters. The majority of the weapon is an alloy of darkened Green Jade with a shaft wrapped in the tanned hide of a long since extinct species of God-Blooded shark.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Skidbladnir</b><br /> <br /> <b>Attunement:</b> Attunement to Skidbladnir is only possible if the wielder already owns a vessel (granted this claim need only be enforceable and not necessarily legal). Attunement automatically unlocks Majestic Warship Ascension.<br /> <br /> <b>Majestic Warship Ascension</b><br /> Cost: - Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The Captain raises her weapon into the air and conjoins its soul with that of her ship, the vessel groans as planks broaden, twist and fuse into a single being of living wood. The vessel\u2019s appearance transforms into a masterwork the likes of which has not been seen since the death of the First Age, details of the ship\u2019s form are left to the Storyteller but ultimately fit the soul of its master.<br /> <br /> This Evocation grants the following benefits to the vessel until it is destroyed or the master dies, at which point it would fall apart, dying with its owner. Firstly the vessel now regenerates lost Hull Points at a rate of (Essence) Levels per month. Secondly the vessel no longer requires a helmsman with the master controlling it reflexively via the Scepter as long as they remain within (Ex10) miles of the vessel. Lastly the vessel gains (E) permanent points to the highest attribute of the ship between Hull Points, Maneuverability and Speed and +1 to the remaining traits. Only one vessel may be blessed with Majestic Warship Ascension at a given time and the wielder gains a Major Tie of affection for the ship.<br /> <br /> <b>Plank-Feast Assimilation</b><br /> Cost: 6m/Hull Point Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Majestic Warship Ascension<br /> <br /> To mar the glory of the Blessed-Vessel is a madman\u2019s endeavor for it will devour the vessels so foolish as to stand against it. This charm may be activated after successfully incapacitating an enemy ship, regaining a Hull Points at a rate of 6m for each level restored. This charm cannot regenerate more levels than the incapacitated ship had to begin with nor may it regenerate more levels than the Master\u2019s Essence rating at any given time. The Incapacitated vessels are destroyed as they are ripped apart by the power of Blessed.<br /> <br /> <b>Faultless Hull Invigoration</b><br /> Cost: 8m, 1wp Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Plank-Feast Assimilation<br /> <br /> The power of the Scepter commands the mighty ship to stand steadfast against those who would fell it. For the duration of the scene the Blessed-Vessel gains (Essence) hull point levels which explicitly allow the vessel to exceed its base number of hull points. The hull points gained in this fashion cannot be damaged by conventional anti-ship weapons or ramming actions (this protection does not extend to vessels composed of First Age alloys or broadsides employing Sorcery or First Age weaponry).<br /> <br /> <b>Masterful Flagship Transmutation</b><br /> Cost: 16m, 2wp Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Day<br /> Prerequisites: Faultless Hull Invigoration<br /> <br /> Embracing its fullest potential the Blessed-Vessel undergoes a glorious transformation to achieve its truest potential. For the duration of a single day the Blessed-Vessel enjoys a bonus to its Maneuverability and Speed equal to its Master\u2019s essence rating. Furthermore the costs of Faultless Hull Invigoration and Plank-Feast Assimilation enjoy a 2m discount for as long as this charm is active.<br /> This charm may only be reset by Calibration as the strain of its transformation would destroy the vessel if used more than single time in a year.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> Upon learning this charm the Master may choose to pay 8xp to gift true life to her beloved ship. The vessel becomes a 3-Dot Familiar which is only capable of Sail-based actions (for the purposes of which it possesses a Sail rating of 4, Intelligence 3 and a Wits 4) with a Defining Tie of loyalty towards its master. Although it may evolve over time the vessel will initially only possess an intellect akin to a very loyal pet and only understand simple commands and instructions unless controlled via the Scepter.<br /> A final benefit of this charm is that the familiar may choose to forcibly activate Masterful Flagship Transmutation for a second time within a year to protect its master but this course of action will result in its destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 06-22-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T09:18:57-07:00","id":919128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu;n919122[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skidbladnir, Scepter of the Dreadnought-Blessed (Artifact [/B]\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <b>Green Jade Goremaul)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Wow!!!<br /> <br /> OK, I regret that I have little to no working knowledge of the Sail system to judge that side of the mechanics. But at a glance it seems well thought-out.<br /> <br /> I have to say I'm VERY impressed conceptually. Not only is it a clever evocation set idea, but it's using GREEN Jade for Sail powers. I don't think anyone saw that coming. And you keep to the Green powers fairly well too! If anyone has Sail knowledge they can be more nit-picky than me, but I think this is magnificent and extremely creative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T09:24:31-07:00","id":919132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919128#post919128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow!!!<br /> <br /> OK, I regret that I have little to no working knowledge of the Sail system to judge that side of the mechanics. But at a glance it seems well thought-out.<br /> <br /> I have to say I'm VERY impressed conceptually. Not only is it a clever evocation set idea, but it's using GREEN Jade for Sail powers. I don't think anyone saw that coming. And you keep to the Green powers fairly well too! If anyone has Sail knowledge they can be more nit-picky than me, but I think this is magnificent and extremely creative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya I figured that it would either look really cool or really silly, glad that it worked out as well as it did. I am still very nervous on the mechanical end since my Sailing knowledge is rather limited but I thought that it needed more artifacts addressing it.<br /> Amusingly enough my thought process was basically 'Hammer+Wood=Ship!'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T10:43:33-07:00","id":919190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919112#post919112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A mixture of both, the series of fights they've already survived have required both approaches from him. He's growing in the defend-other tree of melee.<br /> <br /> Bolsh works on a slow-and-steady mindset. He's an endurance hunter, pursuig his prey down just fast enough that they drive themselves into exhaustion, at which point he calmly and mercifully snaps its neck in one swift move (hands the size of shovels, he has). If there's no neck to snap, a blow with his sledge is enough to kill most animals, though this is messier and attracts all types of scavengers.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first go at it today shaped up alright (not amazing, but ok). But then I looked at it again and realized it was no better than an Artifact 3 and you specifically requested an Artifact 4. I can't just turn this up to 11 to get there, so I'll have to rethink it (and sadly out of time for today). Hopefully someone else comes up with something cool for you! There's a lot of talent in this thread!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T10:59:59-07:00","id":919204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>7 questions vanquish god</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919027#post919027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I currently play a charecter using SPSIVS I'm a fan of your concept. However, there is an inconsistency in the cost of targeting additional opponents using the evocation you've written up - the cost section seems to price additional targets at 3m, while the description text places the cost at 2m.. As for a name, how about &quot;Perfected Voice of Nothing&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I caught that in the doc but not here because I'd already closed the browser for the night. I figured +2m per individual fighter would be an okay balancing (thematically, she's already spread the voice outward, so it's just adding a new listener) so that the battlegroup calculation was appropriately higher.<br /> <br /> And I love the name suggestion! It's not my artifact, so it's really up to her, but I'll definitely send the suggestion (and any suggestions, really) her way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919053#post919053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+3 parry! I don't know if that's reasonable - i'm not great at giving out mechanics advice, but that seems... waaaay out of whack with the same initiative-scaling item you quoted in your inspiration, as well as being a huge increase on the normal defence scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>THANK you! I wasn't really sure what to do, to be honest. <b>Moonlit Huntress</b> gives +3 auto-successes to both rush <i><b>and</b></i> disengage actions, which of course is a pretty amazing deal for someone who needs to stay at an exact range band, but it didn't fit so well with her current concept, so I wasn't really sure where else I could put that for a melee martial artist! Parry worked for the idea of SPSIVS, and I know technically bonus successes are effectively equal to bonus static numbers (because 1 given success effectively cancels out 1 static point, and vice versa), but even as I wrote it, it felt insane--even if it <b><i>is</i></b> just for that brief initiative window.<br /> <br /> Do you have any suggestions, regarding the bonuses in general? So many of the original gave successes (and even non-Charm successes!), and without an extra attunement cost, but I don't know how I might best convert them into something useful for SPSIVS or melee without just saying &quot;+(#) successes on Martial Arts rolls&quot;, which seems even more potent in combat...<br /> <br /> Would an effect lessening wound penalties by 1 work? Maybe I could put that in Sotto Voce (0 or less), move up the +1 Parry to 1-4...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T11:03:06-07:00","id":919206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916517#post916517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Swarming Bees Moonstar</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">(Moonsilver and Orichalcum Shuriken, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Evocations of Swarming Bees Moonstar</span><br /> <br /> A Solar or Lunar who spends an additional two motes to attune this artifact enjoys additional benefits when using its Evocations (described below).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, ominous. A potentially cool approach, allowing exalts to get a little more oomph for more cost, though I doubt many will choose to go for a lesser version to get 2 measily motes back.<br /> <br /> After reading your charms, I would give this effect a keyword or nickname to refer to in later evocatuions. Since it not only has to be a Solar or Lunar, but they have to pay additional motes to get it, and your lines in the evocations don't specify that it requires the additional cost. Something like &quot;A Solar/Lunar who spends 2 motes to attune is considered a &quot;Queen&quot; of the swarm or something. I'm pulling words out of my ass, but the point being later on you can say &quot;For an exalt who is a Queen&quot; or whatever you go with, it's shorter and gets the exact point across. That's just how I'd approach it. The other way is to specify in each evocation that it's &quot;when attuned by a Solar/Lunar who spent the 2 extra motes to attune to it&quot; which is a mouthful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916517#post916517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Angry Bee</span></b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Stackable, Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Three or [Essence] rounds (whichever is higher)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> The Chosen\u2019s shuriken hovers around its target on later turns, diving and swooping so that he remains off-balance. Activate when making a <b>withering</b> attack with Swarming Bees Moonstar. Whether or not the attack succeeds, the shuriken continues to menace the target for a number of rounds equal to the Exalted\u2019s Essence or three (whichever is higher). This is treated as an attack against the target solely for the purpose of imposing onslaught penalties against him, resolved on the wielder\u2019s turn. Multiple bees increase the onslaught penalty as though they were multiple attackers.<br /> <br /> The victim of this Evocation can end it prematurely by moving at least one range band away from the bee on his turn (but see Inescapable Swarm below).<br /> <br /> When attuned by a Solar or Lunar, this Evocation loses the Withering-only keyword and gains the Uniform keyword, instead, allowing the wielder to use it to enhance <b>decisive</b> attacks, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a little unclear how it works. So you throw a bee and it does it's normal attack, and then.. increases the onslaught penalty? By how much? When does it apply? Is it just a +1 to onslaught penalty per bee for 3+ rounds? And is each bee counted separately for its duration?<br /> <br /> I would increase the cost a bit for adding a persistent penalty. 2m at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916517#post916517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Inescapable Swarm</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One round<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Angry Bee<br /> The Chosen\u2019s bees pursue their target wherever he might go. The Exalt can only use this Evocation against an opponent who is currently being harried by one of her bees using the prerequisite Evocation. She may direct one of the bees to make a <b>withering</b> or <b>decisive</b> attack against its victim as long as he remains within close range of the bee. This is considered a Thrown attack made by the Exalt with the shuriken and is always treated as being made at close range from the victim. If used to make a <b>decisive</b> attack it eliminates one of the bees plaguing the target, even if it had duration remaining.<br /> <br /> Additionally, if the victim attempts to move away from the bees, he must make a successful disengage attempt, which the bees resist using the Exalted\u2019s Dexterity + Thrown with automatic successes equal to her Essence.<br /> <br /> When the artifact is attuned by a Solar or Lunar, use of this Evocation extends the duration of one of the bees assailing its target by one additional round.</div> </div> </div> </div>So on one action, the exalt uses Angry Bee to put a bee around the person. On the next action, they can use Inescapable Swarm to use that hovering bee to do an attack against the target. If the victim chooses to move away from the bees AFTER the Simple action is done, then they have to do a successful disengage attempt. The way it interacts in that precise aspect is... a little clunky. I'm not sure how to clean it up, but it feels too separated from the design of this evocation. Otherwise, up that cost to 3m and I think it's ok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916517#post916517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sting to Death</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Inescapable Swarm<br /> The Chosen directs her bees to sting their target to death. The Exalt may spread her total Initiative between a number of <b>decisive</b> attacks not exceeding the number of bees surrounding the target. Initiative must be spread as evenly as possible between the attacks. In addition, the damage roll enjoys double-10s. The wielder\u2019s Initiative does not reset until she has completed every attack. Each attack she enhances with this Evocation reduces the number of bees harrying the target by one.<br /> <br /> When the artifact is attuned by a Solar or Lunar, the wielder may throw another shuriken as part of the activation of this Evocation, increasing the maximum number of attacks by one. She must be able to attack the target with a thrown weapon to take advantage of this effect. He cannot be hidden behind a wall, for example, or beyond the range of her shuriken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916517#post916517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Swarm Ascending</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp or 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One round<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Angry Bee<br /> A single shuriken circling one opponent\u2019s head like a lone hornet shatters into a swarm of bees pursuing every nearby enemy. Choose a target currently affected by Angry Bee. The bees\u2019 onslaught penalty affects all the Chosen\u2019s enemies within short range of the initial target. As long as the primary target is assailed by at least one bee, this Evocation can be renewed on subsequent turns at a cost of three motes.<br /> <br /> When attuned by a Solar or Lunar, the wielder may instead spend eight motes and one Willpower to activate this Evocation. If she does so, the swarm of bees extends to medium range from the primary target.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be an Essence 3 evocation. But otherwise is a pretty cool effect. So someone in the center has to disengage up to 3 times to get out of the swarm? That feels a bit rough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916517#post916517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Deadly Stinging Swarm</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sting to Death<br /> This Evocation upgrades Angry Bee, shrinking the flitting shuriken assailing their targets to the size of insects, allowing them to slip through armor easily. Anyone suffering an onslaught penalty caused by the wielder\u2019s harrying bees also suffers an environmental hazard that deals dice of lethal damage equal to the bees\u2019 onslaught penalty each round. Victims may resist this damage with a successful Stamina + Resistance roll against a difficulty equal to the Exalted\u2019s Essence.<br /> <br /> If attuned by a Solar or Lunar, increase the difficulty and damage dice of this Evocation by one each.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo nasty. I like this one a lot. I'm on the fence about it being free. Takes a lot to get it up there as is, so maybe not that big a deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=916517#post916517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Swarm Descends</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Deadly Stinging Swarm, Swarm Ascends<br /> The wielder can use Inescapable Swarm and Sting to Death against anyone within the swarm. Additionally, activation of Inescapable Swarm against at least one enemy prevents all enemies from leaving the swarm without a disengage action, and Sting to Death counts all the bees within short range of its target when determining the maximum number of decisive attacks it can execute.<br /> <br /> When attuned by a Solar or Lunar, the bees created by the first Evocation of this artifact instead last until the end of the scene (or until used up by Inescapable Swarm or Sting to Death). However, the onslaught penalty any target suffers due to the bees cannot exceed the Chosen\u2019s Essence, regardless of the number of harrying him. Additionally, Sting to Death can attack targets within medium range of its target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personal choice, but I would give this a cost that you activate so that the exalt would have the option. They may prefer to do this the other way so they can have a higher onslaught penalty. If you go that route, make it reflexive with maybe a 5m cost. Like flipping a switch. Then it's still advantageous because they can choose to activate it if they manage to get a high number and hold onto it.<br /> <br /> Overall, a cool design. I like the bee theme, and always fun seeing Moonsilver being used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T11:27:05-07:00","id":919219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=918076#post918076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shield of Melthar-Khun (Orichalcum Shield - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Shield of Melthar-Khun</b><br /> A Solar Exalt who attunes to the shield and takes a Defend Other action subtracts one additional Initiative from any attacker who beats his defense and chooses to strike his defended charge. The Solar steals this additional Initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first sentence is solid. The second one is really strong for a free evocation. I've add an extra mote or two to attunement cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=918076#post918076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Under My Protection</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Those who would strike the defended see their blades turned aside by the edge of the shield, for it will not tolerate their temerity. This Evocation can be activated when the wielder has taken a Defend Other action, his Defense has been overcome by an attacker, and the attacker chooses to strike the defended charge. Each 1 on the attacker\u2019s roll to strike the charge subtracts a success from the attacker\u2019s final roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Niche enough to be solid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=918076#post918076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Iron Body Stance</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Under My Protection<br /> <br /> Let it not be said that the Shield of Melthar-Khun does not protect its wielder as well. Whenever a Solar who knows this Evocation and is wielding the Shield of Melthar-Khun takes a Defend Other action, his Soak is increased by 2 and his Hardness is increased by 1 for the duration of the Defend Other action. This soak and Hardness explicitly stack with all other sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like how everything hinges on pretty specific criteria. Makes it a solid design. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=918076#post918076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Guardian\u2019s Retributive Strike</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Counterattack, Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Iron Body Stance<br /> <br /> Woe to those who would strike the charge of the wielder of the Shield of Melthar-Khun. The wielder may use this Evocation in response to any attack while he is using a Defend Other action that beats his defense and chooses to strike at his protected charge, creating a Melee counterattack with the Shield of Melthar-Khun that occurs after the opponent\u2019s attack result but before the damage has been rolled. This attack functions as a regular <b>decisive</b> attack. Guardian\u2019s Retributive Strike does not count as the wielder\u2019s combat action and cannot be used in response to another counterattack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have nothing to corroborate that it's necessary, but my gut says to add a Willpower to this cost. Some counterattacks require it, some don't. I think it's because it doesn't count as their combat action, but maybe because it's Decisive it's not that bad? Just my gut.<br /> <br /> And then we have...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=918153#post918153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And its companion piece -<br /> <br /> <b>Mushi Armor \u2013 Orichalcum and White Jade Articulated Plate (Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Mushi Armor</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blooded who attunes to this armor gains 1 point of Initiative when taking a Defend Other action. This benefit cannot occur more than once per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>This works more cleanly than the last one. Also, on a personal preference note, I dislike that there are &quot;multiple copies&quot; of this armor. Every artifact in Creation is supposed to be unique. If it's part of a set, I feel like each one should either build off of each other or have their own version of the power set. It's a nitpick, but it's mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid;n918153[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ties that Bind[/B]<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The first power of the armor is to bind its wearer to his charge, ensuring that a firm bond is forged between brothers. This Evocation may be activated whenever the wearer is attacked while taking a Defend Other action while wearing this armor. He automatically gains a Minor Tie of brotherhood toward his charge. If he already has a Tie of brotherhood, that Tie is instead strengthened by one level.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only complaint about this evocation is that it doesn't convey any direct benefit itself other than gaining the Tie. I get that over evocations build on it, but on its own, it's... very minor. Might be personal taste, but it feels like a speedbump power. If it was combined with another one, it wouldn't feel out of place at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid;n918153[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Brother\u2019s Bond[/B]<br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Withering-only<br /> Duration: One turn<br /> Prerequisites: The Ties that Bind<br /> <br /> The stronger the wearer\u2019s love for his brother, the stronger the armor becomes. This Evocation may be activated whenever the wearer is attacked while taking a Defend Other action while wearing this armor. His <b>withering</b> soak increases by an amount determined by the strength of his Tie toward the defended character: +2 soak for a Minor Tie, +3 soak for a Major Tie, or +4 soak for a Defining Tie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solid, except change your wording to specify the Tie of Brotherhood that you defined in The Ties that Bind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid;n918153[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Self-as-Selflessness Stance[/B]<br /> Cost: 1m/Initiative; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: The Brother\u2019s Bond<br /> <br /> \u201cThose who would strike my brother would strike me.\u201d This is the mudra of the Mushi Armor. This Evocation may be activated whenever the wearer is attacked while taking a Defend Other action while wearing this armor. He may steal from the attacker a number of points of Initiative equal to his Tie towards the defended character: 1 Initiative for a Minor Tie, 2 for a Major, and 3 for a Defining Tie. This Initiative is stolen immediately before the attack is resolved, which can affect the outcome of a <b>decisive</b> attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, specify the Tie of Brotherhood if it's going to build off of The Ties That Bind. Additionally, the timing of this FEELS kind of like a Counterattack. I'm not sure how you'd rework it to be that, but because it can change how a Decisive attack works, it feels kind of like that. Then again, I guess this is how some Defensive charms work, so maybe I'm way off-base. The one thing I think should be added is more specific wording around exactly when it's resolved: after a successful attack roll but before damage is rolled. Just to be super clear. Finally, I know you're shooting for all Essence 1 effects, but not only eliminating Initiative from someone, but STEALING it feels too strong for Essence 1.<br /> <br /> Together, this set makes for a motherfucker of a Defender. Cool yo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T12:15:26-07:00","id":919248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=918207#post918207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here is my first complete attempt at creating an artifact with evocations in EX3. Not sure how balanced it is so I'd appreciate some feedback and suggestions to improve/fix it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Charm of the Weasel</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attunement </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with most hunters the weasel can see its prey long before the prey see them any exalt attuned to the charm of the weasel gain +1 on all visual awareness checks and have no difficulty seeing in anything other than pure darkness. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>Seems a solid start. I presume this isn't armor, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=918207#post918207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bones of Rubber</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Allows the exalt to squeeze through any opening that they can get their head through</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The weasel is a predator that\u2019s path cannot easily be barred. This evocation allows the exalt to channel the ability of the weasel to fit through any opening which they can get their head through. One this evocation is active should the exalt be able to move her head through an opening her body flows and adjusts to make it through the space as well. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this power actually, though I'm not sure why it's a scene-long. Seems like you'd just activate it until you've squeezed through the proper opening. I'd keep everything but make it Instant and maybe even Reflexive. It's a cool power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=918207#post918207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prey of the Weasel</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 6m</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Bones of Rubber</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Once the Exalt locates her quarry she chases it until it is hers</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The weasel is a predator that shuns the tactic of stalk and ambush in favor of flush and chase. The exalt may reflexively activate this evocation to mark her prey, be it a person, animal, or item. Once the prey has been mark the exalt will chase it down till it\u2019s hers. The exalt gets +1 to all stamina and perception rolls to locate/acquire her quarry.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special rules: The exalt must see, hear, or smell her prey to activate this evocation and the sense used will determine the difficulty of tracking. Also the exalt must continue tracking until she finds her prey, if she loses the trail or gives up the evocation ends and the prey is no longer marked.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Just a +1 to rolls? For 6m? You can get +1 for 1m with an Excellency? Ain't nothing about this power that's amazing, let alone Essence 3. The scale of this power is Essence 1, but it's STILL overpriced and underbonused to be of any use. I would make this an Essence 1 power, make it start the whole tree. Give it a cost of 2m, and make it give +1 non-charm bonus for tracking. If they track the target successfully while the power is going, give them an additional +1 non-charm bonus to their stealth roll in an Ambush attack. That's an interesting power that's not too strong and would start this tree out nicely at Essence 1. Or you can go a different direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=918207#post918207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Changing one\u2019s Coat</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m, 1wp</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Indefinite</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Prey of the Weasel</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Allows the Exalt to change her outward appearance to blend in with her surroundings </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Just as the weasel changes its coat from brown to white so can the exalted. An exalt using this evocation can change their outward appearance to blend in with the scenery. This evocation allows the exalt to change the color, texture, and feel of their clothing. Additionally the exalt can affect their skin and hair as well changing them to blend with their surroundings. Once the commitment to this evocations lapses the exalts appearance returns to normal </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special rules: Should the charm of the weasel have the chameleon stone socketed into it the following additional effects are available. The evocation allows access to the hearthstones innate ability and expands upon it. The exalt may now change not only their hair, eye, and skin color but also their clothing and equipment to blend into any situation.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is going to need some mechanics for it. Does it offer bonuses to Stealth? Or to Disguise? How much of a bonus?<br /> <br /> It's a cool unique theme, and I like it! Give it a spit-shine and it'll be rockin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T12:41:31-07:00","id":919271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919204#post919204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> THANK you! I wasn't really sure what to do, to be honest. <b>Moonlit Huntress</b> gives +3 auto-successes to both rush <i><b>and</b></i> disengage actions, which of course is a pretty amazing deal for someone who needs to stay at an exact range band, but it didn't fit so well with her current concept, so I wasn't really sure where else I could put that for a melee martial artist! Parry worked for the idea of SPSIVS, and I know technically bonus successes are effectively equal to bonus static numbers (because 1 given success effectively cancels out 1 static point, and vice versa), but even as I wrote it, it felt insane--even if it <b><i>is</i></b> just for that brief initiative window.<br /> <br /> Do you have any suggestions, regarding the bonuses in general? So many of the original gave successes (and even non-Charm successes!), and without an extra attunement cost, but I don't know how I might best convert them into something useful for SPSIVS or melee without just saying &quot;+(#) successes on Martial Arts rolls&quot;, which seems even more potent in combat...<br /> <br /> Would an effect lessening wound penalties by 1 work? Maybe I could put that in Sotto Voce (0 or less), move up the +1 Parry to 1-4...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the lessened wound penalties would work better from a balance point of view, and -1 to all your wound penalties is pretty strong, without being unbalancing or overpowered. +1 parry isn't unreasonable, but remember that being a Reaper Daiklave, the artefact is sporting a +1 parry before you even begin adding attunement bonuses and evocations. I'm not a great person to ask about this, because I like effects that do all kinds of tricksy nonsense, and because i'm not great at mechanical balance.<br /> <br /> Oh, there's Unsung Hero! Ask him, he'll know!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T12:53:16-07:00","id":919277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919219#post919219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Together, this set makes for a motherfucker of a Defender. Cool yo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T13:09:30-07:00","id":919283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919271#post919271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the lessened wound penalties would work better from a balance point of view, and -1 to all your wound penalties is pretty strong, without being unbalancing or overpowered. +1 parry isn't unreasonable, but remember that being a Reaper Daiklave, the artefact is sporting a +1 parry before you even begin adding attunement bonuses and evocations. I'm not a great person to ask about this, because I like effects that do all kinds of tricksy nonsense, and because i'm not great at mechanical balance.<br /> <br /> Oh, there's Unsung Hero! Ask him, he'll know!</div> </div> </div> </div>He's the head honcho, going through all sorts of artifacts in his backlog, so I'll probably wait until I have a more fleshed out concept (though he's always welcome to chime in if he has time!)<br /> <br /> Still, with your advice, I've bumped everything up and gotten rid of the +3 parry, so it looks more like this:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Sotto Voce </b>(0 or fewer Initiative): All wound penalties reduced by 1.<br /> \u2022 <b>Agitato </b>(1-4 Initiative): +1 non-Charm bonus to Parry.<br /> \u2022 <b>Bravura </b>(5-9 Initiative): +2 non-Charm success to rush actions.<br /> \u2022 <b>Subito </b>(10-14 Initiative): The character may aim reflexively for a <b>withering</b> attack.<br /> \u2022 <b>Trionfante </b>(15+ Initiative): The character\u2019s aim actions also convey the benefits (but not costs) of a full defense action.<br /> <br /> This kind of fits the theme even better, to be honest. At 0 initiative or lower, you're obviously doing badly, and probably need the reduced penalties in case the person who crashed you goes to strike. At 1-4, aka where you go after a successful Decisive, the additional parry to help keep them from countering is always nice. Having a +2 to rush at 5-9 is great, because that's probably where your average join battle roll is going to land--perfect for closing the distance the moment conflict begins. At 10-14, being able to reflexively aim for withering is ideal for ensuring crash and getting that last leg up to Trionfante, at 15+, where the SPSIVS user is preparing for that flawless strike.<br /> <br /> Thanks so much for helping me bounce ideas around! If this seems reasonable, then now I turn back to the actual evocation ideas...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":11797,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","user":"Seeker","date":".  Switched the names for Bravura and Subito to be more fitting. 06-22-2016, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T13:37:55-07:00","id":919295,"title":"","content":"So, despite suffering a mental block on the great goremaul I requested, I was able to flesh out the armor I sketched out when The Unsung Hero asked for inspiration for a green jade artifact.<br /> So I present to you, for your entertainment and critique...<br /> <br /> Lakashim, the Pulse of Life<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact: Green Jade Silken Armor<br /> <br /> <u><b>Appearance</b></u><br /> Strands of green jade with the silk of some long lost race of moth are woven into a dozen braided pairs that come together in a spiral on the wearer\u2019s upper left chest, above the heart.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attunement</b></u><br /> Additional Benefits: 0m<br /> - The wearer can add their Performance ability to their join battle result instead of 3 when calculating initiative if they have a Performance specialty in Dance.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Evocations</u><br /> Hear the Pulse of Creation</b><br /> Cost: 5m<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> One Line Summary: Sense all living things nearby and downgrade ambush and surprise attacks to surprise attacks and normal attacks, respectively<br /> <br /> By closing their eyes and opening their senses to Lakashim, the wearer can hear the local beat of the Worldsong. For the rest of the scene, the wearer is aware of all the life around them, gaining a general sense of any creature with a functional heartbeat within medium range. This does not give them an exact location but will provide an accurate number of how many beings are in each respective range band, whether visible or not. With this information, the wearer is also better armed against unexpected attacks by those they have sensed, treating successful ambushes as surprise attacks, and successful surprise attacks as normal attacks, respectively. At Essence 4, the sensory range upgrades to long range. This evocation only works as long as the wearer stands upon Creation.<br /> <br /> <b>Pounding Dance of the Worldheart</b><br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Hear the Pulse of Creation<br /> One Line Summary: Move in tandem with opponents, losing less initiative from withering attacks<br /> <br /> Once in tune with the rhythm of the Creation, the wearer now moves with a grace that only come from following the steps in the dance of all life. In a scene where the wearer has used Hear the Pulse of Creation, a sensed attacker gains only half of the initiative lost (round up) from withering attack against the wearer and does not receive any bonus if they crash the wearer. The wearer loses the full amount of initiative, the attacker can\u2019t seem to take advantage of the situation nearly as well as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Rebounding Inner Rhythm</b><br /> Cost: 2m/1W<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Counterattack<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Pounding Dance of the Worldheart<br /> One Line Summary: Recover from falling with bounce in your step and a fist to their attacker\u2019s face<br /> <br /> Like the silence between heartbeats, sometimes the course of Lakashim falls to rise again with fierce determination. The wearer recovers more readily from being knocked down, gaining 1 initiative after successfully rising from prone. The wearer may ignore the penalty to flurry rising from prone and attacking the opponent that attacked them. In this case, the additional initiative is awarded before the flurried attack is rolled. If the wearer is capable of reflexively rising from prone, they must pay an additional willpower and treat it as a counterattack to take advantage of this evocation.<br /> <br /> <b>One Pulse, One Soul, One Act</b><br /> Cost: -<br /> Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Pounding Dance of the Worldheart<br /> One Line Summary: When your action sync\u2019s up with an ally\u2019s attack, chance to share some successes between both of them<br /> <br /> When many things move in harmony and act as one, Lakashim beats loudest. After Hear the Pulse of Creation, whenever the wearer attacks an opponent on the same tick as an ally, they both may reroll an unsuccessful die once, sharing all successes rolled.<br /> <br /> Example: Wearer rolls 2 successes and their ally rolls 0 successes. They both reroll one die apiece, coming up with 1 success between both of them. The wearer now has 3 successes and the ally has 1 success.<br /> <br /> This effect cannot happen if either the ally or the wearer delayed their action to act on the same tick. All allies that have a pulse that are attacking the same target may partake in this reroll, adding their successes to the shared result, but must do so after all other reroll mechanics. Those who cannot reroll an unsuccessful die cannot partake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T15:08:30-07:00","id":919338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919283#post919283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still, with your advice, I've bumped everything up and gotten rid of the +3 parry, so it looks more like this:<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Sotto Voce </b>(0 or fewer Initiative): All wound penalties reduced by 1.<br /> \u2022 <b>Agitato </b>(1-4 Initiative): +1 non-Charm bonus to Parry.<br /> \u2022 <b>Bravura </b>(5-9 Initiative): +2 non-Charm success to rush actions.<br /> \u2022 <b>Subito </b>(10-14 Initiative): The character may aim reflexively for a <b>withering</b> attack.<br /> \u2022 <b>Trionfante </b>(15+ Initiative): The character\u2019s aim actions also convey the benefits (but not costs) of a full defense action.<br /> <br /> This kind of fits the theme even better, to be honest. At 0 initiative or lower, you're obviously doing badly, and probably need the reduced penalties in case the person who crashed you goes to strike. At 1-4, aka where you go after a successful Decisive, the additional parry to help keep them from countering is always nice. Having a +2 to rush at 5-9 is great, because that's probably where your average join battle roll is going to land--perfect for closing the distance the moment conflict begins. At 10-14, being able to reflexively aim for withering is ideal for ensuring crash and getting that last leg up to Trionfante, at 15+, where the SPSIVS user is preparing for that flawless strike.</div> </div> </div> </div>- Sotto Voce sounds only useful in an extremely limited set of circumstances (you have wound penalties to begin with, but you're also in Initiative Crash, meaning your opponent is so badly outclassing you that they managed to connect with a decisive yet you're still in crash - so you either didn't manage to gain Initiative Shift on them once they reset, or they hit you with a decisive and THEN crashed you). Now, it's a valid design niche to only give a bonus when you're in <i>real</i> trouble, but in such a situation, that 1 wound penalty reduction is unlikely to help you much (after all, your opponent managed to wound and crash you even without those penalties). What I'd give it instead is &quot;if the character spends Willpower to enhance her Defense against a decisive attack, but the attack still hits, she may reduce its raw damage by (Essence) dice&quot;. Incidentally, this also synergizes well with the fact that Single Point can be practiced in medium armor (up to 7 Hardness), and benefits you even if you're completely mote-tapped.<br /> - Agitato has the good idea, but it's also kind of bland. I'd go with &quot;your character may waive the Initiative cost of taking a Full Defense action&quot;.<br /> - Bravura is nice, but given the frankly absurd potency of Single Point's damage enhancers, users of the style will rarely need to make withering attacks in the 10-14 Initiative range. So I'd give it Subito's bonus instead.<br /> - Subito could instead grant +2 automatic non-charm successes to the character's rolls to oppose Disengage actions (because enemies can reasonably be expected to try to outrun a Single Point stylist once she gets the murderball rolling).<br /> - Trionfante is fine as-is (albeit I personally think Shining Ice Mirror's attunement bonus is woefully overrated, and while I appreciate the thematic relevance, it's just not worth an additional 40% of the weapon's attunement cost).<br /> <br /> Other possible bonuses to consider:<br /> - The weapon is considered to have the Two-Handed tag.<br /> - As long as the wielder is in Single Point form, she can ignore her armor's mobility penalty for the purposes of catching enemies.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are two big problems I'm seeing here, unrelated to the bonuses:<br /> a/ the attunement bonus doesn't take into account the fact that Single Point stylists have access to two Initiative tracks (I assumed that its benefits are dependent on the wielder's main Initiative track, but the whole thing could be made <i>much</i> more interesting if somehow both tracks factored into it).<br /> b/ I'm just not seeing how any of this fits either the &quot;singing sword&quot; theme (aside from the names), <i>or</i> the themes of either orichalcum, starmetal or black jade. (Why black jade, anyway? What does water have to do with singing?) Moonlit Huntress' bonus is good because moonsilver is a magical material that has its themes intrinsically tied with change and the moon. I see no similar connection here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T16:14:56-07:00","id":919363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919338#post919338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Sotto Voce sounds only useful in an extremely limited set of circumstances (you have wound penalties to begin with, but you're also in Initiative Crash, meaning your opponent is so badly outclassing you that they managed to connect with a decisive yet you're still in crash - so you either didn't manage to gain Initiative Shift on them once they reset, or they hit you with a decisive and THEN crashed you). Now, it's a valid design niche to only give a bonus when you're in <i>real</i> trouble, but in such a situation, that 1 wound penalty reduction is unlikely to help you much (after all, your opponent managed to wound and crash you even without those penalties). What I'd give it instead is &quot;if the character spends Willpower to enhance her Defense against a decisive attack, but the attack still hits, she may reduce its raw damage by (Essence) dice&quot;. Incidentally, this also synergizes well with the fact that Single Point can be practiced in medium armor (up to 7 Hardness), and benefits you even if you're completely mote-tapped.<br /> - Agitato has the good idea, but it's also kind of bland. I'd go with &quot;your character may waive the Initiative cost of taking a Full Defense action&quot;.<br /> - Bravura is nice, but given the frankly absurd potency of Single Point's damage enhancers, users of the style will rarely need to make withering attacks in the 10-14 Initiative range. So I'd give it Subito's bonus instead.<br /> - Subito could instead grant +2 automatic non-charm successes to the character's rolls to oppose Disengage actions (because enemies can reasonably be expected to try to outrun a Single Point stylist once she gets the murderball rolling).<br /> - Trionfante is fine as-is (albeit I personally think Shining Ice Mirror's attunement bonus is woefully overrated, and while I appreciate the thematic relevance, it's just not worth an additional 40% of the weapon's attunement cost).<br /> <br /> Other possible bonuses to consider:<br /> - The weapon is considered to have the Two-Handed tag.<br /> - As long as the wielder is in Single Point form, she can ignore her armor's mobility penalty for the purposes of catching enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Sotto Voce</b>: That definitely works better.<br /> <br /> <b>Agitato</b>: I'll consider this one, for sure, probably suggest it to her.<br /> <br /> <b>Bravura + Subito</b>: You have these two names mixed up, I think, but I still get the idea. <b>Bravura</b> keeps the rush bonus and <b>Subito</b> changes out the reflexive aim for the disengage opposition... I like it! At the very least, I'll <b>definitely</b> include opposing disengage somewhere...<br /> <br /> <b>Other</b>:<br /> -- Two-handed: Having a Clash bonus feels a bit too situational, but it's certainly more SPSIVS than the a wound-penalty reducer... I'll toy with where it might go.<br /> -- Single Point Form: Oof, this feels awesome, but I have some hesitance, as I'll explain in response to the two problems:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are two big problems I'm seeing here, unrelated to the bonuses:<br /> a/ the attunement bonus doesn't take into account the fact that Single Point stylists have access to two Initiative tracks (I assumed that its benefits are dependent on the wielder's main Initiative track, but the whole thing could be made <i>much</i> more interesting if somehow both tracks factored into it).<br /> b/ I'm just not seeing how any of this fits either the &quot;singing sword&quot; theme (aside from the names), <i>or</i> the themes of either orichalcum, starmetal or black jade. (Why black jade, anyway? What does water have to do with singing?) Moonlit Huntress' bonus is good because moonsilver is a magical material that has its themes intrinsically tied with change and the moon. I see no similar connection here. </div> </div> </div><b>A)</b> While this character is definitely going to be a Single Point stylist, I'm iffy on the idea of making an artifact that's only useful to that small spectrum. It's a personal grievance, of course, not mechanical, but I feel like restricting an artifact in that way takes away from its legend more than fuels it--rather than an amazing Melee swordsman being able to use it as well as a Martial Artist, it's <b><i>only</i></b> fully effective in the hands of that character type. Still, it's something I'll ask her about, and I appreciate the suggestion--maybe this will break me out of that hindrance.<br /> <br /> <b>B)</b> I haven't written out the lore-part of the blade, but the idea is that a spirit of warsong is bound within the metal, and the main magic materials regarding spirit communion and binding are Starmetal and Black Jade. I definitely plan to play more with it in future evocations once I get the balance settled (since I've only done the attunement and the first evocation so far, with a couple other concepts on the burner), but for now I'm just trying to do an early set-up. The idea is that the evocations will revolve around the blade's shifting song (via this attunement) and maybe spreading it to allies, invoking negative mental effects on enemies, or similar... for lack of a better term, &quot;bardic&quot; concepts.<br /> <br /> As for Orichalcum, I've mostly included it as little more than its &quot;amplification&quot; purposes, but will probably play more with its &quot;essence cutting&quot; idea. &gt;_&gt;;; It's all still very much in-the-rough.<br /> <br /> All the same, just like above, thank you so much for your comments! Any refining help is good help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T17:50:02-07:00","id":919410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919363#post919363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Other</b>:<br /> -- Two-handed: Having a Clash bonus feels a bit too situational</div> </div> </div> </div>It really, really shouldn't. With the exception of Gathering Light Concentration, literally all of Single Point's defensive Charms revolve around Clashes. Moreover, since they're decisive-only, they need all the boosts they can get (as they can't benefit from Accuracy).<br /> <br /> Speaking of Clashes, you <i>definitely</i> need an Evocation geared around unleashing a huge, deafening sonic blast as the reverberating blade is struck by the opponent's weapon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919363#post919363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -- Single Point Form: Oof, this feels awesome, but I have some hesitance, as I'll explain in response to the two problems:<br /> <br /> <b>A)</b> While this character is definitely going to be a Single Point stylist, I'm iffy on the idea of making an artifact that's only useful to that small spectrum. It's a personal grievance, of course, not mechanical, but I feel like restricting an artifact in that way takes away from its legend more than fuels it--rather than an amazing Melee swordsman being able to use it as well as a Martial Artist, it's <b><i>only</i></b> fully effective in the hands of that character type.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it could be an Evocation, so the bang-for-your-buck value stays the same, but the Single Point stylist still gets some bennies that interact with her shtick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919363#post919363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>B)</b> I haven't written out the lore-part of the blade, but the idea is that a spirit of warsong is bound within the metal, and the main magic materials regarding spirit communion and binding are Starmetal and Black Jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I'm interpreting it is that black jade helps with Evocations that affect external targets. Freedom's Cadence doesn't need to have black jade components to harness the spirit powers of its originator either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T18:28:07-07:00","id":919430,"title":"","content":"See, this is what I get for trying to help without having given the later SPSIVS charms an absolutely <i><b>thorough</b></i> read-through. Clashes! Augh. Thank you for pointing this out to me! (And that deafening sonic blast post-clash... mmm, already imagining it, too.)<br /> <br /> And yeah, after further looking into the metals after that post, I've gotten rid of Black Jade, so thanks for bringing it to my attention earlier. This thing's really starting to develop!<br /> <br /> <b><u><span style=\"font-size:24px\">YE OLDE EDIT:</span></u></b><br /> <br /> Alright, so after some work, I've got the general bones of the artifact done--and as usual, I could definitely use some balance and cost suggestions!<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Perfected Voice of Nothing</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>(Orichalcum and Starmetal) Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022</b></span><br /> <br /> <i>Tags:</i> Lethal, Melee, Balanced<br /> <br /> [Story Stuff]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><u>Evocations of Perfected Voice of Nothing</u></b></span><br /> Attuning to Perfected Void of Nothing unleashes the singing spirit of the blade, whose ethereal voice sings to the mind and soul of its wielder with enchanting power. As the wielder gains an advantage in battle, the spirit\u2019s voice shifts within her. Further, a Solar or Sidereal who pays 2 additional motes to attune to Perfected Voice of Nothing gains the <b>Aria</b> levels\u2019 passive benefits. They are as follows:<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Sotto Voce (0 or fewer Initiative):</b> If the character spends Willpower to enhance her Defense against a decisive attack, but the attack still hits, she may reduce its raw damage by (Essence) dice<br /> <b>\u2022 Subito (1-4 Initiative):</b> The character may aim reflexively for a <b>withering</b> attack.<br /> <b>\u2022 Bravura (5-9 Initiative):</b> +2 non-Charm successes to rush actions.<br /> <b>\u2022 Furioso (10-14 Initiative):</b> +2 non-Charm successes to oppose enemy Disengage actions.<br /> <b>\u2022 Trionfante (15+ Initiative):</b> The character may delay their action at no cost in preparation for a Clash; if they do not Clash by the end of the round, they lose the -2 Initiative as normal.<br /> <br /> The <b>Aria</b> levels are given quantities 1 (Sotto Voce) through 5 (Trionfante) for the purposes of evocation calculation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Haunting Refrain<br /> Cost:</b> 3m per turn; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> The wielder ushers forth the spirit\u2019s voice from the blade, establishing a mystic link to her target so he hears the blade\u2019s unsettling song. The wielder rolls (Essence + [Aria x 2]) against her target\u2019s Resolve. If successful, the target hears the refrain at full volume, sustaining a penalty to all rolls equal to half the weapon\u2019s <b>Aria</b> (rounded up) at the time of his turn. If the roll fails, the target only hears the murmuring voice at the back of his mind. The roll repeats every turn the evocation is maintained.<br /> <br /> This evocation can target multiple foes, with the cost per turn increasing by 2 motes for every additional target.<br /> <br /> This evocation can target battlegroups. Rather than penalties, however, successful roles deal (Aria / 2) dice of Magnitude damage, as the soldiers ensnared by the effects panic and either go catatonic or flee in terror.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hallowed Warcry<br /> Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Haunting Refrain<br /> <br /> The blade unleashes a mental roar into an enemy\u2019s mind, powered by the frustration of the wielder\u2019s struggling fate, in an attempt to disturb his mind and essence. The wielder rolls (Essence + Willpower) against the target\u2019s Resolve; if successful, the target loses Initiative equal to the threshold successes, disoriented from the spirit\u2019s rage.<br /> <br /> Against foes already affected by <b>Haunting Refrain</b>, this roll receives 1 automatic success, and instead of a single shout, the song instantly and momentarily crescendos before reverting to its normal effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dissonant Revelation<br /> Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp, +2m per success; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Clash, Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Hallowed Warcry<br /> <br /> As foes hear its song, the spirit hears their thoughts, which the blade shares with its wielder. When an opponent targeted by <b>Haunting Refrain</b> attempts to strike the wielder, the blade may hum to reveal the enemy intent to her through ethereal guidance; if allowed, the spirit will push the wielder into a reflexive Clash attack. With the combined force of song and steel, the attack may benefit from non-Charm dice up to half the <b>Aria</b> level, rounded up, on a 2-for-1 cost basis. If successful, the wielder only gains half the Initiative the enemy loses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Crescendo of the Reckoning Star<br /> Cost:</b> 8m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Clash<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Dissonant Revelation<br /> <br /> When steel strikes steel, the spirit\u2019s voice pierces Creation with unshakeable determination, tearing away any destiny woven against the spirit\u2019s wielder. At the moment of a Clash attack, the blade\u2019s voice is projected outward for all to hear in an ear-piercing battlecry that shakes the air itself. This acts as an undodgeable, unblockable <b>withering</b> attack against all enemies within Short range, dealing (Essence + Willpower) in damage dice. This roll gains automatic successes equal to half the <b>Aria</b> level, rounded down (minimum 0).<br /> <br /> Enemies in Close range (excluding the opponent) add their Essence to their Soak; Enemies at Short range add (their Essence + 3), as the shockwave weakens over distance.<br /> <br /> Only initiative lost by the Clashing opponent is gained by the wielder; all other Initiative is simply lost. This is calculated before the Clash completes, with the gained Initiative going toward the Clash itself if <b>decisive</b>.<br /> <br /> This evocation ends<b> Haunting Refrain</b> for all targets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, as mentioned, main concerns are balance (across the board, not for specific styles), cost vs effect, and the like. In particular, I'm still toying with <b>Trionfante</b>'s effect...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":11797,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","user":"Seeker","date":". 06-23-2016, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T22:50:43-07:00","id":919520,"title":"","content":"Yay! Aluminiumtrioxid (Commonwealth, I assume) knows!<br /> <br /> Binaryphantom, Lakashim seems pretty limited. Everything seems to have an extra condition tacked on, and a lot of the evocations don't really grant much in the way of benefit. I think that if I got Lakashim, I wouldn't bother paying precious, precious xp to unlock any of those. Fr'instance, given that you already have to have exactly the same initiative as an ally and also both choose to attack on that exact tick, rerolling one missed die apiece is... underwhelming for the glorious capstone of the entire evocation tree, especially one used at essence 4 where you probably have a craptonne of really great charms you want to buy instead. The costs for the entire set are pretty low, but when every single evocation costs you a charm or a spell, it has to be worth the investment, and to me at least, those are not.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the only constructive feedback I can give is to make some of those numbers bigger, or the effects more encompassing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T02:59:50-07:00","id":919615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919520#post919520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yay! Aluminiumtrioxid (Commonwealth, I assume) knows!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm... not sure I got that reference. Or rather, I'm pretty sure I didn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919430#post919430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><u>Evocations of Perfected Voice of Nothing</u></b></span><br /> A Solar or Sidereal attuned to Perfected Void of Nothing unleashes the singing spirit of the blade, whose ethereal voice sings to the mind and soul of its wielder with enchanting power. As the Exalt earns an advantage, the spirit\u2019s voice shifts within her. The following are the weapon\u2019s <b>Aria</b> levels.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Sotto Voce (0 or fewer Initiative):</b> If the character spends Willpower to enhance her Defense against a decisive attack, but the attack still hits, she may reduce its raw damage by (Essence) dice<br /> <b>\u2022 Subito (1-4 Initiative):</b> The character may aim reflexively for a <b>withering</b> attack.<br /> <b>\u2022 Bravura (5-9 Initiative):</b> +2 non-Charm successes to rush actions.<br /> <b>\u2022 Furioso (10-14 Initiative):</b> +2 non-Charm successes to oppose enemy Disengage actions.<br /> <b>\u2022 Trionfante (15+ Initiative):</b> The character\u2019s aim actions also convey the benefits (but not costs) of a full defense action.<br /> <br /> The <b>Aria</b> levels are given quantities 1 (Sotto Voce) through 5 (Trionfante) for the purposes of evocation calculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how many of the artifact's Evocations revolve around Aria levels, I think it's pretty harsh that only Solars and Sidereals can benefit from them. It should probably say &quot;the following are the weapon's Aria levels; moreover, a Solar or Sidereal who attunes to Perfected Voice of Nothing gains passive benefits associated with the individual Aria levels as described below&quot;. Also, I think this benefit should probably cost an additional 2m attunement cost, some of these are pretty damn nasty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919430#post919430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Haunting Refrain<br /> Cost:</b> 3m per turn; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> The wielder ushers forth the spirit\u2019s voice from the blade, establishing a mystic link to her target so he hears the blade\u2019s unsettling song. The wielder rolls (Essence + Aria) against her target\u2019s Resolve. If successful, the target hears the refrain at full volume, sustaining a penalty to all rolls equal to half the weapon\u2019s <b>Aria</b> (rounded up) at the time of his turn, for as many turns as she maintains the link. If the roll fails, the target only hears the murmuring voice at the back of his mind; the roll repeats every turn the evocation is maintained until successful.<br /> <br /> This evocation can target multiple foes, with the cost per turn increasing by 2 motes for every additional target.<br /> <br /> This evocation can target battlegroups, with the cost multiplied by Size (minimum 3m).</div> </div> </div> </div>This... seems like a fairly weak Evocation to me. Essence + Aria starts out as 6 dice, and can't feasibly go above 10 in actual play (albeit 8 is more reasonable). This means anybody with a half-decent Resolve and an Excellency will basically never ever be threatened by it (despite the reroll per turn, which, I admit, is pretty nasty). I'd make it twice the character's actual Aria level, meaning it has a decent chance to hit even Resolve 5 over the course of multiple turns (unless your opponent uses Excellency/WP, but it's still a net win for you if they have to boost their defense by more than 1, given that it only costs 3m to maintain).<br /> <br /> Now, I admit, the consequences of Haunting Refrain actually succeeding are incredibly nasty (ongoing -3 penalty for basically <i>forever</i>), but the balancing factor really shouldn't be &quot;it's never going to succeed against anybody important enough to warrant stacking penalties on&quot;. On the other hand, if it has a decent chance of success, &quot;once it succeeds, you're stuck with the effect&quot; is probably too powerful. So make it a reroll per turn, regardless of success.<br /> <br /> &quot;Duration: Indefinite&quot; is probably overkill (besides, the effect is basically meaningless outside of combat, where Initiative isn't tracked and therefore Aria levels can't be determined). Make it &quot;one scene&quot;.<br /> <br /> Battle groups, in my experience, are never strong enough for anybody to want to stack penalties on them, so the effect would be useless even if it wasn't grossly overpriced. Instead, make it do (Aria/2) dice of Magnitude damage each turn it's successful (as some soldiers are incapacitated by the cacophony or start fleeing), and keep the price a flat 3m.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll look at the others later today, but right now, duty calls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 06-23-2016, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T08:03:23-07:00","id":919713,"title":"","content":"Well, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar738_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"738\" data-vbnamecard=\"738\">Binary Phantom</a>, I decided to finish my Grand-Goremaul idea. I'm pretty sure it's only a 3-dot though. Hard to tell, the pinnacle evocation is pretty beefy, but not very flashy. This one is very shaky mechanically, so I expect some constructive feedback.<br /> <br /> I've really wanted to do something with the Moonlit Huntress evocation model. I'm not sure I succeeded, but it's at least a little unique.<br /> <br /> Once again, I can't be bothered to write fluff. I am ashamed.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Resilient Pillar (Moonsilver Grand-Goremaul ***)</span></span><br /> <br /> The Resilient Pillar is a Moonsilver Grand-Goremaul that always stands a hand taller than the exalt wielding it. A thick shaft of Wyldwood shifts and adjusts its length and width to suit the exalt attuned to it. At the peak, a smooth almost rounded sledge made of polished moonsilver sits ready to grow in an instant to deliver crushing blows to its enemies. The Grand-Goremaul has 2 hearthstone sockets along its shaft and a third in the side of the sledge.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Evocations of The Resilient Pillar</b></span><br /> A Solar or Lunar who attunes to The Resilient Pillar gains a benefit that changes with the flow of battle. At 5 or less initiative, the exalt may waive the initiative cost of a Full-Defense action. At 6-15 Initiative, the exalt ignores one point of onslaught penalty for every 5 initiative they have. At 16+ Initiative, the exalt gains a single non-charm die bonus to <b>Withering </b>attack rolls for every 6 Initiative they have..<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Adaptive Kata</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Until next action<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> The power of Moonsilver is protean and malleable, finding advantage in every situation. Activating Adaptive Kata allows the exalt to gain all three attunement benefits regardless of their Initiative until the start of their next action.<br /> <i>Author's Notes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A pretty basic effect, obviously based off of the Moonlit huntress. The Withering effect in the attunement bonus was a last-minute addon, but I wanted more than 2 effects. Since this doesn't grant initiative like Moonlit Huntress' single Evocation, I made it cheaper and lower essence. Can be adjusted.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Advantage Stance</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1m, +1m per 1i <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Adaptive Kata<br /> <br /> The Resilient Pillar is a massive weapon, but in the hands of a master, it moves and flows with easy, never making its master exert themselves too hard. Advantage Stance may only be used while the exalt is in Initiative Crash. This evocation may be used to supplement actions that cost Initiative, and replacing the Initiative cost with Essence. Examples of such actions include Smashing attacks, Disengage actions, or using Improvised weapons. Advantage Stance is not compatible with Decisive attacks or Gambits and does not allow the exalt to ignore the Initiative cost on Charms.<br /> <i>Author's Notes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I liked this evocation the best. Being able to change out motes for initiative to do special attacks and moves is good but doesn't seem broken. I'm not sure if it needs the Withering-only keyword. I just wanted to call out it won't let you ignore using Initiative with Decisive attacks and Gambits.<br /> It also JUST occurred to me that this evocation nullifies the usefulness of the 5 or less Initiative attunement bonus. Crap... I need a replacement for it I guess, because I HATE having powers that replace other powers.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Ascendant Power</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 10m, 1wp <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Advantage Stance<br /> <br /> The pinnacle evocation of The Resilient Pillar taps into the relentless power of Moonsilver, its unrelenting and overpowering nature. After successfully dealing a Decisive attack against a foe, the exalt may activate Ascendant Power to not reset to Base Initiative, effectively keeping all of their Initiative. This evocation may only be activated once per day, however using it always raises the exalt\u2019s anima as though they used Peripheral essence to activate it.<br /> <i>Author's Notes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I needed a capstone. I know this is hella strong. I tried to make it expensive to offset. I could also add a longer reset timer. I don't know. Open to thoughts.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T08:49:40-07:00","id":919739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919430#post919430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Hallowed Warcry<br /> Cost:</b> 3+m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Haunting Refrain<br /> <br /> The blade unleashes a mental roar into an enemy\u2019s mind, powered by the frustration of the wielder\u2019s struggling fate, in an attempt to disturb his mind and essence. The wielder rolls (Essence + Willpower + [Spent Motes \u2013 3]) against the target\u2019s Resolve; if successful, the target loses Initiative equal to the threshold successes, disoriented from the spirit\u2019s rage.<br /> <br /> Against foes already affected by <b>Haunting Refrain</b>, this roll receives 1 automatic success, and instead of a single shout, the song instantly and momentarily crescendos before reverting to its normal effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>In its current form, this is way OP. Since there is no upper limit on the motes that can be spent, and successes translate to lost Initiative on a 1-for-1 basis, it can, theoretically, insta-crash almost anyone. Just go with flat (Essence+WP); at WP 10, it has a good chance to hit even Resolve 5, especially if the wielder has high Essence and managed to get Haunting Refrain off the ground.<br /> <br /> Reasons why this Evocation is better than you probably think it is (especially for your player):<br /> - It keys off WP, which any self-respecting Single Point stylist wants to max, because all of their defenses and almost all of their damage boosters use it.<br /> - You can use it before an attack enhanced by Fatal Stroke Flash to effectively gain decisive damage equal to the lost Initiative.<br /> - It can also be used before a big enemy decisive in conjunction with the passive bonus of Sotto Voce, which is a great way to get an opponent to waste all of their Initiative (if the attack is absorbed by Hardness, they still reset to base).<br /> <br /> All in all, I'm very pleased with this one. Lots of neat synergies with Single Point without taking anything away from a regular melee guy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919430#post919430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dissonant Revelation<br /> Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Clash, Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Hallowed Warcry<br /> <br /> As foes hear its song, the spirit hears their thoughts. When an opponent targeted by Haunting Refrain attempts to strike the wielder, the blade may break from its song to reveal the enemy intent to her through ethereal guidance; if allowed, the spirit will push the wielder into a reflexive Clash attack. With the combined force of song and steel, the attack benefits from bonus dice equal to half the <b>Aria</b> level, rounded up.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with this Evocation is that it effectively obviates Horizon-Swallowed Star Flash. It's cheaper (5m 1WP vs 8m 1WP) and more reliable (not only is it Uniform, allowing the wielder to benefit from Accuracy, but it also receives up to +3 bonus dice from Aria). The only thing it doesn't have is the ability to steal Initiative, but that's also slightly redundant with Hallowed Warcry.<br /> <br /> I'd make it a Supplemental effect that lets the wielder spend Initiative to gain non-Charm bonus dice on a Clash up to half her Aria levels on a 2-for-1 basis, essentially allowing them to reduce the damage of decisive clashes in order to maximize their chances of actually succeeding at them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919430#post919430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Crescendo of the Reckoning Star<br /> Cost:</b> 8m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Clash<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Dissonant Revelation<br /> <br /> When steel strikes steel, the spirit\u2019s voice pierces Creation with unshakeable determination, tearing away any destiny woven against the spirit\u2019s wielder. At the moment of a Clash attack, the blade\u2019s voice is projected outward for all to hear in an ear-piercing battlecry that shakes the air itself. This acts as an undodgeable, unblockable <b>withering</b> attack against all enemies within Close range, dealing (Essence + Willpower + Aria) in damage dice.<br /> <br /> This is calculated against the Clashing foe first, with the gained Initiative going toward the Clash itself if <b>decisive</b>. All other initiative gain is completed after the Clash.<br /> <br /> This evocation ends <b>Haunting Refrain</b> for all targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting effect, but I wonder how often you're going to have multiple opponents at Close range. I'd have it reach at least up to Short (especially for an 8m cost).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, 15-20 unavoidable withering damage on multiple opponents, holy crap. Unless your opponent is wearing really heavy armor, their Clash is going to hit like a wet fart even if they succeed (assuming it's decisive). Not to mention all the Initiative you farm off their friends right after resetting. Maybe confining it to Close range isn't a half bad idea (even though it's hardly the air-shaking sonic boom if it barely affects one range band).<br /> <br /> I genuinely have no idea how balanced it is. It's extremely powerful and versatile, and actually not at all that expensive considering what it does. Needs playtesting before I can say anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T10:11:30-07:00","id":919787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919713#post919713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar738_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"738\" data-vbnamecard=\"738\">Binary Phantom</a>, I decided to finish my Grand-Goremaul idea. I'm pretty sure it's only a 3-dot though. Hard to tell, the pinnacle evocation is pretty beefy, but not very flashy. This one is very shaky mechanically, so I expect some constructive feedback.<br /> <br /> I've really wanted to do something with the Moonlit Huntress evocation model. I'm not sure I succeeded, but it's at least a little unique.<br /> <br /> Once again, I can't be bothered to write fluff. I am ashamed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds an awful lot like the Ruyi Bang from the story of Sun Wukong. I'm sure you could riff off of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919713#post919713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Advantage Stance</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1m, +1m per 1i <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Adaptive Kata<br /> <br /> The Resilient Pillar is a massive weapon, but in the hands of a master, it moves and flows with easy, never making its master exert themselves too hard. Advantage Stance may only be used while the exalt is in Initiative Crash. This evocation may be used to supplement actions that cost Initiative, and replacing the Initiative cost with Essence. Examples of such actions include Smashing attacks, Disengage actions, or using Improvised weapons. Advantage Stance is not compatible with Decisive attacks or Gambits and does not allow the exalt to ignore the Initiative cost on Charms.<br /> <i>Author's Notes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I liked this evocation the best. Being able to change out motes for initiative to do special attacks and moves is good but doesn't seem broken. I'm not sure if it needs the Withering-only keyword. I just wanted to call out it won't let you ignore using Initiative with Decisive attacks and Gambits.<br /> It also JUST occurred to me that this evocation nullifies the usefulness of the 5 or less Initiative attunement bonus. Crap... I need a replacement for it I guess, because I HATE having powers that replace other powers.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I would contend that this Evocation and the attunement bonus don't really interact, as the bonus would be taken into account before this power would come into play. BTW: are the attunement bonuses cumulative or separate? If they were separate, this power would be useful in keeping up the pressure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919713#post919713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Ascendant Power</b></span><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 10m, 1wp <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Advantage Stance<br /> <br /> The pinnacle evocation of The Resilient Pillar taps into the relentless power of Moonsilver, its unrelenting and overpowering nature. After successfully dealing a Decisive attack against a foe, the exalt may activate Ascendant Power to not reset to Base Initiative, effectively keeping all of their Initiative. This evocation may only be activated once per day, however using it always raises the exalt\u2019s anima as though they used Peripheral essence to activate it.<br /> <i>Author's Notes</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I needed a capstone. I know this is hella strong. I tried to make it expensive to offset. I could also add a longer reset timer. I don't know. Open to thoughts.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I would definitely avoid resets based on building Initiative. Perhaps tying it to successfully Shifting an opponent would be suitably difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T10:34:39-07:00","id":919802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919787#post919787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would contend that this Evocation and the attunement bonus don't really interact, as the bonus would be taken into account before this power would come into play. BTW: are the attunement bonuses cumulative or separate? If they were separate, this power would be useful in keeping up the pressure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well because the attunement bonuses occur in different ranges of Initiative, they can't occur at the same time without using the opening Evocation. I'm not sure if that's what you meant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919787#post919787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would definitely avoid resets based on building Initiative. Perhaps tying it to successfully Shifting an opponent would be suitably difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're talking about Initiative Shift where you crash the person who crashed you, that's very hard to pull off for sure. So what, it would have to do Initiative Shift, roll your join battle and do a Decisive attack and then get to keep your Initiative? I'd feel somewhat inclined to reduce the cost at that point, as that's pretty hard to pull off. But maybe...<br /> <br /> Yeah I wasn't big on this one. I was tempted to change it to similar to Moonlit Huntress and just have it grants a bunch of Initiative (instead of having anything to do with a Reset) but I don't know, I just didn't like that idea. <br /> <br /> What if I took it a totally different direction? If you crash an opponent you can spend this huge cost to roll join battle and gain that initiative? No, that's probably way too strong. I feel like this last evocation needs a big rework.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your feedback!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T11:26:26-07:00","id":919832,"title":"","content":"I need to write this out to get the balance right. What if <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919713#post919713\">Ascendant Power</a> instead worked like this:<br /> Activate with a Decisive attack to allow an immediate secondary followup Decisive attack against the same target with a damage pool equal to half of the Initiative pool of the previous attack. After the second attack resolution, the exalt is Crashed to -5 Initiative (this includes the penalty for self-crashing). The Break bonus is granted to the target if they survive, or the nearest applicable foe if they do not.<br /> <br /> So functionally it's a big chance to kill one target, but it crashes you... badly. I don't know if that's an appealing option or not, but it makes it feel big with a tradeoff. I'm just spitballing here. I hate having an unfinished artifact...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T11:39:29-07:00","id":919839,"title":"","content":"Thanks a ton, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3443_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3443\" data-vbnamecard=\"3443\">aluminiumtrioxid</a> ! I'veadapted most of your comments pretty much word for word.<b> On Haunting Refrain: </b>I'd honestly meant it only for battle, so I don't know why I didn't just put &quot;One Scene&quot;...<br /> <br /> However, a couple questions regarding the latter two.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Dissonant Revelation</b>: I definitely don't want to make another charm useless, so thank you for point that out. Still, I'd like to keep the reflexive Clash somehow for a non-SPSIVS user. I've gone ahead and made it <b>Withering-only</b>, changed it to 2m per non-Charm success up to half Aria (round up), and added that the wielder only gains half the Initiative the opponent loses post-Clash. Is this reasonable? Maybe if I add an initiative cost...<br /> <br /> If not, and I take the Supplemental route, could I tack on a permanent bit that delaying actions only causes -1 initiative loss instead of -2?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>RE: Crescendo of the Reckoning Star</b>: I've combined your comments for this one.<ul><li>I've removed the Aria dice, and replaced them with auto-successes equal to half-Aria rounded <b><i>down</i></b> (so it can be 0). This part is a lateral step, but in addition:</li> <li>I've added that enemies in the Close band (that are NOT the Clash target) can add their Essence to their Soak (Since it is, effectively, an essence-shout).</li> <li>Having added that it goes up to Short range, I also said that enemies at Short range can add their Essence+3 to Soak.</li> <li>Finally, I've put in that only initiative lost by the Clash-target is actually gained by the wielder; all other initiative is simply lost.</li> </ul><br /> Does this feel more balanced?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T12:20:11-07:00","id":919857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919839#post919839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Dissonant Revelation</b>: I definitely don't want to make another charm useless, so thank you for point that out. Still, I'd like to keep the reflexive Clash somehow for a non-SPSIVS user. I've gone ahead and made it <b>Withering-only</b>, changed it to 2m per non-Charm success up to half Aria (round up), and added that the wielder only gains half the Initiative the opponent loses post-Clash. Is this reasonable? Maybe if I add an initiative cost...</div> </div> </div> </div>So it now costs 5 +2/success motes 1 wp; I guess that's reasonable. It all but ensures that your character will win the clash, but at a steep cost both in motes and Initiative. Sounds about right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919839#post919839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Crescendo of the Reckoning Star</b>: I've combined your comments for this one.<ul><li>I've removed the Aria dice, and replaced them with auto-successes equal to half-Aria rounded <b><i>down</i></b> (so it can be 0). This part is a lateral step, but in addition:</li> <li>I've added that enemies in the Close band (that are NOT the Clash target) can add their Essence to their Soak (Since it is, effectively, an essence-shout).</li> <li>Having added that it goes up to Short range, I also said that enemies at Short range can add their Essence+3 to Soak.</li> <li>Finally, I've put in that only initiative lost by the Clash-target is actually gained by the wielder; all other initiative is simply lost.</li> </ul><br /> Does this feel more balanced?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T12:47:50-07:00","id":919875,"title":"","content":"Thanks so much!<br /> <br /> One last query: after thinking about that permanent bit about delayed action costs, I think that might be better for the <b>Trionfante</b> (15+) bonus. So how does this sound?<br /> <br /> <b>Trionfante</b>(15+ Initiative): The character may delay their action at no cost in preparation for a Clash; if they do not Clash by the end of the round, they lose the -2 Initiative as normal.<br /> <br /> (Note: was originally &quot;Aim + Full Defense - costs&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T12:52:44-07:00","id":919880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=919875#post919875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks so much!<br /> <br /> One last query: after thinking about that permanent bit about delayed action costs, I think that might be better for the <b>Trionfante</b> (15+) bonus. So how does this sound?<br /> <br /> <b>Trionfante</b>(15+ Initiative): The character may delay their action at no cost in preparation for a Clash; if they do not Clash by the end of the round, they lose the -2 Initiative as normal.<br /> <br /> (Note: was originally &quot;Aim + Full Defense - costs&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it's no secret I don't like Shining Ice Mirror's bonus all that much, so I'm fully in support of this change.<br /> <br /> Just please note that benefiting from these passive bonuses should come with an extra attunement cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T12:57:08-07:00","id":919883,"title":"","content":"Right, I added the additional cost as you suggested--all edits are (or should be) on the original artifact post now. As redundant as this might be getting, a million thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T06:54:26-07:00","id":920337,"title":"","content":"Updated Charm of the Weasel based on feedback. Pinnacle evocation may still need some work. For clarification this is not armor, it was based on the idea of an utilitarian artifact based on a hearthstone bracer. <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Charm of the Weasel</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Origin</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Many years ago a lunar craftsman became enamored with the humble weasel and the way this unique and fascinating predator worked. From his fascination came the charm of the weasel a trinket inspired by the weasel and a gift for the lunar craftsman's night caste lover. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Appearance</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This artifact takes the form of a moonsilver armband shaped as a coiled weasel wrapping around the wearers arm. The artifact has a single hearthstone socket between the front claws of the weasel making it appear as if the the artifact is holding onto the hearthstone. Additionally the artifacts eyes change color to mimic any hearthstone that is inserted into it. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Attunement </u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As with most hunters the weasel can see its prey long before the prey see them any exalt attuned to the charm of the weasel gain +1 on all visual awareness checks and have no difficulty seeing in anything other than pure darkness. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Evocations:</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prey of the Weasel</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Once the Exalt locates her quarry she chases it until it is hers</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The weasel is a predator that shuns the tactic of stalk and ambush in favor of flush and chase. The exalt may reflexively activate this evocation to mark her prey, be it a person, animal, or item. Once the prey has been mark the exalt will chase it down till it\u2019s hers. The exalt gets +1 non-charm bonus on all tracking rolls. Should the exalt locate their target while this evocation is active they receive +3 initiative a join battle action to attack her target or +1 non-charm bonus to any larceny action to acquire her target.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special rules: The exalt must see, hear, or smell her prey to activate this evocation and the sense used will determine the difficulty of tracking. Also the exalt must continue tracking until she finds her prey, if she loses the trail or gives up the evocation ends and the prey is no longer marked.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bones of Rubber</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Prey of the Weasel</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Allows the exalt to squeeze through any opening that they can get their head through</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The weasel is a predator that\u2019s path cannot easily be barred. This evocation allows the exalt to channel the ability of the weasel to fit through any opening which they can get their head through. One this evocation is active should the exalt be able to move her head through an opening her body flows and adjusts to make it through the space as well. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Changing one\u2019s Coat</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m, 1wp</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Indefinite</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Bones of Rubber</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Allows the Exalt to change her outward appearance to blend in with her surroundings </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Just as the weasel changes its coat from brown to white so can the exalted. An exalt using this evocation can change their outward appearance to blend in with the scenery. This evocation allows the exalt to change the color, texture, and feel of their clothing. Additionally the exalt can affect their skin and hair as well changing them to blend with their surroundings. These effects provide for +1 non-charm bonus to all stealth checks when not moving Once the commitment to this evocations lapses the exalts appearance returns to normal </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special rules: Should the charm of the weasel have the chameleon stone socketed into it the following additional effects are available. The evocation allows access to the hearthstones innate ability and expands upon it. The exalt may now change not only their hair, eye, and skin color but also their clothing and equipment to blend into any situation. With the chameleon stone the exalt receives +1 non-charm bonus to all stealth checks and larceny checks for disguise.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9195-shadowmage","name":"ShadowMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9195_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T07:00:43-07:00","id":920341,"title":"","content":"So this might be cheating a bit as I am a player in Binary Phantoms Game and know the player and character he wants this for but here is my attempt at a 4 dot grand goremaul. If anyone has seen log horizon I took inspiration for two evocations form there and the last one is obviously a reference to x-men. I'd appreciate any feedback on balancing this or ideas on fixing them if they are broken. <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dissuaders Bulwark</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact: Orialchum and White Jade Grand Goremaul</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Origin</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is a known fact that when you start an ambitious project things don\u2019t always turn out the way one would expect. Such is the case with Dissuaders Bulwark. In the high first age a Twilight artisan was commissioned by his circles Dawn to fashion him an impregnable shield. The twilight craftsmen at once started gathering materials from across creation, Shells from great sea beasts, Shards of the hardest crystal and white jade from the pole of earth itself. The craftsman tooled tireless, working day and night only taking a break during the hours of the early morning when the pure sunlight washed over his creation. When all was said and done the twilight was impressed with his work the finest he\u2019d ever done and presented it to the dawn but there was one issue. In his creative stupor the Artifact he created was not the shield requested but a Grand Goremaul. While taken back on the item put before her the dawn was in awe at the majesty and strength emanating from the weapon. Taking it in hand she could feel this weapon would protect her better than any shield and it served her well in many battles. Had Dissuaders Bulwark been with her when the hands of fate closed in on her circle during the usurpation her attackers may not have faired as well, but alas now Dissuader sleeps awaiting another soul to protect</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Appearance</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dissuaders Bulwark is a mighty Grand Goremaul Standing six feet high with a head two feet long and a foot in diameter. The weapon is an alloy of Orialchum and White Jade with a shaft wrapped in the hide of a long dead Behemoth and the pommel adorned in the shells of tortoises that call the pole of fire home. The head of Dissuaders Bulwark is fashioned of a castle atop a giant turtle with the head of the turtle agape with a giant rock in its mouth for the hammerhead and the tail as the spike. Where one would expect the eyes of the turtle two hearthstone sockets appear. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Attunement </u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m Any exalt who attunes to Dissuaders Bulwark for an additional two motes gain the defense benefit as if it was a medium Artifact Melee weapon and can add +1 to their parry</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost 6m: Any exalt who attunes to Dissuaders Bulwark for an additional six motes may take Defend Other actions at short range</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Evocations:</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anchor Howl</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 4m, 2i</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: 2 combat actions</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: The exalt who uses this evocation paints themselves as the target to anyone within long range and must be attacked or the attacker takes a penalty</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To protect those around themselves the exalt must sometime draw all attention on herself. Upon activation the exalts anima flashes to burning level drawing all eyes to her. This charm interacts with the exalts anima making it impossible to ignore her must attack her. Choosing to ignore the exalt and attack someone else incurs a 4 initiative penalty to the attacker. This charm lasts for three combat rounds and cannot be used again for 4 combat actions.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keystone of the Wall</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 6m</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins:Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Anchor Howl</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Slamming the ground the exalt sends ripples through the ground raising stone and earthen walls creating a funnel for all enemy combatants to the exalt</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes drawing attention to yourself is not enough and you must defend your allies. Upon activating this charm the exalt channels her essence into Dissuaders Bulwark and brings it down upon the ground in front of her. From the Point of impact fissures expand out and two walls of earth and stone erupt from the ground. Each wall is approximately 10 ft tall of sharp ragged stone and earth and should be treated as an environmental hazard of 1L/round difficulty 5 to move through. Each wall extends for approximately 3 range bands at 60 degrees from the exalt and leaves a 10 ft wide gap between them where the exalt stands.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Castle of Stone</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m, 6i</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Until next action</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Keystone of the Wall</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Once activated this evocation makes the exalt impervious to most damage but roots the exalt in place until his next round of combat</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the heat of combat it is sometimes necessary to find a moment to catch one's breath. When Caste of Stone is activated the exalt is routed in place and the her anima wraps around her making a protective shell. The exalt cannot move or be moved until her next action. She is treated as having a hardness of 20 and a soak of 20 till her next turn.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Juggernaut</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 10m, 1wp, 4i</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Perilous</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Action</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Guardian Wall</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: The exalt becomes a moving wall, nearly impervious to damage and unstoppable </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes defense is not enough and you must show the world why they should have been dissuaded in the first place. Upon activation of this charm the exalts essence infuses directly into her skin giving it a reddish brown color. Until her next action the exalt has the following stats Soak 20, Hardness 20, Strength 6, and Athletics 6. This charm can only be used once per combat.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9195-shadowmage","name":"ShadowMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9195_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T07:50:58-07:00","id":920370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowMage;n9203411[FONT=Arial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dissuaders Bulwark</span>[/FONT]<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact: Orialchum and White Jade Grand Goremaul</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Attunement </u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m Any exalt who attunes to Dissuaders Bulwark for an additional two motes gain the defense benefit as if it was a medium Artifact Melee weapon and can add +1 to their parry</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost 6m: Any exalt who attunes to Dissuaders Bulwark for an additional six motes may take Defend Other actions at short range</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the second effect, I hate the first. The Defense of +0 with Heavy Weapons is intentional for balance. Otherwise, it becomes the best weapon design in the game. Highest damage and highest defense. Personal opinion, I'd ditch the first and grant the second for the 2m of the first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowMage;n9203411[FONT=Arial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Evocations:</u></span>[/FONT]<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anchor Howl</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 4m, 2i</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: 2 combat actions</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: The exalt who uses this evocation paints themselves as the target to anyone within long range and must be attacked or the attacker takes a penalty</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To protect those around themselves the exalt must sometime draw all attention on herself. Upon activation the exalts anima flashes to burning level drawing all eyes to her. This charm interacts with the exalts anima making it impossible to ignore her must attack her. Choosing to ignore the exalt and attack someone else incurs a 4 initiative penalty to the attacker. This charm lasts for three combat rounds and cannot be used again for 4 combat actions.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>This power is cool but needs some clarification. There should be an effective range for this power, as it is, it seems to imply everybody everywhere. I personally would give it a range of Medium, but it could feasibly include anyone that can visually see the exalt with hostile intent. You also say it lasts for 3 combat rounds in the text, but list the duration as 2 combat actions in the Duration. I wouldn't describe anything as combat actions, it's either Rounds or Turns. Otherwise, a cool taunt power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowMage;n9203411[FONT=Arial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keystone of the Wall[/FONT]<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 6m</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins:Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Anchor Howl</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Slamming the ground the exalt sends ripples through the ground raising stone and earthen walls creating a funnel for all enemy combatants to the exalt</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes drawing attention to yourself is not enough and you must defend your allies. Upon activating this charm the exalt channels her essence into Dissuaders Bulwark and brings it down upon the ground in front of her. From the Point of impact fissures expand out and two walls of earth and stone erupt from the ground. Each wall is approximately 10 ft tall of sharp ragged stone and earth and should be treated as an environmental hazard of 1L/round difficulty 5 to move through. Each wall extends for approximately 3 range bands at 60 degrees from the exalt and leaves a 10 ft wide gap between them where the exalt stands.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Feet are not used to describe anything in combat in 3e, so adjust your sizes to Range bands so that characters can meaningfully interact with them. Also, how does one &quot;move through&quot; a solid wall of earth, even at Difficulty 5?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowMage;n9203411[FONT=Arial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Castle of Stone[/FONT]<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m, 6i</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Until next action</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Keystone of the Wall</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Once activated this evocation makes the exalt impervious to most damage but roots the exalt in place until his next round of combat</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the heat of combat it is sometimes necessary to find a moment to catch one's breath. When Caste of Stone is activated the exalt is routed in place and the her anima wraps around her making a protective shell. The exalt cannot move or be moved until her next action. She is treated as having a hardness of 20 and a soak of 20 till her next turn.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That hardness level is absurdly big. It would be a huge power if it was 10. If it removed the ability to attack as well I'd buy it but as it stands it just describes being unable to take movement actions, but it also makes them immune to knockback? If you stick with this power, it is undercosted by some essence and a willpower (at least the willpower).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowMage;n9203411[FONT=Arial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Juggernaut[/FONT]<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 10m, 1wp, 4i</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Perilous</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Action</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Guardian Wall</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: The exalt becomes a moving wall, nearly impervious to damage and unstoppable </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes defense is not enough and you must show the world why they should have been dissuaded in the first place. Upon activation of this charm the exalts essence infuses directly into her skin giving it a reddish brown color. Until her next action the exalt has the following stats Soak 20, Hardness 20, Strength 6, and Athletics 6. This charm can only be used once per combat.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>2 things on this one. 1, I think there may end up some unintended side-effects of strictly raising attributes with this power. If the intent is to increase feats of strength, you can more specifically call that out by saying (Sets base die pool for feats of strength to 12 and minimum strength to 6 for purposes of feats of strength). Otherwise, add some Increasing Strength Exercise and that melee multiattack charm and goodbye everything for that action.<br /> 2, this power feels a lot like an upgraded version of the previous power. I can see the difference, but it <i>feels</i> similar. This might just be a personal preference rather than something actually wrong with it, so feel free to disregard point number 2 here, but it feels like not as much variety.<br /> <br /> I will say that it's definitely a juggernaut of an artifact. And you have a very healthy approach to costing evocations, don't lose that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T23:50:07-07:00","id":921875,"title":"","content":"So I figured out a concept, but I don't know how to finish it off. Any advice would be greatly appreciated.<br /> <br /> Ring of Power (Artifact 3-N/A)<br /> Any who take hold of one of these rings automatically gains an intimacy of a strength defined by the power of the ring which endures as long as the ring is in their keeping. Artifact 3 rings bestow a minor intimacy, 4 dot a moderate, 5 dot a major, and N/A a defining. These intimacies are selected from among those of the ring maker at the appropriate strength at the time of its creation and cannot be changed. In all respects they are treated as a natural intimacy, not as a form of mind control or external influence. To the bearer they seem natural, though those radically opposed to the character of the bearer or which clash with an existing intimacy of equal or greater strength may be resisted. This occurs even if the artifact is not attuned.<br /> <br /> Each ring contains a number of evocations equal to their artifact level, the first of which is always available to a bearer even if they are not attuned. Any evocations past the first require attunement.<br /> <br /> The primary power of a ring is to allow attuned bearers to perform a number of sorcerous workings without exhausting their own energies in the process. To that end, each contains a reservoir of experience points which may be used for no other purpose and which can only be used in ways appropriate to the intimacy the ring imposes. Thus a ring dedicated to amassing wealth could assist in workings which caused gold to literally multiply or traders to always give the bearer better deals but could not be used to cause a river to run clean despite defilement upstream. Each ring contains a number of experience points equal to its artifact rating times 10. When performing such a working, the attuned bearer may use the dicepool of the creator or their own, whichever is greater This power requires attunement.<br /> <br /> Finally, rings grant power according to the nature of their bearers. It allows users to perform workings up to the level of sorcery they can natively learn but only for workings which draw from the xp of the ring and motivated by its intimacy. Mortals are thus limited to terrestrial works, gods to celestial, etc. This power requires attunement.<br /> <br /> <br /> The workings performed with the power of a ring are somewhat more fragile than normal and can be undone. Should a ring be destroyed they will immediately end, and if a new user becomes attuned they may unravel the workings of previous bearers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T02:01:04-07:00","id":921902,"title":"","content":"This is my first time making stuff for Ex3, so I have no idea what I'm doing. The idea behind it is to have a weapon that follows Wuxing principles of Overcoming and Generating, but in Creation's terms. Inspired, partly, by the Sword of Gou Jian, which is surprisingly small. <hr /><i><b>The Imperial Daiklave, the Five-Jade Blade (\u7687\u5927\u528d,\u4e94\u7389\u5203)</b></i><br /> Jibei is known as the City of the Sword, and has been known that for ages. The title has always been ceremonial and metaphorical, used to denote the metropolis\u2019 martial arts and culture. Always, that is, until the time of Sword Prince Gensuji and the Imperial Daiklave.<br /> <br /> Also known as the Five-Jade Blade, the Imperial Daiklave was forged at the behest of the Scarlet Empress, a commission of great care and meaning. As Jibei was one of the first cities that would bend knee to her glorious regime, the weapon is a symbol of unity, brotherhood, completion, wisdom, understanding, and universal harmony.<br /> <br /> Five feet long and four inches wide, the Five-Jade Blade is a simple no-frills straight-sword forged the style common in the Spring-And-Autumn Period of the Shogunate. The crossguard is shining steel, etched with a stylized dragon\u2019s face. The hilt - also of steel - is wrapped in wire, and carved into the base of the pommel is a pentacle. The blade itself is an alloy of equal parts red, black, blue, green, black, and white jade. Each jade is an intricate trace of lines in the metal, leaving the blade a brilliant blaze of multicolor. Stamped into one side of the blade, near the base, are five characters, the names of the elements in Old Realm. On the other side are another eight words, also in Old Realm; <i>\u201cSword Emperor, Five Jades, For Sword Prince\u2019s Use.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Legend has it that the Imperial Daiklave can, in the right hands, awaken to any and all elemental evocations, possibly duplicating the powers of such storied weapons as Spring Razor, Shining Ice Mirror, or even the Volcano Cutter. But for now, the Imperial Daiklave\u2019s only known traits are to use one element to encourage or destroy another, in accordance with the elemental cycles.<br /> <br /> The Imperial Daiklave has two hearthstone sockets, both in the crossguard\u2019s \u201ceyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Imperial Daiklave</b><br /> Solars and Dragon-Blooded who attune to the Imperial Daiklave awaken two evocations for free from both the Harmonious or Impeded trees, and may pay 1 willpower to reset all Imperial Daiklave evocations; Dragon-Blooded may also pay 5 motes to reset any one of the Imperial Daiklave\u2019s evocations. Other exalts awaken one evocation for free.<br /> All free evocations are based on caste/aspect associations as a default, such as Air Aspects taking \u2018<b>Air Freezes Water</b>\u2019 or No Moon Lunars taking \u2018<b>Water Freezes Wood</b>\u2019. However, characters may take others if the Storyteller accepts player arguments to the contrary.<br /> <br /> <b>Default Aspect and Caste Associations</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 700px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Aspect</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Solar</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Abyssal</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Lunar</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Sidereal</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Liminal</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Infernal</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Air</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Eclipse</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Moonshadow</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Changing Moon</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Journeys</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Breath</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Scourges</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Earth</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Zenith</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Midnight</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Endings</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Soil</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Slayer</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Fire</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dawn</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Dusk</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Full Moon</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Battles</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Flesh</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Malefactor</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Water</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Night</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Day</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">No Moon</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Secrets</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Blood</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Defiler</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wood</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Twilight</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Daybreak</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Serenity</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Marrow</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Fiend</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <b><i>(Element 1) (Impedes) (Element 2) </i></b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> None; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> Once per scene, if in combat with an opponent of an impeding element (as per the evocation\u2019s title), the Exalt may use a free full Melee or straight-sword-based Martial Arts Excellency to enhance her attack or defenses.<br /> This evocation is a \u201cgeneric\u201d version of the Impeding tree of evocations, and may be taken multiple times, up to 5. The third and fourth evocation in the tree has an Essence minimum of 2. The fifth evocation in the tree has an Essence minimum of 3.<br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> From where the Exalt starts, they must then awaken the next evocation in the line, until they reach the end. The cycle and evocation titles are: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 700px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i><b>Fire Consumes Wood</b></i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i><b>Wood Covers Earth</b></i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i><b>Earth Blocks Air</b></i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i><b>Air Freezes Fire</b></i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i><b>Water Drowns Fire</b></i></td> </tr> </table></div> Evocations can only be awakened in battle. Dragon-blooded may spar with Dragon-blooded of the proper Aspects. Other Exalts must fight other Exalts with their lives on the line.<br /> <br /> <i><b>(Element 1) (Harmonizes) (Element 2) </b></i><br /> <b>Cost:</b> None; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> Once per scene, if fighting alongside a character with a harmonizing element (as per the evocation\u2019s title) of up to short range, the Exalt may grant them a free full Melee or straight-sword-based Martial Arts Excellency to enhance his attack or defenses.<br /> This evocation is a \u201cgeneric\u201d version of the Harmonizing tree of evocations, and may be taken multiple times, up to 5. The third and fourth evocation in the tree has an Essence minimum of 2. The fifth evocation in the tree has an Essence minimum of 3.<br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> From where the Exalt starts, they must then awaken the next evocation in the line, until they reach the end. The cycle and evocation titles are: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 700px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i><b>Wood Refreshes Air</b></i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i><b>Air Fans Fire</b></i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b><i>Fire Renews Earth</i></b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i><b>Earth Channels Water</b></i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i><b>Water Feeds Wood</b></i></td> </tr> </table></div> Evocations can only be awakened in battle. Dragon-blooded may spar alongside Dragon-Blooded of the proper Aspects. Other Exalts must fight alongside other Exalts, with both their lives on the line. <hr />I'm also thinking of a &quot;five elements as one&quot; evocation, but I'm not sure how to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11538,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","user":"kingcrackers","date":". 06-27-2016, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T19:44:14-07:00","id":922379,"title":"","content":"My Night Caste is designed with a strong Assassin's Creed theme running through her, and part of that is having Hidden-Blade-Meets-Antikythera-Mechanism artifacts. Since she recently completed her first Favor for the god who gave them to her, it's now time to unlock her second evocation...<br /> <br /> ...which I hadn't designed ahead of time.<br /> <br /> So, here's my first draft.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>MARVELOUS CLOCKWORK BRACERS</b><br /> The work of the crafting-god Vincible Coil, these paired armbands are a wonderland of interlocking gears and pulleys in alchemically reinforced brass and bronze. Designed to cover the entire forearm from wrist to elbow, and to be easily concealed beneath any but the tightest sleeves, their undersides hide razored blades within retractable armatures. Spring-loaded to deploy with lethal force in an instant, and with essence-triggered hinges that can turn them to be used as ordinary knives, they put the tools of murder instantly at their wearer's hand. Each bracer also has a hearthstone socket, built into its outer surfaces near the elbow.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Bracers</b><br /> When attuned and worn, the bracers' wearer may spend 4m to activate their blades trigger mechanisms, gaining the ability to deploy and retract them reflexively for one scene. The blades are light artifact weapons with the Lethal, Worn, and Concealable tags, and the user may choose from one deployment to the next between the Brawl OR Melee tags. They may be used as style weapons for any Martial Arts style using knives or katars.<br /> <br /> <b>Grapple Launcher</b><br /> Cost: 2m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Archery<br /> Duration: Instant (Indefinite)<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> This evocation adds a spring-loaded launcher to the Bracers which is capable of propelling a dart and line out to Medium range. The head of the dart is enchanted to bond with inanimate material and is incapable of interacting with living flesh, but will flawlessly anchor itself to a living tree or all common architectural substances, as well as to clothing or armor. The line may be severed by any lethal attack, but is otherwise sturdy enough to bear the weight of a single person.<br /> <br /> <b>Switching Brackets</b><br /> Cost: 1m Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Grapple Launcher<br /> <br /> This evocation modifies the mountings of the Bracers' grapples and blades to the same standard, and adds a mechanism to allow them to be swapped. Using it, their wearer may fire the blades as light artifact Archery weapons with the Crossbow tag in place of Grapple Launcher's usual anchoring effect, or anchor herself to a given surface for as long as she chooses without requiring the usual standards of athletics and endurance.<br /> <br /> <b>Feathered Winch</b><br /> Cost: 3m Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: Instant (Scene)<br /> Prerequisites: Switching Brackets<br /> <br /> This evocation gives the Bracers' master finer control over the powered winch that retracts the line fired by Grapple Launcher, allowing her to automatically set it at a certain desired length, and to play them in and out at will for the rest of the scene. A wielder trained in the use of the rope dart, fighting chain, garrote, sling, or other appropriately flexible weapon may use the resulting weighted lines as such.<br /> <br /> <b>Automatic Magazine</b><br /> Cost: - Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: -<br /> Prerequisites: Switching Brackets<br /> <br /> This evocation adds a ring of additional mounting slots to the Bracers, allowing the Switching Brackets to load, and the Grapple Launcher and deployment gears to fire, any suitable small item, attachment, or alternate blade that the Bracers' owner can fit into the slots.<br /> <br /> <b>Redundant Controls</b><br /> Cost: 6m Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Feathered Winch, Automatic Magazine<br /> <br /> As originally designed, the Marvelous Clockwork Bracers could only accept one stream of essence from their wearer at a time, serving as both power source and control mechanism. This evocation modifies them so that each bracer can accept its own, separate stream, letting them be used in concert and allowing the wearer to take two actions involving the Bracers (Any of firing a grapple, making a withering attack, or making a decisive attack, resolved in that order). Double decisive attacks add an additional instance of the wielder's base initiative to their initiative pool, then divide their initiative evenly between the two simultaneous attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T19:55:29-07:00","id":922384,"title":"","content":"I have another artifact idea for a friend, but I really don't want to take away from the above discussions either; mine is literally just a small conversion, and I'd simply like to know if it's plausibly balanced or not.<br /> <br /> The idea was to merge the <b>Belt of Shadow Walking</b> with the <b>Silken Armor</b>. The belt itself already has the &quot;evocations&quot; listed which are, effectively, an attunement bonus and an activated evocation, and the belt itself is 3-dots. The Silken Armor is 4-dots, but also actually, you know, gives benefits to defense.<br /> <br /> <b>So, the question:</b> if the Silken Armor has the &quot;free 3 Stealth dice&quot; as an attunement (say, for an additional +2 investment--or would it be less, since they're <b><i>not</i></b> non-Charm? Or is it automatically non-Charm because it's not an activated charm/evocation?) and the &quot;sink into shadows&quot; evocation (maintaining the 10m cost), would it still be a 4-dot artifact armor? Or should we say 5-dot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T15:32:39-07:00","id":922885,"title":"","content":"I would say that it'd still be a 4-dot artifact; 5-dots, to me, are things that, when you break them out, they're one of the defining elements of the situation - they matter on the <i>strategic</i> level, as well as the tactical.<br /> <br /> As for what the dice count as, I'd go with their being charm dice, just because that is or at least should be the default assumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:05:02-07:00","id":923370,"title":"","content":"I wonder if this is too niche...<br /> <br /> <b>Faekiller (Orichalcum and Starmetal Powerbow - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> The Fair Folk have ever been a threat to Creation, for it stands for all that they hate: stability, definition, reality. The Exalted of the First Age knew this and forged numerous weapons to do battle with the shapeless hordes beyond Creation's rim. One of the least of these weapons is Faekiller, an orichalcum powerbow forged into the shape of a roaring lion's mouth, with fangs of starmetal and starmetal filaments running through the bowstring. Faekiller was wielded by Night's Prurient Scythe, an Eclipse Caste of the high First Age, and was placed in his tomb during the Usurpation. When the Fair Folk invaded Creation, a daring Sidereal whose name has never been successfully recorded broke into the tomb, daring the anger of the Solar's hungry ghost, and retrieved the bow. Where it has gone since that time, no one knows.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Faekiller</b><br /> When a Solar or Sidereal attunes to Faekiller, its attacks deal aggravated damage to Fair Folk. Note that this does not include Wyld mutants, but does include hobgoblins. For an additional 2m commitment, the bow deals aggravated damage to anyone it strikes. <br /> <br /> <b>Subverting the Pretense</b><br /> Cost: Varies; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The magic of the Fair Folk is nothing but dreams and whispers, no match for the harsh truth of reality. This Evocation may be activated when the wielder makes an attack against a target and that target uses Fair Folk defensive magic. The wielder may pay motes equal to the activation cost of the defensive magic to nullify that magic against this attack. If the magic has a duration greater than Instant, it functions normally against further attacks unless the wielder of Faekiller again pays the mote cost to nullify it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ignoring your Imagination</b><br /> Cost: 6m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Subverting the Pretense<br /> <br /> It is not enough to pretend to have armor or weapons. Against Faekiller, you must actually have them. An attack supplemented by this Evocation ignores all soak and Hardness from gossamer armor. Against Fair Folk, it is also unblockable by gossamer weapons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fate Becomes You</b><br /> Cost: 5m (+1W); Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant (One Scene)<br /> Prerequisites: Subverting the Pretense<br /> <br /> This Evocation represents the ultimate weapon against Fair Folk: Fate itself. When an attack supplemented by this Evocation hits a Fair Folk, that Fair Folk is temporarily hauled inside Fate and given a destiny. That destiny is almost always death at the hands of Faekiller's wielder, and so is very short. For the remainder of the scene, the wielder of Faekiller re-rolls 6s on Archery attacks made with Faekiller against that Fair Folk until 6s no longer appear. For an additional Willpower cost, that same destiny (and its resultant re-rolls) can be applied to <i>any</i> target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":".  More edits made 06-29-2016, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:35:27-07:00","id":923386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923370#post923370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if this is too niche...<br /> <br /> <b>Faekiller (Orichalcum and Starmetal Powerbow - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Faekiller</b><br /> When a Solar or Sidereal attunes to Faekiller, its attacks deal aggravated damage to Fair Folk. Note that this does not include Wyld mutants, but does include hobgoblins.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I would say it is a bit too niche, but I don't think it would be too difficult to adjust it into functionality. Basically, I am of the opinion that artifacts should be <b>useful</b> in a lot of situations, but <b>shine </b>in specific situations. That's where you have a power do Effect A, under basic Condition A (which is typically always), but under Condition B it's even a better or cheaper Effect B. All you're missing is Condition A, which is the baseline against everything. That can either go with scaling the power up against Condition B, or scaling it down for Condition A. <br /> <br /> So for the attunement bonus it could add the aggravated damage against everyone for an added reflexive cost or higher attunement. Alternatively, you could create a new initial evocation that treats your target as being Fae for the purposes of evocations of Faekiller. That is probably the simplest route and then you woudln't need to change anything else. It could be a Supplemental effect for 1m that you add onto every attack you want affected in that way, or it could be a Simple 4-5m that lasts for a whole scene. Add a Willpower to the cost if you want them to be treated as Fae for ALL effects and purposes for a scene (like from everyone). That'd be beefy, but possibly outside the scope of Essence 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923370#post923370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ignoring your Imagination</b><br /> Cost: 6m (+1W); Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> It is not enough to pretend to have armor or weapons. Against Faekiller, you must actually have them. An Archery attack with Faekiller supplemented by this Evocation ignores all soak and Hardness from gossamer armor. For an additional point of Willpower, it also ignores Parry Defenses derived from gossamer weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>It ignores the entire Parry defense or the Parry bonus from the weapon? This is a pretty powerful effect for Essence 1, although I know it's trying to balance by being niche. Especially if you go the route of adding an effect that lets it be used against other targets, I might swap this with Subverting the Pretense and maybe bump it up to Essence 2 (that's negotiable to me).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923370#post923370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Subverting the Pretense</b><br /> Cost: Varies; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Ignoring your Imagination<br /> <br /> The magic of the Fair Folk is nothing but dreams and whispers, no match for the harsh truth of reality. This Evocation may be activated when the wielder makes an Archery attack with Faekiller against a Fair Folk target and that target uses Fair Folk defensive magic. The wielder may pay motes equal to the activation cost of the defensive magic to nullify that magic against this attack. If the magic has a duration greater than Instant, it functions normally against further attacks unless the wielder of Faekiller again pays the mote cost to nullify it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923370#post923370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fate Becomes You</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant (One Scene)<br /> Prerequisites: Subverting the Pretense<br /> <br /> This Evocation represents the ultimate weapon against Fair Folk: Fate itself. When an Archery attack made using Faekiller and supplemented by this Evocation hits a Fair Folk, that Fair Folk is temporarily hauled inside Fate and given a destiny. That destiny is almost always death at the hands of Faekiller's wielder, and so is very short. For the remainder of the scene, the wielder of Faekiller re-rolls 6s on Archery attacks made with Faekiller against that Fair Folk until 6s no longer appear.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a habit of repeatedly specifying that an attack has to be used by this weapon AND enhanced by this evocation. You can probably cut out the first half of that sentence every time, because the book explains that Evocations of artifacts only enhance actions using those artifacts unless otherwise specified. It's redundant and you can save yourself a bit of rambling. ^_^<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I like this one. And it balances well when adjusted against non-fae as well.<br /> <br /> I think this can work just fine but I would definitely find a way to let it be useful outside of Wyld creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:43:59-07:00","id":923389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923386#post923386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I would say it is a bit too niche, but I don't think it would be too difficult to adjust it into functionality. <br /> <br /> I think this can work just fine but I would definitely find a way to let it be useful outside of Wyld creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Made some edits. Thoughts? Each Evocation now CAN be useful against non-Fae, but is unlikely to be. For example, Subverting the Pretense can be used against, say an Eclipse Caste who has learned Fair Folk magic. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:53:20-07:00","id":923392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923389#post923389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Made some edits. Thoughts? Each Evocation now CAN be useful against non-Fae, but is unlikely to be. For example, Subverting the Pretense can be used against, say an Eclipse Caste who has learned Fair Folk magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm, it's still too niche for me, but it's probably functional now for open consumption. My distaste is that it's like having a sword that only is cool and magical when fighting in the water, but your game takes you into almost any direction that isn't the West and isn't near a lake. It makes it a mote commitment and a burden to carry around until the situation arises. Obviously, you could have a game set up that's going to ONLY take place in Wyld zones and then it's pretty much always useful. And I have no problem with artifacts that are poorly suited to some scenarios. But when there's odds that scenario could be 50% of the time or more, that's when it feels too niche for me. <br /> <br /> TL;DR is that I don't consider it broken for the game setting, but I wouldn't use it at my table until it was slightly less niche. But then, I probably talked myself into that mindset when I went ahead and wrote out that new opening evocation idea. <b>This is not me telling you that you have to go that route, I'm just single-minded sometimes about stuff</b>. ^_^<br /> <br /> Always a pleasure to see some of your stuff. I do notice you like to stick in the very low Essence range. It's an interesting choice. Obviously it's because you want your character's weapon legend to be relevant sooner than 6 months into a game, which is totally valid. I should make more artifacts with more Essence 1 effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:55:33-07:00","id":923396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923392#post923392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Always a pleasure to see some of your stuff. I do notice you like to stick in the very low Essence range. It's an interesting choice. Obviously it's because you want your character's weapon legend to be relevant sooner than 6 months into a game, which is totally valid. I should make more artifacts with more Essence 1 effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Yeah, I prefer to keep my Artifacts rated at 3 and with Essence 1-2 effects, just because as Essence scales up, I am less and less confident about my ability to create appropriate effects, let alone balance them. Your feedback is invaluable, and I always look forward to your responses!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T05:44:08-07:00","id":923799,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So I finally got around to creating my first homebrew for 3e. Since I have no originality, I basically just made this a port of Reaper's powers from Overwatch into 3e. Which was... surprisingly easy, actually. Still not sure about the balance on a lot of this. Soul Fed Chambers might need to cost more, cause right now it's just completely better than Phantom Arrow Technique, and Death Blossom may need to be nerfed.<br /> <br /> Plasma Tongue Pieces(Artifact Flame Pieces)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Light Archery Weapon</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A pair of firedust weapons with ornate barrels of magical material and grips carved of magically smoothed wood. These are typically used as a pair, and purchasing this artifact gives you two of these weapons. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tags: Lethal, Archery (Short), Flame, Slow</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Flames of Reaping </u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(I need a better name) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Artifact 4 or 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Soulsteel Plasma Tongue Repeater</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Insert fluff text about Reaper-Expy here]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pair of Six Shot Revolver Flame Pieces with large barrels. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evocations</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Solar or Abyssal who attunes to these weapons awakens Feast of Souls at no experience cost. By paying 3 extra motes when attuning the Plasma Tongue Repeaters, the weapon gets one automatic success on all Decisive attacks. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">New Concept: Trivial Opponents</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A number of charms of this weapon refer to Trivial and Non-Trivial Opponents. A Trivial Opponent is an enemy who can be defeated or killed by a Withering attack, such as poorly trained soldiers, civilians, animals with no special abilities, or individuals in a battle group. Player Characters, Exalted and beings with Essence 3+ are never considered Trivial Opponents. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feast of Souls </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: - (2 Soul Charge per 1 HL) Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Flames of Reaping drink in the energies of their fallen foes. This charm creates a 10 point pool that holds Soul Charges, which is initially empty. Whenever the Wielder uses this weapon to kill a non-Trivial foe, he gains a Soul Charge. Soul Charges may be spent as Alternate costs for Evocations of this weapon, or they may be consumed as a Simple Action to heal the wielder at a rate of 1 lethal or bashing HL per 2 Soul Charges. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Soul Fed Chambers</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m; Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Until all 12 shots are fired. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: Feast of Souls</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the Reaper finds himself without ammunition, he does not need to worry. He simply tosses his weapons aside, drawing them again from his shadow, the empty flame pieces dissolving into cinders. This charm instantly reloads both weapons fully, and fire attacks made with Flames of Reaping using these dark firedust charges produce streaks of black flame. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Soul Borne Wraith </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m, 2i or 1 Soul Charge, 2i; Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword: Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Turn</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Soul Fed Chambers</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Abandoning solid shape, the Reaper becomes a being of smoke and cinders to transport himself away from, or toward his enemies. The character becomes intangible but not invisible, which renders him untargetable by attacks not supplemented by Spirit Cutting Attack and other charms which allow one to hit immaterial spirits, though he raises his Evasion stat against those charms by 2. The character cannot make attacks or other Combat Actions when this charm is active. Instead, he may take two move actions that turn, and may move from close to short range away from an opponent without using disengage action. This charm cannot be used again until three turns have passed. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wraith Step </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 7m, 1wp, 2 Soul Charges; Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: Soul Borne Wraith</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stepping between shadows, the Reaper hunts down those who would try to stay away from his flames. Once per scene, the user teleports up to long range anywhere within his line of sight as his movement action. This charm can be reset by successfully damaging a non-trivial opponent with a Decisive attack. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Death Blossom</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 10m, 1wp, All Soul Charges; Mins: Essence 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword: Decisive Only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: Wraith Step</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Laughing at the dead men surrounding him, the Reaper unleashes a storm of fire striking all around him, regardless of friend or foe. The Reaper makes a Decisive attack with these weapons, and adds the total number of Soul Charges he has to his Initiative when calculating damage. He applies his attack roll and damage roll to every character within medium range of him, regardless of direction or affiliation. When he has finished firing, he may activate Soul Fed Chambers for free. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11948-walker-of-the-yellow-path","user":"Walker of the Yellow Path","date":". 06-30-2016, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11948-walker-of-the-yellow-path","name":"Walker of the Yellow Path","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:53:01-07:00","id":924148,"title":"","content":"<b>First-Striking Dawn (Orichalcum and Moonsilver Infinite Chakram - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> Lovely was the Dawn<br /> Stippled in silver and gold<br /> Lethal as a kiss<br /> <br /> A razor-edged ring of orichalcum with the above haiku written on its edges in carefully crafted moonsilver, First-Striking Dawn was made for and named after a warrior-princess from the First Age, a Solar queen of great beauty and combat puissance. Yet, it never fit entirely properly in her hand, and though she wielded First-Striking Dawn with aplomb and dignity, she never unlocked all its Evocations, a fact that often disappointed her Lunar mate (and the craftsman of the weapon). When she was slain, the Lunar, Quick-Witted Aken, stole the weapon from her killers and fled with it into the Wyld. It has been passed down from generation to generation of Lunars, all of whom have failed to unlock its final secret. Whether that is some property of the weapon or merely lack of motivation on the part of its wielders is unknown.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of First-Striking Dawn</b><br /> When a Solar or Lunar attunes to First-Striking Dawn for one additional mote, she gains a +1 non-Charm die bonus on Join Battle rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Striking First</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> First-Striking Dawn is not a complex weapon, forged with a single goal. To that end, she seems to almost materialize in her wielder's hand in her moment of need. This Evocation can be used to enhance a Join Battle roll, allowing its bearer to re-roll 6s on that roll until 6s no longer appear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sure-Striking Dawn</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Striking First<br /> <br /> The second Evocation of First-Striking Dawn, and the most potent yet unlocked by its bearers, is a surety of purpose that comes with unhesitating speed. If the wielder's Initiative is higher than his target's, he may activate this Evocation to supplement an attack against the target. By doing so, he re-rolls all 1s and 2s on the attack roll until 1s and 2s fail to appear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dawn's Final Kiss</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Sure-Striking Dawn<br /> <br /> The final secret of First-Striking Dawn is her true name - Last-Striking Dawn. This Evocations grants double 10s on a <b>decisive</b> damage roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> This final Evocation is unlocked when a user who meets the prerequisites loves her mate without compunction or reservation and seals that love with a kiss. The wielder must be a Solar or Lunar, must have a Defining Tie of Love toward their Solar/Lunar mate, and must kiss that mate while holding First-Striking Dawn. At that moment, Dawn's Final Kiss awakens at no experience cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":". 07-06-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T09:47:28-07:00","id":926464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walker of the Yellow Path</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923799#post923799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Flames of Reaping </u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evocations</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Solar or Abyssal who attunes to these weapons awakens Feast of Souls at no experience cost. By paying 3 extra motes when attuning the Plasma Tongue Repeaters, the weapon gets one automatic success on all Decisive attacks. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Consider that one could buy 3 extra dice for the cost of this automatic success. 2 motes would make this roughly even with an excellency, 3 is overpriced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walker of the Yellow Path</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923799#post923799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">New Concept: Trivial Opponents</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A number of charms of this weapon refer to Trivial and Non-Trivial Opponents. A Trivial Opponent is an enemy who can be defeated or killed by a Withering attack, such as poorly trained soldiers, civilians, animals with no special abilities, or individuals in a battle group. Player Characters, Exalted and beings with Essence 3+ are never considered Trivial Opponents. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm missing something, but I only see Non-Trivial Opponents ever mention in here. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walker of the Yellow Path</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923799#post923799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Feast of Souls </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: - (2 Soul Charge per 1 HL) Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Flames of Reaping drink in the energies of their fallen foes. This charm creates a 10 point pool that holds Soul Charges, which is initially empty. Whenever the Wielder uses this weapon to kill a non-Trivial foe, he gains a Soul Charge. Soul Charges may be spent as Alternate costs for Evocations of this weapon, or they may be consumed as a Simple Action to heal the wielder at a rate of 1 lethal or bashing HL per 2 Soul Charges. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Seems fine, I'm good with this actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walker of the Yellow Path</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923799#post923799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Soul Fed Chambers</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m; Mins: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Until all 12 shots are fired. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: Feast of Souls</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the Reaper finds himself without ammunition, he does not need to worry. He simply tosses his weapons aside, drawing them again from his shadow, the empty flame pieces dissolving into cinders. This charm instantly reloads both weapons fully, and fire attacks made with Flames of Reaping using these dark firedust charges produce streaks of black flame. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>If you put words in here that this charm can't be used until you are full out of ammunition, that adds a little bit of restriction, although it's still reflexive. Maybe keep it reflexive, but state that it can only be used at the end of a turn after attacks are resolved. So you have to use up all of your shots, but you can't reload mid-barrage. Then the cost is appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walker of the Yellow Path</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923799#post923799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Soul Borne Wraith </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m, 2i or 1 Soul Charge, 2i; Mins: Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword: Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Turn</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Soul Fed Chambers</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Abandoning solid shape, the Reaper becomes a being of smoke and cinders to transport himself away from, or toward his enemies. The character becomes intangible but not invisible, which renders him untargetable by attacks not supplemented by Spirit Cutting Attack and other charms which allow one to hit immaterial spirits, though he raises his Evasion stat against those charms by 2. The character cannot make attacks or other Combat Actions when this charm is active. Instead, he may take two move actions that turn, and may move from close to short range away from an opponent without using disengage action. This charm cannot be used again until three turns have passed. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wraith Step </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 7m, 1wp, 2 Soul Charges; Mins: Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: Soul Borne Wraith</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stepping between shadows, the Reaper hunts down those who would try to stay away from his flames. Once per scene, the user teleports up to long range anywhere within his line of sight as his movement action. This charm can be reset by successfully damaging a non-trivial opponent with a Decisive attack. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I like these.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walker of the Yellow Path</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=923799#post923799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Death Blossom</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 10m, 1wp, All Soul Charges; Mins: Essence 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keyword: Decisive Only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: Wraith Step</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Laughing at the dead men surrounding him, the Reaper unleashes a storm of fire striking all around him, regardless of friend or foe. The Reaper makes a Decisive attack with these weapons, and adds the total number of Soul Charges he has to his Initiative when calculating damage. He applies his attack roll and damage roll to every character within medium range of him, regardless of direction or affiliation. When he has finished firing, he may activate Soul Fed Chambers for free. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think my beef with this is the free Medium range attack without AIMing, since it targets everyone. If this was limited to Short range I think it's actually fine as it is, especially since it doesn't distinguish friend or foe. Going out to medium though is generally a battlefield clearer, which is too strong. That said, there are very few (if any) attacks in the book that let you apply a single damage roll to multiple targets. Generally you have to split it up. But the cost is pretty high. Maybe as a final thing adjust the cost to be 1+ Soul Charges, so you have to have at least one? Oh, and restrict this to once per scene, yo.<br /> <br /> I like where you're coming from for these and frankly most of it seems fine to me. I could see someone coming in and saying &quot;hell no&quot; to that last one for reasons I've mentioned above, but I'm ok with it with my adjustments because Essence 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T11:35:42-07:00","id":926538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=926464#post926464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Consider that one could buy 3 extra dice for the cost of this automatic success. 2 motes would make this roughly even with an excellency, 3 is overpriced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be better for 2 successes, or bump it down to 1 or 2?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe I'm missing something, but I only see Non-Trivial Opponents ever mention in here. </div> </div> </div>Originally, Death Blossom had a clause that it autokilled Trivial Opponents. But I included that mostly cause it's a house rule my group uses that's relevant to the Artifact. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seems fine, I'm good with this actually. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you put words in here that this charm can't be used until you are full out of ammunition, that adds a little bit of restriction, although it's still reflexive. Maybe keep it reflexive, but state that it can only be used at the end of a turn after attacks are resolved. So you have to use up all of your shots, but you can't reload mid-barrage. Then the cost is appropriate. </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of upping the price to 5 or 6 motes and/or 1 Soul Charge<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like these. </div> </div> </div>thanks!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think my beef with this is the free Medium range attack without AIMing, since it targets everyone. If this was limited to Short range I think it's actually fine as it is, especially since it doesn't distinguish friend or foe. Going out to medium though is generally a battlefield clearer, which is too strong. That said, there are very few (if any) attacks in the book that let you apply a single damage roll to multiple targets. Generally you have to split it up. But the cost is pretty high. Maybe as a final thing adjust the cost to be 1+ Soul Charges, so you have to have at least one? Oh, and restrict this to once per scene, yo.<br /> <br /> I like where you're coming from for these and frankly most of it seems fine to me. I could see someone coming in and saying &amp;quot;hell no&amp;quot; to that last one for reasons I've mentioned above, but I'm ok with it with my adjustments because Essence 4. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, actually, Medium range does seem rather extreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11948-walker-of-the-yellow-path","name":"Walker of the Yellow Path","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T18:42:13-07:00","id":926762,"title":"","content":"So I finally got around editing Lakashim and am reposting it, seeing that it's been a while since it's initial post and I would like some additional feedback.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><u><b>Lakashim, the Pulse of Life</b></u></span><br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact: Green Jade Silken Armor<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Origin</b></u></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Among the tales written into the Immaculate Texts, there is one passage that relays the story of the first meeting Pasiasp and Sextes Jylis. They met on the shores of the Blessed Isle, where the last of the Immaculate Dragons labored to build a lighthouse to guide sailors safely away from hazardous reefs, and He Who Had Strewn Much Grass had just crossed the breadth of the isle by foot, the first step in his trek to heal the war-ravaged lands.<br /> They spoke of many things, they lamented the tragedies of the war, discussed the nature of their brethren, argued who had the greater task ahead of them, and rejoiced at their shared love of music. It was in that last subject, it is said, that they truly connected, singing, laughing, and trading songs, long into the night. It was under that moonlit night that they learned that neither had a greater quest than the other, for they shared the same goal: to renew Creation. For seven days they worked together, building and learning from one another and seven nights they shared their dreams, their fears, and, for a moment, the same heartbeat.<br /> It is this story that inspired Ragara Joran to make this beautiful piece of clothing for his beloved Ekoro, travelling far and wide from his home in Chanos to learn the elusive art of spinning jade into thread and collecting the materials needed for such a gift. Joran, sadly, never had a chance to give it to him. Ekoro was on business in Thorns when the city was besieged. Without a body ever recovered, Joran dutifully, if apprehensively, arranged for a memorial within his family mausoleum and his silken gift lies draped upon Ekoro\u2019s chair in their library, awaiting the return of its intended owner.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Appearance</span></b></u><br /> Strands of green jade with the silk of some rare race of moth, found only near the Dreaming Sea, are woven into a dozen braided pairs that come together in a spiral on the wearer\u2019s upper left chest, above the heart. In the center of the spiral sits a single hearthstone socket.<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attunement</span></b></u><br /> Additional Benefits Cost: 0m<br /> While wearing Lakashim, the wearer\u2019s awareness rolls now ignore penalties from noisy environs.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Evocations</b></u></span><br /> <br /> <b>Hear the Pulse of Creation</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1W<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> One Line Summary: Sense all living things nearby, quick bump to defenses, and downgrade ambush and surprise attacks to surprise attacks and normal attacks, respectively<br /> <br /> By closing their eyes and opening their senses to Lakashim, the wearer can hear the local beat of the Worldsong. For the rest of the scene, the wearer is aware of all the life around them, gaining a general sense of any creature with a functional heartbeat within medium range. This does not give them an exact location but will provide an accurate number of how many living beings are in each respective range band, whether visible or not. With this information, the wearer is also better armed against unexpected attacks done by those they\u2019ve sensed, treating successful ambushes as surprise attacks, and successful surprise attacks as normal attacks, respectively.<br /> <br /> Additionally, after activation, the wearer\u2019s defense is considered 2 higher until their next turn or until their second turn if activated before combat begins and the wearer wins the join battle roll. At Essence 4, the sensory range upgrades to long range. Useable once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Pounding Dance of the Worldheart</b><br /> Cost: 3m + 1m for each additional use<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Hear the Pulse of Creation<br /> One Line Summary: By moving in tandem with opponents, their withering attacks reward them with less initiative, gambits are more difficult to execute and cost more, and responding with a gambit costs no initiative.<br /> <br /> Once in tune with the rhythm of the Creation, the wearer now moves with a grace that can only come from following the steps in the dance of all life. In a scene where the wearer has used Hear the Pulse of Creation, the wearer may activate this evocation against an incoming attack they can defend against. Against a withering attack, the attacker gains only half of the initiative lost (round up) from against the wearer and does not receive any bonus if they crash the wearer. The wearer loses the full amount of initiative, the attacker simply can\u2019t seem to take advantage of the situation nearly as well as normal. Additionally, the wearer can use this evocation in reaction to a gambit against them, increasing the difficulty of the incoming gambit by 1. Consequently, this will cost the attacker an additional 1 initiative. For successful gambits with variable difficulty, the attacker reaps the reward of the pre-altered difficulty of the gambit instead of the new difficulty\u2019s reward. In either case, the wearer can ignore the initiative cost to commit a gambit against the attacker on their next turn.<br /> <br /> Finally, each use of Pounding Dance of the Worldheart within a scene increases the cost to use it again by 1 . The cost will be reset to 3 at the end of the scene and can be preemptively reset by a 2-point Performance-based stunt during combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Rebounding Inner Rhythm</b><br /> Cost: 7m 1W<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Withering-Only, Counterattack<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Pounding Dance of the Worldheart<br /> One Line Summary: Upon crashing, make a withering counterattack and gain crash protection for 2 turns<br /> <br /> Like the silence between heartbeats, sometimes the course of Lakashim falls to rise again with fiercer determination. Upon suffering initiative crash, the wearer can return the favor with a counterattack, making a withering attack that ignores an amount of the attacker\u2019s defense equal to the amount of initiative below 1 the wearer is now, to a maximum of ignoring all but 1 defense. If the counterattack results in an initiative shift, the wearer cannot be crashed for the next 2 rounds, never dropping below 1 initiative despite the efforts of their opponents. Useable only once per opponent per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>One Pulse, One Soul, One Act</b><br /> Cost: -<br /> Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Pounding Dance of the Worldheart<br /> One Line Summary: When your action sync\u2019s up with an ally\u2019s attack, chance to share some successes between both of them<br /> When many things move in harmony and act as one, Lakashim beats loudest. After Hear the Pulse of Creation, whenever the wearer attacks an opponent on the same tick as an ally, they both may reroll an unsuccessful die once, sharing all successes rolled.<br /> <br /> Example: Wearer rolls 2 successes and their ally rolls 0 successes. They both reroll one die apiece, both of which roll a 10, coming up with 4 successes between both of them. The wearer now has 7 successes and the ally has 4 successes.<br /> <br /> All allies that have a pulse that are attacking the same target at the same time may partake in this reroll, adding their successes to the shared result, but must do so after all other reroll mechanics. None of the shared dice can trigger a botch, nor can they be target of magic that steals successes or treats their failures as successes for the opponent. Those who cannot reroll an unsuccessful die cannot partake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","user":"Binary Phantom","date":". 07-06-2016, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T04:20:45-07:00","id":926979,"title":"","content":"Octopoid, those are just Reaper's charms from Overwatch, aren't they? Now I'm going to have to look through your back catalogue to work out how many of your artefacts are from Overwatch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T04:54:58-07:00","id":926994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=926979#post926979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Octopoid, those are just Reaper's charms from Overwatch, aren't they? Now I'm going to have to look through your back catalogue to work out how many of your artefacts are from Overwatch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhhhh....<br /> <br /> I made the Reaper Expy Charms. Octopoid posted his First Striking Dawn Chakram right under my flame pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11948-walker-of-the-yellow-path","name":"Walker of the Yellow Path","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T05:44:55-07:00","id":927003,"title":"","content":"So I am drawing a blank on an artifact idea and this seems like the proper thread to share. The artifact is a guitar for my Zenith. He was a good enough musician as a mortal that Malfeas invited him to hell to give a command performance, and he exalted during the event right in front of Malfeas, Ligier, et al. Sensing an opportunity to put a solar in his debt, Ligier made several artifacts for the Zenith including a 4 dot artifact guitar as a &quot;proper instrument&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thing is I'm stuck on what it should do and what it's possible evocations might be. I know I want it to be able to sound like any instrument, but that seems kinda tame for a 4-dot artifact so I need something else in addition. My current placeholder is TN6 for performance rolls involving it, but I'm not sure if that's appropriate. Also completely blanking on Evocations.<br /> <br /> Help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T05:57:58-07:00","id":927008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walker of the Yellow Path</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=926994#post926994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhhhh....<br /> <br /> I made the Reaper Expy Charms. Octopoid posted his First Striking Dawn Chakram right under my flame pieces.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whooops. Oh Jesus, your name is even Walker of the Yellow Path. I should have noticed that, my bad. I'm sorry for incorrectly assigning your work to Octopoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T12:11:32-07:00","id":927220,"title":"","content":"At the risk of being too prolific, I've also made Evocations for some demonic tattoos, like Mara's but for Cecaelia, the Heartless Sentinel, a custom 2CD I made back in 2nd Ed. Thoughts and feedback are much welcome!<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Demonic Tattoos of Cecaelia</b><br /> <br /> <b>Turn the Tides</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Cecaelia, the Heartless Sentinel, draws her power from Kimbery, the Sea that Marched Against the Flame, and her sorcerers draw similar power from the ocean. Once per story, when fully submerged in a body of water at least four range bands across, the sorcerer may benefit from a free full Occult Excellency. Note that this Charm has the Mute Keyword; the sorcerer's power is never obvious.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Power from the Sea</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Turn the Tides<br /> <br /> Sorcery is draining on the reserves of a sorcerer; Cecaelia understands this, and reinvigorates her chosen. Once per story, when submerged in a body of water at least four range bands across, the sorcerer may regain one point of temporary Willpower. This cannot take the sorcerer above his normal maximum.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cecaelian Manipulation</b><br /> Cost: None (+1WP); Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The demons summoned by a sorcerer of Cecaelia are often touched by her power and her form. The sorcerer may spend one extra point of Willpower when casting Demon of the First Circle to grant the summoned demon Gills (as per the three-dot Merit) and allow it to swim at its normal movement speed (generally one range band per turn). These benefits last until the demon is killed or its service ends, and always come with some visible alteration to the beast's anatomy. Blood Apes altered by this Evocation might have a strong tail instead of legs, while a Beauteous Wasp might have fins instead of wings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cecaelian Mastery</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Cecaelian Manipulation<br /> <br /> This Evocation permanently enhances its prerequisite, further mutating the demons so summoned and altered. In addition to the normal effects of Cecaelian Manipulation, Cecaelian Mastery grants the demon a non-Charm bonus die to all rolls made while submerged. This Evocation yet further alters the demon's appearance, making it unquestionably aquatic in nature. Blood Apes may retain only the barest vestige of fur, replaced by glistening scales and a series of thick, writhing tentacles in place of legs, while a Beauteous Wasp may have traded in its legs for ephemeral yet beautiful undulating fins.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pull of the Tides</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Cecaelian Mastery, Power from the Sea<br /> <br /> Even the immutable nature of sorcery can be mutable when exposed to the ever-changing waters of the sea. When the sorcerer is fully submerged in any body of water at least four range bands across, his control spell automatically alters to contain aspects of the ocean or ocean life (he may cast Invulnerable Skin of Bronze only to find himself covered in protective barnacles, for example, while Death of Obsidian Butterflies might produce razor-sharp coral anemones instead). Further, once per story, he may invoke this Evocation at no cost to empower his control spell while so submerged. If he does so, the sorcerer finds the spell's cost reduced by either 5 sorcerous motes (to a minimum of 5) or one Willpower (to a minimum of 1).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Reading Kimbery's Depths</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1w; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Pull of the Tides<br /> <br /> In the deepest waters of Kimbery, there are enchanted secrets and forbidden futures. With this final Evocation, the sorcerer can tap into those secrets to find (or craft) a future for himself that is pleasing to him. When the sorcerer uses this Evocation, he describes an event or end he wishes to accomplish. When he completes this description, he plucks that future from Kimbery's depths, gaining (Essence) non-Charm dice to be held in reserve. The greater the detail of the future, the more potent this Evocation becomes; add any stunt dice for the description to these non-Charm dice. For the remainder of the story, the sorcerer may draw from this pool to add up to two non-Charm dice to any roll that is taken in accordance with the fell prophecy he has created. The Storyteller is the final arbiter of what counts as &quot;accordance,&quot; but in general, if the sorcerer is acting toward his desired end, he should be able to draw from the pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":".  Added Reading Kimbery's Depths 07-06-2016, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T12:37:41-07:00","id":927233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=924148#post924148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>First-Striking Dawn (Orichalcum and Moonsilver Infinite Chakram - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of First-Striking Dawn</b><br /> When a Solar or Lunar attunes to First-Striking Dawn for two additional motes, she gains a +1 non-Charm die bonus on Join Battle rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not great at judging the effective cost of non-charm dice but my gut would be to put this at 1m.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=924148#post924148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Striking First</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> First-Striking Dawn is not a complex weapon, forged with a single goal. To that end, she seems to almost materialize in her wielder's hand in her moment of need. This Evocation can be used to enhance a Join Battle roll, allowing its bearer to re-roll 6s on that roll until 6s no longer appear. If the user wins Join Battle, she may reflexively take a Draw/Ready Weapon action to ready First-Striking Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can already reflexively Draw/Ready a Weapon when you roll Join Battle. Like, by default. So that portion of this evocation is not useful. Otherwise, it seems fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=924148#post924148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sure-Striking Dawn</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Striking First<br /> <br /> The second Evocation of First-Striking Dawn, and the most potent yet unlocked by its bearers, is a surety of purpose that comes with unhesitating speed. If the wielder's Initiative is higher than his target's, he may activate this Evocation to supplement an attack against the target. By doing so, he re-rolls all 1s and 2s on the attack roll until 1s and 2s fail to appear.</div> </div> </div> </div>You love your 3m evocations, don't you? Seems fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=924148#post924148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dawn's Final Kiss</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Sure-Striking Dawn<br /> <br /> The final secret of First-Striking Dawn is her true name - Last-Striking Dawn. A <b>decisive</b> attack supplemented by this Evocation counts 10s on its damage roll as two successes.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> This final Evocation is unlocked when a user who meets the prerequisites loves her mate without compunction or reservation and seals that love with a kiss. The wielder must be a Solar or Lunar, must have a Defining Tie of Love toward their Solar/Lunar mate, and must kiss that mate while holding First-Striking Dawn. At that moment, Dawn's Final Kiss awakens at no experience cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can probably condense this rule as &quot;grants double 10's&quot; because that's a thing. My gut says 3m is a little too cheap, I might make it 4 or 5m.<br /> <br /> Also I shed a single tear for the Lunar who's Solar queen did not love him like he thought she did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T12:41:53-07:00","id":927235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927233#post927233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I shed a single tear for the Lunar who's Solar queen did not love him like he thought she did.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As always, thank you for your input! Suggested changes made.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T12:52:17-07:00","id":927238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=926762#post926762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><u><b>Lakashim, the Pulse of Life</b></u></span><br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact: Green Jade Silken Armor<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attunement</span></b></u><br /> Additional Benefits Cost: 0m<br /> At their discretion, the wearer can add their Performance ability to their join battle result instead of 3 when calculating initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in practice, this is effectively 1-2 non-charm automatic successes to join battle rolls. I would not grant that for 0m. I'm not sure what the appropriate cost is, but free ain't it. (As I've stated before, I'm bad at pricing non-charm dice/suc costs, but I know they're good)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=926762#post926762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Hear the Pulse of Creation</b><br /> Cost: 5m<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> One Line Summary: Sense all living things nearby, quick bump to defenses, and downgrade ambush and surprise attacks to surprise attacks and normal attacks, respectively<br /> <br /> By closing their eyes and opening their senses to Lakashim, the wearer can hear the local beat of the Worldsong. For the rest of the scene, the wearer is aware of all the life around them, gaining a general sense of any creature with a functional heartbeat within medium range. This does not give them an exact location but will provide an accurate number of how many living beings are in each respective range band, whether visible or not. With this information, the wearer is also better armed against unexpected attacks, treating successful ambushes as surprise attacks, and successful surprise attacks as normal attacks, respectively. Additionally, after activation, the wearer\u2019s defense is considered 2 higher until their next turn. At Essence 4, the sensory range upgrades to long range. Useable once per scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a big defense bonus. And it's non-charm again, in that it doesn't interact with the dice cap, it just changes your value to be higher. I might add a Willpower to the cost of this, also because upgrading ambushes to surprise attacks is strong (but a cool power). How does the &quot;next turn&quot; timescale work if someone activates it outside of combat, anticipating an attack soon? How long does it last? Because 1 turn is very quick. Otherwise, a neat evocation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=926762#post926762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pounding Dance of the Worldheart</b><br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Dual, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Hear the Pulse of Creation<br /> One Line Summary: By moving in tandem with opponents, their withering attacks reward them with less initiative, gambits are more difficult to execute and cost more, and responding with a gambit costs no initiative.<br /> <br /> Once in tune with the rhythm of the Creation, the wearer now moves with a grace that can only come from following the steps in the dance of all life. In a scene where the wearer has used Hear the Pulse of Creation, an attacker gains only half of the initiative lost (round up) from withering attack against the wearer and does not receive any bonus if they crash the wearer. The wearer loses the full amount of initiative, the attacker simply can\u2019t seem to take advantage of the situation nearly as well as normal.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the wearer can use this evocation in reaction to a gambit against them, increasing the difficulty of the incoming gambit by 1. Consequently, this will cost the attacker an additional 1 initiative. For successful gambits with variable difficulty, the attacker reaps the reward of the pre-altered difficulty of the gambit instead of the new difficulty\u2019s reward.<br /> <br /> In either case, the wearer can ignore the initiative cost to commit a gambit against the attacker on their next turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a potentially powerful evocation for 3m. It's reflexive so it can be used every time they are attacked in combat pretty easily, constantly depriving their foes of Initiative. I'm debating with myself on how to recommend balancing that effect, whether it should be more cost or a limit to how often it can be used per target. Also, it needs language stating that you have to use this evocation to gain that first benefit. As it's worded now, it just says any time you receive a Withering attack after using Hear the Pulse of Creation, which makes it sound free. I'm ok with the rest of it, but it definitely needs a cost bump at least, and may need a use limiter. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=926762#post926762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Rebounding Inner Rhythm</b><br /> Cost: 6m 1W<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Withering-Only, Counterattack<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Pounding Dance of the Worldheart<br /> One Line Summary: Upon crashing, make a withering counterattack and gain crash protection for 2 turns<br /> Like the silence between heartbeats, sometimes the course of Lakashim falls to rise again with fiercer determination. Upon suffering initiative crash, the wearer can return the favor with a counterattack, making a withering attack that ignores an amount of the attacker\u2019s defense equal to the amount of initiative below 1 the wearer is now, to a maximum of ignoring all but 1 defense. If the counterattack results in an initiative shift, the wearer cannot be crashed for the next 2 rounds, never dropping below 1 initiative despite the efforts of their opponents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whew! That's potent! I've given it some thought and I think I'm good with it. Debating whether it needs another mote or two in cost, because of how strong this counterattack is and the potential to gain Initiative Shift so quickly. Maybe it can only be used once per scene too. Otherwise, I like it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Binary Phantom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=926762#post926762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>One Pulse, One Soul, One Act</b><br /> Cost: -<br /> Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Pounding Dance of the Worldheart<br /> One Line Summary: When your action sync\u2019s up with an ally\u2019s attack, chance to share some successes between both of them<br /> When many things move in harmony and act as one, Lakashim beats loudest. After Hear the Pulse of Creation, whenever the wearer attacks an opponent on the same tick as an ally, they both may reroll an unsuccessful die once, sharing all successes rolled.<br /> <br /> Example: Wearer rolls 2 successes and their ally rolls 0 successes. They both reroll one die apiece, both of which roll a 10, coming up with 4 successes between both of them. The wearer now has 7 successes and the ally has 4 successes.<br /> <br /> All allies that have a pulse that are attacking the same target at the same time may partake in this reroll, adding their successes to the shared result, but must do so after all other reroll mechanics. None of the shared dice can trigger a botch, nor can they be target of magic that steals successes or treats their failures as successes for the opponent. Those who cannot reroll an unsuccessful die cannot partake.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, frankly, a very cool evocation and my favorite one of the tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T12:57:39-07:00","id":927242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927220#post927220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Evocations of the Demonic Tattoos of Cecaelia</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Your writing is bad and you should feel bad. Go sit in the corner and think about what you've done.<br /> <br /> But seriously, this is awesome stuff. No commentary really. Mechanically it seems fine, as long as an ST permits it. My only hesitations are whether to allow evocations (or charms really) to add mutations to sentient creatures, which is usually the realm of Workings. But with the focus on 1st Circle Demons and considering the source, that feels like a ST arbitration to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T13:13:26-07:00","id":927248,"title":"","content":"Been a while so I thought I'd update my list. I've now made 20 Artifacts.<br /> <br /> Artifact types<br /> Goremaul--------------1<br /> Warfans--------------- 1<br /> Grand Grimcleaver 1<br /> Shield------------------ 2<br /> Longfang-------------- 1<br /> Razor Harness------ 1<br /> Skycutter--------------1<br /> Chain Shirt----------- 1<br /> Powerbow------------- 1<br /> Reaper Daiklave---- 1<br /> Wrackstaff------------ 2<br /> Articulated Plate---- 1<br /> Grand Daiklave------ 1<br /> Smashfist------------- 1<br /> Direlash---------------- 1<br /> Grand Goremaul-----1<br /> Grimoire-----------------1<br /> Daggers-----------------1<br /> <br /> Magical Materials (1 means a single material was used, 2 means it was half the materials used. Takes two 2's to make 1 artifact)<br /> Black Jade-------------2 1<br /> Blue Jade---------------2 1 2<br /> White Jade-------------2 1 2<br /> Green Jade-------------1 1<br /> Red Jade----------------2 1<br /> Orichalcum-------------2 1 2 1 1 1<br /> Moonsilver--------------1 2 1<br /> Starmetal----------------2 1<br /> Soulsteel----------------1 2 2<br /> <br /> Artifact 3-----------------10<br /> Artifact 4-----------------6<br /> Artifact 5-----------------4<br /> <br /> I admit I'm feeling like I'd like to create something new again, but work just exploded on me and it's possible I won't have any time for the next month or two to create anything at all. But if someone sees a hole in this list and wants to request a concept from me, I'll keep it on the backburner to do either if I get a bored moment, or whenever this project at work is finished. As usual, I make no promises that I'll use anything suggested, but some of my favorite artifacts ended up being suggested by others so this is a working strategy for me thusfar.<br /> <br /> Love seeing all the work everyone's doing. Still surprised at the creative things I see done on this thread!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T13:21:13-07:00","id":927249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927248#post927248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit I'm feeling like I'd like to create something new again, but work just exploded on me and it's possible I won't have any time for the next month or two to create anything at all. But if someone sees a hole in this list and wants to request a concept from me, I'll keep it on the backburner to do either if I get a bored moment, or whenever this project at work is finished. As usual, I make no promises that I'll use anything suggested, but some of my favorite artifacts ended up being suggested by others so this is a working strategy for me thusfar.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you feel like expanding outside of weapons and armor, you could make the guitar I mentioned for my Rockstar Zenith (Made by Ligier, if it matters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T13:23:59-07:00","id":927251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927249#post927249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you feel like expanding outside of weapons and armor, you could make the guitar I mentioned for my Rockstar Zenith (Made by Ligier, if it matters).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally love to see the guitar as designed by The Unsung Hero. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T13:26:22-07:00","id":927252,"title":"","content":"The trick with Guitars is that the Performance ability doesn't have a lot of hooks to hang things off of. A lot of what you CAN do with it is already done by Performance charms, and I'm not sure I see the design space. The other direction is to make it a weapon, but then it's just Nightengale Style. If we flesh it out a little more, I'll consider it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T13:37:04-07:00","id":927257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927003#post927003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am drawing a blank on an artifact idea and this seems like the proper thread to share. The artifact is a guitar for my Zenith. He was a good enough musician as a mortal that Malfeas invited him to hell to give a command performance, and he exalted during the event right in front of Malfeas, Ligier, et al. Sensing an opportunity to put a solar in his debt, Ligier made several artifacts for the Zenith including a 4 dot artifact guitar as a &quot;proper instrument&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thing is I'm stuck on what it should do and what it's possible evocations might be. I know I want it to be able to sound like any instrument, but that seems kinda tame for a 4-dot artifact so I need something else in addition. My current placeholder is TN6 for performance rolls involving it, but I'm not sure if that's appropriate. Also completely blanking on Evocations.<br /> <br /> Help?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would recommend a non-Charm die to Performance rolls for an attunement bonus. It's a simple workhorse. Likewise, I would make the first Evocation the dice trick you mentioned: TN6 for Performance (or re-roll 6s, or something like that). <i>Then</i> break into &quot;sounds like any instrument&quot; Evocation, which reduces penalties (no hard rock at the satrap's birthday party? Play some mellow jazz instead!) and serves as explicit stunt fodder. Finally, cap that sucker with something mind-influencing, something that can make an Instill action or even a Persuade action at a whole room of people at once. <br /> <br /> That's my thoughts. TUH may have more input.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T13:43:09-07:00","id":927260,"title":"","content":"It's Ligier made, so it probably has some green fire themes in it. <br /> <br /> Just throwing Charm tree idea at the wall here right now:<br /> <br /> A charm that lets you compel listeners to dance. <br /> <br /> Charm that makes dancer's who are dancing along to it better, with accompanying green fire effects on the feet and hands. <br /> <br /> Charm that awakens the inner fury inside the hearts of the dancers, turning them into Beautiful and Graceful bezerkers who snap the necks of people trying to stop the music.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11948-walker-of-the-yellow-path","name":"Walker of the Yellow Path","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T13:44:26-07:00","id":927261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927257#post927257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would recommend a non-Charm die to Performance rolls for an attunement bonus. It's a simple workhorse. Likewise, I would make the first Evocation the dice trick you mentioned: TN6 for Performance (or re-roll 6s, or something like that). <i>Then</i> break into &quot;sounds like any instrument&quot; Evocation, which reduces penalties (no hard rock at the satrap's birthday party? Play some mellow jazz instead!) and serves as explicit stunt fodder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that sounds pretty good. Maybe have both TN6 and Reroll 6s as different evocations? This is supposed to be a 4 dot artifact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927257#post927257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Finally, cap that sucker with something mind-influencing, something that can make an Instill action or even a Persuade action at a whole room of people at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that just what Performance does normally?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T13:46:55-07:00","id":927263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927261#post927261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that just what Performance does normally?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but add a Psyche effect. I like Walker's suggestion about making people dance. That seems like something Ligier might throw in. And yeah, more green fire effects! Make every Evocation come with a visual display of green flames or something like that!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T14:07:03-07:00","id":927272,"title":"","content":"So Something like:<br /> <br /> <br /> GUITAR NEEDS NAME BADLY<br /> <br /> By attuning to &quot;ARTIFACT NAME&quot; the Exalt gains a non-charm die to performance actions involving the instrument, on top of the normal one for being Exceptional.<br /> <br /> Hellforged Wonder of Sound<br /> Cost: 2m, Requirements: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Duration: One Performance Action<br /> <br /> &quot;ARTIFACT NAME&quot; sparks with green fire as the exalt strums out a tune worthy of the ages.<br /> <br /> Reroll 6s until sixes fail to appear.<br /> <br /> <br /> Malfeas Pleasing Performance<br /> Cost: 2m, Requirements: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> <br /> &quot;ARTIFACT NAME&quot; was forged to honor a musician who played the best song in the world for The King of Hell, and all later songs played on it glory in that tribute.<br /> <br /> Target number for the Performance action supplemented is 6 instead of 7.<br /> <br /> <br /> Munificent Synthesizer Emulation<br /> Cost: --, Requirements: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Duration: Permanent <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;ARTIFACT NAME&quot; hides within it the secrets of timbre, as well as pitch and volume. &quot;ARTIFACT NAME&quot; may sound like any instrument the Exalt desires. Eliminating any penalties for not having the proper instrument.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> And my creative well has run dry.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T14:09:40-07:00","id":927273,"title":"","content":"Maybe something lowering resolve? I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T14:58:18-07:00","id":927287,"title":"","content":"<br /> Thanks for the feedback, I've updated the artifact and hope you like the changes I've made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927238#post927238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So in practice, this is effectively 1-2 non-charm automatic successes to join battle rolls. I would not grant that for 0m. I'm not sure what the appropriate cost is, but free ain't it. (As I've stated before, I'm bad at pricing non-charm dice/suc costs, but I know they're good)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, changed the effect to be more like how Orichalcum Hunting Hawk's attunement benefit works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927238#post927238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a big defense bonus. And it's non-charm again, in that it doesn't interact with the dice cap, it just changes your value to be higher. I might add a Willpower to the cost of this, also because upgrading ambushes to surprise attacks is strong (but a cool power). How does the &quot;next turn&quot; timescale work if someone activates it outside of combat, anticipating an attack soon? How long does it last? Because 1 turn is very quick. Otherwise, a neat evocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Willpower cost added and modified how the timing works for using it before combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927238#post927238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a potentially powerful evocation for 3m. It's reflexive so it can be used every time they are attacked in combat pretty easily, constantly depriving their foes of Initiative. I'm debating with myself on how to recommend balancing that effect, whether it should be more cost or a limit to how often it can be used per target. Also, it needs language stating that you have to use this evocation to gain that first benefit. As it's worded now, it just says any time you receive a Withering attack after using Hear the Pulse of Creation, which makes it sound free. I'm ok with the rest of it, but it definitely needs a cost bump at least, and may need a use limiter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clarified and gave it an increasing usage cost with a reset clause.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927238#post927238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whew! That's potent! I've given it some thought and I think I'm good with it. Debating whether it needs another mote or two in cost, because of how strong this counterattack is and the potential to gain Initiative Shift so quickly. Maybe it can only be used once per scene too. Otherwise, I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Made it once per opponent per ability and increased the cost by 1m.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927238#post927238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, frankly, a very cool evocation and my favorite one of the tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/738-binary-phantom","name":"Binary Phantom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T15:24:41-07:00","id":927301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927272#post927272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Something like:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Emperor of Hellfire and Ash (Orichalcum and Starmetal Motonic Amplification Instrument - Artifact ****)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Emperor of Hellfire and Ash</b><br /> <br /> By attuning to the Emperor of Hellfire and Ash, a Solar or Sidereal gains a bonus non-charm die to Performance actions involving the instrument, on top of the normal die for its Exceptional quality.<br /> <br /> <b>Hellforged Wonder of Sound</b><br /> Cost: 2m, Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Performance Action<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Emperor of Hellfire and Ash sparks with green fire as the Exalt strums out a tune worthy of the ages. This Evocation supplements a Performance action, re-rolling 1s and 2s until 1s and 2s fail to appear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Malfeas-Pleasing Performance</b><br /> Cost: 2m, Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Performance Action<br /> Prerequisites: Hellforged Wonder of Sound<br /> <br /> The Emperor of Hellfire and Ash was forged to honor a musician who played the greatest song in the world for The King of Hell, and all later songs played on it glory in that tribute. This Evocation supplements a Performance action, reducing the target number for that action by one (normally to 6).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Munificent Synthesizer Emulation</b><br /> Cost: --, Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Malfeas-Pleasing Performance<br /> <br /> The Emperor of Hellfire and Ash hides within it the secrets of timbre, as well as pitch and volume. At no cost, the Emperor of Hellfire and Ash may produce the sound of any instrument the Exalt desires, eliminating any penalties for not having the proper instrument. A strum on the brass strings could produce the melodious whistle of a flute, the discordant blurt of a bagpipe, or even the percussive effects of a drum. Players are encouraged to use this as appropriate stunt fodder.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pied Guitarist of Hell</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: One Performance Action<br /> Prerequisites: Munificent Synthesizer Emulation<br /> <br /> The song performed by the first bearer of the Emperor of Hellfire and Ash brought the Brass Dancer to his feet, and when Malfeas rises to dance, all present follow suit. This Evocation functions as a Performance-based Instill action, made with (Essence) automatic successes. If the roll overcomes a target's Resolve, he or she gains a Minor Principle of &quot;I love to dance.&quot; Demons have their Resolve reduced by two against this effect, and the Intimacy so instilled is at Major strength. Repeated uses of this Evocation can increase the strength of an instilled Intimacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edits and additional Evocation added in quoted text.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'd like to come up with one more Evocation to really cap the whole thing off at 4 dots. I'm working on something - it's percolating. I'll post it as soon as it coalesces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":". 07-07-2016, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T15:39:47-07:00","id":927311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927301#post927301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edits and additional Evocation added in quoted text.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'd like to come up with one more Evocation to really cap the whole thing off at 4 dots. I'm working on something - it's percolating. I'll post it as soon as it coalesces.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, there's already a Solar Performance charm that rerolls 1s and gives a single auto-success, although the reroll's 2s is different functionality and other splats might not get that sort of effect in their native charmset.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, shouldn't Pied Guitarist of Hell have a prerequisite? Or am I not understanding how evocation trees work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T15:42:11-07:00","id":927313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927311#post927311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, there's already a Solar Performance charm that rerolls 1s and gives a single auto-success, although the reroll's 2s is different functionality and other splats might not get that sort of effect in their native charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. Also, I didn't want to re-roll 6s if we're going to reduce the TN to 6, as that ruins some of the effectiveness. So, yeah, re-rolling 2s and adding to other splats' functionality. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T16:08:08-07:00","id":927328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927313#post927313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's fair. Also, I didn't want to re-roll 6s if we're going to reduce the TN to 6, as that ruins some of the effectiveness. So, yeah, re-rolling 2s and adding to other splats' functionality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool.<br /> <br /> You know, I just realized that with the Sid Excellency reducing the TN to 4, Malfeas-Pleasing Performance knocking it down to 3, and Hellforged Wonder of Sound rerolling 1s and 2s, a Sidereal using it can only roll successes. Intended functionality, acceptable for a 4 dot artifact, or too good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T16:13:10-07:00","id":927329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927328#post927328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I just realized that with the Sid Excellency reducing the TN to 4, Malfeas-Pleasing Performance knocking it down to 3, and Hellforged Wonder of Sound rerolling 1s and 2s, a Sidereal using it can only roll successes. Intended functionality, acceptable for a 4 dot artifact, or too good?</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn. That's... good. For a 4-dot Artifact, on a Performance roll? I'm inclined to leave it functioning that way. Especially since your character is a Solar. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T16:43:45-07:00","id":927337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927329#post927329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Damn. That's... good. For a 4-dot Artifact, on a Performance roll? I'm inclined to leave it functioning that way. Especially since your character is a Solar. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Coolio. I hope you can come up with a capstone, cause I'm stumped. On reflection I have to say I really like the Pied Guitarist of Hell Evocation. It's wonderfully evocative of the scene I have in my head of Jubilant Harp* giving a command performance to the Brass Dancer and his Souls, and rolling all 10s.<br /> <br /> And I just realized why they are called evocations.<br /> <br /> <br /> *The name I decided on for the Zenith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T18:49:23-07:00","id":927392,"title":"","content":"And now I'm trying to imagine what a 5 dot version of the Emperor of Hellfire and Ash would look like. Only thing that comes to mind is letting the other evocations augment Silver Voiced Nightingale stuff as if they were performance rolls. Or upgrading Kiais to medium weapons.<br /> <br /> But I can't help but feel that's too specific, and while my Zenith does favor brawl, he isn't yet a martial artist.<br /> <br /> I dunno,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T07:23:55-07:00","id":927604,"title":"","content":"Well then...<br /> <img src=\"https://media.makeameme.org/created/my-work-here-2n7awy.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T07:56:06-07:00","id":927620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927604#post927604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well then...<br /> <img src=\"https://media.makeameme.org/created/my-work-here-2n7awy.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know, if you wanted to chime in with a capstone Evocation, it wouldn't hurt my feelings at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T08:27:57-07:00","id":927628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927620#post927620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, if you wanted to chime in with a capstone Evocation, it wouldn't hurt my feelings at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see no reason for Pied Guitarist from Hell to have a Willpower in the cost. 5m would be fine, imo. Add it it that successive uses increase the intensity of the Principle.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Dance to Your Doom</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m, 1WP <b>Min: </b>Essence 4<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One Round<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Pied Guitarist from Hell<br /> <br /> The guitarist plays a melody that cannot be resisted, much to the dismay of those who hear it. The guitarist beings performing a song that infects those who hear it via a Performance-based Persuade roll that gains double-9's to inspire the desire the dance. On a success, the target is compelled to dance causing a penalty to Defense equal to 1 + Intimacy's strength if they hold a Principle of love for dance. This persuasion costs an extra point of Willpower to resist, and if it is resisted, their defense is still reduced by 1 for a single round. Each time a target is damaged to the point of increasing a level of wound penalty, they may choose to enter another Decision Point to attempt to shake off the influence.<br /> <br /> This evocation may be continued on successive rounds for 5m each round, but if it stops, it must be paid in full to begin again. The guitarist may not take any non-reflexive actions while performing.<br /> <br /> <br /> (This one might be too mean)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T08:30:51-07:00","id":927630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927628#post927628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see no reason for Pied Guitarist from Hell to have a Willpower in the cost. 5m would be fine, imo. Add it it that successive uses increase the intensity of the Principle.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Dance to Your Doom</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m, 1WP <b>Min: </b>Essence 4<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One Round<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Pied Guitarist from Hell<br /> <br /> The guitarist plays a melody that cannot be resisted, much to the dismay of those who hear it. The guitarist beings performing a song that infects those who hear it via a Performance-based Persuade roll that gains double-9's to inspire the desire the dance. On a success, the target is compelled to dance causing a penalty to Defense equal to 1 + Intimacy's strength if they hold a Principle of love for dance. This persuasion costs an extra point of Willpower to resist, and if it is resisted, their defense is still reduced by 1 for a single round. Each time a target is damaged to the point of increasing a level of wound penalty, they may choose to enter another Decision Point to attempt to shake off the influence.<br /> <br /> This evocation may be continued on successive rounds for 5m each round, but if it stops, it must be paid in full to begin again. The guitarist may not take any non-reflexive actions while performing.<br /> <br /> <br /> (This one might be too mean)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Beautiful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927311#post927311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Also, shouldn't Pied Guitarist of Hell have a prerequisite? Or am I not understanding how evocation trees work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, yes, and Avoidance Kata. Suggested edits made to original post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":". 07-07-2016, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T09:25:33-07:00","id":927645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927628#post927628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see no reason for Pied Guitarist from Hell to have a Willpower in the cost. 5m would be fine, imo. Add it it that successive uses increase the intensity of the Principle.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b>Dance to Your Doom</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m, 1WP <b>Min: </b>Essence 4<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One Round<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Pied Guitarist from Hell<br /> <br /> The guitarist plays a melody that cannot be resisted, much to the dismay of those who hear it. The guitarist beings performing a song that infects those who hear it via a Performance-based Persuade roll that gains double-9's to inspire the desire the dance. On a success, the target is compelled to dance causing a penalty to Defense equal to 1 + Intimacy's strength if they hold a Principle of love for dance. This persuasion costs an extra point of Willpower to resist, and if it is resisted, their defense is still reduced by 1 for a single round. Each time a target is damaged to the point of increasing a level of wound penalty, they may choose to enter another Decision Point to attempt to shake off the influence.<br /> <br /> This evocation may be continued on successive rounds for 5m each round, but if it stops, it must be paid in full to begin again. The guitarist may not take any non-reflexive actions while performing.<br /> <br /> <br /> (This one might be too mean)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it is a bit too mean, and it doesn't really fit the image I have in my head of Jubilant Harp's legend. Maybe somthing more along the lines of::<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Show Must Go On</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1WP Min: Essence ?<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: ???<br /> Prerequisites: Pied Guitarist Of Hell<br /> <br /> The hatred and rage Malfeas feels towards the Solar Exalted knows no bounds, yet when the mortal performer exalted as a Zenith right in front of him, his hand was stayed by the quality and emotional resonance of the song. If Music can calm the rage of Malfeas then what being can resist being similarly swayed?<br /> <br /> This charm acts as a performance based Persuade action with (Essence) non-charm automatic successes against the guitarist's enemies to allow the musician and his allies to flee. This persuasion costs an extra point of Willpower to resist. Each use of this charm counts as a new argument for the purpose of decision points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 07-07-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T09:28:49-07:00","id":927646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927645#post927645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think it is a bit too mean, and it doesn't really fit the image I have in my head of Jubilant Harp's legend. Maybe somthing more along the lines of::<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Show Must Go On</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1WP Min: Essence ?<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: ???<br /> Prerequisites: Pied Guitarist Of Hell<br /> <br /> The hatred and rage Malfeas feels towards the Solar Exalted knows no bounds, yet when the mortal performer exalted as a Zenith right in front of him, his hand was stayed by the quality and emotional resonance of the song. If Music can calm the rage of Malfeas then what being can resist being similarly swayed?<br /> <br /> This charm acts as a performance based Persuade action with (Essence) non-charm automatic successes against the guitarist's enemies to allow the musician and his allies to flee. This persuasion costs an extra point of Willpower to resist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works too. Seems fine at Essence 3. Duration seems like Indefinite, as you'd hold on to it until you've successfully Withdrawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T09:31:44-07:00","id":927650,"title":"","content":"I actually added a thing to the end making it stronger. Not sure how balanced it is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:14:35-07:00","id":927730,"title":"","content":"<b>Emperor of Hellfire and Ash (Orichalcum and Starmetal Motonic Amplification Instrument - Artifact ****)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Emperor of Hellfire and Ash</b><br /> <br /> By attuning to the Emperor of Hellfire and Ash, a Solar or Sidereal gains a bonus non-charm die to Performance actions involving the instrument, on top of the normal die for its Exceptional quality.<br /> <br /> <b>Hellforged Wonder of Sound</b><br /> Cost: 2m, Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Performance Action<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Emperor of Hellfire and Ash sparks with green fire as the Exalt strums out a tune worthy of the ages. This Evocation supplements a Performance action, re-rolling 1s and 2s until 1s and 2s fail to appear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Malfeas-Pleasing Performance</b><br /> Cost: 2m, Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Performance Action<br /> Prerequisites: Hellforged Wonder of Sound<br /> <br /> The Emperor of Hellfire and Ash was forged to honor a musician who played the greatest song in the world for The King of Hell, and all later songs played on it glory in that tribute. This Evocation supplements a Performance action, reducing the target number for that action by one (normally to 6).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Munificent Synthesizer Emulation</b><br /> Cost: --, Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Malfeas-Pleasing Performance<br /> <br /> The Emperor of Hellfire and Ash hides within it the secrets of timbre, as well as pitch and volume. At no cost, the Emperor of Hellfire and Ash may produce the sound of any instrument the Exalt desires, eliminating any penalties for not having the proper instrument. A strum on the brass strings could produce the melodious whistle of a flute, the discordant blurt of a bagpipe, or even the percussive effects of a drum. Players are encouraged to use this as appropriate stunt fodder.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pied Guitarist of Hell</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: One Performance Action<br /> Prerequisites: Munificent Synthesizer Emulation<br /> <br /> The song performed by the first bearer of the Emperor of Hellfire and Ash brought the Brass Dancer to his feet, and when Malfeas rises to dance, all present follow suit. This Evocation functions as a Performance-based Instill action, made with (Essence) automatic successes. If the roll overcomes a target's Resolve, he or she gains a Minor Principle of &quot;I love to dance.&quot; Demons have their Resolve reduced by two against this effect, and the Intimacy so instilled is at Major strength. Repeated uses of this Evocation can increase the strength of an instilled Intimacy.<br /> <br /> <b>The Show Must Go On</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp Min: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisites: Pied Guitarist Of Hell<br /> <br /> The hatred and rage Malfeas feels towards the Solar Exalted knows no bounds, yet when the mortal performer exalted as a Zenith right in front of him, his hand was stayed by the quality and emotional resonance of the song. If Music can calm the rage of Malfeas then what being can resist being similarly swayed?<br /> <br /> This charm acts as a performance based Persuade action with (Essence) non-charm automatic successes against the guitarist's enemies to allow the musician and his allies to flee. This persuasion costs an extra point of Willpower to resist.<br /> <br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> Is this a fitting 4 dot artifact? How many more evocations on what level of power would be needed to make it 5 dot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:30:37-07:00","id":927739,"title":"","content":"I like it! I think it's definitely a 4-dot Artifact. I'd give it two or three more Evocations at Essence levels 3-5 to make it a five-dot, but I'm admittedly not very good at five-dot Artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T13:10:31-07:00","id":927752,"title":"","content":"5-dot would have to be huge. Not necessarily ultimate power, but a very broad and visible power. It should not be confused with something a mortal could do, it should be obviously powerful, even if it's not flashy. The important thing when designing an artifact is to keep the goal in mind. You don't want to branch out into multiple themes of a concept, it should fit a fairly narrow path through the concept. You wouldn't make an artifact bow that just fires all arrows better, you make a bow that fires arrows better in a specific situation, or that fires emotions instead of physical ammunition, or shoots the user to the target instead of an arrow.<br /> <br /> In the guitar's case, it shouldn't make all Performance better, it should make one representation of Performance better. So while this thing starts with just &quot;perform better&quot; the last evocation is about letting someone run away because of the music. It turns to distraction. If you keep that evocation, the next one should follow that theme, otherwise it's just a stat stick. So if the highest current power lets you run away, then the next power should build on that and grant you something when you use it to run away, or something like that. Charm-sets are designed to be your broad purpose powers. Artifacts are designed for specialization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T13:44:41-07:00","id":927767,"title":"","content":"In that case I think I'm happy with it being 4 dot. <br /> <br /> Now to wrack my brains for what to do about the razor claws and chain shirt Ligier made for Jubilant Harp (Both 3 dot).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T14:15:31-07:00","id":927776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927767#post927767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now to wrack my brains for what to do about the razor claws and chain shirt Ligier made for Jubilant Harp (Both 3 dot).</div> </div> </div> </div>Toss me themes for them both and I'll see what I can come up with!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T14:25:46-07:00","id":927778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927776#post927776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Toss me themes for them both and I'll see what I can come up with!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't really have themes on hand like I did for the Guitar. They were made by Ligier for Jubilant Harp so that he could be armed and armored as was proper for an Exalt of his stature. Ligier also taught him sorcery. While part of this was the genuine celebration of the excellent performance Jubilant Harp put on for Malfeas, an equally large part was Ligier putting Jubilant Harp in his debt. Which worked, Jubilant Harp has a Major Tie of Gratitude regarding Ligier.<br /> <br /> Other than Jubilant Harp being a performer first and foremost, I don't really have a theme in mind for what Ligier made, and the performance stuff seems like it most belongs with the guitar. Maybe the Razor Claws won't hinder fine manipulation needed for musical performance? But other than that I'm mostly stumped. <br /> <br /> Should I finalize a backstory for Jubilant Harp and give it to you, or would that not really help that much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T14:29:03-07:00","id":927780,"title":"","content":"Sounds like I've got what I need. You're welcome to send me his backstory, though! Is he a Martial Artist, or does he just like Razor Claws?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T14:32:33-07:00","id":927781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=927780#post927780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like I've got what I need. You're welcome to send me his backstory, though! Is he a Martial Artist, or does he just like Razor Claws?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He is a brawler, but has no formal training in any martial arts. He's a musician, and mostly learned how to fight in bar brawls and such. Ligier asked him what ammounts to: Brawl, Melee, Thrown, Archery, or Martial Arts. And Harp answered that he was a brawler more than anything else since he isn't primarily a fighter. So Ligier decided on the low key Razor Claws, for conceal-ability. Same with the chain shirt, not much point in making stuff for him that would out him as a solar when he got back to creation.<br /> <br /> I'm going to modify the Emperor of Hellfire and Ash to work fine for mortals as just exceptional equipment without needing attunement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 07-07-2016, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T07:47:28-07:00","id":928122,"title":"","content":"<b>Shirt of Wicked Brass (Orichalcum Chain Shirt - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> Forged in Hell by Ligier's green fire, the Shirt of Wicked Brass was a kingly gift for a Solar Exalt. Tainted in vitriol, the orichalcum links of the shirt have taken on a brass-like tinge, giving the shirt its name.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Shirt of Wicked Brass</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Infernal Exalt who attunes to the Shirt of Wicked Brass gains a non-Charm bonus die to all Resistance rolls against poison or disease.<br /> <br /> <b>Flash of Hellfire</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> When the light of Creation's Sun reflects off the brazen links of the Shirt of Wicked Brass, it casts a green hue. A skilled wearer can reflect this baleful light into the eyes of his opponent, blinding her. This Evocation is a difficulty 2 gambit made using the wearer's (Charisma + Performance). If successful, the target is blinded for the remainder of the scene, taking a -3 penalty to all actions. The target can remove this penalty by rubbing the green pain from her eyes, a Miscellaneous action which cannot be placed in a flurry.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Retribution of the Damned</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Counterattack, Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Flash of Hellfire<br /> <br /> Those who would strike the Shirt of Wicked Brass would feel the flames of Hell. The wielder may use this Evocation in response to any attack that beats his Defense, creating a special <b>decisive</b> counterattack that rolls (Charisma + Performance) against the target's Defense. This attack otherwise functions as a regular <b>decisive </b>attack. Retribution of the Damned does not count as the wearer's combat action and cannot be used in response to another counterattack.<br /> <br /> <b>Green Sun Wasting</b><br /> Cost: None (+1W); Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Retribution of the Damned<br /> <br /> Malfeas' ire is toxic; so, too, is the fire of Ligier's forge. This Evocation permanently enhances its prerequisite, allowing a successful counterattack to inflict a variant of Green Sun Wasting disease on the target for the cost of one temporary Willpower. This disease has Virulence 3, Morbidity of the wearer's Essence, and an Interval of one day. This disease can be fatal to mortals, and stories tell of even Exalted who have succumbed to it, though these are surely apocryphal...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":". 07-08-2016, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:31:36-07:00","id":928209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928122#post928122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shirt of Wicked Brass (Orichalcum Chain Shirt - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> Forged in Hell by Ligier's green fire, the Shirt of Wicked Brass was a kingly gift for a Solar Exalt. Tainted in vitriol, the orichalcum links of the shirt have taken on a brass-like tinge, giving the shirt its name.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Shirt of Wicked Brass</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Infernal Exalt who attunes to the Shirt of Wicked Brass gains a non-Charm bonus die to all Resistance rolls against poison or disease.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems solid<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928122#post928122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Flash of Hellfire</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> When the light of Creation's Sun reflects off the brazen links of the Shirt of Wicked Brass, it casts a green hue. A skilled wearer can reflect this baleful light into the eyes of his opponent, blinding her. This Evocation is a (Charisma + Performance) roll with (Essence) automatic successes against a target's Dodge Defense. If successful, the target is blinded for the remainder of the scene, taking a -3 penalty to all actions. The target can remove this penalty by rubbing the green pain from her eyes, a Miscellaneous action which cannot be placed in a flurry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this should be a Gambit, otherwise good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928122#post928122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Retribution of the Damned</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Counterattack, Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Flash of Hellfire<br /> <br /> Those who would strike the Shirt of Wicked Brass would feel the flames of Hell. The wielder may use this Evocation in response to any attack that beats his Defense, creating a special <b>decisive</b> counterattack that rolls (Charisma + Performance) against the target's Defense. This attack otherwise functions as a regular <b>decisive </b>attack. Retribution of the Damned does not count as the wearer's combat action and cannot be used in response to another counterattack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to insist on a Willpower cost to this, but you made it basically a copy of Solar Counterattack with a different die pool. I debate with myself whether costs should be balanced around the Solar charmset or not sometimes, but I might add a mote to this to be safe. Not required.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928122#post928122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Green Sun Wasting</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Retribution of the Damned<br /> <br /> Malfeas' ire is toxic; so, too, is the fire of Ligier's forge. This Evocation permanently enhances its prerequisite, allowing a successful counterattack to inflict a variant of Green Sun Wasting disease on the target. This disease has Virulence 3, Morbidity of the wearer's Essence, and an Interval of one day. This disease can be fatal to mortals, and stories tell of even Exalted who have succumbed to it, though these are surely apocryphal...</div> </div> </div> </div>I struggle with this being free, especially at Essence 2. In previous editions, Green Sun Wasting was NASTY and giving it an Interval of one day is nasty still. I think it's a great effect and I'm not convinced I'm qualified to comment on the strength of the disease itself, but I do feel it should have a cost associated with it. It can still be permanent, just an optional addon cost to Retribution of the Damned. <br /> <br /> Always happy to see more armor on here. Everyone wants to make weapons (I am extra guilty of this).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:34:02-07:00","id":928214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928122#post928122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shirt of Wicked Brass (Orichalcum Chain Shirt - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> Forged in Hell by Ligier's green fire, the Shirt of Wicked Brass was a kingly gift for a Solar Exalt. Tainted in vitriol, the orichalcum links of the shirt have taken on a brass-like tinge, giving the shirt its name.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Shirt of Wicked Brass</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Infernal Exalt who attunes to the Shirt of Wicked Brass gains a non-Charm bonus die to all Resistance rolls against poison or disease.<br /> <br /> <b>Flash of Hellfire</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> When the light of Creation's Sun reflects off the brazen links of the Shirt of Wicked Brass, it casts a green hue. A skilled wearer can reflect this baleful light into the eyes of his opponent, blinding her. This Evocation is a (Charisma + Performance) roll with (Essence) automatic successes against a target's Dodge Defense. If successful, the target is blinded for the remainder of the scene, taking a -3 penalty to all actions. The target can remove this penalty by rubbing the green pain from her eyes, a Miscellaneous action which cannot be placed in a flurry.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Retribution of the Damned</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Counterattack, Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Flash of Hellfire<br /> <br /> Those who would strike the Shirt of Wicked Brass would feel the flames of Hell. The wielder may use this Evocation in response to any attack that beats his Defense, creating a special <b>decisive</b> counterattack that rolls (Charisma + Performance) against the target's Defense. This attack otherwise functions as a regular <b>decisive </b>attack. Retribution of the Damned does not count as the wearer's combat action and cannot be used in response to another counterattack.<br /> <br /> <b>Green Sun Wasting</b><br /> Cost: None; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Retribution of the Damned<br /> <br /> Malfeas' ire is toxic; so, too, is the fire of Ligier's forge. This Evocation permanently enhances its prerequisite, allowing a successful counterattack to inflict a variant of Green Sun Wasting disease on the target. This disease has Virulence 3, Morbidity of the wearer's Essence, and an Interval of one day. This disease can be fatal to mortals, and stories tell of even Exalted who have succumbed to it, though these are surely apocryphal...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, what should the attunement cost for the Emperor of Hellfire and Ash be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 07-08-2016, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:37:53-07:00","id":928219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928209#post928209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this should be a Gambit, otherwise good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll need to brush up on my gambit rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928209#post928209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to insist on a Willpower cost to this, but you made it basically a copy of Solar Counterattack with a different die pool. I debate with myself whether costs should be balanced around the Solar charmset or not sometimes, but I might add a mote to this to be safe. Not required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Added a mote to the cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928209#post928209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I struggle with this being free, especially at Essence 2. In previous editions, Green Sun Wasting was NASTY and giving it an Interval of one day is nasty still. I think it's a great effect and I'm not convinced I'm qualified to comment on the strength of the disease itself, but I do feel it should have a cost associated with it. It can still be permanent, just an optional addon cost to Retribution of the Damned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Added a WP cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:44:20-07:00","id":928223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928219#post928219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll need to brush up on my gambit rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give it a difficulty. Disarms are 3, Unhorsing is 4, Distract is 3-5, Grappling is 2, so i'd guess a 2 or 3 probably is appropriate. Making it a gambit give it a small initiative cost (that you don't have to worry about) that allows it to be not entirely spammable. Requires very little change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T09:46:52-07:00","id":928224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928223#post928223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Give it a difficulty. Disarms are 3, Unhorsing is 4, Distract is 3-5, Grappling is 2, so i'd guess a 2 or 3 probably is appropriate. Making it a gambit give it a small initiative cost (that you don't have to worry about) that allows it to be not entirely spammable. Requires very little change.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Edit made!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T10:27:14-07:00","id":928239,"title":"","content":"<b>Claws of Brass and Fire (Orichalcum Razor Claws - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Claws of Brass and Fire</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Infernal Exalt who attunes to the Claws of Brass and Fire for one additional mote can re-roll one failed die on any attack roll made with the claws.<br /> <br /> <b>Claws Strike True</b><br /> Cost: 1m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The Claws of Brass and Fire hunger for their enemies' flesh, and strike true to taste it. This Evocation allows the wielder to re-roll up to (Essence) 1s on an attack roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Green Fire Claws</b><br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Claws Strike True<br /> <br /> The Claws of Brass and Fire live up to their name, bursting into flame at the moment of impact. Flammable materials catch fire when struck by this Evocation. A <b>decisive</b> attack adds one automatic success to its damage roll. If the attack deals at least three levels of damage, the target catches fire and must contend with (wielder's Essence) lethal dice of damage every turn until he's able to extinguish himself. Fire from this Evocation tends to leave wicked scars on any surface it touches, often burning words and Malfeas phrases in Old Realm into flesh, wood, or stone.<br /> <br /> <b>Lash of Hellfire</b><br /> Cost: 6m,3i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Green Fire Claws<br /> <br /> The flame of the claws can be hurled a short distance by a skilled wielder, lobbing a glob of waxy green fire at a target. An attack supplemented by this Evocation can be made at a target at up to Short range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":". 07-08-2016, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:13:35-07:00","id":928284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928214#post928214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, what should the attunement cost for the Emperor of Hellfire and Ash be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I'd say 2 or 3m, since basically all it does without the Evocations is give a minor enhancement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","av