 contend with (wielder's Essence) lethal dice of damage every turn until he's able to extinguish himself. Fire from this Evocation tends to leave wicked scars on any surface it touches, often burning words and Malfeas phrases in Old Realm into flesh, wood, or stone.<br /> <br /> <b>Lash of Hellfire</b><br /> Cost: 6m,3i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Green Fire Claws<br /> <br /> The flame of the claws can be hurled a short distance by a skilled wielder, lobbing a glob of waxy green fire at a target. An attack supplemented by this Evocation can be made at a target at up to Short range.</div> </div> </div> </div>I likes it. <br /> <br /> On the shirt, should the gambit for blinding use Cha+Performance rather than the normal attack pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T12:46:23-07:00","id":928352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928350#post928350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I likes it.<br /> <br /> On the shirt, should the gambit for blinding use Cha+Performance rather than the normal attack pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>I leave that question to the Unsung Hero. I'm inclined to say yes, but since my gambit-fu is weak, I'll wait to see what he has to say.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:47:36-07:00","id":928449,"title":"","content":"I'll put it down as being Charisma+Performance.<br /> <br /> Now Jubilant Harp is properly accoutermented. Let's see, my ISP Shining Topaz doesn't have any artifacts unless you count her Glorious Solar Saber, Twelve Facet Gem doesn't have any artifacts, Honorable Garnet doesn't have any, so it's just Hope's Last Gasp who has a Chain Shirt from the First Age that needs to be fluffed.<br /> <br /> Thank you for the help so far with Jubilant Harp's panoply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T15:01:43-07:00","id":928458,"title":"","content":"It's been my pleasure! I plan to post them to my 'blog when I'm done editing them, too, so they'll be available there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T15:31:15-07:00","id":928470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928458#post928458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been my pleasure! I plan to post them to my 'blog when I'm done editing them, too, so they'll be available there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could I get a link? I'd like to peruse your other artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T15:36:08-07:00","id":928475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928470#post928470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could I get a link? I'd like to peruse your other artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://s0.wp.com/i/blank.jpg?m=1383295312i\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> Octopoid Prevarication </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Foaming at the mouth about Exalted </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Absolutely!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T16:47:58-07:00","id":928504,"title":"","content":"I am stumped on the chain shirt for Hope's Last Gasp.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> In case anyone wants to take a crack at it while I try to think something up: Hope's Last Gasp is a Night Caste Solar who found the Chain Shirt in a safe house manse belonging to one of the previous holders of her Exaltation and was guided there by past life memories after escaping from the Dowager. The Chain Shirt is a normal 3 dot artifact, and it originally belonged to a First Age Night Caste who I have done zilch to develop because they aren't important beyond their memories guiding Hope to the safehouse manse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 07-08-2016, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T20:18:43-07:00","id":928570,"title":"","content":"This weapon is a work in progress and im looking for some help with how to make it work. I understand the final ability is similar to a solar charm but themed around ghosts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Soul Scream (Soulsteel grimscythe) Artifact 5:<br /> <br /> This Soul Steel Grimscythe was created using the souls of the innocent who had power but died before they could use it. Every soul used was selected for its relative skill, mortal sorcerers that mastered the art just before being slaughtered in some freak accident. Mortal Martial artists who had mastered his style and was days from the tournament, when he is struck down by disease. Each soul has a story and it\u2019s a tragedy. Each soul could have been either an abyssal or a solar exaltation in life. The deathlord who created it does not know what he has wrought. He sought to create a deadly scythe for future minions one that would tempt a solars with power. One that could teach the solar secrets and make him want to return for more. The souls of the scythe were not so easily controlled; because the deathlord created a means for a solar to interact with the scythe he created a way for a Zenith to heal the souls of the dead. Whether the Scythes deeper magic will still ensnare its wielder or the Zenith will be able to heal Soul Scream only time will tell.<br /> <br /> Evocations :<br /> Hearing the souls Wail<br /> Cost: - Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keyword: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Zenith<br /> Attuning the scythe unlocks this Evocation for a Zenith. If this Evocation is used none of the dark powers of the Soul Scream may be learned. Zenith caste solar that wields the Scythe may choose to spend an evening meditating on the voices within it, doing so he can muddle his way through the cacophony to find one ghost within the blade. In doing so he can pull forth that ghost and learn from it. The ghost in question must be cleared with the storyteller. If the Zenith accepts the teaching of the ghost he must take the ghosts defining intimacy into him. This intimacy is always somehow connected to the ghost\u2019s teachings. A martial artist ghost might desire the solar win a Martial arts tournament using his style.<br /> <br /> The Soul that Gathers<br /> Cost: 1m 1w Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keyword: Mute<br /> Duration: Until next action<br /> Prerequisites: Hearing the souls Wail<br /> <br /> With a mental request the solar pass the reigns of his spell from his own mind to a sorcerer within the weapon, allowing the ghost within the blade to maintain the spell while the sorcerer deals with the problem at hand.<br /> <br /> This evocation is used to supplemental any action that would lose the solar sorcery motes. Causing the Ghosts within the blade to take over the spell the ghost cannot pull any sorcerous motes but can prevent the loss of any motes.<br /> <br /> This Evocation can be reactive on the solar\u2019s next action to make the ghost continue to hold the spell for him I activated in this manner the willpower cost is waved.<br /> <br /> This ability specifically allows a solar attacked or faced with an emergency during a ritual casting to have the ghost continue the ritual while he deals with an emergency.<br /> <br /> Special requirement: In order to learn this evocation a solar must complete a task related to the sorcerer ghost\u2019s uncompleted task in life. Learning this charm removes the intimacy gained from that ghost forever and empowers the ghost with solar essence. Increase the committed cost of the scythe by 1 and if the ghost ever leaves the scythe it is no longer negatively affected by sunlight as its forever changed into a righteous dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Soul that Warns<br /> Cost 3m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Ref<br /> Keyword: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Hearing the Souls Wail<br /> <br /> The Souls in the scythe are aware of what is going on around them. In response to an attack that the solar is aware of the scythe will leap to his hand from up to short range to return to his hand allowing the solar to reflexively use his parry DV against the attack. This also readies the weapon for use.<br /> <br /> If the solar is asleep or otherwise unable to act the scythe will react if it is within close range it leaps to the solar\u2019s hand attempting to awaken him and ready him for the combat. This does not make the solar automatically aware of a the attack it just removes all penalties to his Per+Awarness due to his condition of being asleep, or similar penalty giving him a chance to notice the threat and defend against it. (Make a reflexive Per+Awarness roll to notice the attack or threat.)<br /> <br /> Special requirement: In order to learn this evocation a solar must complete a task related to the watchmen ghost\u2019s uncompleted task in life. Learning this charm removes the intimacy gained from that ghost forever and empowers the ghost with solar essence. Increase the committed cost of the scythe by 1 and if the ghost ever leaves the scythe it is no longer negatively affected by sunlight as its forever changed into a righteous dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Soul that Strikes<br /> Cost 4m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keyword: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Hearing the Souls Wail<br /> <br /> Within the Solars anima a ghostly image wielding a scythe appears and strikes with him. Any foe being struck by this combo strike is afflicted with the attack\u2019s onslaught penalty prior to the attack being resolved in addition this allows the solar to strike even incorporeal foes he cannot see without penalty, instead of the ghost following the solars strike in the solar follows the ghosts strike in. <br /> <br /> Special requirement: In order to learn this evocation a solar must complete a task related to the Martial artist\u2019s ghost\u2019s uncompleted task in life. Learning this charm removes the intimacy gained from that ghost forever and empowers the ghost with solar essence. Increase the committed cost of the scythe by 1 and if the ghost ever leaves the scythe it is no longer negatively affected by sunlight as its forever changed into a righteous dead.<br /> <br /> Three more Evocations still need to be thought up which means three more basic backstories need to be created.<br /> <br /> ____________________________________________<br /> <br /> <br /> Final Evocation<br /> Freeing the Righteous Souls<br /> Cost \u2013(20M 1W) Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keyword: Uniform<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: 6 ghosts intimacies completed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Learning this evocation permanently changes the function of the Soul Scream. It no longer is made of a metal that forever tortures its makeup ghosts instead the ghosts are freed from the pain and serve the purpose of destroying evil in all its forms. The soul steel becomes white instead of black. This scythe can no longer use the wicked powers that anyone but a zenith would put it to. Only a midnight caste could twist the weapon back to its former disfigured self.<br /> <br /> In addition the solar may now drag one of the ghosts free of the blade turning it into a familiar. This costs 20M and 1W. Build this ghost as a Heroic Mortal with an essence equal to the Solars. The Heroic mortal has half the Solars EXP (And gains half the solars exp after creation) and the ghost charms: Chilling touch, apparition, and materialize. The ghost picks up charms as a solar. The ghost is limited to Celestial circle sorcery and cannot use mastery effects of Martial arts.<br /> <br /> The ghost is also considered to be among the righteous dead. These ghosts are blessed by the unconquered sun and have no fear of sunlight.<br /> In addition while a ghost is removed from the scythe its evocation is unavailable for use by the solar.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8767-rattleingpython","name":"rattleingpython","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:40:01-07:00","id":929942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=928504#post928504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am stumped on the chain shirt for Hope's Last Gasp.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> In case anyone wants to take a crack at it while I try to think something up: Hope's Last Gasp is a Night Caste Solar who found the Chain Shirt in a safe house manse belonging to one of the previous holders of her Exaltation and was guided there by past life memories after escaping from the Dowager. The Chain Shirt is a normal 3 dot artifact, and it originally belonged to a First Age Night Caste who I have done zilch to develop because they aren't important beyond their memories guiding Hope to the safehouse manse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually just musing on what would be useful light artifact armor for a Night with a Dodge/Stealth focus who gets hit very rarely (and thus won't benefit much from soak), and came up with this:<br /> <br /> <b>Eye of the Storm (White Jade Artifact Breastplate ***)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A simple artifact breastplate composed of white jade, with a single hearthstone socket at the center of its chest.<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement:</b><br /> A Solar who attunes to Eye of the Storm automatically awakens Sandstorm at no cost.<br /> <br /> <b>Sandstorm</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m, 1wp, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> With a small push of her Essence, the Solar causes the white jade of the armor to resonate with the local earth. It grinds at the surface of hard marbles and stones, sending flecks into the air, and kicks up sand and dirt. This Evocation may only be used so long as there is a reasonable quantity of elementally-appropriate materials in the surrounding area; if there is not, the Solar will realize it before she spends her motes.<br /> <br /> Once the various materials have been clawed at by the power of her armor, they're thrown into a whirlwind of sand, dust, dirt, and other particulates. As they spin through the air, they inflict a -3 penalty to Awareness rolls to see into or within the whirlwind, as the materials obscure everything within close range of the Solar. This Evocation lasts so long as the Solar wishes it to continue, but she can allow her Essence to lax at any time, causing the whirlwind to quickly end and leaving the various materials strewn around. If the Solar moves range bands, the effect follows her, becoming refreshed by new materials as she moves, other bits being left in her wake.<br /> <br /> Note that this Evocation does not manipulate the air within the storm, only the earth. While it can knock over objects, irritate enemies, and serve as fodder for stunts, it cannot be used to, for example, protect the Solar from a toxic gas.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremor Discernment Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sandstorm<br /> This Evocation enhances an Awareness roll made within the effect of Sandstorm. The Solar reaches out through the resonant white jade, sensing through the maelstrom she stands at the center of. She ignores the normal penalty to Awareness rolls inflicted by Sandstorm, and further, adds a single non-Charm success to her roll. This boost represents a tactile sense for the maelstrom that surrounds her, and as such cannot be applied to objects beyond close range, Awareness rolls relying on differentiating light or color, or similar effects. Awareness Charms which boost the Solar's sense of touch also boost Awareness rolls made using Tremor Discernment Technique.<br /> <br /> <b>Turbulent Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sandstorm<br /> This Evocation enhances an attack made from within the raging chaos of Sandstorm. The kicked up particulates seem to start to die down, coalescing near one another, before the Solar makes her sudden strike. Whether the Solar is making a withering or decisive attack, this Evocation creates a withering attack just before it.<br /> <br /> This withering attack is made with (Dex + combat ability used for the attack it supplements), has a base damage of 10 dice, and Overwhelming 3. It has no inherent accuracy boosts and does not gain a damage bonus from Strength. This bonus attack has its Initiative damage applied before the Solar rolls her subsequent attack. Any Defense penalty for being subject to surprise applies to both attacks.<br /> <br /> Once this Evocation is used, the effect of Sandstorm ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Mother Earth's Caress</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Turbulent Strike<br /> This Evocation enhances its prerequisite. After the chaotic whirl of rock and earth strikes her target, it returns to the Solar, covering her from head to toe in a cake of mud and stone as it resonates with Eye of the Storm, enhanced by the Earth-flavored Essence of her armor. After making an attack enhanced by Turbulent Strike, the Solar increases her soak by six until the end of her next turn. Activating Sandstorm again immediately ends this effect.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's pretty much a first draft and I don't have much experience making artifacts, though. (I wrote it thinking breastplate but you could scratch that out and replace it with Chain Shirt without any problems, I think.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12048,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12048-lvthn","user":"LVTHN","date":". 07-11-2016, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12048-lvthn","name":"LVTHN","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T12:27:57-07:00","id":930469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LVTHN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=929942#post929942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eye of the Storm</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really interesting! Using White Jade for Stealth is a very clever idea, can't really give mechanical advice but it seems like a very good first draft and very thematically interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T12:27:57-07:00","id":930470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LVTHN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=929942#post929942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eye of the Storm</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really interesting! Using White Jade for Stealth is a very clever idea, can't really give mechanical advice but it seems like a very good first draft and very thematically interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T12:27:57-07:00","id":930471,"title":"","content":"Not sure why the system posted it three times","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T13:22:25-07:00","id":930494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LVTHN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=929942#post929942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Eye of the Storm (White Jade Artifact Breastplate ***)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Attunement:</b><br /> A Solar who attunes to Eye of the Storm automatically awakens Sandstorm at no cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Dragon-Blooded should be able to gain all of these benefits as well. Especially since it's Jade. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LVTHN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=929942#post929942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sandstorm</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m, 1wp, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> With a small push of her Essence, the Solar causes the white jade of the armor to resonate with the local earth. It grinds at the surface of hard marbles and stones, sending flecks into the air, and kicks up sand and dirt. This Evocation may only be used so long as there is a reasonable quantity of elementally-appropriate materials in the surrounding area; if there is not, the Solar will realize it before she spends her motes.<br /> <br /> Once the various materials have been clawed at by the power of her armor, they're thrown into a whirlwind of sand, dust, dirt, and other particulates. As they spin through the air, they inflict a -3 penalty to Awareness rolls to see into or within the whirlwind, as the materials obscure everything within close range of the Solar. This Evocation lasts so long as the Solar wishes it to continue, but she can allow her Essence to lax at any time, causing the whirlwind to quickly end and leaving the various materials strewn around. If the Solar moves range bands, the effect follows her, becoming refreshed by new materials as she moves, other bits being left in her wake.<br /> <br /> Note that this Evocation does not manipulate the air within the storm, only the earth. While it can knock over objects, irritate enemies, and serve as fodder for stunts, it cannot be used to, for example, protect the Solar from a toxic gas.</div> </div> </div> </div>After reading the later charms I would probably make this a Simple evocation (don't forget to change all instances of the word Charm to Evocation) instead of Reflexive. It makes more interesting combat choices later on if using Turbulent Strike and how it stops the Sandstorm actually mattered. As long as it's Reflexive, it's just a matter of mote costs. Speaking of which, I'm somewhat inclined to make this 5 so it's considered for Anima purposes (since it's a fairly overt effect).<br /> <br /> All of that said, it's a very COOL effect and a great opener for this armor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LVTHN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=929942#post929942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Tremor Discernment Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sandstorm<br /> This Evocation enhances an Awareness roll made within the effect of Sandstorm. The Solar reaches out through the resonant white jade, sensing through the maelstrom she stands at the center of. She ignores the normal penalty to Awareness rolls inflicted by Sandstorm, and further, adds a single non-Charm success to her roll. This boost represents a tactile sense for the maelstrom that surrounds her, and as such cannot be applied to objects beyond close range, Awareness rolls relying on differentiating light or color, or similar effects. Awareness Charms which boost the Solar's sense of touch also boost Awareness rolls made using Tremor Discernment Technique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems a solid power. Might be overcosted by a single mote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LVTHN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=929942#post929942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Turbulent Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sandstorm<br /> This Evocation enhances an attack made from within the raging chaos of Sandstorm. The kicked up particulates seem to start to die down, coalescing near one another, before the Solar makes her sudden strike. Whether the Solar is making a withering or decisive attack, this Evocation creates a withering attack just before it.<br /> <br /> This withering attack is made with (Dex + combat ability used for the attack it supplements), has a base damage of 10 dice, and Overwhelming 3. It has no inherent accuracy boosts and does not gain a damage bonus from Strength. This bonus attack has its Initiative damage applied before the Solar rolls her subsequent attack. Any Defense penalty for being subject to surprise applies to both attacks.<br /> <br /> Once this Evocation is used, the effect of Sandstorm ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a few issues with this one. It's very cheap for an extra attack, so some questions. Does the exalt gain the initiative lost in this attack or is it just stripping it away from the foe? If they do gain it, this is very powerful to be able to gain initiative and turn around and Decisive in the same action. Not a lot of effects that allow that (if any) and none of them are just 3m. I think it would be awesome if this merely stripped it away and the exalt didn't gain it, but if that's not your direction that's fair. But it should be adjusted accordingly. (Especially since surprise counts for BOTH attacks, an effect that doesn't exist anywhere else)<br /> <br /> So I could see it being fine as is if the exalt doesn't gain any initiative, it merely strips it away. If that's not up your alley, I might make it Withering-Only where you can't follow it up with a Decisive so it's just a bigger advantage gainer. If you want to keep it Uniform, I'd make this 5m, 1wp because that's beefy. Oh and I'd probably also say that <i>might </i>make this an Essence 3 power. My 2 cents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LVTHN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=929942#post929942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mother Earth's Caress</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Turbulent Strike<br /> This Evocation enhances its prerequisite. After the chaotic whirl of rock and earth strikes her target, it returns to the Solar, covering her from head to toe in a cake of mud and stone as it resonates with Eye of the Storm, enhanced by the Earth-flavored Essence of her armor. After making an attack enhanced by Turbulent Strike, the Solar increases her soak by six until the end of her next turn. Activating Sandstorm again immediately ends this effect.[/spoiler]<br /> <br /> It's pretty much a first draft and I don't have much experience making artifacts, though. (I wrote it thinking breastplate but you could scratch that out and replace it with Chain Shirt without any problems, I think.)</div> </div> </div> </div>A very cool power. I'm debating whether it feels to strong to gain free soak after delivering a super powerful attack (discussed above). The nit-picker in me wants to put an added cost on to this, or make it more powerful and make it an alternative way to end Sandstorm instead of Turbulent Strike. As it is, it's not really strong enough to be an Essence 3 power. <br /> <br /> Here's an idea. What if you swapped Mother Earth's Caress and Turbulent Strike? Make this a 3m evocation to end Sandstorm, but unleash it from yourself as a sudden attack with Turbulent Strike at essence 3? I could see that.<br /> <br /> Just some ideas to mull over. A great armor and I really like the concept. A lot! I'd allow it (in a form) in my game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T15:17:14-07:00","id":930544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=930494#post930494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Dragon-Blooded should be able to gain all of these benefits as well. Especially since it's Jade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. There's not really Dragon-Blooded rules and I get the vibe from the core that DB Evocations are going to be less powerful than Solar Evocations. e.g. Volcano Cutter only mentions Solars, there's talk about how unless otherwise noted these Evocations are only for Solars, etc.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=930494#post930494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading the later charms I would probably make this a Simple evocation (don't forget to change all instances of the word Charm to Evocation) instead of Reflexive. It makes more interesting combat choices later on if using Turbulent Strike and how it stops the Sandstorm actually mattered. As long as it's Reflexive, it's just a matter of mote costs. Speaking of which, I'm somewhat inclined to make this 5 so it's considered for Anima purposes (since it's a fairly overt effect).<br /> <br /> All of that said, it's a very COOL effect and a great opener for this armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Re: Simple, when designing the Evocations, I was thinking of how they combined with Solar Charms, particularly Stalking Wolf Attitude. If it's Simple, and SWA is Simple, that's two turns (e: three turns, you also have to enter stealth) working to kick off your Stealth bonuses, which is a lot of time.<br /> <br /> On the cost: yeah, it's overt, but it's intended to combo with Stealth actions, so making it cost 5m seems really harsh for combat (at least if you're not a Night - though, thinking about it, non-Nights do just generally kind of get fucked on any hope of doing a Stealth against a peer-level opponent in a fight), since flaring at the lowest level gives you a -3 and flaring past that makes Stealth outright impossible. I guess I could maybe tick it up a bit more and make it Mute.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=930494#post930494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few issues with this one. It's very cheap for an extra attack, so some questions. Does the exalt gain the initiative lost in this attack or is it just stripping it away from the foe? If they do gain it, this is very powerful to be able to gain initiative and turn around and Decisive in the same action. Not a lot of effects that allow that (if any) and none of them are just 3m. I think it would be awesome if this merely stripped it away and the exalt didn't gain it, but if that's not your direction that's fair. But it should be adjusted accordingly. (Especially since surprise counts for BOTH attacks, an effect that doesn't exist anywhere else)<br /> <br /> So I could see it being fine as is if the exalt doesn't gain any initiative, it merely strips it away. If that's not up your alley, I might make it Withering-Only where you can't follow it up with a Decisive so it's just a bigger advantage gainer. If you want to keep it Uniform, I'd make this 5m, 1wp because that's beefy. Oh and I'd probably also say that <i>might </i>make this an Essence 3 power. My 2 cents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's kind-of-like 7m 1wp, since it burns Sandstorm, but you're probably right on the cost. I feel less and less sure about how it works as I think on it, to the point that I'll probably replace it with a different decisive-boosting effect (like, say, an accuracy booster).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12048,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12048-lvthn","user":"LVTHN","date":". 07-12-2016, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12048-lvthn","name":"LVTHN","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T16:53:48-07:00","id":930591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LVTHN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=929942#post929942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually just musing on what would be useful light artifact armor for a Night with a Dodge/Stealth focus who gets hit very rarely (and thus won't benefit much from soak), and came up with this:</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually quite helpful. I have a smidgeon of inspiration. I want a chain shirt that helps with stealth, so I've named it the Armor of Wily Murk, and it's attunement bonus is an automatic success on the larceny roll to conceal it.<br /> <br /> Not sure what the actual evocations should be at the moment, I checked the Stealth charms, and there doesn't seem to be a full Excellency charm that I could see so the Capstone in my head is currently 1wp=free excellency, since that seems to be an Essence 3 effect. Kinda stumped on the materials and the evocations that would come first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T16:56:18-07:00","id":930592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LVTHN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=930544#post930544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. There's not really Dragon-Blooded rules and I get the vibe from the core that DB Evocations are going to be less powerful than Solar Evocations. e.g. Volcano Cutter only mentions Solars, there's talk about how unless otherwise noted these Evocations are only for Solars, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>No rules yet, you're correct. But it is stated multiple times that the Dragon-Blooded are <b>near equals </b>to the Solars in regards to Evocations, and there are examples in the book of Artifacts that multiple exalt types gain the benefits from.<br /> -Moonlit Huntress, made of Moonsilver, grants it's powers to a Solar or a Lunar<br /> -Spring Razor, made of Green Jade, grants its powers to a Solar or Dragon-Blooded<br /> -Freedom's Cadence, made of Starmetal, grants its powers to Sidereal, Solar, or Getimian<br /> <br /> So if it's a Solar-Only Artifact to you, then so be it. Go for it, I won't tell you it's wrong. ^_^ Just saying that there's precedent in the core and it felt thematically appropriate for Dragon-Blooded to me. That's my feedback. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, I dig it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T17:48:36-07:00","id":930615,"title":"","content":"<b>Armor of Wily Murk (Chain Shirt ***)</b><br /> <br /> [INSERT BACKSTORY HERE]<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Armor of Wily Murk</b><br /> <br /> An Exalt who attunes the Armor of Wily Murk gains an automatic success on the larceny roll to conceal it.<br /> <br /> <b>Hidden by Glare or Darkness Method</b><br /> Cost: 5m,2wp; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Ignore all penalties to stealth based roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Assassin\u2019s Agility Prana </b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Mute, Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Hidden by Glare or Darkness Method<br /> <br /> Supplements an attack made by another ability, if that attack is made from stealth it counts as an ambush.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cover of Darkness Approach</b><br /> Cost: ???; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisites: Assassin's Agility Prana<br /> <br /> Creates a fog of darkness that reaches to short range. Everybody in the cloud except the wearer takes a penalty to all awareness or perception rolls equal to the wearer's Essence.<br /> <br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> It should be noted that I do not feel good about this artifact. The thematics seem confused, I'm not sure if the effects are in the right order, and overall it doesn't sit well with me. Any advice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T20:35:35-07:00","id":930688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=930615#post930615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted that I do not feel good about this artifact. The thematics seem confused, I'm not sure if the effects are in the right order, and overall it doesn't sit well with me. Any advice?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Come up with a simple dynamic or mechanic that you could probably build an Evocation set around. It should be fairly straightforward, and represent something that's true <i>in-universe</i> about the artifact. It's not a bundle of game mechanics (though it is that), it's also something actually physically true about the item. For Eye of the Storm, my original concept was &quot;smokescreen stealth armor.&quot;<br /> 2) Select a magical material that is thematically resonant with the core mechanic. For Eye of the Storm, I considered several other magical materials before settling on White Jade.<br /> 3) Combine the two. You've got a core dynamic and a clear thematic space, mix them together and see what comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12048-lvthn","name":"LVTHN","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T05:18:32-07:00","id":930780,"title":"","content":"Bonecrusher, defender of Palanquin, Starmetal Goremaul ; Artifact 3:<br /> The Goremaul Bonecrusher is mounted on a two yard long haft of black ebony, strenghened by an network of thin starmetal wires entwining the heavy wood in patterns, that are almost impossible to follow with the eyes. The head is styled as an open framework of starmetal bands, embracing a block of white marble, into which the signs of the maidens have been cut.<br /> ----<br /> The Sidereal had forseen the fate of millions for decades and aeons, and as they knew fate, they made weapons well in advance of their eventual use. From the bones of a fallen beast from the first age, the forgotten ones made the marble for Bonecrushers head, from the fate of a royal family they grew the ebony tree that its shaft is made from and when a horror long forgotten struck in the dreaming sea a milennium ago, it was ready since years, wielded by one of the battle maiden's chosen. However, knowing it was not meant to leave Palanquin, the Sidereal left it in the hands of Gewlin, a local god of decay, to hold it until a worthy one would awaken and slay the last of the horrible monsters that had invaded back then. Now... This time has come.<br /> ----<br /> The Goremaul can be wielded by any celestial exalt, but can not leave the archipellagio that Palanquin raises above. If someone tries to bring it away - either by carrying it or by trying to summon it to such a place from Elsewhere - Bonecrusher stops to be attuned to him and immediately reappears in the tomb where Gelwlin keeps it safe.<br /> <br /> <br /> Evocations:<br /> <b>Speech from Beyond</b><br /> Bonecrusher can speak in the mind of its wielder through flashes of past lifes, but it only does so if the wielder is either a Sidereal or has fed it with at least 15 initiative through Feast of Decay on the same day.<br /> <b>Feast of Decay</b><br /> Cost: - Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> <br /> If wielded in battle, Bonecrusher longs to feed its hunger for the undead and the unchanging. If an attack on the wielder fails, it glows up and tendrils of starlight stretch for the opponent, consuming 1 initiative for each 1 in the enemy's attack roll. The maximum initiative it can feed on per round is the wielder's essence or 3, whichever is higher. Should the wielder be a Sidereal Exalt, Bonecrusher adds half of that (rounded down) to the user's initiative. In case the opponent is undead, there is no maximum ammount Bonecrusher can consume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T10:19:20-07:00","id":930922,"title":"","content":"<b>Warplate of Primeval Glory (Artifact </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <b>Green Jade &amp; Moonsilver Articulated Plate)</b><br /> <br /> This ancient armour was created at the dawn of the Exalted, one among countless weapons forged to arm the Celestial host against beings of untold might. Its soul was bathed in the blood of beings older than the world itself and its first memories are of exulting in acts of unimaginable audacity and carnage as Creation itself was bled in this war.<br /> <br /> It grew to crave glory and the most savage parts of battle, the thrill of throwing oneself against impossible odds and achieving things that would break the minds of mortals. For all of the power that it offered it was not frequently worn during the First Age for its vicious nature often proved as damaging to the world around it as it did to its foes, that it began to appear in an ever-growing series of engagements was just one of the innumerable signs of the Sun-Kings growing madness. The ancient city of Sil\u2019Vat was where its final bearer met her end at the hands of her soldiers even as her rage brought the city down with her, the Warplate still lies at the bottom of the vast mountain of marble rouble now known as White Sil.<br /> <br /> Despite its vicious nature the armour itself is in fact quite mesmerizing to behold, intricate murals run across his form. The murals of silver beasts and green vines seem to illustrate countless encounters versus predator and prey speak, exulting in the nature of competition and the glory of the victor. The armour itself has a simplicity to its outline which favours efficiency of action. It is tradition for this those who wear the armour to be referred to as War-Beasts.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Warplate of Primeval Glory</b><br /> Attunement: Committing an additional three motes when attuning, to treat all unarmed actions as Light Artifact, in addition while the Warplate is attuned all wound penalties are treated as one level less in severity, this explicitly stacks with any charm that renders a similar effect. However the Warplate deals one lethal level of damage when attuning or becoming unattuned.<br /> <br /> <b>Dragon-Devouring Lung Expansion</b><br /> Cost: 2wp Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Day<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The war-beast howls as green jade digs into their lungs expanding their ability to respire essence for a single battle, this charm severely taxes the chakra\u2019s of the exalt which take their toll after the heat of battle ends. Gain +(E/2, rounded up) motes per turn for the duration of a battle, take (Essence) levels of lethal damage at the end. Upon deactivation the Exalt takes (Essence) levels of lethal damage due to the punishing nature of this charm.<br /> Repeated usage of this charm in the same area will eventually begin to make the life in the area wither away as it is drained of essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Triumphant Underdog\u2019s Roar</b><br /> Cost: - Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Dragon-Devouring Lung Expansion<br /> <br /> There is no glory in overcoming a weakling, but the euphoria of overcoming a far greater foe is truly unspeakable. After successfully grappling a foe of an Essence rating at least two dots greater than that of the Exalt immediately regain one temporary willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Reality-Shattering Grip</b><br /> Cost: Varies Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Triumphant Underdog\u2019s Roar<br /> <br /> Howling with suicidal audacity the exalt grapples what most men could not comprehend attacking and essence rips through their body as they do the impossible. This charm can be used in one of two ways, first it can be used to supplement any Brawl-based action targeting an immaterial or titanic being by paying 3m, 1wp for every two dots of Essence by which the target outranks the solar, rounded down.<br /> <br /> The second use of this charm is to supplement Feats of Strength against enormous targets or targets which are not solid (rivers, clouds, etc.). This is paid in the same fashion as the primary usage of the charm with Essence being treated as equivalent to (rank on Feat of Strength table/3, rounded down).<br /> <br /> This Charm explicitly ignores any difficulties that may be caused by the targets nature. Furthermore, should the exalt already know Titan-Straightening Method they may forgo the Willpower cost of this charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 07-13-2016, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T11:32:29-07:00","id":930951,"title":"","content":"My pirate captain has one <b>Surging Monsoon</b> goremaul. It's a mostly orichalcum hammer retrieved from the depths, during a scavenge gone awry.<br /> It's themed around, as the name says, sudden storms and tides, and the motion associated with those things.<br /> <br /> I want to build for it evocations around area attacks, bonuses against battlegroups and stormy weather. Ultimately it'll be able to evoke an actual monsoon and capitalize on that.<br /> Right now we have the attunement bonus: Solars attuned to Surging Monsoon waive the defense penalty for smashing attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T18:21:58-07:00","id":931115,"title":"","content":"Hello all, can anyone provide some assistance for creating an armor that allows you to summon the equivalent of mortal thrown weapons? I was thinking Darts, as Javelins would be slipping into melee although that would be just as good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T22:55:55-07:00","id":931200,"title":"","content":"I'd like some feedback on custom evocations for a spell in my game, I'v never written evocations myself before, so I'd like some feedback.<br /> To start, the spell is called Mantle of the Fire Dragon, and is mechanically wood dragon's claws, except it is fire, and uses thrown instead of brawl. The character I'm playing that I want these for is a sorcerer who specializes in fire magic and was raised by fire elementals.<br /> My out-of-character goals with these evocations are to get a useful and fun set of abilities that are mostly used to bolster withering attacks (we have encountered several high soak opponents so far and I'd like to have a bit more on tap for dealing with that), and the native thrown tree doesn't really have much on the withering damage side either. After the details of each evocation is my thinking behind it.<br /> <br /> <b>Gathering The Flames</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keyword: </b><br /> <b>Duration</b>: One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> This evocation allows the sorcerer who has mastered Mantle of the Fire Dragon to stoke the flames generated by that spell, coaxing them to even greater heights. The sorcerer gains a charge of Gathered Flame to a maximum of Essence. Each charge adds 1 to withering damage (pre-soak) and later charms may expend them for dramatic effects. This charm may only be used once per turn.<br /> <i>This is meant to be a slow-ish build up effect to have a little bit more oomph for long fights as well as a resource to leverage with further evocation.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Fire-Stoked Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m/die ; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keyword: </b> Withering-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Gathering The Flames<br /> The Sorcerer channels their passions into the flame, fueling it's rage. This evocation allows the sorcerer to enhance an attack made with the flames against a target towards whom the sorcerer has a negative intimacy or who has attacked someone the sorcerer has a positive intimacy towards. The Sorcerer adds one die per mote to the post-soak damage. The sorcerer may add a maximum number of dice equal to his current charges of Gathered Flames.<br /> <i>This is a straight-up damage adder, since the native solar charmset seems to lack those for some inexplicable reason, it is basically just fire-and-stones strike re-skinned for flames.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Falling Ember Rain</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m 1wp 2+charges ; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keyword: </b> Withering-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Fire-Stoked Strike<br /> The Sorcerer releases the fires they have been building up in a vortex of flame. This Charm generates a number of withering attacks equal to the number of charges spent (the charges do not add to the damage of these rolls) These attacks can be at multiple targets or the same target. The Sorcerer gains only half the normal amount of initiative (rounded up) that they would normally gain from each attack.<br /> <i>I wanted a multiattack charm and based this one off of Errant Orbit Scythe from Black wind.</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Flame's Resolve</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m ; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keyword: </b> none<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Gathering The Flames<br /> The true flame that burns in the heart does not fear conflict or turn away, the sorcerer may add his current charges as a bonus to resolve against any social influence or mental effect that would cause him to flee the battlefield.<br /> <i>To date all of the combats my character has used this spell in have been ones he could have walked away from but chose not to, I'm trying to reflect his choices in its growing legend.</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Fire Does Not Fade</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1+ charges ; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keyword: </b> None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> The Flame's Resolve<br /> The Sorcerer can feed the fires around them into their passions, burning away magical effects that would compel him to alter his course. The Sorcerer may spend any number of charges in place of willpower points to resist mental effects or social influence.<br /> <i>This seemed like a decent extension of the themes from Flame's Resolve, tying it into the Gathered Flames mechanic. Not sure if this should be permanent or a reflexive charm?</i><br /> <br /> <b>Cataclysm</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m 1wp all charges; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keyword: </b>Withering-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Falling Ember Rain, The Fire Does Not Fade<br /> The Sorcerer gathers all of the flames around him and purges them in one cataclysmic detonation that leaves opponents fleeing or broken. This is a withering attack against a battle-group, that does double damage after rolling. Each charge expended adds one automatic success to the attack and damage rolls (After doubling)<br /> <i>Not too sure about the mechanics of this one, it might be a bit too powerful, or maybe not considering things like Leaping Tiger Attack exist. In any event I really wanted a charm to represent a huge fire falling on a battle-group.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9124,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","user":"satoshi","date":". 07-14-2016, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T18:18:19-07:00","id":931734,"title":"","content":"Hello all, I was looking at Righteous Devil Style and thinking of ways to expand it's use with another martial art unfortunately you are restricted to using White Reaper normally, so I thought how about a pair of artifact pistols that allow other martial arts to be used with them, when in hand to hand? So I wrote these up in about an hour, so does anyone have any suggestions. I have tried to keep them conceptually clean without completely breaking the game with their evocations, and special ability. <br /> <br /> <b>(PEACH)</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Twin Dragons</b><br /> These Red Jade, Star Metal, and Orichalum artifact flame pieces were crafted for the legendary Silver Flame, a night caste of some repute who used them to quell a number of criminal organizations, before finally being killed in the death throes of the Black Goat with a Thousand Young, after striking the final blow. (HP Lovecraft Reference) Placed with reverence in the tomb of the Silver Flame, these have been lost to Creation for nearly 2 millennia and were recently looted by a Scavenger Lord working for a House Ragara. <br /> <br /> <b>Twin Dragons:</b><br /> -Artifact 4 (Artifact 3 for only one)<br /> -Attunement: 5 (8 as a pair)<br /> -Medium Artifact Weapon<br /> -Tags: Lethal, Archery (Short), Flame, Mounted, One-Handed, Slow<br /> <br /> -Special: When used as a pair they are allowed to function as artifact chopping swords for the purposes of martial arts charms using the following stats. While still being allowed to use Righteous Devil Style charms if using Righteous Devil Form.<br /> <br /> <b>Twin Dragons:</b><br /> -Medium Artifact Weapon<br /> -Tags: Lethal, Martial Arts, Chopping<br /> <br /> Evocations:<br /> <b>Twin Dragons Roar</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m ; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keyword: </b>Counter-attack, Decisive<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <b>Fluff: </b>Having lost their owner once they roar in triumph when used to strike aside attacks meant to harm their attuned wielder. <br /> <b>Mechanics: </b>When the wielder successfully strikes with a clashing attack, he may make a decisive attack using the weapons ranged attacks stats. <br /> <br /> <b>Dragon's Unblinking Eyes</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m ; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keyword: </b>none<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Twin Dragons Roar<br /> <b>Fluff: </b>The dragons are awake once more, and shall remain vigilant using their claws to punish the Unjust.<br /> <b>Mechanics: </b>When making a melee attack in which you get a bonus for aiming, add Essence non-charm dice to the attack roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T21:29:22-07:00","id":931801,"title":"","content":"Okay, so if I get this right, these are Flame Pieces that, if wielded as a pair, can also function as Reaver Daiklaves<br /> <br /> Which is a little weird given that those are usually wielded two-handed, but let's not nitpick.<br /> <br /> The really weird part is that the evocations read more like daiklaves with a gunslinger twist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=931734#post931734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mechanics: </b>When the wielder successfully strikes with a clashing attack, he may make a decisive attack using the weapons ranged attacks stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I'm not sure if I get what makes this worthwhile. Close Range is terrible for Archery (as opposed to being optimal for Thrown), and even if it weren't, the decisive attack has no weapon accuracy modifiers, nor does it add to its damage.<br /> <br /> This one needs to go back to the drawing board unless I'm really missing something.<br /> <br /> Clash is a solid point to work with here in the evocations (of which I honestly think there should probably be more)--ideally, a wielder is carrying both at once, meaning they already get a bonus to their Clash pools.<br /> <br /> These also have a quirk inasmuch as most artifact weapons have some sort of benefit just for attuning them. Sometimes it's a small bonus, sometimes it's an evocation already unlocked. But these lack that. If that's a deliberate decision, that's fine. But I'm just noting it for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 07-15-2016, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T23:18:19-07:00","id":931841,"title":"","content":"Well Reaver Daiklaves are only 1 handed, the evocation isn't that terrible for flame weapons as they ignore the penalty anyway and its a free out of action attack similar to One Weapon Two Blows but requires clashing which seemed OK to me, but I might be biased. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T01:07:52-07:00","id":931886,"title":"","content":"I made this thing:<br /> <span style=\"color:#860658\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Peace:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#860658\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">(Soulsteel Reaper Daiklave, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Once upon a time there was a great, Old Realm built upon the broken backs of slain Titans, Then there was great uprising and the Old Realm was no more. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Once upon a time there was a great Shogunate built upon the broken back of a golden age. Then there was a great contagion and the Shogunate was no more. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Once upon a time there was an Age of Sorrows built upon the broken back of a Shogunate. Then there will be a final sigh and the Age of Sorrows will be no more.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">This is the story told by the blade known as Peace, a wickedly sharp Soulsteel Reaper Daiklave. It\u2019s blade is completely black, light doesn\u2019t reflect, the dirt carried on wind leaves no impression on it, not even the faces of the dead can be seen in it. Only a single scripture in inlaid meteoric iron may be glimpsed upon the blade:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cOnce there was a dying maiden</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">She was very sick</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Her father tried to help her by stealing</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">But he was thrown in prison</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Then her mother resorted to selling herself</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">But she was scorned and cast away</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Then the maiden pleaded for her life</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">But nobody answered her prayers</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cSuch is my lot in life\u201d Said the maiden who was Creation\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The blade has participated in many battles, most importantly it served in the hands of one of the Deathknights who aided in the taking of Thorns for the Mask of Winters, it has slain five Dragon-Blooded, one of each Aspect, and their blood colors the inscriptions in the blade a fine red.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The original owner of the blade is long dead, slain by the arrows of vengeful Dragons, but his blade remains, lodged in the corpse of a dead Deathknight. The blade lies alone in a grove to the southeast of Thorns, where it\u2019s presence has formed a minor Shadowland, the hungry ghost of it\u2019s previous owner yet defends it with tooth and claw, but even he cannot protect it forever.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#860658\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Evocations of Peace</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A Solar or Abyssal attuned to Peace gains An End to Dreams at no cost, other Exalts must awaken it as usual.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#860658\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>An End to Dreams</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Cost</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mins</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Type</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Simple</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Keywords</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Decisive-Only, Perilous</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Duration</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prerequisite</b>:Charms: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Life is a dream, filled with pain and woe, blood and tears. If a creature is slain by Peace, it is destroyed permanently, even if it would otherwise not be killed. Against effects such as Dual Magus Prana, roll your Essence against the target\u2019s Essence. If he succeeds, he does not die, and if you succeed, murderous Essence will strike him down, even if his effect prevents this.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#860658\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>An End to Thoughts</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Cost</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">5m, 1wp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mins</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Essence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Type</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Keywords</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Psyche, Decisive-Only, Mute</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Duration</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prerequisite</b>:Charms: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">An End to Dreams</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Thought is a curse, knowledge fills it\u2019s bearer with sorrow and pain. This Charm may be used, when a target would take a Crippling wound instead of dying, it allows the target to take an Intimacy of Reverence towards Oblivion with a strength depending on the severity of the wound, instead of taking an injury.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">1-2 health levels: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Minor.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3-4 health levels: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Major.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">5+ health levels: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Defining.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">This Intimacy is permanent, and can only be removed through powerful magic, or at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#860658\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>An End to Difference</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Cost</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Varies; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mins</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Essence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Type</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Simple</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Keywords</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Psyche, Decisive-Only</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Duration</b>: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prerequisite</b>: Charms: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">An End to Dreams</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Difference is a lie, all are part of a greater Unity that must be remade before Creation finally can close it\u2019s tired eyes and die, the wielder may use this Charm to cut away diseases of the mind. For the wielder to use this Charm, the victim must be incapacitated or restrained in some fashion, she must then spend (15 - victim\u2019s Willpower + severity of Derangement) motes and make an attack roll against the victim\u2019s Resolve, she uses his Willpower as his \u201chealth rating\u201d when she fills his Willpower with damage he loses a point of Willpower and his Derangements severity is lowered by one. For the purposes of this Charm, mutations count as derangements, and their dot rating counts as Severity.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":6042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","user":"ManusDomine","date":". 07-15-2016, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T04:22:25-07:00","id":932864,"title":"","content":"Feecback on MagnusDomine`s last artifact<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#860658\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>An End to Dreams</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Cost</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-; </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mins</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Essence 1</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Type</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Simple</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Keywords</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Decisive-Only, Perilous</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Duration</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Instant</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prerequisite</b>:Charms: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">None</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Life is a dream, filled with pain and woe, blood and tears. If a creature is slain by Peace, it is destroyed permanently, even if it would otherwise not be killed. Against effects such as Dual Magus Prana, roll your Essence against the target\u2019s Essence. If he succeeds, he does not die, and if you succeed, murderous Essence will strike him down, even if his effect prevents this.</span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>This is a WAY too powerful and cheap effect for an essence 1 evocation. Your negating an essence 5 charm, gated behind god knows how many craft charms and that costs a bucket load of white experience points, if you manage to beat the opponent in a essence roll. And this costs you nothing and you can do this all day long. I am posting soon my draft of an N/A artifact and I have a bit more beefed up version of this effect as an essence 6 evocation...<br /> <br /> <br /> The second evocation has a cool modification on the crippling mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4567,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4567-volivat","user":"Volivat","date":". 07-17-2016, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4567-volivat","name":"Volivat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T05:06:49-07:00","id":932867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=835897#post835897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have any immediate ideas, but I look forward to seeing it. I have no sense of appropriateness for N/A level artifacts so I won't touch them with a 5 foot pole. Also I would never give one of my players such a weapon, and if an NPC were using it, I'd just make up the numbers without rules anyways. But I'd be fascinated by your direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally finished my draft for the N/A artifact. I would love your thoughts on it.<br /> <br /> To all others:<br /> <br /> Any feedback on this artifact would be greatly appreciated, and I am more than willing to look over one of your own artifacts to give feedback if you deign to give mine some. Feedback on mechanics, evocation names and story, all is fair game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My take on designing N/A artifacts is that their evocations should follow standard evocations design norms as much as possible, so an essence 1 evocation should be as powerful as any 3-5 dot artifacts essence 1 evocation. The N/A aspect comes into play utilizing higher essence charms (6+) or unique evocations that break the norm. In this example I have an essence 5 charm that boosts the wearers essence by 1 for unlocking new evocations for this artifact. That plus the two essence 6 evocations is what gives this artifact the N/A rating in my opinion. Would love to hear others take on this...<br /> <br /> Also N/A artifacts should be really unique and thematically appropriate for its N/A. I have tried to avoid making this into a &quot;I Win&quot; kill-stick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Divine Annihilation \u2013 Short Daiklave \u2013 N/A Artifact</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>Divine Annihilation is imbued with the Unconquered Suns excellence at destruction and the raw force of Solar sorcery. Forged in the holy fires of heaven, celestial capital of Zen-Mu. Quenched in the blood of enemies of creation. Its sole purpose is divine destruction at the behest of its maker. </i><br /> <br /> <i>A short orichalcium daiklave with blood red sorcerous runes etched into both sides of the blade. </i><br /> <br /> <i>During the time of tumult a newly exalted twilight watched in despair as the world was delving into chaos as factions fought over control of dwindling resources and ignored the threats the enemies of creation posed. Even worse was the unforgiveable sin of hunting down Solars. He sought to create a weapon that would channel his rage and divine authority into destruction of the enemies of creation and those who would oppose him.</i><br /> <br /> <i>It is made of Orichalcium and can only be used by Solars.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Divine Annihilation </b><br /> <br /> A Solar who attunes to Divine Annihilation and pays an additional 3 motes when attuning increases the overwhelming stat by +1 and treats opponents whom the bearer have a major/defining tie of hatred towards as CoD.<br /> <br /> Successful withering/decisive attacks generates one Charge each, max six per two rounds. Crashing an opponent or causing a rout check for a battle group generates two Charges.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hateful Obliteration Strike </b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> <i>The runes on the blade starts to glow with a reddish hue and the bearer channels his rage and hatred into the strike. </i><br /> <br /> The wearer adds raw damage dice equal to the value of a negative intimacy against the opponent.<br /> Against CoD the mote cost is reduced by 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>None Shall Oppose</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 2i; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform, Clash-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> <i>Blue lightning dances around the blade and even the smallest touch by the blade delivers a massive current that sends the opponent flying. </i><br /> <br /> Clash attacks are made with the smash rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Glorious Havoc Tempest </b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 6m, 1wp; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b><br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Hateful Obliteration Strike, None Shall Oppose<br /> <br /> <i>The swords runes starts to glow ominously and the sky above darkens. A strong and warm wind starts blowing around the bearer.</i><br /> <br /> Upon activating this charm, the Charges provided by different actions starts to count. Being crashed reduces enough Charges to reduce the level of Charges by two. The same goes for each round of being disarmed. Each health level lost reduces the amount of Charges by one.<br /> <br /> <br /> Only the mechanical effects of the amount of charges in the sword is adjusted up and down. The narrative only builds in strength and remains at the highest charge level until the sword is sheathed or the bearer is incapacitated.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3+ Charges \u2013 <i>The runes on the sword are glowing and arches of lightning can be seen rising from the blade as it gets warmer with each successful strike.</i><br /> No effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> 6+ Charges \u2013<i>The skies above starts to darken and there is little sunlight emerging through the layer of black clouds. The wind is getting stronger and blows intensely around the bearer of the sword.</i><br /> <br /> Anyone within close range suffers -1 modifier from the strong wind and ranged attacks suffer the same penalty.<br /> A dark thunderstorm emerges in the sky above the bearer of the artifact and extends out to medium range.<br /> <br /> <br /> 10+ Charges \u2013 <i>The skies glows ominously red and lightning strikes the ground now and then. Even the noon sun cannot create more light than during twilight through the thick dark skies above.</i><br /> <br /> Anyone within medium range suffers -1 modifier from the strong wind.<br /> The thunderstorm extends out to long range.<br /> <br /> <br /> 16+ Charges \u2013 <i>The lighting intensifies and the thunder drowns out anyone who does not yell. Strong winds with the heat of a forge sweeps the battlefield.</i><br /> <br /> Anyone within long range suffers -2 modifier from the strong wind and heat.<br /> The thunderstorm extends out to 1 miles in radius.<br /> <br /> <br /> 20+ Charges \u2013 <i>The heat from glowing skies permeate everything on the ground. Small droplets of water evaporates and larger pools of water give off vapor.</i><br /> <br /> Anyone within extreme range suffers -2 modifier from the strong wind and heat.<br /> The thunderstorm extends out to 2 miles in radius.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 26+ Charges \u2013 <i>The skies blocks out all sunlight. It would be pitch black where it not for the fires in the sky. </i><br /> <br /> Anyone within extreme range suffers -3 modifier from the strong wind and heat..<br /> The thunderstorm extends out to 5 miles in radius.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hallowed Bolt of Abolition</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m, 1wp, 10 Charges; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Glorious Havoc Tempest<br /> <br /> <i>The sword is raised towards the sky and the bearer utters his judgement \u201cburn\u201d in old realm. A scarlet red lightning bolt from the sky strikes the sword and thousands of electrical arcs dances outward from the sword searing anyone nearby.</i><br /> <br /> All within close range must succeed a reflexive disengage check diff 5 or be subject to a holy fire environmental damage (Lava environmental rules)<br /> <br /> Damage to CoDs is aggravated and knocks them prone.<br /> <br /> Any combustible structure in close range catches fires. Any other material`s surface is scarred.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Heavenly Holocaust</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m, 1wp, 16 Charges; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous, Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Glorious Havoc Tempest<br /> <br /> <i>The sword`s red runes glow intensely as it is raised and slashed in the direction of its target. The skies above his enemies ignites and rains holy fire upon them.</i><br /> <br /> Anyone within <b>long</b> range is a valid target. This attack is unblockable and undodgeable to battlegroups. It is unblockable to anyone else. Anyone within short range of the target is hit as well.<br /> <br /> Extra successes on the attack roll adds to base damage of 16 for Non-Exalts and 8 for Exalts.<br /> <br /> Damage to battlegroups is doubled.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Destruction Incarnate</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2014; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 5<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Heavenly Holocaust, Hallowed Bolt of Abolition<br /> <br /> <i>The power of Divine Annihilation is too great to be completely contained within itself. The destructive powers bleed off into the wearer causing strange effects\u2026 </i><br /> <br /> For meeting the essence requirement of evocations for this artifact the bearer\u2019s essence is treated as one higher.<br /> <br /> While the sword is drawn the wearer scorches any ground he steps on. Combustible materials catches on fire and non-combustible material crumbles. The wearer is immune to any fires created by the evocations of the sword.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Empyreal Assault</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 20m, 2wp, 26 Charges; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 6<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Destruction Incarnate<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cNothing shall remain. Not your memory or name. It will be as though you never ever lived.\u201d The bearer points the sword at his enemy and intense yellow lightning arches to its target, burning their body before exploding those whom blood flows through and burning anything else to slag.</i><br /> <br /> Decisive attack against an enemy within <b>long</b> distance. Add permanent willpower and value of any tie of hate towards opponent as damage dice, 10s count as double on decisive roll.<br /> <br /> The attack is undodgeable and unblockable without magic. It affects dematerialized beings as if they were materialized. If the damage inflicted takes the opponent to incapacitated then he/she/it dies regardless of special rules stating otherwise in terms of living after hitting incapacitated, their soul/spirit torn apart. It would be if as they had never ever existed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b><br /> Only once per season.<br /> <br /> Anyone who witnesses the effects of the evocation <b>Empyreal Assault</b> gains a minor tie of fear if they are hostile to the bearer of the artifact or a minor tie of awe if their views of him are neutral/positive. If they already have such a tie, it is strengthened one level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Divine Judgement</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 20m, 2wp, 26 Charges; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 6<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Empyreal Assault<br /> <br /> <i>The bearer judges the enemies of creation and those who oppose him.<br /> The fires in the skies grows in strength and a massive tornado emerges out of the sky. In the eye of the storm stands the bearer of Divine Annihilation. </i><br /> <i>At the instance the bearer utters his judgement, \u201cDeath\u201d, the tornado ignites.</i><br /> <br /> Anyone within long range of Divine Annihilation must pass a str + athletics test diff 4 and 5 for CoD to avoid being sucked into the tornado and subjected to the holy lava environmental hazard for 3 rounds as they are lifted into the air and shot out of the tornado at extreme range from the ground. If they perish within the tornado, only a fine ash is distributed out of the tornado.<br /> <br /> The fire tornado lasts for 6 rounds. The strong winds pulling in others lasts only for 3 rounds. A success on the str+ ath test makes you safe unless you move within long range of the bearer of the artifact.<br /> <br /> Any combustible materials within long range that is not worn catches fire due to the intense heat radiation from the firestorm.<br /> The storm dissipates over the next hour after this evocation is used. Glorious Havoc Tempest cannot be used until the sun rises and sets again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4567,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4567-volivat","user":"Volivat","date":". 07-17-2016, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4567-volivat","name":"Volivat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T03:26:47-07:00","id":933337,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Idris; The Graceful Heart of Purpose (Artifact Long Spear)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Ardent Lord of an obscure eastern jungle tribe living in the bows of an ancient manse. Idris was a Fae living his dream of mighty conquest justifying his rule; the unique properties of the manse empowered its denizens and he used their archaic beliefs to insinuate himself as a god amongst them. A being to be worshiped and feared, and fed. All this changed when his reach extended past his grasp and the deprivations of his followers caught the attention of a young circle of Solar Exalted. Fearing for his existence, Idris entered into negotiations with the circle\u2019s socialite and found himself convinced of her new path - one of cooperation and unity learned by conquering the game of Serpents and Foxes. The oath he swore has bound his physical form into that he felt most befitting their pact - a seven-foot fountain pen intended to leave the glorious tale of their partnership writ large upon the young Solar\u2019s foes, and indeed, all Creation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Idris now appears as a long wooden fountain pen, Seven foot long by the staff and another foot long at the nib. The staff is plain in appearance and thin like a spear\u2019s haft, but the words and bindings of Idris\u2019 pact are nestled amongst twisting vines and leaves lightly carved across its surface. Invisible normally, but as the Solar\u2019s anima begins to shine and glow, so too do the words of their pact, lifting from its surface and coiling about it in silent recitation as the Solar\u2019s iconic Anima begins to blaze about them. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Idris has the traits of a medium artifact weapon with the Melee, Lethal, Reaching and Two-Handed tags.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Attune:</b> A solar that attunes to Idris adds the Linguistics tag to the weapon.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Sidebar - Linguistics:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>This tag allows a wielder to use their skill in the Linguistics ability to make attacks with the weapon out to short range. These take the form of ephemeral illustrations and script that converge and assault the target. Linguistics attacks cannot be supplemented by charms of other abilities unless otherwise specified. </i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evocations of Idris</span></span></span></i></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Crook to the Opening Heart</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Type:</b> Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Keywords:</b> Uniform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Duration:</b> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawing on the nature of the Raksha Diplomat, Idris and his partner are able to draw out the indulgences of their opponents as they weave their story around them. Successful damage dealt also counts as successes on a read intentions action. Overcoming the target\u2019s guile automatically reveals one random intimacy. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shackle to the Wayward Heart</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost:</b> 4m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Type:</b> Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Keywords: </b>Withering-Only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Duration:</b> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites: </b>Crook to the Opening Heart</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Continuing their synchronous dance about the Serpents and Foxes laid before them, Idris and his partner build the foundations of their glorious future by drawing their quarry right where they want them to be. The target of an attack supplemented by this Evocation has their defense reduced by the rating of the strongest intimacy known to Idris\u2019s partner as if it was their Resolve being targeted by a social action (-1, -2 or -3 for Minor, Major or Defining respectively). Idris\u2019s partner must stunt the attack to target this intimacy in some way. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vessel to the Hesitant Heart</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost: </b>8m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Type:</b> Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-Only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Duration:</b> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Shackle to the Wayward Heart</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entertainers twist and contort to a subject\u2019s desires but, like in the Raksha courts Idris and his partner make dreams reality and desire manifest with their waltz and salsa across the web of Creation. This charm is a difficulty 5 gambit that, if successful, inflicts the target with a persistent haunting daydream that saps a number of initiative equal to the strength of the intimacy targeted (2, 3 or 4 for minor, major or defining respectively). At the beginning of each action, the target can make a Wits + Integrity roll against a difficulty equal to half Idris\u2019 Partner\u2019s Linguistics + Manipulation + the Strength of the Intimacy, rounded up. Success ends the effect, but failure means they lose another 2, 3 or 4 initiative that turn.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blade to the Conquered Heart</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost:</b> 6m, 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Type:</b> Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Keywords:</b> None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Duration:</b> Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Vessel to the Hesitant Heart</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With the triumphant clash of gossamer glass against steel, a warrior forces their foe to accept the reality of the danger they pose, slaying any doubt of threat under the fear of death and that is the final grace Idris offers his partner - their enemy\u2019s heart laid bare and exposed, a thrust of their will closes the final doorway to their escape. This evocation can only be activated while an opponent is currently suffering under the effects of Vessel to the Hesitant Heart. The target becomes enclosed in phantom obstacles created by the ink of Idris that make their haunting daydreams as real to them as any object of creation. These obstacles prevent the target from taking movement actions of any kind and the targets of any attacks they might declare gain the benefits of heavy cover. The dream obstacles can be overcome by succeeding at a gambit with a difficulty equal to the Idris\u2019 Partner\u2019s Essence score + the strength of the intimacy targeted with the prerequisite effect. While under the effects of Blade to the Conquered Heart, any initiative lost through its prerequisite Evocation is gained by Idris\u2019 Partner and the target may not make the Integrity roll to end that Evocation\u2019s effects until they have ended the effect of this Evocation.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":2721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","user":"Elkovash","date":". 07-18-2016, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T11:34:28-07:00","id":933501,"title":"","content":"It's been a while since I originally posted this so I figured I'd re-post it in its entirety. The issues that were pointed out by The Unsung Hero have been addressed and I received some input and tweaks from Binary Phantom on another low level evocation and a rework of the capstone evocation. Be interested in any feedback people might have on the updated grand goremaul.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dissuaders Bulwark</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Artifact: Orialchum and White Jade Grand Goremaul</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Origin</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is a known fact that when you start an ambitious project things don\u2019t always turn out the way one would expect. Such is the case with Dissuaders Bulwark. In the high first age a Twilight artisan was commissioned by his circles Dawn to fashion him an impregnable shield. The twilight craftsmen at once started gathering materials from across creation, Shells from great sea beasts, Shards of the hardest crystal and white jade from the pole of earth itself. The craftsman tooled tireless, working day and night only taking a break during the hours of the early morning when the pure sunlight washed over his creation. When all was said and done the twilight was impressed with his work the finest he\u2019d ever done and presented it to the dawn but there was one issue. In his creative stupor the Artifact he created was not the shield requested but a Grand Goremaul. While taken back on the item put before her the dawn was in awe at the majesty and strength emanating from the weapon. Taking it in hand she could feel this weapon would protect her better than any shield and it served her well in many battles. Had Dissuaders Bulwark been with her when the hands of fate closed in on her circle during the usurpation her attackers may not have faired as well, but alas now Dissuader sleeps awaiting another soul to protect</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Appearance</u></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dissuaders Bulwark is a mighty Grand Goremaul Standing six feet high with a head two feet long and a foot in diameter. The weapon is an alloy of Orialchum and White Jade with a shaft wrapped in the hide of a long dead Behemoth and the pommel adorned in the shells of tortoises that call the pole of fire home. The head of Dissuaders Bulwark is fashioned of a castle atop a giant turtle with the head of the turtle agape with a giant rock in its mouth for the hammerhead and the tail as the spike. Where one would expect the eyes of the turtle two hearthstone sockets appear. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Attunement </u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost 2m: Any exalt who attunes to Dissuaders Bulwark for two motes may take Defend Other actions at short range</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Evocations:</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anchor Howl</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 4m, 2i</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Psyche</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Three Rounds</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: The exalt who uses this evocation paints themselves as the target to anyone within long range and must be attacked or the attacker takes a penalty</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To protect those around themselves the exalt must sometime draw all attention on herself. Upon activation the exalts anima flashes to burning level drawing all eyes to her. This charm interacts with the exalts anima making it impossible to ignore her must attack her. The charm effects all combatants within medium range who can visually see the exalt. Choosing to ignore the exalt and attack someone else incurs a 4 initiative penalty to the attacker. This charm lasts for three rounds and cannot be used again for 4 rounds .</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Gravity of Gravitas</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">M</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ins: Essence 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Uniform</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: 1 Blocked Attack</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Any attack that overcomes the defense of a defend other action must attack the defender</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Even the very weapons of attackers heed Dissuaders Bulwark when it chooses to protect another. While the wielder is acting under a defending other action, the wielder activate this evocation in response to an attack that overcomes their defense in an attempt to hit their ward. After subtracting the defense of the wielder, if the attack roll has fewer successes than the wielder\u2019s Presence and the attacker can chose who to hit, the attack must target the wielder. After fully resolving the attack, the attacker loses 1 initiative.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keystone of the Wall</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 6m</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins:Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Anchor Howl, The Gravity of Gravitas</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Slamming the ground the exalt sends ripples through the ground raising stone and earthen walls creating a funnel for all enemy combatants to the exalt</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes drawing attention to yourself is not enough and you must defend your allies. Upon activating this charm the exalt channels her essence into Dissuaders Bulwark and brings it down upon the ground in front of her. From the Point of impact fissures expand out and two walls of earth and stone erupt from the ground. Each wall is the equivalent of short range in height made up of sharp ragged stone and earth and should be treated as an environmental hazard of 1L/round to move over should anyone attempt to scale it. Each wall extends to approximately long range in a wide \u201cV\u201d out from the exalt and leaves a close range gap between them where the exalt stands.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Castle of Stone</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 4m, 1wp, 6i</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Until next action</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Keystone of the Wall</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: Once activated this evocation makes the exalt impervious to most damage but roots the exalt in place until his next round of combat</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the heat of combat it is sometimes necessary to find a moment to catch one's breath. When Caste of Stone is activated the exalt is routed in place and the her anima wraps around her making a protective shell. The exalt cannot move or be moved until her next action and is incapable of attacking as the shell binds her in place as well. She is treated as having a hardness of 15 and a soak of 15 till her next turn.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Charge of the Juggernaut</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 10m, 1wp, 4i</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins: Essence 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Perilous</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: One Action</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Evocation: Guardian Wall</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Line Summary: The exalt moves and nothing can block its path</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are times when the immovable sets a course of its own, and heaven can do nothing to stop it. On a rush action, this evocation can be used to for the following benefits:</span><ul><li>This evocation allows for a rush action even if engaged, granting Athletics successes as -charm-dice to the wielder\u2019s disengage actions for the duration of the rush.</li> <li>Barriers to their target splinter and crumble before their might. The wielder can crash through walls and other structures, subtracting successes equal to the highest strength requirement needed to punch through any intermediate barriers in their path.</li> <li>Any persons in the way of the wielder must evade the force of nature Dissuaders Bulwark has become. People in between the wielder and their victim must make a reflexive (wits + dodge) roll at difficulty 4 to avoid being trampled. Those who fail are knocked away one range band and suffer 5 initiative damage and 3 health levels of bashing damage. Anyone currently defending the target cannot dodge the attack but with a (Wits + Resistance) roll at difficulty 4 to not be knocked aside but will suffer the aforementioned initiative and bashing damage.</li> <li>On a successful rush, the wielder is impossible to escape. The victim of the rush cannot make a disengage action for the next 2 turns and, if they scored less than half of the successes than the wielder, they are knocked prone.</li> <li>If the wielder fails the rush, they may spend 5m, 2i to continue the effects of the charge through their next turn. In this case, the wielder must rush the same target on their next turn,</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9195-shadowmage","user":"ShadowMage","date":". 07-18-2016, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9195-shadowmage","name":"ShadowMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9195_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T07:36:24-07:00","id":933870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=930615#post930615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Armor of Wily Murk (Chain Shirt ***)</b><br /> <br /> [INSERT BACKSTORY HERE]<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Armor of Wily Murk</b><br /> <br /> An Exalt who attunes the Armor of Wily Murk gains an automatic success on the larceny roll to conceal it.<br /> <br /> <b>Hidden by Glare or Darkness Method</b><br /> Cost: 5m,2wp; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Ignore all penalties to stealth based roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Assassin\u2019s Agility Prana </b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Mute, Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Hidden by Glare or Darkness Method<br /> <br /> Supplements an attack made by another ability, if that attack is made from stealth it counts as an ambush.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cover of Darkness Approach</b><br /> Cost: ???; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mute<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisites: Assassin's Agility Prana<br /> <br /> Creates a fog of darkness that reaches to short range. Everybody in the cloud except the wearer takes a penalty to all awareness or perception rolls equal to the wearer's Essence.<br /> <br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> It should be noted that I do not feel good about this artifact. The thematics seem confused, I'm not sure if the effects are in the right order, and overall it doesn't sit well with me. Any advice?</div> </div> </div> </div>1st Evocation is way over-priced for what it does.<br /> <br /> 2nd Evocation, conversely, is far too cheap for what it does. I might suggest swapping the prices.<br /> <br /> 3rd Evocation: There's a similar charm which just flat-out causes blindness to all living creatures out to medium range, albeit that it can be burnt away by sunlight, including Solar Anima Banners. It costs 8m and is Essence 2. Also, it's the only one that doesn't fit in with the other two. I might suggest adding non-charm successes in darkness or charm successes in light by drawing in the darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T07:45:42-07:00","id":933875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=931734#post931734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all, I was looking at Righteous Devil Style and thinking of ways to expand it's use with another martial art unfortunately you are restricted to using White Reaper normally, so I thought how about a pair of artifact pistols that allow other martial arts to be used with them, when in hand to hand? So I wrote these up in about an hour, so does anyone have any suggestions. I have tried to keep them conceptually clean without completely breaking the game with their evocations, and special ability.<br /> <br /> <b>(PEACH)</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Twin Dragons</b><br /> These Red Jade, Star Metal, and Orichalum artifact flame pieces were crafted for the legendary Silver Flame, a night caste of some repute who used them to quell a number of criminal organizations, before finally being killed in the death throes of the Black Goat with a Thousand Young, after striking the final blow. (HP Lovecraft Reference) Placed with reverence in the tomb of the Silver Flame, these have been lost to Creation for nearly 2 millennia and were recently looted by a Scavenger Lord working for a House Ragara.<br /> <br /> <b>Twin Dragons:</b><br /> -Artifact 4 (Artifact 3 for only one)<br /> -Attunement: 5 (8 as a pair)<br /> -Medium Artifact Weapon<br /> -Tags: Lethal, Archery (Short), Flame, Mounted, One-Handed, Slow<br /> <br /> -Special: When used as a pair they are allowed to function as artifact chopping swords for the purposes of martial arts charms using the following stats. While still being allowed to use Righteous Devil Style charms if using Righteous Devil Form.<br /> <br /> <b>Twin Dragons:</b><br /> -Medium Artifact Weapon<br /> -Tags: Lethal, Martial Arts, Chopping<br /> <br /> Evocations:<br /> <b>Twin Dragons Roar</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m ; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keyword: </b>Counter-attack, Decisive<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <b>Fluff: </b>Having lost their owner once they roar in triumph when used to strike aside attacks meant to harm their attuned wielder.<br /> <b>Mechanics: </b>When the wielder successfully strikes with a clashing attack, he may make a decisive attack using the weapons ranged attacks stats.<br /> <br /> <b>Dragon's Unblinking Eyes</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m ; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keyword: </b>none<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Twin Dragons Roar<br /> <b>Fluff: </b>The dragons are awake once more, and shall remain vigilant using their claws to punish the Unjust.<br /> <b>Mechanics: </b>When making a melee attack in which you get a bonus for aiming, add Essence non-charm dice to the attack roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why no Melee tag? If they function as Chopping Swords.<br /> <br /> Twin Dragons Roar - The mechanics don't make sense. What does this actually do? Is it a free decisive attack? Also, Counter-Attacks and Clashes don't mix. Fluffwise, I was expecting parries to perhaps trigger an attack. Say, on a successful parry you get a counter-attack. Also, that should be Decisive-Only, not simply 'Decisive' in the tags.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it's a nice artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:38:14-07:00","id":934650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volivat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=932864#post932864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feecback on MagnusDomine`s last artifact<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is a WAY too powerful and cheap effect for an essence 1 evocation. Your negating an essence 5 charm, gated behind god knows how many craft charms and that costs a bucket load of white experience points, if you manage to beat the opponent in a essence roll. And this costs you nothing and you can do this all day long. I am posting soon my draft of an N/A artifact and I have a bit more beefed up version of this effect as an essence 6 evocation...<br /> <br /> <br /> The second evocation has a cool modification on the crippling mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, normally I'd totally agree with you here that an Essence 1 effect shouldn't get to do all this, but honestly in this case I make an exception.<br /> <br /> Peace is an artifact, monomaniacally focused on ending things, quickly, efficiently and cleanly. It's not a great blasphemy against Creation, it's just the truth that things die.<br /> <br /> But I do think I'll make some modifications to that Charm.<br /> <br /> What about this?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#860658\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>An End to Dreams</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Cost</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-; </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mins</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Essence 1</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Type</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Simple</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Keywords</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Decisive-Only, Perilous</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Duration</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Instant</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prerequisite</b>:Charms: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">None</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Life is a dream, filled with pain and woe, blood and tears. If a creature is slain by Peace, roll your (Essence + number of Evocations from Peace) against it's Essence. If you succeed, it is permanently destroyed.<br /> At Essence 3, you may purchase this Evocation to allow it to also ignore effects such as Dual Magnus Prana. </span></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:52:23-07:00","id":934660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=934650#post934650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> See, normally I'd totally agree with you here that an Essence 1 effect shouldn't get to do all this, but honestly in this case I make an exception.<br /> <br /> Peace is an artifact, monomaniacally focused on ending things, quickly, efficiently and cleanly. It's not a great blasphemy against Creation, it's just the truth that things die.<br /> <br /> But I do think I'll make some modifications to that Charm.<br /> <br /> What about this?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#860658\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>An End to Dreams</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Cost</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">-; </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mins</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Essence 1</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Type</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Simple</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Keywords</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Decisive-Only, Perilous</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Duration</b>: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Instant</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Prerequisite</b>:Charms: </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">None</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Life is a dream, filled with pain and woe, blood and tears. If a creature is slain by Peace, roll your (Essence + number of Evocations from Peace) against it's Essence. If you succeed, it is permanently destroyed.<br /> At Essence 3, you may purchase this Evocation to allow it to also ignore effects such as Dual Magnus Prana. </span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its still an essence 3 effect canceling out an essence 5 (pinnacle) charm effect. Why not just make it an essence 5 charm? You could make it the pinnacle evocation of your weapon instead of the first evocation. (Know that I am commenting on this from a ST viewpoint, of making it more balanced with the games other effects)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4567-volivat","name":"Volivat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T13:05:36-07:00","id":934672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volivat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=934660#post934660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Its still an essence 3 effect canceling out an essence 5 (pinnacle) charm effect. Why not just make it an essence 5 charm? You could make it the pinnacle evocation of your weapon instead of the first evocation. (Know that I am commenting on this from a ST viewpoint, of making it more balanced with the games other effects)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see your argument, but it's just so fitting for the Artifact that it gets to ignore that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I'll figure something out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T10:20:24-07:00","id":935120,"title":"","content":"<b>The Stormblade (Blue Jade Daiklave - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> Forged in RY 223 by master bladesmith Manosque Zhennan for his cousin Sharmija, the Stormblade was confiscated during the purge of House Manosque and somehow ended up in the coffers of House Peleps, where it has remained until now. Given as a graduation present to the Lost Egg &quot;Peleps&quot; Kyshatrya, it now serves her will aboard the pirate-hunting vessel <i>Lost Dragon's Justice</i>. The Stormblade itself is a long, curved blade with a basket-hilt crafted to look like a web of lightning around the wielder's hand. The wide blade is graven with runes in Old Realm, exhorting the glory of the storm.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Evocations of the Stormblade</b></b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blood who attunes to the Stormblade learns Lightning Strike at no cost.<br /> <br /> <b>Lightning Strike</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Essence lightning arcs along the Stormblade, empowering its strike with the speed and ferocity of striking lightning. The wielder may use this Evocation to take her action (Essence or 3, whichever is greater) ticks higher in the initiative order than her actual initiative would allow. If she uses her turn to make a <b>decisive </b>attack against an enemy who has not yet acted, the damage roll counts the bonus from this Evocation as actual Initiative and receives doubled 10s on its damage roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Thunderbolt</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 3i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Lightning Strike<br /> <br /> Hurling a bolt of Essence lightning from the tip of the sword, the wielder can use this Evocation to make an attack at a target at up to Short range. If the target of a <b>decisive </b>attack enhanced by this Evocation is standing in at least ankle-high water, the wielder may pay an additional Willpower to subject everyone else connected to that body of water to a one-time, lightning-based environmental hazard with the traits of a bonfire.<br /> <br /> <b>Eye of the Storm</b><br /> Cost: 6m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: Thunderbolt<br /> <br /> With the Stormblade held high, the wielder calls the fury of the storm down into it like a lightning rod, protecting herself from the deleterious effects of the tempest. While this Evocation is in effect, the wielder suffers no environmental penalties from storm-based effects and takes no damage from storm-based environmental hazards. She also enjoys (Essence) automatic successes to resist the effects of Charms, Evocations and spells that invoke themes of thunder, wind and lightning.<br /> <br /> <b>Command the Storm</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1W; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Eye of the Storm<br /> <br /> The truest power of the Stormblade is to command storms themselves. By using this Evocation, the wielder can mute or intensify the environmental penalties caused by a storm by one, to a minimum of 0 or a maximum of -3. This can create a storm from nothing or reduce an existing storm to non-existence, dissipating it unnaturally. If activated again in immediate subsequent actions, reduce the cost of the Evocation to 5m, 0W. Storms created by this Evocation tend to last until the end of the scene, though if conditions are right, they may grow and take on a life of their own at the Storyteller's discretion. Finally, while a storm created or enhanced by this Evocation is present in a scene, the wielder may reduce the cost of Thunderbolt to 3m,1i.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":9453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","user":"Octopoid","date":". 07-21-2016, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T13:58:11-07:00","id":935246,"title":"","content":"<b>Armor of the Depths (Black Jade Breastplate - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> Forged by the Outcaste Melchior Stag, King of the Black Sea, in RY 654, the Armor of the Depths served him well in his time as a pirate captain. However, in RY 762, he encountered a Peleps military vessel he could neither outfight nor outrun, and he was taken captive. His armor was stripped from him and given to the commander of the vessel, &quot;Peleps&quot; Kyshatrya, who still uses it to this day. The Armor of the Depths is a black jade breastplate, engraved with swirling nautilus patterns, with a high gorget that rises to conceal the lower half of the wearer's face like a mask.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Armor of the Depths</b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blood who attunes to the Armor of the Depths for two additional motes finds herself able to breathe freely underwater.<br /> <br /> <b>Tidal Pull</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The pull of the tide is inexorable, and so, too, is the pull from this armor. When this Evocation is activated, it creates a momentary pulse of tidal gravity, enough to pull an attacker off-balance. It reverts (wearer's Essence) 10s on the attack roll back to single successes. <br /> <br /> <b>Tidal Crash</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Tidal Pull<br /> <br /> The armor's tidal gravity grows, able to haul an opponent off-balance even when they are not attacking. This Evocation reduces an opponent's Initiative by (wearer's Essence), but only if that would Crash them. The initiative so stolen is not gained by the Armor's wearer, but is lost.<br /> <br /> <b>Tidal Force</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Tidal Crash<br /> <br /> The pull of the armor becomes too great to be borne, separating even the mightiest warriors from their weapons. This Evocation is a Reflexive Disarm gambit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T14:43:25-07:00","id":935270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935120#post935120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Stormblade (Blue Jade Daiklave - Artifact ***)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>A somewhat pedestrian artifact, all in all. Something your players were asking for and you weren't feeling inspired to make?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935120#post935120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Lightning Strike</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Essence lightning arcs along the Stormblade, empowering its strike. An attack supplemented by this Evocation doubles 10s on its <b>decisive</b> damage roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have two problems with this Evocation. First, it is mechanically flavorless. This effect could have literally any other justification. Second, it's somewhat underpowered for its cost - for comparison, Blossom of Inevitable Demise allows you to make an attack up to medium range in addition to doubling 10s for the same cost, while Shining Starfall Execution adds up to 5 damage as well as doubling 10s for 6m.<br /> <br /> What I would do instead is emphasize the speed and ferocity of striking lightning, allowing the character to act (Essence or 3, whichever is higher) ticks higher in the initiative order than her actual initiative would allow. If she uses her turn to make a decisive attack against an enemy who hasn't yet acted in the turn, the damage roll counts the bonus from this Charm as actual Initiative, and receives double 10s.<br /> <br /> I think this effect is about on par with Shining Starfall Execution (<i>much </i>harder to get a +5 bonus to damage, but it also allows you to mildly screw with turn order which can be very powerful). I'd peg it as 5m (Flash-Fire Technique is somewhat similar but limited in different ways, and grants up to +2 Initiative, for 4m), but an argument could certainly be made for making it 6m. Playtest it with your group (but be mindful that the difference between a 5m and a 6m effect is <i>massive </i>- you can use the former without preparation even after you've been mote-tapped, while the latter requires a turn to set up under such circumstances).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935120#post935120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Thunderbolt</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 3i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Lightning Strike<br /> <br /> Hurling a bolt of Essence lightning from the tip of the sword, the wielder can use this Evocation to make an attack at a target at up to Short range.</div> </div> </div> </div>A less risky (no WP cost! yay!) but weaker (no mobility and feat of strength penalty! boo!) version of Cold Moon Slash that you actually have to pay for and doesn't auto-upgrade at Essence 4. Another good comparison point is Iron Raptor Technique, which costs 7m and allows you to attack out to medium range without aiming. All in all, I think it suffers very much from the latter comparison, being weaker in all respects without bringing much to the table to compensate (however overpriced Cold Moon Slash is, at least it does <i>something </i>beyond just giving you a ranged attack).<br /> <br /> Given the capstone, I think it would be interesting to say that if the target of a decisive attack enhanced by this Evocation is standing in at least ankle-high water, the character may pay an additional willpower to subject everyone else connected to that body of water to an environmental hazard with the traits of a bonfire that deals lightning damage. This would make me at least consider buying the Evocation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935120#post935120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Eye of the Storm</b><br /> Cost: 6m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: Thunderbolt<br /> <br /> With the Stormblade held high, the wielder calls the fury of the storm down into it like a lightning rod, protecting herself from the deleterious effects of the tempest. While this Evocation is in effect, the wielder suffers no environmental penalties from storm-based effects and takes no damage from storm-based environmental hazards.</div> </div> </div> </div>A more specific, expensive and limited version of Hardship-Surviving Mendicant Spirit enhanced by Element-Resisting Prana, at Essence 2. I... think I'm okay with that (albeit I'd probably also toss in (Essence) automatic successes to resist the effects of Charms, Evocations and spells that invoke themes of thunder, wind and lightning - as written, your version arguably offers no protection from effects like Wrathful Winds Maneuver, which strikes me as strange and probably unintended).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935120#post935120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Command the Storm</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1W; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Eye of the Storm<br /> <br /> The truest power of the Stormblade is to command storms themselves. By using this Evocation, the wielder can mute or intensify the environmental penalties caused by a storm by one, to a minimum of 0 or a maximum of -3. This can create a storm from nothing or reduce an existing storm to non-existence, dissipating it unnaturally. If activated again in immediate subsequent actions, reduce the cost of the Evocation to 5m, 0W. Storms created by this Evocation tend to last until the end of the scene, though if conditions are right, they may grow and take on a life of their own at the Storyteller's discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. I'd probably also either give a price break on Thunderbolt while a storm created or enhanced by this Evocation is active, or give the character a way to hurl one each turn she maintains Command the Storm, or both. Not sure on the specifics, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T14:48:09-07:00","id":935274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935270#post935270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A somewhat pedestrian artifact, all in all. Something your players were asking for and you weren't feeling inspired to make?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something I was designing for an NPC, actually. Doesn't need to be anything more than pedestrian. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935270#post935270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I would do instead is emphasize the speed and ferocity of striking lightning, allowing the character to act (Essence or 3, whichever is higher) ticks higher in the initiative order than her actual initiative would allow. If she uses her turn to make a decisive attack against an enemy who hasn't yet acted in the turn, the damage roll counts the bonus from this Charm as actual Initiative, and receives double 10s.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it! I will do that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935270#post935270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A less risky (no WP cost! yay!) but weaker (no mobility and feat of strength penalty! boo!) version of Cold Moon Slash that you actually have to pay for and doesn't auto-upgrade at Essence 4. Another good comparison point is Iron Raptor Technique, which costs 7m and allows you to attack out to medium range without aiming. All in all, I think it suffers very much from the latter comparison, being weaker in all respects without bringing much to the table to compensate (however overpriced Cold Moon Slash is, at least it does <i>something </i>beyond just giving you a ranged attack).</div> </div> </div> </div>This one was actually balanced around Uncoiling Serpent Prana, since I felt a Martial Arts effect was a better balancing factor than a Solar Charm. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935270#post935270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A more specific, expensive and limited version of Hardship-Surviving Mendicant Spirit enhanced by Element-Resisting Prana, at Essence 2. I... think I'm okay with that (albeit I'd probably also toss in (Essence) automatic successes to resist the effects of Charms, Evocations and spells that invoke themes of thunder, wind and lightning - as written, your version arguably offers no protection from effects like Wrathful Winds Maneuver, which strikes me as strange and probably unintended).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, hadn't considered it. I like your suggestion!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935270#post935270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. I'd probably also either give a price break on Thunderbolt while a storm created or enhanced by this Evocation is active, or give the character a way to hurl one each turn she maintains Command the Storm, or both. Not sure on the specifics, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T15:01:02-07:00","id":935282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935274#post935274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I was designing for an NPC, actually. Doesn't need to be anything more than pedestrian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Au contraire - after all, PCs are more likely than not to cheat, lie, scheme and murder to get their grubby hands on NPC artifacts*, and more likely than not to succeed at that. You wouldn't want to be unprepared, would you? :P<br /> <br /> *Disclaimer: actual PCs in your actual game may or may not actually be likely to do the aforementioned activities due to having a code of ethics or a bunch of Artifacts they already bought from background dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935274#post935274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one was actually balanced around Uncoiling Serpent Prana, since I felt a Martial Arts effect was a better balancing factor than a Solar Charm. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think a 1m price break doesn't justify having no additional effect whatsoever. Uncoiling Serpent Prana at least lets you do the Scorpion thing. I'd still give it the upgrade I suggested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T16:00:52-07:00","id":935320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935282#post935282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Au contraire - after all, PCs are more likely than not to cheat, lie, scheme and murder to get their grubby hands on NPC artifacts*, and more likely than not to succeed at that. You wouldn't want to be unprepared, would you? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of that, I'm interested in finding a write up for a 3 dot medium artifact armor for Shining Topaz to eventually take off a dynast (and the core book one is 5 dots), yet it seems not a single piece of medium armor has been made in the thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T16:05:59-07:00","id":935327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935320#post935320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of that, I'm interested in finding a write up for a 3 dot medium artifact armor for Shining Topaz to eventually take off a dynast (and the core book one is 5 dots), yet it seems not a single piece of medium armor has been made in the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess Lamellar and Reinforced Buff Jackets don't tickle the imagination. I'd say just grab something that's light armor and refluff it as Medium. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T00:00:40-07:00","id":936440,"title":"","content":"So one of my players wanted a 5 dot grand goremaul, and since we're in the West and will eventually be taking on the Silver Prince (hopefully), I decided to make the weapon one of the Bodhisattva's weapons from when he first took control of Skullstone.<br /> <br /> The problem is I'm not sure if it's worthy of the 5 dot status when compared to similar artifacts, so I turn to you guys for an opinion.<br /> <br /> <b>Wail of Despair<br /> (Soulsteel Grand Goremaul, Artifact 5)</b><br /> <br /> When he first ascended his throne, the Bodhisattva Anointed by Dark Waters knew he needed a weapon that would strike fear into his enemies and inspire loyalty amongst his followers. He worked for several years on the best way to achieve these goals and eventually settled upon this design.<br /> <br /> He spent years collecting the correct materials and forging the weapon into an instrument of destruction and torture that served him well during his rise to power and creation of the New Order, a religion that keeps the people he ruled in check.<br /> <br /> After his disappearance from Dark Mist he decided to send the weapon out into the world rather than keep it close. He felt that its abilities were of no more use to him personally as he had moved onto a more subtle approach to control. It now passes among his agents as a way to ensure their success in missions.<br /> <br /> The shaft of this weapon is made from a rod of pure Black Jade that is wrapped in the hide of a Behemoth. The head is Soulsteel laced with minor traces of starmetal. Its name is derived from the ear splitting screams that come from its victims souls as they are consumed.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Wail of Despair</b><br /> A solar or Abyssal who attunes to Wail of Despair awakens Prison of Penance at no cost. By paying an extra 3 motes when attuning, the wielder may expend a soul stored in Wail of Despair to coat the hammer head so that it can effect immaterial spirits for the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Prison of Penance</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: None<br /> <br /> Upon killing a living being with Wail of Despair, the exalt may invoke this evocation. Ghostly tendrils reach out from the weapon and grab the victims soul as it departs their body. The soul is then dragged screaming into the weapon where it remains to power Wail of Despair.<br /> <br /> The Exalt may store up to Essence x2 souls and each stored soul increases Wail of Despair's base damage by one. If the exalt ever loses commitment to Wail of Despair then all stored souls are lost and pass on to Lethe as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Exchange of Penance</b><br /> Cost: 3m, 1+ souls; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: Prison of Penance<br /> <br /> Upon successfully hitting with a decisive attack the exalt may invoke this evocation. He consumes up to his Essence souls stored in Wail of Despair to power its attack with an equal number of automatic successes on the damage roll. If this damage is enough to kill the target then the exalt may activate Prison of Penance at no cost.<br /> <br /> <b>Voice of the Penitent</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 3, Lore 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene or until all questions are answered<br /> Prerequisite: Prison of Penance<br /> <br /> Calling out to one of the souls trapped inside Wail of Despair, the exalt may offer an exchange of information for freedom. A soul is pulled out of the weapon and as long as they have been trapped for more than a week, will truthfully answer up to Essence questions that the wielder asks. After this, they are free to pass on to Lethe as normal.<br /> <br /> If the soul called has been trapped for less than a week, then it has not yet succumb to the true despair of its prison and will only truthfully answer one question in exchange for its freedom.<br /> <br /> <b>Army of the Broken</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 4, Occult 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Until next sunrise<br /> Prerequisite: Exchange of Penance<br /> <br /> Drawing upon his stored collection of souls, the exalt calls them to his aid. All of the souls are released and appear as Hungry Ghosts (Exalted 3rd edition page 503) that obey the wielders commands but are destroyed if they go more than 2 range bands from the wielder. These ghosts are unlike others and are not harmed by sunlight but are also unable to dematerialise. Whenever they kill a living creature, its soul is automatically dragged into Wail of Despair unless it has already reached its soul limit.<br /> <br /> Whenever the wielder is hit with a decisive attack while this Evocation is active, the damage is transferred to a random ghost until there are no more available to take the damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Special activation rule:</b> If the exalt kills a non trivial opponent and consumes their soul with Prison of Penance, then this Evocation may be activated Reflexively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11486,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11486-darth_versity","user":"Darth_versity","date":". 07-24-2016, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11486-darth_versity","name":"Darth_versity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T05:34:42-07:00","id":936500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=935327#post935327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>I guess Lamellar and Reinforced Buff Jackets don't tickle the imagination</b>. I'd say just grab something that's light armor and refluff it as Medium.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Challenge Accepted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Crawling Garment(Green Jade, Moonsilver and Wax Lamellar, 4-dot Artifact)</b><br /> <br /> The Crawling Garment is a curious construction, consisting of hardened wax plates, infused with Green Jade Dust and bound with Moonsilver. The larger links are forged of amber, each piece containing some long dead insect. The Wax itself is infested with ants, flies, bees, wasps spiders and various other insects, which constantly move through the wax. They constantly repair and restructure the armour in a dozen small ways, spiders reweaving the Moonsilver threads while bees produces wax to be carried by the ants. The flies keep the armour clean, while the wasps and other colourful insects(including the occasional butterfly) give the armour vibrant streaks of colour. A Dragonblood, Lunar or Solar who attunes this armour may have the insects carve his personal seal, the seal of some organisation he supports or indeed anything else onto the front of the armour. The armour automatically fits itself to the wearer and is extremely comfortable besides, inflicting no penalties for extended use.<br /> <br /> <b>Calling the Swarm</b><br /> Cost: 2m; Mins: Ess 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: 1 Round<br /> Prerequisite: None<br /> <br /> With this Evocation, the bearer replenishes the insects within the armour, calling forth any insects in the vicinity. A swarm of insects forms almost immediately, obscuring the bearer from sight and granting him light cover against all attacks for the round. This evocation functions in any area capable of supporting insect life. For the next 3 rounds, due to the insects clinging to the armour, its mobility increases by 1 however, the armour's soak increases by 3 for the same duration. The Evocation may be reactivated reflexively at the end of the 3 rounds, but no earlier.<br /> <br /> <b>Swarm Bursts Forth</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Ess 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: Calling the Swarm<br /> <br /> This Evocation allows the wearer to expel a cloud of insects out to short range. Everyone within the cloud benefits from light cover. However, enemies of the bearer find themselves harassed by the insects. While they deal no damage, any foes suffer a -2 penalty to all movement based actions while within the swarm.<br /> <br /> <b>Becoming the Swarm</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Ess 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Prerequisite: Swarm Bursts Forth<br /> <br /> This evocation may only be used during the 3 rounds after Calling the Swarm has been used. The final evocation of the Crawling Garment transforms the bearer into a sentient swarm of insects. The bearer treats the armoured soak the armour provides as natural soak for all purposes and is no longer treated as wearing armour. However, they also gain the effects of the Hideous Merit as their skin breaks apart into thousands of insects. While in this form, the bearer may fly, fit through any space large enough to fit the constituents of his body(Although it may take some time to fit the entire body through smaller spaces) and may launch hand-to-hand attacks out to short range, stretching his 'arms' to reach that far.<br /> <br /> As a last ditch defense, the bearer may spend 1 Willpower to take a temporary crippling effect, doubling his wound penalties for the rest of the day, to force the swarm to scatter completely. However, until the swarm gathers back together at the end of this evocations duration, the bearer cannot be targeted by any decisive attacks as his form is too scattered to suffer such attacks. However, any attacks he launches may not deal more than the Bearer's Permanent Essence in damage and he may not use any weapons in this form. It is most often used to escape battle safely.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> And now for Round 2!<br /> <br /> <b>Mother's Gentle Embrace(Black Jade and Behemoth Skin Reinforced Buff Jacket, 3-dot Artifact)</b><br /> Originally claimed from the Lintha Pirates by the Realm, this coat is made of pale blue skin reinforced with plates of Black Jade. According to Lintha legend it is a gift from their mother, and they have been hunting for it ever since it was lost, as they believe it to be a sacred heirloom of their people. Cultists of Mara also recognise this as a holy relic<br /> <br /> A Dragon-Blood, Solar or Lintha who attunes to this armour for 7 motes always feels warm and comfortable, ignoring any penalties from inclement weather or uncomfortable places but not uncomfortable positions such as standing still for several hours or holding some contorted position. Furthermore, they find that it is completely compatible with the Black Claw Style.<br /> <br /> <b>Eponymous Embrace</b><br /> Cost: 3m ; Mins: Ess 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: None<br /> <br /> This evocation supplements a Savage action in a grapple. First, it disguises it as an embrace, making the attack seem utterly harmless.<br /> <br /> For Withering Attacks, it causes a degree of confusion in the target, causing them to hesitate. The victim's action now falls as if he had 3 fewer points of initiative.<br /> <br /> When used with Decisive Attacks, the target finds his lungs filling with water instead of any other form of damage. The savage deals lethal damage and if the target is killed by this charm, he appears for all intents and purposes to have drowned. Should the target break free of the embrace (grapple), he must spend an action coughing to get the water out. He may still take another non-reflexive action, but this counts as a flurry. Black Claw Stylists who use this function find that the targets lungs instead fill with liquid shadows.<br /> <br /> <b>Stifling Embrace</b><br /> Cost: 2m ; Mins: Ess 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: Eponymous Embrace<br /> <br /> This evocation supplements a decisive savage. The bearer gains the benefits of Double 10s and may use the savage attack to afflict the target with a poison with the statistics of Curare. Finally, the grapple appears to be a brief tightening of an embrace and despite any cries the victim might make, no-one will hear them unless they hold a major positive intimacy towards the well-being of the victim. The only thing that might seem odd is that the coat itself also wraps around the victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","user":"Myradmir","date":".  Edit: Added a sentence to the end of Stifling Embrace. Also a note that inspiration for these things are easily inspiring. 07-24-2016, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T12:18:26-07:00","id":936657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=936500#post936500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Challenge Accepted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect, the 3 dot artifact is perfect for my dawn to loot off a dragon blood. Now I just need a decent 3 dot reaper diaklave to loot off said DB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T11:17:30-07:00","id":937180,"title":"","content":"<b>Gleaming Crescent (Moonsilver Skycutter - Artifact ***)</b><br /> <br /> <i>Beautiful moonlight<br /> Gleaming on the silver pond</i><br /> <i>Gibbous and deadly</i><br /> <br /> So reads the stanza of Gleaming Crescent, an elegant arch of moonsilver forged near the end of the Shogunate. Baptised in the blood of the Fair Folk, it slew hundreds before its first and only wielder was dragged to his death by the teeming hordes of the Wyld. Now, it rests in the trophy room of the Cataphract-King called the Emperor of Sorrows, still bearing the bloodstains of the raksha it killed. The Emperor reads the haiku every day, sheding a single diamond tear for his fallen kin while he plots vengeance on the world that slew them.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Evocations of Gleaming Crescent</b></b><br /> <br /> A Solar or Lunar who attunes to Gleaming Crescent finds that it will <i>always </i>return to his hand after an attack, even on a botched attack roll. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Strike from Behind</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Gleaming Crescent always returns to its wielder's hand, a fact that can sometimes be surprising to those who engage him. Immediately after making a <b>withering</b> attack at an opponent at least at Short range, the wielder may use this Evocation to unleash a second attack at a different opponent, who must be at Close range to the wielder. This second attack may be <b>withering</b> or <b>decisive</b>. <br /> <br /> <b>Thrown Protector</b><br /> Cost: 6m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Strike from Behind<br /> <br /> With uncanny skill and insight, the wielder of Gleaming Crescent may strike a ranged attack away from one he loves with but a flick of the wrist. To use this Evocation, someone toward whom the wielder holds a least a Minor positive Tie must be the target of a ranged attack. This Evocation is a reflexive (Dexterity + Thrown) roll against the total successes rolled on that attack. Every success on this roll subtracts one success from the attack roll, to a minimum of zero, before it is applied to the target's Defense. As always, Gleaming Crescent immediately returns to its wielder's hand after this &quot;attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Protect Thyself</b><br /> Cost: 4m,1W; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Clash, Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Thrown Protector<br /> <br /> By hurling Gleaming Crescent at an incoming attacker, the wielder may teach the offender that striking him is a fool's errand. This Evocation allows the wielder to make a reflexive Thrown clash attack against an attack directed at him, regardless of his place in the Initiative order. This does not count as the wielder's combat action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:25:05-07:00","id":937213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=936657#post936657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perfect, the 3 dot artifact is perfect for my dawn to loot off a dragon blood. Now I just need a decent 3 dot reaper diaklave to loot off said DB.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Glad to be of service. I didn't know how your Dawn operated so I went with two options. And grappling is generally a good bet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T19:28:57-07:00","id":937409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=937213#post937213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Glad to be of service. I didn't know how your Dawn operated so I went with two options. And grappling is generally a good bet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My dawn is Invincible Sword Princess. I just needed a random 3 dot thing a dynast or lookshyan would be likely to have for her to loot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T10:38:18-07:00","id":937675,"title":"","content":"So my first attempt at an artifact knife. I would appreciate input.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ash: Red Jade and artifact knife (3)<br /> <br /> Crafted in the early days of the scarlet empire, it was actually originally designed by a usurper who attempted to slay the empress with it. That usurpers name was stricken from history, but the blade was not. Passed into house cathak, the knife was used for several generations before being lost out in the threshold. Now it makes its way into hands of assassins and outcastes. It seems though as of recent, it, much like the woman it was made to slay, has vanished...<br /> <br /> Light Melee Artifact knife with the Lethal, Melee, Thrown (Short) Tags<br /> <br /> New Tag: Burn<br /> <br /> Successful attacks with this artifact produce points of Burn, which can be used to enhance evocations. A wielder can hold Stamina + Essence Burn in total.<br /> <br /> Attunement Bonus:<br /> A solar or Dragon blood who attunes to Ash for an additional 2 motes, gets one bonus success on join battle,<br /> and upon rolling starts with 1 point of Burn. (This success counts as dice from charms)<br /> <br /> <b>Searing Wound</b><br /> <br /> Cost 2m,<br /> Essence 1:<br /> Supplemental<br /> Keywords (Withering Only) Burn<br /> Instant<br /> Prerequisite: None<br /> <br /> Many would say a clean cut is best. Ash sees otherwise. This charm adds Essence or 2 (whichever greater) to the raw damage of a withering attack.<br /> On the damage roll, less clean blows hide tainted scouring. Ones on the damage roll increase the weilders Burn by 1. (However the attack must inflict at least 1 point of initiative damage)<br /> <br /> (Wanted to make something that played with dice numbers a different way with this one).<br /> <br /> <b>Ashes to Ashes</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 3m 1i and 1+ Burn<br /> Essence 1<br /> Supplemental<br /> Decisive Only, Burn<br /> Instant<br /> Prerequisite: Searing Wound<br /> <br /> Many don't expect the low boil to be so suddenly deadly. Ash proves otherwise. When making a decisive attack, the Exalt sacrifices a bit of momentum to release the flames withing the blade<br /> The attack does +2 raw damage, +1 for each extra burn spent. The exalt may only spend up to Essence or 3, whichever is greater Burn on this attack. Those slain by this attack leave corpses that have skin as ash that has glowing cracks that fade over time.<br /> <br /> <b>Glowing Coal Beacon</b><br /> <br /> Cost 3m 2 Burn<br /> Essence 2<br /> Duration: Essence Actions<br /> Supplemental<br /> Decisive only? (not sure if that makes it too weak) Burn<br /> <br /> Prerequisite: Ashes to Ashes<br /> <br /> A dimly burning coal is like a beacon in darkness. Upon landing a decisive attack that deals at least 1 level of damage, the exalt may pour burn into that<br /> wound in order to create a beacon. For essence actions, allies targeting the character with ranged attacks find it easier to aim at the red glow within.<br /> Ranged attacks benefit as though they had aimed (though this provides no dice at medium or further without a subsequent aim action).<br /> <br /> The victim may stop this glow by patting out the coal like wound as a miscellanious action on their turn. This is not flurryable.<br /> <br /> <b>Dust to Dust</b><br /> Cost 8m 1wp 2 Burn (Special, see charm)<br /> Essence 3<br /> Keywords: Decisive only Burn<br /> Duration: Varies (See charm)<br /> Prerequisite: Glowing Coal Beacon<br /> <br /> Sometimes a wound gets worse as the battle rages. After landing a decisive attack that does at least 3 levels of damage, the wielder may pay the cost of this charm to leave a small glowing scar. This has no benefit at first, but as the burn intensifies, eventually the truth makes itself known.<br /> <br /> Each time the wielder of Ash would gain Burn, they may filter up to Essence points of it into the wound. This causes it to spread the glow through the veins and chakras of the target. Once they have accumulated 5 or more burn in the wound (Maximum 10) They may at any time choose to release the motes committed to this charm. Doing so causes a searing attack as a flame erupts from the wound to engulf the target. The target may attempt to defend against this attack, however the sudden nature is treated as a normal suprise attack with the usual -2 penalty to defense. The attack roll is 8 dice, but the wielder may spend up to 3 points of burn from within the blade to enhance this attack, adding 1 die per point. This slays trivial opponents without contest. The damage of this attack is equal to 3 + the burn in the wound. This bypasses hardness from armor. Victims killed by this turn into a pile of dust. It also incidentally prevents a hungry ghost from rising.<br /> <br /> A victim can attempt to stop the coming blaze if they are able to make an Intelligence + Medicine roll at a difficulty of 3 to know what is happening. If they succeed, they may spend a miscellanious action and a willpower to attempt to realign their own essence meridians with a Stamina + Resistance roll against a difficulty of the wound's Burn/2 round up. This action cannot be flurried.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> OK so dunno if this is balanced or not. I was concerned about the mechanics a bit more than the fluff itself. I would greatly appreciate input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1777,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","user":"Kell_Tamer","date":". 07-26-2016, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T15:52:07-07:00","id":938403,"title":"","content":"Alright, I've got the first artifact I've ever tried to create on my own, and I KNOW it needs some sort of balancing help, if someone would be so kind. I really wanted to explore an interesting space with the artifact in question, and so I thought of something that plays with the limit track in a very...liminal...kind of way, I suppose. Now I've worked the fluff of the blade, but not really the fluff of the charms just yet, as I want to finalize the charms before I begin making their flavour. So without further ado, I present Sanguis Gladii.<br /> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:36px\"><b>Sanguis Gladii</b></span> <span style=\"font-size:36px\">(Soulsteel/Starmetal Grand Daiklaive</span><span style=\"font-size:36px\">)</span><br /> Acc 1, Dmg 14, Def 0, OW 5, Attun. 8, Lethal/Melee/Balanced/Reaching/Two-Handed<br /> <br /> <i> There once was a god . . . </i>who ruled over the mortal liquid. Styuger, of the Crimson-Consuming River was this god\u2019s given name, and his domain of control was over that of blood. Oft before large scale wars, light skirmishes, or tavern bar brawls, the phrase \u2018blood for the blood god\u2019 would be uttered; none knew who the blood god was, nor if the phrase did anything, but it served as a variable warning to the opposing party that you\u2019d not be pulling any blows. People whom knew the phrase were content with saying it before combat, and those who heard it and lived on would likely also use it for the same purpose. Little did any know that the words DID carry meaning; a secret prayer to the blood god to watch upon their battle, and that any blood that spilled was rightfully his to take. Take the god did, and all blood that fell upon a battlefield while he watched went to fill up his river. To other gods, he was not well liked. He was ruthless, underhanded, and beyond all, blood-thirsty. He downed at least three goblets of blood every day from his river to assure it would never overflow, and every sip was his version of ambrosia. Little could most gods to do him, as he was powerful by his own right by not needing to depend on the ambrosia other gods depended on.<br /> <br /> His first of three strikes came during the day of the Usurpation. A Solar Twilight had locked himself in his study with his numerous artifacts, with hopes that one would be enough to save him. Time was not on his side however, as those of the Blood of Elements busted through his door. As a battle cry, one blessed by the Blood of Elements yelled the phrase that drew Styuger\u2019s eye as he struck down the Twilight. Not minutes after they left with a pile of First Age Artifacts, the god appeared and claimed all the blood of the fallen solar for his own, taking care to keep it in its own cauldron, as those blessed by the Blood of the Sun were rarely slain with his mantra in the air. The Unconquered Sun found out that the Blood God had desecrated the body of a Solar by stripping it of its blood, and demanded the god cast the blood of the Solar back on the land. The god, to keep his graces, spend five years sifting through his river, pretending to collect the blood of the mixed solar, and poured a cauldron of blood onto the floor of the Manse where the Solar had died. He kept the cauldron of Solar blood secretly hidden, on a low boil to ensure it never settled for decades.<br /> <br /> His second of three strikes came during the day the Scarlet Empress rose. Outside of the Great Imperial Manse, those blessed with the Blood of the Moon fought tooth, nail, and claw with the Balorian Crusades. A group of particularly quick Bloods of the Moon who thought it best to seek out the Fair Folk behind the forces did so. The Owl who Knows, Venom Coats the Claw, and The Savage Quoll-Lion, dashed behind enemy lines and struck directly for the Raksha. The group of three found exactly what they were looking for, in a group of nine. The Owl who Knows whispered the words of the mantra to both of his allies, and the battle erupted. Nine Raksha fell, where three blessed by the Blood of the Moon were protected by their tattoos. They left quickly, as there were plenty more Nobles to deal with. There was no blood of mortals to collect here, but the god could still make a gain. He appeared, and with strenuous effort, collected the nine falsified souls of the fallen Raksha, as it was what allowed them to exist here, and was thus the Blood of the Wyld. He stored the mass in an unused cauldron, and sealed it within, as he was unsure if the \u2018blood\u2019 retained Wyld properties, and may just grow legs and leave his care. He was called upon by Luna who stated that she had Chosen that had seen him briefly at the area where Raksha had fallen, and had been expending an exuberant amount of essence. He stated that he\u2019d heard his mantra and showed up to only the dead Raksha, and lied that he had attempted to see if he could derive some sort of physical liquid blood from the fallen Raksha for study by those blessed by the Blood of the Loom, but had ultimately failed any attempt to do so. Luna was suspicious, but accepted the answer, as there was nothing more she could do beyond questioning.<br /> <br /> His third of three strikes came 100 years later, during the day The Maidens finally found reason to cast him out of Yu-Shan. The Maiden of Battles stated that no great battle was complete without blood soaking the land. The Maiden of Journeys stated that the best journeys were earned through blood, sweat and tears; not just sweat and tears. The Maiden of Endings stated that there are some endings that are simply not complete without the blood of the fallen to showcase what happened, and to bring the end to a clean close. The Maiden of Serenity more or less agreed with her sisters. The Maiden of Secrets was by far the most annoyed, as she knew of Cauldron of Solar blood, the captured false souls of the fallen Raksha, as well as the Exigent Blessing that Styuger had stolen from The Unconquered Sun. With the evidence stacked against him, the God of Blood had no defense to turn to. So the maidens cast him from heaven, and down into creation, cursed to flow as a clear river, much like his very own, for the rest of eternity.<br /> <br /> What the maidens were unaware of was that all of those reagents, besides the Exigent Blessing, had been used ten years prior. The Blood God had taken 8lbs. of Soulsteel, and 2 lbs. of Starmetal, and melted them to a liquid, then deposited it into the cauldron of Solar\u2019s blood. He slow-boiled the brew for 40 years, until he was sure that it was cool enough he could reach in and pluck the cooled metal from inside. This was easy, given that all the iron of the blood had soaked into the metal and become a part of it, turning the entire metal a light red. The Blood God pulled the 10 lbs. of metal from his cauldron, and immediately noticed how malleable the metal was. He had expected this, and pulled the nine souls of the Raksha from their confinement, and folded the metal on top of each fake soul. With the metal folded 9 times over each false soul, he folded it one last time and heat-treated the blade in molten-boiling blood. The blade took on a deep red tint, and was substantially more sturdy, much like Soulsteel was supposed to be. He attuned to the blade, and hid it within Elsewhere.<br /> <br /> When he was cast down, any hope to find where the resources that were used to forge it fell with him, and even Nara-O was unsure as to where the reagents may have gone, as it appeared the god was not the only one concerned in the knowledge of how the reagents were used.<br /> The Exigent Blessing that Styuger had stolen was his only saving grace from the curse that was cast upon him. He waits as a river, in the far North-eastern corner of creation, gaining prayer still from those who recite his mantra, because the spark of The Unconquered Sun that lies within the Exigent Blessing is enough to keep the god conscious.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Evocations of Sanguis Gladii</b></span><br /> The wielder, upon attunement, gains the Past Lives merit at the 3-dot level.<br /> <br /> Upon attunement, the blood essence of the sword connects and mixes with that of the wielder, making wielding the blade effortless. The wielder may wield the sword in one hand, but does not remove the Two-Handed Tag of the weapon.<br /> <br /> If wielded by a Chosen that has the Great Curse inflicted upon them, their limit will work differently, as described below. If wielded by something not inflicted by the great curse, they will now have a limit track that works as detailed below:<br /> The wielded has a limit track of 7. On one side, it is labeled Insanity, on the other side, it is labeled curse. The wielded has two different types of Limit, Insanity, and Curse. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Curse Limit works just as normal limit does. Should the track of seven be filled with curse, the wielder will experience the Limit Break Compassionate Martyrdom, as well as losing access to any charm that is not in the Lore, Occult, Investigation, Medicine, and Bureaucracy abilities. </span><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Insanity Limit works the opposite of Curse Limit, growing as the wielder furthers their goals and slips more and more into their own self-righteousness. Once per scene, if the wielder acts in a way that supports a Major Intimacy and has an effect on the scene, they will roll one die of Insanity. Once per scene, if the wielder acts in a way that supports a Defining Intimacy and has an effect on the scene, they will roll two dice of Insanity. Once per scene, if the wielder is ever responsible for the deaths of innocents, and tries to justify the killings or ignores them, they roll three dice of insanity. Should the track of seven be filled with Insanity Limit, the wielder will experience the Limit Break Berserk Anger, and gain [Willpower x 2] Wyld Mutations (as chosen by the Storyteller) that last for the duration of the Limit Break.</span> These tracks fill up starting at opposite ends, and override each other as they are gained. If the wielder is at 4 Curse and 3 Insanity, and does something to further their motivations or intimacies, then they will gain a point of Insanity and lose a point of Curse. After a break occurs, the limit track is emptied. Un-attuning to the blade and not wielding it does make the limit track disappear, but it does not clear it. Any actions that would gain Curse or Insanity do not change the Limit track if the blade is not wielded and attuned to. Picking the blade back up at any time will restore the limit track back to what it was before the wielder left it.<br /> <br /> Evocations of Sanguis Gladii will have the keyword \u201cLimit\u201d on them. Evocations with this keyword will have different effectiveness depending on the wielder\u2019s current limit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Evocations<br /> <br /> Name: <span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Clarity in Care and Madness</span></span><br /> Cost: 5m Mins: Essence 1 Type: Supplemental Keywords: Withering-Only, Limit Duration: Instant PreReq: None <br /> Desc.: Add two non-charm dice to an attack. If Insanity is 5+, reduce the cost of this charm by [Insanity/2], rounded up. If Curse is 5+, add [Curse/2] charm-added dice as well.<br /> <br /> Name: <span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Crimson Flower Kata</span></span><br /> Cost: 4m per petal, 1wp Mins: Essence 2 Type: Simple Keywords: Decisive-Only, Limit Duration: Variable PreReq: Clarity in Care and Madness <br /> Desc.: After making decisive attack, may spend 4 motes up to [Insanity] times, each 4 adding one petal of blood blooming from the struck target. At the beginning of each of the target\u2019s turns, one petal recedes back with enough force to cut flesh, inflicting [Curse] initiative damage. The initiative is lost, not gained by the user of Crimson Flower Kata. If Insanity is 5+ reduce the cost of each petal by 2m. If Curse is 5+, the petals deals 2 dice of decisive damage that ignores hardness instead of dealing initiative damage.<br /> <br /> Name: <span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bloody Double</span></span><br /> Cost: 8m, 2lh Mins: Essence 3 Type: Simple Keywords: Limit Duration: One Scene <br /> PreReq: Crimson Flower Kata <br /> Desc.: Creates a duplicate of the user out of blood and bile. The duplicate acts as a three-dot ally (as per the merit) controlled by the storyteller, with a defining intimacy of furthering the user\u2019s goals, a major intimacy to protect the user, and a negative intimacy to iron. The stats for the Bloody double are as labeled below:<br /> <br /> Essence:1; Willpower: 4; Join Battle: [Insanity+3], HL: -0x[Curse]/Incap; Peripheral Motes: 15<br /> Actions: The bloody double gains all the users favored and caste abilities at half the dot scores.<br /> Combat: Attack (Bloody Grand Daiklaive): Variable dice pool (Damage 13, minimum 3);<br /> Combat movement 6, Evasion [Variable], Parry [Variable], Soak/Hardness: [Curse]/[Insanity]<br /> Cold Iron Ruin: Weapons made of iron deal aggravated damage, and double all decisive damage applied to them.<br /> The bloody double can use Clarity in Care and Madness, and Crimson Flower Kata, and bases their numbers off the users Insanity and Curse. In addition, if the user has Insanity 7, the bloody double has access to the Fae charm [Dreadful Fanged Maelstrom Approach]. If the user has Curse 7, the bloody double has the terrestrial spell [Death of Obsidian Butterflies], and instead gains 5 sorcerous motes every turn instead of regaining normal motes.<br /> <br /> This ability may only be used once per session.<br /> <br /> Name: <span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Unchained Fever Dreams</span></span><br /> Cost: 8m, 2wp Mins: Essence 3 Type: Simple Keywords: Limit Duration: One Scene PreReq: Crimson Flower Kata <br /> Desc.: The wielder channels the deep receded essences of the blade and in a mighty explosion of colors and sound, summons forth dormant creatures. They summon forth lions, wolfs, and/or bears in number equal to the user\u2019s [Curse] / 2. Each creature has a number of wyld mutation dots equal to the user\u2019s [Insanity] x 2. These creatures do not serve the user, but will fight the user\u2019s enemies until they are no more, at which point they may or may not turn on the user, depending on how involved and savage they were in combat. If the user has Curse 5+, all summoned beasts gain 3 extra dice to all actions for they scene, and are more likely to ignore the user. If the user has Insanity 5+, reduce the mote cost of this charm by 2, and the user has a chance of summoning something large, such as a tyrant lizard, river dragon, or Ox-dragon.<br /> <br /> This ability may only be used once per session.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Name: <span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">She Who Walks the Red Path</span></span><br /> Cost: 7m, 1wp Mins: Essence 4 Type: Simple Keywords: Limit Duration: [Insanity] Rounds<br /> PreReq: Bloody Double, Unchained Fever Dreams <br /> Desc. The Blood God\u2019s river revitalizes itself around the wielder, rejoicing in the carnage the wielder brings to a battlefield. All enemies within short range of the wielder treat the ground as difficult terrain. For every non-trivial character, friend or foe that dies within short range of the wielder, the wielder gains: 1 initiative, 1 armor soak, and [Curse] motes. If the size of a group falls while this is active, or two non-trivial opponents fall within range of the river, expand the range the river reaches to medium. The wielder does not treat the ground as difficult terrain, and gets [Curse] non-charm dice to Rush actions, and allows the wielder to rush opponents up to medium range away.<br /> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> So it is an odd blade, with an odd assortment of evocations, but I feel good about its first draft. 2500+ words for an artifact I feel is a decent standard.<br /> So please, give some feedback, balance concerns, and if you have any question about the (Possibly somewhat confusing) mechanics, let me know. And if you think of any way you can loophole through anything, please bring that up to. I'd prefer removing those types of impurities especially.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12184-lazzerusthanatos","name":"LazzerusThanatos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12184_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T19:46:39-07:00","id":943303,"title":"","content":"I couldn't help but notice that nobody seems to have written up Evocations for the tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara initiation. Allow me to take a crack at it with a version mostly centered around sorcerer-assassins, with some token nods toward demon summoning and Black Claw synergy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i64.tinypic.com/9lkd3a.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (Yes, I couldn't resist the urge to indulge my twee self and lay out the Charm tree for the Mara tattoos in a way that spells a giant M, however counterintuitive it is from a &quot;starting Evocations at the top, followups at the bottom&quot; perspective. Sue me.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Evocations of the Demonic Tattoos of Mara</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Night-Drinking Meditation</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m +3m/extra range band, <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Mute<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> Meditating under the night sky for an hour, the sorcerer draws in the essence of the darkness that surrounds her, refining it and storing it in her tattoos for later use. When she releases the motes committed to this Charm, an area of supernatural darkness centered on her current whereabouts springs up for the duration of the scene. This effect encompasses everything within Close range, plus one additional range band in every direction per 3 extra motes paid when activating this Evocation, out to a maximum of Medium at 8m. Within her zone of darkness, nonmagical sources of light only provide illumination out to close range, and even the animas of the Celestial Exalted shed no light beyond short range. Magical effects that explicitly dispel darkness or provide light beyond short range are contested by the sorcerer\u2019s Wits+Occult, with (Essence) automatic successes (roll her opponent\u2019s permanent Willpower score in opposition if the contesting effect doesn\u2019t specify a pool to be used); however, the Evocation has no defense against magic that allows a character to see in total darkness or effects designated uncontestable such as the Eye of the Unconquered Sun.<br /> Releasing commitment to Night-Drinking Meditation may supplement an attempt to re-establish surprise, providing appropriate concealment regardless of the character\u2019s surroundings and penalizing Perception+Awareness rolls to notice the sorcerer as per total darkness.<br /> Reduce the cost of this Evocation by 3m if the meditation takes place during New Moon or Calibration, to a minimum of 1m.<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: I generally prefer starting effects that are costly, but offer an interesting expansion to the character\u2019s tactical repertoire over smaller bonuses. The ability to hide with no cover or concealment is certainly an impactful one*, but I believe the nighttime meditation requirement (which practically translates to a \u201eonce per day\u201d reset condition), coupled with the sheer inconvenience of having to commit the mote cost until you actually use it make it appropriate for Essence 1.<br /> *Solar Stealth grants it at Essence 2, albeit packaged with a scenelong Stealth booster, which likely affects the overall balance of the Charm in question.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>One With Shadows</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 10m, <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> By activating this Evocation, the sorcerer can transform into a living shadow for one scene, carrying all items currently on her person with herself. In this form, she can slip under the space beneath a door or slide through the thinnest crack. In well-lit regions, observers notice the existence of an unusual shadow if they make a (Perception + Awareness) roll at difficulty 3, unless the wearer conceals himself in a larger shadow.<br /> When the character is a shadow, she is dematerialized and can only affect or be affected by other dematerialized creatures or by Charms and weapons capable of attacking dematerialized foes<b>. If the wearer uses such a Charm or weapon while dematerialized, she briefly materializes for the duration of the attack, and can affect material foes \u2013 but she can also be affected by them in turn.</b> Otherwise, she is immune to all materialized threats, although she can be trapped in a room that is sealed tightly enough.<br /> Once the scene ends, the character must remain in solid form for at least ten minutes before transforming back into a shadow.<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: this is practically the basic effect of the Belt of Shadow Walking, except it costs a Charm pick and has been changed to be merely very very powerful instead of being outright broken. Arguably.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Force-Swallowing Darkness Defense</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 6m, <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> When a blow connects, the sorcerer\u2019s tattoos surge with power, straining to break free to defend their master. The mystical markings uncoil from around her chakras, shifting to meet her foe\u2019s blade, and her flesh bulges with arcane energies as if writhing serpents were moving beneath her skin.<br /> After the character is hit by a withering attack but before damage is rolled, she may activate this Evocation to increase her soak by (Essence or 3, whichever is higher). Moreover, if the triggering attack still Crashes her, it causes an eruption of Essence that suffuses her form, causing her to ignore the normal restrictions associated with casting while in Initiative Crash.<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: I love the imagery of mystical tattoos coming alive, but running around half-naked isn\u2019t exactly a viable strategy in Exalted (not without a significant investment in Resistance, at least), and what is the point if you can\u2019t show them off? Thus, a soak booster seemed like a no-brainer \u2013 however, I couldn\u2019t make it </i>too<i> efficient in case someone decided to stack it on top of Spirit Strengthens the Skin. So I bumped up the cost and gave it a situationally powerful extra effect (+1 wp and the equivalent of 3 non-Charm successes on shape sorcery for 6 motes is incredibly good, but I\u2019m not sure how tactically sound is the \u201ekeep gesticulating in front of the dude who just Crashed you\u201d idea in most cases compared to the alternative of looking for an exit strategy).</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wound-Eluding Shadow Substitution</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 7m, <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: One With Shadows, Force-Swallowing Darkness Defense<br /> <br /> Sensing her impending doom, the sorcerer can utter the secret name of her own shadow, compelling it to stand in her place while she seeps through the unseen cracks of the world to avoid the blow.<br /> After the character has been hit but before damage is rolled, she may activate this Evocation to redirect the hit to her shadow. The shadow\u2019s Health Track and healing times are identical to a mortal\u2019s, but all damage caused to it is automatically Aggravated, and it\u2019s immune to poisons and bleeding. This defense is not infallible: any damage in excess of the shadow\u2019s Health Levels spills over to its master.<br /> If the shadow takes damage to any of its -2 Health Levels, the injuries start to show: it might start walking with a limp (no matter how healthy its owner), have big chunks of its \u201eflesh\u201d missing, or whatever visuals the group finds entertaining and/or appropriate. If it ever takes damage to its Incapacitated Health Level, it\u2019s destroyed forever. Noticing an absent or irregular shadow is generally a Difficulty 3 Perception+Awareness roll, albeit the consequences of such a discovery are heavily dependent on social context and should be determined by the GM on a case-by-case basis.<br /> Replacing a destroyed shadow can be done with an Ambition 1 sorcerous working of the Terrestrial Circle; imbuing such a creation with extraordinary powers (for example, extra health levels and faster healing times), however, falls squarely under the purview of the Celestial Circle, with Ambition determined by the potency of said powers.<br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> once this Evocation has been activated, the character may not call upon its power again until her shadow is completely healed.<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: very much straining the limits of even Solar power, this is basically an imperfect perfect at Essence 1 \u2013 a slightly bigger (it can absorb 6 Health Levels without consequences instead of 5) version of Iron Skin Concentration that requires no mote commitment until it\u2019s reset. However, resetting it is </i>way<i> more of a pain in the ass (up to two weeks of waiting instead of just staying in bed for one day while the Twilight slaps Wound-Mending Care Technique on you), with a chance of actually having to </i>pay xp<i> for it. I think it\u2019s just about appropriate for a Solar, but I probably wouldn\u2019t allow it for Celestials and below.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Thousand-Fanged Night Manifestation</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4m 1wp, <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Night-Drinking Meditation<br /> <br /> The darkness pouring forth from the sorcerer\u2019s chakras is more than just an absence of light \u2013 it gives form to unseen terrors, sheltering them and allowing them to prey upon the unwary.<br /> Upon releasing her commitment to Night-Drinking Meditation, the character may activate this Evocation, allowing every First Circle demon she personally summoned and is currently within her zone of darkness to reflexively materialize at no cost and take a re-establish surprise action.<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: this is basically Material Exegesis Prana, except it only works on First Circles, and even then only on ones the character summoned personally, and even then only on those that also happen to hang around in her close vicinity. And it doesn\u2019t have a willpower regain condition either. And it\u2019s tied to a more ore less once per day resource. But it doesn\u2019t require a roll, and it doesn\u2019t require an action, and allows the materializing demons to immediately take advantage of the concealment it provides, which is a pretty massive benefit from an action economy perspective. I think it more or less balances out in the end.</i><br /> <i>(It\u2019s also probably way better if you\u2019re a Twilight, which I\u2019m pretty happy with, because even though I\u2019m not particularly bothered by Twilights not being the best at sorcery, I know that many people are, and I want this to be useful for as many people as possible.)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Unfettered Shade Dissolution</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1wp, <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Night-Drinking Meditation, One With Shadows<br /> <br /> The sorcerer releases the roiling shadows stored within her chakras, and in the same heartbeat, she also releases her grip on her material form, dissolving into the darkness and pulling her body together at a different location.<br /> Upon releasing her commitment to Night-Drinking Meditation, the sorcerer may pay a point of Willpower to reflexively teleport to any point within her area of darkness; this counts as her movement action for the turn (if she activates it outside of her turn, it uses up her movement action in her next turn). This may even take her through walls and other forms of physical obstruction as long as the other side is within range and not specifically warded against teleportation; however, this Evocation provides no information about the perils that await her there.<br /> If the prerequisite was used to supplement a re-establish surprise action, opposing Perception+Awareness rolls may be even further penalized by the character\u2019s sudden disappearance, especially if she used Unfettered Shade Dissolution to reach an unlikely hiding place.<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: another Night-Drinking Meditation upgrade. If it feels like it\u2019s starting to strain from being pulled in too many directions (It helps you in hiding! It lets you manifest your demon army! It\u2019s a repositioning tool! But it also lets you infiltrate places you normally couldn\u2019t! But only once per day!), that\u2019s completely intentional; I want it to be a locus of interesting decisions and/or deliberate planning to set up situations where it can be used for maximum impact. Also worth noting that not every character needs every Evocation: for example, a sorcerer-assassin can probably get great value out of Night-Drinking Meditation and Unfettered Shade Dissolution alone, without branching out into demon summoning.</i><br /> <i>Balance-wise, it\u2019s another \u201efast track to power\u201d, much like Night-Drinking Meditation itself: the ability to cross multiple range bands and to move through impassable obstacles both appear at Essence 3 in the Solar charmset. However, the equivalent in Athletics, Godspeed Steps takes its user across three range bands for 4m 1wp, so I feel comfortable pegging an 8m 1wp, once per day effect that reaches out to medium as appropriate for Essence 2. As for the equivalent in Larceny, Door-Evading Technique, it is bound by the limitations inherent to the Solar charmset; as Unfettered Shade Dissolution represents a strange and esoteric effect gained through a pact with a powerful denizen of Malfeas instead of a logical outgrowth of mortal skill sharpened to a legendary degree, it can be allowed to access overt displays of supernatural might earlier. And, of course, there\u2019s the whole \u201eonce per day\u201d thing, too.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mara\u2019s Embrace</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4m, <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Force-Swallowing Darkness Defense<br /> <br /> The sorcerer\u2019s tattoos rip themselves off of her skin in the form of serpentine shadows that grasp at her opponent, empowered by the same forces that fuel her magic.<br /> This Evocation enhances a Grapple gambit, granting double 9s on the attack roll if the target is standing in darkness or shadow heavy enough to qualify as concealment for attempting stealth, holds an Intimacy of love or lust toward the sorcerer, or if it\u2019s new moon or Calibration. Double 8s if two criteria are met, double 7s if all three are.<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: living tattoos! Black Claw synergy! What more could anybody ask for?</i><br /> <i>Pricing notes: doubles can be devastating or useless, depending on how you roll. On average, they\u2019re worth +0.1 success per die, so 2m per double seems like a reasonable price point for a splat that can go up to 20 dice on a roll (well, 23 with sufficiently advanced munchkinization). Of course, this completely ignores that these are non-Charm successes and should accordingly be priced much more conservatively, but given the fact that maximizing one\u2019s grappling pool is rarely a priority for a sorcerer, and reliably arranging situations where at least two criteria are met takes some planning and forethought which should be rewarded, I\u2019m feeling rather confident that the end result won\u2019t end up being gamebreaking.</i><br /> <i>Of course, if there\u2019s a sudden surge in Supernal Brawlers who express a strong interest in picking up the eerily specific combination of occult, seduction and stealth as their secondary competencies, I may end up revising that opinion.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kiss of Draining Shadows</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m, 1wp; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Until the grapple ends<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Mara\u2019s Embrace<br /> <br /> This Evocation can be used during a grapple attempt initiated by, or targeting the character. After the grapple\u2019s attack and Initiative roll have succeeded, but before the control roll, Kiss of Draining Shadows can be activated to siphon (Essence/2, round up) dots of Strength off of the opponent the sorcerer is grappling with. Dots lost by the victim are gained by the character for the duration of the grapple, explicitly counting as a bonus added by Charms. Kiss of Draining Shadows can\u2019t reduce a character below Strength 1, nor can it increase the sorcerer\u2019s Strength rating above double its normal value.<br /> If the character incapacitates her opponent before the grapple ends, Strength dots gained through this Evocation persist for the duration of the scene; moreover, whenever she takes a shape sorcery action, she may sacrifice a dot of extra Strength to gain three additional sorcerous motes.<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: another riff on the living tattoo aesthetics, this time emphasizing Mara\u2019s vampiric themes. In addition to the Black Claw synergy, it's also intended to help defend against incoming grapples, which tend to be a death sentence for squishy sorcerers.</i><br /> <i>As a side note, it may or may not be worth noting that the wording of this Evocation results in two interesting emergent qualities. First is that at high Essence, it can actually be more beneficial to grapple high-Strength opponents because you can leech more Strength dots off of them, since the victim can\u2019t lose dots that would take them below Strength 1, and only dots lost by the victim are gained by the user. (I like to imagine that Mara would heartily approve of this preference for muscular hunks.) Second is that since Strength dots gained by incapacitating an opponent can be converted into smotes and a character can\u2019t leech off more than his normal rating, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m7RosIoQisA\" target=\"_blank\">high-Strength sorcerers are objectively better at casting spells</a>.</i><br /> <i>Of course, neither of these is likely to become relevant at most tables, since 60 sessions are a lot to play through.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Night-Rallying Call</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: (demon\u2019s Essence)*2m; <b>Essence</b>: 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Thousand-Fanged Night Manifestation<br /> <br /> Drawing upon her patron's affinity for demons, the sorcerer lets out an irresistible call her servants hear and obey immediately, no matter where they are.<br /> In conjunction with activating the prerequisite, the sorcerer may call a demon summoned and bound by her to her side as long as it\u2019s in Creation, regardless of distance, by paying motes equal to twice the demon\u2019s permanent Essence. Demons summoned with Night-Rallying Call are eligible to benefit from Thousand-Fanged Night Manifestation even if they are not of the First Circle.<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: discount Twilight anima power to the rescue! Except it\u2019s good for Twilights as well since they can\u2019t normally bind Second Circles as familiars.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 04-08-2017, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:40:21-07:00","id":946861,"title":"","content":"<b>Sun and Moon Sheath(Articulated Plate, 4-dots)</b><br /> This armour is forged with a thousand scales Orichalcum attached to a thick layer of liquid Moonsilver, each scale is carved with prayer to both The Unconquered Sun and Luna. The Moonsilver constantly shifts through prayers invoking the glory of the heavens themselves, and calling their blessings down on the bearer. It was forged by a cadre of Dragon-Blooded, working with their worst enemies, a small group of Lunars during the Balorian crusade in a desperate attempt to create something that would stem the tides of Chaos. Sadly, the Artifact they created had other ideas, as the craftsmen were assaulted with visions of the celestial bodies in all their glory. The Wyld eventually claimed their hideout as well, but not before they finished the armour. And so, satisfied and their purpose complete, they charged into certain deaths against the Fae, while the armour fell into the Wyld, where it would remain. However, rumours of its existence and location constantly abound, even though none have ever laid eyes on it since it was forged.<br /> <br /> Thanks to Kilbert for helping with the Evocations.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocation</b><br /> A Solar or Lunar that attunes this armour for an additional 2 motes finds that it will always fit them perfectly, reducing its mobility penalty by 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Dawn's Glorious Ascent</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m; <b>Essence</b>: 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Perilous<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> The Heavens bear the wearer up to ever greater heights. This charm supplements a jump, or an action to rise from prone.<br /> <br /> If used to supplement a jump, the bearer does not fall from its apex until his next turn, held in the a halo of light. However, he may not activate this charm to prevent falling damage.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, this evocation may be used to reflexively rise from prone.<br /> <br /> <i>(First Editing run: I like this, I think I'll keep it...)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Mystery Concealing Crescent</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 3m; <b>Essence</b>: 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> <br /> The bearer of the armour may activate this evocation in response to a successful Reed Intentions action. Using this charm, the bearer creates a false intimacy that is read alongside a real one, or a false purpose to be read alongside a real purpose. There is no way to distinguish between the two, though using the charm causes silver crescent to appear around the bearers irises.<br /> <br /> <i>(And this too, I think is fine)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Heavenly Noonday Brilliance</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4m; <b>Essence</b>: 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Dawn's Glorious Ascent<br /> <br /> Drawing deeper on the glory of the Sun, the bearer finds his own glory magnified. If the bearer's anima is at the dim level, he may double 9s on a presence roll. If it is at the glowing level, he may double 8s or ignore the penalty for attempting to influence groups. If it is at the Bonfire level, he may double 7s and ignore the penalties for affecting groups.<br /> <br /> No matter which of the options he chooses, he may only use this charm once per day, resetting the following noon.<br /> <br /> <i>(This is a nice bug evocation. I think I'll bump it up to being the Capstone for the Sun Branch, and drop in magnificent light.)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Blessed Full Moon</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m; <b>Essence</b>: 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Mystery Concealing Crescent<br /> <br /> By spending a turn in prayer to the Silver Lady, the bearer cloaks themselves in mystery and silver light. The caster's movements are difficult to follow as she moves from one location to the next. Nor can the method of movement be discerned. The bearer simply appears to be in one place and then another. Even more insidiously, silver after images flow around her, inflicting a -1 penalty on all attack rolls for the scene.<br /> <br /> <i><b>(In Magnificent Light</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 6m, 3a; <b>Essence</b>: 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Heavenly Noonday Brilliance<br /> <br /> After using Dawn's Glorious Ascent, the bearer sheds their anima, casting it towards the ground like golden rain. For the rest of the scene they gain a brilliant white anima banner which functions like the anima of a Dragon-Blood and may not be exhausted by any means. However, they lose access to any abilities granted to them by their normal anima banner.) Removed</i><br /> <br /> <b>Hollow Black Moon</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 7m; <b>Essence</b>: 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: (Essence) Turns<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Blessed Full Moon<br /> <br /> Spending a further turn in prayer after the activation of Blessed Full Moon causes the cloak of silver light to darken and eventually become completely black. Each turn the bearer spends wreathed in this darkness, the bearer may reflexively choose one real intimacy and generate one false intimacy of matching strength. At the end of the duration these intimacies are switched, and the now false intimacies are cast out, becoming pale reflections of the caster. Until the end of the scene, the caster may move these pale images about as he pleases with but a thought. At the end of the scene, the illusions merge once more with the character, and he may choose which intimacies to retain, while the others are consumed by the armour.<br /> <br /> <i>Removing these. Well. Hollow Black Moon makes enough sense, but In Magnificent Light doesn't so... Scrap that. Replace In Magnificent Light with the following:</i><br /> <br /> <b>Descent of the Celestial Dragon</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: +8m; <b>Essence</b>: 4<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Hollow Black Moon, Heavenly Noonday Brilliance<br /> <br /> Calling on the absolute dominance of the Sun and Moon over the Heavens, the attuned ascends unto the heavens. By paying an 8 mote surcharge on Hollow Black Moon during the night or Heavenly Noonday Brilliance during the day, along with the benefits of either charm, the attuned gains the benefits of Soaring Dragon's Flight. Furthermore, they may cause immediate and drastic changes in the weather by spending a turn making an appropriate stunt; they may not take any other action during this turn<br /> <br /> And I appear to be somewhat all over the place with this, and any help would be appreciated. <i>Still stands.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","user":"Myradmir","date":".  Gave Descent of the Celestial Dragon an effect. 08-11-2016, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T08:21:59-07:00","id":946954,"title":"","content":"This thread continues to be a joy to read. Keep it up everyone!<br /> <br /> I'd like to issue a challenge. Some of you have done this, others haven't. But I challenge you all to make Artifacts that have innate, by-the-rules drawbacks, <b>without </b>removing them in the magic of the Artifact.<br /> <br /> Examples include:<br /> -Make Throwing weapons that <i>don't</i> return to you.<br /> -Make armor with mobility penalty that you don't get to reduce<br /> -Make armor that doesn't magically count as not-armor for martial arts<br /> -Make weapons with tags that don't let you ignore the cost, difficulty, or limitations of those tags (like Smashing)<br /> -Make Heavy Weapons that <i>keep</i> that -1 Defense penalty<br /> <br /> It's so easy to think of magical items as &quot;like the base stuff, but without those pesky drawbacks&quot;. I'll be the first to admit being guilty of this, but the beauty of the Evocation system is that they don't have to work in this way. You'll notice that almost none of the Dev-created Artifacts ignore the innate difficulties of the items. Their advantages are not directly related to the item in question. <br /> <br /> You could make a sword that lets you fly like an eagle. An armor that lets you walk through walls. A shield that purifies any liquid that falls across its surface. A hammer that forges bones together better than metal.<br /> <br /> I challenge you all to embrace the difficulties of the system, and find ways to express your artifact with other advantages. I'll not judge anyone who wants to keep making your heavy artifact armor that works for a snake martial artist if that's what you want to make. But if you do, it's not part of my challenge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T08:35:00-07:00","id":947800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=946954#post946954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread continues to be a joy to read. Keep it up everyone!<br /> <br /> I'd like to issue a challenge. Some of you have done this, others haven't. But I challenge you all to make Artifacts that have innate, by-the-rules drawbacks, <b>without </b>removing them in the magic of the Artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how this one does for your challenge but here is my attempt its all about mote manipulation and its got the built in downside of being normally a melee weapon unless its activated and then its a brawl weapon:<br /> <br /> This weapon comes from an idea for a Zanpakto from bleach. The basic concept is from there so I decided to keep the transforming aspect of release.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Lady(Lord) Gwenevere (Starmetal and Moonsilver Reaper Daiklave) Artifact 5(?)</b></u><br /> <br /> Lady Gwenevere was originally a goddess of trickery and decipetion. She climibed high in the celestial bureaucracy through a mix of betrayal and theft, going so far as to steal prayers from her betters and use the gained power to power overthrow and raise in power. This continued in the first age until she stole from Luna. Getting caught she was quickly turned to starmetal. The twilight that worked on the weapon she as to become found that the metal spoke to him and almost seduced him. The goddess cheated like she always did and was still conciouss in her hunk of starmetal and seduced her crafter into giving her the chance to live again and seduce her weilder. Allowing her to steal the power of her weilder and those she attacks.<br /> <br /> Special: The wielder of this weapon gets a positive intimacy of Romatic Love. The weapon pretends like it is whatever gender the wielder finds attractive.<br /> <br /> Evocation:<br /> <b>Drain Gwenevere</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m -0 LHL <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b><br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Minor Intimacy of Love for the weapon.<br /> The weapon twists and shifts wrapping around the wielders hand like a glove. The tip of the blade splits and strikes into the weilders wrist drawing blood and drawing essence from the wielder awaken the sleeping goddess in the blade. While in this form the weapon has several special abilities:<br /> First it becomes an light artifact weapon with all the normal tags associated with a mundane cetus with meaning the weapon can no longer be used with melee.<br /> Secound all people within medium range must pay an additional essence at each instances of essence use, this tax is also paid by the wielder. This mote tax is always drained from personal essence first. If this tax cannot be paid the person loses 1 Init dues to discomfort of their essence being pulled to the negative.<br /> Finally the weapon gains a 20 mote essence pool that is initially empty. The weapon gains the mote tax from all the people effected by the essence drain in addition it gains one mote per round in combat taking that mote from the wielders normal essence gain. (the wielder only gains 4 motes per round) These motes be used only on attacks with the weapon or on the evocations of the weapon. Should the weapons mote pool be full any excess motes gained are added to the wielders pools.<br /> The essence to activate this weapon is not committed and the health level cost is waived if all of the weilder -0 health levels are already filled with lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Alternate idea:<br /> Secound all people within Medium range lose 1 mote of peripheral essence at each instance of Essence expenditure. This affects the wielder.<br /> Finally the weapon gains a 20 mote essence pool initially with 10 motes in it. The weapon drains 1 mote of the personal pool and adds it to its essence pool with each strike against a person with essence. If the blow hits a person with no personal essence it adds one additional success to the damage or Init roll as its ripped from the affected persons soul.<br /> For the purposes of this effect spirits essence pool counts as both personal and peripheral.<br /> <br /> <b>Taste the Essence</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m <b>Mins: </b>Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b><br /> <b>Duration:</b> Until next turn<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Drain Gwenevere<br /> This Evocation can only be active when Drain Gwenevere is active.<br /> This charm gives the weilder the ability to taste the essence in the air. It allows him to see beings that can wield essence. Spirits are always visible to this charm in any form they take. Beings with separate essence pools are not always fully visible. Any being that has mote left in his personal essence is visible as if he were a spirit. If the being has no essence remaining in his personal essence pool all actions against him take -1 penalty if this is the sense used to locate him. If the being is not a spirit and has no essence remaining in its pools (or has no essence pools to begin with) it is considered invisible to this charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Cult Stealing Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m <b>Mins: </b>Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplmental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b> Decisive only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant (Health levels dealt days)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Drain Gwenevere<br /> This charm supplements a Decisive attack against a spirit. It may strike Immatiel spirit normally. In addition should the spirit have accesss to a cult this attack steals the connection to its cult. For every health level of damage dealt that is how many days the spirit does not gain the benfits of its cult instead the weilder gains it. Should the Spirit be permantly killed the cult rating stays with the solar until the worship ends naturally. (Usually a season).<br /> <br /> <b>Essence burning Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m + 1 willpower <b>Mins: </b>Essence3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b> Withering only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Taste the essence, cult Stealing strike<br /> This Evocation can only be used once per day and only when drain Gwenevere is active. This evocation creates a special withering attack. Instead of damaging the enemies it instead drains motes of essence. This attack ignores soak from armor but adds the foes essence to his natural soak. Every success on the withering damage roll drains 1 mote from the targets essence. If Drain Gwenever is active Gwenevere gains half the essence burned this way. If this leaves the essence pool empty the burn instead deals a lethal health level per 2 motes that would have been burned away. This evocation can be reset by stealing a cult rating from a spirit such as with Cult Stealing Strike.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8767,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8767-rattleingpython","user":"rattleingpython","date":". 08-10-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8767-rattleingpython","name":"rattleingpython","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T08:52:56-07:00","id":947807,"title":"","content":"Could someone adapt the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sharur_(mythological_weapon)\" target=\"_blank\">Sharur</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:02:33-07:00","id":947832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=946954#post946954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I challenge you all to embrace the difficulties of the system, and find ways to express your artifact with other advantages. I'll not judge anyone who wants to keep making your heavy artifact armor that works for a snake martial artist if that's what you want to make. But if you do, it's not part of my challenge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I've stayed within these lines with Sanguis, seeing as you can wield it with one hand, but you do not ignore the Two-Handed tag. You can wield it with one hand as more of a thematic thing.<br /> Which by the way, you seem active on these forums often, and especially here in the A&amp;E one, so I was hoping you might be able to look over my artifact and give some feedback? I'm looking for ways to make sure it's...acceptable, by more than just my standards. I've always been horrendous when it comes to balancing charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12184-lazzerusthanatos","name":"LazzerusThanatos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12184_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:23:09-07:00","id":950400,"title":"","content":"Here is the next iteration of the Armor of Wily Murk. Please critique.<br /> <br /> <b>Armor of Wily Murk</b> (Orichalcum chain shirt ***)<br /> <br /> An exalt who attunes the Armor of Wily Murk gains one automatic non-charm success to the larceny roll to conceal it.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Armor of Wily Murk</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cover of Darkness Approach</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Evocations:</b> None<br /> <br /> The Armor of Wily Murk drinks in light, shrouding everything around it in shadow. This evocation creates a could of darkness around the wearer that extends to short range. Any action taken by someone other than the wearer within this could suffers the -3 penalty for blindness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hidden by Darkness Method</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> --, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Evocations:</b> Cover of Darkness Approach<br /> <br /> This evocation permanently upgrades it's prerequisite, making it count as an attempt by the wearer to establish stealth, perception or awareness based rolls to contest this attempt suffer the -3 penalty for blindness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Grue Imitation Prana</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform, Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Evocations:</b> Hidden by Darkness Method<br /> <br /> This charm supplements an attack roll made by any ability, making it count as an ambush as long as the target is within the cloud created by Cover of Darkness Approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T06:32:40-07:00","id":950530,"title":"","content":"<b>Pact With Mara Demonic Tattoo Evocations<br /> <br /> Apprentice Demonologist</b><br /> Cost: -; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Terrestrial Circle Sorcery, Demon of the First Circle<br /> <br /> The inky black tattoos which cover your chakra points become swirling mandalas of demonic potency, growing as your skill in the dark arts grows. You may reduce the ritual time of Demon of the First Circle by up to (Essence + Occult, Divided by 2, round up) hours. At essence 5+ it becomes possible to cast Summon Demon of the First Circle in combat, it requires 2WP and 25 sorcerous motes.<br /> <br /> <b>Gate of Ruin</b><br /> Cost: 5m 1wp; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Instantaneous<br /> Prerequisites: Apprentice Demonologist<br /> <br /> You are able to open a larger fissure between creation and malfeas, hauling more demons through in one ritual than is probably wise. Your thirst for power however is unquenchable. This charm supplements the binding roll on a Summon Demon of the First Circle ritual. Before making the binding roll choose the number of first circle demons you wish to attempt to summon. For each additional demon, treat the difficulty of the binding roll as one higher. You may attempt to summon up to (Essence + Occult) first circle demons at a time.<br /> <br /> <b>Journeyman Demonologist</b><br /> Cost: -; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Apprentice Demonologist, Celestial Circle Sorcery, Demon of the Second Circle<br /> <br /> Your black chakra tattoos grow even larger and more complex, your mastery of the dark arts growing alongside them. You now have the power to command Demons of the Second Circle, and whats more, you have the skill to do so. Whenever making a binding roll against a Demon of the Second Circle, you are able to attempt banishings even if you fail by three or more on the binding roll.<br /> <br /> <b>The Time is Now</b><br /> Cost: 10m 1wp; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Journeyman Demonologist<br /> <br /> Your skill is now such that not even the position of celestial bodies can prevent you from achieving your goals. The Time is Now. You may summon Demons of the First Circle even during daytime, and Demons of the Second Circle without the presence of a full moon at night. If you have Master Demonologist, you may additionally summon Demons of the Third Circle at night outside of Calibration.<br /> <br /> <b>Master Demonologist</b><br /> Cost: 15m 1wp; Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: -<br /> Duration: Instantaneous<br /> Prerequisites: Journeyman Demonologist, Solar Circle Sorcery, Demon of the Third Circle<br /> <br /> Your black chakra tattoos are now complete, moving and twisting and changing constantly in ways that are slightly painful to look at, you have achieved true mastery of of Demonology. Whenever you roll to bind a demon through any of the Demon of the (Number) Circle spells and fail, you may reflexively activate this charm to roll again with the same modifiers as the previous roll, no additional charms may be used on this roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11632-ramaloke","user":"Ramaloke","date":". 10-11-2016, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11632-ramaloke","name":"Ramaloke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:43:28-07:00","id":950726,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar368_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"368\" data-vbnamecard=\"368\">The Unsung Hero</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9453_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9453\" data-vbnamecard=\"9453\">Octopoid</a> <br /> <br /> I don't suppose either of you would be willing to critique the Armor of Wily Murk?<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11632-ramaloke\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11632\" data-vbnamecard=\"11632\">Ramaloke</a> <br /> <br /> Those are some very powerful evocations. My gut says that the effect against 3rd Circles is too strong for a pact with a 2nd Circle like Mara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T17:13:33-07:00","id":950804,"title":"","content":"Which effect against 3rd circles? The only evocation that assists with that on the 'tree' is the last, which allows you a reroll (aside from the time is now, which is sort of a rehash of an old 2e charm).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11632-ramaloke","name":"Ramaloke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T17:25:41-07:00","id":950811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramaloke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=950804#post950804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which effect against 3rd circles? The only evocation that assists with that on the 'tree' is the last, which allows you a reroll (aside from the time is now, which is sort of a rehash of an old 2e charm).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A reroll is a pretty strong bonus, considering it's solar dice pools. But 'The Time is Now&quot; also strikes me as rilly strong, since the time restrictions are part of what keeps Demon of X Circle balanced.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: To clarify, a pact with Mara helping you bind Erembor to your will, seems off to my gut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 08-14-2016, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T18:00:07-07:00","id":950824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=950400#post950400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the next iteration of the Armor of Wily Murk. Please critique.<br /> <br /> <b>Armor of Wily Murk</b> (Orichalcum chain shirt ***)<br /> <br /> An exalt who attunes the Armor of Wily Murk gains one automatic non-charm success to the larceny roll to conceal it.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Armor of Wily Murk</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cover of Darkness Approach</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Evocations:</b> None<br /> <br /> The Armor of Wily Murk drinks in light, shrouding everything around it in shadow. This evocation creates a could of darkness around the wearer that extends to short range. Any action taken by someone other than the wearer within this could suffers the -3 penalty for blindness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hidden by Darkness Method</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> --, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Evocations:</b> Cover of Darkness Approach<br /> <br /> This evocation permanently upgrades it's prerequisite, making it count as an attempt by the wearer to establish stealth, perception or awareness based rolls to contest this attempt suffer the -3 penalty for blindness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Grue Imitation Prana</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m, <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform, Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Evocations:</b> Hidden by Darkness Method<br /> <br /> This charm supplements an attack roll made by any ability, making it count as an ambush as long as the target is within the cloud created by Cover of Darkness Approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd give Cover of Darkness Approach and Hidden by Darkness Method a Willpower cost, at the <i>least</i>. Being able to inflict a -3 penalty to all actions, no defense, is kind of insanely strong, maybe just too strong <i>period</i> - the Smashing tag, for example, does a similar thing but only if you actually hit with an attack (and inflicting some penalties), which already makes it the best tag in the game. Grue Imitation Prana is also insanely powerful for its cost; even if it was like, 10m 2wp, it seems really close to creating a situation where you can gib somebody with very little they can do about it, which isn't very fun in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12048-lvthn","name":"LVTHN","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T18:11:45-07:00","id":950828,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Stellar Hawk (Grand Daiklave \u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7)</span></b><br /> Stellar Hawk is a long and slender curved slashing sword. Its spine is made of moonsilver and its edge of starmetal. Its hilt is made of plain wood and wrapped in black-dyed spider silk. The Old Realm character for \u201chonour\u201d is inscribed upon the guard in orichalcum. It has a single hearthstone socket under the wrap of the handle.<br /> It was forged by an Eclipse caste and gifted to his Dragon-Blooded bodyguard, who would stand in his place for duels of honour at the court of the deliberative. This Terrestrial warrior died protecting her lord during the Usurpation, and the blade was claimed as a trophy and consigned to the vaults of the shogunate. It is believed it saw use during the Balorian Crusade. Its current location is unknown.<br /> The nature of Stellar Hawk favours precision over strength, and was made to defeat single opponents in formalized duels, often with diplomatic consequences.<br /> <br /> By increasing the attunement cost to 8m, the wielder of Stellar Hawk gains the following benefit: when she takes an aim action she also gains the benefits of a full defence action at no cost <b>only against the opponent she\u2019s aiming at</b>.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Evocations of Stellar Hawk:</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Gentle Kiss of Steel:</b><br /> Cost: 1w; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> The wielder may activate this power upon rolling a decisive attack that would lethally incapacitate her opponent. In an instant, the blade is seen to dematerialize as it passes through her opponent\u2019s body, leaving their flesh unharmed, but slashing away something else.<br /> The attack deals no damage, but the recipient immediately loses all initiative and is crashed (unless they were already at less than zero) and enters a decision point where they must call upon a defining intimacy and spend 3w or surrender. Even if they manage to resist, they take a -4 wound penalty to all offensive actions. This is an emotion effect that lasts until the end of the scene.<br /> Additionally, if any conditions were agreed upon before the fight took place, they gain a defining intimacy towards keeping their word.<br /> <b>Special:</b> only characters who have an intimacy related to honour or keeping their word of at least major intensity can learn this Evocation.<br /> <br /> <b>Humbling Victory Meditation:</b><br /> Cost: 5m 1w; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Gentle Kiss of Steel<br /> All duellists know that instant just after the final blow is struck, a moment of infinite stillness, an ephemeral nirvana. The wisest learn the most of such moments, grasping the threads of their opponent\u2019s life as they extinguish it.<br /> This effect can be activated upon incapacitating a significant opponent with a decisive attack, allowing the wielder to reflexively Join Battle. If used alongside the prerequisite, ignore the willpower cost.<br /> <br /> <b>Momentous Reflection:</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> The duellist alights at the beginning of the encounter, assuming a perfect balance of stillness and motion.<br /> This supplements a Join Battle roll based on awareness, rerolling all 1s. The wielder may take a reflexive aim action against anyone who rolls lower than she does.<br /> <br /> <b>Flowing Quicksilver Concentration:</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Momentous Reflection<br /> The duellist achieves perfect focus, concentrating on her opponent even as she keeps their pace.<br /> This supplements a rush action. If successful, the wielder may take a reflexive aim action against the rushed target.<br /> Additionally, upon unlocking this Evocation, the wielder may take aim actions on turns on which she has moved, and reflexive movement granted by rush or disengage actions, as well as movement granted by charms no longer disrupt her aim. Knockback and knockdown effects can still make her lose her aim, as can taking any actions whose target isn\u2019t her aimed opponent.<br /> <br /> <b>Approaching Disillusion:</b><br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Until Released<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> The duellist slows her breath and visualizes the thread of her opponent\u2019s life as she prepares to strike.<br /> This supplements an aim action. The next attack the wielder makes will benefit from double 10s on the damage roll, or double 9s if it\u2019s withering. If this effect is cast several times on consecutive turns, each turn spent aiming allows to double an additional number, to a maximum of double 7s.<br /> <br /> <b>Perfected Strike Methodology:</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Approaching Disillusion<br /> The duellist relies on precise slashes, cutting her opponents down where they are weakest.<br /> This supplements an attack that benefits from an aim action, adding the aim bonus dice to the post-soak damage of a withering attack or to the raw damage of a decisive attack. Each turn of aiming beyond the first increases this bonus by +1.<br /> <br /> <b>Infinite Eclipse Slash:</b><br /> Cost: 10m 1w; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Flowing Quicksilver Concentration, Perfected Strike Methodology<br /> By virtue of endless repetition and devoted exercise, the duellist has mastered a technique that rivals the arts of the divine. Her blade traces an elegant arc and leaves behind an afterimage, which draws blood a second time as it catches up, striking twice with a single motion.<br /> This supplements an attack that benefits from an aim action, turning all aim dice into successes. The wielder then immediately makes a second attack that also benefits from any aim actions. All valid charms that supplemented the first attack except the Excellency are duplicated at no additional cost. If used as part of a clash, both attacks are considered successful as long as one of them beats the opponent\u2019s roll.<br /> The wielder may make any combination of withering or decisive attacks as she wishes. Once per scene, reset by spending three turns aiming without getting hit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":10131,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","user":"BadassOverlord","date":". 08-14-2016, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T17:09:39-07:00","id":953493,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Submitted for peer review. One of my players is doing a Dawn-caste archer, and he was interested in a powerbow that offered tactical battlefield control -- and that was less wantonly-destructive than Volcano Cutter's can get. We'd determined that he'd be picking this up from his peers in the Wyld Hunt, and that it would subsequently be something jade; the Wood associations followed almost immediately, which ultimately led to my attempt to give Maleficent's conjuration of thorns to a PC.<br /> <br /> If anyone has any suggestions regarding balance or additional effects (though I think these 4 are probably enough), please let me know!</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Emerald Reach</span></b> (Artifact 5 - Green Jade/Orichalcum Long Powerbow)<br /> Hidden texts of the Immaculate Order explains that this bow is how Sextes Jylis defended himself from the dead and the Wyldlings, while he returned life to the lands in the wake of the war against the Anathema. The true story is somewhat stranger -- once, an artisan wished to sojourn to the Elemental Poles, to bear witness to primal elemental flows. The journey, while tremendously dangerous in the days of old, was not without its reward, for the artisan came back inspired.<br /> This long powerbow was forged from green jadesteel; an Immaculate-friendly iconic image of Sextes Jylis the Dragon is coiled around its length, orichalcum flecking visible in its scales, with a hearthstone setting mounted in the Immaculate Dragon's eye. The bowstring is a single hair from the beard of Sextes Jylis himself.<br /> <br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blood who attunes Emerald Reach awakens Life Ever-Blooming for free. They may spend an additional 3m on attunement to cause any arrows fired to sprout thorns mid-flight, increasing Emerald Reach's overwhelming value by 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Life Ever-Blooming</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 5i OR 10m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Uniform, Perilous<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> A surge of verdant Essence coalesces along the the head of a nocked arrow, and the wielder launches it at a target up to Medium range away. Life Ever-Blooming is a [withering] or [decisive] attack. Regardless of whether or not the attack damages its opponent, the arrow drives inevitably into the ground, unleashing a torrent of geomantic fertility. Life Ever-Blooming cannot be used against targets who are not on the ground, or on at least the ground floor of a building, but may be used against a target location. If used in combat, this Evocation costs 5m, 5i. Outside of combat, its mote cost is 10m, and may be used only [Essence] times per scene.<br /> A [bramblesnarl] of thick, thorny, woody vines erupts from the affected site, forming a nigh-impassable barrier-net that obstructs and attempts to snap up everything within Close range. Any characters within Close range of the thorny 'explosion' may attempt to reflexively Disengage from the growth site, rolling Dexterity + Dodge against a difficulty of the Solar's [Essence+3]. Failure at this roll means that the character has been caught within the [bramblesnarl]. Until they escape, their actions are impaired as though they are being grappled (-2 Defense, unable to take Movement actions, unable to flurry, at -1 die to all attacks, not cumulative with actual grapples). On the entangled character's action, they may begin to attempt to escape the bramblesnarl.<br /> The agile may attempt to weave their way through the thorns without injuring themselves. This is an extended miscellaneous action, difficulty 2 with 5 cumulative successes, that may not be placed in a flurry. After an attempt roll, they must avoid the thorns with another Dexterity+Dodge roll; every success below 5 causes 1 die of lethal environmental damage.<br /> The strong and bold may attempt to force their way through. The bramblesnarl may be attacked as if it were a mass combat unit with Defense 0 and Soak 7 (13 against attacks with the Bashing tag); dealing 9 levels of damage is enough to allow one character to cut their way out, or to cut a path to another character caught inside. Cutting apart the bramblesnarl entirely requires superior area-effect firepower, such as Death of Obsidian Butterflies or the burning fury of Volcano Cutter.<br /> A [bramblesnarl], once placed, offers Heavy cover, even for those unfortunate enough to be caught inside. Its Essence-charged state lasts for one scene, after which the Essence fueling the growth fades away. After this time, the bramblesnarl is an ordinary if tough and fire-resistant plant, subject to the ravages of nature.<br /> <br /> <b>Life Ever-Intoxicating</b><br /> Cost: -- (+3m) Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: --<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Life Ever-Blooming<br /> The wielder of Emerald Reach may spend an additional 3m when using Life Ever-Blooming to cause small, purple-and-pink flowers to blossom along the lengths of a [bramblesnarl]. These flowers radiate a syrupy-sweet, narcotic scent, dulling the reflexes and will of anyone nearby. This is an ongoing Poison effect that radiates out to Close distance from the bramblesnarl, with a Stamina+Resistance difficulty of 3 and damage of 2i (1B in Crash). Damage from this poison does not roll over into lethal damage, but anyone who spends more than ten combat rounds unconscious within the radius of the bramblesnarl cannot be awakened for the next week. The duration of this effect can be treated like any other poison with an Intelligence+Medicine roll, difficulty 1, where each threshold success speeds awakening by one day.<br /> The narcotic poison is active for one hour after the bramblesnarl is created, though the sickly-sweet smell remains in the air for up to a day afterward.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Life Ever-Grasping</b><br /> Cost: 4m+1m and 2i per active bramblesnarl Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Life Ever-Intoxicating<br /> With their free hand, the wielder of Emerald Reach forms the Mudra of Sextes Jylis, and all active [bramblesnarls] surge with preternatural life, lashing out with their thorny vines to draw prey into its reaches. Each bramblesnarl may make a [decisive] attack with a dice pool of (Wielder's Archery + Dexterity + Essence); this attack is always an automatically-successful grappling gambit if it connects, rolling (Wielder's Archery+Strength) for the control roll. If the bramblesnarl succeeds at this roll, its thorns inflict an environmental hazard of 3L, Difficulty 3 Stamina+Resistance to avoid damage, and the target is pulled bodily off their feet into the depths of the bramblesnarl before being released by the thorny grapple.<br /> If two bramblesnarls are at Short range from one another, they may alternately surge towards one another, intertwining their vines to effectively extend their reach. This merges the two bramblesnarls into a single, much-larger entity. Any character caught between the two merging bramblesnarls may attempt to Disengage as described in Life Ever-Blooming; failure means they are caught within the larger bramblesnarl as described in Life Ever-Blooming.<br /> <br /> <b>Life Ever-Hungry</b><br /> Cost: -- (+1wp) Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> The thorns of the Emerald Reach rip and tear even the fleshless. This Evocation enhances Life Ever-Blooming, allowing the character to pay a surcharge of +1wp when creating a bramblesnarl; the bramblesnarl's vines can now affect, entrap, injure, and poison dematerialized beings. If an Ever-Hungry bramblesnarl merges with another with Life Ever-Grasping, the resultant larger bramblesnarl is also Ever-Hungry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/736-yai","name":"Yai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:07:04-07:00","id":953529,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Phoenix Heart Blade (Red Jade Reaper Daiklave \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> Phoenix Heart Blade allows her wielder to focus a battle, drawing a single opponent apart from his peers and wearing him down without concern. As the two draw closer, she becomes more effective at piercing her opponents' defenses, and eventually learns to reignite her blade, rejuvenating alongside it as she strikes down her chosen foe and returns to the broader battlefield.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Phoenix Heart Blade is an exquisitely well-designed and balanced red jade reaper daiklave. On close inspection of the blade's surface, one can see the faintest trace of the garda bird feathers that went into the forging. Two hearthstone sockets.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations:</b><br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blooded who attunes to Phoenix Heart Blade gains the following power:<br /> When the wielder first draws Phoenix Heart Blade in battle, her surface flows smoothly out of the sheath, crimson and orange feathers of raw fire following the curve of the blade. Phoenix Heart Blade has seven feathers, which are included in the costs of certain Evocations as &quot;f&quot;. When the plumage of Phoenix Heart Blade is all burned away, her Essence lies in a torpor, not quite dead, but not truly alive either. Her plumage is restored to full when the Solar rolls Join Battle anew from entering a fight, or from certain Evocations.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the act of attuning to Phoenix Heart Blade automatically awakens Ring of Fire Descending for no cost.<br /> <br /> <b>Ring of Fire Descending (4m, 1i, 2f; or 1f)</b><br /> <b><b>Type:</b></b> Reflexive; <b>Duration:</b> One turn; <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only<br /> <b>Prereqs:</b> Essence 1; -<br /> This Evocation is activated reflexively upon successfully dealing Initiative damage with a <b>withering</b> attack. The Solar takes advantage of how close she is to her foe and flicks her wrist in the wake of the strike, letting two feathers from her blade fall to the earth, surrounding her and her foe and bursting into a ring of fire which isolates them from the rest of the battle. When this Evocation is activated, she and her foe are trapped together within the circle; other characters are only caught within it alongside them in exceptional circumstances, at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.<br /> <br /> Until the end of her next turn, all attacks into or out of the circle suffer a -2 penalty. So long as he is within close range of the circle, any character may enter or exit the circle as a reflexive action on his turn, but moving through the circle forces him to succeed at a difficulty 5 (Dexterity + Athletics) roll or suffer 2 Lethal damage in the process. <b>Although it takes place on his turn, moving in or out of the circle does not, by itself, consume the character\u2019s move action.</b> The Solar has no special immunity to any of these clauses - the flames trap her as much as they trap her foes.<br /> <br /> This Evocation may only be activated a second time while the Solar remains within the circle against a target also within the circle - in this case, the circle\u2019s duration is refreshed, keeping all currently trapped within it so held, and it only requires a single feather to refresh it. Otherwise, she must either leave its radius or wait for its flames to die down in order to activate it again.<br /> <br /> <b>Grazing Flame (4m, 1f)</b><br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental; <b>Duration:</b> Instant; <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only<br /> <b>Prereqs:</b> Essence 2; Ring of Fire Descending<br /> This Evocation can only be activated against a target that has entered Initiative crash. If the <b>withering</b> attack it is applied to deals at least three Initiative damage, the target\u2019s hair, clothes, or other peripheral features are set ablaze as the Solar casts aside a single feather from Phoenix Heart Blade.<br /> <br /> Each round he remains alight, the victim suffers one Initiative damage (dealt after his action for that round). Further, for every five points of Initiative he falls below zero, he suffers a -1 to Defense (round down, so -9i means a -1 to Defense). Being on fire in this manner can be put out by the character stopping, dropping, and rolling, which is a miscellaneous action that cannot be placed in a flurry. An ally may also put out the flames by taking a miscellaneous action that cannot be placed in a flurry to douse or pat down the character on fire. Recovering from Initiative crash ends this effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Burning Blade (1+m, 1+f)</b><br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental; <b>Duration:</b> Instant; <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Prereqs:</b> Essence 2; Ring of Fire Descending<br /> The feathers of the blade are consumed to cast it in an ever greater fire, making her attacks hideously bright and dangerous. When this Evocation supplements a <b>withering</b> attack, it increases its raw damage by two per feather and mote expended. If it instead supplements a <b>decisive</b> attack, she turns one dice of raw damage into an automatic success for each feather and mote expended. She may only spend (Essence) feathers and motes on a single attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Special activation rules:</b> If this Evocation is used in conjunction with a multiattack Charm such as Iron Whirlwind Attack which ordinarily allows a given Charm to be applied to every attack at no extra cost, the user must still pay the mote and feather cost for each strike she wishes the bonus of Burning Blade to apply to. A character might spend 2m 2f on the first attack, 3m 3f on the third, and 1m 1f on the fourth, or any other order and number she pleases, but she must spend them individually, and each enhances an individual attack; she cannot spend them in a single allotment to enhance all the attacks generated by such a Charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Funeral Pyre (1m)</b><br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental; <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only; <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prereqs:</b> Essence 3; Burning Blade<br /> This Evocation may only be activated when Phoenix Heart Blade is in its torpor, or when the other Evocations activated alongside Funeral Pyre would spend enough feathers to send the blade into its torpor. If the <b>decisive</b> attack this Evocation supplements successfully kills its target, their body is immolated and the blade renewed to its full plumage. Additionally, if the opponent is a non-trivial foe, the Solar recovers four motes, as the life and power that pulses through her renewed blade reaches her as well.<br /> <br /> If the Solar is currently within the effect of Ring of Fire Descending when she kills an opponent with this Evocation, she gains eight motes instead. In the process, the circle of flame is drawn into the renewed Phoenix Heart Blade, removing it from the field of battle.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Light-Eater (Orichalcum Chain Shirt \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> Light-Eater is a hungry thing, chewing away at all light in its reach, helping to cloak the Solar from sight. Though bits and pieces of its stolen power may be thrown away, the stolen light will inevitably fester and grow large within the armor, until it finally bursts forth, brilliant and uncontrolled, when Light-Eater can hold no more.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Light-Eater is a beautiful, close-fitting weave of chains of orichalcum. When attuned and worn, it passively eats away at light that hits it, giving it an inky black color and serving to blend in with the natural shadows cast by any clothing worn above it. Three hearthstone sockets.<br /> <br /> <b>EVOCATIONS:</b><br /> On attunement, Light-Eater gives the Solar one non-Charm success to Larceny rolls made to conceal the armor and disguise its presence or nature.<br /> <br /> By committing an additional three motes on attunement, the wearer adds two dice to all stealth rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Mechanic:</b> As it operates and absorbs light, Light-Eater may accrue \u201clight charges,\u201d stored luminescent energy held within the orichalcum of the armor. These can be spent for special effects, and are noted with \u201clc\u201d in the costs section of its various Evocations. Charges fade at the rate of approximately one every five minutes, and disperse entirely in a single, extremely obvious, flash of light if the Solar removes Light-Eater. Light-Eater may only hold ten light charges at maximum, and when it gathers that many, it glows with light, removing the effects of its attunement bonus, creating a -3 penalty to Stealth actions, and preventing certain Evocations from functioning.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Design Note:</b> building up a ton of light charges is actually bad. You want to keep the number of light charges down as much as possible, but running Darkness at Noon (which is a really good Evocation for stealth, and expensive to turn off/on) will rapidly tick up your number of light charges in a way that\u2019s hard to slow and virtually impossible to really stop.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Darkness at Noon (8m, 1wp)</b><br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple; <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite; <b>Keywords:</b> Mute<br /> <b>Prereqs:</b> Essence 2; -<br /> While this Evocation is active, Light-Eater passively consumes and eats at the light surrounding the Solar. It creates a supernatural darkness out to close range, obscuring the Solar as light is eaten in the space surrounding them. Awareness rolls based primarily on sight suffer a -3 penalty while Darkness at Noon remains active; the Solar ignores this penalty.<br /> <br /> Additionally, at the end of each round that Darkness at Noon is active, it gathers two light charges. When Light-Eater reaches its maximum number of light charges, this Evocation immediately ends and cannot be reactivated until Light-Eater has fewer than its maximum number of light charges. This Evocation may only be ended voluntarily if the Solar spends an additional three motes.<br /> <br /> <b>Splendid Radiance Protection (5m, 1lc)</b><br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive; <b>Duration:</b> One round; <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Prereqs:</b> Essence 2; Darkness at Noon<br /> Activating this Evocation causes Light-Eater to glow with its consumed light as it strengthens itself against oncoming attacks. It increases the Solar\u2019s soak by four until the end of the round, but gives her a -3 penalty to all Stealth rolls for that period. Against unExalted creatures of darkness, this increases her soak by six instead, and grants her an additional three hardness.<br /> <br /> <b>Hiding in Sunlight (5m, 1lc)</b><br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple; <b>Duration:</b> Instant; <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only<br /> <b>Prereqs:</b> Essence 2; Splendid Radiance Protection<br /> When the Solar activates this Evocation, she surprises her opponents with a brilliant burst of light, briefly obscuring her in its incandescence and distracting them as she slips off. This a difficulty 3 gambit that rolls (Wits + Larceny) against the (Wits + Resistance) of all opponents within two range bands of the Solar, and adds the Solar\u2019s Essence to the initiative roll for the gambit. Record each opponent successfully affected by the gambit.<br /> <br /> Immediately after the sudden flare of light, she makes a (Dexterity + Stealth) roll to enter concealment. Any opponent successfully affected by Hiding in Sunlight\u2019s gambit suffers a -(Essence or 3, whichever is higher) penalty to contest this roll, even if he uses a sense other than sight or an Ability other than Awareness. For unExalted creatures of darkness, this penalty also applies to any other rolls made to detect concealed targets until the end of the next round.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12048,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12048-lvthn","user":"LVTHN","date":".  Whoops, missed an unintended and probably OP interaction with IWA. 08-18-2016, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12048-lvthn","name":"LVTHN","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:21:31-07:00","id":953545,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Submitting this for peer review. I wanted a decent set of armor for a Social-Fu character, because combat is always inevitable. Might as well make them love you for it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fleeting Shadows</span><br /> (Silken Armor, Artifact 5)<br /> Woven from the a captured twilight mist and stitched with silk of bound Anuhles, Fleeting Shadows was made for protection in the not uncommon event that a formal party was crashed by assassins and their ilk, or when a summoning and binding fails. Passed from its original weaver to his son, to his lover to a passing group of cultists, Fleeting Shadows remains an unknowable useful and fashionable protective garb.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Light as a shadow and just as modest, a Solar, Abyssal or Sidereal Exalted may pay three extra motes when attuning this armor to tighten it, thinning the waist, accentuating features, and increasing the wearer's Evasion and Appearance by 1. This may increase the wearer's effective Appearance above five.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Fluttering Fog Dodge</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Uniform, Perilous<br /> Duration: Until Next Turn</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">When the evening fog rolls off of the hills, it is beyond the capabilities of man to proceed with clear sight. Attempts to stop or capture the fog falter as the swirling mist encompasses and penetrates the night sky. Until the wearer's next turn, negate up to (Guile) points of penalties to the wearer's evasion.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Kiss from the Murk</b><br /> Cost: 3m, 2i; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Withering Only, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Fluttering Fog Dodge</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Tales of love found in bittered enemies embroiled on the battlefield are favored by bards and storytellers throughout Creation. After a successful withering attack, instead of rolling damage, perform an instill action upon the target of the attack with bonus dice on the social roll equal to the net hits on the withering attack. Should the instill action be successful, drain 3 points of initiative from the target, who is left reeling, unsure what exactly is happening on the fields of war any more</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Seductive Haze Shintai</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple <br /> Keywords: Uniform, Mute<br /> Duration: Scene <br /> Prerequisites: Kiss from the Murk</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Actions to strike at sources of true beauty are as futile as attempting to capture shapes etched in mist. If the Wearer's Appearance is higher than the Resolve of an attacking opponent, apply the difference as a penalty to the opponent's attack pools, and as a cost of initiative to attack the wearer.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Special Activation Rules: Wearers with the Hideous Merit gain no benefit from this Evocation. This Evocation awakens at no experience cost once the wearer successfully seduces a target who began the night with a preexisting negative intimacy towards the wearer or has attempted to kill the wearer in the recent past.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Shapes in Mist Prana</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Cost: 12m; Mins: Essence 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Type: Simple </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Keywords: Mute</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Duration: (Manipulation) rounds</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prerequisites: Seductive Haze Shintai</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana, arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Many are the </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">tangible</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> things in Creation, but the wearer learns to take after True Love and Beauty; never to be caught or bound, intangible and untouchable like Shapes in Mist. When this evocation is activated, an </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">impenetrable</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> cloud of fog fills the area, extending out to medium range from the wearer. All who look into or out of the mists find themselves thwarted. All vision based awareness rolls fail, even those augmented by all seeing magic such as Eyes of the Unconquered Sun. All attacks except those </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">targeted</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> at the wearer are considered surprise attacks, and all attacks and awareness rolls except those made by the wearer suffer a -3 dice penalty from being forced to rely on senses other than sight (Page 188, EX3). All who attempt to leave the mists must succeed on a (Perception+Awareness) roll against a difficulty of the wearers Manipulation or be turned around and instead move deeper into the mists. The wearer is immune to the </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">penalties inflicted by the mist and can sense the presence of everything inside the mist, causing all forms of stealth or disguise to fail. </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> The wearer may reflexively move to any point in the mist for her movement action, and after successfully dodging an attack.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:28:56-07:00","id":953550,"title":"","content":"I am liking Light Eater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:33:26-07:00","id":953556,"title":"","content":"Increasing Evasion and Appearance by 1 for Attunement is a bit much!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:04:14-07:00","id":953567,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I felt that might be pushing it a bit much, but I figured since it's a 5 dot artifact it might be better have it push the envelope a bit, though I can definitely see it only increase one or the other. I fear that the capstone charm might be a connected to the rest slightly too loosely","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1089921-new-sidereal-homebrew-for-3e-down-came-the-spider\" target=\"_blank\">Down Came the Spider</a>, my 3e Sidereal Conversion! Please comment<br /> Homebrewer of many things","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11713-zx_xz","name":"ZX_XZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T15:52:24-07:00","id":955943,"title":"","content":"Howdy all. I've been toying around with an artifact concept in my head for a while - I know what I want to do with it, but not how best to implement it or how much it should cost. The idea involves a suit of artifact heavy armor that leverages its mobility penalty in the Exalt's favor. For example, I'd like the artifact grant its mobility penalty in bonus dice to:<br /> <br /> - Control rolls following a successful grapple gambit, as the armor's stiffness makes it hard for the opponent to break free, and<br /> - Feats of strength, particularly those involving extended rolls, as the armor can stiffen its joints to bear weight without the Exalt having to exert herself.<br /> <br /> In terms of fluff, the articulated plate has moonsilver fibers and joints that flex in response to the Exalt's Essence, though the weight and bulk of the armor still slows her down. Further Evocations could involve:<br /> <br /> - Powering through difficult terrain (i.e. the Exalt still takes the mobility penalty, but not the usual -3 penalty in any terrain that could be reasonably overcome through brute force such as dense undergrowth or mud),<br /> - Increasing soak and/or hardness,<br /> - Imposing a mobility penalty via a unique crippling effect, and<br /> - Magically increasing the mobility penalty to make the other Evocations stronger at the cost of, well, mobility.<br /> <br /> I'd like those to interact with and scale with the armor's present mobility penalty so the Exalt has some incentive to not magic that penalty away. If possible, it'd be nice if the first two dice, coming from the armor's innate penalty, counted as non-Charm dice. There could also be other niche things here and there like the mobility penalty not applying to certain combat actions like rushes.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? Is this doable? What should the artifact rating be? The mote cost of each Evocation? I don't really have any experience with the system, much less with artifact creation, so constructive feedback would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12245-yatogami-odin","name":"Yatogami Odin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:43:03-07:00","id":960645,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Rightly-Guided Eagle (Orichalcum Chain Shirt \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> Rightly-Guided Eagle lifts and eases the Solar's movement, invisible wings of Essence serving to ease her passage. In battle, she is a terror in the sky, held aloft longer than any mortal could be; outside of it, she makes smooth, easy movements across great distances.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Rightly-Guided Eagle is a work of art, each individual orichalcum ring drawing to mind a feather curled in upon itself, the overall design creating a symmetrical, winged appearance upon the artifact's backside. Two hearthstone sockets, both located on the backside.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations:</b><br /> A Solar who attunes to Rightly-Guided Eagle gains one non-Charm dice on rolls involving leaping, climbing, or other heavily vertical movement. This includes Rush and Disengage actions across appropriate terrain.<br /> <br /> <b>Soar and Dive Technique (4m)</b><br /> <b><b>Type:</b></b> Supplemental; <b>Duration:</b> Instant; <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Prereqs:</b> Essence 1; -<br /> Using this Evocation expends the Solar's move action for the turn, allowing her to leap a single range band in a chosen direction; if this would ordinarily require a Disengage action, she must still roll, and if she fails she is forced to change trajectory and merely rise vertically. More importantly, however, she hovers in the air for a time after leaping. Ordinary melee weapons cannot strike her while she hangs in the air, though those with the reaching tag may, and a weapon or Charm capable of lashing out to short range may still strike her. She may strike at her foes where they rest beneath her, by the same rules.<br /> <br /> At the beginning of her next turn, she falls back to the ground. If she chooses to, she may descend upon a target within close range of her overhead position; this enhances a melee attack, causing it to deal an additional (Athletics) raw damage on a <b>withering</b> attack, or (Athletics/2, round down) raw damage on a <b>decisive</b> attack.<br /> <br /> The Solar may not reactivate this Evocation during the same round on which she hits the ground.<br /> <br /> <b>Hollow Bones Escape (2m)</b><br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive; <b>Duration:</b> Instant; <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Prereqs:</b> Essence 2; Soar and Dive Technique<br /> This Charm may be activated reflexively upon being successfully struck with a <b>withering</b> or <b>decisive</b> attack. It allows the Solar to lighten her body as she is struck, making a Disengage roll reflexively to move along the line of the attack, to which the attunement bonus applies. This provides no safety from hazards or dead ends, however; if she is flung a range band back by the force of the enemy's strike, and thus into an environmental hazard such as a blazing inferno or off a cliff, she has no special protection.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12048,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12048-lvthn","user":"LVTHN","date":". 08-30-2016, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12048-lvthn","name":"LVTHN","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T17:51:33-07:00","id":960765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LVTHN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=960645#post960645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Soar and Dive Technique (4m)</b><br /> <b><b>Type:</b></b> Supplemental; <b>Duration:</b> Instant; <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Prereqs:</b> Essence 1; -<br /> Using this Evocation expends the Solar's move action for the turn, allowing her to leap a single range band in a chosen direction; if this would ordinarily require a Disengage action, she must still roll, and if she fails she is forced to change trajectory and merely rise vertically. More importantly, however, she hovers in the air for a time after leaping. Ordinary melee weapons cannot strike her while she hangs in the air, though those with the reaching tag may, and a weapon or Charm capable of lashing out to short range may still strike her. She may strike at her foes where they rest beneath her, by the same rules.<br /> <br /> At the beginning of her next turn, she falls back to the ground. If she chooses to, she may descend upon a target within close range of her overhead position; this enhances a melee attack, causing it to deal an additional (Athletics) raw damage on a <b>withering</b> attack, or (Athletics/2, round down) raw damage on a <b>decisive</b> attack.<br /> <br /> The Solar may not reactivate this Evocation during the same round on which she hits the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like what this does, but it seems like too many effects in one package. the first effect is very similar to Monkey Leap Technique (arguably stronger); the damage effect is comparable to Falling Scythe Flash. In any case I'd make them separate Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:35:55-07:00","id":960781,"title":"","content":"So I need help coming up with a starting Evocation for a sorcerous relic called the Brand of Elemental Fire. Mechanically I was looking at Mara's Demonic Tattoos for inspiration combined with Pact with the Ifrit Lord.<br /> <br /> The problem I've run into is that I've had a hard time figuring out how to meet certain mechanical needs and to come up with interesting, consistent fluff.<br /> <br /> To give a broad sense of objectives:<ul><li>I want an Evocation which can aid in Sorcery somehow, sticking with a theme of fiery insight or passion. This is sorta hard, since I'm not sure what to do that isn't dice tricks (Dice tricks with a condition?) or something which would be better modeled as a Shaping Ritual. This is pretty low priority, all things equal.</li> <li>An evocation that enhances fire-based attacks. It could be versatile, as in one could use it with a Firewand, Burning Name or even Flight of the Brilliant Raptor. What I've currently got is this kind of thing, and it adds an effect to Decisive Attacks with fire weapons that immolates the target, making them suffer (Essence) Damage Dice per turn until they put out the fire. I could see having 1-2 effects to enhance fire attacks. Maybe one for Withering and one for Decisive? That might not be that interesting.</li> <li>Something interesting and weird might be something about &quot;unlocking one's inner fire.&quot; Some kind of minion-promoting thing with benefits for the subject, maybe moreso if the subject is a fire elemental.</li> </ul>I've been thinking about the idea of using Intimacies as fuel for these Evocations, but my implementation has left something to be desired. Any thoughts would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T19:03:57-07:00","id":960796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=960765#post960765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like what this does, but it seems like too many effects in one package. the first effect is very similar to Monkey Leap Technique (arguably stronger); the damage effect is comparable to Falling Scythe Flash. In any case I'd make them separate Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, good point. I was thinking on how to make Soar and Dive not just a repurchase of Monkey Leap Technique when defining it, and the &quot;can't be hit without reaching/range&quot; was something I was thinking of in terms of flavor more than game effect. As game effect it's obviously pretty good if you've got a whip or a ranged weapon. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12048-lvthn","name":"LVTHN","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:32:59-07:00","id":961971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=946954#post946954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread continues to be a joy to read. Keep it up everyone!<br /> <br /> I'd like to issue a challenge. Some of you have done this, others haven't. But I challenge you all to make Artifacts that have innate, by-the-rules drawbacks, <b>without </b>removing them in the magic of the Artifact.<br /> <br /> Examples include:<br /> -Make Throwing weapons that <i>don't</i> return to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something that I just came here to ask about, actually. It seems like every artifact thrown weapon has a returning or infinite ammunition effect built in as the first priority, often not involving an evocation. I want to make one for a stealthy/throwy night caste in my game, but I want to do something different with it.<br /> <br /> The two concepts I've come up with (but not built any evocations for, because I don't know how I would exactly) are:<br /> <br /> - A javelin/dart type of thrown weapon that creates some sort of essence ribbon, allowing her to pull herself to the weapon. Kind of like the returning weapon in reverse, I guess. Some options for this could be using it like a Terraria grappling hook on the environment, attacking enemies along her path as she zooms by, continuing past her target just as fast to stay at range in a different location, making some kind of grapple-ish gambit from afar by hooking limbs and pulling them off balance, using the ribbon to trip people up or entangle them in conjunction with stuff like Angle-Tracing Edge, or just getting straight into Melee (she dabbles in melee). This one is sort of cheating, because she'd never really lose the weapon, but it still wouldn't be as simple as automatically getting it back every round to make another Thrown attack - she'd have to plan ahead and go out of her way to get into position to use it again.<br /> <br /> - A dart that sticks with an enemy and makes it easier for her to run them down, hide from them, keep track of them, hit them with further attacks, or.. something. Not sure exactly. I haven't put any more thought into this than a &quot;debuff tag.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9749-andrew-d","name":"Andrew D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T09:50:58-07:00","id":963748,"title":"","content":"The following Artifact was created for a campaign of mine. You can read more details <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/962658-help-me-create-a-heart-breaking-artifact-designed-by-a-raksha\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> <b>The Crystal Heart (Artifact ****)</b><br /> <br /> Attunement Cost: 5m<br /> <br /> <br /> The Crystal Heart is an accursed artifact, born of a lover\u2019s sacrifice and twisted by the whims of the fairy queen who forged it.<br /> The Crystal Heart, true to its name, appears to be a stylized heart, forged from a single smooth piece of transparent crystal. While unattuned, the crystal is cold and clammy. Once attuned, a rose-colored liquid manifests in a reservoir within the heart and a comforting warmth emanates from it. The heart settles upon the wearer\u2019s chest, where it silently beats in rhythm with the wearer\u2019s own heart. When one of the Heart\u2019s Evocations is activated, the Crystal Heart glows brightly enough to read by.<br /> <br /> In order to attune the Crystal Heart, the wearer focuses on one of her Major or Defining Ties. Typically this is a positive Tie of affection, friendship, or love, but other emotions may be fine. The Crystal Heart internalizes the Tie, drawing power from the wearer's connection. So long as the Crystal Heart is attuned, no magic can prevent the wearer from applying the Intimacy's rating to her Resolve (where normally applicable).<br /> <br /> The Intimacy cannot be weakened <i>or strengthened </i>by mundane means. If the wearer breaks the attunement, she feels a sickening ache as the Intimacy is weakened by one level. If the Intimacy is ever weakened to Minor, the Crystal Heart stops functioning, but remains attuned.<br /> <br /> If the wearer's Intimacy is ever erased, the attunement immediately ends as the Crystal Heart stops beating, growing cold once more. The wearer gains a Defining Principle that opposes any attempts to rekindle the original or anything like it: for example, a Tie of &quot;My Wife (Love)&quot; is replaced by \u201cI will never love again\u201d. Like the original Tie, this new Principle cannot be degraded by mundane means.<br /> <br /> Storytellers should note that the Crystal Heart is not intended to be a cheap path to power. Any character who would attune the Heart to a Tie \u201cthey can afford to lose\u201d probably does not possess the Intimacy at a rating that would allow the attunement. There are stories to tell about tragic heroes who would voluntarily sacrifice something they hate about themselves, but be wary about allowing Ties that the character would be happy to be rid of.<br /> <br /> Upon attuning the Crystal Heart, the wearer gains access to the following Evocations for free.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart's Fervor</b><br /> <b><b>Cost: </b></b>1wp<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive, Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> The Crystal Heart offers power at a terrible cost. If the wearer taps into the Crystal Heart, she may draw power from her Tie at risk of destroying the Tie itself. The wearer may draw upon their Tie to enhance one rolled action or application of a static value. Rolled actions gain the Intimacy\u2019s rating as non-Charm dice. Static values gain a non-Charm bonus equal to half the Intimacy\u2019s rating (rounded up). After resolving the triggering action, apply the triggering action\u2019s successes against the wearer\u2019s Resolve, with a penalty equal to the Intimacy\u2019s rating. If the triggering action meets or beats the wearer\u2019s Resolve, weaken the Intimacy by one level. Note that if the wearer had activated the Crystal Heart to boost her Resolve, she does not gain that benefit against this, but her Resolve may otherwise be enhanced as normal.<br /> <br /> As a final measure, the wearer may tap even deeper into the Crystal Heart. For three Willpower, the duration extends to one scene; if the wearer has activated the normal version of Heart\u2019s Fervor, decrease this activation cost by one point. At the end of the scene, the Intimacy is erased. The wearer may prematurely terminate this power: in doing so, she gains the Intimacy\u2019s rating as automatic <b>successes </b>on her next rolled action or static value application, but she suffers the consequences immediately thereafter.<br /> <br /> <b>Numb the Fire</b><br /> <b><b>Cost: </b></b>1wp<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> Is life more important than love? This is the question the wearer must ask himself when he feels his heart\u2019s-blood slipping away. The Crystal Heart offers a trade. The wearer may tap the Intimacy held within the Crystal Heart to prevent harm. Preventing <b>1-2 Health Levels</b> weakens the Intimacy by one level. Preventing <b>2-4 Health Levels</b> weakens the Intimacy by two levels. Preventing <b>5+ Health Levels</b> destroys the Intimacy altogether. The Crystal Heart cannot be used in this way if the rating is not high enough to support the harm it would prevent.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T04:33:37-07:00","id":971878,"title":"","content":"<b>A Pair of Reaper Daiklaves(Each Artifact 3)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Principle of Heavenly Motion</b><br /> <br /> Forged in the North, with a hilt of Orichalcum and a blade of Red and Blue Jade around a core of meteoric iron, the Principle of Heavenly Motion is a blade of extreme elegance. It was first wielded by Star Shining Across the Heavens, a Solar who adored the sky and stars, and was inspired by a comet, a Fae weapon launched across the sky at the Silver Throne.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations</b><br /> A Solar or Dragon-Blooded the Principle of Heavenly Motion imbues its wielder with the speed of a falling star, granting them 2 dice to all tests of speed. While using these dice, the character trails brilliant blue light.<br /> <br /> <b>Gathering the Stars</b><br /> Cost: 3m+ Mins: Ess 1 <br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Stackable<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The Exalt creates a sphere of blazing blue fire around her blade, and may create up to (Essence) or 3, whichever is greater such spheres. The sphere lasts until the end of the scene. When she defends herself from an attack later in the scene, she may expend 1 of spheres to inflict a -1 penalty on the attack roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Make Stars Fall</b><br /> Cost: 5m Mins: Ess 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Starshine<br /> <br /> By expending all spheres garnered through the use of the prerequisite, the Exalt may unleash an arc of flame at any target up to Medium Range that is not in contact with the ground. If it strikes, the Exalt may execute a gambit to ground the struck target, with a difficulty of 4. If the Gambit succeeds, the target is dragged to the ground in a corona of blue fire, and knocked prone. They take falling damage as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>A Hundred Burning Stars</b><br /> Cost: 5m/10m Mins: Ess 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Make Stars Fall<br /> <br /> This charm supplements a Decisive attack, allowing for a special gambit. This gambit has a difficulty of 5. If the gambit is successful, the target is hurled skywards, and left hanging at medium range from the ground, surrounded by a corona of blue flame. By paying 10m, the gambit may be executed against a battlegroup of Size 3 or less. Larger Groups require multiple activations of this charm, at a cost of 5m per dot of Size. Anyone or any group struck by this gambit may later be struck by Make Stars Fall, which releases the commitment. Otherwise, they gently float back to the ground at the end of the scene, unharmed.<br /> <br /> <b>Hammering Meteor Strikes</b><br /> Cost: +1m+ Mins: Ess 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: A Hundred Burning Stars<br /> <br /> This is a special, un-blockable, un-dodgeable version of Make Stars Fall, against all targets suspended by A Hundred Burning Stars, paying 1m per target or Size of Battlegroup in addition to the base cost of Make Stars Fall. They are hurled at any point within long range and take damage as if they had been thrown from Long Range above the ground. Upon striking the ground, blasts of blue fire smash craters into the ground, knocking prone anyone within close range of an impact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wheel of Eternity</b><br /> <br /> This sword is forged of Starmetal, Moonsilver and Orichalcum, with a guard in the shape of a wheel and repeating moonsilver wheel motifs along the orichalcum blade that slowly turn. The blade is an example of Sidereal craftsmanship from the First Age, based on certain understanding of time. It was taken by a Solar into battle against the Raksha, and considered a kingly blade even then, even if it wasn't the most powerful. The Sidereals reclaimed the sword during the Usurpation, but it was lost during the Contagion.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations</b><br /> A Sidereal, Lunar or Solar who attunes to the blade for an additional 2m may reroll a single non-success on every damage roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Burning Time</b><br /> Cost: 1hl Mins: Ess 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Aggravated<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Time cannot be controlled. It is well known that the required principles were destroyed by the 3 Spheres Cataclysm. And yet, a way has been found. By feeding one's own lifeforce into the gears of the Wheel of Eternity, one can momentarily take control of one's own time, striking with incredible precision in a perfect moment, with vicious speed and force. This allows for the completion of an aim action instantly and reflexively.<br /> <br /> <b>Screaming Gears</b><br /> Cost: 2m Mins; Ess 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: Burning Time<br /> <br /> By turning the wheels with Essence rather than Lifeforce, the Exalt drives his unbreakable sword against time. The gears scream, and the world rebels against the blow. The Exalt may choose to reduce his attack pool, and for every dice by which he lowers his pool, he adds a dice to the eventual damage pool as the gears tear into the very fabric of his foes being and rip it apart.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Song of the Spheres</b><br /> Cost: 5m Mins; Ess 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Prerequisite: Screaming Gears, A Hundred Burning Stars<br /> <br /> Crossing the Wheel of Eternity and the Principle of Heavenly Motion, the Exalt transcends the material world. He may reflexively materialize and dematerialize for the rest of the scene. Additionally, he may strike any target he can see, though he takes a -1 penalty for every range band between his location and his target, hurling burning blue stars. He may fly above the earth, suffering no penalty for movement within Creation.<br /> <br /> When using Meteor Hammer Strikes, he may simply pay a single mote to use it even if he has no target suspended, congealing time and essence into a sphere of heavenly chromatic light. This projectile explodes on impact, unleashing a decisive attack against all targets within short range with an accuracy of 10 dice and a damage pool of 10 dice+3 for every range band between the wielder of the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T11:59:49-07:00","id":972623,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">As much as I dislike 3e, I've decided to attempt to join a game (hopefully it'll go better than the last ones). My character is an extremely vain femme fatale type, a former Dynast who's convinced that she's an Anathema, though her attempts at evil end up being things that PC's do normally, like rob the guild, spread cults to yourself, fight the Realm, ect.<br /> <br /> She's got a set of Silken Armor call Moon Veils the Sun, 5 dots, Orichalum and Moonsilver. I'm having a bit of trouble coming up with Evocations for it, so I thought I'd make a thread here and see if you all have some ideas/feedback/help. My plan is for it's Evocations to synergize well with Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style and with having a high Appearance.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking for the attunement bonus I'll have +1 Appearance and +3 Motes. Does that break anything?</span><br /> </span><br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:16:47-07:00","id":972632,"title":"","content":"I have to say the new system and how to build interesting and new artifacts is both intimidating and exciting. I've got a couple of artifacts that I would like to field at you to solicit opinions and constructive advice. I really had no idea how to price mote costs or even field mechanics. Hopefully people get where I was coming from and can clue me in where I need to be clearer.<br /> <br /> (Note: I have significantly changed the story of the Celestial Lions from that of 2<sup>nd</sup> edition, but I thought it the idea was cool. I stole liberally from the story of Akodo and the Kitsu from L5R for it. My PC is extremely fixated on the law and justice to some extent. Sometimes it\u2019s a tyrannical drive in her. )<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Righteous Judgment</b><br /> (Level 4 Orichalcum &amp; White Jade Grand Goremaul)<br /> <br /> Crafted for the mighty Dawn Caste, Walker in Glory and Victory, Lion of the Unconquered Sun, Righteous Judgment was used to mercilessly mete out punishments of death often at the head of an army as dictated by The Wrathful Onyx Tyrant before he became the Righteous Devil. Its head is crafted out of the purest of White Jade while the rest is built from Orichalcum.<br /> Upon attunement by a Dawn Caste at the cost of a 3 additional motes, Righteous Judgment grants the user a +1 Accuracy and a +2 Damage modifier in additional to the usual Heavy Artifact Weapon modifiers. Unlike other grand goremauls, its blows are so fierce that is causes Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Order in the Court</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> <br /> Sometimes it is necessary to call a punishment to order and this will demand silence before the words are spoken. Righteous Judgment can silence an entire battle group whose size does not exceed the wielder\u2019s Essence. In effect this will give a +3 non-charm dice bonus to any Stealth-based stratagem or Stealth roll. Note that it does not make the wielder or his battle group invisible; merely silent. It also has the side effect of stifling any noise in the immediate vicinity including the death screams of people killed by the wielder or his forward units. This will work on the smaller scale too and give the wielder and people in his immediate vicinity complete silence. The Evocation does render verbal Orders or even speech impossible however while active.<br /> <br /> <b>Righteous Army Prayer</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>10m; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Order in the Court<br /> <br /> Righteous Judgment grants a potent blessing to troops led by its wielder. A battle group led a Dawn Caste wielder will be granted +1 Might as long as the weapon is held by the unit leader. This stacks with any other similar blessings such as that granted by Tiger Warrior Training Technique\u2019s training regimens.<br /> <br /> <b>Attention before the Court Stance</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>8m <b>Mins: </b>Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Order in the Court<br /> <br /> When the judge stands all must do so as well. When holding Righteous Judgment, the wielder can command all enemies that see it or the wielder to stand up at attention or present themselves visually and verbally if able to the wielder for a moment. Resolve this as a Charisma + Presence roll versus the target\u2019s Resolve. It is only momentary so it does not render them defenseless but it will force them to break stealth or invisibility if able. Should Righteous Judgment be dropped or concealed the magic breaks until it is once again held in the open.<br /> <br /> <b>Kneeling for Judgment Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m, 3i, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Withering, Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Righteous Army Payer, Attention before the Court Stance<br /> <br /> All must kneel so that judgment may be pronounced. The wielder strikes the ground and performs a single Withering attack upon all persons, friend or foe, within Essence yards of the wielder. While this does the normal amount of damage to the targets, the wielder only gains an amount up to his essence for each target. Additionally all targets must make a (Dexterity + Athletics) roll at difficulty 4 or be knocked prone/driven to their knees. When used against a battle group the value gained is multiplied by the group\u2019s size signifying the large amount of people affected.<br /> <br /> <b>Purifying Gavel Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 4<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only, Aggravated<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Kneeling for Judgment Strike<br /> <br /> As a punisher of the guilty, all creatures of darkness or those have committed sins against Heaven or the Unconquered Sun shall meet their just punishment at the end of Righteous Judgment. This Evocation calls upon the unfailing purity of the Unconquered Sun to cleanse the target. The Evocation grants Double-10\u2019s on damage rolls and turns this blow into Aggravated damage. Should the target survive he will have a Major intimacy of Fear towards the wielder and Righteous Judgment<br /> <br /> If the target is truly innocent and is hit anyway, then the wielder takes half the damage as aggravated and the target merely takes the rest as bashing anyway.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis of the First Pride</b><br /> (Level 5 Orichalcum Articulated Plate)<br /> <br /> Long ago after the men and women became the first exalted, one among them that would become known as the Walker in Glory and Victory hunted the first lions. No common lions were these, but the mighty spirits who would one day become celestial lions guarding the very gates of Yu-shan and enforcing heavenly laws. They called themselves the First Pride. At first the Walker hunted them because they served the Primordials, but he began to see the nobility in the beasts. With some effort and assistance from his circle the Walker in Glory and victory won them over to the side of the Gods and their servants the Exalted. A deal was struck as both sides were impressed with the nobility of the other. They began to join battles alongside the Solar Exalted and the leader of the First Pride was wounded mortally and so to save his friend the walker called upon his circle\u2019s twilight for aid. The Pride\u2019s leader was bound and saved. This pact forever changed the Anima of the Walker in Glory and Victory.<br /> The pact was embodied in the Aegis and the First Pride\u2019s Leader was linked to it. Runes symbolizing this pact were hammered into the Orichalcum plate and it shined like the hide of the Celestial Lions once completed. To this day when the power of the Aegis is called upon it will defend the wearer to its utmost. When the wearer leads a group that is willing to uphold his ideals, her might grows and her ability to unshakably fulfill her mission.<br /> <br /> When attuning the the Aegis for an additional 2 motes, the wearer takes no mobility penalty as it conforms to the wearer as a 2nd skin.<br /> <br /> <b>Unshakeable Pride Spirit</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m, 1wp <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>none<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>none<br /> <br /> The leader of the pride is strengthened by its belief in him. With this Evocation Aegis\u2019 wearer adds an amount to the Exalt\u2019s Resolve all attacks versus one intimacy. The amount depends on the Size of the unit she is with. The maximum bonus is up to the wearer\u2019s Essence. If this is an actual Battle Group that the exalt leads then the maximum bonus is Essence+1. Note that a typical circle of Exalts would be at least size 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Orichalcum Hide Spirit</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m <b>Mins: </b>Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Both<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Unbreakable Pride spirit<br /> <br /> The hide of the celestial lions is akin to solid Orichalcum. When invoked the wearer\u2019s skin and hair turn golden and stiffens versus all attacks. It doubles the wearer\u2019s bonus Soak from the armor versus Withering Attacks as well as Hardness versus Decisive Attacks. The protections may not be overcome or lessened in any way.<br /> <br /> <b>Shard of the Pride Summons</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>10m, 3a, 1wp <b>Mins: </b>Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>none<br /> <b>Duration: </b>one Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Orichalcum Hide spirit<br /> <br /> Bringing together a union of armor, Essence, will, and spirit, the Exalt reads the pact from her armor with a triumphant cry, and her anima bursts free as an enormous, brilliant golden lion, which joins the Exalt in battle. This avatar of the armor immediately rolls Join Battle and gains its own Initiative pool. It has the traits of a great cat (p. 565) with the addition that it gains a soak and hardness bonus as if it wore heavy artifact armor (this in no way impedes its movement and it suffers no mobility penalty), and is in all ways considered the Solar\u2019s familiar\u2014including being a valid subject for Survival Charms and Ride Charms, even those that permanently empower a familiar. At Essence 4+, the Solar may pay for Aegis of the First Pride\u2019s instant-duration Evocations by spending points of the anima lion\u2019s Initiative in place of motes on a two-for-one basis. If the anima lion is incapacitated, it vanishes and cannot be called forth again until the Solar successfully hunts and slays a deadly beast or monster that challenges her skills as a warrior. During that time, the cost of all of Aegis of the First Pride\u2019s Evocations rise by one mote, as the armor\u2019s wounded spirit strives to mend itself.<br /> <br /> <b>The Pride Returns </b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>15m, 3a, 1wp, 1lhl <b>Mins: </b>Essence 4<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>none<br /> <b>Duration: </b>one Scene or more<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Shard of the Pride Summons<br /> <br /> This impressive evocation calls upon the pact and summons the slain spirits of the First Pride as well as the living to form an impressive unit of grand golden lions. They form a Size 5, Might 3 unit with unusually high statistics and Perfect Morale. Invoking this has long reaching consequences as it summons all the Celestial Lions and can only be performed once as essentially this ends the Pact with the Walker in Glory and Victory that the Celestial Lions share. They will stay until the battle is won or the wearer of the Aegis is slain<br /> <br /> It\u2019s possible that the Pact may be restored, but such a feat as to impress all of the Celestial Lions with your nobility may be more difficult given their nature now. Such is the stuff the Solar Exalted are made of now though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1580,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","user":"andrewm9","date":". 09-19-2016, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:39:07-07:00","id":972652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=972623#post972623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking for the attunement bonus I'll have +1 Appearance and +3 Motes. Does that break anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have my book handy, but the one thing I find kind of...quirky...about that is, if I'm understanding it right, that the wielder spends motes to commit to this armor, and then gets motes from having attuned it. While I'm shaky on the math of motes in general, it seems a little more complicated than it needs to be in phrasing; IIRC you'd get the same results if it just cost two motes for the Solar to attune to it in the first place.<br /> <br /> Then you're getting into the questions of whether a mere two-mote commitment is too much of a bargain for everything you get from it. But that's a matter for people who have their books about them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:45:43-07:00","id":972740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=972652#post972652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have my book handy, but the one thing I find kind of...quirky...about that is, if I'm understanding it right, that the wielder spends motes to commit to this armor, and then gets motes from having attuned it. While I'm shaky on the math of motes in general, it seems a little more complicated than it needs to be in phrasing; IIRC you'd get the same results if it just cost two motes for the Solar to attune to it in the first place.<br /> <br /> Then you're getting into the questions of whether a mere two-mote commitment is too much of a bargain for everything you get from it. But that's a matter for people who have their books about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly sure the +3m is additional attunement cost, not attunement refund. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:48:36-07:00","id":972742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notanautomaton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=972623#post972623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking for the attunement bonus I'll have +1 Appearance and +3 Motes. Does that break anything?[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>By itself? No, probably not.<br /> <br /> However, if you plan to stack other Appearance-boosting effects to crank your Appearance up into the 7+ range (which I'm guessing you do) then yes, that <i>can </i>break things and is probably not a fantastic idea. I'd recommend coming up with something different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T19:51:36-07:00","id":972891,"title":"","content":"For a different character application, would it break anything if I put Black Wind's evocations on a Daiklave and made them purchasable normally?<br /> <br /> And replaced Dark Life Detection and Soul-Reaving Release with something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","user":"notanautomaton","date":". 09-19-2016, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:11:39-07:00","id":973336,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Prismatic Beauty</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><br /> Prismatic Beauty was made in the first age. Few know exactly when, none wrote it down. But a single myth is told of its creation. A lunar shaman made it as a gift to their bethrothed. Every night for 1,000 nights, the lunar left her home in secret, and played a song to her patron, Luna as she collected wood spider's silk. Then, on the thousand and first night, as she sung her song near a lake to gather her thoughts, the moon's reflection showed the form of a gentle Rabbit, one of the many guises of Luna. The lunar bowed her head, as Luna spoke:</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">&quot;You sing for me though I am not your lover. And I have fallen in love with your voice. I know that my heart cannot take the pain of separating you from your love, nor can I bare these feelings... and so I will grant you a boon to end your song, so I may move on.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">And for her boon, she plucked exactly seven hairs from Luna's tail. These hairs seemed small at first, but as she spun them, it was like each one could wrap around the moon in the sky itself. And so, she spun them into a silken cloth, miles long yet only inches long, and used Luna's moonsilver to gain control of it.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">After nearly 100 years of spinning, she had crafted a masterpiece, a silken armor designed in love's name, given to one who sought justice above all. In time, the armor came to take on it's wearer's personality, showing a desire for style and grace at all times.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Shimmering Guise</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Cost: 1m; Mins: Essence 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Keywords: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Duration: Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prerequisites: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prismatic Beauty shimmers and shifts, altering itself to take the shape it's user desires. It can look like nearly any piece of clothing, though most often takes the form of a long dress, colors shifting to be appropriate. This evocation is granted for free to any who attune to it, and grants the user +1 appearance for the scene. It gets bored of looking the same way for too long, and always pushes the user to allow it to shift for each new event they attend.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Moon Prism Power</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Cost: 1wp, 3a; Mins: Essence 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Keywords: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Duration: One Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prerequisites: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prismatic Beauty feels the warmth of a solar's aura, and pulls it into herself, deepening their communion. The Solar's anima is vented into the armor, and it takes on a dramatic transformation, glowing equally bright, but in a prism of colors in the slivers of moonsilver woven into the silk. The outfit becomes one of impossible beauty, framing the solar's own beauty and giving them a bonus to their appearance equal to their essence for the remainder of the scene. Further, on activation, the solar becomes attuned to the dangerous situation they're in, all thoughts but victory (and style) leaving their mind effortlessly. They are granted 15 initiative. This initiative bonus may not be granted more than once per day, unless the solar spends an additional willpower on this evocation, and may only be done if it is in the name of love or justice.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Stuff I've made:<br /> Ex3 Combat Flowchart &gt; <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/wnh21nkq07uuoct/Exalted%203rd%20Combat.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/wnh21nkq07...d%20Combat.png</a><br /> Ex3 Battlegroup Cheatsheet &gt; <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/byc19z0coe4kzhq/Exalted%203e%20Battlegroups.png?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/byc19z0coe...roups.png?dl=0</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9361-givenflesh","name":"GivenFlesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9361_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:23:15-07:00","id":973348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GivenFlesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=973336#post973336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Shimmering Guise</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Cost: 1m; Mins: Essence 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Type: Reflexive</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Keywords: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Duration: Scene</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prerequisites: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prismatic Beauty shimmers and shifts, altering itself to take the shape it's user desires. It can look like nearly any piece of clothing, though most often takes the form of a long dress, colors shifting to be appropriate. This evocation is granted for free to any who attune to it, and grants the user +1 appearance for the scene. It gets bored of looking the same way for too long, and always pushes the user to allow it to shift for each new event they attend.</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Might consider making the commitment 5m to bring it in line with the other Appearance Boosters. I would honestly suggest making it so that it can't bring your Appearance above 7 either. As it is it seems like a pretty massive huge benefit for the literal smallest cost possible. At the very least, maybe raise the committed cost to 3-4 motes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T14:18:27-07:00","id":973384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=973348#post973348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Might consider making the commitment 5m to bring it in line with the other Appearance Boosters. I would honestly suggest making it so that it can't bring your Appearance above 7 either. As it is it seems like a pretty massive huge benefit for the literal smallest cost possible. At the very least, maybe raise the committed cost to 3-4 motes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I didn't realize there was a charm that increased appearance. Hm. That is fair. It was meant to largely be a very small, flavorful boon, cause the twilight doesn't have a high appearance, but likes being showy. Do you think the 5 mote cost is more caught up in the increasing appearance, or being able to influence without targeting an intimacy / doubling up on social actions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Stuff I've made:<br /> Ex3 Combat Flowchart &gt; <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/wnh21nkq07uuoct/Exalted%203rd%20Combat.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/wnh21nkq07...d%20Combat.png</a><br /> Ex3 Battlegroup Cheatsheet &gt; <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/byc19z0coe4kzhq/Exalted%203e%20Battlegroups.png?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/byc19z0coe...roups.png?dl=0</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9361-givenflesh","name":"GivenFlesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9361_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T14:25:25-07:00","id":973385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GivenFlesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=973384#post973384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I didn't realize there was a charm that increased appearance. Hm. That is fair. It was meant to largely be a very small, flavorful boon, cause the twilight doesn't have a high appearance, but likes being showy. Do you think the 5 mote cost is more caught up in the increasing appearance, or being able to influence without targeting an intimacy / doubling up on social actions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it boosts an Attribute which has farther reaching implications than just providing a boost to an action, I would honestly peg it around 3-4 motes for the scene since it doesn't provide an additional benefit. The combination of those extra abilities are definitely what makes those Charms into Solar Charms, but the ability to break past the hard cap of Attributes at 5 through magic is a pretty big deal, especially when there are pieces of the system that use those attributes to calculate effects. (For example, if you took this and the other three Appearance booster powers and App 5, you'd have an Appearance of 9, which would give you 9 soak using Demure Carp Feint, or give you 4 Automatic Successes against someone with a Resolve of 5 using Threefold Magnetic Ardor, etc.<br /> <br /> I might suggest it just provide a narrative benefit not unlike the Collars of Cleansing Light (It makes your character look really fresh and clean) and maybe provides a bonus to actions using your Appearance rather than just boosting your Appearance, especially because it's temporary.<br /> <br /> It's not the most broken effect ever, but it's a thing which can mess with stuff if you don't anticipate it.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could move the actual Appearance Booster to a 3rd Evocation at Essence 3, and maybe make it have a much more dramatic effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T07:07:05-07:00","id":976503,"title":"","content":"Ok, I've been working on this for a week or two, but after seeing Sunder The Gold's post about throwing melee weapons, I decided to post my work-in-progress. Here's my first ever homebrew weapon, <b><i>Crystalline Sliver of the Infinite</i></b>.<br /> I'm really crunch-weak, and I have next to no idea about how to properly make Artifacts and Evocations, however I have had this idea I wanted to run past the community. Inspired by <b>Fate/Stay Night</b>, <b>Dark Souls</b>, and <b>Soul Eater</b> I wanted to make an artifact that gave the wielder an infinite amount of extremely sharp, extremely breakable weapons that blend utility and &quot;cool factor&quot;, allowing them to rain crystal on foes in melee or at range with the tried and true method of &quot;Blade Spam&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's my Artifact:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Crystaline </b></i><i><i><b>Sliv</b></i></i><b><i>er of the Infinite</i></b><br /> Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Attunement: 5<br /> Tags: Melee, Lethal, Thrown (Short), Special<br /> <br /> <i>Sometimes called the &quot;Crystal Lightening Blade&quot;, &quot;Frozen Moonlight&quot;, or the &quot;Flashing Shard&quot;, legends don't agree on the source of this strange object which looks like a broken sliver of crystal glass: flat, jagged, and partially opaque. Whether it was found in a naturally occurring crystalline leyline or made by a glass-obsessed sorcerer, the strange shard has indisputable powers of reflection and crystal synthesis. At least two of these items are known to exist, but how they are related and what specific properties are intrinsic to them has been a source of debate among scholars for many centuries. </i><br /> <br /> *<i>Note: The Crystalline Sliver is small, about the size of a broken dagger's blade. Attuning to this weapon requires an hour's meditation in which the crystal is slowly, painlessly inserted into the user's heart. Once finished, there is no physical mark about the body and the Sliver can't be detected even by expert medical inspection. This makes especially useful to assassins, diplomats, and other who would prefer to appear unarmed.</i><br /> <br /> This artifact grants the wielder the ability to generate crystalline blades instantly with a flash of their hand, but the blades are very brittle and short lived. At the wielder's discretion, they can Reflexively use a <b>Draw Weapon Action</b><sup><span style=\"font-size:8px\">1</span></sup> to create one of the following weapons in hand: a <b>Daiklave, Reaper Daiklave</b>, <b>Reaver Daiklave, </b>or <b>Short Daiklave</b>. This may be included in a flurry.<br /> <br /> <sup><span style=\"font-size:8px\">1</span></sup> the <i>Join Battle </i>action includes this use of <i>Draw Weapon</i> as though the Solar had been using a &quot;regular&quot; sword, and is considered armed with the weapon of their choice as normal. All ambush rules apply to starting a battle unaware.<br /> <br /> Weapons created by the <b>Sliver</b>are as sharp as they are brittle, they deal an extra 3 (???) damage on <b>Decisive</b> attacks, which also causes them to shatter. The wielder of the <b>Sliver</b> will need to be cautious that they are not caught unarmed before they can create another weapon. All Weapons created by the <i>Sliver </i>will also shatter is they are further than Short Range from the Artifact bearer.<br /> <br /> *<i>Special</i>: Despite not having a sheath, Reaper Daiklaves generated by the shard may be used with the Single Point Shining into the Void style as normal. Confusingly, they still mimic the sheathing and drawing action as normal, although no recording states if this act is explicitly mandatory.<br /> <br /> <u>Evocations of the Crystalline Sliver of the Infinite</u><br /> <b>Infinite Regress of Wielding</b><br /> Cost: 2m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> <br /> The first and most basic of the Crystal Evocations, this technique allows the wielder to create two blades instead of one whenever they use the Draw Weapon action to create a blade. They weapons do not have to be of the same type.<br /> <br /> Special Activation Rule: The character must have shattered a weapon on a Melee Decisive Attack and then drawn a new one afterwards in the same battle.<br /> SAR 2: After Essence 2, AND shattering a blade on a Thrown Decisive attack, the character may create up to [Essence +1] blades instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Reflective Path of the Manifold Mirrors</b><br /> Cost: 3m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Movement<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prereq: Infinite Regress of Wielding<br /> <br /> The character may utilize the strange properties of the reflective blade shards cast around the battlefield. When the Character makes a successful Dodge or takes a Movement (such as a disengage, rush, or the like) they can choose to appear instantly at one of the blades scattered around the battlefield. This requires the character to have non shattered blades around them, within Short Range. This action may ignores any obstructions between the character and the target blade, as long as there is line of sight between the two. The character does not suffer any effects from hostile terrain during this instantaneous movement, such as burning ground, poisonous gasses, or acidic rain. The character suffers these effects as normal if they persist where the movement ends.<br /> <br /> SAR: The character must have made a successful stunt to retrieve a Sliver blade while in combat, either as part of a move, dodge, parry, or the like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lightening Flash of Crystal Mirrors</b><br /> Cost: 3m Mins: Essence (2 or 3??)<br /> Type: Movement<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prereq: <i>Infinite Regress of Wielding</i>, <i>Reflective Path of Manifold Mirrors</i><br /> <br /> As the evocation <i>Reflective Path of Manifold Mirrors</i>, but the Solar may throw a blade and catch it <b>midflight</b> as part of a movement, or attack.<br /> <br /> SAR: Must have used <b>Reflective Path of Manifold Mirrors</b> on a blade that was on a hard to stand location, such as a ceiling, high up a mast or tree trunk, the underside of the Behemoth of Thorns, etc. <i>The location should have been reachable only by stunt or an appropriate charm. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Frost Blades of the Morning Mist</b><br /> Cost: 5m Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: ???<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Prereq: Lightening Flash of Crystal Mirrors<br /> Arguably the most famous Evocation of the<i> Sliver of the Infinite,</i> the character produces dozens of blades in a flash and throws them outward in every direction. Every surface within Short Distance is so packed with blades that the character is never more than arm's reach from one. The indiscriminate nature of this maneuver is such that all characters withing Short Range, friend and foe alike, must make an attempt to protect themselves or suffer damage as from a thrown attack. The attack's indiscriminate nature makes it easy enough to avoid, however, (Easy dodge or block or parry, I don't math here). The ground (and floor, walls, ceiling, etc) are considered dangerous terrain and may cause movement penalties without a stunt or appropriate charm. Any character attempting to make a Rush attack must take care that they do not slice themselves to ribbons, and incur a (minor penalty here).<br /> Also, due to the area nature of this attack, Battlegroups take (extra damage) and have (defense penalty) to stopping the attack.<br /> <br /> SAR: In one scene, the character must have used Lightening Flash as part of a Thrown decisive attack that Killed or Incapacitated a non-trivial foe, AND must have drawn at least 5 blades using Infinte Regress.<br /> -----------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> That's pretty weak mechanically, but it's what I've got so far. Let me know what you think and I'm grateful for any advice crunchwise. The Idea is to make a but of disposable but dangerous blades and utilize a high damage, high mobility hit-and-run style of combat. I also want the blades to break on blocks/parries/clashes but wasn't sure how to word that so you still to do one of those cool &quot;ninja/samurai running one stroke battles&quot; kinda thing.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Inspiration<br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/X_YdP7tB8WM?t=81\" target=\"_blank\">Mifune's &quot;Infinite One Sword Style&quot;</a><br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/S5Vf8obhTd4?t=81\" target=\"_blank\">Archer using &quot;Unlimited Blade Works&quot;</a></b></u><br /> <u><b><a href=\"http://darksouls.wikia.com/wiki/Crystal_(upgrade_path)\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Souls Crystal Upgrade</a></b></u><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 09-26-2016, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T15:16:51-07:00","id":980442,"title":"","content":"Sword of Summer(Orichalum/White Jade Daiklave, ***) (Sorry for lacking Fluff...)<br /> <br /> Forged long ago for a nameless solar of the south, the Sword of Summer was made to keep a clear mind no matter the circumstance. When in blow Wyld winds or restless gods, when desert heat and loss of water would cloud the thoughts of a normal man, the Sword would keep them focused. Over the years, it has made it's way to Volviat in the Dreaming Sea, where it is almost more necessary. Primeval magics and dark wonders lure men and women astray in the strange South Eastern seas. <br /> <br /> Attunement Bonus: For 2 extra motes of attunement, increase the wielder's resolve by 1(This counts as a non-charm addition).<br /> <br /> <b>Without Complaint:</b><br /> Cost: 5m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Perquisite Charms: None<br /> <i>The Sword of Summer recalls </i><br /> <i>more pleasant times</i><br /> <i>To heal wounds of the mind.</i><br /> <br /> This charm may be activated whenever the wielder is reduced to their -1 health levels or lower. After paying the cost, the wielder ceases to suffer from wound penalties for the remainder for the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>As Sure As Steel</b><br /> Cost: 3m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Perquisite Charms: Without Complaint<br /> <br /> <i>The Summer Returns,</i><br /> <i>Again and Again</i><br /> <i>Despite Winter\u2019s Reign.</i><br /> <br /> This charm may be activated after an enemy declares they are attacking, but before dice are rolled. After activating this charm, the wielder resets his onslaught penalty to zero.<br /> <br /> <b>Mind of Jade</b><br /> Cost: 6m Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Perquisite Charms: As Sure As Steel.<br /> <br /> <i>The Summer Sun</i><br /> <i>Banishes Mists</i><br /> <i>Of Distant Lands</i><br /> <br /> This maybe activated whenever the wielder is subject to illusions or pysche keyworded effects. After activating this charm, the blade flashes golden. The wielder gains the benefit of a defining intimacy and a speciality against any such effects for free. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T01:31:31-07:00","id":983214,"title":"","content":"Black Wind is great, but it's definitely not for everyone. I decided to play around with some concepts for other high-powered Thrown artifacts, and landed on something that is along the lines of &quot;Spider-Man meets the Hulk&quot;, with a little Batman-style &quot;jump off a cliff and figure out how not to die on the way down&quot; thrown in for good measure. It's meant for everyone who treats the Feats of Strength chart as a bucket list. Comments welcome and criticism actively sought!<br /> <br /> <b>Shackles of the Steel Dragon (Moonsilver Hearthstone Bracers, Artifact 5)</b><br /> <br /> Among the members of the Solar Deliberative, few were as widely respected as Taenn Mountain-born, a scholar and philosopher renown for his humility and tact. While many of his colleagues were, perhaps, more popular than him, and the majority may have been more accomplished in martial or arcane arts, Taenn was well-liked for his gentle manner and conscientiousness...<br /> <br /> ... outside of battle, anyway. In a fight, Taenn was a terror, not only to his enemies, but to his allies and himself. Prone to destructive rages, he wielded every weapon available to him to destroy those persistent enough to draw his ire, including rocks, furniture, horses, trees, and hapless bystanders. Disturbed by his approach to combat, the sages of Heaven attempted to calm him through study of the martial arts, ritual intoxication, and finally peaceful seclusion. When at last Taenn collapsed a marble temple on himself, they turned to his wife, a gifted No Moon weaver of moonsilver threads. If anyone could mend the cracks in his temper, it would be her, and they beseeched her for assistance despite her curious disregard for her husband's temper.<br /> <br /> She said that she would require the hearts blood of a species hunted to extinction, which the cruel among them spilled for her. She said that she would require the hide of an elemental dragon too bloated with power to be capable of reason, which the mighty among them skinned for her. She said that she would require a sample of the Wyld itself, so pure that even a Raksha could not look upon it, which the blind among them found for her. She said that she would require provisions stolen from the Sun's liquor cabinets, which the daring among them procured for her. Finally she said that she would need two hairs from Luna's own head, which were freely given. With all of these materials, she said that she might fashion shackles capable of binding even her husband's ill-hidden rage.<br /> <br /> She lied. Instead, she made him these.<br /> <br /> The Shackles of the Steel Dragon are moonsilver hearthstone bracers that whisper voiceless temptations of reckless action to their wearer. When a hearthstone is presented to them by their wearer, the moonsilver withdraws around the top of the forearms to reveal orichalcum settings, one in each bracer. Should one of the Solar or Lunar Exalted spend five additional motes (for a total of six) when attuning these bracers, they may ignore penalties for fighting with an improvised weapon, and treat mundane throwing weapons as if they were artifacts of the equivalent size. This improves accuracy and damage, but does not allow weapons which do not normally return to the wielder to do so. Additionally, the following evocations may be awakened:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Inertia-Preserving Focus</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: --; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Uniform<br /> <b>Duration</b>: One Round<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: None<br /> Every time the Exalt uses a thrown weapon to damage an opponent or succeed at a gambit, she gains a non-charm success to all movement actions and (Strength + Athletics) checks until the end of her next turn. If the weapon was improvised, she may reflexively ready another improvised weapon immediately, so long as the new weapon is heavier than the previous one, a condition which will eventually require feat of strength checks. If such a check fails, Inertia-Preserving Focus is disabled for the rest of the scene unless the Exalt takes a Miscellaneous Action to catch her breath.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules</b>: This Evocation awakens at no experience cost when the Solar voluntarily initiates combat against an opponent with a Strength score at least 3 higher than her own.<br /> (If you ignore the imposition of escalation, the second half of this Evocation is flatly superior to Spitting Hand Technique when it comes to improvised weapons, but it doesn't apply to normal armaments. I'm of two minds about this; I feel a little guilty, but it IS an Artifact 5.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Steel Souls Tethered</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Uniform<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: None<br /> Normally, the shackles empower thrown weapons with a nigh-imperceptible filigree wire of essence that vanishes soon after the weapon's flight concludes. This Evocation reinforces that connection, strengthening it into a visible cord of moonsilver that can retract and loose at the wielder's command. This allows the Exalt to retrieve the weapon without a roll, but that is only the simplest of this evocation's uses. When employed in a stunt that involves movement (perhaps through grappling, rappelling, or swinging), this tether contributes one non-charm success.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules</b>: This Evocation awakens at no experience cost when the Solar voluntarily leaps into a drop of at least three range bands.<br /> (I really just want to play Spider-Man.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Stoneheart Avalanche Impact</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Withering-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Inertia-Preserving Focus<br /> Setting aside her reservations to take up arms, the Chosen of the Sun stokes the fury in her breast to new heights in order to cast down an ever more hated foe. This Evocation may only be used when attacking or defending the subject of a Tie. The Solar adds damage dice to the attack equal to her (Essence + Tie's intensity rating). If this attack successfully deals more initiative damage than the Solar's Resolve, the Tie increases in intensity. If the Tie was already Defining, she gains a point of Limit instead. She may only gain Limit once per scene in this fashion. An intimacy escalated by this Evocation may not be voluntarily eroded until the next New Moon.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules</b>: This Evocation awakens at no experience cost when the Solar voluntarily enters combat for no material purpose other than to defend the subject of a negative Tie.<br /> (Twice the cost of Fists of Iron, half the scope, but no worrying about the edge case of an opponent without soak to ignore. On top of that, it gives you probably-unwanted intimacy escalation and Limit! Isn't that great?!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Selfsame Projectile Method</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 6m, 1wp; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Steel Souls Tethered<br /> Immediately following a thrown withering attack that crashes its target, the Solar may use this Evocation to follow up with an immediate Brawl or Martial Arts decisive attack. The thread connecting her to her weapon shines with surging essence and pulls the Solar along the same path as her missile, bringing her into contact with her opponent in a blur of sudden motion. This counts as an automatically successful disengage check, if one is necessary, and may take the Solar up to two range bands. The target may not exercise reflexive movement of any kind until the follow-up attack is complete. If the follow-up attack is made unarmed, the Smashing tag is available for use.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules</b>: This Evocation awakens at no experience cost when the Solar accomplishes initiative shift against a significant opponent.<br /> (This gives you a timing advantage as if you crashed someone from an initiative score below theirs, without requiring that low starting initiative. That's... significant, and worthy of an Essence 3 evocation for a game-defining artifact. On top of that, it's one hell of a ride! Weeee!)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shattered Treasure Vengeance</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 10m, 1wp; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 4<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Stoneheart Avalanche Impact, Selfsame Projectile Method<br /> This Evocation is a last resort reserved for moments of greatest triumph or greatest tragedy. When the subject of one of the Solar's Defining Ties who carries an artifact weapon into battle is incapacitated on the battlefield, she may reach out with the Shackles of the Steel Dragon and claim the fallen weapon in mourning or exultation. A draconian claw of moonsilver will extend at up to medium range to snatch the weapon and return it to the Solar's hands. Overloading it with the essence of reckless violence, she casts it at her enemies and it explodes into a plume of white-hot essence and razor-sharp fragments of the invincible. This is a decisive Thrown attack which affects everyone and everything within long range of the target except the Solar herself. Roll the attack once, and deal normal damage to everyone hit, as well as additional dice of damage equaling the artifact rating of the now-lost weapon. If the Solar knows the charm Fiery Solar Chakram, it may be used as a Supplemental charm for this Evocation.<br /> <br /> This Evocation may only be used once per Lunar Cycle. In the case that the owner of the shattered artifact weapon survives the battle, or that the wielder of the Shackles pays an experience cost suitable to purchase the weapon's Artifact background for herself, a curious miracle takes place on the next full moon. The owner--old or new--will discover the once-lost weapon planted in the earth under the light of Luna, whole but not un-scarred. The restored weapon will be mended with moonsilver kintsugi, and any who attune to it will feel a momentary, searing echo of the grief or satisfaction that shattered it.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules</b>: This Evocation awakens at no experience cost when the Solar voluntarily takes to a battlefield knowing she is outnumbered at least 3:1.<br /> (This is meant to be balanced against Pyroclastic Holocaust Judgment. My primary concern is that it might require much less buildup to attain an explosive finale, since someone can be Incapacitated early on in a fight. Its damage cap is obviously much higher, but its floor is lower. It is also much more difficult to shape the explosion to your liking.)<br /> <br /> (Other thoughts: if putting limitations or restrictions onto these Evocations, it would be nice to use Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina once each in order to reflect the Lunar origins.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2223,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","user":"Ketrus","date":". 10-07-2016, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T18:58:23-07:00","id":989131,"title":"","content":"<b>The Unburdened Blade (Moonsilver Reaper Daiklave, Artifact 4)</b><br /> <br /> This blade was forged by an ancient Lunar sorceress, a shapeshifting crone who lived as a hermit among snow-capped mountains as far from civilization as she could get in creation during the first age. It was crafted in her final years; a gift for her newly exalted solar mate meant to guide him in her absence and keep him from being snared by the world that had, in her mind, taken from her his previous incarnation.<br /> <br /> Fate was not on her side however, and the usurpation claimed the life of her young mate soon after her own death. Given the effect the blade has had on some of its less carefull wielders though, the intentions behind the gift might not have been entirely pure, or perhaps the execution a bit overzealous. Unlike most moonsilver artifacts, the weapon is shunned by most Lunars who know its history despite its undeniable power.<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> While attuned this thin moonsilver reaper daiklave is astoundingly light and implores anyone that attunes it to forsake any other burdens that might weigh them down and live their life free as a bird. As long as the Solar or Lunar that wields it claims no possessions beyond what they could carry on their person (without the use of any strength-enhancing charms or magic), and claims rulership over no lands or men, they will find their blade always swift and ready to strike granting one non-charm success on all join-battle rolls.<br /> <br /> The wielder can summon or create beings with spells such as Demon of the First Circle/Summon Elemental or sorcerous workings and keep the bonus, but they must be called to fullfill a certain task or purpose rather than being bound to the wielder as slaves.<br /> <br /> (I've been back and forth on the attunement bonus. Obviously it's very good with Single Point, but I don't think in general as strong as the +1 Acc &amp; post soak damage from Adorei and the requirements are a lot harsher. I made it a success over dice because 2 dice are stronger with rerolls and double nines and 1 die just seems too weak for all the trouble.)<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> <b>Pierce the Folly of Greed</b><br /> <br /> Cost -; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> The swords teaches its wielder to see through the folly of greed, in himself and others, for it makes you hunger for things that only tie you down. This evocation grants a permanent +2 bonus to Resolve vs. attempts to bribe the wielder, and a -1 penalty to the Guile of those motivated by lust for wealth and power over others against the wielders Read Intentions actions.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Cut Through all Restraints</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Drawing strength from its wielders resolute desire to remain unfettered, the blade moves with impossible speed to strike away any attempt to restrain them.<br /> <br /> This charm applies a penalty equal to the wielders resolve on any attempt do restrain or grapple him that he attempts to parry or clash with the Unburdened Blade, as well as any attempt do disarm the weapon.<br /> <br /> Once the wielder has unlocked this evocation, any attempt to cut physical restraints such as chains or ropes with the blade recieve one non-charm success.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> This charm can only be used when the wielder is in accord with the requirements to gain the blades attunement bonus.<br /> <br /> (I don't know if 3m is too much. The charm is obviously modeled on Doe Eyes Defense and in some ways much worse with not being usable against most attacks, not potentially giving you initiative, and there not being any passive Resolve adders like there's Guarded Thoughts Meditation for Guile. OTOH you can combine it with Hail Shattering Practice + Fervent Blow if someone is silly enough to try to grapple or disarm you.)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Unburdened Blade</b><br /> <br /> Cost: -; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Pierce the Folly of Greed, Cut Through all Restraints<br /> <br /> Growing confident in a wielder that has learned to resist the bonds of material things, the blade feels the burden of its own worries lifting and it becomes light as a feather. When this Evocation is awakened, the blade gains a permanent +1 increase to its Accuracy.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Sever all Ties</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 1 wp, special; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Unburdened Blade<br /> <br /> When those things you value most are used against you or prevent you from having the freedom the blade knows is best for you, it whispers in your mind to <i>just let it all go</i>, and with its guidance you can. Activating this evocation the wielders cares and worries for the world fade away, and in their place remains only self preservation and the purpose woven into the blade.<br /> <br /> All the wielders intimacies except those made involatile by charms such as Righteous Lion Defense or Ties to a Solar or Lunar mate are suppressed; for the duration of the charm the wielder acts as if they do not exist and no new intimacies can be gained. Instead the wielder takes on an involatile Defining Principle that his personal freedom is paramount.<br /> <br /> While this evocation is active the wielder also gains one automatic success on all combat actions, but only while fighting to protect his physical person, the blade itself (while this charm is active these are seen as the same), his mate, or his personal freedom.<br /> <br /> Giving in to the blade is never without cost, and frequent usage of this power comes at a terrible price.<br /> <br /> The first time in a year this evocation is used, the wielder gains its Principle at a Minor level unless he already has it at that or a higher level in which case it remains unchanged. Any subsequent acivations during the same year will increase the Principles intensity by one step. This intimacy cannot be decayed in a year in which this evocation has been used, and cannot be used in a year in which it has been decayed.<br /> <br /> At the end of any scene where this charm is used, the wielder will also lose one intimacy of the same intensity as this Principle, or two intimacies of a lower intensity if one of equal intensity does not exist. These intimacies are chosen by the storyteller but the blade goes for those intimacies that most strongly oppose its purpose first. Again only intimacies protected from decay by magic like Righteous Lion Defense or Ties to Lunar/Solar mates are safe.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> Unlike most charms or evocations, the willpower cost of this charm is payed at the end of the charms duration rather than on activation. If the wielders temporary willpower at that point is 0, no willpower need be payed.<br /> <br /> (Social defense by going temporarily quite insane seemed pretty lunar/moonsilvery, but it's possible the effect of suppressing intimacies like this is just a bad idea. OTOH maybe the penalties are actually so harsh no one would ever pay 8 solar xp to have it when you can barely ever use it if you like your character not being insane or caring about things. The power seemed naratively fitting for the artifact but its probably deeply flawed in play.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 10-17-2016, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:56:36-07:00","id":989162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=950828#post950828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Stellar Hawk (Grand Daiklave \u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7)</span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I know this post is two months old, but did you consider making these charms a martial art rather than a group of evocations? Because a lot of them seem like what I'd imagine charms for a sword-based martial art focusing on aim actions and duels ended with a single perfect strike could look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T05:31:35-07:00","id":989301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=989162#post989162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know this post is two months old, but did you consider making these charms a martial art rather than a group of evocations? Because a lot of them seem like what I'd imagine charms for a sword-based martial art focusing on aim actions and duels ended with a single perfect strike could look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I considered that possibility initially. The only mechanical difference would be allowing more weapon types vs compatibility with Solar melee, which is what I wanted for my character. That said, if you wanted to use it as a martial art at your table, I'm sure it could be easily adapted: the attunement effect should be moved to the form along with some additional effect to make it worth the purchase; the rest of the charms should work out fine.<br /> To be honest I'd imagined Single Point Style would have been something like this, instead of the broken mess it currently is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T02:28:43-07:00","id":992860,"title":"","content":"Hello Everyone<br /> <br /> First of all I would like to thank all of you for the fantastic inspiration that you gave me for my own campain.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m new in this forum and English isn\u2019t my native language so forgive me in advance.<br /> <br /> I would like some advice for the creation of an artifact:<br /> <br /> One of my player wants a Lyre (inspired by Saint Seiya and the character Benetnash Mime) and he thought about an artifact with these evocations:<ul><li>One that allow a gambit to grapple one (or more) target(s) with the string (Short Range I think). Pool dice should be (Manipulation or Charisma + Performance)</li> <li>One that allow to damage target which is locked in the grapple (maybe with the wave made by the music)</li> <li>One that allow to \u201cpuppets\u201d the target to force him to make actions (maybe only miscellaneous actions or Defend other action but no attack action I think). Based on Dexterity + Performance but not sure if it\u2019s better to use target or character Attributes/Abilities</li> </ul>Does it look reasonable ? Anyone have other ideas based on this artifact ?<br /> I\u2019m not very comfortable with homebrew stuff and would be really thankful if someone could help me to create this artifact","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T19:30:49-07:00","id":996400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=992860#post992860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello Everyone<br /> <br /> First of all I would like to thank all of you for the fantastic inspiration that you gave me for my own campain.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m new in this forum and English isn\u2019t my native language so forgive me in advance.<br /> <br /> I would like some advice for the creation of an artifact:<br /> <br /> One of my player wants a Lyre (inspired by Saint Seiya and the character Benetnash Mime) and he thought about an artifact with these evocations:<ul><li>One that allow a gambit to grapple one (or more) target(s) with the string (Short Range I think). Pool dice should be (Manipulation or Charisma + Performance)</li> <li>One that allow to damage target which is locked in the grapple (maybe with the wave made by the music)</li> <li>One that allow to \u201cpuppets\u201d the target to force him to make actions (maybe only miscellaneous actions or Defend other action but no attack action I think). Based on Dexterity + Performance but not sure if it\u2019s better to use target or character Attributes/Abilities</li> </ul><br /> Does it look reasonable ? Anyone have other ideas based on this artifact ?<br /> I\u2019m not very comfortable with homebrew stuff and would be really thankful if someone could help me to create this artifact</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're looking for music inspired artifacts, the other one I'd have to list would be the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/718200-listen-to-my-song-harmonious-symphonic-regalia-artifact-4-armour\">Harmonious Symphoic Regalia</a> based off another anime series you could cannibalize for ideas.<ul><li>See Dreaming Pearl for how it does this. Alternatively you can still grapple at range, just I'd say in this case if the opponent manages to reverse the grapple somehow nothing happens to you at short range (EX: You're not grappled), as you need to be physically next to them.</li> <li>Just make a ravage action for this. Other options can be taken if you want to buff the grapples.</li> <li>Make it based on their Resolve or opposed STR+ATH roll to fight against attacking allies. You still cannot for the held character to use charms against their attack (Controlling the body isn't the same as willing the spirit to activate the charm.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T19:45:36-08:00","id":1005203,"title":"","content":"I've been contemplating an idea for an artifact (a white jade daiklave, named Gravedigger).<br /> <br /> Tentatively, the first Evocation would allow the wielder to shove someone towards or away from another person on the battlefield. I was thinking this could just work as a special form of rush (Dexterity + Athletics, possibly resisted by Dexterity + Dodge instead since the aim is &quot;don't get shoved by earth manipulation&quot; rather than &quot;keep your distance from the guy coming at you&quot;). But I worry that it may be bad design space to let someone manipulate an opponent's position like that, especially if they don't even have to be at close range to shove them toward someone else (maybe they should?). As a side effect it might also be useful for large-scale earthmoving outside combat (although maybe that should be the bonus for attuning the thing instead?).<br /> <br /> The second would be a close-range thing designed to make it difficult for a crashed opponent to escape from close range. I don't see why this would be inherently unreasonable, but I'm not sure what would make for an appropriately brutal increase in difficulty without being completely unfair. (This is kinda the blade's signature trick -- if the opponent is incapacitated with this in effect, it drags them all the way six feet under.)<br /> <br /> If anyone has suggestions, I'm listening. This thing probably needs 1-2 more Evocations, even for an Artifact 3, but most of my ideas for crazy battlefield manipulation seem like <i>really</i> bad ideas, so maybe it should top off with a solid ranged attack instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T00:17:44-08:00","id":1011398,"title":"","content":"Hello, folks. I'm gearing up for the start of a game early next year. I'm building at least one Artifact for it and I could use some advice on balance, costs, and game rule pitfall avoidance. I have no experience with this particular game (although I have very extensive xp in WoD and CoD), so I'm primarily looking for help seeing problems before they come up as some of these mechanics are pretty potent. I've been really impressed with what I've seen here and could use a sounding board. Thanks. Some specific questions:<br /> <br /> 1. The balance issue I am most concerned with is the mitigation of the grapple defense penalty. I think that the drawback of being able to be disarmed is nasty enough without being easier to hit. You cannot use Melee parry while grappling either. Does this seem reasonable?<br /> 2. Is this a 4-dot Artifact? It seems like more of a 3.5. Do I need to add a little something more or does it seem on par with a 4?<br /> 3. Do you have any suggestions about how to clean up the independent movement timing? I struggled with clarity there.<br /> 4. Is Choking Malice too good, too corner case to be useful, or does it seem okay? This is designed as a &quot;knockout&quot; power which might be too early for Essence 2. Thoughts?<br /> (Edit)<br /> 5. Should it have its own initiative entirely independent of the Exalt when using The Slithering Lash? It didn't even occur to me that it might complicate things with regard to initiative by allowing it to attack on its own. Currently I've got it set up to act on my initiative and acting as if I'm attacking.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#850457\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Spinelash (White Jade Direlash, Artifact </span></span><span style=\"color:#850457\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00000a\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The true origins of this weapon are lost to time. One legend claims that Spinelash is the fossilized remains of an actual species of serpent, dead ages past. Another says that it is the creation of a mad sorcerer whose dream of creating a living weapon cost him his life after it strangled him moments after its birth from wyld energies. A third describes Spinelash as an enslaved spirit gifted by a powerful demon to the Solar that mastered him at the height of the First Age. However it came to be, its ownership has been more remarkable and better documented. Spinelash is a weapon of assassins that passes from wielder to would-be victim. The white jade direlash can sense when a victim of its owner would be a more appropriate partner. It will attempt to turn on or abandon its owner if it discovers another to whom it wishes to be attuned. Spinelash has been wielded by a string of assassins after it was rediscovered during the Second Age in a deep cave by a clever bandit named Rufo that had gone to ground there. Rufo became a notorious power in the Eastern woodlands he plundered until Spinelash robbed Rufo of its power as he tried to kill a Dragon-blooded mercenary that had been dispatched to rid the countryside of him. That mercenary likewise fell to Spinelash\u2019s treachery. And so on, and so on. It now rides the hip of a newly-Exalted Night caste merchant prince who has been exiled from his home in Nexus. Is this master the partner the weapon has been seeking or simply another that will be sacrificed to its disloyal whims?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00000a\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Spinelash is comprised of white jade immaculately carved to resemble the vertebrae of a long constrictor. The jade would be nearly indistinguishable from actual bones of an impressively long snake, except for sharp serrations on each vertebrae and the unblemished, stark white color. The \u201cbones\u201d are connected with what looks at first glance to be black leather, but has the feel and tensile properties of sinew. The pommel is jade wrapped with the same connective material that does not easily slip in the hand. At the base of the pommel is the carved skull of a snake with two hearthstone sockets where the eyes would be. Spinelash has the unnerving tendency to appear to move when at the periphery of one\u2019s vision. It doesn\u2019t </span></span><span style=\"color:#00000a\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u>actually</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#00000a\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> move under its own power though\u2026right? </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00000a\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Spinelash has two hearthstone \u201ceye\u201d sockets in the carved snake skull at the base of the pommel.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Special Note</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Spinelash may eventually abandon or turn on its owner. What form this takes varies: it may simply cease working in battle, or slither into the hand of the intended victim it's been ordered to kill, try to strangle its owner in their sleep, or silently slither away in the dark of night. If it does so (and the owner survives it), another Artifact will likely fall into the lap of the very, very lucky Exalt soon.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#850457\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Evocations of Spinelash</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">A Solar or Dragon-Blooded who attunes to Spinelash may explicitly use Brawl charms through it that grapple, unhorse, or disarm. Attacks, grappling control rolls, and grappling combat actions (such as savaging, throwing, etc.) made with it always use the Melee ability, but Brawl charms such as Vicious Lunge (p.275) can be activated while using it. A grapple using Spinelash can be ended immediately by disarming the Exalt wielding it. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Spinelash has a jealous nature. It sees the work it does with its Exalted wielder as an exclusive partnership and brooks no competition. An Exalt that attempts to wield a weapon in the offhand while using Spinelash must spend a Willpower </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>per round </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">or lose attunement with the artifact (the committed motes are lost). As long as its partner abides by this mandate, however, they do not suffer the normal defense penalty while using Spinelash to grapple. The weapon cannot be used to grapple and to parry at the same time; Evasion or an unarmed parry must be employed instead.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#850457\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Grip of the Constrictor</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">2m </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Essence 1 </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Reflexive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Decisive-only </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">One grapple </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prerequisite Charms: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">None</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Exalt feeds Essence into Spinelash after a successful </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Decisive</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> grapple gambit, imploring it to add its strength to the endeavor. It shifts along its victim to find the most vulnerable places to squeeze and mercilessly begins to constrict them. Spinelash grants two automatic successes on the contested control roll. Also, during the grapple, the Exalt does not lose turns of control for being attacked, only for being damaged.<br /> <br /> The weapon loathes giving up its prey and actively assists in holding them tight. </span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">However, Spinelash's reluctance to give up its victim can also be a hindrance. If the Exalt wishes to release a grapple without throwing or incapacitating the target first while using this evocation, the Exalt must drop the weapon or spend a point of Willpower to overcome its desire to keep constricting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#850457\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>The Stirring Snake</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">2m, 2i, special </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Essence 2 </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Reflexive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Perilous </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">One grapple </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prerequisite Charms: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Grip of the Constrictor</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Whispering to the carved jade head on the pommel, the Exalt can begin to ask Spinelash to move on its own. When grappling an opponent under the effects of Grip of the Constrictor where there are at least two rounds of control remaining, the Exalt can use this evocation in lieu of a grappling combat action (even immediately after succeeding on the grapple gambit). By giving up two rounds of control in addition to the other costs, the Exalt may let go of Spinelash and attempt a disengage while the weapon continues to constrict the target via savaging </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">attacks. If the grappled opponent is the only enemy in close range, the disengage automatically succeeds, as the target cannot move. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">After the disengage (successful or not), Spinelash's attacks must be directed using attack actions, but they can be put into flurries at only a -1 penalty to attack. It cannot perform any action but</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">savaging</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">attacks against the target already grappled on behalf of the Exalted. If the target becomes incapacitated, escapes the grapple, or Spinelash is successfully attacked (using the Exalt's Melee parry as a defense), it will drop to the ground and slither back to its partner at one range band per round, sliding back up into the wielder's hand when it enters close range. If Spinelash loses sight of its partner or falls beyond long range, it will follow until it catches up as long as it is attuned. Spinelash moves on the Exalt\u2019s initiative, just before the Exalt.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Special activation rules</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: In order to activate this evocation, at least one of hearthstone \u201ceye\u201d sockets must have a functioning (non-inert) stone placed in it. Hearthstones cannot be removed while the evocation is active.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#850457\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Choking Malice</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2014, (1wp) </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Essence 2 </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Reflexive </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Permanent </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Permanent </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prerequisite Charms: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Grip of the Constrictor</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This evocation improves the effects of its prerequisite. Spinelash relishes every opportunity to crush or choke the air out of its victims. Subjects under the effects of Grip of the Constrictor cannot breath or speak and are subject to suffocation rules as if they were being forcibly drowned (p.232). Any living being that needs to breathe will be incapacitated after (Stamina x 2) rounds. If at any point the grapple is interrupted, the effect ends.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If a target being crushed enters initiative crash while being suffocated in this way, the Exalt may reflexively spend 1 point of willpower to cause them to expel most of their remaining air in a devastating rush. If they cannot escape or end the grapple by the end of their next turn, they are incapacitated.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#850457\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>The Slithering Lash</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">10m, 1wp </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Essence 3 </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Simple </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Dual </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">One scene </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prerequisite Charms: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Stirring Snake</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Once per day, the Exalt can awaken Spinelash entirely. The mouth at the end of the pommel opens with an otherworldly hiss as it slithers out of the Exalt\u2019s hand. The weapon can move around independently for the duration of the scene. The Exalt can direct its movement and attacks at up to long range </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>without</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> taking combat actions to do so. It uses the Exalt's Melee attacks, lashing out as directed. It will perform a clash grapple attack with anyone who tries to pick it up.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00000a\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">On the turn The Slithering Lash is activated and any turn the charm is still in effect, if there are no enemies in close range, it may </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">immediately rush an enemy in short range using the Exalt\u2019s roll or move one range band if not in close or short range of any enemies.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">An enemy can try to end the effect with a difficulty 5 gambit targeting the weapon, but Spinelash defends with the Exalt's Melee Parry. If successful, Spinelash gives up and slithers back to its partner at one range band per round, sliding back up into the wielder's hand when it enters close range. If Spinelash loses sight of its partner or falls beyond long range, it will follow until it catches up as long as it is attuned. Spinelash moves on the Exalt\u2019s initiative, just after the Exalt.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If Spinelash incapacitates a target while moving independently, reset this evocation. Otherwise, reset it at midnight.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Special activation rules</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: In order to activate this evocation, both hearthstone \u201ceye\u201d sockets must have a functioning (non-inert) stone placed in it. Hearthstones cannot be removed while the evocation is active. The Exalt may reflexively activate this evocation at a 5m discount immediately after a victim of The Stirring Snake is incapacitated. Spinelash awakens easily after it takes down its prey.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12709,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","user":"Sir Dragos","date":". 12-05-2016, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T15:19:38-08:00","id":1016274,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Primodial Animus, (Orichalcum/Jade Daiklaive ****)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Concept and Concern- I wanted a daiklave that a battle sorcerer could use not only to give their melee attacks an elementally themed \u201cmagic\u201d feel to them, but also augment their sorcery and enable them to cast effectively while remaining a melee threat. I started to design this with the intent that I could use it in tandem with the shaping Ritual \u201cTalisman Of Ten Thousand Eyes\u201d, swapping the talisman for the sword. Stunting with the sword during combat and sorcery felt very cool to me in theory, and of course the Merits would need some work if I actually managed to play a campaign with this sword. I was slightly inspired by the 2e Sorcery Capturing Chord, but understand that being able to instantly cast a sorcery seemed a bit much. Instead, I wanted to give the feeling of a swordsman understanding the flow of Essence and being able to repurpose Essence and use otherwise wasted energy to fuel sorcery. My concern is mechanical, mostly, and trying to figure out if the attunement bonuses are effective and appropriate for the cost and trying to balance the evocations between too much and too little. Bigger than that though is my concern about the lack of the capstone. For purpose of making no one element outshine the rest, I wanted to make my initial evocation both the bread and butter and the capstone, through higher levels of play. I\u2019m less concerned about overall power of the evocations and more focused on providing a sense of versatility to the wielder. Thank you in advance for all feedback! And I apologize for the long winded nature of the artifact, I fleshed it out 100%, so background is included.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Description- Animus was crafted by a First Age Lunar for his solar mate, a First Age Twilight Sorcerer who mastered both body and mind, using specifically sorcery from afar and with lasting effects to wear his opponents down before sweeping in with his blade to finish off his enemies after they had been wracked by the masterfully cast sorcery.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The sword style of the original user prioritized quick and accurate strikes over powerful and overwhelming might, and as such the evocations of the blade prioritize accuracy and strengthening the weaker strikes of the blade using elemental force. The reason behind this is that the original owner understood that dividing their time between both scholarly pursuits and swordsmanship meant a gap in some department or another, so rather than try to match the physical might of a warrior, he relied on his wits and dexterity to outmaneuver such swordsmen. Wielders of this blade have had their fighting style compared to the swift and fluid grace of dancers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The sword throughout history has been documented and seen very rarely, but has always been wielded by heroes that brought positive change to the world through their actions, whether it be the defense of innocents or the upheaval of dark forces. Especially skilled users were known to be able to use the sword as a focal point for their sorcery, using the blade as one would use a conductor's baton, commanding the flow of Essence intertwining to create masterfully orchestrated sorcery.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The blade of the sword is straight and composed of orichalcum, the handle and hilt of the blade is composed of a five jade composite and set with a small sphere of each color of jade that the hilt is composed of (Black, Blue, Red, White, Green). The Old Realm characters for \u201cWood\u201d \u201cFire\u201d \u201cWater\u201d Earth\u201d and \u201cAir\u201d are written on the flat of the blade in jade lettering corresponding to the element channeled and they glow with ethereal light when the corresponding Essence type is channeled by the user. On the cross-guard of the weapon are two hearthstone settings, one on either side.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Evocations of Primordial Animus- </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A Solar or Dragon Blooded sorcerer that attunes to Animus awakens the first Evocation at no cost. An Exalt attuned to Animus can spend an additional 3m to attune in order to gain deep insight into the blending of sorcery and swordplay. While channeling sorcery, if the user makes a successful attack with Animus, the sorcerer can roll (Occult), gaining the successes as sorcerous motes. This counts as gaining motes for the purpose of not interrupting casting. If the motes meet or exceed the cost of the sorcery, the sorcerer may expend 2i to cast the sorcery immediately. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#BF9000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sorcerous Blade Channeling</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cost: 7m, 1wp (1i) Mins: Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Type: Simple</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Keywords: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Duration: One Scene</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Prerequisites: None</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The sorcerer uses the elemental energy to empower Animus, causing an elemental effect to persist in the sword attacks. Animus vibrates and a single Old Realm word on the flat of the blade lights up with Essence, gaining one of the following powers. The effects also enhance the Evocation of the corresponding element while active. Each element is available only after unlocking the ability to purchase the matching Evocation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FFFF\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Air</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- A gust of wind emanating from Animus disorients nearby enemies and speeds the swordsman's movement. The user may move a single range band in the direction of their choice without making disengage action after a successful dodge or parry. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If another Evocation is unlocked after learning this form of Sorcerous Blade Channeling or the attuned Exalt has learned all of Animus's Evocations, the Exalt can place a protective barrier of wind between them and the enemy that was parried or dodged, preventing them from moving towards the Exalt.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#073763\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Water</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- Water bursts forth from Animus, leaving it's enemies gasping for air. This causes them to lose a point of initiative if the Exalt lands a successful withering attack, regardless of whether or not it dealt damage. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If another Evocation is unlocked after learning this form of Sorcerous Blade Channeling or the attuned Exalt has learned all of Animus's Evocations, if the withering attack while empowered by this variant of Channeling causes crash, the target begins to drown (Page 232 Heavy Exertion). This does not affect those who do not need to breathe. The effect persists until crash ends. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fire</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- Crimson flames dance along the blade of Animus, increasing the strength of successful blows. On a decisive attack, the Exalt can spend (Essence) motes before the attack roll is made. If the attack is successful, an extra dice of damage per mote spent is added to the damage roll. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If another Evocation is unlocked after learning this form of Sorcerous Blade Channeling or the attuned Exalt has learned all of Animus's Evocations, the user can wait to expend the motes until after a successful attack roll.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B7B7B7\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Earth</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- Earthen essence coats the blade in jagged stone, making successful parries heavier and harder to recover from. On a successful parry, the Exalt can steal a point of initiative from the opponent, adding it to their own pool. If another Evocation is unlocked after learning this form of Sorcerous Blade Channeling or the attuned Exalt has learned all of Animus's Evocations, the user can pay an additional mote to steal an extra point of initiative. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#274E13\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wood</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- Beautiful emerald green flowering vines sprout from Animus, shrouding the attuned Exalt with protective growth. Instead of moving during their turn, the Exalt can choose to root themselves in place. While rooted, the Exalt benefits from light cover. Moving or swapping elements end the effects. If you end your turn rooted, you do not lose sorcerous motes even if you did not gain any this turn. If rooted at the start of your turn, you gain a sorcerous mote. </span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If another Evocation is unlocked after learning this form of Sorcerous Blade Channeling or the attuned Exalt has learned all of Animus's Evocations, you gain 3 sorcerous motes at the beginning of your turn while rooted. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The user can expend 1i to switch the elemental focus of Sorcerous Blade Channeling as a reflexive action. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00FFFF\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gusting Gale Gash</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cost: 7m Mins: Essence (1,2,3,4,5)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Type: Simple</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Keywords: Mute, Uniform</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Duration: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Prerequisites: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#7F6000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sorcerous Blade Channeling</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Twisting Animus in elegant spirals, the user creates spinning blades of wind to assault foes from afar. This charm allows the Exalt to make a </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">withering </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">or </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">decisive</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> attack at medium range without aiming. If the attack is used to crash an opponent, the Evocation grants the wielder one point of temporary Willpower. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">While augmented by the Air variant of Sorcerous Blade Channeling, a successful attack using this Evocation adds (Essence) dice to the damage pool of the roll. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Special Activation Rules-</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The attuned can only awaken this Evocation of one of the following conditions are met. The Essence minimum is equal to the order of the Evocation unlocked after Sorcerous Blade Channeling. (1 for First, 2 for Second, so on).</span></span></span><ul><li>After visiting the Elemental Pole of Air and meditating there for one week, the wielder may unlock this Evocation at no cost.</li> <li>After defeating a Dragon Blooded or Elemental of the Air Aspect of a significant threat level to the wielder, the attuned may purchase this evocation.</li> <li>After communicating with a Dragon Blooded or Elemental of the Air Aspect for an extended period of time, the attuned may purchase this evocation.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#073763\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Crushing Current Chop</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cost: 2m Mins: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Essence (1,2,3,4,5)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Type: Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Keywords: Dual</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Duration: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Prerequisites: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#7F6000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sorcerous Blade Channeling</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Demonstrating a knowledge of the finer workings of sorcery and it\u2019s use in augmenting combat strength, the Exalt coats the blade of Animus in rippling blue essence, highly pressurized water shrouds the daiklave and augments its strikes. Like a torrential downpour, the water expands into a crushing wave as the blade strikes its target. On a </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">withering </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">attack, add 2 dice to the raw damage. On a </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">decisive</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> attack, convert up to two extra successes on the attack roll to automatic successes on the damage roll. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">While augmented by the Water variant of Sorcerous Blade Channeling, a successful attack using supplemented by this Evocation also knocks it\u2019s target prone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Special Activation Rules-</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The attuned can only awaken this Evocation of one of the following conditions are met. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Essence minimum is equal to the order of the Evocation unlocked after Sorcerous Blade Channeling. (1 for First, 2 for Second, so on).</span></span><ul><li>After visiting the Elemental Pole of Water and meditating there for one week, the wielder may unlock this Evocation at no cost.</li> <li>After defeating a Dragon Blooded or Elemental of the Water Aspect of a significant threat level to the wielder, the attuned may purchase this evocation.</li> <li>After communicating with a Dragon Blooded or Elemental of the Water Aspect for an extended period of time, the attuned may purchase this evocation.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ballad of Blazing Blades</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cost: 10m Mins: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Essence (1,2,3,4,5)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Type: Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Keywords: Perilous, Decisive-only</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Duration: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Prerequisites: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#7F6000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sorcerous Blade Channeling</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Seeing a gap in the defenses of a foe, the Exalt channels blazing crimson essence through Animus. A brilliant blade of fire flashes forward, mirroring the strike of the Exalt. This Evocation can only be used after a successful withering attack against an opponent with lower initiative score than the user. It allows him to make a follow-up decisive attack with a blade of fire that is produced by Animus at their full dice pool. This Evocation can\u2019t be used more than once on the same turn.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">While augmented by the Fire variant of Sorcerous Blade Channeling, gain one non-charm success on the attack. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Special Activation Rules-</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The attuned can only awaken this Evocation of one of the following conditions are met.</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Essence minimum is equal to the order of the Evocation unlocked after Sorcerous Blade Channeling. (1 for First, 2 for Second, so on).</span></span><ul><li>After visiting the Elemental Pole of Fire and meditating there for one week, the wielder may unlock this Evocation at no cost.</li> <li>After defeating a Dragon Blooded or Elemental of the Fire Aspect of a significant threat level to the wielder, the attuned may purchase this evocation.</li> <li>After communicating with a Dragon Blooded or Elemental of the Fire Aspect for an extended period of time, the attuned may purchase this evocation.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#B7B7B7\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stone\u2019s Stalwart Sheathing</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cost: 7m Mins: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Essence (1,2,3,4,5)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Type: Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Keywords: Withering-Only</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Duration: One Round</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Prerequisites: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#7F6000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sorcerous Blade Channeling</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Earthen essence coats Animus, transmuting into a stony covering around the blade. Striking the stone is like striking pure bedrock. For one round, all post-soak withering damage is halved (round up). This Charm must be invoked when an attack is directed at the Exalt, but before it is rolled. Stronger blows splinter the bedrock, causing stone shards to fly from the blade, making the attacker lose their footing to dodge the shards. 1s on a successful attack roll subtract from the attacker\u2019s Initiative at a rate of -1 for each 1 rolled, to a maximum of half the Solar\u2019s Occult, rounded up. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">While augmented by the Earth variant of Sorcerous Blade Channeling, the initiative subtracted is added to the Exalt\u2019s.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Special Activation Rules-</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The attuned can only awaken this Evocation of one of the following conditions are met. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Essence minimum is equal to the order of the Evocation unlocked after Sorcerous Blade Channeling. (1 for First, 2 for Second, so on).</span></span><ul><li>After visiting the Elemental Pole of Earth and meditating there for one week, the wielder may unlock this Evocation at no cost.</li> <li>After defeating a Dragon Blooded or Elemental of the Earth Aspect of a significant threat level to the wielder, the attuned may purchase this evocation.</li> <li>After communicating with a Dragon Blooded or Elemental of the Earth Aspect for an extended period of time, the attuned may purchase this evocation</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#274E13\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Larcenous Lotus Leech</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cost: 10m (15m) Mins: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Essence (1,2,3,4,5)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Type: Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Keywords: Perilous</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Duration: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Prerequisites: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#7F6000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sorcerous Blade Channeling</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Glowing with verdant green essence, a lotus blossom blooms from the tip of Animus and promptly bursts into a shower of petals. The verdant glow of the flower betrays its nefarious use as it\u2019s scent wafts through the air. The Exalt rolls (Intelligence+Occult), targetting a number of enemies within short range no greater than the wielders (Occult). Those targetted by the Evocation must make an opposed (Dexterity+Dodge) roll to avoid the sharp, sapping, petals. For each failed roll, the user gains 2sm if they are currently shaping a sorcery. If the amount of sorcerous motes gained in this manner exceeds or matches the amount needed to cast the sorcery, the Exalt may expend 2i to cast it immediately. At Essence 4+, the Exalt can pay an additional 5m to increase the range to medium and increase the amount of sm gained to 3. This charm can only be used once per scene.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">While augmented by the Wood variant of Sorcerous Blade Channeling, the attuned Exalt can refresh the use of this charm by casting a successful Sorcery. The charm can only be refreshed this way once per round. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Special Activation Rules-</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The attuned can only awaken this Evocation of one of the following conditions are met. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Essence minimum is equal to the order of the Evocation unlocked after Sorcerous Blade Channeling. (1 for First, 2 for Second, so on).</span></span><ul><li>After visiting the Elemental Pole of Wood and meditating there for one week, the wielder may unlock this Evocation at no cost.</li> <li>After defeating a Dragon Blooded or Elemental of the Wood Aspect of a significant threat level to the wielder, the attuned may purchase this evocation.</li> <li>After communicating with a Dragon Blooded or Elemental of the Wood Aspect for an extended period of time, the attuned may purchase this evocation.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12745-taimageblade","user":"TaiMageBlade","date":".  Added attunement bonus, it didn't copy paste on my initial post. Changed Sorcerous Blade Channeling up drastically, increasing mote cost and making it operate differently. Changed Essence minimums for 12-14-2016, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12745-taimageblade","name":"TaiMageBlade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T22:56:55-08:00","id":1016923,"title":"","content":"TaiMageBlade,<br /> <br /> I am here looking for assistance from more experienced Exalted players as well (see post directly above), so I cannot profess any specific expertise. However, I've waited in vain for feedback, so here is my 2 cents for what it is worth in case nobody else responds to you.<br /> <br /> First, I should note that I really like the idea behind the artifact, especially the concept that an entire chronicle could be built around a quest of discovery unlocking the powers. One concept I had when building characters was a Resistance-Supernal character that wanted to survive all the greatest elemental wonders in Creation to celebrate and advertise the return of the Solars; his goal was to jump into a volcano, surf an avalanche, dive to the bottom of the ocean, fly through a tornado, etc. So a journey to the edges of Creation to meditate upon the elemental poles seems really fun.<br /> <br /> I think the modular feel of the item plays very well into the concept: being able to learn the evocations in a different order is kind of integral, which makes the capstone part more difficult. However, if you were looking to shuffle things around a bit in order to fix that, here are some ideas to do it: First, can you imagine getting all this at Essence 2? Too much. Use an Essence 1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 progression to the powers (or 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3 for a shorter campaign), so that you can only learn Sorcerous Blade Channeling and <i>any one</i> other evocation at Essence 1. Then, instead of having them all grow at Essence 3+, each time you learn another power, give a bonus to the previous ones, representing the character's deeper knowledge of the elements. For example, when you learn the second elemental power, grant an extra die, a reduced cost, or more range, etc. to the previous powers. This way, the one you got first will grow in power as you master new ones. Or, you could reverse it and give the new benefit and all the previous benefits to the new power making the new element the most powerful.<br /> <br /> Sorcerous Blade Channeling has some pretty vague mechanical bits that ought to be cleaned up. For example, it says &quot;on a successful attack&quot; but is that for both decisive and withering? Some of the powers seem more suited to one or the other. Moving other characters is a complicated endeavor. Does the Air version move them away from you, wherever you like, or toward something else? Water will almost assuredly have an 8 difficulty at Essence 3 which seems really high; does this difficulty need to come down or does the roll need to go away and the effect have a per use cost? The Fire power seems more like a decisive damage power while the Water seems like a withering one. The Wood power is so sweet for sorcerous sword-wielders in that it keeps your spell from degrading. I'm not thrilled with the need to whack someone to do it though. How often are you going to want to pause casting to simply hit something with your sword rather than do something else that is so crucial that you are putting off the spell? I LOVE the Earth power, but kind of wish that the various pieces of the whole worked at different times like that.<br /> All this together makes me want to suggest something more like this:<br /> <br /> Open with a Simple action rather than reflexive, as powering up for the fight with access to so much versatility seems like it warrants an action. Ease back on the cost to swap though to 1i; I think this variant will be heavy on swapping. (Keep in mind that you could make Sorcerous Blade Channeling onerous and costly at the beginning and back off of costs and reduce actions, etc. as you gain elements.) You can open into whichever element you want.<br /> Fire: When you make a <b>decisive </b>attack, pay (cost) and get (x dice) extra damage if you hit.<br /> Water: When you make a <b>withering </b>attack, the target loses (x) extra initiative that you don't gain if you successfully hit (even if you deal no damage). If they are crashed with a Water withering attack, they will drown per the heavy exertion rules (see page 232) until they are no longer crashed.<br /> Air: When you successfully dodge, you may move one range band away from the attacker without making a disengage roll. If the attacker was rushing you, end the rush (any other enemies may follow per normal rushing rules).<br /> Earth: Steal (x) initiative on parry. Awesome ability. Super flavorful.<br /> Wood: In lieu of moving during your turn, you may root yourself to the ground and surround yourself with a defensive bramble. You have light cover while rooted, but moving or swapping elements ends the rooted condition. If you end your turn rooted, you do not lose sorcerous motes if you failed to acquire any that turn. If you begin your next turn still rooted, gain a sorcerous mote.<br /> <br /> Not sure on the values of some of this, but these are the directions I think of to solve some of the problems you've described. <br /> <br /> I had also considered what the weapon would look like if you could not access the yet-to-be-obtained elements with the core power until you acquire the greater power. Maybe you could activate the element once you have unlocked <i>permission </i>to buy the evocation, even if you cannot get it yet? If there is a severe power level concern, I could see going this route.<br /> <br /> Edit: This is probably not a Mute power. Anything where you are using your essence to light up your sword like a light show seems...whatever the opposite of Mute is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12709,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","user":"Sir Dragos","date":". 12-14-2016, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:04:26-08:00","id":1017155,"title":"","content":"Dragos,<br /> <br /> Hey thanks for the feedback! I've been reading some stuff and although I'm not too experienced I've been gearing up to offer feedback too, so I really appreciate any and all input! That character concept sounds freaking awesome, I could imagine a Solar surfing an avalanche, haha. I've been looking at the Artifact you posted and the concept is awesome, I've been looking at the mechanics and plan on offering some input soon if you'd like it.<br /> <br /> How do you think I should represent the progression in terms of mechanics? Instead of having a set Essence requirement for the Evocations should the Essence requirement change varied based on the amount of Evocations unlocked before it? For instance, unlocking both the Wind and Water evocation makes the next Evocation require Essence 2 instead of 1? As for powering up the Evocations, should it be like linear? So if I start with Wind, then get Water, Wind gets powered up and so on and so forth? Wouldn't that mean that the last evocation doesn't get powered up? I guess I could add in that after all Evocations are learned from it that it gets the power boost.<br /> <br /> Let me make some edits using what you suggested and some personal thoughts and I'll see what you think? All your suggestions seem pretty spot on to me.<br /> <br /> I changed the sorcerous blade channeling stuff, made it cost more motes initially, added some stuff you suggested word for word and added a little bit of variety for others. I don't really feel concerned about the lack of an &quot;official&quot; capstone Evocation because I feel like the versatility makes up for it. I feel confident this qualifies as a 4 dot artifact because while it's powerful I don't think it warrants a five star rating. I was worried about water and fire being strong on the channeling, but Fire doesn't scale up until you gain more essence now (changed it from Occult to Essence dice) and water doesn't affect targets that don't need to breathe with it's secondary effect. <br /> <br /> I'm currently putting the finishing touches on some observations for yours, hang tight!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12745-taimageblade","user":"TaiMageBlade","date":". 12-14-2016, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12745-taimageblade","name":"TaiMageBlade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T12:47:14-08:00","id":1017224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TaiMageBlade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1017155#post1017155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of having a set Essence requirement for the Evocations should the Essence requirement change varied based on the amount of Evocations unlocked before it? For instance, unlocking both the Wind and Water evocation makes the next Evocation require Essence 2 instead of 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I was thinking. You'd have to decide where the breakpoints were, but getting one at each Essence up to 5 or 1 at Essence 1 (with the base power too), 2 more at Essence 2, and the last 2 at Essence 3 seem the best ways to me. Maybe consider the expected length of the campaign. If you'll never see Essence 5, maybe go with the latter. You still have to pay for them, so it's not that big a deal. You probably won't WANT to buy some until later anyhow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TaiMageBlade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1017155#post1017155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for powering up the Evocations, should it be like linear?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure; it depends a bit on the role you want each ability to play. The Fire one could cost fewer motes per additional power gained or allow you to attack additional targets in close range. The Air power could start as a short range attack and then add ranges per additional power. I say that you should expand them based on how you envision them &quot;getting bigger&quot; as your power grows. Maybe it's more damage, more targets, lower cost, etc. Pick one and explain how it grows.<br /> <br /> I see your edits and I really like how it is shaping up! A complex and expensive series of powers, but it will be style-defining and continue to be very useful throughout the campaign. Nice work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:26:01-08:00","id":1017264,"title":"","content":"1. I think it's perfectly reasonable. Usually when given special abilities like that, you add extra attunement cost. Something like &quot;If attuned using an extra x motes, the user doesn't suffer the defense penalty for grapples while using Spinelash.<br /> 2. I feel like the sentience and unique nature of the artifact lock it in at a solid 4, it's interesting and unique enough that I think it's stronger than a 3 would be.<br /> 3. Independent movement should happen on your initiative.<br /> 4. I don't think Choking Malice has anything to be worried about, other than what I list below. Those are more general than specifically Choking Malice, though. There were Essence 2 or 3 martial arts charms that could incapacitate people at full health just by hitting them, it was one of my favorite Martial Arts actually.<br /> 5. It should act on your initiative and you should have to take attack actions to direct it, having a weapon operating independently seems a little strong if it can move on it's own initiative tick.<br /> <br /> A couple of things, the mote costs seem a little low across the board. Having a weapon operate independently seems really strong, but it makes sense for the direction you're going and you limit it well enough that it doesn't seem too strong. Maybe require that you keep LOS to direct it?<br /> <br /> I wish I had more to say but I'm not really experienced with balance and artifact creation, the above was my first attempt at one. I wish I could help more.<br /> <br /> And yea after your advice and looking at it I think I really like where it's sitting at now, usually GM's I roll with are pretty freewheeling when it comes to allowing changes if things seem unbalanced in either direction. If it's too weak, I could power of some of the Evocations with extra benefits, if they are too strong I could draw it back in a bit. Right now, I like that they get some boosted strength when the Sorcerous Blade channeling is active when the Evocation is used, so I think I'll keep it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12745-taimageblade","user":"TaiMageBlade","date":". 12-14-2016, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12745-taimageblade","name":"TaiMageBlade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T15:18:21-08:00","id":1020001,"title":"","content":"Alright, well, I'm officially <b><i>totally stuck</i></b> on an artifact for a friend. He only really had one request, a very limited rough concept, and absolutely <i>no</i> plot/historical background information. He's coming in very new to the Ex3 system, and on top of that, I'm not our ST--I'm just the guy who's obsessed over the mechanics and artifacts.<br /> <br /> To the point: he's decided on a White Reaper stylist, and he's decided that his artifact scythe should be nature-based--specifically, the one true 'power' he's had in his mind is that where the blade's shadow falls, plantlife withers and dies, but as the shadow passes, it grows back tenfold. I've tried to get more out of him, but because of the long periods of time we've gone without playing or discussing the game (our entire group is kind of waiting on myself and a couple others to get in stable living conditions), he doesn't really have a strong, fleshed-out concept. We've discussed it, and the general decision is that he's totally fine with a small, barely-developed artifact such that he, the ST, and possibly myself can develop and 'discover' its historical legend overtime (increasing its cost as necessary).<br /> <br /> That said? Because I've been away for so long, my mechanical know-how is utterly defunct, and while I read tons of examples in this thread and look back at my own, it seems to just not sink in with regards to this weapon. So, <b><u>PEACH</u></b> is putting it mildly on this one. Let me be clear: all costs, all mechanics, basically everything about this is a first draft, so please pick apart as necessary.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Unnamed Great Scythe</b><br /> <b>(Green Jade, Orichalcum, and Starmetal Grim Scythe) Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Tags:</i></b> Lethal, Melee, Chopping, Reaching, Two-Handed<br /> <br /> [Story Stuff]<br /> <br /> Has 1-2 hearthstone sockets. (??)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Evocations of [Unnamed Grim Scythe]</u></b><br /> A Solar, Sidereal, or Dragon-Blooded attuned to ??? unlocks <b>Reaver of the Primal Harvest</b> for free.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Reaver of the Primal Harvest<br /> Cost:</b> \u2014 (2m, 1 <b>Harvest Point</b> per die); <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b><br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> Life flourishes on death, as all things must consume to persist. The wielder of this artifact takes it up knowing its purpose: to reap the weak such that the strong grow stronger. All <b>decisive</b> and <b>magnitude</b> damage done with this weapon siphons the living energies of the wounded victims into the blade itself in the form of <b>Harvest Points</b> at a rate of one <b>Harvest Point</b> per damage level. The weapon can hold up to a maximum of 2 or the wielder\u2019s Essence in <b>Harvest Points</b>, whichever is higher.<br /> <br /> If the wielder chooses, they may convert these points directly into damage die at a rate of 1 <b>Harvest Point</b> and 2 motes per 1 die.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nature\u2019s Reclaiming Prana</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, (+1 Harvest Point); <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Aggravated, Perilous, Stackable<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Reaver of the Primal Harvest<br /> <br /> All things living die, but life grows stronger on the corpses of the lost; nature recycles, and wise is the farmer who learns from it. The wielder attunes herself and her weapon to the living energies of the world, inspiring new life where once only death tread. For the remainder of the scene, whenever the wielder swings the scythe in such a fashion as to reap crops, plantlife swiftly gives in under the blade\u2019s shadow, falling dead in an instant. However, as the shadow passes, the wielder\u2019s essence suffuses the sunlight that strikes the earth, causing new, stronger produce to grow from the remains of the dead. This effectively enhances a crop or natural overgrowth by roughly a factor of ten; however, such an essence-rich area cannot be similarly enhanced for the remainder of the season except through sorcery.<br /> <br /> In combat, however, the blade turns nature into a deadly weapon. On any successful <b>decisive</b> attack, the wielder makes an opposed roll of her [Willpower + Essence] against the victim\u2019s [Stamina + Resistance]; if she so desires, she may spend any number of <b>Harvest Points</b> to convert the same number of 5s or 6s into successes. If successful, and if the weapon has stored <b>Harvest Points</b> (after conversion), the blade plants seeds in her target\u2019s flesh, which begin to sprout from the wounds made by the scythe\u2019s blade. On the victim\u2019s next turn, and every turn thereafter, he takes ([wielder's Essence]/2) aggravated damage, rounded up, as the plants consume the target\u2019s life. Should the victim\u2019s health track be filled with aggravated damage, with the last level of damage caused by these sprouts, the plants will rapidly overwhelm his form, growing over him entirely and rooting into the ground as a tree befitting the local region, save for its eerily crimson leaves.<br /> <br /> The sprouts can be removed in a number of ways: using Simple actions to do so, at a rate of one Simple action per level of damage being done; upon the target reaching a Burning anima banner or equivalent; by various medicinal aids; or by other forms of overwhelming effects that would, theoretically, destroy or remove them, as decided by the ST.<br /> <br /> This evocation can affect battle groups as is, except that it may also occur with <b>withering</b> attacks; when the battle group loses a point of Size specifically due to the damage of the saplings, those fighters lost are converted into trees.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Field Culling Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m, +1 or more <b>Harvest Point(s)</b>; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Nature\u2019s Reclaiming Prana<br /> <br /> When the gods of the field go to harvest, they do so with divine grace and precision. The wielder who channels the field guardians\u2019 glory through this artifact invokes their guiding hands to ensure that no swing is wasted.<br /> <br /> The wielder may add her Essence to an attack roll. If her enemy is already infested with saplings from <b>Nature\u2019s Reclaiming Prana</b>, she instead adds her Essence in successes, feeling the pull of nature\u2019s energy from her target\u2019s overgrown wounds. Enemies slain by this Charm dissolve into the soil, leaving that patch of earth particularly fertile for years to come, with the saplings well-rooted into the ground.<br /> <br /> If she desires, she may further enhance a <b>decisive</b> attack by spending a <b>Harvest Point</b> to regain motes of Essence equal to the damage levels done (first filling Peripheral, then Personal). Against a foe already infested by <b>Nature\u2019s Reclaiming Prana</b>, she may opt to instead (on a successful <b>decisive</b> attack) to pay all accumulated <b>Harvest Points</b> (minimum 1) to consume the saplings\u2019 absorbed life force, restoring a number of her health levels equal to half the of damage done by the saplings, rounded up. Consequently, this <b>decisive</b> attack does not generate more <b>Harvest Points</b>.<br /> <br /> This evocation affects battle groups as is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Notes:<br /> <br /> As you can tell, the barebones of <b>Nature's Reclaiming Prana</b> is literally the only part he's specifically requested. The other two are my attempts to just... give the thing some unique overgrowing-life-centric theme. Even the Harvest Points concept was a tack-on, because I've got so little idea of what direction he's going to want to take it.<br /> <br /> So, end goal questions:<ul><li>Where is it broken, and what are some ways I can fix it?</li> <li>Should I cut the HP concept out entirely?</li> <li>Will the idea of <b>Nature's Reclaiming Prana</b> work <i>at all</i>, whether as is or with repair?</li> </ul><br /> I know this probably isn't the most original thing out there by any measure, but that middle evocation concept was his one specific request, so it's something I've got to work with somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T15:58:09-08:00","id":1020025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1020001#post1020001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, end goal questions:<br /> <br /> Where is it broken, and what are some ways I can fix it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly the biggest problem here is that you don't know what this thing is yet. Trying to write Evocations for an artifact should happen after you already know what the artifact is all about. You're going about it backwards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Should I cut the HP concept out entirely? </div> </div> </div>I think you should. There's nothing inherently wrong with it, but your player will already be tracking Halos for White Reaper Style and adding a second custom resource to track is not a good idea. Stick to motes, initiative, and willpower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will the idea of <b>Nature's Reclaiming Prana</b> work <i>at all</i>, whether as is or with repair? </div> </div> </div>The &quot;helps crops grow&quot; is fluff and is fine. You don't need mechanics for that. The combat effects are almost infinitely malleable. Once you know what this weapon is, you can take another look at the specific effects of its Evocations and decide if they are worth salvaging or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T16:10:48-08:00","id":1020035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1020025#post1020025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you should. There's nothing inherently wrong with it, but your player will already be tracking Halos for White Reaper Style and adding a second custom resource to track is not a good idea. Stick to motes, initiative, and willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconding this. Exalted is very bookkeeping-intensive. Secondary resources and abilities with lots of weird edge cases are to be avoided whenever possible, otherwise most players will either avoid the option like the plague, or - what's possibly even worse, since it will then take up valuable cognitive and character development resources - pick it and almost never use it/use it suboptimally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T23:03:11-08:00","id":1020197,"title":"","content":"Thank you both. I kind of figured as much, especially looking through the WR charms and trying to find some way to synergize.<br /> <br /> I know I'm going about it backwards, but at this point it's the only path I really have without pulling teeth and getting him to spend time reading and digging and plotting long before our sessions begin.<br /> <br /> I suppose, as long as I'm keeping some manner of <b>Nature's Reclaiming Prana</b> fluff and foregoing evocations until some later date, I should probably leave that as the first evocation and make the 'attunement bonus' that free unlock, thus leaving him to figure it out over time. Once again, thanks so much!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T07:52:57-08:00","id":1020879,"title":"","content":"Been a while since I've used this place, but since I've been playing again my brain is starting to tick. I've asked my GM to let me have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=826295#post826295\">Searing Wisdom</a> eventually in the game, but he said that if I have a fancy custom artifact, I have to design ones for each of the other players as well. Challenge accepted! <br /> <br /> Player 1 is a Giant amazon woman barefisted unarmored brawler dawn. She prefers to remain unarmed and unarmored. Brawl is a great place to launch from, but it's tricky when they want to use their bare fists. So I'm thinking a bracer or something to aid in Brawl stuff. I've considered cannibalizing <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=905032#post905032\">Torrid Pugilism</a> for the concept and that's my default idea if I can't come up with something else, but I'm hoping to come up with something better. This one is going to have to get creative.<br /> <br /> Player 2 is actually my wife, who is playing an aristocratic charming swordsman from Onyx, who's family helped set up the newly deceased with a good second living. He (the character's a guy) is very posh, very fancy, and very &quot;proper&quot; and fights with a straight sword. Currently uses Light armor (buff jacket). This one is actually giving me a little more trouble than the brawler because I've spent so long ignoring swords that I don't have any great ideas. Since the character has an affinity and affection for the dead (a fun duality, since he's a Zenith) I'm thinking maybe something with soulsteel, but I could easily see it going in a different direction. Maybe something to aid in Social stuff, since he's a social monster. This could be a sword weapon or light armor.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for broad ideas and themes here that I can then spin into mechanics. I'm lacking the concept that could then be turned into a cool item. So forumites, anyone got some thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T13:54:25-08:00","id":1020996,"title":"","content":"Unsung, first off, what level of artifact are you aiming for with these? A level 3 artifact looks pretty different from a level 5.<br /> <br /> I think your instinct with bracers is dead-on, that's the first thing I thought with a brawler. If she's staying unarmored, it's probably the best option. Maybe focus on some defensive powers, such as deflecting missile attacks towards others, or allowing a counterattacking disarm gambit against melee attacks as strikes ring off the metal.<br /> <br /> Going with the defensive theme, there's no reason to necessarily focus on a weapon for player 2. A snazzy suit of armor could work just as well. To go along with the posh, refined theme, it could have some benefits akin to Silken Armor, not looking like armor, or some other side benefits like being instantly don-able with a single action or something like that, maybe adding on an effect like Collar of Dawn's Cleansing Light to make it clean and neat reflexively. It could have soulsteel filigree, if you want to go the dead-y route. Are there any abilities that the Zenith focuses on other than combat stuff that it could augment, like Performance or Presence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11685-sundance","name":"Sundance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:09:15-08:00","id":1021030,"title":"","content":"There's a hearthstone in the 3rd core book that allows you to speak to the dead, have you thought about maybe using that power as an Evocation or maybe combining it with the sword to give it a dead-y flair? Maybe bonuses to the weapons stats and abilities for giving the dead some peace of mind or hearing them out on a regular basis, would give the character some cool motivations too. White Jade may be cool to combine with soulsteel (Grave soil, etc) and give the dashing swordsman an elegant white blade to use. I can't help but think fencer when I think of a posh and fancy swordsman, so maybe stuff that allows you to counter attack or turn your opponents strength against them?<br /> <br /> And I know it's the holidays and people are probably very busy, but I've only gotten one person to comment on my artifact and some more feedback to either stroke my ego and tell me I'm in the right spot for custom artifacts or crush my dreams and tell me to spruce it up would be great. I'm thinking about STing if I can't find a game by the middle of January and like to give my players some cool toys to mess with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12745-taimageblade","user":"TaiMageBlade","date":". 12-22-2016, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12745-taimageblade","name":"TaiMageBlade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T12:51:18-08:00","id":1023385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td align=\"left\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">I'm a bit stuck with Artifact creation. I just started running my first 3e campaign and I am not yet fully up to speed on the system and artifacts.<br /> <br /> Any help is greatly appreciated. Perhaps Artifact 4 would be easier?<br /> <br /> This is the second draft after a little thought. I do want to avoid being too cheesy, but also have to try and deliver what the player thinks is cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Devastating Rain (Orichalcum Siege Crossbow ***)</b><br /> <br /> Devastating Rain is an exquisite Orichalcum Siege Crossbow with a single Hearthstone socket on the top of the stock above the firing trigger.<br /> <br /> The Solar General Imperious Sage of Conquest is rumoured to have used this powerful weapon in the youthful campaigns of his first few centuries. With Devastating Rain the Imperious Sage supported his Circle mates and troops from points of tactical advantages, directing the movements of battle while laying down covering fire, destroying fortifications and blasting breach points in the defences of their enemies.<br /> <br /> It is said that those that Devastating Rain was so moved by the love and concern the Imperious Sage felt for his Circle mates and those men and women that served under him that she altered herself to better serve Imperious Sage in his need to protect and support those he went into battle with.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Devastating Rain</b><br /> Solars who attune to Devastating Rain for +1 mote cause onslaught penalties of -2 instead of -1 when attacking with Devastating Rain.<br /> <br /> <b>Golden Hail</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Withering-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> <br /> The bolts loosed by Devastating Rain fall amongst their targets like thunderbolts from heaven, and even those that do not find flesh make enemies flinch as they pulverise stone to dust, smash wood to splinters and punch through metal as if it were paper. Targets of this Golden Hail don\u2019t dare stick their head out of cover, often overrun by the infantry charge they never saw coming.<br /> <br /> In the event of a successful Withering attack the user may elect to pass the benefit of the Initiative damage to an ally. The ally must have been within short range of the target of the attack. If the attack causes Initiative Crash the user may pass the benefit of Initiative Break to the ally as well.<br /> <br /> The If the users ally does not use an attack action against the target of the users initial attack on their next turn then the effects of the attack, including all Initiative damage and gain are negated.<br /> <br /> <b>Shieldwall Transformation</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>- <b>Mins: </b>Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b><br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Golden Hail<br /> <br /> When an Exalt has acquired a sufficiently deep understanding and bond with Devastating Rain the artefact will trigger a change in itself. The stock will elongate and a reservoir for bolts will appear on the underside of the weapon and a second set of arms appear beneath the first. An ingenious mechanism for loading and firing Devastating Rain significantly improves the efficiency of operation.<br /> <br /> Devastating Rain now fires and reloads quickly losing the Slow tag.<br /> <br /> <b>Sunburst Detonation</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m; 1wp <b>Mins: </b>Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b><br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Shieldwall Transformation<br /> <br /> Devastating Rain draws power from its exalt users Anima generating a massive charge of essence that sparks and crackles around the weapon. When unleashed the enhanced bolts strike with terrifying power and the resulting explosion of Essence is incredibly destructive.<br /> <br /> This evocation is used to perform a demolition feat of strength as a ranged attack. This evocation is only useful for destroying obstacles and physical objects. The feat of strength is resolved using a dicepool of (Dexterity + Archery + Essence).<br /> <br /> Additionally, the explosion will create an Environmental Hazard for any character at Close Range. The hazard manifests as a bonfire (p236) but occurs instantly and therefore has no Interval.<br /> </td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12751,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12751-wizball","user":"Wizball","date":". 12-29-2016, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12751-wizball","name":"Wizball","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12751_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T13:23:08-08:00","id":1023400,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12751-wizball\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12751_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12751\" data-vbnamecard=\"12751\">Wizball</a> , I'll give feedback later on individual evocations, but overall your 3 dot artifact's evocations are already much much too powerful to be 3 dot, and are absurdly cheap. Look at something like Spring Razor or Shining Ice Mirror or Moonlit Huntress. Your Evocations are already stronger than Orichalcum Hunting Hawk (4 dot) and are approaching Volcano Cutter.<br /> <br /> Broadly, it's hard to give feedback or suggestions when we don't know the story behind the weapon, or its legend, which is kind of key to evocations in 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T13:51:04-08:00","id":1023414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PraxisCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1023400#post1023400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12751-wizball\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12751_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12751\" data-vbnamecard=\"12751\">Wizball</a> ,overall your 3 dot artifact's evocations are already much much too powerful to be 3 dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cheers! Removed some stuff<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12751-wizball","name":"Wizball","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12751_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T18:24:11-08:00","id":1023526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wizball</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1023385#post1023385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Golden Hail</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Uniform<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None</div> </div> </div> </div>Uniform is not a valid type, it is a keyword, and it is incompatible with Decisive-Only.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T03:58:17-08:00","id":1023659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1023526#post1023526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uniform is not a valid type, it is a keyword, and it is incompatible with Decisive-Only.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you. I noticed some other issues and had a re think about some of the Evocations. I will edit the original post with the new version.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12751-wizball","name":"Wizball","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12751_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T20:57:44-08:00","id":1025699,"title":"","content":"This is a huge thread, and I only read a handful of the Artifacts, but seems groovy quality to my virgin eyes, any help or advice on how to use this thread as a catalogue? I mean do I need to skim, does anyone have suggestions that they took from this thread that they really enjoyed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T08:24:59-08:00","id":1025952,"title":"","content":"I think I've found that evocations are the most... well <i>evocative </i>when they aren't straight-up hit-number boosters. Evocations work best when they change the way you approach combat and don't just make you do the same thing you were already doing but better. It should encourage different or even riskier gameplay, with the benefit of bonuses when you do. Evocations should work with each other and build off of each other, but ALSO remain useful when used individually. And finally, Artifacts are the most interesting when they're weird and not swords (I'm super biased on this point).<br /> <br /> Sadly, I agree that a first timer would have a lot of trouble navigating this thread for the first time at the length it's gotten. There's a lot of great stuff here, but condensing it all down to even a 2 hour parse with any hope of comprehension is unreasonable. Some folks have put their own artifacts in separate threads (I put mine on a website, linked in my sig) to sort through. But obviously, this thread has the highest concentration of feedback and constructive thoughts. I suppose I'd say that the first 8-10 pages probably had some of MY favorite feedback. No knock to later folks, but I stopped participating a bit after that, so can't comment strongly on it.<br /> <br /> Good luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T23:20:28-08:00","id":1026352,"title":"","content":"Here is a new one - my Dawn Caste Brawler has been lugging around an unnamed set of heavy orichalcum armor for a while and in a recent battle it was severely damaged and requires repair. So we took the opportunity to give it a bit of personality and below is the result.<br /> <br /> Sorry about the formatting, I'm posting from my phone and the clean up I normally do is agonisingly dofficult. I'll come back in a few hours and fix it up.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Radiant Halo of Incandescent Might (Orichalcum Full Plate \u2022 \u2022 \u2022 )</b></u><br /> Once belonging to the supreme ruler of Hollow and all its surrounds, Radiant Halo of Incandescent Might is a full set of articulated orichalcum plate armor, complete with helmet, greaves, gauntlets and pauldrons. Its aesthetic follows the personal banner of its first owner, the Prime and Prideful Lion, emblazoned with the Dawn Anima Caste Mark across its torso and back, the pauldrons are roaring lions and each joint stylized to mimic the rustling fur of a lion's mane. The helmet itself is another great lion head, it's jaw wide open in regal command to frame the face of its wearer with the sharpened golden teeth of its maw. Padding the armor is treated yeddim-hide leather and soft cottons and silks to let the set breathe around its wearer. A single hearthstone socket resides in the front chest-plate within the center of the golden emblem embossed on its surface.<br /> <br /> The set was designed, forged and ensorcelled by an Earth Aspected artisan in Pride's court, though the elderly dragonblood would have gladly worked such a piece for free, she was in fact commissioned by a lover of Pride's who saw that the Might and majesty that she was so infatuated with was not seen with equal eyes amongst his peers. The Lion lacked social grace, as was his remit but careless arrogance could breed rebellion and she wished for a piece that would show the world how she felt and bring to them the dawning light of understanding. Unfortunately for the lover, the work was such a great work of artisanship and beauty that she could not resist embracing its plates as she has embraced her great love even before the process had completed, the orichalcum still white hot incinerated her immediately upon contact. Pride did not notice her absence, but he wore the armor occasionally.<br /> <br /> <i>A Solar who attunes to Radiant Halo of Incandescent Might with an extra 3m gains two non-charm bonus dice on all inspire, persuade and instill actions that create or exploit positive ties to the Solar.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Glorious Mane of the Solari Prime</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple <br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite <br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> Drawing down the brilliant and iconic display of their Anima, the solar infuses Radiant Halo of Incandescent Might with the majesty of their totem, storing the 3a inside the plates of its armor which glow as brilliantly as the iconic display itself for the duration of this evocation - this makes stealth impossible and can be seen for miles as if the Solar were still at maximum Anima. Each level of Anima stored in the armor this way raises the effective appearance of the attuned Solar by one when comparing against the resolve of targets to their social actions. The solar can reflexively end the commitment to this evocation, immediately flushing his Anima with all remaining levels stored within. The armor may hold a maximum of 3a in this way.<br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> This Evocation is unlocked at no cost at the time of attunement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Roaring Decree of the Almighty King</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1a; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Glorius Mane of the Solari Prime<br /> When the true king commands it, fealty takes the heart of even the coldest souls. By paying the cost and shedding one level of Anima, either from his own banner or a point stored in the armor, the solar may increase the willpower cost of resisting their social influence by one. Additionally, if the target cannot pay the cost to resist an instill effect supplemented by this evocation, the resulting intimacy may not be eroded until the end of the story. Used to supplement a persuade action, the Solar may treat the targeted intimacy as one level higher in relation to determining the limits their subject will be willing to go to complete the command. However, targeting a defining intimacy has no additional effect.<br /> <i>Clarification: This Evocation lacks the Stackable Keyword and can only be used once per social influence attempt</i><br /> <br /> <b>Subjugating Writ of the Lion's Paw</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 2a; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Roaring Decree of the Almighty King<br /> The mighty blow from a King of Kings lays low the defiance of nations, asserting their dominance in both austerity and power. This evocation may supplement any <b>withering</b> attack action, using its successes as a bonus social action to instill a tie of awe or respect towards the solar. If such an intimacy already exists and the effect is not resisted, the intimacy is automatically upgraded one level of strength without needing to target a second supporting intimacy. The Anima cost for this evocation may only be paid from the levels stored within the armor itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Manifest Stance of Prideful Repudiation</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 3a; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Subjugating Writ of the Lion's Paw<br /> Swathed in the regalia of their own divine right to rule and command, no king is subject to any other and may dismiss such trivial contention by burning the glory of their true self into the eyes of their detractors. This evocation may be activated in response to any attempt at social influence targeting the solar, creating a contested roll using the solar's [Appearance + Presence + Essence] as a dice pool. Success negates the influence immediately as if it had failed to surpass the target's resolve. Additionally, if the social influence targets a group the solar is part of, this evocation extends its protection to all targets, refunding any costs to resist the same social influence already paid and automatically instilling such protected characters with a tie of gratitude towards the solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":2721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","user":"Elkovash","date":". 01-11-2017, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T23:22:14-08:00","id":1027469,"title":"","content":"I figure that now that i'm trying to be more active on the forums, i'll drop something I made a while back. I don't really have a backstory for it, but the idea was to use it with Single Point to focus on a much more aggressive playstyle.<br /> <b>Fulminating Luster: Blue Jade Reaper Daiklave (Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /><br /> Touchstones: Lightning, Swift, Charging<br /> <br /> New Cost: Blade Anima = ba<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement: </b>The wielder of Fulminating Luster is attuned to the flows of air essence throughout Creation, allowing them to more easily understand the concept of lightning and speed through it. This allows the wielder to easily correct mistakes in their strike, even as it is occurring. A Solar or Dragonblood attuned to Fulminating Luster who pays two extra motes to attune may reroll two unsuccessful dice on a withering or decisive attack roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Gathering Storm Invocation<br /> Cost: </b>2m;<br /> <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> Perfecting the flows of lightning essence within the blade, the wielder strikes with Fulminating Luster, beginning to gather up the excess essence and power in the air. Each strike more powerful than the last, the sword begins to glow with a blue aura. This is a passive effect tracked like anima levels an exalt would have. Each time the wielder is subject to an attack, they can pay 2m to clash the attack with one of their own. Success on this clash deals no damage, but instead will add 1 point of charge to the blade, to a maximum of 3. At the first level there is merely a feeling of electrical charge in the air, and a faint blue glow that emanates from the blade. At the second the blue aura is much more defined, flowing off the blade and lightning seems to occasionally leap from the blade. At its brightest the blade shines, and lightning flows up and down it, leaping and dancing through the air. Each level of \u2018anima\u2019 the blade retains, converts 1 die of post soak damage of a withering attack to an automatic success, at 3 levels of \u2018anima\u2019 this converts one die on a decisive attack to an automatic success.<br /> <br /> <b>Sating the Storm<br /> Cost: </b>3m, 1ba;<br /> <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Dual<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Gathering Storm Invocation<br /> Waiting for the opportune moment to unleash the perfect strike is practical, but sometimes unnecessary, the wielder of Fulminating Luster knows this well. For 3 motes, this evocation can be used to drain a level of charge, allowing the wielder to discharge it into their target. This adds 3 or Essence dice, whichever is higher, of additional damage to a withering attack, or (essence/2 minimum 1) to the raw damage of a decisive attack. Only one level of charge may be discharged this way per attack, and if this evocation is used, the wielder does not gain a charge from the attack. This effect stacks with the effect of the remaining levels of blade anima.<br /> <br /> <b>Lightning Surge<br /> Cost: </b>5m, 2ba;<br /> <b>Mins: </b>Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Power Draining Strike<br /> Unleashing a wreath of shocking electricity the wielder strikes with Fulminating Luster, bathing their enemy in the wrath of the storm. This supplements a decisive attack, burning away 2 levels of blade anima, this adds (Essence) additional damage on a decisive attack and converts 1 dice to and automatic success for every 4 dice to be rolled, rounded down. Further, every 3 levels of damage dealt inflicts a stacking -1 penalty to the opponents actions for the next 3 rounds after.<br /> <br /> <b>Crashing Lightning Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>10m, 1wp, 3ba;<br /> <b>Mins: </b>Essence 4<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Lightning Surge<br /> Sheathing the blade and concentrating their essence through its overwhelming aura, the user draws and strikes in a single instant with a wave of electrical fury, an afterimage of crackling energy immediately strikes from a mirroring angle in the same instant. This evocation supplements a decisive attack made on an opponent. It attacks the opponent twice before initiative resets and copies all charms used in the original strike, following all the same steps to do so. This attack can only be used once per day, as the blade needs time to rekindle its full power after using it.<br /> <br /> <b>This final evocation is one that didn't quite fit the thematics of the weapon beyond being lighting. It's incredibly busted and would almost certainly qualify this blade as an Artifact 5 on its own. I consider it not cannon, but a neat thing you could add to it.<br /> <br /> Rampaging Dragon Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>15m, 1wp, 3ba, 3a;<br /> <b>Mins: </b>Essence 5<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> Though the blade was made famous for its synergy with the Single Point style of martial arts, it was also feared for its greatest power, not seen in creation since it was lost. Holding the blade level, the wielder sweeps the blade across, shedding its considerable stored power, and doubling, then redoubling its power with their own. Clouds appear as if from nowhere as the sky darkens, columns of lightning sweep upwards from the air where the blade shed its power and constant crashing of thunder explodes out from in front of the user. This is a special decisive attack that strikes everything within a short range band wide and medium range outward. The attack is rolled with either Dex + Melee + Essence, or Dex + Martial Arts (Single Point) + Essence, and has a raw damage of (Wielders initiative + Current temporary willpower + extra successes). This attack cannot be dodged or parried, however a successful disengage maneuver at a difficulty of the wielders essence allows it to count as dodged. Battlegroups are especially weak to this attack and take a -2 to their defense, and add extra dice equal to the wielders essence if they are a mortal army not protected by magic. Once per story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I make martial arts sometimes they're in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1026355-momo-s-scroll-of-mixed-martial-arts\" target=\"_blank\">Scroll of Mixed Martial Arts</a>.<br /> I also made an entire 3rd circle and her <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pQyoFEWTsTss1yrPSmC1-Doj1r3i5Om6JcNFjjiud1I/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">soul structure</a>.<br /> My repository of random media rip offs, from Anime to book series. Mostly Anime. It's all in my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ISpN9ktMe3ahX06HWdAidg33u8XdEo1Rxamv7i3gij0/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Manuscript of Merry Mischief.</a><br /> Total weeb.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12830-momoyo-is-best-girl","name":"Momoyo is Best Girl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T19:49:37-08:00","id":1029436,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone. New Storyteller here with a few fresh creations for you all to tear apart due to my inability to think around my players ability to creatively destroy anything I throw there way! All kidding(?) aside, I would like to get some feed back on these artifacts, beyond the Storyteller of the game I am a player in. So lets get into shall we?<br /> <br /> This first one is aimed to be a re-creation of the weapon of Sun Wukong from The Journey to the West, as the player in question wanted to try and re-create the Monkey King as a Solar.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Compliant Golden-Hooped Rod </i></b>(***** dot) Red Jade/Orichalcum Wrackstaff [p.596]<br /> Attunement Cost: 5m (3m)<br /> Hearthstone slots: 2<br /> <br /> Story:<br /> No one is sure where this weapon originated. No one is sure who created it, or gave it such powers. Some say that it was once a grand pillar that held up the dome of the great palace, where the divine play their unending games. Others claim that it was the smallest needle of sunlight to grace creation, and the adoration of all those who witnessed it gave it the will and power to become something greater. The only thing that is known for sure is that it is as much a weapon as it is a companion, and savoir.<br /> In the first age, it was wielded by a Solar whose name has been lost to time, but he, with his Lunar mate, traveled the whole of creation, making a great pilgrimage from the farthest edges of the East to the greatest islands of the West. During their travels, they aided all who would seek help, more so at the Lunars behest than the Solar\u2019s kind heart. Legends would have been told, and ballads sang of these great Exalted\u2019s deeds, had it not all been lost during the Usurpation. And in that time of anguish, so to was lost this miraculous rod...<br /> <br /> Evocations:<br /> Exalts who attune to this artifact gain an innate understanding of the weapons dimensions including length, width, weight, and so forth. The exalt does not need to make any specific checks to determine if size altering evocations may backfire in any conceivable way. For an additional attunement cost, the artifact can always support the attuned exalt, regardless of its present dimensions.<br /> <br /> <b>The Grandest Needle</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant/Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> What better weapon could there be than one that is always there, whether or not it can be seen? This evocation allows the artifact to shrink to the size of a needle, primarily, for storage purposes. At this size the artifact is considered attuned at all times and cannot be lost or stolen by conventional means. Should attunement be broken, or the exalt enter the <u>Glowing</u> anima level, the artifact will return to its original size to aid it\u2019s exalt. The motes spent on this evocation are considered committed until released. Should this evocation be used mid-combat, the exalt must take a <u>Draw/Ready Weapon</u> action when the artifact returns to original size.<br /> <br /> <b>Titanic Mass</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> The exalt knows the true weight of his weapon is measured is deeds and actions, the weightiest of materials. On a decisive attack, the exalt can call on the full weight of the artifact, adding the tag effects for <u>Smashing</u>, and <u>Lethal</u>. Should a successful attack deal at least 3 Health Levels of damage, the target is knocked back a range band, taking falling damage should they impact walls, floors, ceilings, are so for. The distance of this knock back is determined by an Strength + Melee check, against the opponents Athletics + Stamina. Every 3 success in the exalts favor increases the number of range bands the defender is knocked back.<br /> <br /> <b>Reach Unto the Heavens</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m per increment / 1m per round <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant/Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> Let them big there spears and rid atop their horses, for only there greatest of archers could compare with this reach! The artifact extends, lengthwise, and may remain in this state for a cost. Per the payment of a beginning mote cost, the artifact grows by an increment of arbitrary length. These increments are determined by the exalts essence level, whereas each essence level acts as a multiplier. For example, at Essence 1, there will be no change in length while at essence 2, the artifacts length is doubled. Once lengthened, the exalt must pay a mote per round for the artifact to remain at this increased size. In combat, the artifact at double its original size may make attacks on those in the next range band out, given that the exalt pays 2 initiative to attempt and sacrifices 2 defense until their next turn. Any larger sizes become too unwieldy, even for the attuned exalt, to use properly.<br /> <br /> <b>So Shall the Mountains Bow</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> The Grandest Needle, Titanic Mass<br /> How better can one serve than to change when ordered? So how better can one change than to become what one is not? This evocation allows the artifact to change in its entirety. The inners of the staff break open to reveal golden chains within. This changes the artifact from a Wrackstaff to a Serpent-Sting Staff; gaining new tags (refer to page 596). In this form however, the artifact can still be considered a melee weapon, and it is up to the exalt to choose between the melee or martial art tags for attack calculations. In this form, the exalt may still use the Titanic Mass evocation, but losses access to The Grandest Needle and Reach Unto the Heavens. The cost must be payed again to revert the weapon back to staff form mid-fight, but the artifact will return to its original form at the end of the scene, of sunset, whichever occurs first.<br /> <br /> <b>Pillar of Creation</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp (5m) <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Reach Unto the Heavens, So Shall the Mountains Bow<br /> <br /> \u201cIn my master\u2019s hands, I shall prop up the sky. Alike, I shall hold him firm in his time of need.\u201d - <i>Compliant Golden-Hooped Rod</i><br /> <br /> For the scene used, the exalt is infused with the same great magic as that of his artifact. His body, mind, and soul alike become flexible and easily mending. For this scene, the exalt may take advantage of the <u>Pain Tolerance</u> merit, regardless of if they have purchased it prior. They also enjoy a number of additional die to Athletics checks equal to the number of Health Levels/3 (round down). The Exalt also does not suffer broken, dislocated, crippled or otherwise damaged bones, not matter the damage done to them. Limbs can still be lost. Finally, should the exalt be at Bonfire/Iconic anima levels with this evocation active, for the payment of an additional 5 motes, Titanic Mass is able to open chasms in the ground where it strikes. These chasms are considered to be a long range fall.<br /> <br /> __________________________________<br /> <br /> This second one was for the stereotypical viking from the north type character. I am presently trying to tie it to a forgotten god of Ice and Burial Ceremonies at the moment, so the lore can be considered place holder, and the stronger charms are intentional made with this gods champion or exalt in mind. There is the thought of giving it a paired shield at the moment as well.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Grace of the Glacier </i></b>(**** dot) Blue/Black Jade Grand Grimcleaver [p.597]<br /> Attunement Cost: 5m<br /> Hearthstone slots: 2<br /> <br /> Story:<br /> None truly know who or what crafted this massive double headed axe, but all who have laid eyes upon it know it to be an object of cold beauty, not unlike the peace felt in the presence of the final breath\u2026 but not a force of destruction.<br /> A grand axe, long as a man is tall, with its blades as broad across. Perhaps oddest is the blade itself, as they could be likened to the wings of a raven, waiting for the chance to be spread wide in flight. The blade itself is crafted neigh entirely of Blue Jade, a rare shade at that, which shone like cold freshly, formed ice. The shaft of the axe and much of the iconography is done in Black Jade, and depicts images of great mountains and the slow movement of mighty glaciers across the land. Oddly, there are semi-circular patterns where \u201cwings\u201d of the blade meet with the main body. No explanation has ever been formed for these portions, though it is believed to be for the placement of items of power.<br /> There is a surprising amount of storytelling related to this grand blade, though there is little history to speak of. It is said that great warriors who once held this weapon could split the earth and rise raise walls of fridge cold, and gladly did they do so against those that would threaten their lands, homes, and people. But all who wielded the weapon in such a way were said to fall to the ice in the end, where only the carrion birds might know of their resting place. There is word that death is bound close to this blade, bound deep into its wielder, and that those who lack respect for the deceased will suffer a fate to never truly find peace, no matter the rites that follow their body. The last warrior to hold the weapon was said to have spent his final years beneath the earth, close to the blades birth place, believing that this might break the cycle or curse that clings to the blade. It has not seen the light of the sun, moon, or stars since\u2026 but the ice is patient.<br /> <br /> Evocations:<br /> Solars or Terrestrials attuned to <i>Grace of the Glacier</i> automatically gain access to the \u201cMajesty of the Tundra\u201d evocation.<br /> <br /> <b>Majesty of the Tundra</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -<br /> <b>Type: </b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> To wield something so wondrous mean that its wielder to is worthy of pause and praise. So long as an exalt remains attuned to <i>Grace of the Glacier</i>, they put off a majestic aura, not unlike a great beast of the wilds. The Exalt gains 2 automatic non-Charm success to Threaten and Appearance based checks, but suffers the loss of 2 dice to all stealth checks while attuned.<br /> <br /> <b>Incased in Wonder</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m or 4m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant/Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> How durable is the flesh? How durable is the ice? In tandem can they work to endure greater wraths. The wielder may pay to form an outer layer of essence that encases their flesh in a sheet of cold armor. For 2 motes this increases the exalts soak by 4 against a single attack per round. For 4 motes, this increases the exalts soak for an entire scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Weight of the Ages</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m, 5i <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Counterattack, Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> The ice will crush all given the time. Let them come, for the cold can wait. This attack requires the wielder to be attacked and to have neither acted nor moved during combat this round, in addition to successfully dodged the oncoming attack. The exalts turn will be consumed on use, but this decisive attack cannot be parried. At the payment of 5 initiative, this attack also cannot be dodged. Hardness still applies.<br /> <br /> <b>Grasp of the North</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -(4m) <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Incased in Wonder<br /> The wind blows, the cold grows, the ice encases all\u2026 but it does not treat all equally. Purchasing this evocation improves the prerequisite, extending its affect to decisive attacks as well as withering. This means that hardness against successful attacks is increased by 4, similar to soak.<br /> Activating this evocation for 4 motes however, allows the user to deal a reflexive counterattack to any enemy that successfully strikes the exalt for the remainder of the scene. This counterattack comes in the form of an outreach of grasping ice, leaping from the exalts frozen essence. This counterattack automatically hits the opponent, ignoring defenses, and reduces the opponent\u2019s initiative by 3. This can crash an enemy.<br /> One can only counterattack the same number of times as their essence level, and counterattacks are automatic. Once all counterattacks are used up, this evocation and its prerequisite deactivate and cannot be used for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Wonder Given Flight<br /> Cost: </b>6m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Weight of the Ages, Grasp of the North<br /> This is the moment of ultimate beauty. <i>Grace of the Glacier</i> opens its wings outward, letting loose an aura of ultimate cold. The clear, cold wonder of the ice can now be shared. This decisive attack reduces the targets defenses by the users essence/2 (rounded up), and when used to successfully deal damage to the opponents health levels, the opponent will only have their respective essence rating plus stamina rounds before they are incased in ice.<br /> Freezing individuals suffer negatives based off the number of rounds spent freezing. This is a -1 at 1-2 rounds, -2 at 3-4 rounds, -3 at 5-6 rounds, and -4 at 7 rounds onward. Should the frozen target be damaged to severely (this is up to Storyteller interpretation, or the loss of 3 health levels, whichever is preferred) they will shatter, killing them. The frozen individual is considered to be in suspended animation while frozen and does not witness events going around them or suffer the progress of time. They will thaw out in a full days\u2019 time, given no outside influence to speed or slow the process. An individual frozen in this way more than twice must be unfrozen via sorcerous means, else they will remain in a statue like state permanently, or until shattered.<br /> <br /> _____________________________<br /> <br /> These next two have a story that gives them a connected origin. They were an attempt to create artifacts based off songs from the musical version of The Count of Monte Cristo, specifically the songs &quot;A Story Told&quot; and &quot;Hell to Your Doorstep&quot; and I have hopes to be able to give the rest of the song track a similar treatment.<br /> <br /> <b>A Story Told</b> (**** dot) Orichalcum and Starmetal Short Powerbow [p.598]<br /> Attunement Cost: 5m<br /> Hearthstone slots: 2<br /> Story:<br /> It is said this was one of the final creations of an Exalted craftsman of incredible skill and talent alike. The design of care of the creation speak of its creators skill and dedication to their craft, from the flexible and perfectly curved Orichalcum, to the intricate and elaborate Starmetal filigree that decorates the length of the bow. It is truly a work of art, and a pitying piece to ever see used as a weapon.<br /> Legend says that long ago a dispute was held among four colleges, each one of them counting among the Exalted. Three of them believed that that the purest among them, the most radiant of the four, had slighted them all in some way and all three wished to find a way to gain their shared vengeance. Rather than have their revenge in blood and violence, they would have it in wealth, prestige, and status\u2026 but that is by far a harder won victory. However, when few to none of their colleagues and charges would believe the claims they brought against their compatriot, they turned to the greatest craftsman in the land, asking him to create a work that would reveal the truth of the matter. In his eagerness to create such a unique work, he agreed\u2026 only to find that night after night as he labored away on his craft, the three would approach in kind, each offering incentive to twist the nature of his creation. Be it money, status, pleasures of countless natures, or even blackmail they all approached and offered until far more desperate measures were taken. The three saw to the kidnapping and imprisonment of the artisans\u2019 only living relations, his dear daughter. With the life of his only child hanging in the balance, the work was completed with its new twisted purpose, and though the artisan regained his child, he in turn lost a very close friend to lies told by his own creation. As for the tale of this wronged Exalt and his former friends\u2026 the ending of this tale has been lost to the ages.<br /> <br /> Evocations:<br /> When attuned to this artifact, an exalt gains a +1 to all Bureaucracy, Larceny, and Socialize actions. An exalt also must pay an extra dot willpower to lower the intensity of negative intimacies when the opportunity arises. Positive intimacies also can only be gained at a lower intensity level than they normal would apply.<br /> <br /> <b>We Are Friends</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWe are friends, are we not? And our interests are the same\u2026We\u2019ll collaborate, and trust in fate to parcel out the blame\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Keep your friends close, and your enemies closer\u2026 surround yourself with foes and let your friends fall for you. For the scene, the exalt may add their essence level in automatic successes to any social actions make against someone they have an outwardly positive intimacy with (this intimacy can be negative, but the exalt must have maintained the guise of an amiable relationship with the target). This evocation may still take effect should the target have a positive intimacy towards the exalt, while the exalt lacks an intimacy towards the target.<br /> <br /> <b>Middle of the Night</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m or 1wp <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWho\u2019s going to question what goes on in the middle of the night? Not a tinker, not a tailor, not their parents, not their partners, nor a jailer!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> A crafty mortal knows that men and gods alike care not about the acts that happen out of sight and out of mind. With a stubble honeyed word, the exchange of ill-gotten coin, or a promise to never be kept the exalt needs not sneak for those that would watch as they conveniently\u2026 forgot about their presence. An exalt may add their choice of Bureaucracy, Larceny, or Socialize non-charm die to stealth checks. For an alternative payment option, the exalt may add their Stealth in non-charm die to social actions to convince others to forget about encountering them.<br /> <br /> <b>The Softest Things</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Middle of the Night<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWhere the softest things he\u2019ll touch are stones and darkness\u2026 Deep in a craggy isle and dungeons keep!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The most comforting thing one will ever experience is a mother\u2019s embrace, and the warm glow of life that comes just before the icy grip of death. So long as the target is not within close range of the exalt, the exalt has an unbroken line of sight with their target, and the target is neither mounted nor grappled; paying this cost creates an <i>ambush </i>attack (p.203). This evocation can only be used on a specific target once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>It\u2019s Him or Me</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1wp <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> We Are Friends<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cBut I can see it\u2019s him or me! / Let him sit there and rot till he\u2019s forgot!</i><br /> <b><i>LET HIM ROT!</i></b><i>\u201d</i><br /> <br /> When faced with an obstacle you must run from, you need not be the fastest\u2026 only faster than you friends. For the cost an exalt may make a gambit to force an ally at close range take the impact of an attack. This is a contested (Strength + Athletics) against the targets (Dexterity + Awareness). Should the target have a useable intimacy towards the exalt, this counts as a social action and uses (Charisma + Socialize) instead.<br /> <br /> <b>History is a Story</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> The Softest Things<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cHistory is a story told by the winners of the fight! / History is a story told by the men who make the laws! / History is the story told by the people who survive!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> History is written by many authors. But every story written has an editor to\u2026 fix, the writer\u2019s mistakes. With this an exalt becomes that editor. Forming an arrow of invisible essence the exalt makes an attack action that, when successful, creates the opportunity to change the memories of the target as an instill, persuade, or inspire action. The exalt makes an (Manipulation + Presence) check against the targets Resolve. The target cannot use their intimacies to change their Resolve, or use Willpower unless the influence threatens one of their intimacies. Should the exalt be successful, the effect in instantaneous and cannot be undone via mundane means.<br /> <br /> <b>End the Story</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> It\u2019s Him or Me, History is a Story<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cSo goes this story! / Stick to the story! / Here ends the story!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The story ends when there is no one left to tell it. End the story. The exalt makes a decisive attack that cannot be improved with the use of charms, on a target they have a major or greater intimacy with or the knowledge that the target has an intimacy of major or greater towards the exalt. Should this attack successfully deal damage, the target has their fate temporarily re-written. The next decisive attack that would deal damage to the target will kill them, despite the remaining health levels. The target must crash, incapacitate, reach extreme range in distance from the exalt that used this evocation, or simply avoid being struck for 5 rounds to negate the effect of this evocation. This evocation can only be used on a target once per story, and is both easily noticeable and traceable by the watchers of Heaven.<br /> <br /> __________<br /> <br /> Sort of the same as above, just a paired artifact version.<br /> <br /> <b>Hellfire &amp; Damnation</b> (*** dot each) Red Jade &amp; Soulsteel paired Reaper Daiklaves<br /> Attunement Cost: 5m [5 motes per weapon, or 5 total when wielding both]<br /> Hearthstone slots: 2 [1 each]<br /> Story:<br /> It is said that these were the final creations of one of the most skilled and talent Exalted to ever work magical materials. However, unlike all of their countless other works, these blades shown clear signs of haste in their making; as though the craftsman was under much pressure to finish this piece. The cutting blades are curved and tapered to create cruel edges to cause as much pain as possible in a single cut. There is little decoration along the length of the blades, beyond the simple flame patterns beaten into the metal. Oddest still, both blades are naked, having no metal or wood to protect the hand from the bare metal of the blade. To hold these is to hold an unfinished piece of art.<br /> Tales say that the creation of these blades came from a wronged Solar. Betrayed by all the ones he had trusted, he let his wrath consume him, his lust for revenge becoming his sole sustenance in his faraway prison. The day he was finally let free, he sought out the greatest craftsman he knew to make him the tools needed to exact his vengeance. Where this Solar obtained a wicked metal like Soulsteel remains a mystery even to the worker of the steel, but the craftsman agreed to forge the Solar his blades. It was only when the blades were near completion that the Solar asked why the craftsman would aid him so. The craftsman admitted in that moment that a piece of his own work had been used against the Solar\u2026 From that day onward legend tell us not what became of these two, but many believe that the two slayed each other, the craftsman defending himself from the Solar\u2019s rage. All that is known is that the blades were never truly finished\u2026<br /> <br /> Attunements:<br /> When attuned together, the artifacts share the burden placed on the exalt, lessening the normal attunement cost by half of the normal amount. Attuning to Hellfire grants the wielder automatic access to the evocation Ignite the Pyre. Attuning to Damnation imposes a difficulty increase of 2 on all social rolls.<br /> <br /> Evocations (Hellfire):<br /> <br /> <b>Ignite the Pyre</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m per every 2 charges <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 round per charge<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cFirst there\u2019s retribution I must prepare.</i><br /> <i>Mighty vengeance is mine!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Fire can fuel the greatest of feats. Let the fire burn within you, bright and furious, to burn away those that have wronged you. The exalt pays the cost to generate and store a number of charges. So long as the exalt holds a pool of these charges, they gain a +1 to melee and all melee related abilities. These charges will be consumed, 1 per round, if they are not used to fuel a different evocation. The exalt may not use Ignite the Pyre again so long as there is are any charges remaining within their pool. The exalt generates the greater of 6 or Essence*2 charges at most, and can store no more than 20 charges at most.<br /> <br /> <b>Drag them to Hell</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1-3 charges <b>Mins: </b>Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Ignite the Pyre<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cOnce you\u2019re in my shining cathedral heed the tolling bell.</i><br /> <i>It\u2019s the final sound you hear as you descend to hell!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> They made you see hell on earth\u2026 you\u2019ll make them see worse. The exalt makes an attack on the target, and when successful, reduces the targets initiative by the number of charges spent on the action. This cannot crash an opponent and does raise the exalts initiative.<br /> <br /> Evocations (Damnation):<br /> <br /> <b>Shatter the Heart</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -(2m) <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cAnd love is a lie! Swearing that no matter what it won\u2019t die\u2026</i><br /> <i>Disappearing like a star in the sky,</i><br /> <i>In the hot light of morning.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> You have been wronged, by friend and love alike. What do you have for a heart now? The exalt may pay an initial cost to sacrifice a positive relationship intimacy, and gaining an intimacy of revenge of equal intensity. The exalt does not suffer penalties to Resolve when these new intimacies are applied, and all Resolve bonuses using these intimacies gain a +1 in addition to the value granted by intensity. Multiple intimacies can be affected this way, and they do not revert when no longer attuned to the artifact.<br /> <br /> <b>Revenge Served Ablaze</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m, 2 charges <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Shatter the Heart<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cWell, tables can turn as my enemies will soon enough learn\u2026</i><br /> <i>I will strike a match and then watch them burn!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Do not let your rage cool, for then it will become brittle and shatter. Let it burn bright enough to burn away all that would stand between you and your pray. The exalt lets their lust for vengeance burn into the arc of their blade. The exalt adds the intensity of any revenge based intimacy held toward the target to their attack as automatic successes. Negative intimacies can be substituted at a -1 effect comparison. If no such intimacy exists, they add 2 non-charm die to the attack roll. This evocation does not affect damage.<br /> <br /> Evocations (Paired):<br /> <br /> <b>To Your Knees</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 4 charges <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Ignite the Pyre, Shatter the Heart<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cFall down on your knees,</i><br /> <i>Fall down and let me hear you pray\u2026</i><br /> <i>Fall down on your knees,</i><br /> <i>\u2019till I can hear you bargaining, scheming, begging and screaming to me!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> What need is there for mercy? They had none for you. The exalt is able to command a very wounded (2/3<sup>rds </sup>of total health levels) or crashed opponent to prostrate before them. This is a Threaten action that is empowered by the remaining number of charges remaining in their pool, acting as non-charm die if used. Charges used this way are considered to be consumed. On success, the exalt has the freedom to force the target to obey a single command that they would reasonably be compelled to do, or attack the target as though they were crashed and have a Defense of 0. Mercy cannot be shown.<br /> <br /> <b>Bearer of Hell</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m, 3 charges (1wp) <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Ignite the Pyre, Revenge Served Ablaze<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI will carry hell to your doorstep; you will rue the day!</i><br /> <i>You will reap the hate you\u2019ve sown no matter how hard you pray\u2026 </i><br /> <i> I will carry hell to your doorstep; I will make you pay!</i><br /> <i>You will reap the hate you\u2019ve sown on my judgment day!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The exalt has become a pyre of wrath, existing only to deliver out their own version of justice on those who have sinned against them. Even should the flames consume them, they will see their mission finished. The exalt begins to generate charges at a rate of (Essence + 3) each round. The exalt also gains the ability to expend 2 charges to increase their parry by 1 once a round. This evocation can be used a second time at an increased cost of 1wp to increase the number of charges produced each round by (Essence/2, round up).<br /> <br /> <b>Blood-stained Justice </b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 10 charges <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> To Your Knees, Bearer of Hell<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cNo forgiveness, no way out\u2026</i><br /> <i>Only justice!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The moment has come. The moment of truest, long overdue justice. The exalt makes a decisive attack that cannot be dodged. Should the exalt have an intimacy of revenge towards the target, their parry is considered to be halved prior to any charm or abilities that would increase parry. On a successful hit, the exalt may add the intensity of any intimacy applied as raw damage. Should no such intimacy exist the exalts initiative resets to the greater of 4 or their remaining pool of charges.<br /> <br /> ________________<br /> <br /> I hope that this isn't to much of a content dump for my first post here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Enjoy the moment with all your might,<br /> Whether its gloomy, whether its bright.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12786-libaros","name":"Libaros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T01:59:49-08:00","id":1029969,"title":"","content":"There's a couple charms that I don't understand why they're supplemental, when instead they should be simple or reflexive. I can't decide which since I'm not good at balance but this seems like a mechanical problem to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Pillar of Creation</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp (5m) <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement </div> </div> </div>Maybe it supplements the first Athletics action they make? But I don't know any supplementals that then persist for the scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Majesty of the Tundra</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> -<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental </div> </div> </div>This type should be permanent since it's duration is &quot;while attuned&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Incased in Wonder</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m or 4m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental </div> </div> </div>If you rolled soak I could see it being supplemental but this is just a reflexive, very similar to Spirit Strengthens the Skin (but superior to it in all ways so maybe way too good).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>We Are Friends</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement </div> </div> </div>This is either reflexive or simple, providing a scenelong bonus much like Harmonious Presence Meditation<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Middle of the Night</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m or 1wp <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene </div> </div> </div>I'm not aware of ANY scene-long supplementals, but this as well doesn't fit what a supplemental should do. Again, simple or reflexive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ignite the Pyre</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m per every 2 charges <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 round per charge<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cFirst there\u2019s retribution I must prepare.</i><br /> <i>Mighty vengeance is mine!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Fire can fuel the greatest of feats. Let the fire burn within you, bright and furious, to burn away those that have wronged you. The exalt pays the cost to generate and store a number of charges. So long as the exalt holds a pool of these charges, they gain a +1 to melee and all melee related abilities. These charges will be consumed, 1 per round, if they are not used to fuel a different evocation. The exalt may not use Ignite the Pyre again so long as there is are any charges remaining within their pool. The exalt generates the greater of 6 or Essence*2 charges at most, and can store no more than 20 charges at most. </div> </div> </div>If these charges affected a single melee action then it could maybe be supplemental, but as written it's definitely reflexive or simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9018-ennuideblase","name":"EnnuiDeBlase","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T01:46:36-08:00","id":1030474,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any ideas on a direlash, that would be focused on providing climbing and swinging benefits? I am interested in an Indiana Jones / Alucard character for my next game, and was hoping someone had something already made up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T17:48:56-08:00","id":1030888,"title":"","content":"HEART EATER (Soulsteel/Moonsilver Reaver Daiklave, Artifact 3 probably) <br /> <br /> This is my first attempt at an artifact (made with Unsung's process)---well, I have two more in the works already (I had a long wait at work and it was raining very hard outside) but this is the one I finished. At least, finished my first pass on---I'm sure this will come out of the thread rather changed for the better.<br /> <br /> Image (a little large):<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i134.photobucket.com/albums/q106/Beans-tastic/heart-eater_2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Heart Eater was originally just a random reaver daiklave I made for my first homebrew Abyssal and I didn't intend to put Evocations to it. However, looking at this thread, I decided I wanted to try. Since I already named it, I thought about what Heart Eater could be a good name for, and settled on what I have here: a sword designed to facilitate hunting down and slaughtering entire families or groups of boon companions.<br /> <br /> <b>Backstory:</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Degara of the Twilight Caste was noted both as a brilliant sorcerer and a terribly strong swordsman. His Lunar bondmate was not his lover but his deepest friend, a masterful weaponsmith named Eight Shining Eyes; the spider-woman was planning on constructing Degara a wedding present in the form of a great chopping sword of orichalcum and moonsilver (perhaps that she might not be totally forgotten once he was settled in with his husband---Eight Shining Eyes was said to be a little jealous, after all). She had the moonsilver edge ready to be enfolded with sun-metal when things, as they do, went bad.<br /> <br /> Raincloud Breath, a woman of ghostly blood from a family of death-royalty, killed Degara\u2019s husband-to-be, but her gauntlets of soulsteel were wrested from her in the struggle and she had to flee before she could reclaim them. Mad with grief, Degara brought the gauntlets to Eight Shining Eyes and demanded she use this terrible metal for his sword. It could not be his wedding present, so it would be his instrument of revenge. The Lunar hesitated, but set to work reforging the strange, horrid material. Degara\u2019s brilliance came in handy, as she needed his help to unravel the necromantic processes necessary to get soulsteel to behave properly. The metal drank in his grief and fury as he stood over the smith, and she shuddered when it was done---the thing may not have been quite evil, but it was certainly rank with the taint of wretched intent.<br /> <br /> Degara killed the son Raincloud Breath sent after him, and the next two. Every time, it got easier---the sword seemingly leapt straight into their flesh to cleave and tear. When Raincloud Breath sent her children and husbands into hiding, he hunted them down. Finally he found her---he, drunk on the empty high of ten-thousand-eyes-for-an-eye; she, stripped of her family and power. When he finished cleaning her gore from the blade, he walked into the land of the dead to find his husband and never came back. Perhaps they had their union. Perhaps his husband saw what Degara had become and could not face him any more.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>ATTUNEMENT</b>: For +1 extra mote in attunement, Heart Eater allows its wielder to add one non-charm die to attack rolls (<b>withering </b>or <b>decisive</b>) against a target who the wielder has, through Read Intentions or some other means, determined to be the subject of a Tie Intimacy of love (familial, platonic, romantic, whatever), deep friendship, or true admiration. These Intimacies are hence referred to as Bonds within the context of this Artifact and its Evocations.<br /> <br /> <b>TASTING THE RED STRING</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental <br /> <b>Keywords</b>: <b>Decisive</b>-Only <br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> Heart Eater tastes, in blood and in steel, the ties that bind. It is always looking for these vulnerabilities.<br /> On landing a successful <b>decisive</b> attack or parrying a <b>decisive </b>attack (including in a Clash), the wielder may make a reflexive Read Intentions roll with the intent of discovering Bonds. Damage exceeding target Guile is added to the Read Intentions roll as dice.<br /> ((Is this too narrow? Should Withering attacks also be included?))<br /> <br /> <b>CUTTING GROOVES IN THE HEART</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m 1wp (+3m/1m); <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: <b>Decisive</b>-Only <br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Tasting the Red String<br /> Heart Eater\u2019s moonsilver edge is a living, hating thing; when it has felt the ties within somebody it makes itself ever sharper in order to tear them apart. When it snuffs out their life, it reaches in and steals the love from their heart, carefully scribing a hit list in their cooling blood.<br /> After discovering a Bond in a target, the wielder may use this to enhance a decisive attack made at 15+ Initiative. It converts damage dice to successes equal to the positive value of the highest Bond known in the target.<br /> This Evocation has a secondary effect. On a decisive attack that kills (whether enhanced by this Evocation or not), the wielder may pay 3m to absorb (number) Bonds from the target. If the primary effect of this Evocation was used to enhance the killing blow, it instead costs only 1m.<br /> <br /> <b>SCENTING TIES IN BLOOD</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 3m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Cutting Grooves in the Heart<br /> In wracking, red-tinged heartbeats of visions, Heart Eater tells its wielder where to find the next target. When it tastes them in the air, it nearly shivers to get at their flesh.<br /> Having discovered a Bond, the wielder may commit motes to this Evocation, gaining the Bond\u2019s value plus 1 in non-Charm bonus dice to all rolls to discover the location of the Bond\u2019s subject. In addition, whenever in the target's presence, they are alerted to this fact.<br /> <br /> <b>HEART EATER TRIUMPHANT</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m, 1wp; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-Only <br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Scenting Ties in Blood <br /> The satisfaction of having murdered one person drives Heart Eater to bloodthirsty glee when it is about to taste the blood of the first victim\u2019s son, lover, friend---its edge becomes a narrow sea of ripping teeth.<br /> This Evocation may be used when knowingly attacking a character who is the subject of a Bond held by someone the wielder killed with this weapon. It adds the Bond value to the damage dicepool of a decisive attack, whose damage becomes Aggravated; if the target reciprocated the Bond, the value on their end (which may or may not be the same as the Bond\u2019s value from the dead person\u2019s end) is converted to automatic successes.<br /> ((Is this too much, or too little? I really don\u2019t know. I thought it was too little, so I added the automatic success bit; if it\u2019s too much and I should only keep one of those, which should I keep?))<br /> <br /> I fully expect I've gotten half the numbers wonky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 01-14-2017, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T13:29:12-08:00","id":1031304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1030474#post1030474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any ideas on a direlash, that would be focused on providing climbing and swinging benefits? I am interested in an Indiana Jones / Alucard character for my next game, and was hoping someone had something already made up?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm interested in this too. My Direlash artifact is on page 42, but is designed for melee grappling (I could still use some more advice from any experienced artifact builders). However, I built a story-driven endpoint to the use of my weapon--see the built in betrayal mechanic--and may end up designing a new one later. If I do, it will likely be a utility weapon for movement like you've described for awesome stunts. Whips are fantastic for stunts and gambits, so a focus there will likely be the next iteration. If you find something, please link/post it here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12709-sir-dragos","name":"Sir Dragos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T22:22:36-08:00","id":1031451,"title":"","content":"Please take a look at this and give some feedback (PEACH) either here or on the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NoAWw2dg5NYUNhFOTY9XPohHU_EDb8I6I3jZAUNHe5s/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Google.doc</a><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#073763\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Phalange of Omnibu\u2019Shen</span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#741B47\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Relic Wrackstaff (Longfang or Direlance works too), Artifact (\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7)</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">This staff carved from the blackened glass finger bone of Omnibu\u2019Shen, The Keeper of Words of Power, Fallen Fetch Soul of He Who Bleeds the Unknown Word. The base of the stave is shod in starmetal etched with a single sigil of power, and capped with a pair of orchalcum prods, and a floating adamant sphere suspended between them. Though impressive as the staff is the most catching thing is the moonsilver filagree along the shaft telling a story in old realm of a clever lunar that tricked Omnibu\u2019Shen with a riddle so complex and arcane that it drove him mad in the process of solving it. When he finally solved the riddle he spoke aloud the answer, that was the moment he realized it was a trap. The answer was an inversion curse to reverse the fated outcome of the speakers next action. Some say the curse was the cause of his speech, that it twisted his essence inverting its soul hierarchy, turning every aspect of himself upon each other. </span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Those that wield the stave claim it speaks in furious screams heard as if from a great distance and offers them hallucinations from deep within it\u2019s primordial mind. Sometimes from the moment of death where all the words of power escaped from his skull at once, other times sigils, glyphs, and symbols overwhelmly poured across their vision and minds. These visions often come without warning and instill a an unspeakable rage within the wielder. However each image, word, and glyph imparts primordial power to the wielder reshaping their understanding of the foundations of creation. </span></span> <hr /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Sidebar - Thematics and Function</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Evocations of the Phalange of Omnibu\u2019Shen follow several themes including words and language, rage, madness, power, curses, deep understanding and contemplative enlightenment. The Shaping Rituals, Mysteries, and Absorptions tap into both his wisdom and insight as well as the insanity of Omnibu\u2019Shen. A few Evocations and Shaping Rituals tap into themes and concepts from He Who Bleeds the Unknown Word, as well as hint at his reincarnated as Elloge the Sphere of Speech. </span></span> <hr /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">She may spend 3 additional motes while attuning to the Omnibu\u2019shen grants 1 point of syntax on a successful withering or decisive attack. In addition she gains 1 non-charm die to all forms of silent communication, powers that depict symbols, glyphs, sigils, per tier of sorcery mastered. </span></span> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Evocations of Omnibu\u2019Shen</span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Transubstantiation of the Furious Soul</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Cost</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: 6m, 1wp; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Mins</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Type</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Keywords</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Duration</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: One Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Prerequisites</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Terrestrial Circle Sorcery</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Bleeding the unbound potential of their own exalted soul into the interface of Omnibu\u2019Shen it swells with arcane syntax. On any turn in which the Solar wields Phalange of Omnibu\u2019Shen in combat she may convert 1 point of initiative into 1 sorcerous mote, upto a maximum of her essence+1 per turn these motes are referred to as syntax(nx). If the wielder joins battle with a higher initiative than all opponents this evocation may be activated reflexively. </span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Special Activation Rules</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Rather than being bought with experience, Transubstantiation of the Furious Soul is learned after first time the wielder gains a crash break in combat. </span></span> <hr /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Sidebar - Syntax(nx)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Sorcerers wielding Omnibu\u2019Shen in combat have a number of ways of generating and storing energy into the interface, the adamant sphere capping the stave, this energy is called Syntax(nx). The staff can store up to the attuned sorcerers Intelligence + Occult in syntax a time and absorbing into the interface after a scene. Syntax can be converted into sorcerous motes reflexively on a 2:1 bases or be spent to power its evocations as a 1:1.</span></span> <hr /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Burning Sigil Strike</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Cost</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: 2m, 2nx; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Mins</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Type</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Keywords</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Uniform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Duration</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Prerequisites</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Transubstantiation of the Furios Soul</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">By channeling syntax through the core of the Phalange the sigils on the shaft burn with a brilliant crimson light pulsing at the striking plane. This evocation is activated after the attack is rolled but before damage is applied, increasing the minimum damage by the sorcerers tier of sorcerous initiation. </span></span> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Oeuvre of Inversion</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Cost</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: 4m, 4nx; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Mins</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Type</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Keywords</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Duration</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: One Scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Prerequisites</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Transubstantiation of the Furious Soul</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Blinding the shinma of separation and the principle of identity into a blurred glyph within the interface she breaks the lines of reason and comprehension to all who would act upon her. Anyone attempting to take action on the wielder or staff suffers a shaping effect that reduces their potential, lowering their maximum natural dice pools by the sorcerers tier of sorcerous initiation +1. This does not affect static numbers such as defense or resolve only rolled effects.</span></span> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Trembling Lip Curse</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Cost</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: 1nx per attack; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Mins</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Type</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Keywords</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Uniform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Duration</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Prerequisites</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">: Transubstantiation of the Furious Soul</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Her mind erupts in a cascade of forgotten pain as fragment of Omnibu\u2019Shens death curse escapes from her lips. The words explode from her throat in a horrifying death scream, allowing her to make attacks against against enemies with the stats of the Phalange removing the default accuracy bonus and adding the thrown (short) tag. </span></span> <b>Shaping Rituals</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">The relic of Omnibu\u2019Shen resonates with world shaping power. Those that attune to it and gaze into the sphere experience a terrible enlightenment as the fragment of Omnibu\u2019Shen\u2019s soul that still survives in its heart, speaks primordial words of power blasting open the doors of her soul. To the wielder, the world is redefined as an arbitrary system of of interacting symbols that she can manipulate through its syntax. These sorcerers tend to see everything in terms of symbols and communication: map and territory, call and response, rhetoric and games.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Sitting in silent contemplation of the complexity of the laws that govern creation, sorcery, and its primordial creator. Her will is eroded away as she loses herself in the endless diagrams, sigils, and equations burning a willpower, she rolls (Intelligence + Occult) gaining one syntax per success. Her caste mark acts as the sorcerers own artificial interface storing the syntax until she casts them in a spell or her anima lights up to the bonfire level. These syntax can be spent for spellcasting at 1:1. </span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Writing a sutra about Omnibu\u2019Shen and the fate of the written word the sorcerer expands the mythos of the fallen primordial soul. This takes no less than one hour and at the culmination of the ritual she consumes the writing and internalizes the story tuning the words into a prayer to herself and the staff. She rolls ((Charisma or Manipulation) + Linguistics) each success grants 1 sorcerous mote that lasts for up to a week. </span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">When the sorcerer takes the first shape sorcery action to begin casting a spell and stunts it with a description of how she casts the spell through the Phalange or draws on its power, she gains (stunt rating + 2) sorcerous motes towards completing this spell. This benefit can only be received once per scene. Stunts to enhance spells with spoken or written components do not count against the once per scene limit.</span></span> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Mysteries (Other Benefits)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Inculcate the Unknown Word Merit (\u00b7\u00b7)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">The presence of the the Phalange of Omnibu\u2019Shen inculcates an understanding of language into the wielder so deep that she may learn to communicate without words to any being that understands Old Realm. This language is a series of gestures, ticks, postures and is written into the foundation of all spiritual beings. She may teach this language to any that gaze into the interface of Omnibu\u2019Shen willingly. </span></span> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Semantics of Sorcery Merit (\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Initiates of Omnibu\u2019Shen intuitively understand the syntax of creations schinmatic underpinnings and the sorceries derived from it. By studying sorceries she may invent new words of power based on the root meaning though changing the overall structure of their manifestation. Allowing the sorcerer to invent new version of the spells she already knows. She may changing one aspect of its manifestation such as the shape of its area, manifested substance or elemental nature, or point of origin. The spell costs the same amount of sorcerous motes and cannot be more powerful than the base spell. The experience cost and training time to invent and learn the new spell is half the normal amount. </span></span> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Absorbing Shinmatic Syntax Merit (\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Those that witness the mind of the Omnibu\u2019Shen and absorb his maddening vision also touch upon his enlightened understanding of the complexity of sorceries. By witnessing a sorcerous spell of working of a circle in which she can normally attain she gains an immediate understanding of what she witnessed. This grants the sorcerer the ability to learn any spell she has witnessed by parsing out the structure of the spell costing the normal amount but taking twice the training time. In addition the difficulty to detect and discern the location of any sorcerous working is lowered by 1 to a minimum of 1. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T20:01:11-08:00","id":1031944,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">So I worked on this for a player of mine in a game that's stalled out a little bit - either way, I figure it doesn't hurt anything to post it and see if there are any tweaks that need to be made. I liked the idea a fair bit, but tunnel vision and all that.<br /> <br /> <b>What She Carried (Artifact 5 Soulsteel/Red Jade Dragon Sigh Wand)</b><br /> <br /> </span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Once there was a woman\u2026<br /> \u2026who lost everything in the fires.<br /> Then she found her breath again and went on a journey.<br /> There she became strong - undeniably.<br /> She practiced kindness - in a manner of speaking.<br /> She even became wise - from a certain point of view.<br /> But she never stopped being angry.</i></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>One day, she learned who had started that old fire.<br /> So she went to meet him again.<br /> (But not before she took some things with her.)<br /> A little jade from a burnt-up forest, for warmth.<br /> A piece of steel, cold and black as the wicked thing\u2019s heart.<br /> And inside that piece of steel?<br /> Forty-three people, just as angry as she was.<br /> (And only a little more dead.)</i></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>She put a little piece of herself into the thing she made.<br /> Every artist does, of course.<br /> But only some of them cut it off and burn it first.<br /> So when she showed up and said to that old wyrm - <br /> - \u201cOld wyrm, do you know me?\u201d<br /> It didn\u2019t know her.<br /> But it knew she meant business.<br /> (That\u2019s why it breathed flame all over her.)</i></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>She just laughed at that, <br /> right through her blackened lips.<br /> \u201cYou can\u2019t kill me that way,\u201d she said,<br /> \u201cI\u2019ve been burning my whole life.\u201d <br /> And it was true.<br /> And she killed the wyrm, then and there.<br /> But not before it killed her dead. <br /> (Only a little more dead than it had already killed her,<br /> but that was enough.)</i></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>She didn\u2019t say anything when it was done.<br /> (You know, being a little more dead and all.)<br /> She just blew away on the wind - <br /> - with the rest of the ashes.<br /> But first she set that thing she\u2019d made down.<br /> \u201cSomeone else might need it,\u201d she didn\u2019t say.<br /> (\u201cThere\u2019s always an ending,\u201d she also didn\u2019t say.<br /> Because sometimes -</i></span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What She Carried is a thick, angular thing of soulsteel, half again the length of a human\u2019s forearm. The jade used in its construction was crushed into flecks and worked into an alloy with the metal, catching the light as red and orange gleams. Sculpted to resemble a dragon like similar weapons of its caliber, the weapon\u2019s twin barrels sit side by side in the dragon\u2019s empty eye sockets, allowing its wielder to fire both before the weapon\u2019s firedust reservoir is exhausted.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Statistics<br /> Accuracy +1/+5/+3 (close/short/medium range; the last only through magic); Damage 18; Overwhelming 5; Attunement 5<br /> Tags: Lethal, Archery (Short), Flame, Slow (two shots before reloading)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Evocations of What She Carried<br /> A Solar, Abyssal, or Dragon-Blood who attunes to What She Carried adds one bonus die to all threaten actions, as well as any attempts to inspire fear, despair, or similar emotions. This bonus increases by one for every ashen health level she possesses.<br /> <br /> </span></span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Flesh of Ash</b><br /> Cost: 2m or 1m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Stackable<br /> Duration: One scene or until healed<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None</span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What She Carried drinks in the agony its fires cause, inflicting that same pain on its wielder to give them the vitality of a thing already burned. Upon making a successful decisive attack, the character may pay this Evocation\u2019s cost to create an ashen health level, the ash and lingering smoke from her shot clinging to her and cinders burning within her injuries. Ashen health levels are temporary -0 health levels, which take damage before any other health levels and may be created even if the character has taken damage to their -1 health levels or further. The character may stack Flesh of Ash up to (Essence) times, more and more ash and smoke gathering about her, although she may only create one ashen health level per decisive attack. This Evocation costs 2 motes, or 1 mote if the attack killed or destroyed a non-trivial opponent. Ashen health levels not filled with damage expire at the end of the scene; damaged ashen health levels must be healed before the Charm\u2019s commitment can be lifted and the ash fades.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>White-Hot Hateful Heart</b><br /> Cost: 6m 2i; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Counterattack, Perilous<br /> Duration: Until next turn<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Flesh of Ash</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Rage bursts forth in a thick heat haze as What She Carried glows like a forge-fresh iron. Until the start of the character\u2019s next turn, anyone who hits her with an attack at close range takes one die of lethal damage, ignoring hardness. This damage is also applied to anyone grappling with her while the heat flare lasts. When this damage is applied, she may optionally make a special disarm gambit as a counterattack, which does not require an attack roll and receives bonus dice on the Initiative roll equal to the number of ashen health levels she possesses. A successful gambit superheats the attacker\u2019s weapon, forcing them to choose between suffering a second die of lethal damage or dropping the weapon at their feet. Against natural weapons, it instead forces the choice of a second die of lethal damage or taking a -2 penalty to all their dice rolls from the intense pain, which lasts for the remainder of the scene and does not stack with subsequent uses of this Charm.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Special activation rules: The character must have at least one ashen health level to use this Evocation.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Self As Kindling</b><br /> Cost: 1 ahl; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Until next turn<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Flesh of Ash</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">The pain of self-immolation drives all lesser frailties from the mind. Until the start of the character\u2019s next turn, she ignores all her wound penalties. In order to use this Evocation, she must have an ashen health level which is either empty or filled with bashing or lethal damage, which becomes filled with aggravated damage as the glowing cinders filling her wounds roar into full flame. If she burns an uninjured ashen health level in this way, the surge of power as her body is consumed restores three motes to her.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Fuel for the Pyre</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Counterattack, Decisive-only, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Self as Kindling, White-Hot Hateful Heart</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">The wraith of the ashes drags its enemies down with it into Oblivion - or claws its way out over their corpses. If the character would be incapacitated or killed by a decisive attack, she may make a decisive counterattack before the result of the damage roll is applied to her health track. If her counterattack inflicts damage, she may use Flesh of Ash as many times as she wishes to add ashen health levels before the damage from the triggering attack is dealt to her, potentially saving her from death. Should she kill or destroy her opponent with the counterattack, she still takes the damage from the triggering attack, but the number of ashen health levels she may have at once is raised by one for the scene, and she receives an ashen health level at no cost.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Candle-Soul Conflagration</b><br /> Cost: 10m 1wp; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Fuel for the Pyre</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">At the heart of What She Carried are fourscore and four souls who have known what it is to burn utterly. The weapon\u2019s master may turn it on herself to partake of those deaths, drowning in its roaring flame. When she emerges, she has become a creature of cinder and ash, burning brighter and hotter with each life she takes.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">On the turn she uses Candle-Soul Conflagration, White-Hot Hateful Heart activates for free as the heat of her transformation scorches all who dare approach. At the start of her next turn, the flames explode outward to reveal her new form - all her flesh burnt to ash, falling away in the hot winds that dance around her, and a dreadful firelight glowing within the cracks in her immolated skin. The earth scorches where her feet fall, and if her anima flares, its light is the dancing orange of a wildfire, shot through with rising smoke.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">While she bears this dreadful curse, the other Evocations of What She Carried are enhanced:</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Flesh of Ash</b>: This Charm may now be stacked a number of times equal to the character\u2019s total health levels. Temporary health levels added by Charms such as Iron Skin Concentration do not raise this limit, but those from Permanent Charms such as Ox-Body Technique do.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>White-Hot Hateful Heart</b>: Mundane weapons disarmed by this Charm are instead destroyed, burning away or melting into slag. The penalty applied to an attacker using a natural weapon increases to -3 and does not automatically heal at the end of the scene; special care may be required to restore the injury.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Self as Kindling</b>: Wound penalties negated by this Charm are applied as bonus dice to the character\u2019s attack rolls while it lasts, as well as any social influence rolls to which the attunement bonus applies.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Fuel for the Pyre</b>: This Charm loses the Perilous keyword and may be used in Initiative Crash, explicitly allowing a Crashed character to make a decisive counterattack and giving her counterattack a raw damage equal to her base Initiative. A character in Crash who misses on the counterattack loses 2 Initiative as though she had missed a normal decisive attack, while a successful counterattack does not cause her to reset to base Initiative.</span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Should she die while so transformed, her body crumbles into cold, grey ash, only to be carried off by the wind. All that remains of her is What She Carried and any other similarly durable belongings.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Special activation rules: The character must possess at least four ashen health levels, at least one of which is damaged, to use this Evocation.</span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11517-bozwevial","name":"Bozwevial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T05:25:56-08:00","id":1032094,"title":"","content":"Here I goes again! I seem to like Soulsteel. Given I'm working on Abyssals that's probably natural. Anyway,<br /> <s><br /> <b>THIN-SKINNED COURTESAN (Soulsteel/Black Jade Grand Goremaul, Artifact... \u2022\u2022\u2022? Maybe \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022?)</b><br /> <br /> <u><b>Backstory:</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">All-Appraising Dayu was a Zenith Caste, a songstress and courtesan above all others. She had charmed godly crafters into constructing for her an instrument like an overlarge sanxian taller than she was; this instrument became popular for its soulful tones and spawned many imitators, and the oversized class of instrument is still called a <i>dayu </i>to this day. It has gone through cycles of obscurity and popularity; the Empress herself was not known to like them very much, but following her disappearance they may be coming back into vogue.<br /> <br /> All-Appraising Dayu was also known---though never to her perfect face---as Thin-Skinned Dayu. She took insults badly, and was well-known to bring retribution upon those who slighted her. When the man she desired was known to love another woman, she was driven to madness with jealousy and spite. Making a gracious offer to play at the man\u2019s wedding feast, she brought her well-tuned instrument and played a song that set the guests to murderous frenzy; the walls dripped blood as the ceiling licked with fire and Dayu laughed. Seeing her desired man try to protect his wife only drove Dayu to further fury, and she slew them both by cracking their heads with the instrument.<br /> <br /> Her dayu broken, the still-fuming Solar was not done. She called up darkly-muttering gods of the forge and journeyed to the Underworld itself to exact favors from ghostly smith-lords. The souls of the wedding party she had gathered up and pounded agonizingly, combined with strange dark ore, into soulsteel. Along with fine black jade, this was used to build her an instrument that would never break from being used to crack a few skulls. Its strings were behemothgut wrapped in fine strands of soulsteel; across its great resonator-box was stretched the skin of a demon-snake.<br /> <br /> After Dayu was strangled in bed with her weapon\u2019s own string, the accursed instrument inherited her moniker. Thin-Skinned Courtesan popped up a lot of places over the centuries; a No Moon once won it from a Deathlord, a god of assassins once had it played while a whole room of Air Immaculates utterly failed to assassinate him, and the Scarlet Empress herself was said to have chucked it out a window (she was heard to have said she found soulsteel to be a revolting material befitting Anathema and the foul lords of the dead, but a rumor persists that she found the instrument frustratingly difficult to play)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thin-Skinned Courtesan is a sort of oversized sanxian about six feet tall. Its body is constructed primarily of soulsteel and its strings are soulsteel-wrapped behemoth-gut; its resonator is clad in the darkly iridescent skin of a demon-snake. Its fingerboard and tuning-pegs are black jade, and black jade panels are set into its resonator with inlaid mother-of-pearl designs. The whole thing combines fearful instrument and massive warhammer in one terribly lovely whole.<br /> <br /> When attuned for one extra mote, attacks on foes who have been socially influenced toward negative emotion in the current scene reroll one non-successful <b>Withering </b>damage die. It also counts as an Exceptional instrument and grants one bonus die on Performance rolls that make use of its throaty tones.<br /> However, Thin-Skinned Courtesan is a fussy artifact and will not accept attunement from any character who does not meet the following requirements: <b>Performance </b>\u2022\u2022, <b>Presence </b><i>or</i> <b>Linguistics</b> \u2022, <b>Socialize </b>\u2022\u2022, <b>Appearance </b>\u2022\u2022. Curiously, it will happily accept the attunement of a character with the Hideous merit; perhaps it feels that being strikingly awful is as good as being strikingly lovely.<br /> <b>TAGS</b>: Melee (Heavy), Bashing, Reaching, Smashing, Two-Handed<br /> <br /> <u><b>EVOCATIONS</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>SAFETY IN SORROW</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m or 4m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Psyche<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: None<br /> As they turn aside the slingstones and spearpoints of foes with their instrument of murder, the wielder may strike a doleful chord and utter a few words that cut to the heart. The sudden wash of despair may cause foes\u2019 weapons to feel a little heavier and clumsier in their hands.<br /> When defending against an attack, this Evocation allows the user to reflexively make a Performance-based social influence attempt against the attacker (so long as they are within Short range); the attempt must seek to instill a Principle of melancholy and futility. For an additional cost of 2 more motes, the user may add the threshold successes of the Performance roll over Resolve to their Defense, to a maximum addition of (Essence + 2).<br /> [[Reflexively make a Performance attempt to make people sad when you Defend against their attacks, and if you spend more Essence you increase your Defense by how well your Performance roll exceeded their Resolve.]]<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ARISE, O WRETCH</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 6m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: <b>Decisive</b>-Only, Psyche<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Safety In Sorrow<br /> Thin-Skinned Courtesan is not done with you once it bashes your brains out---its wielder may pluck a stream of notes to wrest you, wailing, from your battered carcass. You had best hope your loved ones are not on the battlefield, lest they join you.<br /> Upon killing a target, this Evocation may be used to wrench their Hun soul into ghostly and visible form, where they are termed a Mournful Ghost. They have a magical Defining Principle of futility and melancholy. This creates a Performance-based social attempt (out to Medium range) to instill melancholy; characters who held a Major positive Tie toward the deceased reduce Resolve by 1. For Defining ties, 2. The Performance roll rerolls away all 1s.<br /> <br /> Mournful Ghosts are bound to the wielder for a scene; they may have (Essence) ghosts bound at a time. They can be used in the two following Evocations, but can be used in other ways. Sorcerous or Necromantic Shaping Rituals that involve sacrificing bound souls for sorcerous/necromantic motes can make use of Mournful Ghosts. Additionally, the Twilight and Daybreak Anima Power to bind spirits to oneself may be used at the end of the scene by the wielder or another with the wielder\u2019s permission; the Mournful Ghosts return to their natural ghost state, downgrading their magical Defining Principle to a Minor one, as well as having a Major Tie of fear toward the wielder. Mournful Ghosts who are not consumed or bound return to their senses at the end of the scene, retaining the Minor Principle of melancholy and Major Tie of fear as stated above.<br /> [[When you kill someone, turn them into a mournful ghost and bind them to you; you can use them to power later Evocations or for other stuff, and just seeing it happen bums everyone out, especially if they liked the person you killed.]]<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>TWICE BEREAVED, ONCE BITTEN</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m, 1 Mournful Ghost; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: <b>Withering</b>-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Arise O Wretch<br /> A wailing wraith may be torn apart before his comrade\u2019s eyes, slowing his limbs against the crushing swings of Thin-Skinned Courtesan.<br /> This Evocation enhances a <b>Withering </b>attack by spending motes and consuming a Mournful Ghost. The wielder rolls their Performance and converts <b>Withering </b>damage dice equal to the Performance successes into automatic damage successes. If the target had a Major or Defining Tie to the now-consumed Mournful Ghost, the wielder rerolls away all 1s and 4s on the accuracy roll.<br /> [[Consume a Mournful Ghost and convert a few <b>Withering </b>damage dice to autosuccesses; if the target liked the Ghost you just consumed you get to reroll some of your accuracy dice.]]<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ACCEPTANCE OF DESPAIR</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m, 1 Mournful Ghost; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 3<br /> <b>Type</b>: Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: <b>Decisive</b>-Only<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Twice Bereaved Once Bitten<br /> Seeing their friends or loved ones killed and then destroyed as ghosts, along with hearing the soul-throttling tones of the great sanxian\u2019s lugubrious voice, is enough to make a warrior want to lay down and accept death---even if the urge lasts only a moment, that moment is a fatal hesitation when Thin-Skinned Courtesan\u2019s wielder wishes you to fall.<br /> This Evocation enhances a <b>Decisive </b>attack by spending motes and consuming a Mournful Ghost. The wielder reflexively rolls a Performance-based influence attempt to instill melancholy; if the target had a Tie to the now-consumed Mournful Ghost, the influence attempt gains bonus dice equal to the value of the Intimacy. Threshold successes over Resolve are subtracted from the target\u2019s Defense, and the damage roll adds three dice.<br /> [[Consume a Mournful Ghost and make a Performance attempt against the target of your <b>Decisive </b>attack, which gets bonus dice depending on how much they liked the Ghost; the better you do, the more their Defense gets reduced, and your damage roll has three bonus dice.]]</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As with Heart Eater before it, I'm sure I've got cost or effect scaling problems. I actually realized early on that my original direction was too similar to Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel/Red Jade Grimscythe like 20+ pages back) and then remembered that Black Jade has the capability to do stuff with spirits. Thus we got the Mournful Ghost mechanic!<br /> <br /> I hope I was able to make each Evocation useful without needing the following Evocations---I'll admit that <i>Arise, O Wretch</i> might be a little less useful if you don't have the followups yet and can't make use of the Mournful Ghosts for a Shaping Ritual or the Twilight Anima, since at that point it basically just makes more people subject to the modest attunement benefit of getting to reroll one damage nonsuccess on a Withering attack. With the full four Evocations the idea's basically to bum people out so you can a little more easily build up Initiative, use that Initiative on Decisives to kill people and turn them into Mournful Ghosts (thus bumming more people out and making it easier to Wither on them a little), who you then spend to better kill <i>more </i>people and turn <i>them</i> into ghosts until you run out of people to beat into foie gras.</s><br /> Needs toning down evidently. Check back later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 01-16-2017, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:33:23-08:00","id":1032717,"title":"","content":"Half baked idea, but throwing it out here for feedback:<br /> <br /> Smashfist made of white &amp; green jade. Basically gives my Solar &quot;earthbending.&quot; Mostly I see it as stunt fodder (e.g., when parrying a giant rock juts out of the ground). The idea I have for an evocation is inspired by Armstrong from FMA. Punch the ground and a line of big stone spikes shoots toward your enemy. Something like...<br /> <br /> &quot;Cost: 3m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Evocations: None<br /> <br /> The wielder slams their fist into the ground, causing a row of head-height stone protrusions to erupt from the ground in the direction of their enemy. This charm supplements a Brawl attack, increasing it's range to short. The spikes it leaves behind create a zone of difficult terrain.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pretty basic and seems comparable to entry level Brawl charms like Thunderclap Rush. Impairs the opponent's mobility and adds fodder for Heaven Thunder Hammer stunts (e.g., punch people into spikes for lethal dmg, etc.) Obv need to punch up the flavor text for the final draft, and of course write the rest of the tree.<br /> <br /> LMK if it sounds too OP for a first evocation (that would be granted on attunement like Spring Razor, i.e., no other bonuses). <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11690-mizzlfoshizzl","name":"mizzlfoshizzl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:41:43-08:00","id":1032725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mizzlfoshizzl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1032717#post1032717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Half baked idea, but throwing it out here for feedback:<br /> <br /> Smashfist made of white &amp; green jade. Basically gives my Solar &quot;earthbending.&quot; Mostly I see it as stunt fodder (e.g., when parrying a giant rock juts out of the ground). The idea I have for an evocation is inspired by Armstrong from FMA. Punch the ground and a line of big stone spikes shoots toward your enemy. Something like...<br /> <br /> &quot;Cost: 3m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Evocations: None<br /> <br /> The wielder slams their fist into the ground, causing a row of head-height stone protrusions to erupt from the ground in the direction of their enemy. This charm supplements a Brawl attack, increasing it's range to short. The spikes it leaves behind create a zone of difficult terrain.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pretty basic and seems comparable to entry level Brawl charms like Thunderclap Rush. Impairs the opponent's mobility and adds fodder for Heaven Thunder Hammer stunts (e.g., punch people into spikes for lethal dmg, etc.) Obv need to punch up the flavor text for the final draft, and of course write the rest of the tree.<br /> <br /> LMK if it sounds too OP for a first evocation (that would be granted on attunement like Spring Razor, i.e., no other bonuses).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you're better off splitting this into two evocations. Brawl is really negated by the fact that it tends to be close range only, because it's able to deal really massive amounts of damage really quickly with it, and the solution to brawl is &quot;get away.&quot; Giving someone the ability to do some of the crazy brawl combos from short range really increases the utility of brawl in a way that I would cost as more than 3m. Alternatively, if you create an entire evocation for this artifact, it would be fine if you let it extend the range only for evocations of this artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:53:03-08:00","id":1032737,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> <br /> <br /> These effects are much much too strong for Artifact 3, and maybe too good for artifact 4. The first evocation alone is wildly powerful compared to any of the first evocations that you'll see in the core book for artifact 3 or 4 weapons. Along with the ability to deal pretty massive withering damage using the mournful souls + additional intimacies, I'd be inclined to say that this is artifact 4 / 5. <br /> <br /> Something to consider about adding defense or subtracting defense is that, functionally, they act as an automatic success, reducing your barrier to hitting as well as increasing your total damage, or preventing damage to you all together. That is extremely, extremely powerful, and it seems to be thrown around in evocations sets without a lot of thought for their mechanics. Artifact 3 weapons do things like &quot;you can roll a read intentions when you hit:&quot; and &quot;add one die of damage.&quot; They are not &quot;Decrease their defense by 3, grants a number of withering autosuccesses&quot;. Something to note is that a withering autosuccess isn't mentioned in the melee charmset until Immortal Blade Triumphant. it is an extremely, extremely powerful effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:58:54-08:00","id":1032739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PraxisCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1032725#post1032725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're better off splitting this into two evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>As in, difficult terrain creation in one evocation, short range attack in another?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PraxisCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1032725#post1032725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Giving someone the ability to do some of the crazy brawl combos from short range really increases the utility of brawl in a way that I would cost as more than 3m.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give an example? Because I'm not seeing how it's that different than Thunderclap Rush (which is reflexive, and lets you automatically move into range, AND do all of that out of initiative order)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11690-mizzlfoshizzl","name":"mizzlfoshizzl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:06:50-08:00","id":1032743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mizzlfoshizzl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1032739#post1032739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As in, difficult terrain creation in one evocation, short range attack in another?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yup!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Can you give an example? Because I'm not seeing how it's that different than Thunderclap Rush (which is reflexive, and lets you automatically move into range, AND do all of that out of initiative order) </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a mechanical difference between moving into close range from short, where melee and other brawl characters can hit you back, or certain dodge charms can kick in, and being able to kite enemies from afar by reflexively moving away and forcing them to rush you to even be able to hit you, while you're dealing massive brawl wombo combos.<br /> <br /> Also, TRA has a scene limitation:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted 3E corebook, page 275</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Charm can be used once per target, per scene, but can be refreshed against a single target by crashing that target.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:07:01-08:00","id":1032744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PraxisCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1032737#post1032737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8026_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8026\" data-vbnamecard=\"8026\">Beans</a> <br /> <br /> These effects are much much too strong for Artifact 3, and maybe too good for artifact 4. The first evocation alone is wildly powerful compared to any of the first evocations that you'll see in the core book for artifact 3 or 4 weapons. Along with the ability to deal pretty massive withering damage using the mournful souls + additional intimacies, I'd be inclined to say that this is artifact 4 / 5. <br /> <br /> Something to consider about adding defense or subtracting defense is that, functionally, they act as an automatic success, reducing your barrier to hitting as well as increasing your total damage, or preventing damage to you all together. That is extremely, extremely powerful, and it seems to be thrown around in evocations sets without a lot of thought for their mechanics. Artifact 3 weapons do things like &quot;you can roll a read intentions when you hit:&quot; and &quot;add one die of damage.&quot; They are not &quot;Decrease their defense by 3, grants a number of withering autosuccesses&quot;. Something to note is that a withering autosuccess isn't mentioned in the melee charmset until Immortal Blade Triumphant. it is an extremely, extremely powerful effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suppose I'll have to look into adjusting it, then. Care to look at the one I have further up the page? Probably as terrible if not worse, given my track record, of course.<br /> <br /> Might come up with something to put a space between the first and second ones on Courtesan, unless that one'd be alright with some toning down rather than needing to be shoved up a shelf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 01-16-2017, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:34:48-08:00","id":1032758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PraxisCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1032743#post1032743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a mechanical difference between moving into close range from short, where melee and other brawl characters can hit you back, or certain dodge charms can kick in, and being able to kite enemies from afar by reflexively moving away and forcing them to rush you to even be able to hit you, while you're dealing massive brawl wombo combos.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking through it more, you're right. This is really more of a Simple charm, in that it's a specific action in it's own right. Back to the drawing board...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11690-mizzlfoshizzl","name":"mizzlfoshizzl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:20:56-08:00","id":1034735,"title":"","content":"-nevermind!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":225,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","user":"Growls","date":".  Found one another place! 01-19-2017, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T21:46:38-08:00","id":1035621,"title":"","content":"Ok, new direction for the green and white jade smashfist. <br /> <br /> Working on an idea that it sprouts vines that entangle the enemy. Looking for feedback, especially on cost, because stackable debuff is kind of an unexplored design space in the core. <br /> <br /> Cost: 6m<br /> Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Stackable, Withering-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Evocations: None<br /> <br /> On a successful withering attack, a tendril from the gauntlet ensnares the target. For each tendril, the target suffers a -1 penalty to Defense and disengage attempts. The target can use a combat action to clear all tendrils.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11690-mizzlfoshizzl","name":"mizzlfoshizzl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11690_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T04:36:13-08:00","id":1039926,"title":"","content":"So the players just stole a Moonsilver Grimcleaver, called Spine of the Moon's Shadow, and they hid it because they were trying not to get caught. But in flashback dreams of the First Age the Lunar made it stretch and decapitated some Giraffes with it, I'm thinking something similar to that Dude in Bleach Renji and his Zabimaru. I'm thinking it can attack maybe short distance by becoming a whiplike spine. How much should be Evocations and what should be inherent power? The example artifacts seem to hint like the default power of the Artifact counts as something like a free evocation, is that basically representing powers available to Solar/whoever it resonates with?<br /> <br /> Is something here already similar to what I described that I could use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T13:54:38-08:00","id":1040195,"title":"","content":"I just finished writing up a pair of artifacts, both meant for the same character, and I would love some feedback on the first one here. I'm not currently in any Exalted games, but I'm still hoping to use them some time. The original concept for the first artifact was an improvised artifact weapon. I put some commentary after each evocation in a spoiler. I hope that clarifies some of my design decisions.<br /> <br /> I want to keep this first one at artifact 3. I think it may be too powerful, so I'd definitely appreciate any help toning it down where appropriate. Keep in mind that, as an improvised weapon, this is used with Brawl.<br /> <br /> <b>The Kraken's Nail</b> (Black Jade and Orichalcum Anchor, artifact 3)<br /> Originally the anchor for an artifact ship from an age past, he Kraken's Nail has long since broken off from the ship proper. Once, it manipulated gravity to become incomparably heavy, anchoring its ship to the seabed without fail. Now, its terrible powers lend itself to its new purpose as a weapon, cumbersome but powerful.<br /> <br /> Legend has it the patron god of the ship on which the Kraken's Nail originally served was given power and independence, and was the one who decided to separate anchor from ship. Sometimes called Captain Cegus, the formerly-patron god went on his own adventures, wielding the anchor as a weapon against the monsters of the deep.<br /> <br /> Yet there are more legends, saying the ship once attached to the Kraken's Nail sunk at sea, picked at by scavengers until only the anchor remained, its gravitic powers preventing anyone from moving it...until the right woman came along. Stories give her many different names, but most agree she was a shining golden champion. The anchor responded to her touch as she was diving in the waters, allowing itself to be wielded as a weapon...of sorts.<br /> <br /> One final legend says the ship meant for the Kraken's Nail was actually never finished, leaving the anchor adrift in the world, used as a weapon since it lacks any other purpose. Scholars agree this is the most likely out of all the legends surrounding the Kraken's Nail, if only out of fear of imagining the kind of ship that would go along with something so terribly powerful.<br /> <br /> The Kraken's Nail is a stockless anchor over six feet long, and more than a match for a grand daiklave in weight. Around the arms and lower shank of the anchor is an emblem of an octopus, made from orichalcum filigree. Most of the rest is made of black jade. It still has the ring, along with a small length of orichalcum chain. It has no hearthstone sockets.<br /> <br /> The Kraken's Nail is a heavy artifact weapon, so heavy in fact that attuning it requires a feat of strength (and thus Strength 3+). Its tags are: Bashing, Improvised, Reaching, Smashing, Two-Handed.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Kraken's Nail</b><br /> The Kraken's Nail is about as merciful as the rip current. A decisive attack against a crashed target gains bonus dice equal to the initiative spent on the tags (i.e., improvised and smashing) and evocations of the Kraken's Nail, up to three.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This has the potential to be a very powerful and efficient bonus, hopefully balanced out by the fact it requires spending some initiative. Trading initiative for mote efficiency will be a running theme with this artifact. For reference, the maximum initiative that can be spent on one attack with this artifact is 9, and it is balanced with that in mind.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Vandal's Tide</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m, 1i; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> The Kraken's Nail shatters all who oppose it. When the wielder makes a decisive attack with the Kraken's Nail, she may roll all initiative spent on the tags (i.e., improvised and smashing) and evocations of the Kraken's Nail as a special disarm gambit if she hits. This gambit does not require another attack, costs no further initiative, and is made at difficulty 2 as if it had the Disarm tag. If successful, the wielder may choose to destroy a non-artifact weapon or shield instead of disarming it. The attack enhancing function of this evocation may be used once per fight, reset by gaining initiative break.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, this charm may be used in a feat of strength to break an object using the Kraken's Nail, adding two non-charm successes as if the Kraken's Nail was appropriate for breaking the object in question.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The power of disarming someone is hopefully balanced out by the reset condition and its reliance on spending lots of initiative. I want to keep the current reset condition so it can synch up with the final evocation.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Crashing Metal Tsunami</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1i; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1;<b> Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> The Kraken's Nail crashes through defenses like a tsunami through a sand castle. On a withering attack, for each initiative spent on the tags (i.e., improvised and smashing) and evocations of the Kraken's Nail the wielder may transfer one extra success to the post-soak damage instead of the raw damage. On a decisive attack, for every three such initiative, round down, the wielder may convert one die of damage into an automatic success, and the damage is made lethal.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Designed to make the Kraken's Nail more useful against the likes of Octavian or artifact heavy armor users. Getting hit by an anchor should always hurt! Like all other Kraken's Nail evocations, it is heavily dependent on spending initiative, so it is mote efficient.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gravity Squall</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1i;<b> Mins:</b> Essence 1; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> A swing of the Kraken's Nail changes the direction of gravity, sending the target tumbling through the world. For every three initiative spent on the tags (i.e., improvised and smashing) and evocations of the Kraken's Nail, round down, the target is knocked back one range band in any direction, landing prone. If they collide with an obstacle that could reasonably stop them, they take falling damage appropriate for the remaining distance. When knocking a target straight up, reduce the distance by one range band.<br /> <br /> This evocation overrides other knockback effects, including the smashing tag and Heaven Thunder Hammer. Normally, this evocation cannot do more than knock down an opponent significantly larger than the wielder. Combining this evocation with Heaven Thunder Hammer or similar magic, however, allows the wielder to knock back prodigiously large targets such as tyrant lizards.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b> Gravity Squall may only be awakened after incapacitating a non-trivial opponent with a smashing attack using the Kraken's Nail. The target must not have had any damage in their health track beforehand.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I don't like Heaven Thunder Hammer. I don't like how powerful it is, and I think it takes too many paragraphs to explain its effects. I designed this charm as a hopefully more reasonable alternative for my character, without obsoleting Heaven Thunder Hammer completely. It requires some shenanigans to unlock, as it's at least a little bit more powerful than the other two essence 1 evocations.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Looming Iron Surge</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1i; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2; <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Vandal's Tide, Crashing Metal Tsunami, Gravity Squall<br /> <br /> With an ominous hum, the Kraken's Nail uses its gravitic powers to magnify its weight, becoming simply too heavy for anyone to counter its momentum. If the initiative spent on the tags (i.e., improvised and smashing) and evocations of the Kraken's Nail is equal to or greater than the parry defense of the target of a withering or decisive attack the attack becomes unblockable. Otherwise, their parry suffers a -2 penalty.<br /> <br /> The momentum of one attack carries through to the next. If the attack was decisive and either the target was incapacitated or accepted a crippling injury, the wielder gains two initiative if she dealt 1-10 decisive damage, or three if she dealt 11+, including damage prevented by accepting a crippling injury. This also includes any damage added by Gravity Squall.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It should be hard to parry something so heavy. Unblockable is a very rare property for a good reason, so I hope this evocation costs enough and requires enough initiative spent to compensate. The second paragraph is there so it's not totally useless against people who use dodge, or have low defenses in the first place, and so the wielder can use its evocations after a decisive attack without crashing.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Inward Vortex</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m, 2i, 1wp;<b> Mins:</b> Essence 3; <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Looming Iron Surge<br /> <br /> A hit from the Kraken's Nail turns the relentless forces of gravity onto the victim, crushing them from all angles instead of just one. This evocation creates a decisive attack. If it hits, the target is forced to accept a crippling injury (which does not count against the once per story limit), negating as much damage as she can, or an amount equal to half the initiative spent on the tags (i.e., improvised and smashing) and evocations of the Kraken's Nail, round up, whichever is less.<br /> <br /> Once per scene, reset by crashing a non-trivial target who originally had 11+ initiative with a single withering attack. Inward Vortex may then be used on that target on the wielder's next attack.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I revised this one so many times. Originally inspired by Crimson Spray Blur from Octavian, it's meant to be able to end a fight instantly. An earlier version dealt lots of bonus damage if the target refused to accept an injury, but I decided it was too much for an artifact 3 capstone.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1543-iethloc","user":"Iethloc","date":".  More revisions 02-06-2017, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1543-iethloc","name":"Iethloc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1543_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T05:36:12-08:00","id":1041211,"title":"","content":"<b>Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive</b> (Artifact 3, Orichalcum Grand Daiklaive)<br /> <br /> It is said that in another age a man called Huqod was Exalted by the Sun while he hunted down and slaughtered the brigands that murdered his wife, Saeema. Later, Saeema\u2019s ghost returned to Huqod, and the two tried to resume their relationship. It seemed that the two loved one-another again, until one fateful day when the Dawn snapped and rent the echo of his wife apart forever. Ghosts, he had determined, were not the people whom they resemble, but malicious copies that had no business existing.<br /> <br /> As the years passed, Huqod\u2019s hatred of ghosts only grew, as well as the terrible destructions he would put them through. He sought a tool that would help him tear apart the denizens of the Underworld, and, dissatisfied with anything else, delved into artifice in order to see his vision come to being. The result was Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive, a weapon seething with so much malice towards the dead that any wielder cannot help but feel it. As for Huqod, it is said that he died violently less than a dozen years after crafting his blade as he took it deep into the unknown heart of the Underworld in an attempt to destroy whatever strange forces bring ghosts into existence.<br /> <br /> Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive hates the fact that ghosts can cross over into Creation and after any scene where any of its evocations are used, the wielder must spend one willpower (and roll a die for limit if applicable) or gain or strengthen a principle of, \u201cI will destroy those who cross the border of death.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive</b><br /> <br /> As a strange quirk of its being, though Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive is made from Orichalcum, its evocations function perfectly for Abyssals and Liminals as well as Solars, and they receive Your<br /> Corpus is Brittle for free. Any of the aforementioned Exalted who commit an extra two motes to the weapon when they attune to it find themselves able to harm dematerialized ghosts (or other death-essenced beings).<br /> <br /> <b>Your Corpus is Brittle</b><br /> Cost: 2m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> The first lesson that Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive teaches is that hatred can be used to destroy. This functions only against death-essenced beings (see sidebar below), and the wielder finds himself momentarily feeling the same hatred that the sword feels.<br /> <br /> If used as part of a successful withering attack, add post-soak damage dice equal to the intensity of the wielder\u2019s intimacy of \u201cI will destroy those who cross the border of death.\u201d If the wielder has no such intimacy, count it as one. When dealing magnitude damage to a battlegroup, these post-soak dice are converted to successes. Note that in neither case does the wielder receive the extra initiative; it is all absorbed by the sword. On a decisive attack, ignore an equal amount of hardness.<br /> <br /> <b>Your Soul Hides Nothing</b><br /> Cost: 3m Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Your Corpus is Brittle<br /> <br /> Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive\u2019s second lesson is that a quick burst of violence can reveal a victim\u2019s vulnerabilities to the aggressor. A successful decisive attack supplemented by this evocation acts as a successful read intention against a death-essenced foe, and reveals a strong intimacy to the attacker. Alternatively, against a foe that has a method of escaping destruction (a spirit with a sanctum, or a Deathlord with an immortality clause, for example), it reveals the existence and nature of one method of revival or protection.<br /> <br /> By committing a single mote in the instant after learning of an intimacy or immortality clause, the wielder of Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive may hold on to a fragment of the victim\u2019s soul and use it against them. Immaterial chains of hazy essence as black and gold as the corona of an eclipse snake off from the sword into the distance, visible only to the wielder and anyone that can see dematerialized spirits, which leads towards the subject of the intimacy. If a ghost cares for her daughter, the chains will lead to her. If a Deathlord may only be destroyed by throwing his original bones into the Elemental Pole of Fire, the chain will lead to the bones or perhaps to an ancient library detailing such a ritual. Regardless, as long as the mote is committed, the wielder receives three charmless dice on any attempt to find the subject of the intimacy such as tracking, investigating, researching, or anything else appropriate. As long as these motes are committed by the wielder of Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive, the victim is inherently aware that their secrets are in danger and are likely interested in safeguarding their intimacies or immortality.<br /> <br /> <b>Your Purpose is Extinguished</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1 wp Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Your Soul Hides Nothing<br /> <br /> The final lesson of hatred taught by Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive is that to truly defeat an opponent, you must destroy everything that they care about. Strike at their greatest loves, and you strike at them as well. Use of this evocation causes Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive to glow oppressively golden like the hateful noon sun over the Burning Sands.<br /> <br /> This evocation requires the use of its prerequisite, notably the committed mote that links sword and intimacy. It is used when the wielder destroys an intimacy that the sword is linked to, and can be activated reflexively should that instant of destruction be mid-combat. If a ghost cares for her daughter, the wielder would slay that daughter to activate this charm, but if a ghost cared about the library that she maintained in life, it may be activated when the library is burned down and the sword swung across its ashes. For intimacies to abstract principles or cosmic beings (devotion to the Immaculate Faith, or to a Neverborn, for example) the destruction can be of a significant symbol of that principle or being, as the Storyteller sees fit. In all situations there must be destruction involved.<br /> <br /> This takes the form of a special automatically successful decisive attack that strikes the being from whom the intimacy was taken no matter where they are, even across dimensional boundaries. The damage pool for this attack is Essence + the level of the intimacy \u201cI will destroy those who cross the border of death\u201d + double the level of the intimacy that the victim had for what was destroyed. Hardness does not apply against this aggravated damage, and 10s are doubled. If the intimacy was destroyed in front of the victim, double 8s. Add the dice from any stunt for a grisly or harrowing destruction to the raw damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Sidebar: On Death-Essence<br /> Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive hates those who cross the border of death. Normally that includes many creatures hailing from or suffused with the essence of the Underworld. Being such as ghosts, zombies, hekatonkhires, Deathlords, Abyssals, Liminals, some necromancers, and Neverborn comprise a non-exhaustive list. Those are the beings that the evocations of Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive work against.<br /> <br /> Well, those being s are those that cross the border if you\u2019re in Creation, Yu-Shan, Malfeas, or the Wyld. However if you\u2019re in the Underworld, those beings are native and Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive has no ill-feeling towards them. Instead, while in the Underworld, all the evocations work against beings native to Creation. Humans and animals, some behemoths, most Exalted, Elementals, and Gods are all strangers in the Underworld and there the sword only functions against such beings. In a Shadowland, the sword works equally well against both Creation-natives and Death-essenced beings, making it very formidable.<br /> <br /> The bearer of Vicious Censurer of the Liminal Fugitive does not automatically have knowledge of this, potentially leading to some dangerous situations.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","user":"Kunoichi","date":". 01-31-2017, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T05:39:38-08:00","id":1041212,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">I had a quick look through the thread and couldn't see anyone tackling a sorcerous phylactery artifact in the style of the Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes, so here's my attempt. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The Coil of Ahiahep</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>(Starmetal sorcerous phylactery, artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">The Shogunate was an era of upheaval and destruction. The Dragon-Blooded attempted to assert their new dominion over the world they had claimed, its wonders fell to ruin and wars were waged over those that survived. Many petty tyrants carved out empires in this period, unchecked by a Shogunate burdened with internecine strife and corruption. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">One such tyrant was the sorcerer-prince Ahiahep, a mysterious figure who appeared out of the forest wilds and claimed to be the last inheritor of the lost Devonian Library, and he bore a black ring that he claimed granted him dominion over the powers of Hell and the spirits of the East. Whatever the provenance of his sorceries they were real enough; using them he subjugated mortal kingdoms, spirit courts and rival Exalts alike and forged them into a nascent empire, razing forests from horizon to horizon and fashioning mighty ziggurats in his own name. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Before long, this nascent empire seemed poised to strike at the heartlands of the Eastern daimyos of the Shogunate, but almost overnight it collapsed and fragmented as Ahiahep vanished. The story goes that a daring mortal thief charmed the black ring from his finger and left him to be torn apart by his resentful minions. Whatever the truth, the ring continued to have a bloody history independent of its master until it was lost during the Great Contagion. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">The Coil of Ahaiep is a ring of blackened starmetal in the form of an intricately carved dragon swallowing its own tail. The way light glitters across its finely worked scales makes it look uncannily lifelike. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><u>Evocations of the Black Ring</u></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">When attuned for three motes by a sorcerer and worn, the Coil of Ahiahep reduces by one the Willpower cost of the first spell the sorcerer casts during the day. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">The ring\u2019s evocations can be paid for with motes or sorcerous motes, which can be gathered with a Shape Sorcery action for this purpose. Sorcerers without a mote pool can wear the ring and learn and use its first two evocations in this way, though they cannot gain its attunement bonus.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Knowledge Comes from Within</b></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Cost</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">: 3m; </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Mins</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Essence 1</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Type</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Simple</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Keywords</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:None</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Duration</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:One scene</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Prerequisite Charms</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:None</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">The first lesson of Ahiahep\u2019s black ring teaches of what can be known by sufficient magical intuition. For the remainder of the scene, the sorcerer gains two bonus dice on all rolls on Occult rolls to examine spirits, fair folk and other non-human magical beings. She also gains this bonus any Shape Sorcery rolls to cast sorcery against them. Should she Join Battle against such beings, she gains a number of sorcerous motes equal to her successes, which last for the duration of the scene. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Balance in Emptiness</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Cost</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">: 1wp; </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Mins</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Essence 1</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Type</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Simple</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Keywords</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:None</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Duration</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Instant</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Prerequisite Charms</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Knowledge Comes from Within</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">The master of the black ring can use this Evocation to trap a minor spirit in the empty void within, compelling it to use its powers on her behalf. Balance in Emptiness allows the ring to function exactly as a Yasal Crystal, save that it can imprison up to (sorcerer\u2019s Essence) spirits of Essence 2 or lower. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The End is the Beginning</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Cost</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">: 10m; </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Mins</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Essence 2</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Type</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Simple</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Keywords</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:None</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Duration</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Instant</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Prerequisite Charms</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Balance in Emptiness</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Precious seeds of magic fall still in the Age of Sorrows, never to come to fruition. Better to nurture them, and give them a chance to fulfil their purpose. If the sorcerer finds a way to counter a magical curse that should have been fatal or extremely debilitating, she may use this Charm to trap the magic in the structure of the ring. The ring can sustain the curses of sorcery, the Charms of spirits, the death-curses of ghosts, the bans of the Fair Folk and even stranger and more exotic magics. At any time thereafter, upon seeing the originator of the curse, she can use this Charm again to inflict an identical curse upon them. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The Unbroken Coil</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Cost</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">: 1wp; </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Mins</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Essence 2</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Type</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Supplemental</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Keywords</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:None</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Duration</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Instant</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Prerequisite Charms</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Knowledge Comes from Within</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Few in this fallen age understand more of the nature of sorcery than the force that slumbers within the black ring, a beginningless legacy stretching back through time. It whispers guidance to its master, warning her against pretenders to this power. A sorcerer can use this Evocation to attempt to counter or distort a spell of one circle greater than that into which she is initiated (Celestial for a Terrestrial sorcerer, Solar for a Celestial). A Solar sorcerer can use this Evocation to gain her Occult in non-Charm bonus dice to a roll to counter or distort a spell.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Beyond the Black Rainbow</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Cost</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">: 5m, 1wp;</span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Mins</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Essence 3</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Type</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Simple</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Keywords</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:None</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Duration</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:Instant</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Prerequisite Charms</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">:The End is the Beginning, The Unbroken Coil</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">The ring remembers a Time Before, through it flows a river of sorcerous power long since etched into the very fabric of the world, fact made mystery by the passage of ages. Once per story, the sorcerer can reach beyond the veil of the material world and grasp at the sorcerous power that courses beneath. Doing so grants her knowledge of a single spell of the Emerald circle. She can only cast this spell once or incorporate it in as means in a single sorcerous working, after which the power recedes once more from her grasp. She can counter and distort the spell for the remainder of the story as though she knew it, however. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Alternatively, the sorcerer can reach for knowledge of an even greater power. She understands the fundamental truth of a spell of the Sapphire or Adamant circle. She cannot cast this spell, but can counter and distort is as though she can. She must still use The Unbroken Coil to counter a spell of a circle she cannot cast.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 01-31-2017, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T09:27:58-08:00","id":1041306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1039926#post1039926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the players just stole a Moonsilver Grimcleaver, called Spine of the Moon's Shadow, and they hid it because they were trying not to get caught. But in flashback dreams of the First Age the Lunar made it stretch and decapitated some Giraffes with it, I'm thinking something similar to that Dude in Bleach Renji and his Zabimaru. I'm thinking it can attack maybe short distance by becoming a whiplike spine. How much should be Evocations and what should be inherent power? The example artifacts seem to hint like the default power of the Artifact counts as something like a free evocation, is that basically representing powers available to Solar/whoever it resonates with?<br /> <br /> Is something here already similar to what I described that I could use?</div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=841300#post841300\">Ivy Carillon</a> has, as its attunement bonus, the ability to attack at short range for two initiative. It otherwise doesn't seem to fit what you are looking for, though I'm not familiar with Bleach.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1543-iethloc","name":"Iethloc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1543_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T00:57:19-08:00","id":1041729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Ubuntu\">Should she Join Battle against such beings, she gains a number of sorcerous motes equal to her successes, which last for the duration of the scene. </span></span> </div> </div> </div>With that clause, an Awareness-favored sorcerer is going to be opening with Death Ray on turn 1 after a single easy shape sorcery action. I'd make sure that's what you want, but it seems hella powerful and severely out of balance for E1.<br /> <br /> Would Beyond the Black Rainbow be too good if you could 1/story grab a spell of a circle your are initiated into? Seems pretty good to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9018-ennuideblase","name":"EnnuiDeBlase","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:59:07-08:00","id":1041922,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone. After reading through this thread, I found the inspiration to make some artifact of my own. My first few are just small attempts at creating a simple artifact, but after getting some practice in I decided to try something a bit bigger.<br /> <br /> This artifact is meant to be wielded by a warrior-scholar type. The idea is for the wielder to be able to absorb the knowledge and wisdom of those he defeats, even if he slays them. It certainly needs some more work, both in the wording and the balancing, but I was hoping I could get some feedback on my first draft. The last evocation in particular feels a bit clunky as it is written right now, and I feel a bit unsure about the evocation bonus <br /> <br /> <i><b>Ematril, The Library of the Passed</b></i><br /> Starmetal Wrackstaff, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> Brilliant Sorrow was a Chosen of the Maiden of Secrets. Both a warrior and a scholar, he found sadness in the knowledge that was lost with each life on the battlefield. After a year of meditation in the libraries of Heaven, he found the inspiration to forge Ematril.<br /> <br /> Ematril would be a solid staff of starmetal, 6 feet long, on which everything that was known to Brilliant Sorrow would be engraved with orichalcum. The staff greedily took in every secret he gave it, the runes shifting and shrinking to make space when there seemed to be none left. Finally, after decades of restless work, the staff knew everything Brillant Sorrow did, even the knowledge he was not aware he possessed.<br /> <br /> Brilliant Sorrow was not satisfied however. His own knowledge preserved for all time, he began the next step in Ematril`s creation. Through sorcery, he created a spirit of knowledge and bound it to the staff, to curate the impressive library the staff would one day be. To this spirit he gave the power to read the minds of those whom the staff struck, so it could copy their knowledge for the future.<br /> <br /> Safe knowing that he would no longer rob Creation of knowledge and wisdom carrying out his duties to Heaven, Brilliant Sorrow spent the rest of his life serving the Maidens, perishing when he defined heavens will and saved one who was fated to die, binding himself to the staff in his final moments to aid those who would carry his legacy.<br /> Ematril has three hearthstone sockets, placed such that they divide the staff into four sections of equal length.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of Ematril, The Library of the Passed</b><br /> A Solar or Sidereal that attunes to Ematril finds their minds filled with knowledge. They receive +2 to any Lore or Occult rolls based on recalling information or knowledge while holding the staff. Other beings find the staff impossible to attune to, as the spirit within judges them unable to comprehend the knowledge within, and refuses them. Such being can attune to the staff if they have a combined Lore, Occult and Intelligence of at least 10, although they will be unable to learn Ematrils final evocation.<br /> <br /> <b>Student Reading Strike </b><br /> Cost: 2m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Uniform<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> If an attack boosted by this evocation hits an opponent, the wielder learns their Lore rating, as well as any specialties they have in Lore. If the successes on the damage roll is enough to beat the targets guile, the wielder also learns of any knowledge based intimacies the target may have.<br /> This evocation can also be used out of combat, as a Simple charm, in which case it involves a simple tap of the staff against the target. If the target wishes, such a use of this evocation reveals all relevant intimacies without a roll. Otherwise, make a Read Intentions roll, using (Lore + Perception) instead of the successes on the damage roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> Unless there is a special reason not to, it is usually safe for the Storyteller to assume that most characters have between zero or two dots in Lore, with perhaps one specialty relevant to their occupation. <br /> <br /> <b>Enigmatic Tutor Lecture</b><br /> Cost: 3m Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Withering-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Student Reading Strike<br /> <br /> This evocation supplements a <b>withering</b> attack against an opponent struck by its prerequisite earlier in the scene. It adds the difference in the characters Lore ratings to the raw damage of the attack if that difference is positive. Specialties add to each of the characters Lore ratings for this purpose.<br /> <br /> <b>Mentor Enlightening Student Method</b><br /> Cost: 3m 1wp Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only, Stackable<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisites: Student Reading Strike<br /> <br /> Upon landing a <b>decisive </b>attack on a foe that has been struck at least once with the prerequisite, the exalt can activate this charm to learn from their foe. They learn one of the Lore specialties for as long as the motes remain committed, and it is considered a known specialty for all purposes. When the commitment is dropped, the knowledge fades from their minds. The specialty can be added permanently at any point by paying for it as normal, with no training time required.<br /> If the target is willing, this charm can be used without the need of a decisive attack, in which case it is treated as a Simple charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Heavenly Cage Invitation</b><br /> Cost: 4m 1wp Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only, Psyche <br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisites: Enigmatic Tutor Lecture, Mentor Enlightening Student Method<br /> <br /> A crippled warrior can still serve as a teacher and give council. This evocation allows the saying to apply to those slain by the exalt.<br /> Upon striking a killing blow, the exalt can activate the charm and offer the target a chance to remain a little longer to guide those who remain. Treat this as an instill action, targeting a Major intimacy, unless the exalt knows of any stronger intimacies to exploit. Wound penalties do not apply to the targets Resolve for this action. The exalt may substitute Lore for a social ability, if desired.<br /> <br /> If the instill attempt is successful, a phantom copy of the target is put into the staff. This phantom knows everything it did in life, but cannot meaningfully do anything but talk to the holder of the staff. The phantom keeps any intimacies it may have had in life, but also gains a Defining intimacy towards aiding the staff`s holder in scholarly pursuits and in training the holder.<br /> The phantom is not a ghost, nor is it made of the person\u2019s soul. It is still possible for the enemy to rise as a ghost in the future, or for their soul to be reincarnated. While inside the staff, the phantom enjoys a heavenly life, where all their needs and desires are met, though they may never leave the staff. The holder may revoke or grant privileges if the phantom turns out to be unruly. <br /> <br /> Once commitment to the evocation ends, or a new phantom is created, the phantom fades into the infinite library of the staff. He is still there, and still lives in the heavenly world, but he is no longer reachable to the holder. The wielders ability to influence the phantoms world also ends at this point, allowing it to enjoy eternity without restrictions placed upon it by the wielder.<br /> <br /> <b>Opening the Grand Library</b><br /> Cost: 15m 1wp (1wp) Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous<br /> Duration: One Day<br /> Prerequisites: Heavenly Cage Invitation<br /> <br /> Having shown himself a worthy scholar, Ematril opens its doors fully to its wielder. Meditating for a moment on the true purpose of knowledge, he then taps the staff into the ground creating a brilliant flash of essence. Once it passes, the exalt, and anyone he wishes to bring with him, disappears.<br /> <br /> This evocation brings the exalt and anyone he wishes into the great library of Ematril, located in Elsewhere. Anyone can resist this pull with a (Willpower + Essence) roll at a difficulty of the holder`s Essence.<br /> <br /> The library is a massive collection of the memories and knowledge of anyone the staff has ever touched. The attunement bonus from the staff increases to +4, and anyone else gains +2 to applicable rolls. If Heavenly Cage Invitation is active, the phantom can be summoned or banished by a gesture from the holder of the staff. This action is a miscellaneous action in combat. The amount of motes a character recovers each round of combat is limited to the highest of their Occult or Lore while inside the library. While inside the library, the holder can spend a few minutes concentrating to make changes to its layout, such as creating reading rooms, living areas, rearranging shelves and so on, though this is rarely useful in combat.<br /> <br /> Anyone forced inside the library can leave by paying one willpower and willing themselves to do so as a miscellaneous action, rolling (Intelligence + [Lore or Occult]) against a difficulty of (The holders Essence - 2). If the holder is conscious, he can oppose this roll reflexively without paying any willpower. Those who entered willingly, or where invited, can leave without a roll, unless the holder wishes to prevent them from doing so. He can also force someone to leave paying on willpower and making the same opposed roll against the targets (Essence \u2013 2). In this case the target does not need to pay any willpower.<br /> <br /> While inside the library, the holder can spend a few minutes concentrating to make changes to its layout, such as creating reading rooms, living areas, rearranging shelves and so on. This ease of access makes it easy to research subjects while inside the library. The interval of any extended action related to researching something using Lore or Occult becomes one hour, unless it would normally be shorter.<br /> <br /> Ematril is hesitant to open its doors, even to a worthy wielder. This evocation can only be used once a season, unless reset by gaining a dot of Lore or Occult, or a new specialty in one of those abilities towards which the wielder pays experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Special:</b> This evocation can only be learned after discovering a great secret of Creation unknown to Ematril, such as the Great Curse or the weakness of one of the Deathlords. After doing so, this evocation is learned for free when all its prerequisites are met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12865-maiflow","name":"MaiFlow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:45:20-08:00","id":1042005,"title":"","content":"So has anyone bothered to index this thread? Like maybe Ferryman you started the Thread it would make things much easier for folks to use if we had an index page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T09:14:33-08:00","id":1042465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1042005#post1042005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So has anyone bothered to index this thread? Like maybe Ferryman you started the Thread it would make things much easier for folks to use if we had an index page.</div> </div> </div> </div>I applaud the desire, but how would you even organize them? By author? By weapon-type? By Artifact level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T10:26:17-08:00","id":1042502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1042005#post1042005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So has anyone bothered to index this thread? Like maybe Ferryman you started the Thread it would make things much easier for folks to use if we had an index page.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been considering it, but a couple of things have given me pause so far. The biggest barrier is simply the time it would require to do it. When I find myself wanting to sit down and work on Exalted, it's usually to plan the game that I'm running rather than organizing this thread. I'd like to, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T20:01:03-08:00","id":1042767,"title":"","content":"Perhaps organize it by Level, and then by who they harmonize with? But at least organizing by level, and having all the names/links in one spot would be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T06:20:43-08:00","id":1042900,"title":"","content":"Most of the artifacts on here are weapons or armor of some kind, so it would make sense to index them by type, if such a job is to be done. How granular it should be could be debated, but organizing them in something along the lines of &quot;Melee&quot;, &quot;Ranged&quot;, Possibly with &quot;Thrown&quot; as another section seems logical. Other artifacts are mostly a minority and could probably fit under a &quot;Misc&quot; category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12865-maiflow","name":"MaiFlow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T06:43:58-08:00","id":1042907,"title":"","content":"I can add most of the <a href=\"http://exalted3e.wikidot.com/ae:the-three-burials-shroud\" target=\"_blank\">Evocation</a> here to the wiki if people want ~","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 02-03-2017, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T09:35:40-08:00","id":1042996,"title":"","content":"If you want to Jen, you have my permission to add all of mine there, though they're probably easier to pull from my website, linked in my signature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T10:37:33-08:00","id":1043029,"title":"","content":"I'd be fine with my evocations being added to the wiki. For convenience, they're all <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=897187#post897187\">here</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=912889#post912889\">here</a>, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1040195#post1040195\">here</a>. I just made some revisions to the third one, the Kraken's Nail, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1543-iethloc","name":"Iethloc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1543_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T07:00:15-08:00","id":1043522,"title":"","content":"Is this <a href=\"http://exalted3e.wikidot.com/ae:affable-crag-leaves\" target=\"_blank\">format </a>readable for you guys ? Better ask first before creating a bunch of pages that burns people eyes out...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T07:15:03-08:00","id":1043529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1043522#post1043522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this <a href=\"http://exalted3e.wikidot.com/ae:affable-crag-leaves\" target=\"_blank\">format </a>readable for you guys ? Better ask first before creating a bunch of pages that burns people eyes out...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah that looks swell. I am unfamiliar with this wiki. So without an official wiki I take it things are insanely divided online?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T07:32:33-08:00","id":1043537,"title":"","content":"There is only 3 wiki about Exalted at the moment so I wouldn't say that it's insanely divided. Plus this wiki is focused on Ex3 and the UI is pretty newbie-friendly so I decided to use it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 02-04-2017, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:26:35-08:00","id":1045386,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m working on the final evocation for a fairly complex 5-dot artifact one of my players purchased, and could use some outside input on how it should function.<br /> <br /> The artifact concept is a daiklave constructed out of the dragonfly wing of a raksha lord, transmuted into a blade via Wyld-shaping charms to imprison him in a tortured stasis for all time. Each charm in the tree is keyed to a Grace, a spiritual focus comprising one of the raksha\u2019s Virtues, with a power themed accordingly, which can be purchased after cultivating a relevant Intimacy \u2013 what would have been getting a 4+ in the relevant virtue in 1e/2e. I\u2019ll post the whole thing here if there\u2019s any interest.<br /> <br /> The charm I\u2019m working on now is the capstone. Conceptually, it\u2019s about forcing open the raksha\u2019s sealed up Virtue-eating Graces, waking it up enough to realize it\u2019s starving and imprisoned, and letting it rip the consciousness and dream-stuff out of anyone sufficiently heroic to provide it with sustenance. It\u2019s an ongoing Willpower and Intimacy drain on multiple targets acting on a separate initiative tick, and the more it drains, the more it charges up the other four evocations. The drawback is that the more Willpower / Intimacies it drinks, the harder it is to <i><i>turn it off</i>,</i> and if it gets enough to first open all four evocations, then unlock the fifth, the imprisoned raksha escapes the sword by fashioning a god-monster body and porting his Heart Grace over to it, then going on a Wyld-spewing kaiju rampage.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m currently struggling with two issues: <i><b>targeting</b></i> the Willpower drain, and <i><b>pacing</b></i> the rate of evocation buffs and the eventual \u201cOh shit I created a behemoth\u201d doomsday clock. The two are so closely linked that I\u2019m having trouble pulling them apart.<br /> <br /> <u>Targeting:</u> Who gets hit by the Willpower drain, and why? I want it to be algorithmic rather than controlled by the swordsman, but predictable in such a way that it can be manipulated through clever play. Is it based on something the target <i>does</i>, like mote or Willpower expenditure that draws the raksha\u2019s attention? Is it based on something the target <i>is / has</i>, like a Major or Defining Intimacy \u2013 possibly ones the raksha is particularly interested in, such as ones related to Valor (personal prowess and greatness, terror and dissolution, etc.) or Conviction (upholding a principle of governance, cultural structure, etc.) ? Or is it based on something that is <i>done to them</i>, like being the target of earlier evocations in the tree? And if multiple targets fit the criteria for draining, can it affect them all on a single turn?<br /> <br /> At the moment I\u2019m inclined to have it be some combination of something the target does, and something they are or have, but I haven\u2019t been able to nail it down yet. Partly that\u2019s because the choice of who gets drained influences\u2026<br /> <br /> <u>Pacing:</u> How quickly does the drain fill up the Grace pools, empower other evocations, and unleash a monster? Given that the pace of any combat serious enough for a capstone evocation to get brought out is probably going to be pretty slow and rocket-tag-y, should the Graces unlock rapidly (a turn or two of successful charging) so that they can actually get used? Or should it be more gradual, so that the PCs have more time to dance on the edge of impending doom, balancing the build-up of the evocations with the growing threat of their own weapon turning against them?<br /> <br /> <u>Other Considerations:</u> The swordsman in question is a Melee- and Presence-focused Eclipse Caste of the \u201cflare up hard and Terrifying Apparition everything\u201d variety, paired up with a pretty standard stealth-archer Night Caste, in a two-player game with long (8+ hour) sessions. Earlier evocations in the tree are:<ul><li>Rush enhancer that penalizes Disengages and prevents some onslaught from resetting.</li> <li>Reflexive Persuade after crashing someone to get them to surrender or switch sides, and empowers them if they do.</li> <li>Bulwark Stance equivalent that substitutes Resolve (+ applicable Intimacies) for Parry, and uses Intimacies to defend unblockable attacks.</li> <li>Expend a resource built up with the other charms to create an AoE environmental hazard / difficult terrain that protects the subject of an Principle Intimacy.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts? Suggestions? This is my first evocation-building attempt, and I've certainly thrown myself into the deep end to learn how to swim, so I'm open to critique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12964-kestral","name":"Kestral","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:23:17-08:00","id":1045423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kestral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1045386#post1045386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m working on the final evocation for a fairly complex 5-dot artifact...<br /> <br /> I\u2019m currently struggling with two issues: <i><b>targeting</b></i> the Willpower drain, and <i><b>pacing</b></i> the rate of evocation buffs and the eventual \u201cOh shit I created a behemoth\u201d doomsday clock. The two are so closely linked that I\u2019m having trouble pulling them apart.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Suggestions? This is my first evocation-building attempt, and I've certainly thrown myself into the deep end to learn how to swim, so I'm open to critique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just thoughts for now. <br /> #1 Creation of a behemoth seems completely out of context to the other evocations seemingly unrelated on any level.I.E. See Shark Jumping. <br /> #2a Ignoring the first problem; Is the behemoth controlled by the player? <br /> #2b If not, is there benefit to the player for slaying the behemoth? <br /> #3 How does the Behemoth relate to intimacies? <br /> #4 Evocation 4 protecting a principle intimacy doesn't make sense, do you mean defining?<br /> #5a Do you have the mechanics of the 4 previous evocations?<br /> #5b if so please post them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:24:55-08:00","id":1045424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1043522#post1043522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this <a href=\"http://exalted3e.wikidot.com/ae:affable-crag-leaves\" target=\"_blank\">format </a>readable for you guys ? Better ask first before creating a bunch of pages that burns people eyes out...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can you create a navigation pane that has links to the beginning of each thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T18:10:42-08:00","id":1045535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maudova</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1045423#post1045423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just thoughts for now.<br /> #1 Creation of a behemoth seems completely out of context to the other evocations seemingly unrelated on any level.I.E. See Shark Jumping.<br /> #2a Ignoring the first problem; Is the behemoth controlled by the player?<br /> #2b If not, is there benefit to the player for slaying the behemoth?<br /> #3 How does the Behemoth relate to intimacies?<br /> #4 Evocation 4 protecting a principle intimacy doesn't make sense, do you mean defining?<br /> #5a Do you have the mechanics of the 4 previous evocations?<br /> #5b if so please post them.</div> </div> </div> </div>#1: It suffers from lack of context. There's lore behind it, but it's irrelevant to anyone outside our game and to mechanics design, so I won't waste anyone's time with it here unless requested.<br /> <br /> #2a: Emphatically not, hence the risk presented by the countdown. The concept is a charm that whose effects are tempting, but which is actively dangerous to keep running too long and inclined to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_meltdown#China_syndrome\" target=\"_blank\">China Syndrome</a> if you aren't careful and a bit lucky.<br /> <br /> #2b: Good question, actually. Killing the damned raksha once and for all, probably. There's what remains of a Lunar trapped in there somewhere too, so they could in theory free what's left of her as a grandiose act of compassion.<br /> <br /> #3: Again, long story. The evocation unlocks are triggered by cultivating intimacies keyed to the virtue the charm represents, either in a form in the sleeping raksha approves of (the easy way) or which it must grudgingly accept (the hard way). It's a very slow, subtle form of manipulation designed to either make the swordsman into itself - beautiful and terrible and heartless and mad - or make its captor do a stupid, terrible, eminently Solar-Great-Curse thing by accidentally or deliberately letting a powerful enemy out of its cage. More directly, the behemoth itself takes its shape from the swordsman's intimacies, and directs its rampage at them.<br /> <br /> #4: A principle is a form of intimacy, as opposed to a tie. Beliefs and ideals for principles, attachments to concrete entities for ties. Read it as &quot;a Defining Principle-type Intimacy.&quot;<br /> <br /> #5a/b: The mechanics are draft-one complete, pending a second-draft pass once the fifth evocation is done. They're in draft form rather than completed write-ups, however, so it would take a lot of formatting and copy-editing to get them in a state where I'd want to post them on a forum. I'm in the midst of that, but I can answer questions about them in detail in the mean time if necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12964-kestral","name":"Kestral","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T22:01:22-08:00","id":1045613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maudova</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1045424#post1045424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Can you create a navigation pane that has links to the beginning of each thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean something like <a href=\"http://exalted3e.wikidot.com/artifacts-with-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this </a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:53:16-08:00","id":1045755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1045613#post1045613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean something like <a href=\"http://exalted3e.wikidot.com/artifacts-with-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this </a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Badass! While I applaud and appreciate the effort to organize stuff, with the emphasis and encouragement on the mixing of magical materials this edition, I feel weird trying to categorize all of these artifacts by material. Just a gut feeling. That said, the work is appreciated and I'm probably the only person who likes to mix magical materials a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:02:23-08:00","id":1045760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1045755#post1045755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Badass! While I applaud and appreciate the effort to organize stuff, with the emphasis and encouragement on the mixing of magical materials this edition, I feel weird trying to categorize all of these artifacts by material. Just a gut feeling. That said, the work is appreciated and I'm probably the only person who likes to mix magical materials a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no no, I didn't create that page, I only link it to Maudova in case they can't find where all the Evocation is listed.<br /> <br /> In what way would you prefer it to be categorized though ? By dots ?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 02-08-2017, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:20:31-08:00","id":1045770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1045760#post1045760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no no, I didn't create that page, I only link it to Maudova in case they can't find where all the Evocation is listed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually yeah, I kind of just figured that out after reading the page a little more.. If an artifact has 2 materials, it lists it twice. Interesting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:07:36-08:00","id":1046094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1045613#post1045613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean something like <a href=\"http://exalted3e.wikidot.com/artifacts-with-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this </a>?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. Like that. It would be less obtrusive if it were a sidebar though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:58:05-08:00","id":1046117,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this breaks up the flow of the discussion, but this is still a workshop right? Here's a few new ones I threw together recently, all once again based off a musical soundtrack.<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ ____________________<br /> <br /> <b>Death Mocking Shroud</b> (***dot) Five Jade Mask<br /> <b>Attunement Cost</b>: 5m<br /> <b>Hearthstone slots:</b> NA<br /> <b>Story:</b><br /> Originally crafted to be a death mask for her husband\u2019s funeral, the item took on a new life when the would be wearer seemingly returned to life. Named the Death Mocking Shroud in celebration of this event, the title quickly took on a new meaning when everything began to spiral out of control. The man who had seemingly returned to life had been missing for close to a decade, but despite the embrace of his wife and children, claimed to be a different man entirely. Whether or not this was a cruel charade or not is lost to time, as the great celebration the renamed reviver threw for unknown reasons quickly became a bloodbath. If there were any survivors, time does not recall them. It does however leave us with this item, burned with the blood of the lover who forged it and the man whom it was for.<br /> The Death Mocking Shroud was originally designed as a death mask, an item that would cover the face of the recently departed as they were sent on to the whatever lies beyond. This mask was as much a work of love as it was of skill and talent. The majority of the mask is comprised of White Jade, giving the appearance of a pale specter. Two great tear like streams of Blue Jade descend from the ovals of Black Jade that surround the eye holes. Bright with passion, or perhaps embarrassment, are two rings of Red Jade, one on each cheek. The interior of the mask is a mirror of the exterior, different only in the fact that where there had once been White Jade flesh, there was now Green Jade flesh. The mask is surprisingly flexible and could be worn with either side facing away from the wears face, but neither side holds even the slightest hint at a gap for one\u2019s mouth. It is considered a great work of art by many, and ownership is a symbol of status within the Scavenger Lands. Who holds it now is unknown, though it is likely to change ownership thrice over within a passing of the season. By what means does it change hands is\u2026 not always pleasant.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations:</b><br /> On attunement the exalt gains no noticeable affects. When attuned and wearing the <i>Death Mocking Shroud</i> however, the exalt must choose to automatically activate one of the evocations <i>\u201cI Know Those Eyes\u201d or \u201cThis Man is Dead.\u201d</i> The evocation activated remains in effect until the mask is removed. <br /> <br /> <b>This Man is Dead</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - (2m x hour) <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute, Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThis man is dead. He is no more. He died a little each day\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> A mask makes the wearer a new person. Does this not mean the person they once were is, in some way, dead? By donning the <i>Death Mocking Shroud</i> the exalt kills the person they once were. All their intimacies, while they still exist, no longer matter to the exalt, and no new intimacies can be instilled. This blissful state of uncaring can only be ended by the removal of the artifact, a feat impossible for an hour after first donning the mask. For an incremental payment of motes when donning the mask initially, the removal can become impossible for great spans of time. Whether this is to escape ones reality, or cut out the feeling heart for the sake of the mission\u2026 is arguable at best.<br /> <br /> <b> I Know Those Eyes</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI know those eyes following me, Dark and familiar and deep as the sea\u2026<br /> I know that face, strange though it seems, Younger and kinder it haunts all my dreams\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The eyes are said to be the window to the soul. No matter the training or mental fortitude none can hide the flash of emotion or spark of passion within their own gateways. So long as the exalt wears the <i>Death Mocking Shroud</i> they can reflexively make a Read Intentions or Profile Character action on any individual they can see the eyes of, gaining 3 none-charm die in the process. If the exalt has an intimacy towards the target, or knew them in a past life (Storyteller digression advised [this does not assume Eidetic Memory includes past lives]) they gain extra die equal to the strength of the intimacy.<br /> <br /> <b>Walk Among the Living</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> none<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>This Man is Dead</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI am a ghost; just a mirage\u2026 Who chases traces of you.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> None notice the passage of the benign spirit. None would notice the passage of the vengeful spirit if the specter could mask their intent. With this, you have learned to be both specter and hider of dark thoughts. The exalt is allowed to make a Stealth action, adding their Resolve as non-charm die. As this evocation can only be used if <i>This Man is Dead </i>is in effect, attempts to raise or lower the exalts Resolve automatically fail.<br /> <br /> <b>Strange Form, Familiar Eyes</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m (5m) <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplement<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>I Know Those Eyes</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cIn eyes once familiar a stranger I see,<br /> With so many words left to say\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Time can change us in many ways. It can find features far better than any disguise ever could. But the eyes\u2026 the eyes never change. The exalt gains 3 non-charm die to a disguise roll, be it themselves or a single individual. By paying the listed additional cost in addition to the base cost the exalt, should they have disguised themselves, will have a disguise flawless to every being of Creation that has not already seen their eyes. Those who have not seen the exalts eyes before will have their attempts to pierce the disguise be non-magic means reduced by 2 successes. Those who have become familiar with the exalts eyes will gain 2 automatic success on attempts to look past the disguise. This evocation can only be used if <i>I Know Those Eyes </i>is active.<br /> <br /> <b>Fool the Stars Above</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>7m <b>Mins: </b>Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>This Man is Dead / Walk Among the Living<br /> <br /> \u201cThe mind plays tricks, You are confused,<br /> The man you seek is long gone!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The mind is a feeble thing, easily tricked by light and sound. The heart is not so easily swain, but for many it is by far an easier task to twist the hearts of others than their own. The exalt may make a reflexive Instill or Inspire action to convince the target that they are not the person they believe them to be. If the exalt has an intimacy towards the target, they make convert that intimacies level of intensity into automatic successes. If the target has intimacies towards the exalt, the intensity of those intimacies are treated as one level lower than normal for the purpose of changing Resolve or Guile. The effect of this evocation lasts until the exalt has enter Extreme Range from the target, Short Range if successfully used on their celestial mate. This evocation can only be used if <i>This Man is Dead</i> is in effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Lovers Take Wing</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>10m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> none<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>I Know Those Eyes / Strange Form, Familiar Eyes<br /> <br /> \u201cMy Gods, my heart beats faster! And my mind is racing\u2026<br /> Could it be\u2026?<br /> Could it be that you\u2019ve come back to life?\u201d</i><br /> <br /> When the heart runs wild, and mind flees from logic, it is the actions of emotions alone that fuel the form. The exalt locks eyes with a target, and until they release this evocation, that target is all they can focus on. Any and all actions related to the target gain 2 non-charm die, while actions not related to the target lose 2 die. Should the action be a Rush, or Defend Other, the exalt gains an additional die for the action. If the exalt has a positive intimacy of major intensity or higher towards the target, they are able to communicate with the target through glances alone for 3 rounds. This evocation can only be used if <i>I Know Those Eyes</i> is in effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Two Faces, One Heart<br /> Cost:</b> 15m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> none<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Fool the Stars Above, Lovers Take Wing<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd why does the truth seem too hard to be true?<br /> With so much broken, And so much damage\u2026<br /> There are no words, Left to say\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Discord and turmoil and burned for long enough. A two faced hero is nothing more than a villain of different colors. Bind together the chaos, or sever it forever. The exalt may use this evocation once, and once only. This evocation has two different effects that the exalt must choose from. <br /> The first effect is to bind together the two facets of the <i>Death Mocking Shroud,</i> removing the requirement to use <i>\u201cThis Man is Dead,\u201d or \u201cI Know Those Eyes\u201d</i> when wearing the artifact or as a prerequisite to other evocations. The artifact also becomes naturally impossible to perceive by non-magic means to all but its attuned user. This invisibly effect is lost if it is not attuned to at all. However, choosing this option removes all benefits granted by intimacies within the previous evocations. <br /> The second effect permanently separates the two facets of the <i>Death Mocking Shroud,</i> effectively rendering the artifact useless. Doing this however, does not only grant the artifacts weight in all five types of Jade, but reveals a core of Starmetal hidden within the masks forehead, large enough to made into a ring if used in its entirety. If the exalt has at least 5 Craft charms, choosing this option generates 15sxp, 10gxp, and 5wxp (see Crafting tables for uses).<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ ___________<br /> <br /> <b>Embrace of the Stardust Oath Keeper</b> (**** dot) Starmetal Chain Shirt<br /> <b>Attunement Cost: </b>4m (+3m)<br /> <b>Hearthstone slots:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <b>Story:</b><br /> An ancient item that has been passed through the hands of many a Chosen of the Maidens hands, even the long records of heaven have forgotten the maker of this wondrous raiment. Forged for a star of Mercury who ran alongside a star of Jupiter long ago, it is believed that the masterwork of Starmetal was created to protect and remind the allies of Jupiter\u2019s Chosen in tasks they alone could not endure the hardships of. Others believe that it was crafted to be a parting gift for a close ally, perhaps something more, of a Chosen of Venus. There are as many tales about this garment as there are stars in the heavens, but only the Chosen of Mars and Mercury have ever been recorded to don the garment in the recent past.<br /> A sleeveless tunic, near a shroud or vest in appearance, it is forest green in color and was once matched with a cloak of Cornwall blue. It is unique among many similar garments as it reflects no light but starlight, even when placed into the heart of great fires or set before the light of the sun. When records appear relating to its former owners, each has claimed in similar words that the garment stills their heart to calmness when worn, as though by the embrace of a loved one. Beyond this though, little else is known about the item; known to anyone aside from its present owner.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations:</b><br /> The flowing, liquid like nature of this armor allows for it to reform itself to include pauldrons, vambraces, bracers, and a great flowing cloak in a moment\u2019s notice. While these can be used to deflect oncoming attacks in the form of blocks and parries, they do not count as true armor. When attuned a Sidereal, Solar, or Lunar Exalted may pay an additional 3m to change the armor from a Chain Shirt to Silken Armor. This payment must be made when donning the armor and is automatically deactivated when crashed.<br /> <br /> <b> Lovers Embrace Anew</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - <b> Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>none<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cIn the light that falls at moonrise, In the rhythm of the rain,</i><br /> <i>In the miracle of ordinary days, In the hush of night,</i><br /> <i>I will be in the whispers of lovers\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Time heals many wounds, but the ever constant wound of true love only grows greater with time and distance. Once donned, the <i>Embrace of the Stardust Oath Keeper </i>recognizes the attuned exalt as though they were a long lost love. Wrapping its body tight around the exalt, the armor applies a reassuring pressure to the body at all times, as though forever held within the arms of another. All social actions that would attempt to threaten or scare the exalt wearing this artifact have their difficulty increased by 2.<br /> <br /> <b> Speechless is the Heart</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m<b> Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> none<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><i>Lovers Embrace Anew</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cIn a language never spoken, With the promises we made</i><br /> <i>In the endless low that owns me heart and soul,</i><br /> <i>In the certainty I will always be true and as near as my next prayer\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> For those that truly care for another, they need not words to communicate\u2026 but the lovers separated know not if their prayers reach their partners ears. The exalt may make a social influence roll that relies on a targets positive intimacy without observable action. The target is unable to act against this social influence roll unless they can observe the intent of this evocation via a Read Intentions action. This action goes unnoticed by the target should it fail, and the same target becomes immune to this evocation for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b> Step Across the Starlight</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m<b> Mins: </b>Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> none<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Speechless is the Heart</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cIn the rustle of a curtain, In the bustle of the world,</i><br /> <i>In a thousand little unexpected ways, When you lift your gaze,</i><br /> <i>I will be like the shimmer of one small star!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> One came run a million miles again and again when Mercury and Venus work in turn. Only Jupiter knows how far one most run to reach their goals. This evocation supplements an athletics roll related to running, or a stealth roll related to crowds and similar conditions. These actions gain (Essence) non-charm dice under normal circumstances. If there is no other light source out to Long Range of the exalt aside from the moon and stars, these actions gain (Essence) automatic successes instead.<br /> <br /> <b> Wave Bending Practice</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m<b> Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> none<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><i>Speechless is the Heart</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cIn the echo of the ocean, In the haunting of the wind,</i><br /> <i>In mysterious extraordinary ways, Through the darkest sky,</i><br /> <i>I will be like the shimmer of one small star!\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Everyone has been given a mission once in their many lifetimes that must be seen to the end, no matter what may come to cut them down. The armor has seen too many of these missions and the carnage they cause its beloved bearer; so it has learned to move its bearer before they themselves realize they need to move. For the remainder of the scene, so long as <i>Embrace of the Stardust Oath Keeper</i> does not change its form (see attunement bonus) it forgoes defense in favor for the ability to avoid conflict. Soak granted by this artifact is reduced by 2, but the exalts evasion increases by (Essence/2 round up) to make up for this loss.<br /> <br /> <b> Oath Keepers Welcomed Companion</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - (10m) <b> Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>none<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Step Across the Starlight, Wave Bending Practice</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cI will be there,</i><br /> <i>Beside you, Through the lonely nights that fall,</i><br /> <i>So close your eyes\u2026</i><br /> <i>Remember my embrace!</i><br /> <i>I will be there.</i><br /> <i>Like mercy! / Like freedom! / Like justice!</i><br /> <i>I will find you through it all!</i><br /> <i>This do I swear\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Those who have love and lost have lost more than their time and trust. Those who have loved and lost and continue to love show fortitude, or foolishness worthy of praise. The exalt has become that fool. On purchasing this evocation the exalt makes a roll of (Essence + 4) against a target number assigned by the Storyteller. Should they succeed, the artifact has whispered to its owner the legend or location of something wondrous, such as a First Age Solar Manse that a previous owner of the artifact has encountered. The exalt does not receive more than the knowledge of the wonders existence unless they pledge an oath to the artifact, stating that they will show it something of equal or greater slender somewhere in the whole of Creation. Should the exalt fail the initial roll, be unable to keep their oath (or the Storyteller does not wish to create such a secondary plot line) the exalt can pay 10m while wearing the artifact to scan the stars for an answer to a single question. If the question has an answer that Fate is willing to disclose, the exalt will receive the information in the sound of tinkling bells emanating from the artifact, spelling out a riddle that only they can hear. However, once this question is asked, whether or not the exalt receives an answer, the artifact ceases to have any magical attributes until the next time is bathed completely in starlight. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Enjoy the moment with all your might,<br /> Whether its gloomy, whether its bright.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12786-libaros","name":"Libaros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T16:57:16-08:00","id":1047988,"title":"","content":"Having difficulty imagining the starting evocation for an Artifact Spine of the Moons Shadow Level Three Grimcleaver I'm thinking for Solars and Lunars may spend an initiative to obfuscate the weapon with shadows and its rippling making those attacked by it to suffer a minus two sense penalty to defend against it unless they succeed in an Awareness perception roll difficulty of the wielders wits.? Maybe spend an initiative to get it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T01:08:31-08:00","id":1048117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1047988#post1047988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having difficulty imagining the starting evocation for an Artifact Spine of the Moons Shadow Level Three Grimcleaver I'm thinking for Solars and Lunars may spend an initiative to obfuscate the weapon with shadows and its rippling making those attacked by it to suffer a minus two sense penalty to defend against it unless they succeed in an Awareness perception roll difficulty of the wielders wits.? Maybe spend an initiative to get it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds pretty much like an altered version of Foe-Vaulting Method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:50:02-08:00","id":1053206,"title":"","content":"So, I wanted to make an Artifact for one of my players \u2013 a Combat Crafter \u2013 which supplements their character concept by bringing Combat and Craft a little closer together. It's their first Exalted game, and we've been rolling in prologue mode for a while, but they're about to Exalt as a Twilight as they enter their soon-to-be past incarnation's Library-Tomb and grasp the following artifact.<br /> <br /> The character is a Guild Artisan blacksmith, mostly concerned with Money (defining: I will seek profit) and Lore (Major: Conservation of Knowledge). They fight with a sledge-hammer and have Melee 5, 4 charms and Specialty. (Also: Craft 5, 9 charms and a specialty)<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a rough draft (more of a general direction really) and I would appreciate input and suggestions, as I'm not at all sure of the balance of the thing.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Kamenkraft, hammer of the Ever-Hearth. Artifact \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <br /> Kamenkraft is an Orichalcum Grand Gore-Maul with an ever-burning Red Jade core. Its design is reminiscent of a highly stylized forge.<br /> Kamenkraft itself is an impatient brute of an artisan, quick to anger and eager to start and complete artisanal works. While it is a grand-goremaul, attuned crafters find Kamenkraft surprisingly wieldly and accurate as a forging tool, its many edges and protrusions perfectly suited towards all manner of delicate and precise work. Its essence seems to permeate crafting materials in a manner that brings to mind Craftsman Needs No Tools, though this power is turned to different ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Burning Everforge</b><br /> Type: permanent<br /> Kamenkraft comes with its own Major Crafting Slot. On a Join Battle roll, if the slot is empty it can be filled; if not, the project can be changed (cancelled and re-chosen, or simply modified). At the end of combat, if the slot has a project and Kamenkraft has enough stored materials, the Project can be rolled for completion. Every time Kamenkraft doesn't successfully craft something during or at the end of a combat, its Hearth cools down and its Evocations become unusable. The Everforge is re-ignited only by crashing an opponent or completing a Crafting project with an Exceptional Success.<br /> <b>Special Activation:</b> This evocation is acquired for free upon completing a Major, Superior or Legendary project with an Exceptional Success while in the presence of Kamenkraft.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insatiable Hunger</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Duration: Until next action<br /> Kamenkraft glows molten-hot and its Orichalcum begins to flow like thick molasses. Successfully parrying mortal weapons destroys them entirely as Kamenkraft snares them in its churning Orichalcum, breaking them down into raw materials for use in crafting. Every snared weapon generates 2 initiative and 2 temporary sxp which, if not used, fades at the end of the scene.<br /> Artifacts are not destroyed instantly, they remain retrievable with a difficulty 4 gambit until the end of the Scene, and resist the melting power for the rest of the story. If the Artifact is retrieved, those initiative and cxp points are lost. At the end of the Scene, the artfact sinks into Kamenkraft's Everforge, where only the Crafter (and weapon-teleportation Charms) can retrieve it. At the end of the Story, they are unmade into purified components and magical materials.<br /> These materials exist Elsewhere and can be called forth for any Project in which Kamenkraft is used, including Evocations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Inspiration in Violence</b><br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Kamenkraft's Ever-hearth roars with heat and gutters with flame, burning with the heat of creation as it strikes. If this attack Crashes or slays a foe, it generates [Craft] temporary sxp and heats up Kamenkraft's forge with a cumulative +1 non-charm damage bonus, up to [The wielder's preferred Craft rating], until the end of the next round. If this causes an Initiative Shift, this Evocation also generates temporary sxp equal to the successes on the wielder's Join Battle roll. Activating Insatiable Hunger also prolongs this effect.<br /> <br /> This damage bonus applies both to Withering and Decisive attacks made with Kamenkraft. Going into Crash resets this damage bonus to 0, but does not prevent it from being built up again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Forged in conflict</b><br /> Cost: 3m or 5m + 10sxp<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Health Levels of Damage dealt by the supplemented attack are treated as Craft succeses divided among any number of Basic Projects (minimum of 1 each). If a foe is killed using this Evocation (and Kamenkraft has the appropriate Materials, including those on the slain foe's person) the character may pay an extra 2 motes and 10 sxp for these successes to be used to complete the Project in Kamenkraft's Major Slot and, if completed, a new project may be chosen immediately, either by the wielder or by Kamenkraft itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You get made into a bone-statue! And YOU get made into a bone-statue! YOU ALL GET MADE INTO BONE-STATUES!! </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-22-2017, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T18:35:16-08:00","id":1053564,"title":"","content":"I like this hammer a lot, but you might want to include some essence requirements for the later charms, I would suggest Essence 2 for Insatiable Hunger, and Essence 3 for the other 2. Also Inspiration in Violence should not be a simple charm, permanent or reflexive for a scene sound fine. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1053206#post1053206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I wanted to make an Artifact for one of my players \u2013 a Combat Crafter \u2013 which supplements their character concept by bringing Combat and Craft a little closer together. It's their first Exalted game, and we've been rolling in prologue mode for a while, but they're about to Exalt as a Twilight as they enter their soon-to-be past incarnation's Library-Tomb and grasp the following artifact.<br /> <br /> The character is a Guild Artisan blacksmith, mostly concerned with Money (defining: I will seek profit) and Lore (Major: Conservation of Knowledge). They fight with a sledge-hammer and have Melee 5, 4 charms and Specialty. (Also: Craft 5, 9 charms and a specialty)<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a rough draft (more of a general direction really) and I would appreciate input and suggestions, as I'm not at all sure of the balance of the thing.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Kamenkraft, hammer of the Ever-Hearth. Artifact \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> <br /> Kamenkraft is an Orichalcum Grand Gore-Maul with an ever-burning Red Jade core. Its design is reminiscent of a highly stylized forge.<br /> Kamenkraft itself is an impatient brute of an artisan, quick to anger and eager to start and complete artisanal works. While it is a grand-goremaul, attuned crafters find Kamenkraft surprisingly wieldly and accurate as a forging tool, its many edges and protrusions perfectly suited towards all manner of delicate and precise work. Its essence seems to permeate crafting materials in a manner that brings to mind Craftsman Needs No Tools, though this power is turned to different ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Burning Everforge</b><br /> Type: permanent<br /> Kamenkraft comes with its own Major Crafting Slot. On a Join Battle roll, if the slot is empty it can be filled; if not, the project can be changed (cancelled and re-chosen, or simply modified). At the end of combat, if the slot has a project and Kamenkraft has enough stored materials, the Project can be rolled for completion. Every time Kamenkraft doesn't successfully craft something during or at the end of a combat, its Hearth cools down and its Evocations become unusable. The Everforge is re-ignited only by crashing an opponent or completing a Crafting project with an Exceptional Success.<br /> <b>Special Activation:</b> This evocation is acquired for free upon completing a Major, Superior or Legendary project with an Exceptional Success while in the presence of Kamenkraft.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Insatiable Hunger</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Duration: Until next action<br /> Kamenkraft glows molten-hot and its Orichalcum begins to flow like thick molasses. Successfully parrying mortal weapons destroys them entirely as Kamenkraft snares them in its churning Orichalcum, breaking them down into raw materials for use in crafting. Every snared weapon generates 2 initiative and 2 temporary sxp which, if not used, fades at the end of the scene.<br /> Artifacts are not destroyed instantly, they remain retrievable with a difficulty 4 gambit until the end of the Scene, and resist the melting power for the rest of the story. If the Artifact is retrieved, those initiative and cxp points are lost. At the end of the Scene, the artfact sinks into Kamenkraft's Everforge, where only the Crafter (and weapon-teleportation Charms) can retrieve it. At the end of the Story, they are unmade into purified components and magical materials.<br /> These materials exist Elsewhere and can be called forth for any Project in which Kamenkraft is used, including Evocations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Inspiration in Violence</b><br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Kamenkraft's Ever-hearth roars with heat and gutters with flame, burning with the heat of creation as it strikes. If this attack Crashes or slays a foe, it generates [Craft] temporary sxp and heats up Kamenkraft's forge with a cumulative +1 non-charm damage bonus, up to [The wielder's preferred Craft rating], until the end of the next round. If this causes an Initiative Shift, this Evocation also generates temporary sxp equal to the successes on the wielder's Join Battle roll. Activating Insatiable Hunger also prolongs this effect.<br /> <br /> This damage bonus applies both to Withering and Decisive attacks made with Kamenkraft. Going into Crash resets this damage bonus to 0, but does not prevent it from being built up again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Forged in conflict</b><br /> Cost: 3m or 5m + 10sxp<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Health Levels of Damage dealt by the supplemented attack are treated as Craft succeses divided among any number of Basic Projects (minimum of 1 each). If a foe is killed using this Evocation (and Kamenkraft has the appropriate Materials, including those on the slain foe's person) the character may pay an extra 2 motes and 10 sxp for these successes to be used to complete the Project in Kamenkraft's Major Slot and, if completed, a new project may be chosen immediately, either by the wielder or by Kamenkraft itself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T07:07:58-08:00","id":1057075,"title":"","content":"Hello<br /> <br /> I'm working on a Twilight's armor and my player want the attunement power to be kind of a &quot;sublimation&quot; of his anima's power which give him Hardness.<br /> <br /> If he use his anima's power with his armor attuned, he wants to have Hardness = 5+x instead of Hardness = 5<br /> <br /> Does it look OP ? If not, what number could be x ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T18:04:45-08:00","id":1058225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1057075#post1057075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello<br /> <br /> I'm working on a Twilight's armor and my player want the attunement power to be kind of a &quot;sublimation&quot; of his anima's power which give him Hardness.<br /> <br /> If he use his anima's power with his armor attuned, he wants to have Hardness = 5+x instead of Hardness = 5<br /> <br /> Does it look OP ? If not, what number could be x ?</div> </div> </div> </div>One question I have is what kind of armor is it? is it silken armor? Is it Orichalcum super heavy plate? or is it something like 2ed's Discreet Essence Armor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13093-inksplatterm","name":"inksplatterm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T13:23:39-07:00","id":1062455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inksplatterm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1058225#post1058225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question I have is what kind of armor is it? is it silken armor? Is it Orichalcum super heavy plate? or is it something like 2ed's Discreet Essence Armor?</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact he found an illustration from Magic the Gathering which exactly fit his vision of the armor:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/images/g5uyxo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/images/g5uyxo\" target=\"_blank\"> Redirect Notice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/images/g5uyxo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://goo.gl/images/g5uyxo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">It looks like to be an orichalcum armor but not a superheavy one<br /> <br /> Sorry for taking so much time to answer but my player didn't remember the name of the card which inspire this artifact</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T15:39:32-07:00","id":1064963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1062455#post1062455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact he found an illustration from Magic the Gathering which exactly fit his vision of the armor:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/images/g5uyxo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/images/g5uyxo\" target=\"_blank\"> Redirect Notice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://goo.gl/images/g5uyxo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://goo.gl/images/g5uyxo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">It looks like to be an orichalcum armor but not a superheavy one<br /> <br /> Sorry for taking so much time to answer but my player didn't remember the name of the card which inspire this artifact</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. So from the image, I'm guessing that the best armor &quot;template&quot; that you'd work on is a breastplate, by which I mean that while you have some aesthetic changes, such as the bracelets from the picture, you'd be using the stats for artifact light armor.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, then it's not OP in my opinion, and you can have some fun eventually developing evocations for it. I'd put that &quot;X&quot; could be the character's permanent essence. So for an essence 1 character, it'd just be a hardness of 6, but will have increasing returns as his character levels up. The hardness 6 is then also on top of the hardness of light artifact armor (4), so up to you if you want the two hardness ratings to stack or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13093-inksplatterm","name":"inksplatterm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T01:58:26-07:00","id":1065143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inksplatterm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1064963#post1064963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No worries. So from the image, I'm guessing that the best armor &quot;template&quot; that you'd work on is a breastplate, by which I mean that while you have some aesthetic changes, such as the bracelets from the picture, you'd be using the stats for artifact light armor.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, then it's not OP in my opinion, and you can have some fun eventually developing evocations for it. I'd put that &quot;X&quot; could be the character's permanent essence. So for an essence 1 character, it'd just be a hardness of 6, but will have increasing returns as his character levels up. The hardness 6 is then also on top of the hardness of light artifact armor (4), so up to you if you want the two hardness ratings to stack or not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with the Artifact Light Armor and I really like the idea of the &quot;X&quot; evolving with the Character's Permanent Essence. I've always loved the concept of artifacts evolving in parallel with the power of his bearer.<br /> <br /> I also note that the two hardness (Anima and Artifact) can stack ? Is that at the ST discretion ? Because I've always believed that it doesn't stack","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T10:25:16-07:00","id":1065301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1065143#post1065143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree with the Artifact Light Armor and I really like the idea of the &quot;X&quot; evolving with the Character's Permanent Essence. I've always loved the concept of artifacts evolving in parallel with the power of his bearer.<br /> <br /> I also note that the two hardness (Anima and Artifact) can stack ? Is that at the ST discretion ? Because I've always believed that it doesn't stack</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I double checked the guide. the base rules do say that various Hardness levels don't stack &quot;unless it explicitly says so&quot; (EX3, pg 195), and the Twilight's anima power explicitly can't be stacked with other Hardness raising magic (EX3, pg 176). (Can argue your armor power idea gets around that becuase the power of the armor is not stacking with the Anima power, really, but making a way to improve upon it.)<br /> <br /> So the answer is yes and no. Yes, it is up to ST discretion when you're making up new artifacts becuase you can explicitly write in the powers of your homebrew artifact that the Hardness stacks, but in general every Hardness source is it's own thing and the player can choose which Hardness source to use against a decisive attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13093-inksplatterm","name":"inksplatterm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T23:09:20-07:00","id":1068194,"title":"","content":"I am absolutely horrible with trying to come up with custom Charms and Evocations. I can never seem to be able to balance the costs with the effects for the powers. I have a character in a 3e game that our Storyteller has allowed me to have the Infinite Resplendence Amulet from DotFA, and I'm trying to ponder up some Evocations that might be in line with it. Can anyone help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13139-sherwood","name":"Sherwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T02:13:13-07:00","id":1068225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sherwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1068194#post1068194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am absolutely horrible with trying to come up with custom Charms and Evocations. I can never seem to be able to balance the costs with the effects for the powers. I have a character in a 3e game that our Storyteller has allowed me to have the Infinite Resplendence Amulet from DotFA, and I'm trying to ponder up some Evocations that might be in line with it. Can anyone help?</div> </div> </div> </div>The big question would be 'what do you want it to do?'. For a start, the IRA's basic abilities shift a bit depending on its magical material. Secondly, most evocations are things that trigger through active use. an IRA is a quickchange device, running through different costumes and outfits. How would you use your clothes for Unimaginable Magical Power?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T07:06:49-07:00","id":1070032,"title":"","content":"So, one of my players \u2013 a Twilight Sijanese Deadspeaker and Martial Artist (Funerary-flavoured DPC) who'll pick up Sorcery or Necromancy soonish (depending on his character arc) \u2013 has these Soulsteel <a href=\"http://i.ebayimg.com/images/i/400535657203-0-1/s-l1000.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Mala beads</a> which we treat as a Dire Chain that's compatible with DPC. They come from the defiled tomb of a buried client (who secretly asked the PC to steal them after the burial for ~mysterious reasons~).<br /> <br /> Problem is, neither of us have any idea of what they could do; not even if they should have Evocations or a one-off effect (they're rated 3 so are capable of Evocations). The player doesn't really have a preference and I'm getting blank page syndrome.<br /> <br /> Brainstorming/ideas would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 03-29-2017, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T13:10:35-07:00","id":1070253,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://\u200bhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F1Vgu237AbU\" target=\"_blank\">Beads, you say?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T12:24:03-07:00","id":1071781,"title":"","content":"So this is my first attempt at making an artifact and evocations in 3e, so I'm looking for feedback <br /> <br /> Edge of Clarity<br /> 4 point White Jade and Orichalcum Daiklave<br /> <br /> Razu-Khan was known as the Scholar King in the early days of his life, for he spent much of his formative years collecting scrolls, tomes, and books from every corner of creation. Even Twilight's grew envious of his massive libraries.<br /> <br /> The only thing greater than his libraries was his talent of awareness. Nothing escaped his notice. What started as simply rooting out treachery and preventing theft from his precious libraries, soon blossomed into full paranoia and pettiness, as every imagined conspiracy or minor slight became reason for retribution. <br /> <br /> To facilitate this, Razu-Khan commissioned a Daiklaive, to help hunt and slay his foes.<br /> <br /> Upon attunement, I get an extra die on join battle rolls. If I'm facing an opponent I've struck before, it becomes an automatic success <br /> <br /> First evocation, which if you're alright with unlocks when I attune (seems alright given some of the other artifacts at level 4 do the same thing)<br /> <br /> Inescapable Vengeance <br /> Cost: 3m, 1wp<br /> Mins: 1 essence<br /> Type: Reflexive <br /> Duration: Special<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> Upon striking an enemy, or up to 24 hours after, the exalt can attune 3 motes to this evocation. While attuned, it becomes almost impossible to escape the exalts wrath. I automatically succeed at any tracking checks difficulty 2 or less, and I add my essence in automatic successes to any other tracking checks. Distance is no longer a factor. So long as the opponent is on the face of creation, they are able to be tracked, even over water.<br /> This automatically fails if the opponent leaves creation. If they enter a shadowland, or the border marshes, then this charm will take me to the closest border, but will not function any further.<br /> <br /> Unrelenting Stalker<br /> Cost: 5m<br /> Requirements: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Duration: Special<br /> Prerequisites: Inescapable Vengeance<br /> So long as the attuned exalt is pursuing the opponent for which the previous evocation is focused on,the earth itself seeks to help. So long as travel only takes place on solid ground, travel times are halved for the exalt. 2 additional motes may be committed per additional traveler, so long as their goal is the same. <br /> This has no effect on air or water travel, and ceases to function if the exalt is unable to track the opponent (say, because they have left creation, though it will function up to the border of a shadowland or border marshes)<br /> <br /> Defense rending strike<br /> Cost: 3m, 1wp<br /> Requirement: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental <br /> Duration: Instant <br /> Prerequisite: Unrelenting Stalker<br /> When your foe is finally within your grasp, nothing can slow their destruction. The next withering attack supplemented by this charm ignores (essence x 2) of an opponents armor rating. <br /> <br /> That's what I have so far. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11839-cofdave","name":"CofDave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T00:57:16-07:00","id":1071949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofDave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1071781#post1071781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Upon attunement, I get an extra die on join battle rolls. If I'm facing an opponent I've struck before, it becomes an automatic success</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Feels somewhat uninspired and also not particularly beneficial for someone who's supposedly a master of Awareness. Your first big JB enhancer is Awakening Eye, which gives you a full excellency (therefore the bonus die becomes irrelevant except in fights where you don't want to go all-out) <i>and</i> cascading rerolls. Since automatic successes count against the Charm cap as two dice, a master of Awareness is actually <i>worse off</i> by using this sword against an opponent they've struck before - the result of two dice will average out to one success, but replacing them with a success locks you out of the rerolls you potentially could've gotten out of them, therefore lowering the value you get out of Awakening Eye.<br /> <br /> Here's what I recommend:<br /> <br /> &quot;A Solar or Dragon-Blooded who attunes to Edge of Clarity can double a single 9 on join battle rolls. If she joins battle against an opponent she has tracked or stalked before, double an 8 instead. If said opponent has also personally wronged her in the past, double a 7 instead.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is basically an extra success that doesn't count against Charm limits. The first tier of the benefit is obviated by Sensory Acuity Prana, but it's not cost-efficient to use SAP in every single fight, so who cares.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofDave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1071781#post1071781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inescapable Vengeance<br /> Cost: 3m, 1wp<br /> Mins: 1 essence<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Duration: Special<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> Upon striking an enemy, or up to 24 hours after, the exalt can attune 3 motes to this evocation. While attuned, it becomes almost impossible to escape the exalts wrath. I automatically succeed at any tracking checks difficulty 2 or less, and I add my essence in automatic successes to any other tracking checks. Distance is no longer a factor. So long as the opponent is on the face of creation, they are able to be tracked, even over water.<br /> This automatically fails if the opponent leaves creation. If they enter a shadowland, or the border marshes, then this charm will take me to the closest border, but will not function any further.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Almost the same effect but worded better:<br /> <br /> &quot;...Duration: Indefinite...<br /> Upon striking an enemy, or up to 24 hours after, the Exalt can activate this Evocation, making it almost impossible to avoid her wrath. Add (Essence or 2, whichever is higher) to tracking rolls. Distance is no longer a factor...&quot;<br /> <br /> Explanation: <br /> - You attune to Artifacts, not Charms. The precise wording is &quot;commit motes to [Charm/Evocation]&quot;, but the mote cost of Charms with any duration other than Instant is always committed, making it redundant to explicitly spell that out in the text as well.<br /> - Adding 2 auto-successes to a tracking roll causes you to automatically succeed on difficulty 2 or less, and really, having the Charm give you +1 success for 10 sessions (ie. until you hit Essence 2), compared to the original writeup is not such a huge change to meaningfully affect balance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofDave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1071781#post1071781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelenting Stalker<br /> Cost: 5m<br /> Requirements: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Duration: Special<br /> Prerequisites: Inescapable Vengeance<br /> So long as the attuned exalt is pursuing the opponent for which the previous evocation is focused on,the earth itself seeks to help. So long as travel only takes place on solid ground, travel times are halved for the exalt. 2 additional motes may be committed per additional traveler, so long as their goal is the same.<br /> This has no effect on air or water travel, and ceases to function if the exalt is unable to track the opponent (say, because they have left creation, though it will function up to the border of a shadowland or border marshes)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Duration should be Indefinite, and it's &quot;bordermarches&quot;, not &quot;border marshes&quot;. Otherwise this seems okay.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofDave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1071781#post1071781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defense rending strike<br /> Cost: 3m, 1wp<br /> Requirement: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: Unrelenting Stalker<br /> When your foe is finally within your grasp, nothing can slow their destruction. The next withering attack supplemented by this charm ignores (essence x 2) of an opponents armor rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>- Defense-Rending should be hyphenated.<br /> - Essence*2 can be anything between 4 and 10, but considering that Shattering Strike lets you ignore 8 for 2m 1wp, I would say this is on the underpowered side, if anything.<br /> - The correct term is &quot;armored soak&quot;, not &quot;armor rating&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T20:49:28-07:00","id":1072345,"title":"","content":"I'm a little stuck with crafting a spear with one of my players, with a character concept of &quot;Combat Librarian&quot;. She's pretty open with what she wants out of it (throw lightning) and is excited about my suggestions to expand beyond that (effective against ghosts, elementals, and demons). But I kinda feel stumped with ideas on putting it together into a set of evocations. Currently I have three, but would like to have one or two more. I would love advice/constructive crit/any sort of comment. (&quot;??&quot; is a place holder for something undecided)<br /> <br /> <b>Surge</b><br /> Blue Jade Longfang, 3-dot Artifact<br /> Medium artifact weapon<br /> Tags: Lethal, Melee, Thrown (short), Piercing<br /> <br /> <i>summary of origin</i>: Product of very early shogunate artifact creation, made immediately post-Usurpation. Slightly incomplete. Impatience imprinted into the longfang, along with collected lightning strikes. Has a white jade &quot;grounding&quot; handle on the butt end, and a setting for one hearthstone just below the head.<br /> <br /> When Surge is used in a successful withering attack, the target of that attack needs to make a (Resistance + Stamina) roll, at difficulty 3. If they fail the roll, the target takes a -2 penalty to any rolls made on their next action, because of the lightning coursing through them.<br /> So long as there is no hearthstone set into Surge, its wielder must also make that (Resistance + Stamina) roll, with the same penalty should they fail the roll, at the beginning of their turn in combat while they are holding Surge, and before every non-combat action where they are going to use Surge.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations for Surge</b><br /> <i>Special activation</i>: Evocations may not be awakened if Surge lacks a hearthstone. Once a hearthstone is set into surge, the wielder may work to awaken the longfang's evocations. Also, the hearthstone cannot use its innate ability while set into Surge.<br /> <br /> <b>Ride the Lightning</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp. Mins: Essence 1.<br /> Type: Reflexive. Tags: none.<br /> Duration: one hour<br /> prerequisites: none<br /> <br /> Mechanics as the athletics charm &quot;Racing Hare Method&quot; (Exalted, pg 264).<br /> <br /> <b>Static Cage</b><br /> Cost: 3m, 1 wp. Mins: Essence 2.<br /> Type: Simple Tags: none.<br /> Duration: concentration<br /> Prerequisites: none <br /> <br /> Surge's wielder strikes the ground with the butt of the longfang, and crates a bars of stable lightning around a spirit, materialized or de-materialized, that she sees/senses. Spirit, in this case, means a ghost, a demon, or an elemental. The trapped spirit cannot move, is forced to materialize if they aren't already, and must make a (Resistance + Stamina) roll at difficulty equal to the wielder's Resolve stat. If they fail the roll, they take must follow 1 simple order given by Surge's wielder or truthfully answer 3 questions. If they succeed, they take no penalty, and if they have extra successes equal to or exceeding Surge's wielder's permanent essence score, the cage breaks. After a success that does not break the cage, Surge's wielder may spend 3m more to make the trapped spirit roll (Resistance + Stamina) again.<br /> The wielder may also dismiss Static Cage when they wish.<br /> <br /> <b>Thunderbolt</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp. Mins: Essence 3.<br /> Type: Simple Tags: Aggravated, Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: instant<br /> Prerequisites: Ride the Lightning, Static Cage<br /> <br /> With a shout, Surge's wielder summons a spark of lightning within Surge and fires it into their opponent. <br /> If within close or short range, the attack is made with (Dexterity + Melee), but if it's made from Medium or long range, the attack uses (Dexterity + Thrown). In either case, the decisive attack does aggravated damage with a base damage equal to the attack roll's successes. The attack ignores hardness, and cannot be blocked or dodged without the use of a Charm. It does not include initiative in it's damage roll, but it does reset initiative to base. <br /> <br /> special activation rules: After Thunderbolt is used, Surge needs to be recharged before it can use Thunderbolt again. To achieve this recharge, Surge may either be left out in a thunderstorm to be struck by lightning, or it cannot be used at all in the next two combat scenes. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13093-inksplatterm","user":"inksplatterm","date":".  made edits after comments by The Unsung Hero. Thanks again! 04-03-2017, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13093-inksplatterm","name":"inksplatterm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T08:09:31-07:00","id":1072546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>inksplatterm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1072345#post1072345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Thunderbolt</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 3i, 1wp. Mins: Essence 3.<br /> Type: Simple Tags: Aggravated, Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: instant<br /> Prerequisites: Ride the Lightning, Static Cage<br /> <br /> With a shout, Surge's wielder summons a spark of lightning within Surge and fires it into their opponent.<br /> If within close or short range, the attack is made with (Dexterity + Melee), but if it's made from Medium or long range, the attack uses (Dexterity + Thrown). In either case, the decisive attack does aggravated damage with a base damage of the attack roll's successes. The attack ignores hardness, and cannot be blocked or dodged without the use of a Charm. It does not include initiative in it's damage roll, but it does reset initiative to base.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The only part that really caught my attention was this last evocation. It doesn't use initiative for the damage roll but it does reset. But it also has initiative in the cost. So where does that initiative get spent? Is it irrelevant because the exalt will just reset anyways? If so, why is it in the cost? Or does it take place AFTER resetting to base, in which case they're going to crash themselves every time? (unless they're a Dawn who resets to 4) If it doesn't matter, I'd remove it.<br /> <br /> After that, I'd ask how powerful is it to give someone a decisive attack they can spam without regard for Initiative that ignores Hardness? That sounds like a great way to kill anyone every fight ever. Something this strong sounds like a &quot;once per scene&quot; sort of deal, or at LEAST with a heavy reset condition, or a complex trigger in the first place. There needs to be some sort of limiter, because if I had this power I'd just wreck everything every combat.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, looks cool to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T08:37:18-07:00","id":1072557,"title":"","content":"So I've made progress on the thing, still not really feeling it though. Suggestions, ideas and criticisms are welcome. <hr /><br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Ancestors' Anguish</b> \u2013 soulsteel &amp; black jade bead chain (dire chain, Artifact \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Tags: Bashing, Grappling, Martial Arts, Disarming, Flexible, Reaching<br /> <br /> Created some time during the Shogunate by a Champion of Sijan, Ancestor's Anguish is a man-long string of fist-sized Black Jade beads, each with a Soulsteel core forged out of the nephwrack patrons of a now-extinguished ancestor-cult of Deadspeakers.<br /> <br /> Ancestor's Anguish is compatible with DPC and other martial arts that use decorative items such as scarves and sashes.<br /> <br /> <b>Embraced by the damned</b><br /> Cost: 3m per hl<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Duration: indefinite<br /> Keywords: ???<br /> Minimums: Essence 1<br /> <br /> The Exalt wears the beads around their neck and says a prayer, calling upon the ghosts imprisoned in Ancestor's Anguish to protect her with their own corpus. A subtle shroud of ectoplasm, visible only to those who can see the immaterial, covers the wielder and provides up to [Essence] temporary -0 health levels. When releasing motes committed to this charm during combat, the damage they contain is converted into initiative: 1i for each point of Bashing Damage and 2i for each point of Lethal or Aggravated Damage.<br /> <br /> These health levels don't simply vanish, they are a part of the souls imprisoned in Ancestors' Anguish and at most 10 health levels can be filled before they need to be recharged ((or &quot;healed&quot;?)) either by submerging the Artifact in blood (which it drinks) or through an hour-long prayer ritual in remembrance of one's ancestors, using incense, prayer strips and burnt offerings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Striking Fear</b><br /> Cost: 5m 2i<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Duration: 1 action (target)<br /> Keywords: Uniform, Psyche (fear)<br /> Minimums: Essence 2<br /> Prerequisites: Embraced by the damned<br /> <br /> The Exalt makes an unholy mudra against a target as an Occult-based ranged attack that uses Thrown accuracy rules, pounding a ghostly symbol into their chest that freezes their body with fear. As well as dealing damage, treat successes on the damage roll as Social Influence creating or reinforcing a Tie of Abject Terror. If this influence succeeds, the target may not move towards the character on their next turn. Moving away requires a Disengage attempt as far as Medium Range. Faced with this influence, Mortals normally attempt to run away.<br /> <br /> This Evocation can be used outside of combat, ignoring the initiative cost and rolling an Instill action in place of an attack. This version of Striking Fear deals no damage, but may be used against groups at the usual penalty.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Heart-Chilling Snare</b><br /> Cost: 7m 2i or 7m 1wp (The initiative cost is paid <b>after</b> resetting to base)<br /> Type: reflexive<br /> Duration: Special<br /> Keywords: Psyche (apathy, lethargy)<br /> Minimums: Essence 2?<br /> Prerequisites: Striking Fear<br /> <br /> The damned reach out of their prison, their limbs mirroring the actions of their master. The wielder activates this Evocation after rolling the damage of a Decisive Attack in which Ancestor's Anguish was used, dulling a number of intimacies whose total (positive) value is equal to or less than the health levels inflicted. For example, with 5 damage one can dull a Defining Intimacy (4) or one Minor and one Major (2+3). The wielder must be aware of the intimacies they wish to affect.<br /> <br /> Until the next sunrise or until the next time they see the sun, whichever is longer, the wielder may treat the intimacies affected in this way as their own while the originator treats those intimacies as one degree lower, having them tainted with lethargy and doubt.<br /> Only one use of this Evocation may be active at a time.<br /> <br /> This Evocation may be used outside of combat, substituting the initiative cost by 1wp and rolling an Instill action in place of a Decisive Attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-03-2017, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T11:23:43-07:00","id":1072627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1072546#post1072546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only part that really caught my attention was this last evocation. It doesn't use initiative for the damage roll but it does reset. But it also has initiative in the cost. So where does that initiative get spent? Is it irrelevant because the exalt will just reset anyways? If so, why is it in the cost? Or does it take place AFTER resetting to base, in which case they're going to crash themselves every time? (unless they're a Dawn who resets to 4) If it doesn't matter, I'd remove it.<br /> <br /> After that, I'd ask how powerful is it to give someone a decisive attack they can spam without regard for Initiative that ignores Hardness? That sounds like a great way to kill anyone every fight ever. Something this strong sounds like a &quot;once per scene&quot; sort of deal, or at LEAST with a heavy reset condition, or a complex trigger in the first place. There needs to be some sort of limiter, because if I had this power I'd just wreck everything every combat.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, looks cool to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your comments!! <br /> <br /> taking them into consideration here's an edit<br /> <br /> <b>Thunderbolt</b><br /> Cost: 6m, 1wp. Mins: Essence 3.<br /> Type: Simple Tags: Aggravated, Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: instant<br /> Prerequisites: Ride the Lightning, Static Cage<br /> <br /> With a shout, Surge's wielder summons a spark of lightning within Surge and fires it into their opponent. <br /> If within close or short range, the attack is made with (Dexterity + Melee), but if it's made from Medium or long range, the attack uses (Dexterity + Thrown). In either case, the decisive attack does aggravated damage with a base damage equal to the attack roll's successes. The attack ignores hardness, and cannot be blocked or dodged without the use of a Charm. It does not include initiative in it's damage roll, but it does reset initiative to base. <br /> <br /> special activation rules: After Thunderbolt is used, Surge needs to be recharged before it can use Thunderbolt again. To achieve this recharge, Surge may either be left out in a thunderstorm to be struck by lightning, or it cannot be used at all in the next two combat scenes. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13093-inksplatterm","name":"inksplatterm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:13:44-07:00","id":1076028,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hello!<br /> I've been working on a pair of artifacts for my night caste archer, the main idea for this set was to have a bow that could be stealthily concealed in the cloak and be drawn directly from its fabric, then it sort of evolved into full cloth/loom set. The thing is, I've no idea how to balance them or what their ratings should be. I'd really appreciate any kind of feedback, mostly regarding blatantly overpowered/useless stuff, and possible costs (required essence and motes - for both artifacts, every evoc has all the previous ones as prereqs). Don't worry about styling/wording errors, I'd like to get the mechanics down first. Any feedback would be greatly appreciated, as this is basically my first time attempting to come up with any sort of evocs, much less an entire set of artifacts.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hands of the Invisible Seamstress, Moonsilver Cloak and Starmetal Bow (5*, 5*)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These twinned artifacts were forged in the image of Fateweaver, a mythical figure known only by the word of mouth, by a Sidereal named Outstanding Contribution to the Historical Process. Having heard the legends of the seamstress who could manipulate the fabric of reality itself, the exalt decided to make the legend come true and create items that would reflect Fateweaver\u2019s legendary prowess. Coincidentally, by assuming Fateweaver\u2019s identity, she managed to erase the legend from the minds of people of Creation.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cloth</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> appears as a dark, tattered cloth made out of Moonsliver threads. Its protection is equal to that of an artifact light armor.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Loom </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">is a Starmetal artifact powerbow with spindle motifs and several perpendicular moonsilver thread bowstrings.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evocations:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Rule: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cloth (cloak) and Loom (powerbow), the component artifacts of the Hands of the Invisible Seamstress, only work in tandem with each other. To gain benefits of any, the user has to attune to both. In addition, its evocations are purchased in pairs for double the usual price.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By attuning to the Hands of the Invisible Seamstress, the wielder gains the ability to fully conceal the bow in the fabric of the cloak, appearing as a starmetal pattern on its back. The user is always treated as having the bow in her hands, ready to strike, as long as her hands are empty.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Loom cannot fire regular arrows, only those made out of Cloth\u2019s threads, which require no additional cost. They are fully compatible with archery charms such as Fiery Arrow and so on.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After a long, intensive battle with many arrows shot, the Cloth may (up to the Storyteller\u2019s discretion) appear as nothing but a small swatch due to losing so many strands, decreasing its soak and hardness until the threads recover at midnight.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special Resource: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Cloth and Loom use a special resource called spun threads (st) to fuel their evocations. By default, the pool contains 3 threads, and resets to that value once per day, at midnight. In addition, the user can collect additional threads:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attacking an enemy with an arrow fired from the Loom awards the user 1 spun thread (always 1, even in case of multi-target/multi-arrow attacks)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whenever an enemy has been struck by an arrow fired from the Loom (again, only the main target for multiple target attacks. If there is no main target, the one chosen by the user), a thin bond of fate is created between the Cloth and the enemy struck. Whenever a </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bonded</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> target advances on the wielder, award 1 spun thread for every range band moved.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For every spun thread in reserve, ignore 1 die penalty to stealth attempts.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Creation and Destruction</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Requirements: essence 2, stealth 2, archery 2 </i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Loom: Needle Follows the Thread</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[4m 1+st]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supplemental; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tags: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stackable, Withering-only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Fateweaver can effortlessly retrace and recreate her steps, finding it easier and easier to replicate an existing pattern. Using this evocation increases post-soak damage by 3, provided the target has been previously </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bonded</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. For every subsequent use of this evocation on attacks against the same enemy, increase post-soak damage by 3 more (so 3, then 6, then 9 etc), but also increase the st cost by 1. Cap is equal to the user\u2019s essence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cloth: Thread Follows the Needle [4m 1+st]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supplemental; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tags: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dual</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Fateweaver can effortlessly retrace and recreate her steps, finding it easier and easier to repair a damaged pattern. Use this evocation while attempting to re-enter stealth during combat. Waive the usual penalty for entering stealth in combat, and increase soak by 3 and hardness by 2 against the next attack that successfully hits the user. Subsequent activations of this evocation increase the st cost by 1 and boost the bonus soak by +3 and hardness by +2 . This increases for every use up to the Solar\u2019s essence. (eg up to 9 soak and 6 hardness for 1 attack in exchange for 3 st). If she has not been hit yet, the new instance of the evocation replaces the previous one. If the user wishes so, this evocation can be used to heal normally instead of creating temporary hls. In that case, subsequent uses heal a number of hls equal to the spun threads spent, but the evocation becomes a simple action that cannot be placed in a flurry. The user still cannot heal more hls per day than her essence. In both cases, the user must spend 1 more st with every activation up to the essence cap - she cannot opt to depower the evocation to lower the cost.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unity and Division</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Requirements: essence 3, stealth 3, archery 3</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Loom: Two Strands Converge [5m 1wp 2st]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Simple; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tags: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withering-only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As fickle as ever, The Fateweaver pays little attention to the whereabouts of her threads. Having them mingle with one another only refines her work further. The user fires a withering arrow that splits in flight, aiming at two opponents who share a range band. Halve the raw damage of the attacks if they hit. (min. Overwhelming damage still applies, add any post-soak damage as usual as well) If both enemies are hit, their essences are interwoven. One cannot move without the other, necessitating a delay action until both can act on the same tick if they wish to change range bands. They also suffer an accuracy penalty equal to each other\u2019s essence. Either character can lessen his penalty by tagging a positive intimacy towards the other (by the usual worth of the intimacy). The effect lasts for an amount of turns equal to the amount of successes on the lower damage roll + the user\u2019s essence, divided by two, rounded up.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cloth: Lone Strand Diverges [5m 1wp 2st]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reflexive; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tags: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perilous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As fickle as ever, The Fateweaver pays little attention to the whereabouts of her thread. Having it disjoint only refines her work further. When the user succeeds on a disengage attempt, she may reflexively activate this charm. Refund the initiative cost of disengage. The user\u2019s being begins to unravel, blurring her form. Until the end of the subsequent round after this evocation was used, all combatants wishing to attack her must first delay their actions by at least 3 ticks as their hesitation makes them unable to mount a precise strike. The initiative lost as a result of delaying actions is awarded to the solar with a cap of the user\u2019s essence*2.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fateweaving </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Requirements: essence 4, stealth 4, archery 4</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Loom: Fate, Unraveled [1m per st, all remaining st]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Simple; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One Round; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tags: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Decisive-Only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When she is not satisfied with the results of her work, the Fateweaver simply discards the failure without thought, and spreads new cloth in its place. This evocation uses up all remaining spun threads and severs the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">bonds</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, disabling the ability to gather more spun threads until the artifact restores itself at midnight. The user launches an attack up to the weapon\u2019s range that ignores hardness equal to the amount of threads used. If the attack deals at least 1 health level of damage, convert all damage levels recorded in the target\u2019s health track to aggravated damage, up to the number of spun threads used. Based on the amount of health track filled with aggravated damage after being attacked by this evocation, one of the following occurs:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Less than half </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - the target becomes partially woven out of Creation, taking a missing limb flaw of their choosing. Any positive intimacy towards the user is dropped by a level - </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">minor </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">intimacies disappear. These penalties last until all aggravated damage is removed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Less than full </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- the target becomes almost fully woven out of creation, taking both missing limb flaws. Any positive intimacy towards the user is dropped by two levels - both </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">minor </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">major </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">intimacies disappear. These penalties last until all aggravated damage is removed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Full health track </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- the target is woven out of creation. They die instantly, any trace of their existence is removed from history, and from memories, except the artifact wielder\u2019s. The user can share her memories with people she has at least a major intimacy towards, granting them full recollection of the removed character.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cloth: Fate, Rewoven [10m 1wp]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reflexive; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tags: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Uniform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When she is not satisfied with the results of her work, the Fateweaver simply sets the failure aside, and uses it as a guideline to improve her next work. In order to make use of this evocation, the wielder of the Hands must first erase a character with Fate, Unraveled. When subject to an attack, the user can recall the removed character\u2019s memory. The recalled character proceeds to protect the user to the best of his ability, acting on the tick he has been summoned on (before the attacker\u2019s strike against the wielder resolves.. The character can clash attacks aimed at the user, can use distract gambits (using the wielder\u2019s init but not actually reducing it), use social attacks to dissuade the enemies from attacking, and so on - up to the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, but always to the best of his ability. In case of social actions, the enemies cannot spend wp to resist them. Any enemy that used to have a positive tie towards the returned character is assaulted by a sudden, painful influx of memories, taking a -3 penalty to all mental ability-based rolls for (user\u2019s essence) days. The character protects the user for a number of turns equal to her essence, then disappears forever. The user can store up to essence characters in her memory. If another one is Unraveled while the cap is full, choose a single character to remove. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively, this charm can be used to summon the forgotten character outside combat. In this case, the evocation becomes a simple action. The returned character is compelled to answer up to essence questions to the best of her knowledge, then disappears forever.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13200-grusin","user":"Grusin","date":". 04-11-2017, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13200-grusin","name":"Grusin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T14:22:54-07:00","id":1078532,"title":"","content":"I've been working on some armor for the group's Dodge Supernal Dawn Caste; she's a Martial Artist of the Dreaming Pearl Courtesan style. \u200bThis is what I've come up with; it's my first attempt at a homebrew artifact, so comments are very welcome! Thanks, all!<br /> Humble Pearl \u2013 Artifact 4 Silken Armor<br /> <br /> Humble Pearl is a set of Silken Armor with Starmetal bindings and whispersilk cloth. Humble Pearl was created by a Celestial God that was infatuated with Dancing Smile, a Chosen of Serenity. Which Celestial God it was is currently unknown, as the God forged himself into Humble Pearl in order to be as close to the object of his infatuation as possible. Dancing Smile came to appreciate the benefits of such an arrangement with the God and thereafter never took off Humble Pearl.<br /> <br /> Humble Pearl was no artifact sockets.<br /> <br /> The only valid dice pool for instilling Intimacies into Humble Pearl is Appearance + Martial Arts. For this purpose, Humble Pearl has a Resolve of 5.<br /> <br /> Attunement Benefits<br /> In addition to the normal benefit of Silken Armor, the wearer may pay a 2m surcharge on the attunement cost to reduce the Essence Requirement of Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Form by 1.<br /> Resonant: If a character is Resonant with Humble Pearl, the mote surcharge is reduced by 1.<br /> Dissonant: This benefit does not apply.<br /> Once a character reaches Essence 2 naturally, this surcharge obviously does not apply.<br /> Evocations:<br /> <br /> Pearls Before Swine<br /> Cost: -<br /> Min: Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Tags: None<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Humble Pearl does not exert himself and does not put himself forward. Humble Pearl emphasizes the character's beauty, charm, and wit at the 'expense' of himself. A character who wishes to realize that Humble Pearl is, in fact, armor does so against a difficulty of the wearer's Appearance. If this roll fails, then the character believes that they either missed cleanly or that their attack was lost in the folds of the garment. This benefit does not apply to characters directly perceiving Essence flows, such as with All Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight.<br /> Resonant: This difficulty also applies to attempts to realize that Humble Pearl is even an artifact.<br /> <br /> Flashing Pearl Weave<br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Min: Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Tag: Withering-Only<br /> Prerequisites: Pearls Before Swine<br /> <br /> Such is the effectiveness of Humble Pearl's emphasis on his wearer's features instead of his own that the attacks with Humble Pearl's sweeping sleeves and draping weaves are not noticed until almost too late. When using this Charm with an attack that uses Humble Pearl, the wearer can raise the Overwhelming characteristic of his attack to be equal to the wearer's Appearance.<br /> <br /> Languid Pearl Movement<br /> Cost: 4m, (Optionally, 3m, +1 WP)<br /> Min: Essence 2<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Tags: None<br /> Prerequisites: Flashing Pearl Weave<br /> <br /> Humble Pearl can also affect the senses of those watching his wearer. This Evocation allows the wearer to roll Appearance + Martial Arts vs. Resolve to reestablish surprise during combat. Outside of combat, the wearer may spend 3 motes and a Willpower and activate this charm when the character makes an Ambush attack. This usage, called Pearlescent Drowning Waves, allows the wearer to roll Appearance + Martial Arts to establish the difficulty to even be considered as a possible source of the attack, even if she is the only possible person. For example, if she used this while strangling a lover amidst their sheets and an Investigator failed to beat the number of successes the wearer rolled, the Investigator would likely conclude the lover died by suffocation by his own sheets.<br /> <br /> Distracting Pearl Hue<br /> Cost: 3m, 1 WP<br /> Min: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Tag: Psyche<br /> Prerequisites: Pearls Before Swine<br /> <br /> Humble Pearl's movements whilst the wearer performs the katas of the Dreaming Pearl Courtesan style can trigger a fixation on the wearer that is difficult to overcome. When the wearer activates Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Form, she may also reflexively activate this Evocation to roll an Appearance + Martial Arts pool against the Resolve of each opponent who can see her. Opponents whose Resolve is beaten must spend 2i to attack a character or battle group other than the wearer. An affected character may spend a point of Willpower to overcome this effect for a turn. Once a character spends Willpower points such that their Resolve+Willpower spent is greater than the wearer's Appearance, this effect is removed from the character for the rest of the scene.<br /> Resonant: If within Short Range of an opponent who spends initiative to ignore this, gain the initiative spent.<br /> Dissonant: An affected character only has to spend 1 WP to overcome the effect for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> Flashing Weave Defense<br /> Cost: 1m per die, 1 WP<br /> Min: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Tags: Perilous<br /> Prerequisites: Distracting Pearl Hue<br /> <br /> Humble Pearl will not suffer his charge to be hit easily. In major matters, he can move himself in ways to bend his wearer out of danger. When defending herself, the wearer may choose an intimacy not tied to Humble Pearl that is directly applicable to the current contest to add non-Charm dice to the roll equal to the intensity of the intimacy (or half that much to a static value). In so doing, the character gains an Minor Tie of Gratitude to Humble Pearl; if the character already has a Tie of Gratitude to Humble Pearl, it increases by one level (up to Defining). Once per session, reset by the character performing a burnt offering to Humble Pearl sufficient for the level of the Intimacy and succeeding on an Appearance + Martial Arts roll (see rules for prayers to Spirits).<br /> <br /> Resonant: This charm can be used once per scene.<br /> <br /> Sacrifice of Pearls<br /> Cost: Special<br /> Min: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Tags: None<br /> Prerequisites: Flashing Weave Defense, Languid Pearl Movement<br /> <br /> By this point, Humble Pearl will not suffer his charge to be permanently harmed or scarred. A character who knows this Evocation may not choose to accept a physical debilitation instead of being killed. However, Humble Pearl himself will sacrifice himself for his charge if the need is great. Once per season, in a situation where the choice exists to accept a physical debilitation or to die, Humble Pearl will sacrifice himself rather than allow his charge to die. This sacrifice manifests itself as the loss of all Evocations accessed in Humble Pearl (and the concomitant experience). This also reduces Humble Pearl to simple court garb until the wearer (or another, if the wearer still ends up dying) performs an Appearance + Martial Arts roll vs Difficulty 5 as well as sacrificing a minimum of Resources 4 to reawaken Humble Pearl.<br /> <br /> Resonant: After using this charm, the wearer only spends half the normal amount of experience to learn the Evocations of Humble Pearl.<br /> <br /> Dissonant: A character who uses this Charm may not ever reattune to Humble Pearl, although they may perform the prayer roll to reawaken Humble Pearl.<br /> <br /> Special: This charm may not be learned until the wearer has a Defining Tie of Gratitude to Humble Pearl and the wearer has created a Defining Tie of Adoration in Humble Pearl to herself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13250-khazadir","name":"Khazadir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T16:49:04-07:00","id":1081629,"title":"","content":"Hey everybody! It's been a hot minute since I posted here last, but here I go again. Two artifacts again this time, one focused on poison (which probably needs a lot of work), and one built around Fae despite my rather loose knowledge on them. I hope they aren't <i>too </i>unplayable.<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ _________________<br /> <br /> <b>Ebon Fang of Corpse Breath </b>(*** dot) Soulsteel Longfang<br /> <b>Attunement Cost:</b> 5m<br /> <b>Hearthstone slots:</b> 0<br /> <b>Story:</b><br /> I was not always a tool of death. I was once a tool of the hunt. I was something that was built to bring down the greatest of beasts for the good of all. Now I am something more, and something less. My name, my title, has changed. Once, I was the <b>Emerald Spire of Singing Serpents</b>, but that was before the fall.<br /> Created in the First Age for the sole purpose of combating the greatest beasts of the land, the <b>Emerald Spire of Singing Serpents</b> was a glorious spear of Green Jade and Moonsilver decoration. Its beauty however masked its true reason for being, the toxic heart of a behemoth stretched to wring out vile ills lie inside, forever bleeding its poison blood by the magic of the Sun\u2019s that placed it within. It was thus a serpent, glorious scales shining as it arced through the air, only to pierce the hide of vile beasts and deliver unto them nightmares in the blood. For many centuries it served its purpose well\u2026 until its master lay slain, the artifact buried in the belly of some unknown horror for ages. Until the day that its master returned, garbed no longer in the clock of sunlight, by whispering the secrets of the grave.<br /> No eyes to see, no ears to hear, no senses to witness the place it was brought to. Had the <b>Emerald Spire of Singing Serpents</b> been able to speak of this place, it would refuse to, for the transformation came about in this dark place. Unmade without stripping away metal, metaled down without fire, the Soulsteel that now adorns the artifact closed around. Names and purpose changed, if only slightly. This was the birth of the <b>Ebon Fang of Corpse Breath</b>, whose touch could now only bring rot.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations:</b> While attuned this artifact exudes and coats its metal in a thin layer of acid. The attuned exalt is rendered immune to the effects of this acid, but all other naturally occurring materials will begin to burn away as though exposed to a flame when contact is made. This can be used in attacks if stunted accordingly, and is considered to deal damage equal to 1A/Contact where the interval is defined as physical contact. Difficulty 5 (Stamina + Resistance) to ignore effects; this roll must be made each time the acid makes contact with living material.<br /> <br /> <b>Unfurled Wings</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - <b> Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> So long as the artifact remains attuned to the exalt, this weapon can be used for thrown attacks out to Long range and will return to the exalt when ordered, as though under the effects of <i>Call the Blade</i> (p.347). For an additional payment of 1wp the range can be increased an additional range band per Strength level, but the exalts suffers -2 die to hit for each additional range band.<br /> <br /> <b>Seven Bleeding Fangs</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m (+2m per additional effect)<b> Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><i>Unfurled Wings</i><br /> By activating this evocation, a toxin is chosen to coat the head of the weapon. There are exactly seven potential effects to choose from, which must be witness in effect before that specific effect can be selected on activation. A random effect is to be selected if the exalt does not select one before rolling to attack. These effects include\u2026<br /> <br /> Paralytic (Minor): 1i/round, 5 rounds, -2, damage ~ Crashed enemies suffer a -2 on all withdraw, disengage, and rush actions.<br /> Paralytic (Major): 3i/round, 10 rounds, -4, damage ~ Crashed enemies suffer the same effects as Paralytic (Minor), suffering a -1 to Parry and Dodge in addition.<br /> Hallucinogenic: 2i/round, 15 rounds, -3, damage ~ Crashed enemies lose a point of wp or enter a waking dream like state for the remaining rounds.<br /> Flame Stealer: 1L/round, 4 rounds, -1, damage ~ While under the effects of this poison, the afflicted will suffer a -2 to all defenses against Water or Air related attacks.<br /> Flame Granter: 1L/round, 4 rounds, -1, damage ~ While under the effects of this poison, the afflicted will suffer a -2 to all defenses against Fire related attacks.<br /> Sense Thief: 1B/Round, 3 rounds, -4, damage ~ While under the effects of this poison, the afflicted will suffer a -4 to all Perception or Awareness rolls. This poison can leave the afflicted permanently damaged.<br /> Blackout: 2i/round, 5 rounds, -2, damage ~ Crashed enemies are considered to be rendered unconscious. The poison ceases to affect the afflicted at this point.<br /> <br /> <b>Welcoming Grave Rot</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp<b> Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b><i>Seven Bleeding Fangs</i><br /> Should this evocation be activated on a successful decisive attack, the opponent is exposed to the most powerful venom sleeping within the weapon. As this toxin takes effect, the living material of the afflicted begins to rot away as though the mask of life had been pulled away to reveal the rot that lay beneath. It is not possible to purge the system of this toxin by mundane means, and only the greatest of the Exalted have endured or cured those afflicted. Thankfully, the artifact holds a single vial of antidote for all of its poisons in the base of the weapon. Unfortunately, the effects of this specific poison can only be cured by an antidote that is recently regenerated, as it loses the potency to do so 6 hours afterwards. This vial refills itself over the course of 2 days.<br /> This toxin is unique as its effects can be modified by the exalt on application. At the most effective, the toxin has a Damage/Interval of 5L/round, a duration of (wielders Essence) rounds, a Penalty of (Afflicted Stamina), and the damage Vector. This toxin\u2019s Damage/Interval, Duration, and Penalty can be modified to sleep within the afflicted system waiting to take effect. The longest possible Damage/Interval time-frame is 1L/4days, Duration of Indefinite, Penalty -0. Modifying the potency of the toxin does not require anything outside of forethought. <br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ _______________<br /> <br /> <b>Will of the Broken Bulwark</b> (**** dot) Articulated Plate<br /> <b>Attunement Cost:</b> 6m<br /> <b>Hearthstone slots:</b> 0<br /> <b>Story:</b><br /> There is only so much one can do to combat the Courts of the Fair Folk. Even for a god, sometimes there is so, so little. The <b>Will of the Broken Bulwark</b> is part of what little one god could do.<br /> Deep at the border between the Scavenger Lands and East lays a great valley. Little grows within this valley, but the earth brings forth great treasures for those that seek it. In one such site a great god of the forge made his home, worshiped by all for miles around. He used the metals of the earth and fire of his belly to shape great wonders, and taught the arts to those that would offer him service and sacrifice. But he was as crafty of mind as he was of tool, \u201cconveniently\u201d leaving out key knowledge to shape true works of art so that his students would always return. He did not realize that both their reverence and their hatred for his trickery became a fragrant breeze in the darker places of Creation\u2026<br /> None were prepared for the Fair Folks arrival. They arrived like the wind, setting up like traveling merchants in abandoned quarries, feeding on those foolish enough to wander to close, or stupid enough to leave their homes unlocked. In response to their prayers, the forge god set the elements under his command to strike at the Fair Folk. They dealt a devastating blow, but the Fae regrouped too quickly. The god knew he and his followers would be lost far too soon if he did not act. So he did.<br /> Taking the bodies of slain Fae his surviving elementals had collected, he shaped the strange and Wyld materials into recognizable shape and form. In time, he had nearly completed what would be his greatest work. And with great sacrifice, he gifted both the newly forged armor and much of his power to a mortal woman. She became his champion. She became the Fair Folks doom. It was not until the chosen of the god had returned with the rakshasa\u2019s head that he was able to complete his creation. The greatest armor the god would ever shape, the <b>Will of the Broken Bulwark.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Evocations:</b><br /> While attuned to and wearing this artifact, the exalt gains the Hideous merit. The exalt also gains one of the Derangement flaws (chosen randomly) of a random severity (selected by Storyteller) at the first activation of one of the artifacts evocations. The Derangement lasts the reminder of the scene in which it is gained. Consult p.168 for flaw details.<br /> <br /> <u>Special rules:</u> As armor comprised of Fae components, this armor is weakened to cold iron (see the Cold Iron Bane merit). Against enemies using iron weapons, this armor counts as light artifact instead of heavy. <br /> <br /> <b>Steel Resolve Stance</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> Sometimes, a strong will is all one needs to keep fighting. Against a withering attack, the exalt may use this evocation and cite a relevant intimacy (battle or protection related intimacies always apply) to add their Resolve score to their Soak. Against a decisive attack, (Resolve/2, round up) is added to Hardness instead. A given intimacy may only be used once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Wyld Courses Within</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1wp <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Steel Resolve Stance</i><br /> The taint of the Wyld lingers\u2026 shall we share it? On a decisive attack, the exalt may force a target to use their Resolve in place of Soak and Hardness, should it be lower. If the target has a Major or Defining intimacy related to courage, valor, or similar fear resistant qualities, they may pay a point of willpower to become immune to this effect for the scene. <br /> <br /> <b>Care for Hungry Tools</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2wp <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Wyld Courses Within</i><br /> Something within the armor still seeks the dreams and nightmares of the mortal mind. What would happen should we feed it? Using this charm empowers the armor for the remainder of the scene, removing the willpower cost of all prerequisite evocations. If activated before the Derangement flaw is applied (Evocation section) the exalt will not suffer from the flaw for this scene. Only base willpower can be used for this evocation (temporary, cult merit, etc. cannot be used).<br /> <br /> <b>The Little Toy Shop</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>10m, 3wp <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> <i>Care for Hungry Tools </i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThe doors are open little one, come along and play. Once the doors are closed little one, forever you shall stay\u2026\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Activating this evocation should be carefully considered. On activation, the exalts shadow elongates and from the inky depths arises a troupe of nightmarish toy like creatures numbering that of a battle group Size (Essence/2 round up). This battlegroup will obey the commands of the artifact until they are destroyed or dismissed and share stats with Hobgoblin\u2019s (p.536), these stats are upgraded to Buck-Ogre\u2019s at Size 3 or higher.<br /> <br /> <u>Special Notes:</u> The Little Toy Shop is a dangerous evocation. Unknown to even the creator the Will of the Broken Bulwark is actually a slumbering raksha trapped in the form of a suit of armor. Should the exalt wearing this artifact expend more than 5 willpower, the storyteller is to roll to determine if the Fae awakes (how this roll is determined is up the Storyteller). Should the evocation The Little Toy Shop be activated to meet the minimum, the raksha is immediately awoken. Once awoken all willpower spent on evocations are fed to the raksha, which on accumulation of 15 points of spent willpower is free to become its own entity, appearing to others as a moving suit of armor. Accumulated willpower consumed by Will of the Broken Bulwark decays at a rate of 1 willpower per week.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Enjoy the moment with all your might,<br /> Whether its gloomy, whether its bright.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12786-libaros","name":"Libaros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12786_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:18:01-07:00","id":1083561,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Not a complete artifact more a general outline hoping for some input, direction, ideas, etc.<br /> <br /> A bit about the character.<br /> I will be a Zenith with Integrity supernal.<br /> Giant, Sorcery and a Familiar (Agata, The Beauteous Wasp, Demon of the First Circle)<br /> <br /> I like the demon especially<br /> <b>Shimmering Crystal Beauty: </b><span style=\"font-family:Mercury Text G2,Mercury Text G2\"><span style=\"font-family:Mercury Text G2,Mercury Text G2\">Anyone who looks upon the agata is treated as having a Minor Tie of wonder towards it for purposes of social influence rolls </span></span><br /> <b>Jeweled Heart Allure </b><span style=\"font-family:Mercury Text G2,Mercury Text G2\"><span style=\"font-family:Mercury Text G2,Mercury Text G2\">(6m; Reflexive; One scene; Essence 2): The agata radiates beauty that dumbfounds even battle-hardened warriors, forcing characters to pay a point of Willpower before they can attack it in a scene unless they have an Intimacy that represents ruthlessness, pitilessness, or a desperate reason to fight it that is greater than the Minor Tie created by Shimmering Crystal Beauty. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mercury Text G2,Mercury Text G2\"><span style=\"font-family:Mercury Text G2,Mercury Text G2\">and I though it would be cool to have a similar artifact (i.e. armor, crown, necklace, etc.) that would give my character similar abilities. I can see <b>Shimmering Crystal Beauty</b> being part of the basic package possibly giving it an automatic Instill roll instead of automatic effect. And <b>Jeweled Heart Allure</b> as an evocation.<br /> <br /> I would appreciate your thoughts (3 point or 4 point artifact), how viable/overpowered this could be (or just plain silly), and any additional evocations you may think fits.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>while (horse.state == dead)<br /> {<br /> beat();<br /> }","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/830-amdramnar","name":"Amdramnar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T17:33:15-07:00","id":1086392,"title":"","content":"So, I'm trying to come up with an Artifact 5 Soulsteel (with a comparatively small amount of Black Jade) Grand Daiklave if anyone would like to help. Theme around it is blood, health and hate for the living (the blade has the hate, not the wielder). I know that I want the attunement bonus to be some sort of life drain or otherwise tie into that. I was thinking an additional attunement cost of 1LHL that can't be healed as long as it's attuned by any means and grants healing a single health level when you kill a noteworthy opponent or lower the level of a Battlegroup with the Grand Daiklave (not counting Route). Some of the evocations should cost one or more health levels and most of them shouldn't work against anything that isn't living. I do have a short history for it as well.<br /> <br /> A berserker in the First Age, Sinare was never satisfied with her weapons and armor and often discarded them as not being right for her. Eventually her Circle had had enough. Pooling together their resources, they forged Hateful Death (working name, might stick with it), a Grand Daiklave made of Soulsteel with a fuller of Black Jade. The ore for the Soulsteel they processed themselves, taking only the hungry ghosts of powerful warriors known for rushing into battle and trusting to their armor to protect them. Ghosts that they purposefully made sure existed. Sinare, who thirsted for blood in battle nearly as much as Hateful Death, found the blade to her liking. Especially when she found that killing the living bolstered her own health. The blade was buried with its master after her eventual death during the Usurpation, for the blade hates its wielder nearly as much as the rest of the living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T17:53:04-07:00","id":1086400,"title":"","content":"I was told to post this here.<br /> <br /> Hey guys I am new to exalted and I'm in a game starting next Sunday the 7th. Well I am playing a night caste investigator with Supernal Dodge and a focus on stealth and thrown. I have bought a 4 point chakram that I am naming Light cuts from Darkness, as I wanted it to be focused on attacking from stealth and helping the user regain and maintain stealth. I was thinking oraculum and maybe a touch of soulsteel but idk. Thing is as I am new to exalted I am at total loss when it comes to making both attunement bonuses and evocations. I have looked through the example artifacts but it didn't really help me. So I'm hoping you good people can help me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:42:47-07:00","id":1086628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gfrobbin84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1086400#post1086400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as I wanted it to be focused on attacking from stealth and helping the user regain and maintain stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar set is already pretty damn good at that though, so I can't think of anything to add that wouldn't be redundant or better expressed as a custom charm of that ability. What other possible aspects can you think of that you'd want to explore? This might be a bit of personal opinion, but I think Evocations are better suited to more &quot;out-there&quot; or heavily themed mechanics, so maybe you cold start by figuring that part out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T08:36:23-07:00","id":1086654,"title":"","content":"Well he sees himself as a protector of the Poor and Weak who can not protect themselves. Despising those who would use their power or reach to hurt or take advantage of them without the means to retaliate. So maybe something focused on protecting user and allies, like making ranged counter attacks or reflexively using it to impede attacks. If that is still to broad maybe specifically focusing on countering ranged attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T09:30:01-07:00","id":1086670,"title":"","content":"Let some ideas play out here and maybe y'all can help me codify it into some evocations. Building off my last post of protecting yourself and others from the reach of those who seek to hurt them without retaliation. <br /> <br /> Reach of the Mighty Undone<br /> Attunement: when attuned to this chakram the very air around the users seeks to deter strikes against him. Any ranged attacks against him have their dice pool reduced by x.<br /> <br /> Then maybe a charm that let's you reflexive (dex+thrown) opposed roll against ranged attacks against him or persons he can see and has a least a minor positive intimacy too. Possibly allowing either base or as an upgrade letting you follow up with an attack against the originator of the triggering attack of the chakram user wins the opposed roll, the chakram like trace back down the projectiles path to the attacker.<br /> <br /> Maybe something that increases the die penalty from the attunement and/or let's him apply it to others he has a positive intimacy too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T16:05:09-07:00","id":1087378,"title":"","content":"OK so I have come up with something and would love if I could get some critiques on it. I am especially unsure on the cost of things but gladly accept critiques on any of it as I am very new to this and unsure of the power level of this.<br /> <br /> <b>The Defender's Blade</b> <b>(Orichalcum Chakram) * * *</b><br /> <b>Attunement Cost: 5</b>m<br /> <b>Hearthstones: </b> 1 slot<br /> <br /> The Defender's Blade belonged to a 1st age Dawn caste devoted to defending his allies and found the reach of a daiklave to limiting in reach to truly defend those he cared for. So he developed this special Chakram to defeat attacks even when they occurred outside of his immediately reach. The Defender's blade was lost to time when it's owner fell, in the East, during usurpation.<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations:</b><br /> While attuned to The Defender's Blade it hovers next to the wielder and just requires 1 free hand to command it about the battlefield.<br /> <br /> <b>\u200bGuard the Field</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m+1m/attack <b>Minimums:</b> Thrown 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Turn<br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> None<br /> <br /> This Evocation represents a special Defend Other action. It follows the rules for Defend Other with the following exceptions: First, it applies to all characters within Short Range that the wielder has a Positive Tie towards. Secondly, it uses the wielder's (Dexterity+Thrown+Specialty)/2 to calculate the Parry of the Defense. Lastly, the attacker cannot choose to hit the wielder of this Artifact. Each attack intercepted costs 1m. This Evocation ends after any attack exceeds the Parry of The Defender's Blade.<br /> <br /> Resonant: This Evocation applies to all applicable characters within Medium Range.<br /> <br /> <b>Guard's Retribution</b><br /> <b>Cost: 5</b>m <b>Minimums: </b>Thrown 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Guard the Field<br /> <br /> The Wielder of this blade always makes sure an offender pays for striking those he cares for. Once per round when someone who the Exalt has at least a minor Positive tie to is attacked and within short range of the Exalt, or Medium if he takes the Guardian action, he can use this charm to make a reflexive counter attack at the offender.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u200b<b>Zone of Defense</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - (1 WP) <b>Minimums:</b> Thrown 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Guard's Retribution<br /> <br /> Zone of Defense upgrades Guard the Field permanently in the following ways. First of all, it makes Guard the Field Reflexive. Secondly, it allows Guard the Field to protect characters out to Long Range, and, while active, allows Guardian's Retribution to Counterattack out to Long Range. Lastly, for an extra cost of 1 WP when activating Guard the Field, it makes the Duration of Guard the Field one Scene. <br /> <br /> Activations of Guard the Field after the first scene-long activation may drop the WP cost for the scene.</span><br /> </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","user":"gfrobbin84","date":".  Edited based on feedback much thanks to Khazadir 05-05-2017, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:08:23-07:00","id":1087400,"title":"","content":"Gfrobbins: This blade looks pretty darn powerful to me. For a three dot artifact, I think this verges on broken-in-half territory. <br /> <br /> \u200bFirst, for only two extra motes of attunement, it allows you to parry with Thrown. As that is a built-in limitation of the Ability, I would be hesitant to allow that, particularly as a permanent effect. I would, personally, prefer a standard attunement cost with the first Evocation being automatically unlocked if Resonant, and the first Evocation is a 2m charm that allows parrying with the Chakram. Granted, my play experience is currently limited, so please take this and all my evaluation with a slight grain of salt.<br /> <br /> Evocations:<br /> Guard the Field: Really, really nasty. It allows the character, for 3m per attack intercepted, to effectively increase the Defense by my (Dex+Thrown)/2 with no other negative effects. This is, effectively, in most circumstances, 3m for +5 Defense to anyone I have a positive Tie to (which, I imagine, is going to be the entire Circle I'm part of). Way over the top. Note: It doesn't even impede me from attacking! I would recommend a few changes. First, to use it at Medium or Long range, it requires me to take a Miscellaneous Action that can't be flurried (effectively, an Aim action with no specific target). Secondly, if the attacker exceeds my defense, the chakram is knocked from the air and has to be retrieved before it can be used at all again. Lastly, I'd recommend at least double the cost. I think some combination of these would balance this ability out. Another option to bring this into a bit more of balance is to have it only be usable once per round.<br /> <br /> Guard's Retribution: This is, again, too cheap for the effect. I would increase the cost and simply remove the requirement to parry the opponent's attack. If you attack anyone he has a Positive Tie towards, he can counterattack. You might want to stipulate that it can only be used if the target takes damage from the attack.<br /> <br /> Zone of Defense: This is basically bonkers. Read my commentary on the first charm, then apply it to everyone on my side on the field. An effective +5 Defense for everyone for the LOW-LOW price of 5m, 1WP (+3m per attack beyond the first)? This is a similar cost as Flow Like Blood type effects, and that only removes penalties (and sometimes only conditionally). I assume that it just allows the Exalt to Parry, but what happens when I use this and then pull even a regular sword out? Assuming I have Melee 5 (and the aforementioned Dex 5), does that give me an effective Parry of 10? I think this ability would be fair if it did two things: 1) Remove the required action specified in Guard the Field comments above, and 2) allowed a free use of Guard the Field.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13250-khazadir","name":"Khazadir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T17:38:01-07:00","id":1087413,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback, I really appreciate it. I figured I would need to do some editing since I am very new to the system. At least now people can see what I was going for.<br /> <br /> Ok Edited the original entry from the feedback. Would still love more feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","user":"gfrobbin84","date":". 05-03-2017, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T15:53:02-07:00","id":1087963,"title":"","content":"You're welcome.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs further feedback, the first Evocation can probably now be back at 3m, or even 2m; it now takes your action in the round, so you can't attack anymore while doing it. I'd also suggest, if you want to plus it up a bit, is that it can be used continually for the round until an opponent exceeds its 'Parry' value. That way, it's freakishly effective against people who can't garner at least 5 successes, but basically once per round against Exalts and others who can generate a dice pool in excess of 10 regularly.<br /> <br /> I would recommend this rewrite:<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bGuard the Field<br /> Cost: 3m+1m/attack Minimums: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Duration: 1 Turn<br /> Prerequisite: None<br /> <br /> This Evocation represents a special Defend Other action. It follows the rules for Defend Other with the following exceptions: First, it applies to all characters within Short Range that the wielder has a Positive Tie towards. Secondly, it uses the wielder's (Dexterity+Thrown+Specialty)/2 to calculate the Parry of the Defense. Lastly, the attacker cannot choose to hit the wielder of this Artifact. Each attack intercepted costs 1m. This Evocation ends after any attack exceeds the Parry of The Defender's Blade.<br /> <br /> Resonant: This Evocation applies to all applicable characters within Medium Range.<br /> <br /> If I understand it correctly, this should give you everything you were looking for while minimizing the mechanical language (and piggybacking off the Defend Other work in the book).<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13250-khazadir","name":"Khazadir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T16:12:36-07:00","id":1087972,"title":"","content":"I do really like that and makes a lot of sense as the entry evocation, but how will this enteract with the Defensive Zone evocation as it is meant to allow one free parry on attack against an ally per round while still acting as normal other wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T16:20:08-07:00","id":1087975,"title":"","content":"Try this:<br /> <br /> \u200bZone of Defense<br /> Cost: - (1 WP) Min: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite: (Previous Evocations)<br /> <br /> Zone of Defense upgrades Guard the Field permanently in the following ways. First of all, it makes Guard the Field Reflexive. Secondly, it allows Guard the Field to protect characters out to Long Range, and, while active, allows Guardian's Retribution to Counterattack out to Long Range. Lastly, for an extra cost of 1 WP when activating Guard the Field, it makes the Duration of Guard the Field one Scene. <br /> <br /> Activations of Guard the Field after the first scene-long activation may drop the WP cost for the scene.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13250-khazadir","name":"Khazadir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T16:33:41-07:00","id":1087982,"title":"","content":"Ok cool thanks a lot man. I'll edit the post when I get home from work later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T17:01:04-07:00","id":1088002,"title":"","content":"I like creating these kind of things, so I'm glad I could help.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13250-khazadir","name":"Khazadir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T00:52:49-07:00","id":1088137,"title":"","content":"Ok I have a bit of an odd concept and need to know if it'd be better as a god, elemental, or artifact. It's very artifact-esque so I figured this might be the place to start.<br /> <br /> Basically it's a sapient magical sword that can take humanoid form. In the sword form it has a few neat evocations, and in humanoid form it can act somewhat independently and attack as if it was wielding itself, plus one of the upper tier evocations would be to allow it's attuned user/person with the familiar merit concerning the sword-spirit (i'm not sure which should apply, or maybe both?) to use charms with the sword spirit even when it's operating in humanoid form at a distance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T04:09:56-07:00","id":1088187,"title":"","content":"Soul: In my opinion, it all revolves around a few questions.<br /> <br /> \u200b1) Does the sword naturally roll Join Battle for itself in combat?<br /> 2) Can it employ its Charms (as a Spirit) or its Evocations (as a weapon) itself?<br /> 3) Does it have its own Essence Pool?<br /> <br /> If the answer to #1 is No (at least as a baseline), it probably is best to be an Artifact. If the answer to #3 is No, it should, in my opinion, again should be an Artifact.<br /> <br /> I think the fairest way to represent it is to have the base form and the lower level Evocations represent the sword prior to it being fully conscious. Once you learn the Evocation that fully wakes up the sword, you have a couple of different ways to go:<br /> <br /> 1) Permanently change the Sword into a Spirit (I would change it from a 3-dot Artifact to a 3-dot Familiar and take all the xp invested in Evocations and turn it into xp to power up the Familiar (either through Familiar boosting Charms or via direct boosting) OR<br /> 2) The final Evocation acts like a Sprit's Materialize charm; when activated, the Spirit manifests. For balance purposes, it might be fairest to have the Exalt who wields the sword pay the cost of Materialization (as, otherwise, he gets the best of both worlds). If that balance point isn't a concern, though, the Spirit could pay for it.<br /> <br /> I recently made a Powerbow whose final Evocation was to animate it. I modeled the power off of the Single Point Shining in the Void Form charm.<br /> <br /> Hope these ideas help!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13250-khazadir","name":"Khazadir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T23:11:20-07:00","id":1089017,"title":"","content":"1.) Not without heavy exp investment from a wielder.<br /> <br /> 2.) A few, it has a couple tricks. It can reshape it's grip to suit the wielder, if the physical body/sword is destroyed without employing spirit killing techniques it will pop up again at some future point, and if it crosses paths with the nimrod who let that happen it'll be annoyed, it can choose to refuse to attune to wielders it dislikes, and it can take the from of a lesser blade in order to temporarily accommodate unattuned or mortal wielders, or as a disguise. Of those only the last is really a charm in my mind.<br /> <br /> 3.) Yes, but without investment and attunement it has a limited ability to use that pool.<br /> <br /> The idea of the sword being only partly conscious until you learn the final Evocation has merit, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","user":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","date":". 05-07-2017, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T05:11:42-07:00","id":1093185,"title":"","content":"Hello there Awesome thread! Can I make a request for an artifact that I haven't seen yet?<br /> <br /> I wanted an artifact Barding (armor for mounts). Aside from the attunement cost to be paid by the exalted Cool evocations that would be nice to have would be:<br /> <br /> an evocation that would make a big animal have a chibi cute form <br /> an evocation that would allow to spend essence to feed your animal<br /> an evocation that would protect your animal from extreme environment<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9774-archangelazrael","name":"ArchangelAzrael","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T22:43:58-07:00","id":1094781,"title":"","content":"Not sure if I should make this a separate thread or not but I would like some help on two artifacts I gave to the players. I gave them the artifact versions with only one evocation at the time with the plan of adding more in the future. One is the Oni slayer from Dark souls 3. I wanted to give him the biggest, baddest bow I could think of so it was stated an artifact heavy archery. The second weapon is a chakram. He wanted the infinite Chakram from the core book but I want to make it more.<br /> <br /> Now the bow I have more of an idea for. I want it to be more effective against opponents with high soak. The first one I gave him (before I really understood how evocations worked) was basically a charm that added his essence to the post soak damage or added to decisive damage. I told him it was irreducible dice but does not go around hardness. The Chakram user is a sorceress so the evocation I gave him is the ability to store up to 5 sorcery motes that he can use later on but goes away at the end of the day. While it has that charge, it increases the weapon damage by that much. He has not been using it much as he has been relying on his sorceries more so I am not sure if I should keep that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Recently I saw a charm in the righteous devil martial arts tree that fits more of what I want for the bow (Azure Abacus Meditation on page 451). It allowed the exalt to ignore all soak if the target is not in any cover (and ignore reduced amount of soak depending on cover) One question I want to ask is how powerful would this be on a bow? Another charm I was thinking to be the show stopper is a decisive only attack that converted so much of the targets soak into decisive dice (I was thinking half the soak) . Would that be too powerful? In context to the enemies they have been facing, some of them have had high soak but not all of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the Chakram, I want to surprise him with this one but I am not sure what direction to go with it. I do want it to compliment his character's sorcery style. (He has been using his sorcery from time to time to compliment his martial arts style with the wooden claws. Most of the time it is obsidian butterflies followed up with brilliant raptor). I would like to hear some general ideas you all have here to help.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. The Unsung Hero: I am using your nasty weapon that can cut the gods, the one that got forged by several different people over the years. I made it a grimscythe instead to fit but I am loving the idea of it. The funny thing is, nobody in the party has the intimacies to unlock that weapon's full potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Nobody ever expects the immaculate inquisition!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13386-brambleclaw","name":"Brambleclaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13386_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T10:02:10-07:00","id":1095524,"title":"","content":"<b>Benevolence for the Alter I </b><b>(Artifact 3) \u2013 </b>Moonsilver and orichalcum barding breastplate<br /> <br /> Once there was a Solar who loved exploring the world, he would often venture to the unknown pushing the boundaries of creation and taming the wild. Of course in his adventure he was never alone he had his faithful familiar on his side. Alas what familiar can survive all the dangers that the world has to throw? He lost his first companion, a sabretooth tiger, due to hunger when they became trapped in the bowls of the earth after an extremely violent earthquake. Although he was able to survive without food and water for the 2 months it took him to escape, his familiar was not. Devastated he mourned for a year and a day before allowing himself to bond with another animal. This time it was a powerful tyrant lizard towering over all of his kind. For many years they explored the eastern edges of the world until they were trapped in a maze of primordial wild constructed by a powerful Raksha for his amusement and hunted by a horde of Fae. In the end exhausted and battered they managed to locate an exit albeit one only as wide as the size of barrel. With no way to retreat he choose to make his final stand with his tyrant lizard but the brave companion would have none of that, with a mighty shove he pushed him to safety. The dying throes of his second familiar hunted him for years to come. His third and last companion was a Mice of the Sun. Together they explored the vastness of the western seas. They discovered many island and new wonders, from islands made of Orichalcum to fountains that could restore youth. Eased in his knowledge that his friend could accommodate him everywhere and never starve to death he become overconfident and hubris was not far behind. While exploring the most dangerous part of an area filled with whirlpools a storm that put all storms to shame broke lose. Under the fury of the nature he and his companion were sucked to the depths of the sea in a place where even the rays of the sun failed to reach. The pressure was immerse but the solar had ways to protect himself. The same could not be said for his familiar. He lamented in his inability to extent his protection to his small friend and in his powerlessness to save him. He vowed to never let history to repeat itself. He would not acquire another familiar ever again before he could make certain that he could protect it. With the help of his circle twilight and his better-half Lunar they crafted a powerful barding of Moonsilver, Orichalcum and his solidified guilt and love for each of his fallen companions. The result was <b>Benevolence for the Alter I. </b> However as fate would have it, he was never given the chance to use it as the usurpation occurred not too long afterwards and the barding was lost along with the body of Solar.<br /> <br /> <i>Attunement: 4m<br /> Type: Light (+5 Soak, 4 hardness, -0 mobility penalty)<br /> Tags: none<br /> Hearthstone slots: 2</i><br /> <br /> <i>Evocations of the Benevolence for the Alter I.</i><br /> The barding resonates with the familiar and the exalted strengthening the bond they already share. The Exalted master attuned to it can allow a familiar to wear the barding and benefit from the unlocked evocations when active by the Exalted. No additional cost is required from the familiar as all the essence cost and willpower cost are paid by the master, this includes the attunement cost. Upon attunement the exalted my equip her familiar with the barding which changes its size and shape to accommodate for the familiar in question. By paying 2 additional motes on attunement the Exalted may make the armor merge with the familiar effectively making the armor discreet.<br /> <br /> Lastly Hearthstones inserted on the baring affect the familiar if appropriate but any essence cost that might be need to use the powers or evocation required must be paid by the Exalted master<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Disperse the Hunger</b><br /> <i>Cost: 1m or 5m or 10m Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Day<br /> Prerequisites: None</i><br /> <br /> Even mighty familiars need to sleep eat, drink and recover their strength. While the familiar may sate hunger and thirst by normal means that is not always possible. With this evocation the Exalted master may also feed and quench her familiar thirst by feed her familiar a single mote of Essence to restore her vigor for a single day. If the familiar is larger than a hound the cost raises to 5 motes per day, while if it possess the Legendary Size merit the cost raises to 10 motes per day.<br /> <br /> <u>Resonance:</u> A Solar or Lunar activating this charm also alleviates any penalties that might come from lack of sleep or physical exhaustion for a single day.<br /> <br /> <u>Dissonance:</u> This evocation can be used for a number of consecutive days equal to the exalted survival score before needing at least 1 day to reset in which the familiar is fed and watered normally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>As One</b><br /> <i>Cost: 2m Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Day<br /> Prerequisites: Disperse the Hunger</i><br /> <br /> The Exalted can endure even the harsh environment of the poles or the frenzy energies of the wild and is able to surpass countless hardships if he is so incline. With this evocation he may extent his protection on his second self. When activating any charm with a duration longer than a scene he may pay two extra motes to have it also affect her familiar. The storyteller may decide that certain charms with a scene duration are also thematically appropriate to be shared with the familiar and allow them. Furthermore the Exalted master may grant the familiar any of the benefits of his anima banner for free when he uses them himself, or may pay separately to activate them on the familiar\u2019s behalf. This is not compatible with anima effects that allow characters to acquire permanent traits, such as an Eclipse\u2019s ability to learn certain spirit Charms or a Twilight\u2019s ability to bind spirits as familiars. In addition, the familiar may reflexively surround itself with radiance emulating its master\u2019s anima banner at the burning level.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Resonance:</i></u> A Solar or Lunar can also commit 2 motes to allow the familiar to gain the benefit of a protection she is under ,not granted by a charm, such as the protection the wielder of the artifact Stormcaller enjoys against environmental penalties from wind, precipitation, and other weather.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Inseparable</b><br /> <i>Cost: 5m, 1w Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Day<br /> Prerequisites: Disperse the Hunger</i><br /> <br /> No place is too small or too narrow that the familiar can\u2019t follow its master for the exalted that have unlocked this evocation. The Exalted Master may commit 5 motes and change the size and the appearance slightly of his familiar. This evocation shrinks the familiar roughly 1 size (from a tyrant lizard like statue to a horse like statue and from a horse like statue to a cat like statue, and from a cat like statue to a mouse like statue). The familiar might lose any merits associated with its size such as Legendary Size merit for the duration of the evocation or even gain appropriate merits such as Tiny Creature merit subject to storyteller\u2019s jurisdiction. Furthermore for each size category that the familiar shrinks it reduces its strength and stamina scores by 2 (minimum 1) and raises its dexterity score by 1 (maximum 5).<br /> If the familiar in question is of a smaller statue than her exalted master the artifact may awaken a different evocation in its place that works the other way around.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Resonance:</i></u>A Solar or Lunar don\u2019t have a restriction on the shrinking steps they can take and for example could if they wanted reduce the size of a tyrant lizard to that of a mouse. Furthermore they can make the familiar look harmless and cute in the new size making highly more likely to be allowed to follow the exalted in civilized places that might have otherwise shunt the presence of a terrifying tyrant lizard.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Never Again</b><br /> <i>Cost: 5m or 5m, 1w, 1hl Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Indefinitely, Special<br /> Prerequisites: As One, Inseparable</i><br /> <br /> Familiar and Master share a bond so strong it almost impossible to discern if they are two souls or one sharing two bodies. The familiar may unknit its physical substance to vanish into the Masters essence until its master calls it back, this cost 5 motes which remain committed for the duration. <i>While those motes stay committed the familiar speeds her natural healing by a factor of (Exalted's Essence x 5)</i> In addition, if the familiar would be killed, it instead vanishes into the fires of its master anima, slowly reforming over the course of the story. Once the next story has begun, the familiar emerges at an unforeseen moment to aid its master, this costs 5m, 1w and 1hl.<br /> <br /> <i><u>Resonance:</u> A Solar or Lunar that unlocks this evocation also grants to the familiar extra defenses against poison and diseases. When the familiar has to roll (Stamina + Resistance) in response to a poison or disease it gains the Exalted's essence as automatic successes. This effect is permanent and incurs no additional cost for the Exalted</i><br /> <br /> <i><u>Dissonance:</u></i> The master of this evocation unlocks only the second part of the evocation that triggers upon the death of the familiar.<br /> <br /> <br /> SO IT IS DONE! please critic and evaluate. Some ideas are not original so please don't be to harsh on those.<br /> <br /> EDIT: On the Evocation <b>Never Again </b> The Italics part have been edited in after taking into consideration remspeedwagon advice. I am considering changing the <i><u>Dissonance </u></i> to exclude the life saving part instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9774,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9774-archangelazrael","user":"ArchangelAzrael","date":". 06-09-2017, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9774-archangelazrael","name":"ArchangelAzrael","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T08:49:50-07:00","id":1101653,"title":"","content":"You should probably buff Never Again a bit... The not dying is nice, but only once per story, and then summon the loyal steel for your familiar seems a bit...small, for a capstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13555-remspeedwagon","name":"remspeedwagon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T02:35:13-07:00","id":1101898,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your feedback... hm ok I see your point although unlike other powerful artifacts its is only an artifact 3 and the essence for the capstone is 3... I could add some increased healing mechanics and perhaps poison immunity. Expect version 1.1 soonish","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9774-archangelazrael","name":"ArchangelAzrael","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T09:59:21-07:00","id":1102025,"title":"","content":"<b>Skofnung</b> (Soulsteel Daiklave, Artifact \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> An ancient sword forged from the souls of the twelve greatest kings of the North. It calls out to fallen warriors, compelling them to once more raise their swords in battle.<br /> <br /> Accuracy: +3*<br /> Damage: +12*<br /> Defense: +1*<br /> Overwhelming: 5<br /> Attunement: 5<br /> Tags: Lethal, Melee, Balanced<br /> Hearthstone slots: 3<br /> <br /> Skofnung can house the souls of the fallen. Those who have been called to serve by previous wielders describe the world inside as a vast battlefield surrounding a single great hall of black stone. They would fight from grim morning until a darkness as complete as Oblivion fell, and then feast in the torch-lit hall until morning when the fallen would once more pick up their weapons and join a battle without purpose.<br /> <br /> When Skofnung contains souls, it gains the following bonuses to its traits depending on the number<br /> 1-6: +1 Accuracy<br /> 7-36: +1 Damage<br /> 37-144: +1 Defense<br /> 145-1200: +1 Accuracy<br /> 1200+: +1 Damage<br /> <br /> <b>Calling Home the Fallen</b><br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: None<br /> <br /> Solemnly placing the sword point first into the soil bloodied by war, the wielder calls to those fallen in battle all around them and compels them to find a new home within Skofnung. Roll (Charisma or Manipulation + Presence) to influence the ghosts of all those fallen in battle no longer three days and three nights before, and who are close enough to be affected. All those whose Resolve is low enough to be influenced are automatically compelled, unless they have an Intimacy they could use to resist the call, in which case they may spend a point of Willpower to resist the call of Skofnung. The range of this power depends on the wielder's Essence rating in the following manner:<br /> Essence 1: Close range<br /> Essence 2: Short range<br /> Essence 3: Long range<br /> Essence 4+: Extreme range<br /> <br /> If the wielder is Resonant with Skofnung, their Essence counts as one higher than it is for the purpose of determining range, and only a Major or Defining Intimacy can protect a ghost from being called.<br /> <br /> <b>Unleashed from Beyond</b><br /> Cost: 5m, (1lhl); Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Calling Home the Fallen<br /> <br /> Raising the sword high, the wielder summons the fallen to fight once more. This brings forth a Battle Group of the fallen from within Skofnung. This Battle Group has size (Essence/2 rounded up + 1), though it cannot be larger than the total of all souls contained within Skofnung. They arrive armed and ready to fight, but are Immaterial unless the wielder has spent the extra activation cost of (1 lhl), Materializing them through their own blood. Any ghosts slain while called into the world like this return unharmed to the blade once the Charm has run its course, or once they fall in battle.<br /> <br /> The Battle Group's traits are determined by the average member, it further has Perfect Morale and Might 1.<br /> <br /> If the wielder is resonant with Skofnung, the Battle Group is of size (Essence/2 rounded up + 2), though still limited by the number of souls contained within the blade. <br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom of the Gravebound</b><br /> Cost: 5m, (or less); Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisites: Unleashed from Beyond<br /> <br /> Holding the sword close to their heart, the wielder calls forth an individual contained within the blade to serve them in a wider capacity than simply as part of an army. Those called forth come fully realized with all the memories and knowledge of their former life, as well as their Intimacies, though they have acquired an additional Defining Intimacy of loyalty (or a similiar emotion) towards the wielder. While the Charm is active, it may be activated once more to call forth another ghost to serve. The cost to activate the Charm goes down by 1m for each ghost already manifested in this manner. No more than (Essence + 1) ghosts can be manifested at once.<br /> <br /> If the wielder is resonant with Skofnung, the number of ghosts than can be simoultaneously manifested is doubled.<br /> <br /> <b>Relics of the Dead</b><br /> Cost: -; Mins: Essence 3<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisites: Unleashed from Beyond<br /> <br /> When the dead come forth, they do so with the finest gear taken from all the battlefields of Creation. Every time the wielder calls forth the ghosts bound within Skofnung, they may decide how the ghosts are armed and armoured (or even dressed with Wisdom of the Gravebound). Furthermore, when called forth with Unleashed from Beyond, the Battle Group formed has Might 2 rather than 1. Similarly, when called forth with Wisdom of the Gravebound, the ghosts may have simple Thaumaturgical items to aid them.<br /> <br /> If the wielder is resonant with Skofnung, the ghosts become valid targets for Training Charms such as Tiger Warrior Training Technique or Flowing Mind Prana.<br /> <br /> <b>Irresistible Call of Oblivion</b><br /> Cost: 10m; Mins: Essence 4<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Psyche<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Wisdom of the Gravebound<br /> <br /> By placing the pommel of the sword on the forehead of one recently dead, the wielder may force them into service. Activating this Evocation requires no roll, and cannot be resisted, even with a Defining Intimacy. However, such intimacies still remain, so the wielder of Skofnung should take care when calling forth the ghosts of those who hate them.<br /> <br /> <b>What the Void Spews Forth</b><br /> Cost: 10m (1ahl/scene); Mins: Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisites: Relics of the Dead, Irresistible Call of Oblivion<br /> <br /> Raising the blade above their head, the wielder calls calls upon the Void itself to empower the ghosts under their command, and the Void answers. In return for the souls of the slain, Skofnung's ghosts come clad in the raiments of Death itself, and fight with the strength of the Void. When called forth with this Evocation, there is no size limit to the Battle Group summoned, every single soul is called from within Skofnung. They arrived armed and armoured in Soulsteel, granting them a Might rating of 3, and each ghost counts as two for the purposes of determining the Size of the Battle Group. However, once the Charm has run its course, every single ghost as well as the souls of all those slain by this army of the dead is doomed to Oblivion. Skofnung is empty once more, and the forbidding castle in its core falls silent.<br /> <br /> If the wielder is resonant with Skofnung, they may prolong its Duration by spending paying 1 Aggravated Health Level per additional scene. This damage may not be healed while the Charm is active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3693-esbilon","name":"Esbilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T05:49:25-07:00","id":1102781,"title":"","content":"<b>Skofnung</b> (Soulsteel Daiklave, Artifact \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) <hr /> Although it is not as awe-inspiring as volcano cutter and stormcaller with their environment changing properties I would argue it is just as (if not more) strong. Furthermore when powered up ( which is not hard to accomplice) it becomes better stat-wise than any printed artifact. The +2 defense in particular is very strong. Therefore an artifact 5 would be more appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Calling Home the Fallen</b> <hr /> Seems well balanced. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Unleashed from Beyond</b><br /> <hr /> This seems strong to me for an essence 1 evocation\u2026 maybe essence 2? Also it needs to have a reset condition so it can only be used 1 per day as the exalts could just use it again to have almost always max size battlegroup. There is a lhl cost but I think it needs further restrictions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom of the Gravebound</b><br /> <hr /> I am not too sure for this charm\u2026 For 15m committed you get to have 2 to 6 (or more realistically 4-12) Ghost retainers. It seems too much to me. Essence 3 for the evocation and reduce the number of ghost to be equal to Essence. Perhaps also add A dissonance so that the number of Ghost are essence/2 round down for everyone else<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Relics of the Dead</b> <hr /> I think balance wise this is a good evocation for its essence requirement. I would be tempted to switch the resonance power with the rise in might as it seems to be the strongest of the two and weaker exalted have worse \u201ctraining armies charms\u201d usually anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Irresistible Call of Oblivion</b> <hr /> Ok the no roll to resist seems inappropriate to me. I would have at least but some restriction like cannot target a creature with an essence score higher than yours or something similar. Still if it is recently dead it more likely than not means the exalted in question defeated him so he clearly was able to overcome him. I just think it can bypass some mechanics and can force in combination with the last evocation some entities that would be hard to completely destroy into oblivion. Also as a player I would be pissed off if I was told no chance to resist it, it just happens (despite the fact that my char would be dead by then :P).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What the Void Spews Fort</b><br /> <hr /> I like this charm a lot! But I think it can be too strong depending on how dedicated the player was in filling it with souls. Perhaps the artifact should have a max soul capacity? Other than that the fact that the defeated fall into oblivion as well without a roll to resist it is not to my liking. Now balance wise I think its ok for an essence 5 evocation on a lvl 5 artifact. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9774-archangelazrael","name":"ArchangelAzrael","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T08:11:17-07:00","id":1102815,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot for your feedback <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1102781#post1102781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Skofnung</b> (Soulsteel Daiklave, Artifact \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) <hr /> Although it is not as awe-inspiring as volcano cutter and stormcaller with their environment changing properties I would argue it is just as (if not more) strong. Furthermore when powered up ( which is not hard to accomplice) it becomes better stat-wise than any printed artifact. The +2 defense in particular is very strong. Therefore an artifact 5 would be more appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you're saying. The ST of the game I'm proposing this for was OK with 4, but I wouldn't be opposed to raising it to 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1102781#post1102781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unleashed from Beyond</b><br /> <hr /> This seems strong to me for an essence 1 evocation\u2026 maybe essence 2? Also it needs to have a reset condition so it can only be used 1 per day as the exalts could just use it again to have almost always max size battlegroup. There is a lhl cost but I think it needs further restrictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading of the rules is that you can't activate a Scenelong charm multiple times for increased effect, so you'll only ever get the size of battle group that fits your Essence. Also, I want it at Essence 1 so that it is available to a starting character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1102781#post1102781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Wisdom of the Gravebound</b><br /> <hr /> I am not too sure for this charm\u2026 For 15m committed you get to have 2 to 6 (or more realistically 4-12) Ghost retainers. It seems too much to me. Essence 3 for the evocation and reduce the number of ghost to be equal to Essence. Perhaps also add A dissonance so that the number of Ghost are essence/2 round down for everyone else</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a bit much, but the benefit of having multiple ghosts running around you at all times isn't very great compared to the benefit of just summoning whoever you need, it seemed mostly a flavor thing to me. Plus, I wanted to be able to have 12 souls since that fits the sword's legend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1102781#post1102781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Relics of the Dead</b> <hr /> I think balance wise this is a good evocation for its essence requirement. I would be tempted to switch the resonance power with the rise in might as it seems to be the strongest of the two and weaker exalted have worse \u201ctraining armies charms\u201d usually anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make it rather useless to those who aren't resonant, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1102781#post1102781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Irresistible Call of Oblivion</b> <hr /> Ok the no roll to resist seems inappropriate to me. I would have at least but some restriction like cannot target a creature with an essence score higher than yours or something similar. Still if it is recently dead it more likely than not means the exalted in question defeated him so he clearly was able to overcome him. I just think it can bypass some mechanics and can force in combination with the last evocation some entities that would be hard to completely destroy into oblivion. Also as a player I would be pissed off if I was told no chance to resist it, it just happens (despite the fact that my char would be dead by then :P).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was a bit iffy about the no roll to resist thing. Perhaps having a roll, but revoking it if the victim died as a consequence of the wielder's action (eg. death by poison or backstabbing in an alley). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1102781#post1102781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What the Void Spews Fort</b><br /> <hr /> I like this charm a lot! But I think it can be too strong depending on how dedicated the player was in filling it with souls. Perhaps the artifact should have a max soul capacity? Other than that the fact that the defeated fall into oblivion as well without a roll to resist it is not to my liking. Now balance wise I think its ok for an essence 5 evocation on a lvl 5 artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>As written, Battle Groups only go up to size 5, so the benefit of summoning a million souls is limited, though probably the ST would house rule around that. I had intended the bit about the enemies also being dragged into the Void to be a penalty since otherwise, you could just replace one army with another, effectively negating the cost of the Charm, but I see what you're saying. Perhaps limit the effect on enemies to mortals (since Extras is no longer a concept)?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3693-esbilon","name":"Esbilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T01:37:55-07:00","id":1103042,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Unleashed from Beyond</i></b><br /> <br /> I see if that\u2019s the case then no worries. I can understand the need to have it available as soon as possible for your character concept. It just that I find it more of an essence 2 evocation really. There are hearthstones that unlocks higher essence evocations earlier if you don\u2019t mind doing it that way. Anyway since the ST is ok with it don\u2019t mind me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Wisdom of the Gravebound</i></b><br /> <br /> My main concern is that in the new system things start to break if you have multiple people attack one. The Ghost have essence and charms (although in the book there are not many atm) and they can easily have max dice in attack and defense with training so they will most likely never count as trivial opponents. At essence 2 you can have 6 ghosts assist you, against an opponent without onslaught negation or something to protect its initiative it can turn very easily to one sided battle. Perhaps in combat have them count as a size 1 battle group? Other than I don\u2019t have that much of a problem with the evocation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Relics of the Dead</i></b><br /> <br /> Not necessarily\u2026 Might 2 is quite strong although to be fair an army comprised of war ghost is already might 2 by the rules as a default so I might be on the wrong side on this one. Perhaps having the training as a resonance ability is the stronger of the two.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Irresistible Call of Oblivion</i></b><br /> <br /> Yea that sounds more fair.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>What the Void Spews Fort</i></b><br /> Actualy \u201cIf <i>appreciably </i>more than a Size 5 battle group worth of combatants are present, they are represented by creating an additional battle group (or groups). 20 extra combat\u00adants are a drop in the bucket, but if an extra 300 are present, that\u2019s worth starting up a second Size 3 battle group\u201d So you could have like 10 size 5 battlegroups with this charm\u2026<br /> <br /> I see your concerns about negating the cost of the charm. Hm ok then leave it as it is. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Overall I really like the artifact. I would certainly want it as a player and would allow it as ST. You can easily make a mirror artifact as well by changing the theme a little to be more traditionally \u201cgood\u201d by making the stay inside the artifact like classic Viking paradise and replacing oblivion with lethe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9774-archangelazrael","name":"ArchangelAzrael","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T04:50:48-07:00","id":1103079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1103042#post1103042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Unleashed from Beyond</i></b><br /> <br /> I see if that\u2019s the case then no worries. I can understand the need to have it available as soon as possible for your character concept. It just that I find it more of an essence 2 evocation really. There are hearthstones that unlocks higher essence evocations earlier if you don\u2019t mind doing it that way. Anyway since the ST is ok with it don\u2019t mind me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like the artifact to not be dependent on a (Greater) Hearthstone in order to fulfill its base function. The calling power is a bit lackluster on its own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1103042#post1103042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Wisdom of the Gravebound</i></b><br /> <br /> My main concern is that in the new system things start to break if you have multiple people attack one. The Ghost have essence and charms (although in the book there are not many atm) and they can easily have max dice in attack and defense with training so they will most likely never count as trivial opponents. At essence 2 you can have 6 ghosts assist you, against an opponent without onslaught negation or something to protect its initiative it can turn very easily to one sided battle. Perhaps in combat have them count as a size 1 battle group? Other than I don\u2019t have that much of a problem with the evocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you're saying. If used in combat, they should definitely be a Battle Group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1103042#post1103042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Relics of the Dead</i></b><br /> <br /> Not necessarily\u2026 Might 2 is quite strong although to be fair an army comprised of war ghost is already might 2 by the rules as a default so I might be on the wrong side on this one. Perhaps having the training as a resonance ability is the stronger of the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much which is stronger. To my mind, Resonant abilities can be a bit circumstantial, but the core effect should always be worth it. If I'm a non-resonant character picking up this sword who doesn't have any training charms, if the powers were reversed, this Evocation would do <i>nothing</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1103042#post1103042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Irresistible Call of Oblivion</i></b><br /> <br /> Yea that sounds more fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good, I'll implement that, then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1103042#post1103042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>What the Void Spews Fort</i></b><br /> Actualy \u201cIf <i>appreciably </i>more than a Size 5 battle group worth of combatants are present, they are represented by creating an additional battle group (or groups). 20 extra combat*ants are a drop in the bucket, but if an extra 300 are present, that\u2019s worth starting up a second Size 3 battle group\u201d So you could have like 10 size 5 battlegroups with this charm\u2026<br /> <br /> I see your concerns about negating the cost of the charm. Hm ok then leave it as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right. Mmm, it makes by far the most thematic sense to empty out the sword entirely, and it means you can't hoard your best ghosts and just send out the dross when using the pinnacle. Still, presumably, the number of souls you have available is somewhat commensurate with the number of foes you are facing. Remember, the mass-calling Evocation can only be used on those fallen in battle. You can't slaughter villages to fuel the sword.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=1103042#post1103042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall I really like the artifact. I would certainly want it as a player and would allow it as ST. You can easily make a mirror artifact as well by changing the theme a little to be more traditionally \u201cgood\u201d by making the stay inside the artifact like classic Viking paradise and replacing oblivion with lethe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not sure I'd personally OK a mirror artifact that did the same, but was nice to people. It seems very much the province of Soulsteel to do this, but of course each to their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3693-esbilon","name":"Esbilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T17:16:38-07:00","id":1104038,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#3c78d8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Vivids Eyes of Mechanical Grace \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, N/A (repaired), (last update 10/06/17, by Nyimayad)</b></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">In the age of dream, there has been a lots of wonders, it was also the age of sorcery, the solars knew that they only see a portion of the world. Through ages of work, Bright Shattered Ice knew she had much to discover and grow. She creates this artifact in order to infuse herself, the greatest scholar, with a greater knowledge of the world.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Attunement special rule : Only solar can attune to the Vivid Eye of Mechanical Grace, it require high precision surgery and can\u2019t be unattuned without removing it. This surgery is an extended minimum of Intelligence and Dexterity + Medicine roll with difficulty 5, goal 40, terminus 6. Failure result in essence combustion. Attunement cost 3 motes that are only restored by removing the artifact (difficulty 5, goal 30, terminus 6).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Prosthesis :</b>This artifact is a prosthesis, repairing a defectuous prosthesis is a craft roll. And no organ can replace a prosthesis for two month and a day after being removed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#860659\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">New Keywords : Broken</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Some artifact build a long time ago have endure some harsh treatment, when they do so they remove the access to some of their might in order to prevent unexpected effect. Unlike regular repairing, a broken artifact require multiple repair to unlock new power. In some old artifact, there could be more than one broken steps, in which case, the degree of repairs required will be denote by Broken 2, Broken 3\u2026 When reaching each steps of repair, all corresponding defect are repaired</span></span> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#860659\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Evocations of The Vivids Eyes of Mechanical Grace</b></span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Using the eye to actually see or use any of it\u2019s evocation require to channel your essence threw it, lasting for a scene. When the solar do so, roll Essence against 1, failure result in the loss of one health point for the remaining of the scene. In any case, it allow the user to see and use Broken 1 Evocation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#860659\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Terrestrial circle initiation</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Upon attunement, the solar get initiation to Terrestrial Circle Sorcery and get access to basic sorcery.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i><b>Shaping ritual :</b></i></span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">A sorcerer with an Essence pool may spend a scene in meditation to commit to commit a total of 10 motes. Once she begins shaping a spell while wearing the talisman, she may draw on the power she\u2019s invested, contributing up to Essence+2 sorcerous motes towards the spell until the full commitment of ten motes has been converted into ten sorcerous motes, or the spell is cast (or countered).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Committed motes are converted to sorcerous motes on a one-to-one basis normally, but are converted into two sorcerous motes when casting the sorcerer\u2019s control spell. The sorcerer must wait until she\u2019s had a full night\u2019s sleep before she can charge the talisman again.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">While motes are commited, an image of the sun rising shine in her eye.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#860659\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Broken 1 :</b></span></span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Terrestrial Sorcerous working, ambition 3 (goal number 20), finesse 5 (difficulty 5), terminus 5.<br /> Superior project, difficulty 5, terminus 6, goal 100, 10 gold point per attempt. The roll is made with Craft(Jewelry), Craft(Artifact) or Medicine, which- ever the smallest.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Upon repair, the artifact no longer require essence roll. It\u2019s active whenever the user is willing to, allowing the solar to see and use Evocation at will.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#860659\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Subliming the immaterial</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Cost: \u2014</b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Mins: Essence 1</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Type: </b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Keywords: </b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Broken 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Duration: </b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Prerequisite Charms: </b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Spirit Detecting Glance (Rulebook p354), first circle sorcery (Rulebook p360)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">The solar is forever transformed by the knowledge of first circle sorcery. This charm permanently lowers the mote cost of Spirit Detecting Glance by one mote at broken 1, two motes at broken 2 and for free at broken 3.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#860659\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Plain sight in plain darkness</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Cost: \u2014</b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">; </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Mins: Essence 1</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Type: </b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Keywords: </b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Broken 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Duration: </b></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\